P -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nnl -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nnn-NO -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\noc -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\npa-IN -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\npl -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\npt-BR -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\npt-PT -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nrm -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nro -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nru -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nsk -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nsl -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nson -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nsq -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nsr -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nsv-SE -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nta -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nte -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nth -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\ntl -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\ntr -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\ntrs -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nuk -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nur -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nuz -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nvi -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nwo -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nxh -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nzam -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nzh-CN -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\nzh-TW -\u003e 48d93a2e79fe91518b850a6de8eedd03f26ebaf9\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "a89b3dda914c465fdf71692816c56f6a5d4f8114", "git_parents": ["b147363df6d9f7129a82fa3c99c91f9b11eec415"], "node": "a6a138c06bf3852528d5141aaafc2a17f2f63bc7", "parents": ["77990d2d898dd465ce43181260f407c09e9acdb9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Reitano \u003cjreitano@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069514 - Use documentGlobal instead of the removed ownerGlobal in PdfJsParent. r=pdfjs-reviewers,calixte\n\nNode.ownerGlobal was renamed to documentGlobal, so browser?.ownerGlobal\nevaluated to undefined rather than throwing. The\ngetMostRecentBrowserWindow() fallback therefore ran on every call: with a\nsingle window open that is the same window, so the bug was invisible, but\nwith several open the certificate tab could land in a window other than\nthe one showing the PDF.\n\nAdded a browser test for the multi-window case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323803\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_view_certificate_window.js"], "git_node": "d30e4ee05ee555a3353365479db5dd31e3219a73", "git_parents": ["a89b3dda914c465fdf71692816c56f6a5d4f8114"], "node": "e6703fbdf2c715d17efd071b0cb80c11ceac3565", "parents": ["a6a138c06bf3852528d5141aaafc2a17f2f63bc7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070788 - Rename RenderCompositor::GetAndResetReleaseFence() to GetAndResetReadFence() r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nReadFence is used more frequently in gfx than ReleaseFence.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324860\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/AsyncImagePipelineManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/AsyncImagePipelineManager.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositor.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorANGLE.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorANGLE.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorEGL.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorEGL.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderThread.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RendererOGL.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RendererOGL.h"], "git_node": "700a8304455e663679d83b703194bfac3f85e604", "git_parents": ["d30e4ee05ee555a3353365479db5dd31e3219a73"], "node": "bb56002b2b8564dfd22ed8494ce8a943a6178f9c", "parents": ["e6703fbdf2c715d17efd071b0cb80c11ceac3565"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071151 - Cherry-pick the upstream clang 23 fixes and fix cctools-port and winchecksec. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nllvmorg-24-init-8185-gbe215a25f001.patch and llvmorg-24-init-8187-gbc6c76a4d4f8.patch are the upstream\nextract_symbols.py fixes for the clang::interp exports and the Registry\u003cT\u003e accessors, so\nfilter-symbols_clang_23.patch shrinks back to the Mozilla-specific size reductions. That also keeps it\napplying to clang-trunk, which already has both fixes. llvmorg-24-init-7807-g651d01e873c6.patch cherry-picks\nthe upstream fix for a TypePrinter infinite recursion on FullyQualifiedName template parameters, which the\nmozsearch plugin hits on UniquePtr\u003cT[N]\u003e.\n\nlibdispatch trips the new -Wunused-but-set-global (backport of the upstream fix the tpoechtrager fork lacks),\ncctools-port's configure needs to copy LLVM 23's new llvm-c/Visibility.h and llvm-config.h next to lto.h, and\npe-parse's unused to_string template fails the /W4 /WX build whenever clang has -Wunused-template in -Wall\n(23.1.0 did, 23.1.1 backed it out pending a libc++ cleanup), so keep it off explicitly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325225\n", "files": ["build/build-clang/clang-23.json", "build/build-clang/filter-symbols_clang_23.patch", "build/build-clang/llvmorg-24-init-7807-g651d01e873c6.patch", "build/build-clang/llvmorg-24-init-8185-gbe215a25f001.patch", "build/build-clang/llvmorg-24-init-8187-gbc6c76a4d4f8.patch", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/misc.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-cctools-port.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-winchecksec.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/cctools-llvm-c-headers.patch", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/libdispatch-unused-but-set-global.patch"], "git_node": "5b744297960052799525874b6f21b8643d39be98", "git_parents": ["700a8304455e663679d83b703194bfac3f85e604"], "node": "b7d4fceaebf06062a88c8ad1c16281892978bb1b", "parents": ["bb56002b2b8564dfd22ed8494ce8a943a6178f9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068375. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325172\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContextHelper.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContextHelper.h", "dom/canvas/OffscreenCanvas.h", "dom/html/HTMLCanvasElement.h"], "git_node": "df6bb4f2c80e52f4d68dd3433eb4c71d7aeee6cb", "git_parents": ["5b744297960052799525874b6f21b8643d39be98"], "node": "fec0e68c2165a4be2ee6a530ffe85c079347fdd0", "parents": ["b7d4fceaebf06062a88c8ad1c16281892978bb1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068585 - Get rid of collections.OrderedDict r=ahochheiden\n\ndict is ordered since 3.6\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322955\n", "files": ["python/mach/mach/site.py"], "git_node": "55bee541e7dd24092f761ca21f3ba11e4db82613", "git_parents": ["df6bb4f2c80e52f4d68dd3433eb4c71d7aeee6cb"], "node": "ddfe9bcdfed27c1882fd709b2fca196a4dc74459", "parents": ["fec0e68c2165a4be2ee6a530ffe85c079347fdd0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068585 - Get rid of collections.OrderedDict r=ahochheiden\n\ndict is ordered since 3.6\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322956\n", "files": ["python/mozboot/mozboot/bootstrap.py"], "git_node": "ba3c806e8da60c676926d476dc4bc758dc9e6114", "git_parents": ["55bee541e7dd24092f761ca21f3ba11e4db82613"], "node": "ebb4eedf18cb2abc64a44e05e86730512599fc55", "parents": ["ddfe9bcdfed27c1882fd709b2fca196a4dc74459"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068585 - Get rid of collections.OrderedDict r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\ndict is ordered since 3.6\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322957\n", "files": ["layout/tools/reftest/reftestcommandline.py"], "git_node": "dae4ee5b8026f70b36a3747e3f9cb5ea6d3aa547", "git_parents": ["ba3c806e8da60c676926d476dc4bc758dc9e6114"], "node": "2bc550d5ec8dd92e91d15af56e2814093a40c215", "parents": ["ebb4eedf18cb2abc64a44e05e86730512599fc55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069689 - storage: Move some constructors and destructors out of line for C++23 compatibility. r=dom-storage-reviewers,janv\n\nC++23 P2448R2 [1] relaxed the requirements for constexpr destructors.\nIn C++23, UniquePtr's destructor, move constructor, and null assignment\noperator constexpr.\n\nFileSystemDatabaseManagerVersion001's inline destructor destroys\nUniquePtr\u003cFileSystemFileManager\u003e while FileSystemFileManager is only\nforward declared. LSWriteOptimizerBase's inline constructors and Reset()\ncan destroy or reset UniquePtr\u003cWriteInfo\u003e before the nested WriteInfo\ndefinition.\n\nMove these definitions to the corresponding .cpp files, where the\nUniquePtr pointee types are complete.\n\n[1] https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2022/p2448r2.html\n\nobj-aarch64-apple-darwin25.3.0/dist/include/mozilla/dom/LSWriteOptimizer.h:43:3: note: in instantiation of member function 'std::unique_ptr\u003cmozilla::dom::LSWriteOptimizerBase::WriteInfo\u003e::~unique_ptr' requested here\n   43 |   LSWriteOptimizerBase() : mLastSerialNumber(0), mTotalDelta(0) {}\n      |   ^\nobj-aarch64-apple-darwin25.3.0/dist/include/mozilla/dom/LSWriteOptimizer.h:31:9: note: forward declaration of 'mozilla::dom::LSWriteOptimizerBase::WriteInfo'\n   31 |   class WriteInfo;\n      |         ^\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323892\n", "files": ["dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemDatabaseManagerVersion001.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemDatabaseManagerVersion001.h", "dom/localstorage/LSWriteOptimizer.cpp", "dom/localstorage/LSWriteOptimizer.h"], "git_node": "1ccbebd6adafe46ecd530cd8169d1b4e50ca691f", "git_parents": ["dae4ee5b8026f70b36a3747e3f9cb5ea6d3aa547"], "node": "12434dea3007374be17f76b2e02fc375c3a7d780", "parents": ["2bc550d5ec8dd92e91d15af56e2814093a40c215"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069691 - gfx: Move RenderSourceNLRS's destructor out of line for C++23 compatibility. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nC++23 P2448R2 [1] relaxed the requirements for constexpr destructors.\nIn C++23 mode, Clang makes RenderSourceNLRS's defaulted destructor\nautomatically constexpr. Clang defines that destructor in NativeLayer.h\nwith only a forward declaration of gl::MozFramebuffer.\n\nDefining RenderSourceNLRS's destructor instantiates the destructor of\nits UniquePtr\u003cgl::MozFramebuffer\u003e member. Its default deleter requires\nMozFramebuffer to be complete, so libc++'s completeness check fails.\n\nTo resolve this, move RenderSourceNLRS's destructor to NativeLayer.cpp,\nwhere MozFramebuffer.h provides the complete type. This avoids adding\nits GL header dependencies to NativeLayer.h.\n\n[1] https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2022/p2448r2.html\n\nMacOSX26.4.sdk/usr/include/c++/v1/__memory/unique_ptr.h:75:19: error: invalid application of 'sizeof' to an incomplete type 'mozilla::gl::MozFramebuffer'\n   75 |     static_assert(sizeof(_Tp) \u003e= 0, \"cannot delete an incomplete type\");\n      |                   ^~~~~~~~~~~\nobj-macos/dist/include/mozilla/layers/NativeLayer.h:264:7: note: in instantiation of member function 'std::unique_ptr\u003cmozilla::gl::MozFramebuffer\u003e::~unique_ptr' requested here\n  264 | class RenderSourceNLRS : public profiler_screenshots::RenderSource {\n      |       ^\nobj-macos/dist/include/mozilla/layers/NativeLayer.h:264:7: note: in implicit destructor for 'mozilla::layers::RenderSourceNLRS' first required here\nobj-macos/dist/include/mozilla/layers/NativeLayer.h:22:7: note: forward declaration of 'mozilla::gl::MozFramebuffer'\n   22 | class MozFramebuffer;\n      |       ^\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323893\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/NativeLayer.cpp", "gfx/layers/NativeLayer.h"], "git_node": "82b54c3f40ddd0c5661fd75c82e905f4a6bf39b6", "git_parents": ["1ccbebd6adafe46ecd530cd8169d1b4e50ca691f"], "node": "2fec21527a2a787bea88dc5faa56da796aa555d3", "parents": ["12434dea3007374be17f76b2e02fc375c3a7d780"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069686 - uniffi: Move PromiseHandler's destructor out of line for C++23 compatibility. r=nika\n\nC++23 P2448R2 [1] relaxed the requirements for constexpr destructors.\nC++23 makes UniquePtr's destructor, move constructor, and null\nassignment operator automatically constexpr.\n\nClang defines PromiseHandler's virtual destructor inline when the\nenclosing AsyncCallbackMethodHandlerBase class is still incomplete.\nThis instantiates the destruction path for\nUniquePtr\u003cAsyncCallbackMethodHandlerBase\u003e, whose default deleter\nrequires AsyncCallbackMethodHandlerBase to be complete.\n\nTo resolve this, move PromiseHandler's destructor definition to\nCallbacks.cpp where AsyncCallbackMethodHandlerBase is complete.\n\n[1] https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2022/p2448r2.html\n\nMacOSX26.5.sdk/usr/include/c++/v1/__memory/unique_ptr.h:75:19: error: invalid application of 'sizeof' to an incomplete type 'mozilla::uniffi::AsyncCallbackMethodHandlerBase'\n75 |     static_assert(sizeof(_Tp) \u003e= 0, \"cannot delete an incomplete type\");\n   |                   ^~~~~~~~~~~\ntoolkit/components/uniffi-js/Callbacks.h:137:5: note: in instantiation of member function 'std::unique_ptr\u003cmozilla::uniffi::AsyncCallbackMethodHandlerBase\u003e::~unique_ptr' requested here\n137 |     ~PromiseHandler() = default;\n    |     ^\ntoolkit/components/uniffi-js/Callbacks.h:137:5: note: in defaulted destructor for 'mozilla::uniffi::AsyncCallbackMethodHandlerBase::PromiseHandler' first required here\ntoolkit/components/uniffi-js/Callbacks.h:75:7: note: definition of 'mozilla::uniffi::AsyncCallbackMethodHandlerBase' is not complete until the closing '}'\n75 | class AsyncCallbackMethodHandlerBase {\n   |       ^\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324858\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/uniffi-js/Callbacks.cpp", "toolkit/components/uniffi-js/Callbacks.h"], "git_node": "edcf975216e1dbd66b3ab8a0ea8730a314d82426", "git_parents": ["82b54c3f40ddd0c5661fd75c82e905f4a6bf39b6"], "node": "147db67f1ef8b29322ac739798b94bd2a68f5351", "parents": ["2fec21527a2a787bea88dc5faa56da796aa555d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069687 - intl: Move the Encoder and Decoder factory methods out of the Encoding class definition for C++23 compatibility. r=hsivonen\n\nC++23 P2448R2 [1] relaxed the requirements for constexpr destructors.\nIn C++23, Clang makes UniquePtr's destructor automatically constexpr.\nClang eagerly instantiates its body for the local UniquePtr\u003cEncoder\u003e\nand UniquePtr\u003cDecoder\u003e variables in Encoding's inline factory methods.\nEncoder and Decoder are only forward-declared at that point, so the\ndeleter's complete-type check fails.\n\nTo resolve this, move the NewDecoder() and NewDecoder factory methods\nafter the Encoding class definition so they have complete class\ndefinitions for Encoder and Decoder.\n\n[1] https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2022/p2448r2.html\n\nMacOSX26.1.sdk/usr/include/c++/v1/__memory/unique_ptr.h:76:19: error: invalid application of 'sizeof' to an incomplete type 'mozilla::Encoder'\n76 |     static_assert(sizeof(_Tp) \u003e= 0, \"cannot delete an incomplete type\");\n   |                   ^~~~~~~~~~~\nMacOSX26.1.sdk/usr/include/c++/v1/__memory/unique_ptr.h:300:7: note: in instantiation of member function 'std::default_delete\u003cmozilla::Encoder\u003e::operator()' requested here\n300 |       __deleter_(__tmp);\n    |       ^\nMacOSX26.1.sdk/usr/include/c++/v1/__memory/unique_ptr.h:269:71: note: in instantiation of member function 'std::unique_ptr\u003cmozilla::Encoder\u003e::reset' requested here\n269 |   _LIBCPP_HIDE_FROM_ABI _LIBCPP_CONSTEXPR_SINCE_CXX23 ~unique_ptr() { reset(); }\n    |                                                                       ^\nobj-aarch64-apple-darwin25.0.0/dist/include/mozilla/Encoding.h:736:24: note: in instantiation of member function 'std::unique_ptr\u003cmozilla::Encoder\u003e::~unique_ptr' requested here\n736 |     UniquePtr\u003cEncoder\u003e encoder(encoding_new_encoder(this));\n    |                        ^\nobj-aarch64-apple-darwin25.0.0/dist/include/mozilla/Encoding.h:28:7: note: forward declaration of 'mozilla::Encoder'\n 28 | class Encoder;\n    |       ^\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323890\n", "files": ["intl/Encoding.h"], "git_node": "78cb174eb3d24671df0e6bddcf9434908a8eba18", "git_parents": ["edcf975216e1dbd66b3ab8a0ea8730a314d82426"], "node": "7237a02436160cff7382923505039ad57085e170", "parents": ["147db67f1ef8b29322ac739798b94bd2a68f5351"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069692 - Make some JSAPI global variables constexpr or constinit for C++23 compatibility. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nC++23 P2448R2 [1] relaxes the requirements for constexpr functions.\nA defaulted destructor is now constexpr when it meets the general\nconstexpr function requirements. This makes the affected test object\ntypes eligible for constant initialization, so the global-variable\ninitialization checker rejects their MOZ_RUNINIT annotations.\n\nTo resolve the checker warnings, make the immutable JSClass,\nexternal-string callback, and proxy-handler objects constexpr. Make the\ncallback and proxy-handler constructors constexpr as required.\n\nTestJSPrincipals must remain mutable because its reference count changes.\nMark system_principals constinit and directly initialize the JSPrincipals\nbase with RefCount. Define the constexpr TestJSPrincipals constructor in\nthe header so its definition is available when system_principals is\nconstant-initialized.\n\n[1] https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2022/p2448r2.html\n\njs/src/jsapi-tests/testSetPropertyIgnoringNamedGetter.cpp:42:1: error: Global variable flagged as MOZ_RUNINIT but actually has constant initialisation. Consider removing the annotation or (as a last resort) flagging it as MOZ_GLOBINIT.\n42 | MOZ_RUNINIT const CustomProxyHandler customProxyHandler;\n   | ^\n\n/builds/worker/checkouts/gecko/js/src/jsapi-tests/tests.cpp(421,19): error: non-constexpr declaration of 'TestJSPrincipals' follows constexpr declaration\n421 | TestJSPrincipals::TestJSPrincipals(int rc)\n    |                   ^\n/builds/worker/checkouts/gecko/js/src/jsapi-tests/tests.h(303,22): note: previous declaration is here\n303 |   constexpr explicit TestJSPrincipals(int rc = 0);\n    |                      ^\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323894\n", "files": ["js/src/jsapi-tests/testChromeBuffer.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testExternalStrings.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testSetPropertyIgnoringNamedGetter.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/tests.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/tests.h"], "git_node": "1f929f12427cf61eaa85d16313d201b8215cb038", "git_parents": ["78cb174eb3d24671df0e6bddcf9434908a8eba18"], "node": "085253e7d9306eb3e6fde34e25fb4f48e955b492", "parents": ["7237a02436160cff7382923505039ad57085e170"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069688 - mozglue: Include ProfileBuffer.h in ProfilerBacktrace.cpp for C++23 compatibility. r=profiler-reviewers,dcarver\n\nC++23 P2448R2 [1] relaxed the requirements for constexpr destructors.\nC++23 makes UniquePtr's destructor constexpr. Clang instantiates\nconstexpr function templates when they are first referenced. The\n'= nullptr' default argument for aProfileBufferStorageOrNull creates\na temporary UniquePtr\u003cProfileBuffer\u003e, so callers may instantiate its\ndestructor while parsing ProfilerBacktrace.h.\n\nThe destructor requires a complete class definition for ProfileBuffer,\nbut ProfilerBacktrace.h only forward declares ProfileBuffer.\n\nInclude ProfileBuffer.h so ProfileBuffer is complete at the point of\ninstantiation.\n\n[1] https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/papers/2022/p2448r2.html\n\nIn file included from mozglue/baseprofiler/core/ProfilerBacktrace.cpp:7:\n...\nMacOSX26.1.sdk/usr/include/c++/v1/__memory/unique_ptr.h:76:19: error: invalid application of 'sizeof' to an incomplete type 'mozilla::baseprofiler::ProfileBuffer'\n   76 |     static_assert(sizeof(_Tp) \u003e= 0, \"cannot delete an incomplete type\");\n      |                   ^~~~~~~~~~~\nmozglue/baseprofiler/core/ProfilerBacktrace.h:45:62: note: in instantiation of member function 'std::unique_ptr\u003cmozilla::baseprofiler::ProfileBuffer\u003e::~unique_ptr' requested here\n   45 |       UniquePtr\u003cProfileBuffer\u003e aProfileBufferStorageOrNull = nullptr);\n      |                                                              ^\nmozglue/baseprofiler/core/ProfilerBacktrace.h:21:7: note: forward declaration of 'mozilla::baseprofiler::ProfileBuffer'\n   21 | class ProfileBuffer;\n      |       ^\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323891\n", "files": ["mozglue/baseprofiler/core/ProfilerBacktrace.h"], "git_node": "4886ee24f53fc720052479988e8da8bf222495a7", "git_parents": ["1f929f12427cf61eaa85d16313d201b8215cb038"], "node": "dd9f632c4ca3534de5ba5628eb93946df079e548", "parents": ["085253e7d9306eb3e6fde34e25fb4f48e955b492"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Punam Dahiya \u003cpdahiya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071073 - Give Smart Window pref-state metrics application lifetime so they report on every ping r=Mardak\n\nsmart_window.model, smart_window.memories_optin and smart_window.set_default_optin are current-state mirrors of prefs, set once per session in SmartWindowTelemetry.init() and re-set on change by the pref observers. They used the default `ping` lifetime, so the value was cleared after the first metrics ping of a session and was absent from every later ping. Reading any of them off a client's most recent ping reported the `unset` sentinel for most clients that actually have a value.\n\nThis gives all three `lifetime: application`, matching the already-correct smart_window.enabled. `application` clears on restart but init() re-sets the value each session, so it stays current without going stale, and it is now carried on every metrics ping.\n\nThis also closes the updateModelMetric race: because the value now persists rather than being cleared after the first ping, a value that resolves too late for the first ping is still reported on subsequent pings instead of being lost for the whole session.\n\nNote for data stewards: this changes how often these existing metrics are transmitted, not what is collected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325133\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "06db999ddd8b56a360518bc13fdff66f59267458", "git_parents": ["4886ee24f53fc720052479988e8da8bf222495a7"], "node": "896d50164f217d2983b834fafa9c97b94ed7d193", "parents": ["dd9f632c4ca3534de5ba5628eb93946df079e548"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070844 - Add a SWGL submodule. r=lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324904\n", "files": ["mots.yaml"], "git_node": "1eed015ea320634a3500fd65a9b126f2c078c791", "git_parents": ["06db999ddd8b56a360518bc13fdff66f59267458"], "node": "6fb6357ceeb45550538a5930673d9fc688a73a5a", "parents": ["896d50164f217d2983b834fafa9c97b94ed7d193"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070844 - Make Lee Salzman the module owner of Moz2D. r=lsalzman,shtrom\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324905\n", "files": ["mots.yaml"], "git_node": "c7588ee9e1a86e3642fe76199a755b8c64a28842", "git_parents": ["1eed015ea320634a3500fd65a9b126f2c078c791"], "node": "f9baddcc4cdcc68bd85ce652b6fba1cab284ef1e", "parents": ["6fb6357ceeb45550538a5930673d9fc688a73a5a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2027953 - [devtools] Don't sync breakpoints against a destroyed target, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\n`newGeneratedSources` checks that a source actor's target is alive when the\nresource comes in, but not after awaiting the source maps, and then dispatches\n`checkPendingBreakpoints` without awaiting it. A target destroyed in that window\nleaves an unhandled `targetFront.getSourceContentForResource failed: TypeError:\nthis.commands is undefined` rejection, which fails\nsourcemaps/browser_dbg-sourcemaps-reloading.js and browser_dbg-reloading.js.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325031\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/actions/sources/newSources.js"], "git_node": "535a0dee531d3e40fa157a39ae169cfdced8472d", "git_parents": ["c7588ee9e1a86e3642fe76199a755b8c64a28842"], "node": "ae1cc277945bb0e0f11122f3790079d16be24715", "parents": ["f9baddcc4cdcc68bd85ce652b6fba1cab284ef1e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070920 - [devtools] Re-enable browser_dbg-reloading.js, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nThe test named its source by a partial path, which stopped matching when\nBug 1755736 narrowed `findSource` from a substring search to an exact file-name\nmatch; that bug kept full-URL support for pages like this one, where several\noriginal sources share a file name, so the narrow match stays as it is. The\nreloads also waited on the document's path, which never named a source.\n\nAbandoning a reload leaks the toolbox window: the last one cannot settle until\nthe page load the breakpoint holds completes, so `navigateTo` stays suspended\nwith `dbg` in its frame until shutdown. Resuming at the end settles all three.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325032\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-reloading.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_qz.toml"], "git_node": "e7d24be42b01dea04bde4accfff0867ab03a9284", "git_parents": ["535a0dee531d3e40fa157a39ae169cfdced8472d"], "node": "7c05d98ed710e9f67374aa605dfe56ca48704ee1", "parents": ["ae1cc277945bb0e0f11122f3790079d16be24715"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070917 - [devtools] Re-enable browser_dbg-sourcemapped-stepping.js, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nBug 1528855 removed the pause points that kept stepping on original statement\nboundaries, and the loop that stepped past a position the previous step already\nreported. It disabled this test in the same landing. Neither came back, so the\nexpectations here are the positions the debugger reports today rather than the\npre-2019 ones.\n\nThree changes passed the test by while it was off: Bug 1755736 made `findSource`\nmatch a filename or a full URL, so its `input.` URL stopped matching `input.js`;\nBug 1849998 made test-facing columns 1-based; and Bug 1856270 added\n`shouldWaitForLoadedScopes` for pausing in original sources.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325030\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/shared-head.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/sourcemaps/browser.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/sourcemaps/browser_dbg-sourcemapped-stepping.js"], "git_node": "048573cab61b83b305a1486acfcead14f0cfc0df", "git_parents": ["e7d24be42b01dea04bde4accfff0867ab03a9284"], "node": "21a9fc6de4413bd35a92ac4088cb802ad1b6b577", "parents": ["7c05d98ed710e9f67374aa605dfe56ca48704ee1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070970 - [devtools] Stop leaving preview popup waits polling in browser_dbg-preview-invalid-tokens.js, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nwaitForElement polls through waitUntil, which re-arms a timeout on the top\nlevel browser window for as long as its predicate is false. Racing it against\na timeout and then taking the timeout branch leaves that poll running, and its\nclosure retains dbg, and with it the debugger, webconsole and toolbox\ndocuments, until shutdown. Asserting on findElement after a plain wait leaves\nnothing behind, so the flush hover added by Bug 1767711 is no longer needed\nand the debug skip added by Bug 1958748 can go.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325023\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-preview-invalid-tokens.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_gp.toml"], "git_node": "0abaeaf6404961a5e8e834cbe793e80e8ebfa10c", "git_parents": ["048573cab61b83b305a1486acfcead14f0cfc0df"], "node": "b386bffd2f49abe7a61c84a67573fb6fde5cb83e", "parents": ["21a9fc6de4413bd35a92ac4088cb802ad1b6b577"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2001947 - Focus the browser element directly, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nSpecialPowers.focus() takes a window, and its windowGlobalChild lookup does not\napply to a browser element, so every call logged a TypeError. The element was\nfocused regardless, which is all this helper wanted.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325037\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-event-breakpoints.js"], "git_node": "0cef53fdf12961283bc02e890c79a0878e7192d1", "git_parents": ["0abaeaf6404961a5e8e834cbe793e80e8ebfa10c"], "node": "d4ba6f2cb5e90907ca24c6f953d1e0cf2f19aa86", "parents": ["b386bffd2f49abe7a61c84a67573fb6fde5cb83e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2001947 - Deselect the compositionend event breakpoint once its round is over, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nLeft enabled, this one pauses the debuggee once more after the textInput step, so\nthe smooth scrollTo of the scrollend step never resolves and the test hangs there.\nBug 2001947 comment 0 is that hang.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325038\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-event-breakpoints.js"], "git_node": "8ba72e18a7b55fd3c5db87eb102597da85194ca9", "git_parents": ["0cef53fdf12961283bc02e890c79a0878e7192d1"], "node": "1469362b50bbfa0be121c00937d666d30192a30c", "parents": ["d4ba6f2cb5e90907ca24c6f953d1e0cf2f19aa86"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070932 - Identify the ember app's router.js by URL, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nFour original sources on the ember quickstart page are named router.js, three of\nthem from vendor.js, and findSource() returns the first one in insertion order.\nWhen vendor.map is processed before quickstart.map the test picks\nember-routing/services/router.js, whose line 13 is a comment, so addBreakpoint()\nnever dispatches SET_BREAKPOINT and the helper waits until the test times out.\n\nNaming a source by its full URL is the case Bug 1755736 kept URL support for\nwhen it narrowed findSource() to an exact file-name match.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325040\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-ember-original-variable-mapping-notifications.js"], "git_node": "8987e9a119c54218c156b006f20b1222eac281bd", "git_parents": ["8ba72e18a7b55fd3c5db87eb102597da85194ca9"], "node": "4e7ff632efecf98c9bcca56ec52d520913392cff", "parents": ["1469362b50bbfa0be121c00937d666d30192a30c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070797 - Stop skipping debugger tests on tsan, asan and mac, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nNo failure on try. Bug 1607636, cited by one of them, is a general intermittent\nrather than a tsan defect; Bug 1591064 is a task about enabling ToolboxTask\ntests on asan.\n\nBug 1959062's mac skip can never apply on macosx1470-64, whose test set is\ncppunittest only, and Bug 2028047 mirrored it onto macOS 15 across every test\ncarrying it, without evidence for this file.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325019\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_af.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_gp.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/integration/browser.toml"], "git_node": "0e7fcd812fddf07590db039ae863565c6e701667", "git_parents": ["8987e9a119c54218c156b006f20b1222eac281bd"], "node": "6cb4fd2f9b69d3daea454caa93328006e2c66b4b", "parents": ["4e7ff632efecf98c9bcca56ec52d520913392cff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2015089 - Simplify scroll event handling. r=hiro,layout-reviewers\n\nThis makes the scroll event handling more per-spec, and I think it's a\nmuch simpler approach than bug 2015089.\n\nNote that this subtly changes behavior around the edges, which I'm not\ntotally happy about: With this patch, if you reframe, you might end up\nwith two scroll events in the same frame, while pre-patch you end up\njust with one. However, pre-patch has a separate set of issues, e.g. you\nmight end up with _zero_ scroll events rather than one if you scroll and\nthen go display: none or reframe.\n\nWith this setup it is very easy to fix tho, by keeping mWeakFrame in\nScrollEvent and refusing to fire if the frame is dead. So if this causes\ntrouble it is trivial to go back to the previous behavior. But I think\nit's better to incorrectly fire one more event than incorrectly not\nfiring any event...\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324919\n", "files": ["dom/base/VisualViewport.cpp", "dom/base/VisualViewport.h", "layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/base/PresShell.h", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/events/scrolling/scrollend-event-fired-after-instant-scroll-in-microtask.html.ini"], "git_node": "5b5dced46d8fb0426da11dd389d85766e36cf9c8", "git_parents": ["0e7fcd812fddf07590db039ae863565c6e701667"], "node": "9db9e1767922f8242308c3e927371dd358754da3", "parents": ["6cb4fd2f9b69d3daea454caa93328006e2c66b4b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1900953 - Use raster space instead of world space in shaders. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nWorld space is the root coordinate space. The coordinate space in shaders that is a device scale away from device space is actually raster space.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324880\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/res/prim_shared.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_split_composite.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_text_run.glsl"], "git_node": "bbac0edf66f3814a8488fbae33f8f0cc3340a7fc", "git_parents": ["5b5dced46d8fb0426da11dd389d85766e36cf9c8"], "node": "d60afdd04c6463c2556ffb8f980be0992e3aa179", "parents": ["9db9e1767922f8242308c3e927371dd358754da3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1900953 - Use Device space instead of world space in composite.glsl. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nThe shader already conflates the two with code that like 'world_pos = mix(device_rect.xy, device_rect.zw, aPosition.xy);'. For the compositor, device space and world space happen to be the same because we only composite at the root, however device space is a more useful concept (a space that lines up with the pixel grid of the destination texture) while world space tends to be a bit of a trap (the hard-coded root of the spatial tree) that is best avoided.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324881\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/res/composite.glsl"], "git_node": "8e9079528d4f517df6761c303caafae59255d7e4", "git_parents": ["bbac0edf66f3814a8488fbae33f8f0cc3340a7fc"], "node": "386c96e135d713b4aabe6bcf9e9a4c8a219bad7e", "parents": ["d60afdd04c6463c2556ffb8f980be0992e3aa179"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069385 - Stop running the SpiderMonkey source checks as part of regular builds r=linter-reviewers,spidermonkey-reviewers,sergesanspaille,mgaudet\n\nThe SpiderMonkey style, opcode and MacroAssembler checks ran from `mach build`,\nso every build paid for a lint pass unrelated to compilation. Expose them\nthrough mozlint as the `spidermonkey` linter instead, which is what CI already\nschedules, and drop the build-time invocation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323629\n", "files": ["config/run_spidermonkey_checks.py", "docs/code-quality/lint/linters/spidermonkey.md", "js/src/build/moz.build", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint.yml", "tools/lint/spidermonkey.yml", "tools/lint/spidermonkey/__init__.py", "tools/lint/test/python.toml", "tools/lint/test/test_spidermonkey.py"], "git_node": "0bf3dd619716c9bc6a4feb0c0b2627a19a9ed10d", "git_parents": ["8e9079528d4f517df6761c303caafae59255d7e4"], "node": "8fc3f72b063f464eb5b6cbe36b222c43ddb295fd", "parents": ["386c96e135d713b4aabe6bcf9e9a4c8a219bad7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069385 - Move the SpiderMonkey check scripts into tools/lint/spidermonkey r=linter-reviewers,spidermonkey-reviewers,sergesanspaille,mgaudet\n\nNow that the checks no longer run from `mach build`, mozlint is their only\nconsumer, so keep them next to the linter that drives them instead of in\nconfig/.\n\ncheck_js_opcode.py derived topsrcdir from its own depth in the tree, so bump\nit to match the new location.\n\nSince /config/** was packaged wholesale into the standalone SpiderMonkey\nsource tarball but /tools/ is cherry-picked, add an explicit filter so the\nchecks stay available there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323630\n", "files": ["config/check_js_opcode.py", "config/check_macroassembler_style.py", "config/check_spidermonkey_style.py", "docs/code-quality/lint/linters/spidermonkey.md", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/make-source-package.py", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint.yml", "tools/lint/spidermonkey.yml", "tools/lint/spidermonkey/__init__.py", "tools/lint/spidermonkey/check_js_opcode.py", "tools/lint/spidermonkey/check_macroassembler_style.py", "tools/lint/spidermonkey/check_spidermonkey_style.py"], "git_node": "a166bc2c6922df2721d404813befe9443d38d578", "git_parents": ["0bf3dd619716c9bc6a4feb0c0b2627a19a9ed10d"], "node": "0890710e0a88916433b14930b54c09eaf3f0d741", "parents": ["8fc3f72b063f464eb5b6cbe36b222c43ddb295fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2015089 - Follow-up null-check + consistency nits. r=hiro,layout-reviewers\n\nMake the code more similar between scroll / scrollend and add a missing\nnullcheck.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325293\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "4ce0e4ecddb209c4b203d3e8b35194a1b13959ff", "git_parents": ["a166bc2c6922df2721d404813befe9443d38d578"], "node": "88a4b2dab83d1f66bfa554158754c83ce3d1b18a", "parents": ["0890710e0a88916433b14930b54c09eaf3f0d741"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988569 - Bump the A-C changelog to the next nightly version during merge-day main bump r=tthibaud,releng-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\nAutomate the changelog step of the nightly development cycle by adding a\nregex-replacement to the bump-main behaviour, so landoscript opens a new\n'In Development' section for the upcoming version and demotes the\ncurrent one when main is bumped. This replaces the manual changelog edit\npreviously done by mobile/android/beta-cut.py.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324635\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/merge-automation/kind.yml"], "git_node": "265666bcba5e23d012325160d0119fc63f39e533", "git_parents": ["4ce0e4ecddb209c4b203d3e8b35194a1b13959ff"], "node": "0a05af3d81774aab679abeb862874a1f52da6d55", "parents": ["88a4b2dab83d1f66bfa554158754c83ce3d1b18a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070947 - Clarify the integer precision limit in the Hexadecimal marker format doc. r=canova,profiler-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nThe note on MarkerSchema::Format::Hexadecimal claimed values wider than a\n32-bit unsigned integer might get truncated. The actual limit is JS\nNumber.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER (2^53-1) and it applies to every integer format,\nso say that, and point at the supported way to display a 64-bit value:\nconvert it to a hexadecimal string in StreamJSONMarkerData and use the\nString format.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324988\n", "files": ["mozglue/baseprofiler/public/BaseProfilerMarkersPrerequisites.h"], "git_node": "6e3d0df73f15b018ccf1a455e8d094b3cec356ea", "git_parents": ["265666bcba5e23d012325160d0119fc63f39e533"], "node": "641492bc5c22a4184dc5dc7c983d899936b08740", "parents": ["0a05af3d81774aab679abeb862874a1f52da6d55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "geppy \u003chello@geppy.im\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1981904 - make chatbot inert during onboarding r=ayeddi,Mardak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D283788\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/chat.js", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_sidebar.js"], "git_node": "a993bf5ca9f5056dab73019bd03e9e28157a53c4", "git_parents": ["6e3d0df73f15b018ccf1a455e8d094b3cec356ea"], "node": "922ff36889e894596bfb5719552b25288b8b07ce", "parents": ["641492bc5c22a4184dc5dc7c983d899936b08740"], "tags": []}, {"author": "zhuangxiaosen \u003cxiaosen.zhuang@speediance.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069515 - Use documentGlobal instead of the removed ownerGlobal in FormAutofillPreferences r=credential-management-reviewers,dimi\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324835\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillPreferences.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "bc3360c732ba4ae98719e6081f44c339214ddd9a", "git_parents": ["a993bf5ca9f5056dab73019bd03e9e28157a53c4"], "node": "c51d907c468ab678c42f4244b9b159237b2a19e2", "parents": ["922ff36889e894596bfb5719552b25288b8b07ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071196 - Avoid 32-bit overflow when converting chunk indices to file offsets in CacheFile (Coverity CID 1286534) r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nkChunkSize is an int32_t and the chunk index is a uint32_t, so\n`aIndex * kChunkSize` is evaluated in 32 bits and wraps once the index reaches\n16384, i.e. for entries larger than 4GB. Both results feed int64_t offsets.\nCacheFile::BytesFromChunk already casts before multiplying; do the same at the\ntwo remaining sites.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325296\n", "files": ["netwerk/cache2/CacheFile.cpp"], "git_node": "2fafa1ee1d71a795353a9b7b6c8bf9b6691a0184", "git_parents": ["bc3360c732ba4ae98719e6081f44c339214ddd9a"], "node": "41970502eed049553d352c038afe991843316b51", "parents": ["c51d907c468ab678c42f4244b9b159237b2a19e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067718 - Update generated TS type definitions, including the Glean one r=zombie\n\nThis was done using:\n\n  mach ts build\n  mach ts update\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323513\n", "files": ["tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.darwin.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.dom.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.glean.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts", "tools/ts/config/error_list.json"], "git_node": "0f1d79018230ce4162c9a259f4dbf3a9c9f7b3a4", "git_parents": ["2fafa1ee1d71a795353a9b7b6c8bf9b6691a0184"], "node": "f70b871a17a5799d0dc59a483ab61d220830855a", "parents": ["41970502eed049553d352c038afe991843316b51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070987 - Rename BaseMarkerType::StoreName to ETWStoreName. r=profiler-reviewers,sandbox-reviewers,bobowen,canova\n\nStoreName only ever controlled whether the name passed to an individual\nmarker call is emitted as an extra MarkerName field on the ETW event; the\nprofiler's own marker storage always records the name. The old name did not\nconvey that, so rename it to ETWStoreName.\n\nAlso rewrite its documentation, in BaseMarkerType and in markers-guide.md,\nto explain when to set it: leave it false when every marker of the type is\nrecorded with the same name, since the name then carries no per-marker\ninformation, and set it to true only when callers pass a distinct name per\nmarker and the duplication cost of a copy of that string in every recorded\nETW event is acceptable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325300\n", "files": ["dom/base/ChromeUtils.cpp", "mozglue/baseprofiler/public/BaseProfilerMarkers.h", "mozglue/baseprofiler/public/BaseProfilerMarkersPrerequisites.h", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxtarget/TargetGeckoServicesImpl.cpp", "tools/profiler/docs/markers-guide.md", "tools/profiler/public/ETWTools.h", "xpcom/threads/nsThread.cpp"], "git_node": "0653ae5f15f53af08612b5dd12e641514dd27772", "git_parents": ["0f1d79018230ce4162c9a259f4dbf3a9c9f7b3a4"], "node": "f017cde0c84417e96a6a94a989d2e2e891a916f0", "parents": ["f70b871a17a5799d0dc59a483ab61d220830855a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1868149 - use moz-phab instead of arcanist in periodic-updates job. r=releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D283288\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/Dockerfile", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/periodic_file_updates.sh", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/setup.sh"], "git_node": "6f7068b2be2f76eb99a652da957f31e3f024b744", "git_parents": ["0653ae5f15f53af08612b5dd12e641514dd27772"], "node": "56a0cee4e351e9b18532cb9c2c6697af51e9c300", "parents": ["f017cde0c84417e96a6a94a989d2e2e891a916f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071176 - Only capitalize a bug reference where a sentence or a commit subject starts. r=padenot,ai4dev-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325249\n", "files": ["AGENTS.md"], "git_node": "4d90f4a73603e33e3ec56827c6d2a487fd375a62", "git_parents": ["6f7068b2be2f76eb99a652da957f31e3f024b744"], "node": "747fcbf2d98520a8150cae1a78ac63f032330cb0", "parents": ["56a0cee4e351e9b18532cb9c2c6697af51e9c300"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071163 - Give the branding wordmarks a dark-mode fill fallback. r=sylvestre\n\nThe added rule only declares color-scheme, which is what makes light-dark() resolve; nothing competes with the context-fill in the presentation attribute, so the chrome consumers that supply one are unaffected. The fallback is what a web embed paints, since context paint is restricted to chrome://, resource:// and a short allowlist.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325246\n", "files": ["browser/branding/aurora/content/firefox-wordmark.svg", "browser/branding/nightly/content/firefox-wordmark.svg", "browser/branding/official/content/firefox-wordmark.svg", "browser/branding/unofficial/content/firefox-wordmark.svg"], "git_node": "0ab1a9f0dcd690ebbbdd10e0eb82e294003e8aad", "git_parents": ["4d90f4a73603e33e3ec56827c6d2a487fd375a62"], "node": "f7272db47dbc595c6c8eb177974fcd435965c7bc", "parents": ["747fcbf2d98520a8150cae1a78ac63f032330cb0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071163 - Derive a dark color scheme for firefox-source-docs. r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nsphinx-rtd-theme has no dark mode and no custom properties to re-point, so the override is derived from the theme's own stylesheets at build time rather than checked in.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325247\n", "files": ["docs/_addons/dark_mode.py", "docs/conf.py"], "git_node": "63ce0ef60c58e6e03cbde9dc40048b5f3e415ebc", "git_parents": ["0ab1a9f0dcd690ebbbdd10e0eb82e294003e8aad"], "node": "ad8a35458ea44d933c90d19a2bf947b6849f190e", "parents": ["f7272db47dbc595c6c8eb177974fcd435965c7bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071163 - Let mermaid diagrams follow the page color scheme. r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nBug 2070774 pinned both mermaid themes to the light one because the page could not follow. A classDef or style that hardcodes a fill keeps that color in either scheme, so those nodes need an explicit color too, or the dark theme's label color lands on a light fill at 1.4:1.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325248\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/lazy-browsers.md", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/tab-events.md", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/ranking.md", "docs/bug-mgmt/guides/bug-pipeline.md", "docs/conf.py", "tools/moztreedocs/docs/mermaid-integration.md"], "git_node": "1074aebedd1ca81883c4ca061640e55f1bcff1c7", "git_parents": ["63ce0ef60c58e6e03cbde9dc40048b5f3e415ebc"], "node": "9bf5714c3f85d1f3ed68f3e9bba46305ade75e95", "parents": ["ad8a35458ea44d933c90d19a2bf947b6849f190e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - license: don't document files that don't ship r=sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325178\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/license.html"], "git_node": "3f60675a4e9bfa538802df4b904fcadf4a520bf1", "git_parents": ["1074aebedd1ca81883c4ca061640e55f1bcff1c7"], "node": "cd78ecd33ab5c8e9e0f52b6c1af6dff291fb1f6d", "parents": ["9bf5714c3f85d1f3ed68f3e9bba46305ade75e95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071213 - Unmap the keymap on the xkb_context failure path in KeymapWrapper::HandleKeymap (Coverity CID 1695158) r=stransky,gtk-reviewers\n\nThe mmap of the compositor-provided keymap succeeds before xkb_context_new is\ncalled. The failure path closed the fd but returned without munmap, leaking the\nmapping every time xkb_context_new fails in a handler the compositor can call\nrepeatedly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325330\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "05357d46ccf57202d7aa8fc631ace6884f2cbce6", "git_parents": ["3f60675a4e9bfa538802df4b904fcadf4a520bf1"], "node": "26ceee2288320d257cf245d06bd0b349edb0d8e0", "parents": ["cd78ecd33ab5c8e9e0f52b6c1af6dff291fb1f6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062203 - Guard null worker private in FetchStreamReader::ReportErrorToConsole (Coverity CID 1416404) r=dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317481\n", "files": ["dom/fetch/FetchStreamReader.cpp"], "git_node": "337ccdaedbb6c02eeb3eff88694507a7181bdaad", "git_parents": ["05357d46ccf57202d7aa8fc631ace6884f2cbce6"], "node": "4e23c655f4546448d0b9c27b48944cd04a1fed00", "parents": ["26ceee2288320d257cf245d06bd0b349edb0d8e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070908 - Activate the application when asked to raise a window on macOS, r=mac-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,bradwerth,jdescottes.\n\nRaise::Yes did nothing while Firefox was not the active application, where GTK\nactivates through gtk_window_present_with_time. Only nsFocusManager::RaiseWindow\nreaches this on macOS, after BrowsingContext::CanFocusCheck grants the raise,\nand mozilla.widget.raise-on-setfocus is a kill switch. The mac arms un-skipped\nhere are the browser-chrome harness waiting forever for a focus event once the\nBrowser Toolbox has taken activation: Bug 1937229, Bug 1937315, Bug 1767721,\nBug 1781499.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325018\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_af.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/integration/browser.toml", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm"], "git_node": "66f7f4704be73edc9efa3d58bdfd500aa814fc22", "git_parents": ["337ccdaedbb6c02eeb3eff88694507a7181bdaad"], "node": "8320591aecd117b8c4d62e5aaec20cd0dde266d7", "parents": ["4e23c655f4546448d0b9c27b48944cd04a1fed00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eemeli Aro \u003ceemeli@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064983 - Remove Glean metrics for urlfixup.suffix. r=aryx,urlbar-reviewers,daleharvey\n\nThe metrics show that URL fixup is actively used via\neach of the `fixup`, `urlbar`, and `smartbar` call sites,\na bit under 1 million times a day.\nThe vast majority (over 99%) use the default `.com` suffix,\nbut the localized regional variants `.cz`, `.sk`, `.dk`, and `.no`\nare also each used at least 1000 times a day.\n\nThis reverts commit e79790d0b7e2bbade46be27e62471eb1b2dbfc16.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324959\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_canonizeURL.js", "docshell/base/URIFixup.sys.mjs", "docshell/base/metrics.yaml", "docshell/test/unit/test_URIFixup_forced.js", "docshell/test/unit/test_URIFixup_info.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.glean.d.ts"], "git_node": "662ff4754442f476019bf33261e53fcded28c425", "git_parents": ["66f7f4704be73edc9efa3d58bdfd500aa814fc22"], "node": "f69541a0967d40439d9608b89a26717295681111", "parents": ["8320591aecd117b8c4d62e5aaec20cd0dde266d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068585 - Get rid of collections.OrderedDict r=ipc-reviewers,mccr8\n\ndict is ordered since 3.6\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322958\n", "files": ["ipc/ipdl/ipdl/lower.py"], "git_node": "aa399322c60014043eede71b95104eb53a169dfb", "git_parents": ["662ff4754442f476019bf33261e53fcded28c425"], "node": "f0fb67bf978cf2c72b11617e694cc7814ffa5e77", "parents": ["f69541a0967d40439d9608b89a26717295681111"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068585 - Get rid of collections.OrderedDict r=whimboo\n\ndict is ordered since 3.6\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322959\n", "files": ["remote/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "f63822ff432493b9f4486e9331728eddc17ec08e", "git_parents": ["aa399322c60014043eede71b95104eb53a169dfb"], "node": "d26961dd4b1ccaca76c8795b423a24b02ac2b7b3", "parents": ["f0fb67bf978cf2c72b11617e694cc7814ffa5e77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068585 - Get rid of collections.OrderedDict r=mozperftest-reviewers,aglavic\n\ndict is ordered since 3.6\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322960\n", "files": ["python/mozperftest/mozperftest/metrics/notebook/perftestetl.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/test/browsertime/runner.py"], "git_node": "59dd421fef7ff13c50b040cd93ea889e271c4413", "git_parents": ["f63822ff432493b9f4486e9331728eddc17ec08e"], "node": "c9f1cb4f4e25d14d3695bd3534cb15ece93443db", "parents": ["d26961dd4b1ccaca76c8795b423a24b02ac2b7b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070806 [Linux] Init mMappedRegionData and move class members init to header r=emilio,gtk-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324882\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.h"], "git_node": "e986c9e88a0d51aa38dbc82ce771c03685bd3d9b", "git_parents": ["59dd421fef7ff13c50b040cd93ea889e271c4413"], "node": "ac65faaf0a2acaec7e0c81205420e93eb4958637", "parents": ["c9f1cb4f4e25d14d3695bd3534cb15ece93443db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068800 - Stop presenting network resets on https as SSL errors r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug,valentin\n\nNS_ERROR_NET_RESET and NS_ERROR_NET_INTERRUPT on an https URI are not evidence\nof TLS version intolerance: the heuristic applies only during the handshake,\ninsecure fallback was disabled in bug 1479501, and genuine TLS failures reach\nnssFailure2 by their own path.\n\nGive netReset and NS_ERROR_NET_EMPTY_RESPONSE distinct error-page configs, and\ntest the empty-response case with an actual empty response.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323597\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/about/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutNetError_emptyResponse.js", "browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutNetError_netReset.js", "browser/base/content/test/siteIdentity/browser_navigation_failures.js", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/test/browser/browser.toml", "docshell/test/browser/browser_displayLoadError_netReset.js", "toolkit/content/errors/net-errors.mjs", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/neterror/netError.ftl"], "git_node": "a82f8263961ed01627d406cc676665309471b24a", "git_parents": ["e986c9e88a0d51aa38dbc82ce771c03685bd3d9b"], "node": "5ad18f0b0aad6c7bb1d69747f25560ee1e3112c1", "parents": ["ac65faaf0a2acaec7e0c81205420e93eb4958637"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070126 - Make about:logging capture the threads required by a preset passed by URL r=padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324250\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/aboutLogging/aboutLogging.mjs", "toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_about_logging.js"], "git_node": "7287c0a261fdc2113e79ab639841e1e47d7e95b5", "git_parents": ["a82f8263961ed01627d406cc676665309471b24a"], "node": "1faf6ad99175c5f08905d6ae6d16fe119c14afd0", "parents": ["5ad18f0b0aad6c7bb1d69747f25560ee1e3112c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069391 - Make main thread atom caches work for the UTF-8 path as well. r=smaug\n\nClaude wrote the tests but they look sensible to me (basically a copy of\nthe utf-16 string).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323649\n", "files": ["layout/style/GeckoBindings.cpp", "xpcom/ds/nsAtom.h", "xpcom/ds/nsAtomTable.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestAtoms.cpp"], "git_node": "744fd55cbfb8745b0cade008e7c7e67a90b54e41", "git_parents": ["7287c0a261fdc2113e79ab639841e1e47d7e95b5"], "node": "78d999f3bddd4b1c990f6b0f2824bd266abba348", "parents": ["1faf6ad99175c5f08905d6ae6d16fe119c14afd0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789143741, "git_changesets": ["d7cb04ea8f35d1de5416f362d04f1f1785507e99", "b2bfc797299929ea9190e9c02561887dc5ff47f0", "3fa9e2861b471e0f65374d3930b904bee9d228ff", "b147363df6d9f7129a82fa3c99c91f9b11eec415", "a89b3dda914c465fdf71692816c56f6a5d4f8114", "d30e4ee05ee555a3353365479db5dd31e3219a73", "700a8304455e663679d83b703194bfac3f85e604", "5b744297960052799525874b6f21b8643d39be98", "df6bb4f2c80e52f4d68dd3433eb4c71d7aeee6cb", "55bee541e7dd24092f761ca21f3ba11e4db82613", "ba3c806e8da60c676926d476dc4bc758dc9e6114", "dae4ee5b8026f70b36a3747e3f9cb5ea6d3aa547", "1ccbebd6adafe46ecd530cd8169d1b4e50ca691f", "82b54c3f40ddd0c5661fd75c82e905f4a6bf39b6", "edcf975216e1dbd66b3ab8a0ea8730a314d82426", "78cb174eb3d24671df0e6bddcf9434908a8eba18", "1f929f12427cf61eaa85d16313d201b8215cb038", "4886ee24f53fc720052479988e8da8bf222495a7", "06db999ddd8b56a360518bc13fdff66f59267458", "1eed015ea320634a3500fd65a9b126f2c078c791", "c7588ee9e1a86e3642fe76199a755b8c64a28842", "535a0dee531d3e40fa157a39ae169cfdced8472d", "e7d24be42b01dea04bde4accfff0867ab03a9284", "048573cab61b83b305a1486acfcead14f0cfc0df", "0abaeaf6404961a5e8e834cbe793e80e8ebfa10c", "0cef53fdf12961283bc02e890c79a0878e7192d1", "8ba72e18a7b55fd3c5db87eb102597da85194ca9", "8987e9a119c54218c156b006f20b1222eac281bd", "0e7fcd812fddf07590db039ae863565c6e701667", "5b5dced46d8fb0426da11dd389d85766e36cf9c8", "bbac0edf66f3814a8488fbae33f8f0cc3340a7fc", "8e9079528d4f517df6761c303caafae59255d7e4", "0bf3dd619716c9bc6a4feb0c0b2627a19a9ed10d", "a166bc2c6922df2721d404813befe9443d38d578", "4ce0e4ecddb209c4b203d3e8b35194a1b13959ff", "265666bcba5e23d012325160d0119fc63f39e533", "6e3d0df73f15b018ccf1a455e8d094b3cec356ea", "a993bf5ca9f5056dab73019bd03e9e28157a53c4", "bc3360c732ba4ae98719e6081f44c339214ddd9a", "2fafa1ee1d71a795353a9b7b6c8bf9b6691a0184", "0f1d79018230ce4162c9a259f4dbf3a9c9f7b3a4", "0653ae5f15f53af08612b5dd12e641514dd27772", "6f7068b2be2f76eb99a652da957f31e3f024b744", "4d90f4a73603e33e3ec56827c6d2a487fd375a62", "0ab1a9f0dcd690ebbbdd10e0eb82e294003e8aad", "63ce0ef60c58e6e03cbde9dc40048b5f3e415ebc", "1074aebedd1ca81883c4ca061640e55f1bcff1c7", "3f60675a4e9bfa538802df4b904fcadf4a520bf1", "05357d46ccf57202d7aa8fc631ace6884f2cbce6", "337ccdaedbb6c02eeb3eff88694507a7181bdaad", "66f7f4704be73edc9efa3d58bdfd500aa814fc22", "662ff4754442f476019bf33261e53fcded28c425", "aa399322c60014043eede71b95104eb53a169dfb", "f63822ff432493b9f4486e9331728eddc17ec08e", "59dd421fef7ff13c50b040cd93ea889e271c4413", "e986c9e88a0d51aa38dbc82ce771c03685bd3d9b", "a82f8263961ed01627d406cc676665309471b24a", "7287c0a261fdc2113e79ab639841e1e47d7e95b5", "744fd55cbfb8745b0cade008e7c7e67a90b54e41"], "user": "asilaghi@mozilla.com"}, "45310": {"changesets": [{"author": "Adham-A \u003c57870101+Adham-A@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1985986 - Fix RTL glyph ink overflow measurement for contained glyphs. r=layout-reviewers,jfkthame\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324373\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFont.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/rtl-glyph-extents-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/rtl-glyph-extents.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/support/fonts/generate-rtl-ink-overflow.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/support/fonts/rtl-ink-overflow.ttf", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/support/rtl-glyph-extents.css"], "git_node": "adde773bf47e81e86fea6db4ce83ea05ef1489b0", "git_parents": ["744fd55cbfb8745b0cade008e7c7e67a90b54e41"], "node": "4e3ccb2e438249fe2e9a27908752cf57ff10cf01", "parents": ["78d999f3bddd4b1c990f6b0f2824bd266abba348"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070796 - Don't use the scratch double register in convertUInt32ToDouble on x86. r=iain\n\nThis is building on bug 2057638 part 1.\n\nInstead of materializing `0x1p52` in `ScratchDoubleReg`, we can OR/subtract it\nusing the constant pool. This gives us a single implementation of `convertUInt32ToDouble`\non x86. The overload taking a `ScratchDoubleScope` (and clobbering the input) existed\nonly for `MacroAssembler::boxUint32` after bug 2057638.\n\nAssembly before, when a scratch register was available (version added in bug 2057638 part 1):\n```\n  vmovq     \u003cpool\u003e, %xmm7        8 bytes\n  vmovd     %ecx, %xmm1          4\n  por       %xmm7, %xmm1         4\n  subsd     %xmm7, %xmm1         4\n```\n\nAssembly before, when no scratch register was available (only `boxUint32` after bug 2057638):\n```\n  subl      $-2147483648, %edx   6 bytes\n  xorpd     %xmm7, %xmm7         4\n  cvtsi2sd  %edx, %xmm7          4\n  addsd     \u003cpool\u003e, %xmm7        8\n```\n\nAssembly after, used in all cases:\n```\n  vmovd     %ecx, %xmm1          4 bytes\n  por       \u003cpool\u003e, %xmm1        8\n  subpd     \u003cpool\u003e, %xmm1        8\n```\n\nThe `Uint32Array`-to-double path is 3-4% faster on a micro-benchmark. The two\nBaseline paths that call `boxUint32` are ~2% faster. Wasm `f64.convert_i32_u` and\natomics on a `Uint32Array` are neutral. Wasm `f32.convert_i32_u` is ~0.5% slower.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324864\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/x86/MacroAssembler-x86-inl.h", "js/src/jit/x86/MacroAssembler-x86.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86/MacroAssembler-x86.h"], "git_node": "e8c5f7d307369ffdb441eb13fea33ea9b4b16268", "git_parents": ["adde773bf47e81e86fea6db4ce83ea05ef1489b0"], "node": "f2de26c1103b4723f729b657a96fcf1c3a84fe95", "parents": ["4e3ccb2e438249fe2e9a27908752cf57ff10cf01"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045957 - Add test. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nSee also bug 2045958. The generator-return implementation is very different now\nafter bug 2063576 but still good to have a test case for this.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325056\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/explicit-resource-management/bug2045957.js"], "git_node": "21d827cca7e037bf6e235ae26e7cd06385afe14f", "git_parents": ["e8c5f7d307369ffdb441eb13fea33ea9b4b16268"], "node": "4dedc95e4c499e10dc291ce9d1c4fd3143d78ed5", "parents": ["f2de26c1103b4723f729b657a96fcf1c3a84fe95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070923 - Render the toolbox toolbar before Toolbox.open() resolves, r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes.\n\nToolboxController renders no tab and no command button until its canRender state\nis set, and open() only schedules that from an idle callback, which can be\nstarved past the end of open(). The tracer tests then hand a null\ncommand-button-jstracer to synthesizeMouseAtCenter.\n\nBug 1399548 added the gate to stop the component rendering before the toolbar\nbuttons were built, when #buildButtons() was asynchronous; it is synchronous now,\nso no intermediate render is left to prevent. Awaiting the idle callback instead\nwould leave open() pending once its window is gone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325033\n", "files": ["devtools/client/framework/components/ToolboxController.js", "devtools/client/framework/toolbox.js"], "git_node": "6abfa5161bb2cd217883ff9d4ca979acd360a254", "git_parents": ["21d827cca7e037bf6e235ae26e7cd06385afe14f"], "node": "fb271811d4e799d10b766a5fd91df85364bf0016", "parents": ["4dedc95e4c499e10dc291ce9d1c4fd3143d78ed5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cfqueze@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070924 - Do not skip remote worker debugger registration on an early wake-up, r=edenchuang,dom-worker-reviewers.\n\nEnableRemoteDebugger waited for the worker thread to bind its\nPRemoteWorkerDebugger child endpoint with a bare if rather than a while\n(Bug 1899503), so an early wake returned without registering, leaving the\nworker invisible to nsIWorkerDebuggerManager and DevTools with no target actor\nfor it.\n\nLooping on mRemoteDebugger alone would hang when the worker thread never binds\nat all, the case the bare if was written for, so the predicate is a separate\nflag, cleared whenever a new endpoint pair is armed: a worker frozen into the\nbfcache unregisters its debugger and binds again on thaw.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325035\n", "files": ["dom/workers/WorkerPrivate.cpp", "dom/workers/WorkerPrivate.h"], "git_node": "4ccc3b2b3b09552873a004296a70b50c629f5d3d", "git_parents": ["6abfa5161bb2cd217883ff9d4ca979acd360a254"], "node": "b8b717bcd592e427053500668731c11221187860", "parents": ["fb271811d4e799d10b766a5fd91df85364bf0016"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cfqueze@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070925 - Make setDebuggerReady(false) suspend the debuggee again, r=edenchuang,dom-worker-reviewers.\n\nThe hold suspended nothing: !mDebuggerReady && !mRemoteDebuggerReady can never\nboth be true, since the two flags are cleared on mutually exclusive\nUseRemoteDebugger() branches. So no debuggee runnable has been queued since\nBug 1899503.\n\nRestoring the hold means the three flush sites drop the mDebuggerRegistered term,\nwhich a remote worker never sets, and which RegisterDebuggerMainThread has\nnormally already set for a local one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325036\n", "files": ["dom/workers/WorkerPrivate.cpp", "dom/workers/WorkerPrivate.h"], "git_node": "52f64e7e39f8ba7734ffae0f3a73dfb896cc6737", "git_parents": ["4ccc3b2b3b09552873a004296a70b50c629f5d3d"], "node": "abae7abb41eaee6bcb9ee4a7e3b7b0c8f270c46c", "parents": ["b8b717bcd592e427053500668731c11221187860"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2001947 - Let each IME composition finish in the content process, r=jdescottes,devtools-reviewers.\n\nPausing focuses the toolbox frame, which blurs the content browser and makes the\nparent process commit the composition in progress while the content process is\nstopped in the debugger and cannot finish it. Starting the next composition on\ntop of that leaves the two processes disagreeing, and the parent can then assert\nin ContentCacheInParent::OnCompositionEvent.\n\nCommitting explicitly is not open to the test: once it resumes,\nnsITextInputProcessor.commitComposition already fails with NS_ERROR_FAILURE, so\nit can only avoid Bug 2070926.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325039\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-event-breakpoints.js"], "git_node": "678b7bcf9a21951b2ce9f3aa034cb174c1a04119", "git_parents": ["52f64e7e39f8ba7734ffae0f3a73dfb896cc6737"], "node": "72eac03b1b607ea4b6025118d7d2427564fefe57", "parents": ["abae7abb41eaee6bcb9ee4a7e3b7b0c8f270c46c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cfqueze@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070933 - Give the sectioned-source-map test its own page, r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe.\n\nOnly browser_dbg-breakpoints-sourcemap-with-sections.js needs xbundle.js's\nuncleared throwing setInterval; the nine other tests that load\ndoc-sourcemaps.html inherit it. Its output keeps lastOutputTime fresh, so\nbrowser-test.js reads a hung test as merely slow and grants it every\nMAX_UNEXPECTED_TIMEOUTS extension instead of failing it after one window.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325041\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-breakpoints-sourcemap-with-sections.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/examples/doc-sourcemaps-with-sections.html", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/examples/doc-sourcemaps.html"], "git_node": "f002e44b0066a891754906cf5c23f75bf63a441f", "git_parents": ["678b7bcf9a21951b2ce9f3aa034cb174c1a04119"], "node": "7013be0e11f3e73f10168bd765d6ad74ce26de31", "parents": ["72eac03b1b607ea4b6025118d7d2427564fefe57"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1932082 - [devtools] Wait for the syntax tree before asserting shift+tab focus, r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy.\n\nbrowser_dbg-keyboard-navigation.js pressed shift+tab as soon as .cm-content\nexisted. CodeMirror only renders a fold button for a line its syntax tree says\nis foldable, and that parse is incremental, so on a slow run focus went to the\nsource header's end pane toggle instead - what the test expected when\nCodeMirror 5 had no fold gutter (Bug 1924829).\n\nThe expected side of that assertion was already a constant: the fold gutter\nalways contains a visibility: hidden spacer button, so the lookup matched\nwhether or not any button was focusable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325043\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-keyboard-navigation.js"], "git_node": "7982471ee8689e4820848c881dac5a6fa2fc0ae9", "git_parents": ["f002e44b0066a891754906cf5c23f75bf63a441f"], "node": "39dbdb13c6eb3733deea68eeca2277a8b2347c09", "parents": ["7013be0e11f3e73f10168bd765d6ad74ce26de31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1767707 - Flush the pref file synchronously before launching the background task, r=jdescottes,devtools-reviewers.\n\ndevtools.browsertoolbox.enable-test-server reaches the browser toolbox only\nthrough #initProfile copying this profile's prefs.js, so it took effect only\nwhen the write happened to win the race against the task's startup. Without it\ninstallTestingServer() is never called and initBrowserToolboxTask's connect\nloop spins until the test times out.\n\npreferences.allow.omt-write cannot serve here: Preferences.cpp caches it on\nfirst use, so flipping it in a test is a no-op.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325045\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_af.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-backgroundtask-debugging.js"], "git_node": "1a3bcfb869ceac47fd960e53053cf825a1b56672", "git_parents": ["7982471ee8689e4820848c881dac5a6fa2fc0ae9"], "node": "502d0990429d2ba4630e163b7b06c0a933f30d1a", "parents": ["39dbdb13c6eb3733deea68eeca2277a8b2347c09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Janika \u003cjneuberger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070529 - Update enteprise compatibility for AppUpdateURL, Bookmarks, DisablePrivateBrowsing r=bsmth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325324\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json"], "git_node": "2f745fb803bc8fd7e70da495ffab127ae8355485", "git_parents": ["1a3bcfb869ceac47fd960e53053cf825a1b56672"], "node": "f6f8c0d4ee7f4fba6e52509603ccee288667fb7e", "parents": ["502d0990429d2ba4630e163b7b06c0a933f30d1a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070739 [Linux][Vulkan Video] Size DMA-BUF copy queues from lavu's created count. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nInitCtx used the ICD hardware queueCount, which can exceed the queues actually passed to vkCreateDevice (limit_queues, NVIDIA caps). vkGetDeviceQueue2 then fails and Cleanup waits on uninitialized fences.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324797\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.h"], "git_node": "b2c8bedfdf07139f1e460eb0de68814b6c08d2ca", "git_parents": ["2f745fb803bc8fd7e70da495ffab127ae8355485"], "node": "f583b0fbb7cdc5ddf78318724cdc5c0f372b2dc9", "parents": ["f6f8c0d4ee7f4fba6e52509603ccee288667fb7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071285 - Add Promise::MaybeSafeResolve and use it for Streams r=mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324569\n", "files": ["dom/promise/Promise.cpp", "dom/promise/Promise.h", "dom/promise/tests/test_promise_safe_resolve.html", "dom/streams/ReadableByteStreamController.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStream.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStreamBYOBReader.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStreamDefaultController.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStreamDefaultReader.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStreamTee.cpp", "dom/streams/TransformStream.cpp", "dom/streams/WritableStreamDefaultController.cpp", "js/public/Promise.h", "js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp", "js/src/builtin/Promise.h", "js/src/jsapi.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/api/response/response-body-read-task-handling.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/streams/readable-byte-streams/patched-global.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "b8df7498e43bb4075feba31aae51250d021b7b8f", "git_parents": ["b2c8bedfdf07139f1e460eb0de68814b6c08d2ca"], "node": "b5ac1b5a6e8f6a9a588d6fd8955522174314ad2f", "parents": ["f583b0fbb7cdc5ddf78318724cdc5c0f372b2dc9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071089: Skip null elements when tracing Wasm GC ref-array payloads. r=bvisness\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325177\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmGcObject.cpp"], "git_node": "28c4ba65eef83ebfba994e7b0cffab3dcd00b2a0", "git_parents": ["b8df7498e43bb4075feba31aae51250d021b7b8f"], "node": "2d37695208b1add4b02cadbc72c0a238ab18fda8", "parents": ["b5ac1b5a6e8f6a9a588d6fd8955522174314ad2f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059617 [Wayland] Rename session ID to workspace ID r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324870\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.h"], "git_node": "90b9841a0a202cacdf17bce3b89f90e8a6f395b8", "git_parents": ["28c4ba65eef83ebfba994e7b0cffab3dcd00b2a0"], "node": "bc25b13eff3cf193aef8fe139dbc120e876f43c2", "parents": ["2d37695208b1add4b02cadbc72c0a238ab18fda8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059617 [Wayland] Convert integer workspace id to uuid r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nInteger workspace ID causes conflicts on session restore so use uuid everywhere and ignore integer ones to avoid protocol errors.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324871\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.h"], "git_node": "1dd3ee55286f2d6b07aef83f32aaa5d25df91447", "git_parents": ["90b9841a0a202cacdf17bce3b89f90e8a6f395b8"], "node": "a208c3cdbe858dd9ba5d8ab29379f31e9228244d", "parents": ["bc25b13eff3cf193aef8fe139dbc120e876f43c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059617: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp"], "git_node": "06e2cfc0604fcf6305948158510b632e2ade72e6", "git_parents": ["1dd3ee55286f2d6b07aef83f32aaa5d25df91447"], "node": "5211632b77cfff53a337ebbca66bcd262f7a7673", "parents": ["a208c3cdbe858dd9ba5d8ab29379f31e9228244d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070028 - Fix confirm/alert dialogs not shown when triggered from a webextensions popup and sidebar panels. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,kcochrane,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324922\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-action.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_browserAction_popup_confirm_dialog.js", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css"], "git_node": "f3f505a9a46b4af1ce18aab55424f0d5ea9b6170", "git_parents": ["06e2cfc0604fcf6305948158510b632e2ade72e6"], "node": "7e1ee6f94fa607ee551940742acc1854ebd05ec0", "parents": ["5211632b77cfff53a337ebbca66bcd262f7a7673"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070815 [Wayland] Disable session restore on Gnome due to Bug 2064100 r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324876\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsAppShell.cpp"], "git_node": "16ec491ea9caae64dd3488fbc37c26d2973fbe76", "git_parents": ["f3f505a9a46b4af1ce18aab55424f0d5ea9b6170"], "node": "62c7c23192dd6886b7aa16ad1ce96ee24ed6bc3a", "parents": ["7e1ee6f94fa607ee551940742acc1854ebd05ec0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070816 [Wayland] Enable session restore on release r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324877\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "8c7bfdabd0c297ddcf9a28fad1fe4454b2b2f882", "git_parents": ["16ec491ea9caae64dd3488fbc37c26d2973fbe76"], "node": "f20ceff78ceeab111bd94963e29f936857156cc8", "parents": ["62c7c23192dd6886b7aa16ad1ce96ee24ed6bc3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068160 - Part 14 - Retire VisPixel in favour of RasterPixel. r=gw\n\nVisibility space is now always a surface's raster space, so the transitional\nVisPixel unit and the parallel \"visibility spatial node\" naming no longer\ndescribe anything distinct. VisPixel, VisRect and LayoutToVisTransform become the\nexisting RasterPixel, RasterRect and LayoutToRasterTransform, which already carry\nexactly this meaning in the quad code: the raster node's local space, unscaled,\nwith RasterPixel * device_pixel_scale = DevicePixel.\n\nSurfaceInfo::visibility_spatial_node_index was a copy of\nraster_spatial_node_index, so it goes, along with the visibility_node() function\nthat had become an identity. DirtyRegion's field and doc comment, and the\nremaining locals and parameters, are renamed to match.\n\nPure rename plus field removal; no behaviour change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322981\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/profiler.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/units.rs"], "git_node": "1745b6748da8b8ccae8393440d66c9615b72a85b", "git_parents": ["8c7bfdabd0c297ddcf9a28fad1fe4454b2b2f882"], "node": "f9de350ec09f1ff247c0b70e3ca20029c0899ba9", "parents": ["f20ceff78ceeab111bd94963e29f936857156cc8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062329 - Add use counters for the SpeechRecognition API. r=dom-core-reviewers,webidl,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319563\n", "files": ["dom/base/UseCounters.conf", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "dom/webidl/SpeechRecognition.webidl"], "git_node": "84ede0b820c0145e9c5fc9c99ce120e5ff625ffa", "git_parents": ["1745b6748da8b8ccae8393440d66c9615b72a85b"], "node": "b0e2d35261994e5fbf83c4ad7420382009cf309b", "parents": ["f9de350ec09f1ff247c0b70e3ca20029c0899ba9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062329 - Record speech recognition usage, outcomes and errors with Glean. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu,TravisLong\n\nsession_ended is recorded from Reset(), the one path every teardown goes\nthrough. No transcript text or audio is recorded.\n\nA session_id on both events pairs them, so a start and its outcome can be\njoined instead of subtracted as two populations across a day boundary.\n\nsession_started also reports the model and locale the session negotiated to,\nnot just the tag the page asked for: en, en-US and en-us all run the same\nmodel, and only the negotiated locale can be grouped on.\n\ninit_failure records the start failures whose cause content knows, because\nthe error codes the spec makes us fire are coarser: service-not-allowed alone\ncovers four distinct causes. The unsupported-language one is rejected before\n[[started]], so it records no session events at all and would otherwise be\ninvisible; it is also exactly why error and session_ended do not add up.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319564\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/metrics.yaml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_telemetry.js", "toolkit/components/glean/metrics_index.py"], "git_node": "39db08efe30cc8bcaac479f1c73975d78d3c39e7", "git_parents": ["84ede0b820c0145e9c5fc9c99ce120e5ff625ffa"], "node": "a2b9f81f8b1b870c382eb84f710afdf642c7f03d", "parents": ["b0e2d35261994e5fbf83c4ad7420382009cf309b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062329 - Measure speech recognition latency in the content process. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nTwo timing distributions are recorded content-side:\n\n- session_init_time measures the page-visible wait between start() and the\n  model becoming ready for recognition. It only has a sample when init\n  succeeded, so its description says to read it against init_failure: a\n  regression turning slow inits into failures would otherwise look like an\n  improvement.\n- result_latency records one sample per session: the mean capture-to-JS\n  latency of its results, using the capture timestamps already plumbed end to\n  end by AudioCaptureTiming.h.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319565\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/metrics.yaml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_telemetry.js", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_parakeet_e2e.html"], "git_node": "189550601ac9731dd888abdb513584a543755cc9", "git_parents": ["39db08efe30cc8bcaac479f1c73975d78d3c39e7"], "node": "c5006d2e9e0b6b3687878b9e272d789c37fbc6ac", "parents": ["a2b9f81f8b1b870c382eb84f710afdf642c7f03d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062329 - Measure inference cost and init failures in the HWInference process. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nRecorded in the utility process, where inference happens:\n\n- model_load_time measures reading the GGUF into memory. Like\n  session_init_time it only has a sample on success, which its description\n  now says.\n- inference_realtime_factor records one per-session mean of per-chunk\n  throughput as audio duration divided by compute time, times 100 (400 means\n  4x faster than real time). Recognition happens continuously on chunks of\n  similar size, so getting the average is meaningful here. The range reaches\n  100x rather than 20x, because hardware that runs this model comfortably\n  sits above 20x and would otherwise land entirely in the top bucket; the\n  bounds also put a bucket boundary exactly at 100, so falling behind real\n  time is a clean cut.\n- init_failure gains the inference-process labels, one per step that can\n  fail, so a spike says where init broke rather than only that it did. The\n  previous model_load_failed covered six unrelated steps, two of which were\n  not model loads at all, and other covered four.\n\nThe tests verify that starting without an installed model reaches the\ncorresponding failure label and run real recognition end-to-end. They check\nthat the timing metrics have one session-level sample and log values rather\nthan asserting timings, since those depend on the machine.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319566\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/metrics.yaml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionParent.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_inference_telemetry.js", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "7783c6fb9ede108cb441318523ec67230fb499f1", "git_parents": ["189550601ac9731dd888abdb513584a543755cc9"], "node": "2312e32d921a6192a1181fa783cbc5027dedec57", "parents": ["c5006d2e9e0b6b3687878b9e272d789c37fbc6ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062329 - Attribute MLModelHubService downloads to the requesting task. r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\n\nMLModelHubService used the constant \"ml-model-hub-service\" as the feature ID for every native caller, so the existing firefox_ai_runtime.model_download events could not be selected by feature.\n\nPass the caller-provided task name as featureId, matching getModelBlob(). The browser test downloads through nsIMLModelHub and checks that every lifecycle event is attributed to speech-recognition.\n\nRemove an attribute that was wrongly added and causes this to fail.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322658\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ml/MLModelHubService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "62a4a5d638f3fd31af6fe9e06a8b49676d98c1b9", "git_parents": ["7783c6fb9ede108cb441318523ec67230fb499f1"], "node": "a4f920859c24ddb51f1569c3deea292b21a06d99", "parents": ["2312e32d921a6192a1181fa783cbc5027dedec57"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abel Kalu \u003c59095867+BlessedOneKobo@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059979 - Fix network monitor opening files in last tab. r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325233\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/src/utils/firefox/open-request-in-tab.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_open_request_in_tab.js"], "git_node": "3327bb6f5cceb916ecc50983f175432c90812c06", "git_parents": ["62a4a5d638f3fd31af6fe9e06a8b49676d98c1b9"], "node": "729af2dd9d4afc915b5a2083a2cdfecd73ddf5a7", "parents": ["a4f920859c24ddb51f1569c3deea292b21a06d99"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2071285 - Add Promise::MaybeSafeResolve and use it for Streams r=mgaudet\" for causing build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit b8df7498e43bb4075feba31aae51250d021b7b8f.\n", "files": ["dom/promise/Promise.cpp", "dom/promise/Promise.h", "dom/promise/tests/test_promise_safe_resolve.html", "dom/streams/ReadableByteStreamController.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStream.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStreamBYOBReader.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStreamDefaultController.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStreamDefaultReader.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStreamTee.cpp", "dom/streams/TransformStream.cpp", "dom/streams/WritableStreamDefaultController.cpp", "js/public/Promise.h", "js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp", "js/src/builtin/Promise.h", "js/src/jsapi.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/api/response/response-body-read-task-handling.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/streams/readable-byte-streams/patched-global.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "175bf52313f7e7f6790a890a46beceb01c7a544d", "git_parents": ["3327bb6f5cceb916ecc50983f175432c90812c06"], "node": "2d61cb0bb27b78ef7ea6cecf64bd2737844f2fe1", "parents": ["729af2dd9d4afc915b5a2083a2cdfecd73ddf5a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059979 - Fix network monitor opening files in last tab. r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\" for causing lint failures\n\nThis reverts commit 3327bb6f5cceb916ecc50983f175432c90812c06.\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/src/utils/firefox/open-request-in-tab.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_open_request_in_tab.js"], "git_node": "21e13a7a944a7e87e97a36d7860786fd380e1510", "git_parents": ["175bf52313f7e7f6790a890a46beceb01c7a544d"], "node": "2189cdec42a270d2cecad800287eb7b21c2ecc8b", "parents": ["2d61cb0bb27b78ef7ea6cecf64bd2737844f2fe1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057690 - Add Wikipedia search for Sardinian. r=search-reviewers,scunnane\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318805\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/searchconfigs/test_searchconfig.js"], "git_node": "a5be3e6db7eb4137a97a5dca052d6d6c349d3101", "git_parents": ["21e13a7a944a7e87e97a36d7860786fd380e1510"], "node": "e2720bd238117e3ebc1b7c640c948226d69867b9", "parents": ["2189cdec42a270d2cecad800287eb7b21c2ecc8b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings tld-suffixes ct-logs - r=release-managers,diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325139\n", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/ai-window-prompts.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-config-icons.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-config-v2.json", "toolkit/components/certviewer/content/components/logNameTable.mjs"], "git_node": "6a72702b8ae5b23569e89a681ed535e3385ddc52", "git_parents": ["a5be3e6db7eb4137a97a5dca052d6d6c349d3101"], "node": "dde979aef320f6c5063afa33ca35ae527b25e409", "parents": ["e2720bd238117e3ebc1b7c640c948226d69867b9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070424 - Update metadata for css/css-borders/corner-shape/render-corner-shape.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325374\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/render-corner-shape.html.ini"], "git_node": "2589de2295f2b4989e67473df7abdf5f757450c8", "git_parents": ["6a72702b8ae5b23569e89a681ed535e3385ddc52"], "node": "0693de2ab93e871665f012c4c4d0192e70ff8815", "parents": ["dde979aef320f6c5063afa33ca35ae527b25e409"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070944 - [ci] Add ability to key attributes.code-review by project and level, r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324983\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/source_test.py"], "git_node": "f634efe2ebc3c46285dee63190add70adda2db55", "git_parents": ["2589de2295f2b4989e67473df7abdf5f757450c8"], "node": "2f71e2d9e4a9961e0594b1e6087be64affa522d3", "parents": ["0693de2ab93e871665f012c4c4d0192e70ff8815"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070944 - [ci] Don't schedule clang-external in non-try L1 reviewbot graphs, r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nThis task has a dependency that requires a secret, so don't schedule it\nin L1 contexts. We exempt try from this because reviewbot is already\nrestricted to trusted users there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324984\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/clang.yml"], "git_node": "b835aaa0883d5a197678bad4e21d362952987084", "git_parents": ["f634efe2ebc3c46285dee63190add70adda2db55"], "node": "1a614f2c34fa09af6050a5635e13d87e147916e9", "parents": ["2f71e2d9e4a9961e0594b1e6087be64affa522d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068624 - Remove unused environment.build fields r=TravisLong\n\n`environment.build` has the honour of being the only section of the\nEnvironment that has required fields. And some of those required fields\nmust be of specific types and/or specific patterns.\n\nThis means that \"removing\" the seven unused fields results in:\n* 2 set to \"\" to satisfy required strings\n* 2 set to \"00.\" to satisfy required strings with version patterns\n* 1 set to null as vendor is required but can be null or string\n* 2 actually removed (displayVersion and updaterAvailable)\n\nAnd it only results in one decrement of the count, for updaterAvailable,\nas the rest weren't ever mirrored in Glean inside the Environment\n(because they were either already instrumented in client_info, or they\nweren't useful data to mirror).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323061\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/environment.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/TelemetryEnvironmentTesting.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "96ff9e8d845eb6783ad4897960d86eab1c286144", "git_parents": ["b835aaa0883d5a197678bad4e21d362952987084"], "node": "773f60467832e3f0dff121af8fcdd5f412f4993b", "parents": ["1a614f2c34fa09af6050a5635e13d87e147916e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068624 - Remove unused Legacy Telemetry environment.settings pieces r=TravisLong\n\nThis does deliberately decrease the frequency of\nenvironment-change-reason \"main\" pings for when private browsing mode\nhas a separate search engine and that search engine's data changes.\nThis is not a currently-shipping configuration and search counts are\ndetermined by events not by this configuration, so we're fine.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323062\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/environment.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/TelemetryEnvironmentTesting.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_TelemetryEnvironment.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_TelemetryEnvironment_search.js"], "git_node": "a34a04ddefbf8ff25ee7f7333934b9fc47601b55", "git_parents": ["96ff9e8d845eb6783ad4897960d86eab1c286144"], "node": "bed92fadb1f6f656781dddcba385bf34af8c56f4", "parents": ["773f60467832e3f0dff121af8fcdd5f412f4993b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068624 - Remove unused Legacy Telemetry environment.services r=TravisLong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323063\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/environment.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_TelemetryEnvironment.js"], "git_node": "4486568ab6d437b4995e3399a5926b6dedfe0015", "git_parents": ["a34a04ddefbf8ff25ee7f7333934b9fc47601b55"], "node": "f0d6502a83a1906cd487ab679d26202819348042", "parents": ["bed92fadb1f6f656781dddcba385bf34af8c56f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068624 - Remove unused Legacy Telemetry environment.system fields r=TravisLong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325164\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/environment.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/TelemetryEnvironmentTesting.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "2878a668e9d42eec99033f9306b9e970c1f83d5f", "git_parents": ["4486568ab6d437b4995e3399a5926b6dedfe0015"], "node": "1985b7bdde64d34b26228824197fb0602480a1a3", "parents": ["f0d6502a83a1906cd487ab679d26202819348042"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068624 - Remove unused Legacy Telemetry environment.system.cpu fields r=TravisLong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325165\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/environment.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/TelemetryEnvironmentTesting.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f18845100acfe9fdf00f04465b2f34a1c5fbab58", "git_parents": ["2878a668e9d42eec99033f9306b9e970c1f83d5f"], "node": "0277d85bada45c15ed1fcea6318ac06038b87f3b", "parents": ["1985b7bdde64d34b26228824197fb0602480a1a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068624 - Remove unused Legacy Telemetry environment.system.os fields r=TravisLong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325166\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/environment.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/TelemetryEnvironmentTesting.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f08f25d1dea5da779075aafb9aa2355b1973096e", "git_parents": ["f18845100acfe9fdf00f04465b2f34a1c5fbab58"], "node": "eb214e188fd4d14a2d1c0831d4c0cf26637a810c", "parents": ["0277d85bada45c15ed1fcea6318ac06038b87f3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068624 - Remove unused Legacy Telemetry environment.system.hdd fields r=TravisLong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325167\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/environment.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/TelemetryEnvironmentTesting.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "aae565df3a9f1d30af87537f0f0f72694e8e24e7", "git_parents": ["f08f25d1dea5da779075aafb9aa2355b1973096e"], "node": "7abb0ca49d4e58f0bcf4cf0f1d881f100bf1a72a", "parents": ["eb214e188fd4d14a2d1c0831d4c0cf26637a810c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068624 - Remove unused Legacy Telemetry environment.system.sec section r=TravisLong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325168\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/environment.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/TelemetryEnvironmentTesting.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "af16f91c517d313c5f98bffba698e7b346601720", "git_parents": ["aae565df3a9f1d30af87537f0f0f72694e8e24e7"], "node": "1e04216fbbcc57ec26a19b6d0522a88325c7f38a", "parents": ["7abb0ca49d4e58f0bcf4cf0f1d881f100bf1a72a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068624 - Remove unused Legacy Telemetry environment.profile fields r=TravisLong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325169\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/environment.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/TelemetryEnvironmentTesting.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "9e4c0ceb5f3d62014c03da133a834f10dd3e9bdc", "git_parents": ["af16f91c517d313c5f98bffba698e7b346601720"], "node": "3057d1c37c80bbc42fa8f3a7a3a34e7d614b27eb", "parents": ["1e04216fbbcc57ec26a19b6d0522a88325c7f38a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Danielle Graham \u003cdgraham@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2036958 - consider pending tabs when blurring to tab on close r=jswinarton,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nSince findTabToBlurTo would select an unloaded tab when closing the active tab, even if a loaded tab was right next to it, I opted to add a filter on the visible tabs for just loaded(pending) tabs (as long as theres at least one) before running the rest of the adjacent-tab/MRU selection logic. If everything left is unloaded, falls back to the old behaviour since we have to pick something.\n\nFor a possible case where the MRU tab is unloaded and that pref is on, this will also fall back to the next loaded tab instead of reloading it, since that case seemed more likely to be expected based on this bug report and also like an edge case but open to other opinions on that!\n\nThis also should not impact the successor/owner selection, those should still take precedence.\n\nAdded a few tests as well - these tests unload the tab using a discardTab helper that calls discardBrowser and handles a race condition I came across with browserLoaded. Otherwise this looked to be the same path that unloading a tab takes but let me know if I'm missing anything there.\n  - the basic case from the bug report (adjacent tab unloaded skips to loaded one)\n  - same thing through the MRU path when MRU pref is on\n  - multiple unloaded tabs in a row, to make sure it keeps walking past all of them\n  - a test confirming successor still wins even when unloaded\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324747\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_selectMRUOnClose.js"], "git_node": "b3d24d4d770f97f6a395007b319fcd72840cc238", "git_parents": ["9e4c0ceb5f3d62014c03da133a834f10dd3e9bdc"], "node": "95b8bdfdd851c08c89650ae0365f9073a5ec0d61", "parents": ["3057d1c37c80bbc42fa8f3a7a3a34e7d614b27eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007202: Implement WebTransport getStats() r=saschanaz,necko-reviewers,webidl,kershaw,smaug,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277255\n", "files": ["dom/webidl/WebTransport.webidl", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.cpp", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.h", "dom/webtransport/parent/WebTransportParent.cpp", "dom/webtransport/parent/WebTransportParent.h", "dom/webtransport/shared/PWebTransport.ipdl", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http2WebTransportSession.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http2WebTransportSession.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3WebTransportSession.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3WebTransportSession.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/WebTransportSessionBase.h", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/WebTransportSessionProxy.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/WebTransportSessionProxy.h", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/nsIWebTransport.idl", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/NeqoHttp3Conn.h", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/src/lib.rs", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestHttp2WebTransport.cpp", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestHttp3ConnectUDPStream.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/stats.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "903617b6e0facc3a6553b1cc31cb95602bc64047", "git_parents": ["b3d24d4d770f97f6a395007b319fcd72840cc238"], "node": "4e674f7236f0afcf73d8bac40e13f72d8469e505", "parents": ["95b8bdfdd851c08c89650ae0365f9073a5ec0d61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007202: Get stats from a WebTransport connection on close r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D287811\n", "files": ["dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.cpp", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.h", "dom/webtransport/child/WebTransportChild.cpp", "dom/webtransport/child/WebTransportChild.h", "dom/webtransport/parent/WebTransportParent.cpp", "dom/webtransport/parent/WebTransportParent.h", "dom/webtransport/shared/PWebTransport.ipdl", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3WebTransportSession.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3WebTransportSession.h", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/WebTransportSessionProxy.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/WebTransportSessionProxy.h", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/nsIWebTransport.idl", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/NeqoHttp3Conn.h", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestHttp2WebTransport.cpp", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestHttp3ConnectUDPStream.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/stats.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "a8818bc810c783244bd1d979f6cba07ad6c2a797", "git_parents": ["903617b6e0facc3a6553b1cc31cb95602bc64047"], "node": "e640a40cbee53dc38c7d899930d01ce2ca5829c8", "parents": ["4e674f7236f0afcf73d8bac40e13f72d8469e505"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007202: Update WebTransport getStats tests to include all fields r=jib\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D280255\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/stats.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/handlers/stats-data-transfer.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/stats.https.any.js"], "git_node": "fc737da6ff20254b34824f2d8bdf06f0235903a3", "git_parents": ["a8818bc810c783244bd1d979f6cba07ad6c2a797"], "node": "7ee47aa073140a354cd2f067e15a4083d3192fc5", "parents": ["e640a40cbee53dc38c7d899930d01ce2ca5829c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007202: Add more tests for getStats edge cases r=jib,necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D286505\n", "files": ["dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.cpp", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/src/lib.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/stats.https.any.js"], "git_node": "04abbb6397820490a609a1b7a898c89df759d0f0", "git_parents": ["fc737da6ff20254b34824f2d8bdf06f0235903a3"], "node": "c3b462aeb15ea27894e6c356862e2f171171cb82", "parents": ["7ee47aa073140a354cd2f067e15a4083d3192fc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007202: report real WebTransport stats after a server-initiated close r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nneqo drops the session while processing the close, so by the time we drain\nthe SessionClosed event webtransport_session_stats() fails and we fell back\nto Http3WebTransportSession's default-constructed mCachedStats: getStats()\nafter a server-initiated close reported zeros for every field.\n\nEverything in WebTransportStatsData other than the session's datagram\ncounters comes from connection-level neqo counters, which are still\navailable at that point, so fall back to those rather than to zeros.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318359\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/NeqoHttp3Conn.h", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/src/lib.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/stats.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "15ceda062ddc3126360adc0901f1fe284e98f106", "git_parents": ["04abbb6397820490a609a1b7a898c89df759d0f0"], "node": "bca2b9ecd0bb481dbe4b6a008f423d9f09b87700", "parents": ["c3b462aeb15ea27894e6c356862e2f171171cb82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007783: Add support for WebTransport supportsReliableOnly attribute r=dom-core-reviewers,webidl,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D285404\n", "files": ["dom/webidl/WebTransport.webidl", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.cpp", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/idlharness.https.sub.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "dd81880e298551d3cc85df5ba5e3d607e8b123a8", "git_parents": ["15ceda062ddc3126360adc0901f1fe284e98f106"], "node": "872987f626fc23483ac07d9f4ee1f3e895f30105", "parents": ["bca2b9ecd0bb481dbe4b6a008f423d9f09b87700"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007202: Make a scriptable interface for WebTransport stats data for xpcshell tests r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324954\n", "files": ["dom/webtransport/parent/WebTransportParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http2WebTransportSession.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3WebTransportSession.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/WebTransportSessionBase.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/WebTransportSessionBase.h", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/WebTransportSessionProxy.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/nsIWebTransport.idl", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestHttp2WebTransport.cpp"], "git_node": "11452663c19fcae454e756568c00510d6e67e406", "git_parents": ["dd81880e298551d3cc85df5ba5e3d607e8b123a8"], "node": "4ae5d03207fe0d5ce6fa48d509482d4e0efef049", "parents": ["872987f626fc23483ac07d9f4ee1f3e895f30105"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065915 - Distinguish target-language fluent strings in Full-Page Translations r=gregtatum,fluent-reviewers,translations-reviewers,bolsson\n\nThis commit distinguishes the target-language fluent string label\nin the main view of the FullPageTranslationsPanel from the target-language\nfluent string label in the revisit view of the panel. These strings are\nthe same in English, but may not be the same in every language, so we\nshould not reuse the same string across these two different contexts.\n\nhttps://github.com/projectfluent/fluent/wiki/Good-Practices-for-Developers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321756\n", "files": ["browser/components/translations/content/fullPageTranslationsPanel.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/head.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/translations.ftl"], "git_node": "db89fb90554799b84a178819abbafb5c54188bed", "git_parents": ["11452663c19fcae454e756568c00510d6e67e406"], "node": "cd89f89608737eb4cf857898e4178068ecf653c8", "parents": ["4ae5d03207fe0d5ce6fa48d509482d4e0efef049"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Guichard \u003cnicolas.guichard@kdab.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070023 - Call grcov with --llvm in parse_build_tests_ccov.py. r=marco\n\nFor bug 2008110 I added the --llvm flag in codecoverage.py but missed\nit here.\n\nThis aims to fix lots of errors like:\n```\n[ERROR] Error when running gcov: gcov execution failed on uniffi-40f9f7591a3b9d67_1.gcno\ngcov stdout:\ngcov stderr: uniffi-40f9f7591a3b9d67_1.gcno:version 'B11*', prefer 'B22*'\n```\non Android CCov builds\n\nand\n```\n[ERROR] Error when running gcov: Failed to execute gcov process\n```\non Linux/Windows CCov builds.\n\ngrcov should never call gcov because our CCov builds are always built\nwith Clang.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324372\n", "files": ["testing/parse_build_tests_ccov.py"], "git_node": "9234a501f99f7c7d3a1aa57d5b666fb534f2ea7e", "git_parents": ["db89fb90554799b84a178819abbafb5c54188bed"], "node": "5c7b3d954606ef2dd7a8e10179accba7c009f24c", "parents": ["cd89f89608737eb4cf857898e4178068ecf653c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Guichard \u003cnicolas.guichard@kdab.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033336 - Update grcov to v0.10.8. r=marco\n\nThis new grcov release includes a bugfix for GCNOs pointing to C++\nfiles outside the objdir with relative paths, as we typically get when\nbuilding with unified sources.\n\nSee https://github.com/mozilla/grcov/pull/1519 for details.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325306\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml"], "git_node": "08f3e323f0e0d36be1727a401fc8652f7fb542db", "git_parents": ["9234a501f99f7c7d3a1aa57d5b666fb534f2ea7e"], "node": "4cd6e8d4c6690c489332f56110b72643485210eb", "parents": ["5c7b3d954606ef2dd7a8e10179accba7c009f24c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1586591 - Move the smartbar off moz-input-box onto the shared text context menu. r=tgiles,flozia\n\nThe AI window's document had no text context menu of its own, so it now loads editMenuOverlay.js. The smartbar reaches it through the document hosting the input, which in smartbar mode is not this.document.\n\nEditContextMenu grows two things the smartbar needs: an anchor for a menu opened from a keyboard contextmenu event, and the input it was opened on, so the ProseMirror paste workaround only fires for the smartbar's own input.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321475\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/aiWindow.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_context_paste.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_smartbar_contextmenu_autofill_dismiss.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "toolkit/content/editMenuOverlay.js"], "git_node": "e33ac8a34a80743cd0e7d5cfed34485486ab6765", "git_parents": ["08f3e323f0e0d36be1727a401fc8652f7fb542db"], "node": "a737d504fdf688cf150ab046cc1f77cee3b28d3a", "parents": ["4cd6e8d4c6690c489332f56110b72643485210eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1586591 - Remove moz-input-box. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles,emilio\n\nThunderbird's compose window was the last consumer outside this repo; it moved off in bug 2066237, which has landed in comm-central.\n\nThe urlbar's a11y-checks exemption goes with it, since the wrapper no longer carries the combobox role that the check keyed on; the old searchbar still does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321477\n", "files": ["browser/components/multilineeditor/multiline-editor.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/findInPage.js", "testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/AccessibilityUtils.js", "toolkit/content/customElements.js", "toolkit/content/editMenuOverlay.js", "toolkit/content/jar.mn", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/chrome-nova.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/chrome.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/test_mozinputbox_dictionary.xhtml", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-box.js", "toolkit/themes/shared/global-shared.css"], "git_node": "b03a1a7a10fac10658216a0ae8d75d34f7d8500a", "git_parents": ["e33ac8a34a80743cd0e7d5cfed34485486ab6765"], "node": "4f7fd0cb7c5638547d289644df2db0dc280ceeec", "parents": ["a737d504fdf688cf150ab046cc1f77cee3b28d3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Danielle Graham \u003cdgraham@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068080 - replace aiwindow website select borders with token r=flozia\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323425\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-confirmation/ai-website-confirmation.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-select/ai-website-select.css"], "git_node": "6ca1f7140b6a48ed893a6e53e760eb28e601c83b", "git_parents": ["b03a1a7a10fac10658216a0ae8d75d34f7d8500a"], "node": "4415afd6b19983a42c889ebe8a9aab5515cbf7d8", "parents": ["4f7fd0cb7c5638547d289644df2db0dc280ceeec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nickgrato \u003cngrato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062112 - [Monitor Agent][FE] Create monitor component in tool bar panel r=ngrato,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,sfoster,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321407\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/agent-watch-empty.svg", "browser/c