08eb05b11e0ca"], "node": "4933c91b1c4b31c79b163ba456837bbdd3fc6ef6", "parents": ["4f06d3d170c9e4cc52d33418cd79b4a5585eccc1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antti Koivisto \u003cantti@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070175 [wpt PR 62456] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323319, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323319 (#62456)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6832bf17e64a59954a2884c0df055dcb27cd8c85\nwpt-pr: 62456\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/tree-counting/sibling-function-container-query.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/tree-counting/sibling-function-if-style-query.html"], "git_node": "70faf6d52fe10324e3c78d4e8d7153dab8e4b425", "git_parents": ["766c2a128fce815aac487ae7d709eca45c0783ad"], "node": "ee005e736a0ad57c715bfe196f370ad4d6e898aa", "parents": ["4933c91b1c4b31c79b163ba456837bbdd3fc6ef6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070175 [wpt PR 62456] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62456\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/tree-counting/sibling-function-if-style-query.html.ini"], "git_node": "d2342f3d6692bb39664d036e9d01195bd1065768", "git_parents": ["70faf6d52fe10324e3c78d4e8d7153dab8e4b425"], "node": "fa254a5a2d7931c96be41ad969855a68691e5733", "parents": ["ee005e736a0ad57c715bfe196f370ad4d6e898aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070181 [wpt PR 62368] - Omit firing change events synchronously on removal, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nOmit firing change events synchronously on removal\n\nThis is still under the same OmitBlurEventOnElementRemoval flag, as\nthose events are fired together with blur/focusout events.\n\nAlso use an enum instead of a boolean for this behavior.\n\nBug: 41484175\nChange-Id: Ib7e6d9c0b3f4b10e20e30328674ab8af1832de37\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8313948\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1692334}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: af50fa206c0effac2fea2f81c0cf797376938bbe\nwpt-pr: 62368\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/insertion-removing-steps/change-event.window.js"], "git_node": "e82bc132ecdd3a5c157426b3740d0a0cbb048e44", "git_parents": ["d2342f3d6692bb39664d036e9d01195bd1065768"], "node": "cc750534524373220d7d3b2495e6cc2a3a4844b9", "parents": ["fa254a5a2d7931c96be41ad969855a68691e5733"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070188 [wpt PR 62434] - [HiC] Allow negative width and height for src and dest rects, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Allow negative width and height for src and dest rects\n\nThe spec says drawElementImage() should use the bounding rect\nwhen given negative width or height. Implement this and add tests.\n\nWe need to check WebGL and WebGPU to see what they expect.\n\nBug: 512509721\nChange-Id: Ieb41221d6e30a0daf53fe9cbcd463ef2a6a87807\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8265530\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1692361}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c922a747efb68fd9bbeba2741cab1715f5c384c6\nwpt-pr: 62434\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/drawElementImage-dest-rect.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/drawElementImage-src-rect.tentative.html"], "git_node": "bfabd671b43019017cb4bbfbece9986a22b632c8", "git_parents": ["e82bc132ecdd3a5c157426b3740d0a0cbb048e44"], "node": "9cb6658335330c17f1236dded24ec1e05a8dcde2", "parents": ["cc750534524373220d7d3b2495e6cc2a3a4844b9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070188 [wpt PR 62434] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62434\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/drawElementImage-dest-rect.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/drawElementImage-src-rect.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "61b74323927d35ad52948152d9013923ec81742c", "git_parents": ["bfabd671b43019017cb4bbfbece9986a22b632c8"], "node": "5e1ef457701958ecf560fa6e2d4c7baa2dab20ee", "parents": ["9cb6658335330c17f1236dded24ec1e05a8dcde2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070191 [wpt PR 62450] - streamHTML: Use the adopted element's execution context for TT check, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nstreamHTML: Use the adopted element's execution context for TT check\n\nTrusted Types essentially applies to a node tree. Consistently\nuse the ContainerNode's ExecutionContext, rather than the ScriptState's (which is the ExecutionContext of the currently executing JavaScript thread). Those are mostly the same, but would differ e.g. a document can reach into an iframe (or vice versa).\n\nBug: 556013783\nChange-Id: I0c8eed185aa12d335ea0f1c287bd751817e66be4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8339912\nReviewed-by: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1692368}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4a5da312b17ceb66e4c4f6fbf2664d700d261ce8\nwpt-pr: 62450\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/all-stream-methods-with-trusted-types-no-policy.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-with-trusted-types-adopt.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-with-trusted-types-from-non-tt.html"], "git_node": "0ec87e8852799fa919ca17308afc4428785b2eda", "git_parents": ["61b74323927d35ad52948152d9013923ec81742c"], "node": "ed48c22e3446ca84d11f5bc21183ccf539e65907", "parents": ["5e1ef457701958ecf560fa6e2d4c7baa2dab20ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070191 [wpt PR 62450] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62450\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/all-stream-methods-with-trusted-types-no-policy.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-with-trusted-types-adopt.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-with-trusted-types-from-non-tt.html.ini"], "git_node": "fa05226170942cea6db12d0f0af112045569c73d", "git_parents": ["0ec87e8852799fa919ca17308afc4428785b2eda"], "node": "4fb25aeb47a3ec04ed05327cc0d0502f1d8f7350", "parents": ["ed48c22e3446ca84d11f5bc21183ccf539e65907"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070192 [wpt PR 62452] - Do RuleSet invalidation before ResetStyle, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDo RuleSet invalidation before ResetStyle\n\nThe RuleSet invalidation does selector matching which will reject\nrules in implicit @scopes when an element has not seen an implicit\nscope. When we do not simply append sheets, we call ResetStyle() in\norder to rebuild metadata properly, including the information on\nElements whether it has seen an implicit @scope.\n\nThe problem is that we need that information when doing the selector\nmatching when invalidating for removed stylesheets. Otherwise, we will\nnot invalidate for selectors inside implicit scope rules for any removed\nstylesheets.\n\nEffectively, we need to have the implicit scopes for both the added and\nremoved stylesheets. Add the implicit scopes for the new active\nstylesheets before doing RuleSet invalidation. Then, if the change is\nnot an append, we reset style and rebuild everything as necessary,\nincluding implicit scopes.\n\nBug: 555286423\nChange-Id: I08a32b546ca75d22ce47a383c1bb3508d35d11d0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8352487\nReviewed-by: Anders Hartvoll Ruud \u003candruud@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1692379}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0a399602563b82d26b1fd869ae6253ec3e6da3b5\nwpt-pr: 62452\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-cascade/scope-implicit-remove-sheet.html"], "git_node": "72ece59468823be1d920dc57a224abe1ec63ef1d", "git_parents": ["fa05226170942cea6db12d0f0af112045569c73d"], "node": "8421652279f35bd9a75f77e3881016521f3b3a82", "parents": ["4fb25aeb47a3ec04ed05327cc0d0502f1d8f7350"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064579 [wpt PR 62029] - [Proofreader] Re-enable Proofreader WPT tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Proofreader] Re-enable Proofreader WPT tests (#62029)\n\nUnskips external/wpt/ai/proofreader/* across AIExpectations_Manifest*\nand re-enables the includeCorrectionTypes test case now that the\ndedicated small expert model component is configured.\n\nFollows https://crrev.com/i/9691777.\n\nBug: 446717936\nChange-Id: I5cdabe0acd916ca307faad0b4c5a5bd8f8c8e5f5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8262246\nReviewed-by: Reilly Grant \u003creillyg@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1681719}\n\nCo-authored-by: Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commi