desc": "Bug 2070331 [wpt PR 62512] - Test an SVG image with a height of 0 and no width, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest an SVG image with a height of 0 and no width\n\nSee https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/73144.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 92054a74d0c6a1ed2e9024d71ebf2880f2af02e2\nwpt-pr: 62512\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/svg-img-zero-height-with-viewbox.html"], "git_node": "2c6f75449b636a77dbb8f7c715475b3ec79815cd", "git_parents": ["7f296bf960e14073b8ab4b3a9995bd22bfddb85e"], "node": "e8683e4e98afc6bc0c33861c34a61be11d0a57da", "parents": ["fc714e391f94fdfdca71aa645ffa64e0682880e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shannon Booth \u003c35911232+shannonbooth@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065897 [wpt PR 62160] - [webdriver] Test same-URL navigation replaces the current history entry, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[webdriver] Test same-URL navigation replaces the current history entry\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12824\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e6d42a5ffcc6d6a4f66401ecaadd21f2c688ddbe\nwpt-pr: 62160\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/navigate/navigate.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/navigate_to/navigate.py"], "git_node": "28eefa27c8e6d038c0f3f486a5b626f1a470fa88", "git_parents": ["2c6f75449b636a77dbb8f7c715475b3ec79815cd"], "node": "1171eeadbb9c3be69d654188b03c25d36e01019b", "parents": ["e8683e4e98afc6bc0c33861c34a61be11d0a57da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065897 [wpt PR 62160] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62160\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/navigate/navigate.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/navigate_to/frame.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/navigate_to/navigate.py.ini"], "git_node": "a11d39d5b7d26bb201bcad2f6f53197201138fd6", "git_parents": ["28eefa27c8e6d038c0f3f486a5b626f1a470fa88"], "node": "3629f5067031cb50faa84b431a263395315f9c92", "parents": ["1171eeadbb9c3be69d654188b03c25d36e01019b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "youennf \u003cyouennf@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070536 [wpt PR 62419] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323290, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323290 (#62419)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 94fb622d35cf4a979e99538a6e441068de93cb87\nwpt-pr: 62419\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/range/resources/video-with-range.py"], "git_node": "8d61d63e0f86fe42b2ca8d1c1c14212dc1167abd", "git_parents": ["a11d39d5b7d26bb201bcad2f6f53197201138fd6"], "node": "e941e8ac6169ec81824bbe2ad14d7b22e1dad371", "parents": ["3629f5067031cb50faa84b431a263395315f9c92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Felipe Erias \u003cfelipeerias@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070541 [wpt PR 62494] - [CSS] Handle color-mix() and palette-mix() percentages adding up to zero, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[CSS] Handle color-mix() and palette-mix() percentages adding up to zero\n\nWhen the two percentages of color-mix() add up to zero, CSS Color 5\nspecifies a progress percentage of 0.5 and an alpha multiplier of 0,\nso the result is transparent.\n\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-5/#color-mix-result\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14013\n\nCSS Fonts 4 applies the same rules to palette-mix().\n\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/css-fonts-4/#font-palette-prop\n\nBlink rejected color-mix() and palette-mix() at parse time when both\npercentages were literally `0%`. When the zero sum came from calc()\ninstead, the values parsed but percentage normalization reported\nfailure. Then color-mix() went on with a progress percentage of 0,\nand palette-mix() was replaced by the normal palette, as if the value\nhad not been specified.\n\nRemove the parse-time rejection. Make\nCSSColorMixValue::NormalizePercentages() always produce a progress\npercentage and an alpha multiplier, using 0.5 and 0 for a zero sum. Keep\na palette mix with equal endpoints when the alpha multiplier is not 1,\nas collapsing it into a single palette would drop the multiplier.\n\nTests:\n  external/wpt/css/css-color/parsing/color-valid-color-mix-function.html\n  external/wpt/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-color-mix-function.html\n  StyleBuilderConverterTest.ResolveColorValue_ZeroCombinedPercentage\n  StyleBuilderConverterPageTest.PaletteMix_ZeroCombinedPercentage\n\nBug: 445726759\nChange-Id: I79682e00f313722a09f3a9a337aac4eabd0cb0c6\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8337347\nCommit-Queue: Felipe Erias \u003cfelipeerias@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Anders Hartvoll Ruud \u003candruud@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693091}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 16cc06485392b22d0c96dc54d290480dfac2d695\nwpt-pr: 62494\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-color-mix-function.html"], "git_node": "59ec4a319dd87772a40d567763da267e5564dad9", "git_parents": ["8d61d63e0f86fe42b2ca8d1c1c14212dc1167abd"], "node": "3e44eb48539f92b0b2a6dea67f589ff96c40248e", "parents": ["e941e8ac6169ec81824bbe2ad14d7b22e1dad371"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070541 [wpt PR 62494] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62494\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-color-mix-function.html.ini"], "git_node": "10759d068d1c2cdafa95e6710a6d1cdcdac1c2f3", "git_parents": ["59ec4a319dd87772a40d567763da267e5564dad9"], "node": "bf192caee9d640ad3a8b4093c2f844a1e1ce6b53", "parents": ["3e44eb48539f92b0b2a6dea67f589ff96c40248e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jiacheng Guo \u003cgjc@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070542 [wpt PR 62499] - Revert \"Fix WebAssembly.Module messaging with AudioWorklet\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRevert \"Fix WebAssembly.Module messaging with AudioWorklet\"\n\nThis reverts commit 4b8042b1960f0fdc9eafb3ace18fb951628bb8c3.\n\nReason for revert: Causing CI failure\n\nFailure Link: https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/builders/ci/Win10%20Tests%20x64%20(dbg)/55231/overview\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Fix WebAssembly.Module messaging with AudioWorklet\n\u003e\n\u003e Worklets have opaque origins but share their creator's agent cluster.\n\u003e Use the creator document's origin for Chromium's additional same-origin\n\u003e check when an AudioWorklet message requires it only for WebAssembly\n\u003e modules.\n\u003e\n\u003e Keep strict same-origin checks for File System Access handles, including\n\u003e mixed messages, and retain the agent-cluster check. Add WPT and unit\n\u003e coverage for the global and processor ports and rejection cases.\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: 40210558\n\u003e Change-Id: I556705cbd7491eec71e7e6a060eada9b77ace87d\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8334848\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Hongchan Choi \u003chongchan@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Aaron Teo \u003chocheung@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Jeremy Roman \u003cjbroman@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1692867}\n\nBug: 40210558\nChange-Id: I8920bffbd1ccb61564c7a312eb18a98da47a4654\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8365744\nOwners-Override: Jiacheng Guo \u003cgjc@google.com\u003e\nBot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Jiacheng Guo \u003cgjc@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693158}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0312887a72b0592da8fa7a2244256e5da96d5e30\nwpt-pr: 62499\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworklet-messageport-wasm.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/processors/wasm-port-processor.js"], "git_node": "6693270407bc013dd2114b921733e4e8735b8a00", "git_parents": ["10759d068d1c2cdafa95e6710a6d1cdcdac1c2f3"], "node": "29e9b0733febeffa678bc26463d52df8ae5c7bdd", "parents": ["bf192caee9d640ad3a8b4093c2f844a1e1ce6b53"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Nguyen \u003ctungnh@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070543 [wpt PR 62506] - [PEPC] Disallow container-type, container-name, and contain-intrinsic*, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[PEPC] Disallow container-type, container-name, and contain-intrinsic*\n\ncontainer-type: size enables size containment, which causes the\nelement's fit-content width to resolve from contain-intrinsic-width\ninstead of the user-agent controlled shadow-DOM label. The width bounds\napplied in AdjustStyle() are expressed as calc-size(fit-content, k *\nsize), so an author-supplied intrinsic width can replace the label width\nthose bounds are meant to track, allowing clickjacking boundaries to be\nbypassed.\nSince contain is already disallowed, remove\nvalid_for_permission_element: true from container-type, container-name,\nand contain-intrinsic-* (width, height, inline-size, block-size, size)\nas well.\n\nFixed: 514061289\nChange-Id: I09daff39d72a39da4ebe687bd33b0a9d37fae9dc\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8363545\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Thomas Nguyen \u003ctungnh@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693346}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6a9ec55672f8bdda04f8ae619d52c2f798ab9eeb\nwpt-pr: 62506\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/geolocation-element/invalid-css-properties.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/install/invalid-css-properties.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/usermedia/invalid-css-properties.html"], "git_node": "567fd48e8d7a65957b4aac332cc132b4482a61d6", "git_parents": ["6693270407bc013dd2114b921733e4e8735b8a00"], "node": "d13375fd85d81fe7c734b04b95ac47bf4e527a15", "parents": ["29e9b0733febeffa678bc26463d52df8ae5c7bdd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070546 [wpt PR 62477] - [Sanitizer] Fix initialization of default PI allow/remove lists., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Sanitizer] Fix initialization of default PI allow/remove lists.\n\nObserve the |allowCommentsPIsAndDataAttributes| flag when initializing\na Sanitizer config with neither allow- nor remove-lists for PIs.\n\nAlso fix the test case which had malformed test data. This caused the\ntest to silently fail and hide the bug.\n\nRef: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dynamic-markup-insertion.html#canonicalize-the-configuration, step 3.*\n\nFix: 556213916\nChange-Id: I80950f53de418f4d2478dfc795fa7364d1435c08\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8352664\nCommit-Queue: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693355}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 47287651c23621ce276cae0dc1a437ab705fb92a\nwpt-pr: 62477\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-processing-instructions.html"], "git_node": "0baecbd39ca24e80006d451b06ef248d22f871f5", "git_parents": ["567fd48e8d7a65957b4aac332cc132b4482a61d6"], "node": "4a505a4fb5e4c63a6fe51640d112be3f5d40fed8", "parents": ["d13375fd85d81fe7c734b04b95ac47bf4e527a15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070546 [wpt PR 62477] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62477\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-processing-instructions.html.ini"], "git_node": "f4aa850cfa48885c763244479bc39c9f880d521f", "git_parents": ["0baecbd39ca24e80006d451b06ef248d22f871f5"], "node": "ce114fd01d544f72fbf7eebbc86da88a3b0a73db", "parents": ["4a505a4fb5e4c63a6fe51640d112be3f5d40fed8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Nguyen \u003ctungnh@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070548 [wpt PR 62507] - [CE[ Use HasTagName for tag checks in HTMLCapabilityElementBase, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[CE[ Use HasTagName for tag checks in HTMLCapabilityElementBase\n\nHTML elements created with an XML namespace prefix (such as via\ncreateElementNS) retain a prefix in their QualifiedName. Direct equality\ncomparisons using TagQName() == html_names::kInstallTag evaluate to\nfalse due to the prefix difference, preventing tag-specific logic from\nmatching.\nReplace direct QualifiedName comparisons with HasTagName() across\nHTMLCapabilityElementBase. This ensures subframe and sandbox state\nvalidation correctly handles prefixed install elements.\n\nFixed: 517366426\nChange-Id: Ib1a96940975207c5d23ec789745d0fdc7e8f9550\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8364205\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Thomas Nguyen \u003ctungnh@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693416}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cb3918a1725342ff9e0876558383723833ee6e5b\nwpt-pr: 62507\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/install/iframe-not-allowed.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/install/sandbox-not-allowed.tentative.html"], "git_node": "ac8d270d48e8d2a97529e344327be943dc26473c", "git_parents": ["f4aa850cfa48885c763244479bc39c9f880d521f"], "node": "6f8b3251069edeb55e3c034577be60043f1c94aa", "parents": ["ce114fd01d544f72fbf7eebbc86da88a3b0a73db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070548 [wpt PR 62507] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62507\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/install/iframe-not-allowed.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "fca1c39e1238b9b844fca34118d325858de05ba7", "git_parents": ["ac8d270d48e8d2a97529e344327be943dc26473c"], "node": "8c4ef20f64fc09646b22b997fe8a92b471427fda", "parents": ["6f8b3251069edeb55e3c034577be60043f1c94aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070553 [wpt PR 62497] - Check is_shutting_down_ in PipeToEngine::ReadRequestChunkStepsBody, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCheck is_shutting_down_ in PipeToEngine::ReadRequestChunkStepsBody\n\nWhen a WritableStream errors during pipeTo with preventCancel: true,\nWritableError schedules a microtask that shuts down the pipe and\nreleases the writer lock. If a chunk is enqueued to the ReadableStream\nin the same tick, ReadRequestChunkStepsBody runs in a subsequent\nmicrotask. Without checking is_shutting_down_, it attempts to write to\nthe released writer, triggering a CHECK(stream) crash.\n\nBail out early from ReadRequestChunkStepsBody if is_shutting_down_ is\ntrue, matching the Streams Standard requirement that no writes be\ninitiated after shutdown has begun.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=ed3e939c-7110-4854-b07e-e1c1faad30db\n\nBug: 556160930\nChange-Id: Ic86ca5f52534e349076c8dfde93a70524439f958\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8351108\nReviewed-by: Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693472}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 27c8d8bee624b851f2ab7cd6c32ad07fc19f3007\nwpt-pr: 62497\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/streams/piping/error-propagation-backward.any.js"], "git_node": "6b600d3979d3f41fd8913b08ff88332234ebd405", "git_parents": ["fca1c39e1238b9b844fca34118d325858de05ba7"], "node": "a9597fa8671c90ea4957e4691c08d4d053e9ef24", "parents": ["8c4ef20f64fc09646b22b997fe8a92b471427fda"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jason Leo \u003ccgqaq@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070558 [wpt PR 62508] - Require an explicit alpha argument in CSS alpha(), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRequire an explicit alpha argument in CSS alpha()\n\nFollow the CSSWG resolution [1], with a stable runtime flag for rollback.\n\n[1]: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14070#issuecomment-5202934726\n\nBug: 543376113\nChange-Id: I6006309440c0ae96a85bcea89d1ac611115498ea\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8361849\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Jason Leo \u003ccgqaq@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693478}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1e1d8dd80740aabb3add63644a768b3ebd9b12de\nwpt-pr: 62508\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/alpha-color-parsing-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/color-valid-relative-color-opaque-alpha.html"], "git_node": "e6493d2ad09ff8c8573a4a8a37405a96ff6adb17", "git_parents": ["6b600d3979d3f41fd8913b08ff88332234ebd405"], "node": "5e6168b7e182e5d257c6b152f64b807deba7ca3c", "parents": ["a9597fa8671c90ea4957e4691c08d4d053e9ef24"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070603 [wpt PR 62509] - Stabilize text-combine-upright-compression reftests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nStabilize text-combine-upright-compression reftests\n\nThese tests use a custom font. The screenshot was taken before the font\nfinished loading, so the page first rendered with a fallback font.\nThis CL adds reftest-wait so the screenshot waits until the font is\nready. A small 1px difference still remains, so this also adds a fuzzy\nmatch.\n\nBug: 40527323\nChange-Id: I58c2400e868b40cb3d25e770ccc62e090f365c9a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8357089\nCommit-Queue: Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693486}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 28380411f7ec46e8c2e5e4f8c603c51188aeeddd\nwpt-pr: 62509\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/support/wait-for-width-test-font.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-005a.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-combine-upright-compression-006a.html"], "git_node": "e012e6ebfd280b684c56497a874c9a26e6cfdbd0", "git_parents": ["e6493d2ad09ff8c8573a4a8a37405a96ff6adb17"], "node": "2ce420c78de54d4fda8c54267ff5156460d0ac25", "parents": ["5e6168b7e182e5d257c6b152f64b807deba7ca3c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070605 [wpt PR 62510] - Roll jxl: 0.6.0 =\u003e 0.7.1 in //third_party/rust, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRoll jxl: 0.6.0 =\u003e 0.7.1 in //third_party/rust\n\nThis CL has been created semi-automatically. The expected review process\nand other details can be found at //tools/crates/create_update_cl.md.\n\nUpdated crates:\n\n* jxl: 0.6.0 =\u003e 0.7.1; https://docs.rs/crate/jxl/0.7.1\n* jxl_macros: 0.6.0 =\u003e 0.7.1;\n  https://docs.rs/crate/jxl_macros/0.7.1\n* jxl_simd: 0.6.0 =\u003e 0.7.1;\n  https://docs.rs/crate/jxl_simd/0.7.1\n* jxl_transforms: 0.6.0 =\u003e 0.7.1;\n  https://docs.rs/crate/jxl_transforms/0.7.1\n\nUpdate the Chromium integration for the 0.7 API changes, including\nthread-count reporting, ordered parallel task scheduling, fallible\npixel-format setup, and the new dithering table input. Update affected\nJPEG XL progressive web test tolerances.\n\nVersion 0.7.1 includes https://github.com/libjxl/jxl-rs/pull/947, which\nmoves large static data behind boxes to avoid a binary size regression.\n\nBug: None\nChange-Id: Ida280ae6f3d5b1050175af2d18ac22a68fd3448a\nBinary-Size: Size increase is unavoidable\nFuchsia-Binary-Size: Size increase is unavoidable.\nDisable-Rts: True\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8366384\nReviewed-by: Luca Versari \u003cveluca@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nSLSA-Policy-Verified: SLSA Policy Verification Service \u003cdevtools-gerritcodereview-exitgate@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: \u0141ukasz Anforowicz \u003clukasza@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693573}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a5efc221a1f71f22df7e6e61c5531e93e8589e5d\nwpt-pr: 62510\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/progressive-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/progressive-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/progressive-3.html"], "git_node": "fd38fde73b476b22c61ed082e7e0a6854a04351e", "git_parents": ["e012e6ebfd280b684c56497a874c9a26e6cfdbd0"], "node": "b01c9dd7a310e9ce8b5e773fa6348e2518ca6bd6", "parents": ["2ce420c78de54d4fda8c54267ff5156460d0ac25"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Takashi Toyoshima \u003ctoyoshim@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070607 [wpt PR 62515] - OOR-CORS: Avoid CorsURLLoader restart on redirect, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nOOR-CORS: Avoid CorsURLLoader restart on redirect\n\nCorsURLLoader previously restarted requests from scratch via\nStartRequest() on redirects requiring CORS or preflights. This destroyed\nthe underlying URLRequest redirect history, causing Fetch Metadata\nheaders (e.g. Sec-Fetch-Site) to be incorrectly computed.\n\nThis CL introduces base::Feature kAvoidCorsURLLoaderRestartOnRedirect\n(enabled by default) to handle redirects in-place via\nnetwork_loader_-\u003eFollowRedirect() and update headers directly. If a\nredirect requires a CORS preflight, CorsURLLoader runs the preflight\nasynchronously without tearing down the active loader.\n\nKey changes:\n- In-place redirect and preflight handling in CorsURLLoader under\n  kAvoidCorsURLLoaderRestartOnRedirect.\n- Strict validation of redirected URLs and origin permissions via\n  OriginAccessList for credentials and client certificates.\n- WHATWG Fetch compliant credential handling across cross-origin\n  redirects.\n- Parameterized test coverage for both in-place and legacy restart\n  paths.\n\nBug: 513518289\nChange-Id: Ic250535f64bf316df656d6cbe29e27cdbac7272a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8278433\nReviewed-by: Kenichi Ishibashi \u003cbashi@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Takashi Toyoshima \u003ctoyoshim@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693621}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cbe79fa305818bc3adc21500db2ded241c887aee\nwpt-pr: 62515\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/credentialless/reporting-subresource-corp.https.window.js"], "git_node": "e49341649a1c79529ed441c04cd6f4f60a841d31", "git_parents": ["fd38fde73b476b22c61ed082e7e0a6854a04351e"], "node": "162d854451cce8eb0581f7436f3d2f0936d4aa3a", "parents": ["b01c9dd7a310e9ce8b5e773fa6348e2518ca6bd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seokho Song \u003cseokho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070610 [wpt PR 62527] - Store container selector cache in ContainerQueryList, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nStore container selector cache in ContainerQueryList\n\nThe selector cache maps each container selector to its resolved\ncontainer element, reducing container lookup from O(N) in tree\ndepth to O(1) once the cache is set.\n\nHold the cache on each ContainerQueryList instance and use it when\nevaluating the query list. The cache is not used while the element\nis in a display:none subtree.\n\nInvalidate the cache when the resolved container may change:\n- A style change affects container query evaluation\n  (DiffAffectsContainerQueries). This bumps a controller cache\n  generation, invalidating all caches.\n- The element's layout tree is detached. This invalidates the caches\n  of the lists on that element.\n\nA local microbenchmark reading matches on 500 lists under a 1000-deep\nancestor chain:\n\n---Before---\n\nTime:\navg 8.175000011920929 ms\nmedian 8.149999976158142 ms\nstdev 0.19432745050615563 ms\nmin 7.800000071525574 ms\nmax 8.600000023841858 ms\n\n---After---\n\nTime:\navg 1.0600000083446501 ms\nmedian 1.0499999523162842 ms\nstdev 0.1698296159003472 ms\nmin 0.8999999761581421 ms\nmax 1.6999999284744263 ms\n\nBug: 40887402\nChange-Id: I38d4be957c61067d615046dddc41487fa97c7d1a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8255022\nCommit-Queue: Seokho Song \u003cseokho@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693827}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7926f3ca1cd9f7f1df88db0bb0cee14f278a559b\nwpt-pr: 62527\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/match-container-change-event.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/match-container.tentative.html"], "git_node": "a2f8d2609219a1d1d7bf251f2132ac5dfe7b7af2", "git_parents": ["e49341649a1c79529ed441c04cd6f4f60a841d31"], "node": "ddf7ce9a2baaba4fa3bfe34332e4bdd8724fc923", "parents": ["162d854451cce8eb0581f7436f3d2f0936d4aa3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070610 [wpt PR 62527] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62527\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/whitespace-update-after-removal.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/match-container-change-event.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/match-container.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "9530dfc1b4e6aac0adf4432f21bc470e9f5ceb8e", "git_parents": ["a2f8d2609219a1d1d7bf251f2132ac5dfe7b7af2"], "node": "3b3eaba9071c2c766c6b29f2856a336942d95760", "parents": ["ddf7ce9a2baaba4fa3bfe34332e4bdd8724fc923"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Page \u003cadam@adampage.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1873378 [wpt PR 43874] - Add tests for invalidly nested heading nodes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd tests for invalidly nested heading nodes (#43874)\n\n* add nested heading tests\n* add parity checks for parsing error correction and accname accumulations\n* reset aria-utils and relocate heading-related functions\n* refactor ancestor role tests to check computed role\n* reorganize tests to ease parity comparisons\n* identify test as tentative\n* add new subtest for heading impostors\n* move failing subtests into tentative test\n* replicate passing subtests back into main test\n* remove tentative test\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0dc7683798d856f39fe0ade75300e4d64929a1ea\nwpt-pr: 43874\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html-aam/heading/invalid-nesting.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/wai-aria/heading/invalid-nesting.html"], "git_node": "fa13dbaaa922ba4c3012e2b1db5b552d3b6b6e21", "git_parents": ["9530dfc1b4e6aac0adf4432f21bc470e9f5ceb8e"], "node": "63d897941fdf4b1696286ac7b1e998691a067913", "parents": ["3b3eaba9071c2c766c6b29f2856a336942d95760"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070618 [wpt PR 62530] - Changed TrustedParserOptions to an empty TrustedHTMLParserOptions, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nChanged TrustedParserOptions to an empty TrustedHTMLParserOptions\n\nAs part of recent spec review.\n\nR=vogelheim\n\nBug: 491743369\nChange-Id: Ia03a2b1e27b40684d60f673036a4f4914c93ed16\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8361511\nCommit-Queue: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693835}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1fad8a9882fb980dbcf9b997a899adf7b465c386\nwpt-pr: 62530\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/positional-methods-with-parser-options.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-with-trusted-types-pass-trusted.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/parsehtmlunsafe-with-trustedtypes.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes-createParserOptions-null.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes-createParserOptions.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes-immutable.tentative.html"], "git_node": "415b5266c8fd81ed10146e4d11364365fb5484bf", "git_parents": ["fa13dbaaa922ba4c3012e2b1db5b552d3b6b6e21"], "node": "bd55c54debe9d91620127a7f5e43cfc48f0aa58c", "parents": ["63d897941fdf4b1696286ac7b1e998691a067913"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070618 [wpt PR 62530] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62530\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/positional-methods-with-parser-options.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-with-trusted-types-pass-trusted.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/parsehtmlunsafe-with-trustedtypes.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes-createParserOptions-null.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes-createParserOptions.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes-immutable.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "51428e2b7ce1447a967c7aeaad44255aa3714edc", "git_parents": ["415b5266c8fd81ed10146e4d11364365fb5484bf"], "node": "5a5678516107c6f9b728d9475500770cb6ead6b2", "parents": ["bd55c54debe9d91620127a7f5e43cfc48f0aa58c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johann Hofmann \u003cjohannhof@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070623 [wpt PR 62532] - Delete Top-Level Storage Access API Web Platform Tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDelete Top-Level Storage Access API Web Platform Tests\n\nFollowing the deprecation and removal of document.requestStorageAccessFor\n(crrev.com/c/8261139), this CL removes the obsolete Web Platform Tests\nand associated test expectations and filter entries:\n\n- Delete external/wpt/top-level-storage-access-api/\n- Delete external/wpt/html/anonymous-iframe/requestStorageAccessFor.tentative.https.window.js\n- Clean up skip entries in NeverFixTests\n- Clean up entries in TestLists/chrome.filter and TestLists/rel-ready.blink_wpt_tests.filter\n- Clean up entries in FlagExpectations/surface-embed\n\nBug: 551997654\nTAG=agy\n\nChange-Id: I21dbea5c42678c9cb00e98119db11e747fb29239\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8361509\nAuto-Submit: Johann Hofmann \u003cjohannhof@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Chris Fredrickson \u003ccfredric@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Chris Fredrickson \u003ccfredric@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693930}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b46e71b2f22c73fbcecaf26009e3082fddbaa744\nwpt-pr: 62532\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/anonymous-iframe/requestStorageAccessFor.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/top-level-storage-access-api/META.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/top-level-storage-access-api/README.md", "testing/web-platform/tests/top-level-storage-access-api/requestStorageAccessFor-insecure.sub.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/top-level-storage-access-api/requestStorageAccessFor.sub.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/top-level-storage-access-api/resources/permissions-iframe.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/top-level-storage-access-api/resources/requestStorageAccessFor-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/top-level-storage-access-api/resources/requestStorageAccessFor-iframe.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/top-level-storage-access-api/top-level-storage-access-permission.sub.https.window.js"], "git_node": "566ff02dfd16ab8388373000d947aa802d993dee", "git_parents": ["51428e2b7ce1447a967c7aeaad44255aa3714edc"], "node": "0703ad2fc78108988eb1c1724cc4f182145ccaf7", "parents": ["5a5678516107c6f9b728d9475500770cb6ead6b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ho Cheung \u003chocheung@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070628 [wpt PR 62535] - Reland \"Fix WebAssembly.Module messaging with AudioWorklet\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReland \"Fix WebAssembly.Module messaging with AudioWorklet\"\n\nThis reverts commit 6e3202a1d816a4e5e156bdf9bd0fd0244ba65892.\n\nReason for revert: Fix Wasm attachment loss in component-build tests.\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Revert \"Fix WebAssembly.Module messaging with AudioWorklet\"\n\u003e\n\u003e This reverts commit 4b8042b1960f0fdc9eafb3ace18fb951628bb8c3.\n\u003e\n\u003e Reason for revert: Causing CI failure\n\u003e\n\u003e Failure Link: https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/builders/ci/Win10%20Tests%20x64%20(dbg)/55231/overview\n\u003e\n\u003e Original change's description:\n\u003e \u003e Fix WebAssembly.Module messaging with AudioWorklet\n\u003e \u003e\n\u003e \u003e Worklets have opaque origins but share their creator's agent cluster.\n\u003e \u003e Use the creator document's origin for Chromium's additional same-origin\n\u003e \u003e check when an AudioWorklet message requires it only for WebAssembly\n\u003e \u003e modules.\n\u003e \u003e\n\u003e \u003e Keep strict same-origin checks for File System Access handles, including\n\u003e \u003e mixed messages, and retain the agent-cluster check. Add WPT and unit\n\u003e \u003e coverage for the global and processor ports and rejection cases.\n\u003e \u003e\n\u003e \u003e Bug: 40210558\n\u003e \u003e Change-Id: I556705cbd7491eec71e7e6a060eada9b77ace87d\n\u003e \u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8334848\n\u003e \u003e Reviewed-by: Hongchan Choi \u003chongchan@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e \u003e Commit-Queue: Aaron Teo \u003chocheung@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e \u003e Reviewed-by: Jeremy Roman \u003cjbroman@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1692867}\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: 40210558\n\u003e Change-Id: I8920bffbd1ccb61564c7a312eb18a98da47a4654\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8365744\n\u003e Owners-Override: Jiacheng Guo \u003cgjc@google.com\u003e\n\u003e Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Jiacheng Guo \u003cgjc@google.com\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693158}\n\nBug: 40210558\nChange-Id: If77a370294b719823627b9d24d44809f4414e526\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8364650\nReviewed-by: Jeremy Roman \u003cjbroman@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Aaron Teo \u003chocheung@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693925}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: da984a3bceec321e72a1fe53e44145fc7c7d34d4\nwpt-pr: 62535\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworklet-messageport-wasm.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/processors/wasm-port-processor.js"], "git_node": "87fce733e566bd74579430c0f94a1a2f512c8bb4", "git_parents": ["566ff02dfd16ab8388373000d947aa802d993dee"], "node": "56e235b997007836bf4eba6479dbf74b83b1a6ae", "parents": ["0703ad2fc78108988eb1c1724cc4f182145ccaf7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070631 [wpt PR 62469] - [Align] Parse `flow-start` and `flow-end` keyword, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Align] Parse `flow-start` and `flow-end` keyword\n\nParse the `flow-start` and `flow-end` keywords and ensure that they\nevaluate to the same value as `start` and `end` when no placement\nreversals are applied. The change is gated behind a separate flag from\ngrid lanes, since it will apply to all layout modes. We decided we\nwanted those keywords in the resolution of this CSSWG issue [1].\n\nA follow-up change will be needed to implement and test `flow-start` and\n`flow-end` when `fill-reverse` and `track-reverse` are applied, as well\nas for using the `kFlowStart/End` keyword in the code instead of\n`kFlexStart/End`.\n\nCopies of tests were added in both the `css-flex` and `css-align`\nfolders.\n\n[1] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14052\n\nBug: 343257585, 555299635\nChange-Id: I5dc0707fbcfeff3674d1884aaf38afa1c9e860fa\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8307932\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693943}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 272061587f284327e2f620b29c6444e7a193f628\nwpt-pr: 62469\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-content-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-content-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-content-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-items-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-items-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-items-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-self-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-self-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-self-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-content-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-content-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-content-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-items-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-items-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-items-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-self-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-self-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-self-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/place-content-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/place-content-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/place-items-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/place-items-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/place-self-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/place-self-valid.html"], "git_node": "bed7bb8a3a546324be4d1fd31c38e9466d709321", "git_parents": ["87fce733e566bd74579430c0f94a1a2f512c8bb4"], "node": "da90a06441f8f26533db66a90fafcd0e23276c5c", "parents": ["56e235b997007836bf4eba6479dbf74b83b1a6ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070631 [wpt PR 62469] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62469\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/align-content-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/align-content-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/align-items-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/align-items-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/align-self-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/align-self-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/justify-content-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/justify-content-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/justify-items-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/justify-items-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/justify-self-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/justify-self-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/place-content-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/place-content-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/place-items-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/place-items-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/place-self-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/place-self-valid.html.ini"], "git_node": "07fba7c28d491a0ba0b208c258210a9ef9e54824", "git_parents": ["bed7bb8a3a546324be4d1fd31c38e9466d709321"], "node": "2d0a10381c5416d989077949ddee91cb4e0a34ce", "parents": ["da90a06441f8f26533db66a90fafcd0e23276c5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070635 [wpt PR 62529] - [parser] Store stable element identity in adoption agency Bookmark, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[parser] Store stable element identity in adoption agency Bookmark\n\nPreviously, HTMLFormattingElementList::Bookmark stored a raw interior\nEntry* pointer into the HeapVector\u003cEntry\u003e entries_ buffer.\nDuring HTMLTreeBuilder::CallTheAdoptionAgency(), DOM operations (such\nas reparenting the furthest-block in step 4.14) can synchronously\ndispatch events when subtrees are detached, notably the pagehide event\non an iframe. An event listener could then call document.write(),\nre-entering the parser and appending to active formatting elements.\nThis would reallocate the HeapVector and leave the Bookmark's raw\ninterior pointer dangling, leading to a UAF / use-after-poison write\nwhen SwapTo() resumes.\nThis CL fixes the issue by:\n1. Changing Bookmark to store a stable Element* reference instead of\n   an interior Entry* pointer into HeapVector storage.\n2. Updating SwapTo() to resolve elements dynamically via ReverseFind(),\n   failing closed safely if re-entrant script cleared or modified the\n   list.\n3. Removing the step 4.13.4 bookmark-regeneration workaround that\n   existed purely to work around Entry* vector shifts.\n4. Validating that formatting_element and furthest_block remain in\n   OpenElements() after step 4.14 DOM insertion before continuing.\n5. Adding a regression crashtest for re-entrant document.write() via\n   iframe pagehide.\n\nFixed: 557729858\nChange-Id: I337a48aa7c0ad1d7fc0c08380b7df4864cb1cc39\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8363808\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693910}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7108d5cc4493efb6dc8c6b82fc3d91589e0ba9e6\nwpt-pr: 62529\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/crashtests/adoption-agency-custom-furthest-block.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/crashtests/adoption-agency-pagehide-reentrant-write.html"], "git_node": "bd7acb1349035d1e8ec574c9086efa6b0f6c0e7c", "git_parents": ["07fba7c28d491a0ba0b208c258210a9ef9e54824"], "node": "627ff0f73b0536f323adf5007a949af9f0ffd90e", "parents": ["2d0a10381c5416d989077949ddee91cb4e0a34ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070635 [wpt PR 62529] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62529\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/syntax/parsing/crashtests/adoption-agency-pagehide-reentrant-write.html.ini"], "git_node": "6881cfae85ca9faa558498818dadd724386f8f7d", "git_parents": ["bd7acb1349035d1e8ec574c9086efa6b0f6c0e7c"], "node": "a5a625160a2a58e71f3bb93b0dd56924f8f29091", "parents": ["627ff0f73b0536f323adf5007a949af9f0ffd90e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070638 [wpt PR 62538] - [Masonry] Support row spanner fragmentation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Support row spanner fragmentation\n\nRow spanners mostly already worked since they are only laid out in the\nfirst lane they start in, and unlike columns, don't impact breaks in\nsubsequent rows.\n\nHowever, row grid-lanes fragmentation used the immediately preceding\nphysical lane to determine whether a later row should wait for the next\nfragmentainer. A row spanner adds non-start entries to every row it\ncovers, so that lane may appear complete even while the spanner's owning\nlane still has a continuation.\n\nTrack completion only for items that start in each lane, and use the\npreviously processed lane when deciding whether an existing continuation\nwill resume later rows. This keeps row spanners associated with their\nfirst row while allowing independent items in later rows to be processed\nwhen their tracks begin in the current fragmentainer.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: I984981d27098ab42eecd7ea5df63623a04c3dbe9\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8352700\nCommit-Queue: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694076}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7ae93982098471da9c37a180dde9968166aa1a18\nwpt-pr: 62538\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-009.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-010.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-011.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-012.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-013.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-014.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-015.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-016.html"], "git_node": "ed7b9aef510ae3f6c7a452dd05624c9dc1dd50b4", "git_parents": ["6881cfae85ca9faa558498818dadd724386f8f7d"], "node": "eff308edf1deab225c03e5673e3fc07e897a1c75", "parents": ["a5a625160a2a58e71f3bb93b0dd56924f8f29091"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070638 [wpt PR 62538] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62538\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-009.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-010.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-011.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-012.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-013.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-014.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-015.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-016.html.ini"], "git_node": "e2e5f448aecc8949c37adfa994b1fe48442dddd3", "git_parents": ["ed7b9aef510ae3f6c7a452dd05624c9dc1dd50b4"], "node": "27429cf69db2debf8ab757c81745b41664040fb8", "parents": ["eff308edf1deab225c03e5673e3fc07e897a1c75"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070640 [wpt PR 62539] - Fix flaky combined interest/command invoker web tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix flaky combined interest/command invoker web tests\n\nIn interestfor-command-invoker and menubar-interest-command-invoker, an\ninvoker element with both interestfor and command=toggle-popover was\nconfigured with interest-delay: 100ms. When clickOn() runs in automated\ntests, it first dispatches pointer moves over the element. If the\naction sequence takes more than 100ms before dispatching the\npointerdown/up actions, the start delay expired and opens the popover\nvia interest. The subsequent click event triggered the toggle-popover\ncommand on the already-open popover, toggling it closed and causing the\nassertion to fail.\n\nThe tests only need the end delay (interest-delay-end) to be short to\nquickly verify that loss of interest does not close a popover opened\nvia command. Fix this by setting interest-delay to \"1000s 100ms\",\nproviding a large start delay while preserving the 100ms end delay.\n\nFixed: 557681063, 558137248\nChange-Id: I827cab079c8da5c267c0a41157af4eba4a1e9ab0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8373386\nCommit-Queue: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694179}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9386f5829dfcaa0988dad8c4e4813b5012ff4f4a\nwpt-pr: 62539\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-command-invoker.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menubar-interest-command-invoker.tentative.html"], "git_node": "2f200b82dac6b6a3284aa351e7729a2f95c61ffa", "git_parents": ["e2e5f448aecc8949c37adfa994b1fe48442dddd3"], "node": "9ef3a06c64ee469586b9aa5285431e8990bdd6dd", "parents": ["27429cf69db2debf8ab757c81745b41664040fb8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070643 [wpt PR 62537] - [css] Add 'before' keyword to scroll-snap-stop, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css] Add 'before' keyword to scroll-snap-stop\n\nAdd the 'before' keyword to the 'scroll-snap-stop' property, guarded by\nthe CSSScrollSnapStopBefore runtime enabled feature.\n\nAlso update CSSParserFastPaths to recognize 'before' when the runtime\nflag is enabled, and add a tentative web platform test for parsing.\n\nBug: 556233544\nChange-Id: I5b14ebc68dfac83594373266f4e1c51e989553e4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8344868\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694180}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4b2491428345116c0b4d94c5cb6b1467a1f31b81\nwpt-pr: 62537\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/parsing/scroll-snap-stop-before.html"], "git_node": "ac5e05c1558a1ce32df0b5eb904806e11ffe2d7a", "git_parents": ["2f200b82dac6b6a3284aa351e7729a2f95c61ffa"], "node": "4c0b22e760b56226ddee180e811779e5f91e1b1e", "parents": ["9ef3a06c64ee469586b9aa5285431e8990bdd6dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070643 [wpt PR 62537] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62537\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/parsing/scroll-snap-stop-before.html.ini"], "git_node": "f75f90027be78de8797b456d58a34de3e7602efb", "git_parents": ["ac5e05c1558a1ce32df0b5eb904806e11ffe2d7a"], "node": "b11b771d944661d03541564e285e2a6f2f25f7b8", "parents": ["4c0b22e760b56226ddee180e811779e5f91e1b1e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Euclid Ye \u003cyezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070646 [wpt PR 62513] - wpt: Make more `touch-action` pointerevents tests work under 800x600, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nmake more pointerevents `touch-action` tests work with 800x600\n\nSigned-off-by: Euclid Ye \u003cyezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0f3d7adfe0b0f8cebd7e911363f8810aec2a133b\nwpt-pr: 62513\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/pointerevent_touch-action-inherit_child-pan-x-child-pan-x_touch.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/pointerevent_touch-action-none-css_touch.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/pointerevent_touch-action-pan-down-css_touch.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/pointerevent_touch-action-pan-left-css_touch.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/pointerevent_touch-action-pan-right-css_touch.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/pointerevent_touch-action-pan-up-css_touch.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/pointerevent_touch-action-pan-x-css_touch.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/pointerevent_touch-action-pan-x-pan-y-pan-y_touch.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/pointerevent_touch-action-pan-y-css_touch.html"], "git_node": "ab36e4cb66788522c669f44d97ab4df8d45b00b6", "git_parents": ["f75f90027be78de8797b456d58a34de3e7602efb"], "node": "825fca4bf49f523a8d63689b7e512eb3501f1f20", "parents": ["b11b771d944661d03541564e285e2a6f2f25f7b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1977508 [wpt PR 53779] - Fix #51279: HTTP/2 port should be configured like any other port, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix #51279: HTTP/2 port should be configured like any other port\n\nThis makes HTTP/2's port configuration comparable to the WebTransport\nover HTTP/3 server, while still obeying the command line flags.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 28c0e0b8a87f9d9775a3adef3ba596a30a47b98b\nwpt-pr: 53779\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/serve/serve.py"], "git_node": "9a9eabcced3d276180fdbcff942ec4a6bd761a66", "git_parents": ["ab36e4cb66788522c669f44d97ab4df8d45b00b6"], "node": "d8e2eda2f399d8fbf40ab33de03ac1c3e63039b4", "parents": ["825fca4bf49f523a8d63689b7e512eb3501f1f20"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060691 [wpt PR 61730] - Fix Android Emulator install/startup on macOS, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDrop unneeded logging.basicConfig() calls, already handled within wpt.py\n\n--\nRaise on HTTP errors when downloading Android SDK cmdline-tools\n\ndownload_and_extract() never checked the HTTP status code, so a 404\n(or any other error) response body was written to disk and handed to\nunzip, producing an opaque \"End-of-central-directory signature not\nfound\" failure instead of the actual cause.\n\n--\nFix macOS Android SDK cmdline-tools download using wrong OS tag\n\n`platform.system().lower()` returns \"darwin\" on macOS, matching the\nsupported OS check, but then the actual tag matching used \"macosx\",\ncausing it to silently fall through to the Linux cmdline-tools zip. To\navoid this, we rearrange the conditions to make the unsupported\nplatform error the fallback and not a separate branch.\n\nThe tag, had it ever been returned, was also wrong: the pinned\ncmdline-tools version uses \"mac\".\n\n--\nFix Android emulator setup crashing when ANDROID_USER_HOME is set\n\nandroid.py previously set ANDROID_SDK_HOME, intending it as \"the SDK\nis installed here\", but that isn't what it is: ANDROID_SDK_HOME is the\nlegacy (Android Studio \u003c= 4.3) variable for the prefs/AVD root, not\nthe SDK install location.\n\nThis becomes even worse if ANDROID_USER_HOME is set in the user's\nenvironemnt: if ANDROID_USER_HOME and ANDROID_SDK_HOME are both set\nbut point at different paths, avdmanager ends up outputting the\nconfusing and hard to action message \"Can't locate Android SDK\ninstallation directory for the AVD .ini file\".\n\nThus, all we need to actually do is set ANDROID_SDK_ROOT, the variable\nthat actually means what its name suggests.\n\n--\nPre-create the AVD directory before running avdmanager create avd\n\navdmanager only honors ANDROID_AVD_HOME as the AVD directory if that\ndirectory already exists on disk, thus the the AVD lands somewhere\nandroid.py does not expect, leading to start-android-emulator being\nunable to find it.\n\n--\nInstall a native arm64 Android image on arm64 hosts\n\nNormalize CPU arch names to match canonical forms expected by\nmozrunner and the Android emulator; mozrunner expects Firefox's\ncanonical build-config CPU name, and on macOS where uname returns\n\"arm64\" and not \"aarch64\" it fell through to the 32-bit \"arm\" AVD.\n\nThe Android emulator's QEMU2 backend requires the AVD system image to\nmatch the host architecture, thus we also add and install\nAVD_MANIFEST_ARM64 (arm64-v8a system image, mozemulator-arm64 AVD) on\narm64 hosts instead.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ed83091d791ef609b6aee574ebdf3c5a9e88409a, fd0a3fddff8490663c62b96c4cc37c08691ced24, 006e8ac86a1f56c5280eb31beb03952fc328491e, 2c53cd1bd03686cef080cdfc46c966e15869e782, 703cb532d9edd1637ceb03b7fc7c12420206c788, a7a7685c5c075830b999e1d0cd1277902abe4c0f\nwpt-pr: 61730\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/android.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/commands.json"], "git_node": "a31d9a717ceb88187ff20729c8ef46e261702e8b", "git_parents": ["9a9eabcced3d276180fdbcff942ec4a6bd761a66"], "node": "ad71752c19e37a0ad84481a5155ce58ec58fa293", "parents": ["d8e2eda2f399d8fbf40ab33de03ac1c3e63039b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070654 [wpt PR 62482] - [WebAudio] Add tests and baseline failure for unaligned looping, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebAudio] Add tests and baseline failure for unaligned looping\n\nThis is Part 1 of a 2-part CL addressing crbug.com/553218226.\n\nThis CL introduces test coverage for looping AudioBufferSourceNodes\nacross boundary conditions, refactors the test suite using a factory\nand generator paradigm to reduce boilerplate, and checks in the baseline\nfailure for unaligned buffer looping:\n\n1. audiobuffersource-loop-continuous.html:\n   WPT test covering multi-cycle looping of unaligned buffer lengths\n   (65,201 frames) and grain duration boundaries.\n\n2. audiobuffersource-loop-continuous-expected.txt:\n   Captures the existing trunk failure where frame 65,200 is duplicated\n   and frame 0 is skipped upon wrap.\n\n3. AudioBufferSourceHandlerTest:\n   - Refactored test fixture to AudioBufferSourceHandlerTestBase with\n     shared ProcessOnAudioThread helper returning std::array.\n   - Introduced CreateAudioBuffer generator helper and\n     CreateEnvironmentWithBuffer factory helper, cutting boilerplate.\n   - LoopOffsetBeyondLoopEndPositiveRate: Tests clamping when\n     offset \u003e= loopEnd.\n   - LoopOffsetBelowLoopStartPositiveRate: Tests intro playback before\n     loopStart.\n   - LoopSingleSampleBuffer: Tests 1-sample buffer looping without\n     division by zero.\n   - LoopInvertedBoundsFallbackToWholeBuffer: Tests fallback to whole\n     buffer when loopStart \u003e= loopEnd per W3C \u00a71.15.3.\n   - LoopNegativeRateBackwardWrap: Tests backwards looping with negative\n     playbackRate, including boundary wrap back to loopEnd.\n   - LoopingUnalignedBufferFractionalLoopEndInterpolation: Tests\n     fractional loopEnd interpolation.\n   - DISABLED_LoopingUnalignedBufferPrecision: Reproduction of\n     bug 553218226, to be re-enabled in Part 2.\n   - DISABLED_LoopingUnalignedBufferExplicitLoopEnd: Tests explicit\n     loopEnd = buffer.duration, to be re-enabled in Part 2.\n   - DISABLED_LoopingGranularityWrapPrecision: Granularity matrix\n     reproduction in AudioBufferSourceGranularityTest, to be\n     re-enabled in Part 2.\n   - DISABLED_VaryingRatesInterpolatedWrapPrecision: Rate 0.5 wrap\n     reproduction, to be re-enabled in Part 2.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=dcf17c2a-023a-4313-a7d5-deba45eca250\n\nBug: 553218226\nTest: external/wpt/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audiobuffersourcenode-interface/audiobuffersource-loop-continuous.html\nTest: out/Release/blink_unittests --gtest_filter=\"*AudioBufferSource*\"\nChange-Id: I4262acd240362268b5a1dff20b8c6721e3c2d8bb\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8333135\nReviewed-by: Michael Wilson \u003cmjwilson@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694250}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9eac876da93ec14a01a1633087c15d4430330013\nwpt-pr: 62482\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audiobuffersourcenode-interface/audiobuffersource-loop-continuous.html"], "git_node": "5844804a83589c35331e27720081cdea5d30b79f", "git_parents": ["a31d9a717ceb88187ff20729c8ef46e261702e8b"], "node": "3e0cae962d83dc1a8eef7356e787d64beef01f00", "parents": ["ad71752c19e37a0ad84481a5155ce58ec58fa293"], "tags": []}, {"author": "BruceDai \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070656 [wpt PR 62541] - webnn: allow 0-D output for gather operator, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebnn: allow 0-D output for gather operator\n\nThis CL updates the minimum allowed rank of gather's output to 0 in\nrequired_datatypes_ranks.json by executing the script\ntools/generate-required-datatypes-ranks.py, per Spec change [1].\n\nNo new conformance tests are needed: the existing conformance tests\nand validation tests already exercise the 0-D output path.\n\n[1] Spec change: https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webnn/pull/953\n\nChange-Id: If127608d7e5cf80a402e0544169e9fa67237d66c\nBug: 557288874\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8361354\nAuto-Submit: Dai, Feng \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Hu, Ningxin \u003cningxin.hu@intel.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Reilly Grant \u003creillyg@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hu, Ningxin \u003cningxin.hu@intel.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694279}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fadb01bc53cd4a9fac9352c977df1787425b856e\nwpt-pr: 62541\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/resources/required_datatypes_ranks.json"], "git_node": "8c89ce89e3a8b3d4167479d998e94fad5a311c91", "git_parents": ["5844804a83589c35331e27720081cdea5d30b79f"], "node": "902d66c103f79f1052e2cfdd6fec2cd4ef437d4d", "parents": ["3e0cae962d83dc1a8eef7356e787d64beef01f00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "chicoxyzzy \u003cchi187@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070863 [wpt PR 62352] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322115, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322115\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3fa23e3dda225639447aeadbeeb73f5445a6e999\nwpt-pr: 62352\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/webapi/esm-integration/exported-names.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/webapi/esm-integration/resources/js-wasm-cycle.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/webapi/esm-integration/wasm-js-cycle.tentative.html"], "git_node": "f2f3eb9cea89ba9e762c7e6dba417a6b1bab962d", "git_parents": ["8c89ce89e3a8b3d4167479d998e94fad5a311c91"], "node": "6361ab4438ad627d650330bb79c230193739e5ac", "parents": ["902d66c103f79f1052e2cfdd6fec2cd4ef437d4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070878 [wpt PR 62491] - [css-fonts-4] Update palette-mix() tests for recent changes spec changes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-fonts-4] Update palette-mix() tests for recent changes spec changes (#62491)\n\nDiscussed in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14452\n\n- Moved tests into css/css-fonts/parsing\n- Updated computed value tests to include testing values with 1 and more than 2 components.\n- Updated computed value tests to include testing values with interpolation method elided.\n- Updated computed value tests to follow color-mix/CSS Value 5 mix function rules.\n- Added specified value tests (palette-mix-valid.html)\n- Added invalid value tests (palette-mix-invalid.html)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3a1177e6c76f1a7f854f3ae4b93a00835e171fad\nwpt-pr: 62491\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/palette-mix-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/parsing/palette-mix-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/parsing/palette-mix-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/parsing/palette-mix-valid.html"], "git_node": "2f4def44b876350e4678cb4b2cee054cbb284bd3", "git_parents": ["f2f3eb9cea89ba9e762c7e6dba417a6b1bab962d"], "node": "7c5322218e0e02844e645c73aa28ce32e50746e3", "parents": ["6361ab4438ad627d650330bb79c230193739e5ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070878 [wpt PR 62491] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62491\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-fonts/palette-mix-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-fonts/parsing/palette-mix-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-fonts/parsing/palette-mix-valid.html.ini"], "git_node": "25e8ea5dbe9eb3835dd6bc5facf8ca12dd69dd47", "git_parents": ["2f4def44b876350e4678cb4b2cee054cbb284bd3"], "node": "6e202dd5c89653b57301f411265c312361a47321", "parents": ["7c5322218e0e02844e645c73aa28ce32e50746e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070907 [wpt PR 62531] - [compression-dictionary] Tweak server to follow RFC9842's \"Vary\" header requirement, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[compression-dictionary] Tweak server to follow RFC9842's \"Vary\" header requirement\n\nOur tests currently add \"Vary\" headers to some resources in order to\nmake sure the test server fulfills the minimal requirement of\nhttps://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9842#section-6.2. However, this\nis not done for `compressed-data.py`, so fix that. Note that\nfetch/compression-dictionary/resources/static/Makefile adds that header\nbut in general the script might not properly merge the headers when\na compressed output is later used as a dictionary, so add a comment about\nto clarify that.\n\nBug: 522338661, 40255884\nChange-Id: I6be14f7418cce81b4fafeecb2510dc4aaca9ade3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8163980\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694354}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f27884313681660c06919a389a9bba1d23bfbdd9\nwpt-pr: 62531\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/resources/compressed-data.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/resources/static/Makefile"], "git_node": "49c296050459601bcf4b3fc319389310dec1addf", "git_parents": ["25e8ea5dbe9eb3835dd6bc5facf8ca12dd69dd47"], "node": "e735b910affc6f4997414aeb6d21109e2fe7b958", "parents": ["6e202dd5c89653b57301f411265c312361a47321"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070910 [wpt PR 62536] - [scroll-axis-lock] Add basic tests for inheritance/animation., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[scroll-axis-lock] Add basic tests for inheritance/animation.\n\nAdd tests to cover initial value, inheritance and discrete animation\ntype. Also add test for the invalid value \"proximity\" that was initially\nconsidered in an early proposal.\n\nBug: 479472367\nChange-Id: I109114965e2e312aacb263f157f73f347a722930\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8352984\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694355}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cdba7c5a8588cfe67dfc2156704f8b074d76170b\nwpt-pr: 62536\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/parsing/scroll-axis-lock-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock-inheritance.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock-interpolation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock.html"], "git_node": "17a31fe0a6e962bb7a41d2e2250d470ef9bd65e8", "git_parents": ["49c296050459601bcf4b3fc319389310dec1addf"], "node": "fad54974525a4ee0f6be2d9506bf83c8fa48323d", "parents": ["e735b910affc6f4997414aeb6d21109e2fe7b958"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070910 [wpt PR 62536] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62536\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock-inheritance.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock-interpolation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-in-display-none-column-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "96588ccb45e0e31dd1c568691424e8e230092516", "git_parents": ["17a31fe0a6e962bb7a41d2e2250d470ef9bd65e8"], "node": "06aff915099f8e3e1fd959f5e6786fb2edd8e666", "parents": ["fad54974525a4ee0f6be2d9506bf83c8fa48323d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras Tenorio \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070916 [wpt PR 62543] - [gap-decorations] Fix crash with huge row gaps, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[gap-decorations] Fix crash with huge row gaps\n\nWhen a row-gap offset saturated during grid fragmentation (due to a\nvalue higher than LayoutUnit::Max), the spillover calculation could\nproduce an incorrect adjustment, due to the saturation hiding the true\ndistance past the edge. The adjustment persisted in the break token,\nwhich corrupted later fragments and led to a null dereference.\n\nSkip the adjustment when the gap offset is saturated. The difference\ncannot be represented safely, and suppressing it avoids corrupting\nsubsequent fragments. Add a regression crash test.\n\nFixed: 542066231\nChange-Id: I0489c0990f26ac3541397a90aff28790f57a0323\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8349009\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694366}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 30e0b7899c8b1988d81296397413100f504d2651\nwpt-pr: 62543\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-038-crash.html"], "git_node": "760fe1c453e0fd1d99bb0a2909561e32d5e426d5", "git_parents": ["96588ccb45e0e31dd1c568691424e8e230092516"], "node": "f63df25d4dfa18b355cd304121d5de187705ba22", "parents": ["06aff915099f8e3e1fd959f5e6786fb2edd8e666"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Felipe Erias \u003cfelipeerias@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070921 [wpt PR 62542] - [CSS] Support smooth text-decoration-thickness transitions, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[CSS] Support smooth text-decoration-thickness transitions\n\nCSS Text Decoration requires `text-decoration-thickness` to animate by\ncomputed value:\n\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-decor-4/#text-decoration-thickness-property\n\nHowever, `text-decoration-thickness` was missing from both\nLengthPropertyFunctions::GetLength() and `transition: all`,\nso text thickness changed immediately instead of transitioning.\n\nLengthPropertyFunctions::GetLength() extracts the value of\n`text-decoration-thickness` from the computed style into a `Length`,\nunless that value is `from-font`. Both `from-font` and `auto` keep\nanimating discretely.\n\nMark the property interpolable so it participates in `transition: all`.\n\nTests:\n  external/wpt/css/css-text-decor/animations/text-decoration-thickness-interpolation.html\n  external/wpt/css/css-text-decor/animations/discrete-no-interpolation.html\n\nBug: 361393675\nChange-Id: Ic16c7077570ca242d61e6122a143256ad4acf242\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8335028\nCommit-Queue: Felipe Erias \u003cfelipeerias@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694368}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 047b14a0c3401e88571ef853942a6ea7581e4aef\nwpt-pr: 62542\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/animations/discrete-no-interpolation.html"], "git_node": "fb622640e648cc54576aa11319b3a59e0c75f45e", "git_parents": ["760fe1c453e0fd1d99bb0a2909561e32d5e426d5"], "node": "f73ae3b8dde15d9377e7376e9907deb6f0361067", "parents": ["f63df25d4dfa18b355cd304121d5de187705ba22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070931 [wpt PR 62560] - Mark XML fragments' scripts as already started., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMark XML fragments' scripts as already started.\n\nHTML spec says: \"If the parser was created as part of the XML fragment\nparsing algorithm, then the element's already started must be set to true.\"\nThis CL does that. Also adds a test.\n\nBug: 542115030\nChange-Id: Id3925fb343a8919d0c8f9dba7f71ccce31ec41c5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8356066\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694473}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 56cbcaa233de2a233884ccfe07f6e626cc70a6c3\nwpt-pr: 62560\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing-xml-fragments/innerHTML-already-started.html"], "git_node": "40b874626b6343ab174eff754b1f6e4a35d99f22", "git_parents": ["fb622640e648cc54576aa11319b3a59e0c75f45e"], "node": "a5446e533bdd52d8b7561e2f07ea6f83136c1582", "parents": ["f73ae3b8dde15d9377e7376e9907deb6f0361067"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Romain Menke \u003c11521496+romainmenke@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070939 [wpt PR 62549] - [css-color] fix fuzzy color tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-color] fix fuzzy color tests (#62549)\n\n* [css-color] fix fuzzy color tests\n\n* fmt\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 26c986aeff1d15dd441ccf7e5fdb9aa07f0ce50b\nwpt-pr: 62549\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-none.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-powerless.html"], "git_node": "20c4c1ce4d2926b24b808032814b9ec7cf49fc5c", "git_parents": ["40b874626b6343ab174eff754b1f6e4a35d99f22"], "node": "bf84c2fcc8c8bebd0dae4bbfc1cfe3fb645a96b3", "parents": ["a5446e533bdd52d8b7561e2f07ea6f83136c1582"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070939 [wpt PR 62549] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62549\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-none.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-powerless.html.ini"], "git_node": "616d45ed9863e96d881c99a6e8d117b37afe8be0", "git_parents": ["20c4c1ce4d2926b24b808032814b9ec7cf49fc5c"], "node": "3d11be7fc53a9d1675de8c06f1a0bf4047b9f392", "parents": ["bf84c2fcc8c8bebd0dae4bbfc1cfe3fb645a96b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "br