desc": "Bug 2058821 - doc: apply the markdownlint fixes over the tree r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ipc-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,releng-reviewers,android-reviewers,bhearsum,nchevobbe,ahal,tcampbell DONTBUILD\n\nMostly mechanical: `markdownlint-cli2 --fix` over the directories the md\nlinter covers (blank lines around fences and lists, list indentation, bare\nURLs wrapped in angle brackets, stray spaces inside code spans).\n\nA few spots needed to be fixed by hand because they were malformed in the\nfirst place: reference links left dangling by the RST conversion in\nipc/docs/ipdl.md and devtools/docs/user/debugger-api/index.md, an `{image}`\ndirective whose options had escaped the fence in\ndocs/contributing/debugging/capturing_minidump.md, and text where a literal\nasterisk or underscore was being parsed as emphasis.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315001\n", "files": ["devtools/docs/contributor/preferences.md", "devtools/docs/user/debugger-api/index.md", "devtools/docs/user/settings/index.md", "docs/ai-agent-tools/firefox-devtools-mcp.md", "docs/bug-mgmt/processes/accessibility-review.md", "docs/bug-mgmt/processes/security-approval.md", "docs/contributing/debugging/capturing_minidump.md", "docs/gtest/index.md", "docs/performance/bestpractices.md", "docs/performance/dtrace.md", "docs/performance/memory/heap_scan_mode.md", "docs/performance/profiling_with_xperf.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/ads_client.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/autofill.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/breach_alerts.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/context_id.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/filter_adult.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/init_rust_components.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/logins.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/relevancy.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/remote_settings.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/search.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/suggest.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/sync15.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/tabs.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/tracing.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/viaduct.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/webextstorage.md", "docs/rust-components/developing-rust-components/index.md", "docs/rust-components/developing-rust-components/uniffi.md", "dom/docs/handling_shadowDOM.md", "gfx/docs/AsyncPanZoom.md", "ipc/docs/ipdl.md", "mobile/android/fenix/docs/Firebase-Cloud-Messaging-for-WebPush.md", "mobile/android/fenix/docs/architecture-overview.md", "mobile/android/focus-android/docs/UI-Test.md", "modules/libpref/docs/index.md", "taskcluster/docs/platforms.md", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/src/templates/api-doc.md", "tools/moztreedocs/docs/mdn-import.md"], "git_node": "e173c24599a3524be313b5828c606870ae0d1980", "git_parents": ["b14ad10e3f7593276d59cede793ffbdd4b3a7a11"], "node": "6eb6a63ad9fdfdc1829ded43c96699e93186748e", "parents": ["54705c210097444e94a73f886799c4c2b484967a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066697 - Quote file-bug.py arguments in the bug-filing skill r=ai4dev-reviewers,padenot DONTBUILD\n\nUnquoted field=value arguments break when the value contains shell glob\ncharacters, e.g. a see_also URL with a query string.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325257\n", "files": [".agents/skills/bug-filing/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/bug-filing/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "d489e02a8c4db6de67cd50612c3123fd594e2cc7", "git_parents": ["e173c24599a3524be313b5828c606870ae0d1980"], "node": "a95b024e62172a2d0eff9c36725ec0ffaf796876", "parents": ["6eb6a63ad9fdfdc1829ded43c96699e93186748e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ruhollah Majdoddin \u003cr.majdodin@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065751 - Advertise the Escape shortcut in the find bar's close button tooltip while the bar has focus. r=mstriemer,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nThe find bar's close button tooltip is only \"Close find bar\", so nothing in\nthe UI says that Escape closes the bar.\n\nEscape is handled by a capturing keypress listener on the find bar element\nitself, so it only closes the bar while focus is inside it. Following bug\n1199929, the shortcut is advertised only while that holds: the tooltip\nswaps between two Fluent ids as focus enters and leaves the bar.\n\nThe key name is hardcoded rather than looked up.\nShortcutUtils.getKeyString(\"VK_ESCAPE\") would read it from\nkeys.properties, but that table has no per-platform variant and would\ngive capital \"Esc\" on macOS, where the existing Escape strings use\nlowercase, and .properties is a legacy format. { $shortcut } does not\napply either -- there is no \u003ckey\u003e element here, and this Escape\nhandling is not remappable.\n\nThis work was done with AI assistance; I have reviewed and can explain\nevery line.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320643\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_findbar.js", "toolkit/content/widgets/findbar.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/main-window/findbar.ftl"], "git_node": "186a3b9047b2d3a92365465dfda8f80e58241c7e", "git_parents": ["d489e02a8c4db6de67cd50612c3123fd594e2cc7"], "node": "4e6b6e1dc72a02d112887f3ee25e74cc6ecd4838", "parents": ["a95b024e62172a2d0eff9c36725ec0ffaf796876"], "tags": []}, {"author": "any1here \u003cany1here@duck.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070378 - Hide Manage AI and Labs quick actions when disabled by preference or policy r=urlbar-reviewers,Standard8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324472\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/QuickActionsLoaderDefault.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-quickactions/browser_general.js"], "git_node": "367638bee9e61114e01755ff59c55d548adda36d", "git_parents": ["186a3b9047b2d3a92365465dfda8f80e58241c7e"], "node": "64ee6392356c5aede6a67329ca281fee3889e65f", "parents": ["4e6b6e1dc72a02d112887f3ee25e74cc6ecd4838"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071118: Fix interruptRegexp for PBL r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325200\n", "files": ["js/src/irregexp/RegExpShim.h", "js/src/jit-test/tests/regexp/bug1697077.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/regexp/interrupt-regexp-and-fail.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/regexp/interrupt-regexp-with-gc.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/regexp/interrupt-regexp-with-nested-regexp.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/regexp/interrupt-regexp-with-regexp.js"], "git_node": "065193d6071c92ad9c1e8311a35460639b7b5b4c", "git_parents": ["367638bee9e61114e01755ff59c55d548adda36d"], "node": "16ff791f588bfb9dba3ad691fddf2ebc99509c76", "parents": ["64ee6392356c5aede6a67329ca281fee3889e65f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070973 - Wait until after promise is resolved to clear scheduling state r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325060\n", "files": ["dom/webscheduling/WebTaskScheduler.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/scheduler/tentative/yield/yield-inherit-across-promises.any.js"], "git_node": "70abc663a860d26b6d7faab3971d1c7f31463a28", "git_parents": ["065193d6071c92ad9c1e8311a35460639b7b5b4c"], "node": "729f5dabb3d9cc46972c941928d868525293a9ca", "parents": ["16ff791f588bfb9dba3ad691fddf2ebc99509c76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071261 - Quote the Norwegian locale tag in the speech recognition model mapping. r=media-webspeech-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nYAML reads a bare `no` as false, so the multilingual model's supported_locales\ndeclared \"False\" instead of \"no\": a key the model's prompt dictionary does not\nhave, offered to language negotiation as if it were a tag. Requesting it\nnegotiated fine and then failed in parakeet_capi_stream_begin_lang. This\nwas failing to set an explicit language, and falling-back to\nautodetection, which wasn't intended.\n\ngen_speech_models.py now rejects a non-string locale rather than stringifying\nwhatever YAML handed it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325362\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/gen_speech_models.py", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/models.yaml"], "git_node": "477e1f9b546f99ba5d0f95af4cf9038bce1daf8a", "git_parents": ["70abc663a860d26b6d7faab3971d1c7f31463a28"], "node": "42efe2e219543a94fbe4c590abe5be8b313e11cf", "parents": ["729f5dabb3d9cc46972c941928d868525293a9ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sarah Clements \u003csclements@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065486 - Update illustration for sync disconnected state in sidebar r=fxview-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,nsharpley,emilio\n\n* Add asset property for sync error map and consolidate the getMessageCardForState logic\n* Remove height and width from new svgs so they scale\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321595\n", "files": ["browser/components/firefoxview/SyncedTabsController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/firefoxview/firefox-view-synced-tabs-error-handler.sys.mjs", "browser/components/firefoxview/tests/browser/browser_syncedtabs_errors_firefoxview.js", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar/kit-page-history.svg", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar/kit-qr-tabs-devices-empty.svg", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar/kit-tabs-devices-error.svg", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar/kit-tabs-devices.svg"], "git_node": "d89caae212e8f862dad014f2d0d9d6c416f1aa0d", "git_parents": ["477e1f9b546f99ba5d0f95af4cf9038bce1daf8a"], "node": "f541b4b344ebad23404b5e44e8118580676ab55c", "parents": ["42efe2e219543a94fbe4c590abe5be8b313e11cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071106 - Part 1: Request an input trust authority for a clear lead video stream. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nBug 2022030 Part 5 (D287632) made `IsEncrypted()` return false on the clear\nlead segment to reflect the real encryption status. That function also tells\nMedia Foundation whether the stream needs the protected media path, which a\nclear lead still does because the encrypted part follows in the same stream.\n\nThe video descriptor was therefore marked `MF_SD_PROTECTED`, but the\n`IMFInputTrustAuthority` Media Foundation asked for while resolving the\ntopology was refused with `MF_E_NOT_PROTECTED`. It cannot resolve a protected\nbranch without one, so the topology failed with `MF_E_TOPO_UNSUPPORTED`.\nReverting this makes clear lead PlayReady streams play on Netflix again.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325208\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFMediaEngineVideoStream.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFMediaEngineVideoStream.h", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFMediaSource.cpp"], "git_node": "2f0d4e5ac5134b04567ba0699cc8a0942090e36d", "git_parents": ["d89caae212e8f862dad014f2d0d9d6c416f1aa0d"], "node": "2f661f65d1ced7bdfdb1f0e77daa892d5942bc65", "parents": ["f541b4b344ebad23404b5e44e8118580676ab55c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071106 - Part 2: Add a pref to disable the protected activation recovery, off by default. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nWhen activation failed with `MF_E_TOPO_UNSUPPORTED` or\n`MF_E_INCOMPATIBLE_SAMPLE_PROTECTION` we re-drove the protected pipeline\nthrough the hardware-context-reset path, which closes every session with\nreason `hardware-context-reset`. Per the EME specification that invites the\napplication to create new sessions and retry, so a conformant player retries\nindefinitely. Netflix reported this as repeated `F7717-1273 (unexpected\nhardware-context-reset)`.\n\nNeither error is documented as transient. Microsoft publishes no guidance for\neither code, and Chromium, which drives the same Media Engine and PlayReady\npath, treats both as terminal and reserves hardware-context-reset for\n`DRM_E_TEE_INVALID_HWDRM_STATE` alone. The retry could not have helped in any\ncase, because `ExternalEngineStateMachine::SetCDMProxy` does not re-send the\nCDM proxy to the recreated engine, so the new engine never sets its media\nsource and never builds a topology.\n\nThe mechanism is left in place behind a pref so this can be flipped back on a\nrelease branch if disabling it regresses something. Removing it belongs in a\nfollow-up.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325209\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFProtectedPathReadinessMonitor.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/gtest/TestMFProtectedPathReadinessMonitor.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "c0682d0a705005ec89c3420b70002a64be9fbe52", "git_parents": ["2f0d4e5ac5134b04567ba0699cc8a0942090e36d"], "node": "42620182869f3f678ee2002e546e77af44fd9a67", "parents": ["2f661f65d1ced7bdfdb1f0e77daa892d5942bc65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071106 - Part 3: Log the image size and encryption state of the media engine setup. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nThe metadata log reported only the display size, and the media source summary\nreported neither size, so both now carry the image and display size.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325210\n", "files": ["dom/media/ExternalEngineStateMachine.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/MFMediaEngineParent.cpp"], "git_node": "3dee287405fcbcab5ad61a2ce73a6ba89dc6d463", "git_parents": ["c0682d0a705005ec89c3420b70002a64be9fbe52"], "node": "2831fb683e7db9a52472c9d92747d77eab44e4cf", "parents": ["42620182869f3f678ee2002e546e77af44fd9a67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071106 - Part 4: Test that a clear lead stream is granted an input trust authority. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nAdds TestMFMediaSourceProtection, which builds an MFMediaSource the way\nMFMediaEngineParent does and drives IMFTrustedInput against a mock CDM.\n\nThe failure this covers needs SL3000 hardware DRM and a licence server, so it\ncannot be reached from a mochitest, but we can test it on gtest.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325211\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/gtest/TestMFMediaSourceProtection.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "767274e9d69ecb011addba36230949cd159126c8", "git_parents": ["3dee287405fcbcab5ad61a2ce73a6ba89dc6d463"], "node": "38e64a410fb0ac00a73e2923339e3a179e212aea", "parents": ["2831fb683e7db9a52472c9d92747d77eab44e4cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068811 - Add newtab nova launch message strings r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324452\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "f88ffead06f622bc88e78948b61cc69942d64670", "git_parents": ["767274e9d69ecb011addba36230949cd159126c8"], "node": "659a65271f080ed6968403ab199c859c1a56a519", "parents": ["38e64a410fb0ac00a73e2923339e3a179e212aea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066474 - Restore selected checkmark on lists widget switcher menu. r=maxx\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321275\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Lists/Lists.jsx"], "git_node": "7494a82306da54ae5beca9d8f317322f3c652b97", "git_parents": ["f88ffead06f622bc88e78948b61cc69942d64670"], "node": "843155ca8ee99b215cc92db5ed993962bc3899f5", "parents": ["659a65271f080ed6968403ab199c859c1a56a519"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071208 - Make sure recent searches widget can be enabled by Nimbus. r=maxx\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325331\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsRegistry.test.jsx"], "git_node": "d6f561d0061af7965598166bf16dfd9212c9f3b6", "git_parents": ["7494a82306da54ae5beca9d8f317322f3c652b97"], "node": "71f7c8ff5d85dd59ee1c629544f22ec5d879f646", "parents": ["843155ca8ee99b215cc92db5ed993962bc3899f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070838 - Don't report a speech recognition session stopped during init as an error. r=media-webspeech-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nBringing the engine up takes as long as loading the model's weights, so stop()\ncan land while the session is still initializing. The engine's abandoned init\nthen reached the page as \"network\", instead of the nomatch and end that\nstopping a session owes it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324937\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_parakeet_stop_during_init.html"], "git_node": "0d8a98b84c657fceb042598861b8413ea3997bfe", "git_parents": ["d6f561d0061af7965598166bf16dfd9212c9f3b6"], "node": "e9867b7a4750924ad368877bb9ffc9dee34422a8", "parents": ["71f7c8ff5d85dd59ee1c629544f22ec5d879f646"], "tags": []}, {"author": "jsimplicio \u003cjsimplicio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054561 - Message bar spec update for Nova r=desktop-theme-reviewers,mkennedy,translations-reviewers,thecount,nordzilla,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311913\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/nova/_tokens.scss", "browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/preferences/preferences.css", "toolkit/components/translations/content/about-translations.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/infobar.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.tokens.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/nova/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/nova/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/nova-export-clean-variables.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/info-bar.tokens.json"], "git_node": "4c91297a52ff28cc4b8d190020e006e4f2bffdc6", "git_parents": ["0d8a98b84c657fceb042598861b8413ea3997bfe"], "node": "cae76fac36c8340238c07dfdb9725ced3141740d", "parents": ["e9867b7a4750924ad368877bb9ffc9dee34422a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062847 - Let the android-gradle-build python tests use non-shippable artifact builds r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThe android-gradle-build python tests run artifact builds, but\n`mach artifact install` only searches the `.shippable` index for opt\nbuilds. For each of the 50 candidate pushheads it looks up\n`gecko.v2.autoland.shippable.revision.\u003crev\u003e.mobile.android-\u003carch\u003e-opt`.\nShippable Android builds aren't scheduled by default on autoland, so when\nnone of the last 50 autoland pushes ran a shippable build, the search\ncomes up empty, fails with \"no built artifacts found\", and every\nartifact-build test in the suite fails at once. It passes only when one\nof those 50 pushes happens to have a shippable Android build, which is\nwhy it shows up as an intermittent.\n\nAdd a MOZ_ARTIFACT_ALLOW_NON_SHIPPABLE environment variable that makes\nthe index lookup fall back to the regular per-push opt build when no\nshippable build is found, and set it for the android-gradle-build task.\nThe shippable index is still tried first, so branches that only publish\nshippable builds (central, beta, release, esr) keep resolving to those.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324866\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifacts.py", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/python-android.yml"], "git_node": "e10bbf0dae2f5c6033f99ccfb3edc0476ddf0dd4", "git_parents": ["4c91297a52ff28cc4b8d190020e006e4f2bffdc6"], "node": "9a8f3f568ec859e5c15c466d4ac3b5ce64dcc811", "parents": ["cae76fac36c8340238c07dfdb9725ced3141740d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035575 - Add a `duplicate` transform to copy another kind's tasks with overrides r=ahal,taskgraph-reviewers\n\nManually duplicating every task definition produced by a kind lets the copy\ndrift as the source changes. Test variants already avoid this for a single\ntest task, but a difference compiled into artifacts needs a separate build of\nevery task it affects.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320191\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docs/attributes.md", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/python.toml", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_duplicate.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/duplicate.py"], "git_node": "115df1170bdb67b6523bfd5c19473c322654a874", "git_parents": ["e10bbf0dae2f5c6033f99ccfb3edc0476ddf0dd4"], "node": "015bf8c0f76e63ef5ec7e97ab7940cd38696f586", "parents": ["9a8f3f568ec859e5c15c466d4ac3b5ce64dcc811"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moyin \u003cmadeyemi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064846 - Calculate the duration of a piece of article r=android-reviewers,matt-tighe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324962\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/synthesis/AudioFormatInfo.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/synthesis/SpeechRate.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/synthesis/AudioFormatInfoTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/synthesis/SpeechRateTest.kt"], "git_node": "af13762c4c1e7ebd836bdea629e166fb1180051b", "git_parents": ["115df1170bdb67b6523bfd5c19473c322654a874"], "node": "3e8efe73c8a5ceb2e94bb0460dc74f833617f965", "parents": ["015bf8c0f76e63ef5ec7e97ab7940cd38696f586"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adham-A \u003c57870101+Adham-A@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1985986 - Fix RTL glyph ink overflow measurement for contained glyphs. r=layout-reviewers,jfkthame\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324373\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFont.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/shaping/shaping-000.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/shaping/shaping-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/shaping/shaping-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/shaping/shaping-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/shaping/shaping-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/rtl-glyph-extents-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/rtl-glyph-extents.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/support/fonts/generate-rtl-ink-overflow.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/support/fonts/rtl-ink-overflow.ttf", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/support/rtl-glyph-extents.css"], "git_node": "ea6b888b0b8aa968ade17700c79e06170f77ac58", "git_parents": ["af13762c4c1e7ebd836bdea629e166fb1180051b"], "node": "e7bf54ef6d2463216c43233e6cc38b6a354d477a", "parents": ["3e8efe73c8a5ceb2e94bb0460dc74f833617f965"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071205 - Fix SVGPathSegment API r=emilio,webidl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325320\n", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGAnimatedPathSegList.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGAnimatedPathSegList.h", "dom/svg/SVGPathElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGPathElement.h", "dom/svg/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/svg/test/test_getPathSegmentAtLength.html", "dom/svg/test/test_getPathSegmentAtLength_with_d_property.html", "dom/svg/test/test_pathAnimInterpolation.xhtml", "dom/webidl/SVGPathElement.webidl", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/path/interfaces/SVGPathSegment.svg.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-css-d-vs-attribute.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-during-smil-animation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-during-web-animation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/path/interfaces/setPathData-malformed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/path/interfaces/setPathData-mutation-observer.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/path/interfaces/setPathData-overrides-d.html.ini"], "git_node": "cdabea1dc908e604182ad0f463692f244d5d54c0", "git_parents": ["ea6b888b0b8aa968ade17700c79e06170f77ac58"], "node": "4c09f582943b007ceaede1526d4c7ccd4d7e77cf", "parents": ["e7bf54ef6d2463216c43233e6cc38b6a354d477a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071252 - Fix browser search metrics.yaml to use literal rather than block scalar headers for descriptions for better formatting. r=search-reviewers,scunnane\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325354\n", "files": ["browser/components/search/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "59030f02670135419938f10f8d0975cccdb8858b", "git_parents": ["cdabea1dc908e604182ad0f463692f244d5d54c0"], "node": "108080e4c4855ca43aec8a406f2a6c38d2719eb7", "parents": ["4c09f582943b007ceaede1526d4c7ccd4d7e77cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071252 - Fix urlbar metrics.yaml to use literal rather than block scalar headers for descriptions for better formatting. r=urlbar-reviewers,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325355\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "7bd194b64b8b297a288a84790fd7b793a32486a1", "git_parents": ["59030f02670135419938f10f8d0975cccdb8858b"], "node": "bc3050d1f0e1f1bef53e84178011eef362e95a07", "parents": ["108080e4c4855ca43aec8a406f2a6c38d2719eb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037691: Support arm64 in SIMD.h r=jandem\n\nClaude wrote the first draft of this quite a while ago. I went through and eyeballed that it looked mostly like the existing x86 implementation, and there are reasonable justifications for the differences. In particular, the difference between _mm_movemask_epi8 (which produces a 16-bit result with 1 bit per SIMD lane) and NeonMovemask (which produces a 64 bit result with 4 bits per SIMD lane) explains why we have (eg) `orMask & 0xf` vs `orMask & 0xffff` in Check4x4Chars. Note also that x86 support for sizeof(TValue) == 4 and sizeof(TValue) == 8 is only available in SIMD_avx2.cpp, whereas arm64 supports all sizes unconditionally.\n\nI didn't spend much time reviewing the correctness of the underlying algorithms; I did that a lot for the initial landing, and we haven't had any problems with the x86 version, so I think we should be fine as long as the translation is right.\n\nI also had a fresh instance of Claude review the patch. The main interesting point from its review was that our memchr implementation is competing against hand-tuned libc implementations. On x86 our primary competition is the Windows C runtime, which is (IIUC) less aggressively optimized, so Alex's benchmarking in bug 1776013 eventually convinced us that we should use our own memchr. That might not be true here. CI results were inconclusive, leaning if anything towards the default memchr being fastest. I'm conservatively disabling SIMD::memchr for now.\n\nCodex's review didn't find anything else.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325185\n", "files": ["mozglue/misc/SIMD.cpp", "mozglue/misc/SIMD.h"], "git_node": "b9c3e085ff5be51502f464ccf6a1c2255dacecdd", "git_parents": ["7bd194b64b8b297a288a84790fd7b793a32486a1"], "node": "9abaf09cc90219151df93b58bd5d46bb601dd264", "parents": ["bc3050d1f0e1f1bef53e84178011eef362e95a07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070562 - about:addons default and AMO curated nova themes preview should follow the current OS light/dark mode. r=willdurand\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324746\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/aboutaddons-utils.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/theme-preview.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_html_themes_picker.js"], "git_node": "b80046bff037863a5d6afb09184c41de21c0aa35", "git_parents": ["b9c3e085ff5be51502f464ccf6a1c2255dacecdd"], "node": "07bf242f2c6137dfd62ba2d841cd2ce0fbcd0564", "parents": ["9abaf09cc90219151df93b58bd5d46bb601dd264"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067259 - Rework the criteria used to determine whether font-family names are quoted. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis reflects the decision in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5846,\nand expectations of some recent WPTs (see later patch updating metadata).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325334\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-family-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/font-family-serialization-001.html"], "git_node": "11750f08e266e97699c656ba876d6b9555a98689", "git_parents": ["b80046bff037863a5d6afb09184c41de21c0aa35"], "node": "624c15f5c76c03b886de63e769b523446f554540", "parents": ["07bf242f2c6137dfd62ba2d841cd2ce0fbcd0564"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067259 - When FamilyName is used for font names in src:local(), force its syntax to be Quoted. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nAlthough the spec seems a little unclear on this IMO, it matches the behavior of both Chrome and Safari,\nand is what css/css-fonts/font-family-src-quoted.html asserts:\nhttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/59ff8a4854a8d2d32ca0dc113760f2aaad70f4b5/css/css-fonts/font-family-src-quoted.html#L7\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325335\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/font_face.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/font-family-src-quoted.html"], "git_node": "9b5381db886516a1a0b676b6576dcf929a32742a", "git_parents": ["11750f08e266e97699c656ba876d6b9555a98689"], "node": "94da3427b48aa913bc234ed2444362ac49e9389b", "parents": ["624c15f5c76c03b886de63e769b523446f554540"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067259 - Update WPT metadata to reflect revised behavior. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nMostly we're passing a bunch more tests now. The only \"new\" failure is because we don't implement\nthe ui-* generics, and therefore don't force things like (quoted) \"ui-serif\" to retain String syntax.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325337\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-font-loading/fontface-css-connected-descriptors.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-family-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-family-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-fonts/variations/font-weight-matching-installed-fonts.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom/font-family-serialization-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom/serialize-values.html.ini"], "git_node": "2d8ea0cf9bf0a949ee641fd71a37dadf1edf409f", "git_parents": ["9b5381db886516a1a0b676b6576dcf929a32742a"], "node": "805593f719e0b08f7e783a6c02340012fac5de99", "parents": ["94da3427b48aa913bc234ed2444362ac49e9389b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067259 - Update mochitest expectations for revised font-family quoting behavior. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325338\n", "files": ["layout/style/test/test_font_face_parser.html", "layout/style/test/test_font_family_serialization.html"], "git_node": "df98b6d9d51f31da65c27639fcf3567a50160c89", "git_parents": ["2d8ea0cf9bf0a949ee641fd71a37dadf1edf409f"], "node": "5a2fbb5721bdda95f6612b6cadb77a552ca0fdbd", "parents": ["805593f719e0b08f7e783a6c02340012fac5de99"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2036256: Add test r=jonco\n\nI'm not sure how bad the bug is, so I'm putting the test in a separate patch just in case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297931\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug2036256.js"], "git_node": "cf52112a2b7fb83213c959a3c30099fb7d36132a", "git_parents": ["df98b6d9d51f31da65c27639fcf3567a50160c89"], "node": "f624a5e13e8a474f2bc72ee80376b38813d6882a", "parents": ["5a2fbb5721bdda95f6612b6cadb77a552ca0fdbd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeff Muizelaar \u003cjmuizelaar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068188 - Use a string-literal wrapper type for simple payload marker field names. r=bas,profiler-reviewers,canova\n\nThis avoids the need to create the `defined_name_##arg` constants which will\nlet us add support for named arguments using string literals. It's also\nsimpler.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322682\n", "files": ["tools/profiler/public/ProfilerMarkers.h"], "git_node": "721c564be40c728278020553980161ef0ae9b0d1", "git_parents": ["cf52112a2b7fb83213c959a3c30099fb7d36132a"], "node": "4262a7edef542a2984cb799f705c8777c7758672", "parents": ["f624a5e13e8a474f2bc72ee80376b38813d6882a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070911 - Give the event listener category expander an accessible name, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nbutton.event-listener-expand holds only an arrow image, so it had no accessible\nname and nothing exposed whether its category was open. Name it after the\ncategory text shown beside it and add aria-expanded. head.js clicks this button\non every toggleEventBreakpoint(), which is what put \"Interactive elements must\nbe labeled\" behind the two Bug 1849028 annotations retired here. The tracer\nsidebar's Bug 1924435 skip also fails on the tree defect, so Bug 2070909\nretires that one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325021\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/components/shared/EventListeners.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_af.toml"], "git_node": "638fd537f9efc3f7b4e168951b653c20399b85d1", "git_parents": ["721c564be40c728278020553980161ef0ae9b0d1"], "node": "8623c429dbb26a7df0923b81566f4293db8e6cca", "parents": ["4262a7edef542a2984cb799f705c8777c7758672"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1814093 - [devtools] Re-enable browser_dbg-watchpoints.js, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nDisabled for a `selectSource` timeout in Bug 1814093, and forward-ported as the\nBug 2028047 arm of the same skip. While it reported nothing, Bug 1911054 renamed\n`getSelectedInlinePreviews` and dropped an `await`, and Bug 1843320 added a\nlocation line to the \"why paused\" panel.\n\nThe test also clicks source tree and scopes rows, which are not reachable from\nthe accessibility API until Bug 2070909, so it is annotated for a11y_checks\nuntil that lands and removes the annotation.\n\n`rightClickObjectInspectorNode` waited for an object inspector node count change\nthat a right click never causes, so its poll ran on until shutdown holding the\ntoolbox window, which the window-leak check reports; it now only opens the menu.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325029\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-watchpoints.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_qz.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/shared-head.js"], "git_node": "cc84399405805f3a63a9bb8ec1a660ed0de5d8ca", "git_parents": ["638fd537f9efc3f7b4e168951b653c20399b85d1"], "node": "dbc96f54160a3f288d796633464de59b9a99956e", "parents": ["8623c429dbb26a7df0923b81566f4293db8e6cca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070955 - Let the variable preview popup's object tree manage focus, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nObjectInspector turns focusable: false into onFocus: null, and Popup.js is its\nonly caller, so no item in the popup's tree ever becomes focused and\nTree._onKeyDown returns on its first line: a role=\"tree\" that a click focuses and\nevery key ignores. Bug 2070909 names an active descendant only on a tree that\nmanages focus, so the popup's rows satisfy the keyboard focusability check only\nonce both have landed; Bug 2070909 removes the four annotations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325022\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/components/Editor/Preview/Popup.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-preview.js"], "git_node": "cf40a6341581b7c4e59c6aab8981c886c4fdb42f", "git_parents": ["cc84399405805f3a63a9bb8ec1a660ed0de5d8ca"], "node": "28916995ee79a4a5e77402b9ca3ed7ef0095af11", "parents": ["dbc96f54160a3f288d796633464de59b9a99956e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1985564 - Stop expecting the wrapped line to be exactly six line heights tall, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nThe long line wraps over five rows on mac and Windows and six on Linux, so\nbrowser_dbg-preview-wrapped-lines.js perma-failed on both and was turned off as\nflaky. What it tests is the previews on a wrapped line, so it only needs to\nknow that the line wrapped; pinning the font does not make the count portable,\nwhich D262814 measured with Ahem. The test drags the split box splitter, which\nis not keyboard operable until Bug 1860733, so the fail-if that was sitting\ncommented out is now live and Bug 1860733 removes it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325027\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-preview-wrapped-lines.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_gp.toml"], "git_node": "e5e3a5b9cd2f20caac6164b7fac963d5b556cc3a", "git_parents": ["cf40a6341581b7c4e59c6aab8981c886c4fdb42f"], "node": "8a76a9f5e0a3728bb8d6eefd2d47bac81364628c", "parents": ["28916995ee79a4a5e77402b9ca3ed7ef0095af11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063316: Add tests for CheckCompatibility and download ping generation. r=nika\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320428\n", "files":