vert \"Bug 2053678 part 3 - Remove dead code for handling Ion post write barriers. r=iain\"\n\nThis reverts commit ecf18b29efb90c1e61ea27a40caec9daa30e4e43.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053678 part 2 - Use a MIR pass for inserting post write barriers. r=iain\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9842f02e9295488eb4a667e25fdf4284dec45432.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053678 part 1 - Rename MIR needsBarrier_ flags to needsPreBarrier_. r=iain\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7883828ae458ecba0d30ed913e70b0b3eb44af0c.\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/Ion.cpp", "js/src/jit/IonAnalysis.cpp", "js/src/jit/IonAnalysis.h", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.h", "js/src/jit/ScalarReplacement.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpCacheIRTranspiler.cpp"], "git_node": "11229eb0d835aba359653b41aeca59f991ea1fa1", "git_parents": ["adfe26ebb671a2b7c860fe49ac02682750ce0fd1"], "node": "810d319dfb717e4d74c853f476c9f79303acb321", "parents": ["22220685dce79d81f904197c14e202472d8ab0e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070537 - Restore StoreName on marker types that lost it when they were migrated to BaseMarkerType. r=canova,profiler-reviewers\n\n- TimerMarker and AddRemoveTimerMarker, migrated in Bug 2040410\n  (105b050a1ece).\n- LogMarker, migrated in Bug 2022540 (62c1ad5e7db6).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324624\n", "files": ["tools/profiler/public/ETWTools.h", "xpcom/base/Logging.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TimerThread.cpp"], "git_node": "adc274c21198e7dd69a6c2d3c6a410d7ce76bb14", "git_parents": ["11229eb0d835aba359653b41aeca59f991ea1fa1"], "node": "ce6bbfef5793b0d019757aa2e970f11a329ffa3f", "parents": ["810d319dfb717e4d74c853f476c9f79303acb321"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jakub Stasiak \u003cjakub@stasiak.at\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1719394 - Preserve early WebSocket frames. r=devtools-reviewers,necko-reviewers,kershaw,jdescottes\n\nFrames can be delivered before webSocketOpened reaches the DevTools\nwatcher. Carry the HTTP channel ID on every frame callback so those\nframes can be associated immediately instead of being discarded.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320711\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/test/file_ws_early_backend_wsh.py", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/websockets/browser.toml", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/websockets/browser_net_ws-early-connection.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/websockets/html_ws-early-connection-page.html", "devtools/server/actors/resources/websockets.js", "devtools/server/tests/xpcshell/test_websocket_watcher.js", "devtools/server/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "dom/websocket/tests/test_websocket_frame.html", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/PWebSocketEventListener.ipdl", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerChild.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventService.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventService.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/nsIWebSocketEventService.idl", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts"], "git_node": "ff6a772594c7b43fbf06cf81dd36b734c6b25023", "git_parents": ["adc274c21198e7dd69a6c2d3c6a410d7ce76bb14"], "node": "0ba5a6dc22402bbb81d000f32fcfc219ba06afd4", "parents": ["ce6bbfef5793b0d019757aa2e970f11a329ffa3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jakub Stasiak \u003cjakub@stasiak.at\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1719394 - Remove WebSocket connection map. r=devtools-reviewers,necko-reviewers,jdescottes,kershaw\n\nD320711 makes the HTTP channel ID available without consulting the\nWebSocket connection map for frame notifications. Carry the ID on close\nnotifications as well so the DevTools watcher can remove that map.\n\nDepends on D320711.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324117\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/resources/websockets.js", "dom/websocket/WebSocket.cpp", "dom/websocket/tests/test_websocket_frame.html", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/PWebSocketEventListener.ipdl", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerChild.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventService.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventService.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/nsIWebSocketEventService.idl", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts"], "git_node": "37266c1ac0e3440704215a11613f640f19389fd3", "git_parents": ["ff6a772594c7b43fbf06cf81dd36b734c6b25023"], "node": "53e05637fde107a13c24cbf20ddac1ac0e1023b2", "parents": ["0ba5a6dc22402bbb81d000f32fcfc219ba06afd4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071683 - Fix broken links in the accessibility documentation r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,Jamie DONTBUILD\n\nThe Architecture page pointed at a DocAccessible creation anchor that no\nlonger matched its heading, and the mochitest-plain FAQ link used a .html\ntarget where the source file is .md.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325692\n", "files": ["accessible/docs/Architecture.md", "accessible/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "b6a4abae5308c210052655bf86cc3de353529b45", "git_parents": ["37266c1ac0e3440704215a11613f640f19389fd3"], "node": "9094a45c80184d9f5f81b1da88ae9f9e1b5a9f8f", "parents": ["53e05637fde107a13c24cbf20ddac1ac0e1023b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071683 - Point the Rust build docs at the writing and testing Rust pages r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nBoth links were relative paths with no extension, which MyST cannot\nresolve.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325694\n", "files": ["build/docs/rust.md"], "git_node": "dff9b3078ad5e17ac87444b01f91c31d898cd473", "git_parents": ["b6a4abae5308c210052655bf86cc3de353529b45"], "node": "522ba0333e2e74dcd8396cc144bf5cd22c011a70", "parents": ["9094a45c80184d9f5f81b1da88ae9f9e1b5a9f8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071683 - Document the anchor rules in the documentation skill r=ai4dev-reviewers,suhaib DONTBUILD\n\nMost of the warnings fixed in this bug were anchors written by hand against the\nslug myst_heading_anchors generates, which deletes punctuation rather than\nreplacing it. Also covers the two checks that disagree about which anchors\nexist, scoping an allowed_warnings entry, why substitutions do not survive an\neval-rst block, and which pages are generated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325715\n", "files": [".agents/skills/documentation/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/documentation/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "d6f01f6e9282c3ab4cd8168e0069f0cd095f4f3f", "git_parents": ["dff9b3078ad5e17ac87444b01f91c31d898cd473"], "node": "921133d29c8686e8f4f89576dc2df0820fadd53b", "parents": ["522ba0333e2e74dcd8396cc144bf5cd22c011a70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071683 - Fix broken links in the remote documentation r=webdriver-reviewers,whimboo DONTBUILD\n\nThe geckodriver link needed the index.md it points at, and the automatic\nlinting anchor is now the heading slug.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325701\n", "files": ["remote/doc/CodeStyle.md", "remote/doc/marionette/CodeStyle.md", "remote/doc/marionette/index.md"], "git_node": "4ac1c9c8c5ec3bf3881e8d1f661f40c6e8a970dc", "git_parents": ["d6f01f6e9282c3ab4cd8168e0069f0cd095f4f3f"], "node": "d2121a27ade494ddae24deee7b7ed68f0f299abc", "parents": ["921133d29c8686e8f4f89576dc2df0820fadd53b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070755 - Use xorps for SSE zeroing idioms on x86 r=jandem\n\nThe self-XOR zeroing idioms differ only in encoding length: pxor and xorpd\ncarry a 66 prefix that xorps does not, so xorps zeroes an xmm register in\nthree bytes where the other two need four. XOR is typeless -- the mnemonic\nsuffix picks an execution domain, not a result -- and all three self forms\nwrite the same 128 zero bits, leave the upper YMM/ZMM bits and the flags\nalone, and raise no exceptions. Every core since Sandy Bridge and Bulldozer\nrecognizes all three at rename time, so no uop executes and the\ninteger-versus-float domain question never arises.\n\nSwitch every self-form site the x86-shared macroassembler and code\ngenerator emit: zeroDouble, the SIMD inline helpers, splatX16, the\nunsigned float-to-int conversions, unsignedWidenHighInt32x4 and the wasm\nall-true reduce-and-branch. That covers the vxorpd in\nunsignedTruncSatFloat64x2ToInt32x4 as well. The AVX encodings are all the\nsame length, so this only changes the legacy encoding the assembler picks\nwhen src0 equals the destination. The data-XOR sites keep pxor: those\nreally execute, and routing them through the float domain between integer\nconsumers can cost bypass latency on older cores.\n\nThe wasm SIMD codegen tests pinned the old mnemonic, and two of their\nexpectations carried comments deferring the choice of mnemonic -- one asking\nfor xorps, the other for xorpd. Zeroing has no domain to match, so both\nare answered here, and both comments go.\n\nAn x86lint survey of a full JetStream 3 run counts 14,974 \"suboptimal SSE\nzero idiom\" sites before this change and none after (Ion 14,514, Baseline\n457, Other 3): every legacy self-XOR the JIT emits is now the three-byte\nform. On a deterministic Richards+DeltaBlue+Crypto workload the category\ngoes 26 -\u003e 0 and Baseline shrinks by exactly 17 bytes -- its 17 findings,\none byte each -- at an unchanged instruction count.\n\nFound via x86lint.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324808\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/simd/const-x64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/simd/cvt-x64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/simd/neg-abs-not-x64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/simd/reduce-x64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/CodeGenerator-x86-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/MacroAssembler-x86-shared-SIMD.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/MacroAssembler-x86-shared-inl.h", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/MacroAssembler-x86-shared.h"], "git_node": "5af34b122e9c79505059e35b2792099abbcf42f8", "git_parents": ["4ac1c9c8c5ec3bf3881e8d1f661f40c6e8a970dc"], "node": "2a7fbc2ee7162e090b2d9de35ed0e6966e6b6732", "parents": ["d2121a27ade494ddae24deee7b7ed68f0f299abc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071527 - Make JS_UNINITIALIZED_LEXICAL the first JSWhyMagic value. r=jandem\n\nThe JITs materialize MagicValue(JS_UNINITIALIZED_LEXICAL) at every TDZ\ncheck and every lexical slot initialization; it is by far the most\nmaterialized magic Value (51,062 sites in one JetStream 3 run on arm64,\nagainst 10,213 for JS_IS_CONSTRUCTING and 1,453 for JS_ELEMENTS_HOLE,\nwhich held payload 0 before this change).\n\nOn ARM64 the constant's cost depends on its payload. With payload 9 a\nstore needs a three-instruction movz/movk chain and a compare needs\nthat chain plus the cmp. With payload 0 the value has 47 trailing\nzeros, so a store needs two instructions and vixl folds a compare into\na single movn plus a shifted-register cmp:\n\n  mov  x16, #9                       mov  x16, #-0xb\n  movk x16, #0x8000, lsl #32    -\u003e   cmp  x2, x16, lsl #47\n  movk x16, #0xfffa, lsl #48\n  cmp  x2, x16\n\nMeasured on a JetStream 3 run with an instrumented shell, the 18,785\nTDZ compares (Baseline 11,201, Ion 7,584) each lose two instructions\nand the 32,277 stores and pushes each lose one; the 4,400 hole\ncompares and stores that move the other way cost about 7K back, for a\nnet of roughly 60K fewer JIT instructions (about 240KB) per run.\n\nNothing depends on the enumerators' numeric values: whyMagic() and\nMagicValue() go through the enum, the JS_WHY_MAGIC_COUNT offsets used by\nArgumentsObject and the Ion recover machinery are unchanged, and the gdb\npretty-printer reads the enum from debug info. Full debug jit-tests pass.\n\nFound with armlint.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WsnsqJvQCmPUe3GWmsM77Q\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325572\n", "files": ["js/public/Value.h"], "git_node": "a3fed8650ef71cc4aabd9472a93342e759a53331", "git_parents": ["5af34b122e9c79505059e35b2792099abbcf42f8"], "node": "9ebeddbe6b55444f8e2369929717ede903e1f1df", "parents": ["2a7fbc2ee7162e090b2d9de35ed0e6966e6b6732"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071530 - [mips64] Port D313940 to mips64. r=jseward\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325576\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/mips-shared/CodeGenerator-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/MacroAssembler-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/MacroAssembler-mips-shared.h"], "git_node": "b3360322ed44adcf0e4e6445464608a78f8141ac", "git_parents": ["a3fed8650ef71cc4aabd9472a93342e759a53331"], "node": "e111ea2ccd6c8deb2ff53f84a6689cc722140cb9", "parents": ["9ebeddbe6b55444f8e2369929717ede903e1f1df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071530 - [loong64] Port D313940 to loong64. r=jseward\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325575\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/CodeGenerator-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.h"], "git_node": "c9e6413b7a973957df56f217627d6c04936c457b", "git_parents": ["b3360322ed44adcf0e4e6445464608a78f8141ac"], "node": "9af5eaa9850c0ce887e2c12da533b6e1072e07db", "parents": ["e111ea2ccd6c8deb2ff53f84a6689cc722140cb9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789380801, "git_changesets": ["a2aa1f4bc58a40bc11e228e6d1e3aa3e062f35af", "eb161faade83590917d5725e244b8537f6946001", "bdd5cf9106982b1f77289ecda1a2ec700d657250", "616fc3496f70afb99ee8e0a1caa2ff1cfd52427e", "be1400a6c2e3d4a8f69d206bb66ecafb011891bc", "638e7c695938206ea95fed8984ea10bfa392488c", "5a2bdaf2b5a46434be0dc72ba78928e0fd92ccd8", "3de5e7f93770e1db5a888a8de5d3b460109d8879", "92b7c0614ff117a55e59efefa6dfa469de0d020b", "d7973ff41988a12f498cde0a1e8fb21fa3b7c28f", "8b01cbd53910c9afe432d125a4f27438ff735ad6", "7883828ae458ecba0d30ed913e70b0b3eb44af0c", "9842f02e9295488eb4a667e25fdf4284dec45432", "ecf18b29efb90c1e61ea27a40caec9daa30e4e43", "66ede4498be5ab829ecc8321ab29761168559d74", "ddb5a3c0706ba6337b79709667729fd382e40057", "2f48d963212733d04678d019356c406f27e792f7", "c39c8bf49ae4da21baab037c218037763e75779c", "adfe26ebb671a2b7c860fe49ac02682750ce0fd1", "11229eb0d835aba359653b41aeca59f991ea1fa1", "adc274c21198e7dd69a6c2d3c6a410d7ce76bb14", "ff6a772594c7b43fbf06cf81dd36b734c6b25023", "37266c1ac0e3440704215a11613f640f19389fd3", "b6a4abae5308c210052655bf86cc3de353529b45", "dff9b3078ad5e17ac87444b01f91c31d898cd473", "d6f01f6e9282c3ab4cd8168e0069f0cd095f4f3f", "4ac1c9c8c5ec3bf3881e8d1f661f40c6e8a970dc", "5af34b122e9c79505059e35b2792099abbcf42f8", "a3fed8650ef71cc4aabd9472a93342e759a53331", "b3360322ed44adcf0e4e6445464608a78f8141ac", "c9e6413b7a973957df56f217627d6c04936c457b"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45321": {"changesets": [{"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1719394 - Remove WebSocket connection map. r=devtools-reviewers,necko-reviewers,jdescottes,kershaw\" for causing dt failures @browser_net_ws-early-connection.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 37266c1ac0e3440704215a11613f640f19389fd3.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1719394 - Preserve early WebSocket frames. r=devtools-reviewers,necko-reviewers,kershaw,jdescottes\"\n\nThis reverts commit ff6a772594c7b43fbf06cf81dd36b734c6b25023.\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/test/file_ws_early_backend_wsh.py", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/websockets/browser.toml", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/websockets/browser_net_ws-early-connection.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/websockets/html_ws-early-connection-page.html", "devtools/server/actors/resources/websockets.js", "devtools/server/tests/xpcshell/test_websocket_watcher.js", "devtools/server/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "dom/websocket/WebSocket.cpp", "dom/websocket/tests/test_websocket_frame.html", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/PWebSocketEventListener.ipdl", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerChild.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventService.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventService.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/nsIWebSocketEventService.idl", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts"], "git_node": "478de77eda46abc170cf95a11c484edb2e890650", "git_parents": ["c9e6413b7a973957df56f217627d6c04936c457b"], "node": "cab028bbad37d5f9714de554265cfd9a63580412", "parents": ["9af5eaa9850c0ce887e2c12da533b6e1072e07db"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789380951, "git_changesets": ["478de77eda46abc170cf95a11c484edb2e890650"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45322": {"changesets": [{"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2066020 - Enable SharedSurface_AndroidHardwareBuffer with WebGL on Android r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\" as requested by dev.\n\nThis reverts commit e9d9b51aac5d385bdb8936edda813661a81c1462.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/CanvasRenderer.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "1713b2fe116495380852077e8f7f3618d4380721", "git_parents": ["478de77eda46abc170cf95a11c484edb2e890650"], "node": "980b80614bdd65e23da0d3ba757a68844271f1c6", "parents": ["cab028bbad37d5f9714de554265cfd9a63580412"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789381587, "git_changesets": ["1713b2fe116495380852077e8f7f3618d4380721"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45323": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging f698bd67d5a3a3614e22ee46c8c4517be99cb566 with FIREFOX-ANDROID_157_0b1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "bdfdbb689de520be4229b00e12a7b06639d80404", "git_parents": ["90783c7f985235f6037206718b719c3ea99aa3e2"], "node": "5450dd05d9a30ab0a8dbd0f7f67f4ecc9ef21527", "parents": ["a692ef9b5992455e3a62b82c3b206cf19ff7edd1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789395239, "git_changesets": ["bdfdbb689de520be4229b00e12a7b06639d80404"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45324": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging f698bd67d5a3a3614e22ee46c8c4517be99cb566 with DEVEDITION_157_0b1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "cb67ba687679f8d5f79b57dd60d7c91d108ec88e", "git_parents": ["bdfdbb689de520be4229b00e12a7b06639d80404"], "node": "dd07be33b6b0f64ada10499f1d31f56b47d95781", "parents": ["5450dd05d9a30ab0a8dbd0f7f67f4ecc9ef21527"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789397945, "git_changesets": ["cb67ba687679f8d5f79b57dd60d7c91d108ec88e"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45325": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging f698bd67d5a3a3614e22ee46c8c4517be99cb566 with FIREFOX_157_0b1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "d0bc0447545eb07fdc3bd5ab032e0d2889560db7", "git_parents": ["cb67ba687679f8d5f79b57dd60d7c91d108ec88e"], "node": "352582303be69cbd4f9a386df29225cc8308f7c2", "parents": ["dd07be33b6b0f64ada10499f1d31f56b47d95781"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789398039, "git_changesets": ["d0bc0447545eb07fdc3bd5ab032e0d2889560db7"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45326": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062542 - Sync addresses through the Rust store's bridged engine r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers,sync-reviewers,bdk,markh\n\nSync has to read and write the same store the browser does. Register the two\naddress engines as alternatives on rust.active, so whichever store is serving\nis the one that syncs -- otherwise incoming addresses land where nobody reads\nthem and local ones are never uploaded.\n\nBridgedAddressesEngine is a BridgedEngine, since reconciliation happens inside\nRust. resetLastSync stands in for a bridge method the autofill component\nimplements but does not expose, and FormAutofillTracker is reused rather than\ngiven a Rust-specific counterpart as logins did: it only scores notifications,\nwith no JSON-store change list to get wrong.\n\nApplying inside Rust also means nothing fires formautofill-storage-changed, so\nFormAutofillStatus never refreshes FormAutofill:savedFieldNames and a profile\nthat receives its addresses from sync is offered no autofill until restart. The\nengine announces them itself, once per sync, through a notifySyncApplied() on\nRustAutofillAdapterBase -- that is where the private the announcement needs\nlives after bug 2068865 split the adapter, and credit cards inherit the same\nhook once they have an engine.\n\nSplit out of bug 2058441, which migrates the addresses, so that bug is only\nabout moving the data. rust.enabled is off by default, so no profile serves\nRust while sync still points at JSON.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322610\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_address_bridged_engine.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_address_sync_engine.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "services/sync/modules/service.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillSync.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillAdapterBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillAddressStorage.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "3ea34a236763d366ea1d36c6b33e2e4652dcb31c", "git_parents": ["c9e6413b7a973957df56f217627d6c04936c457b"], "node": "b82b4b357ec3a1eeece575eedf78c23a814f86ff", "parents": ["9af5eaa9850c0ce887e2c12da533b6e1072e07db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Guichard \u003cnicolas.guichard@kdab.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070393 - Skip test_group_checkerboarding.html on Android ccov. r=botond,hiro\n\nThis test times out with the added code coverage overhead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325627\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml"], "git_node": "ecc315895bf2df93804419c9de2e97cf31522bb5", "git_parents": ["3ea34a236763d366ea1d36c6b33e2e4652dcb31c"], "node": "319e7eca987b5ff8c8673afdb8f8f86963b209b6", "parents": ["b82b4b357ec3a1eeece575eedf78c23a814f86ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Guichard \u003cnicolas.guichard@kdab.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070392 - Skip test_cache_eviction.html on Android ccov. r=tnikkel\n\nThis test times out with the added code coverage overhead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325628\n", "files": ["image/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml"], "git_node": "04d22a41e65593280353461b37f1fa298074ae65", "git_parents": ["ecc315895bf2df93804419c9de2e97cf31522bb5"], "node": "aba409181e695a3f2a04ee33765d47f78805df97", "parents": ["319e7eca987b5ff8c8673afdb8f8f86963b209b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abel Kalu \u003c59095867+BlessedOneKobo@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059979 - Fix network monitor opening files in last tab. r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325233\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/src/utils/firefox/open-request-in-tab.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_open_request_in_tab.js"], "git_node": "98ecaa6b7fb77575b5ec0233078034fbedec073f", "git_parents": ["04d22a41e65593280353461b37f1fa298074ae65"], "node": "e474388bb827c9fffeb4d672390042e12b867dd7", "parents": ["aba409181e695a3f2a04ee33765d47f78805df97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071224 - Decide whether to use AA segments based on the device space footprint. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nPreviously the use of AA segments was based on the local space size. If the primitive was scaled down enough that AA segments overlap, it would cause glitches.\nFor now we also compare against the local bounds, because the projected footprint of a thin rotated primitive can be very large (For example wrench/reftests/aa/rotated-line.yaml).\nA better solution would be to compare against a the local rect with only the an extracted scale applied, however this will come after some light refactoring of the quad code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325333\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/quad-huge-scale-down-aa-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/quad-huge-scale-down-aa.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/reftest.list"], "git_node": "32c1275d86356b6e05c79a03435eb085e98e47c7", "git_parents": ["98ecaa6b7fb77575b5ec0233078034fbedec073f"], "node": "2330f3fb4331e213c218129ff9aa70e4fa53a1e0", "parents": ["e474388bb827c9fffeb4d672390042e12b867dd7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johannes Salas Schmidt \u003cjoschmidt@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070129 - Reject instead of hanging when the Rust login store fails to initialize. r=dimi,bdk,theidkamp\n\n`LoginManagerRustStorage.initialize()` created a promise chain without error handling, so anything that threw or rejected inside it left the promise pending forever. `LoginManager._getStorage()` awaits that promise before handing out the backend, so every async login manager call waited on it indefinitely.\n\n`initialize()` is now an ordinary async method whose `try`/`catch` logs and rethrows.\n\nAlso configure the `logins` and `breach_alerts` namespace as `AsyncWrapped` throughout.\n\n`_registerShutdownBlocker()` moves to the start of initialization, before anything is opened. Opening the store hands the JS `PrimaryPasswordAuthenticator` to Rust, and with an awaited constructor there was a window in which the store held it and no blocker was waiting to close it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324279\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/passwordmgr/storage-rust.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/unit/test_storage_rust_shutdown.js", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustLogins.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/config.toml"], "git_node": "06cce60e0bb06d69b30ad3821745f0f7879b2d87", "git_parents": ["32c1275d86356b6e05c79a03435eb085e98e47c7"], "node": "882abb21ca4bb070965e0aaf98e9c57cba440e0b", "parents": ["2330f3fb4331e213c218129ff9aa70e4fa53a1e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053678 part 1 - Rename MIR needsBarrier_ flags to needsPreBarrier_. r=iain\n\nAlso renames `NewUnbarriered` to `NewNoPreBarrier`.\n\nThe `MStoreDynamicSlotFromOffset` constructor had an unused `barrier` argument.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325302\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/IonAnalysis.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.h", "js/src/jit/ScalarReplacement.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpCacheIRTranspiler.cpp"], "git_node": "0b4edc03a3f15af837f044180c6e23cb3c83c82e", "git_parents": ["06cce60e0bb06d69b30ad3821745f0f7879b2d87"], "node": "75d4f0d064dfcbea2c454fa9282dfc64e51812df", "parents": ["882abb21ca4bb070965e0aaf98e9c57cba440e0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053678 part 2 - Use a MIR pass for inserting post write barriers. r=iain\n\nWe implement the post barrier for store instructions as a separate MIR instruction.\nThe store and the barrier should execute as a single unit (no GC or unexpected\nbailout in between) but some optimization passes can move or insert instructions,\nand this makes it hard to reason about these barriers.\n\nWith this patch we insert the post barrier MIR instructions after all optimization\npasses. It avoids the code motion problem and simplifies the code in a number of\nplaces. It also gives us a single place to insert `MAssertCanElidePostWriteBarrier`\nin debug builds.\n\nThis only changes the JS post barriers. Wasm code could probably use the same\nmechanism in the future, but it also has some post barrier code that's more\ncomplicated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325303\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/Ion.cpp", "js/src/jit/IonAnalysis.cpp", "js/src/jit/IonAnalysis.h", "js/src/jit/MIR.h", "js/src/jit/ScalarReplacement.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpCacheIRTranspiler.cpp"], "git_node": "343a86091f8edefffe661ed2a1389d9997db99de", "git_parents": ["0b4edc03a3f15af837f044180c6e23cb3c83c82e"], "node": "b54feb694e5f05941686c6c014d6b9a67cee096c", "parents": ["75d4f0d064dfcbea2c454fa9282dfc64e51812df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053678 part 3 - Remove dead code for handling Ion post write barriers. r=iain\n\nEarlier passes no longer have to handle `MPostWriteBarrier` and `MPostWriteElementBarrier`\nbecause these instructions are now only created after the other MIR optimizations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325304\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/IonAnalysis.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.h", "js/src/jit/ScalarReplacement.cpp"], "git_node": "92e29c819105ed75995c1d7752800751d8a75dd8", "git_parents": ["343a86091f8edefffe661ed2a1389d9997db99de"], "node": "9b9d79baeac172754ebebded55ab2cb4385374b3", "parents": ["b54feb694e5f05941686c6c014d6b9a67cee096c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053678 part 4 - Use ValueNeedsPostBarrier in AddPostWriteBarriers. r=iain\n\nThis also adds a check for `MConstant` to `ValueNeedsPostBarrier`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325305\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/ion/bug2053678.js", "js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/IonAnalysis.cpp", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.h"], "git_node": "8c5c111be7b005251bef6acb11c21af70c5c001b", "git_parents": ["92e29c819105ed75995c1d7752800751d8a75dd8"], "node": "796dd890b86ea41b4fa957f858ae5bef05ccfed9", "parents": ["9b9d79baeac172754ebebded55ab2cb4385374b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070998 - Add blob image instrumentation and SVG activity threshold prefs. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nCount group blobs, fallback blobs, blob pixel area, items painted into\ngroup blobs by type, and group splits by the type of the item that caused\nthem. The counters are reset per display list build and reported as a\n\"WebRender blob images\" profiler marker so that the effect of making more\nSVG items active can be read off a profile.\n\nWhen gfx.webrender.debug.highlight-painted-layers is set, group blobs are\nnow tinted green (fallback blobs keep the red tint) so the two kinds can be\ntold apart.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325070\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.h", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "b6d7f713c4d1e3ebd7c53616953660f94c02a7a4", "git_parents": ["8c5c111be7b005251bef6acb11c21af70c5c001b"], "node": "5709a300bdb72ee87ece018393a9d6aee333b253", "parents": ["796dd890b86ea41b4fa957f858ae5bef05ccfed9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070998 - Make the SVG blob activity thresholds work as documented. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nTwo long standing bugs meant the thresholds in the grouping code never\napplied: ConstructGroups computed isLast with iterator::HasNext(), which is\ntrue for every item the loop visits, so the middle-of-list \"Should\"\nthreshold was never used; and AssessBounds compared the item size in app\nunits against a threshold documented in pixels, so anything wider than about\neight device pixels counted as large. The effective behavior was that every\nitem that could be active was.\n\nisLast is now computed from the next iterator and AssessBounds works in\ndevice pixels.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325071\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "ac2788a57449b163513d144ac0b57fb89b4c9ca9", "git_parents": ["b6d7f713c4d1e3ebd7c53616953660f94c02a7a4"], "node": "11de34f03090da67c434a40f7a71a1ab47713b07", "parents": ["5709a300bdb72ee87ece018393a9d6aee333b253"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070998: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "462f5d210513ec3393d40a0388bd77bb89df9f47", "git_parents": ["ac2788a57449b163513d144ac0b57fb89b4c9ca9"], "node": "7af2b286ab5040815464ca9c5a7cf11abc226d6a", "parents": ["11de34f03090da67c434a40f7a71a1ab47713b07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068590: Report the time since install and update in the new-profile ping. r=jhirsch\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322906\n", "files": ["toolkit/profile/ProfileMetrics.sys.mjs", "toolkit/profile/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_profile_metrics_seconds_since_install.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_profile_metrics_seconds_since_no_files.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_profile_metrics_seconds_since_update.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "363edddb2de800eb50f91a0599f5b829c6ee6e2c", "git_parents": ["462f5d210513ec3393d40a0388bd77bb89df9f47"], "node": "7a95d16ba5f4d54f527703600694cc9234a2f7e7", "parents": ["7af2b286ab5040815464ca9c5a7cf11abc226d6a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988776, part 1 - Use main-thread atomization for observer filters. r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325662\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.cpp"], "git_node": "e7bc47e55ddbafa11db86486100023941f36768c", "git_parents": ["363edddb2de800eb50f91a0599f5b829c6ee6e2c"], "node": "359c2e74b20c8bef5ba0b9e21acde8ff53e5c7d9", "parents": ["7a95d16ba5f4d54f527703600694cc9234a2f7e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988776, part 2 - Check the observer telemetry flag first. r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325663\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.cpp"], "git_node": "c3ff76070416f6fd43f7ac77e725e9f7b7d1c999", "git_parents": ["e7bc47e55ddbafa11db86486100023941f36768c"], "node": "1c44ebe7bfb7aa6a39999b54e9b1e4f4e8d62414", "parents": ["359c2e74b20c8bef5ba0b9e21acde8ff53e5c7d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988776, part 3 - Inline small observer attribute filters. r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325664\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.cpp", "dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.h"], "git_node": "78ad85001bdd2923ecd008483a41c27c6af17356", "git_parents": ["c3ff76070416f6fd43f7ac77e725e9f7b7d1c999"], "node": "f4202d8c0767b32f2af79efce573794debc79fad", "parents": ["1c44ebe7bfb7aa6a39999b54e9b1e4f4e8d62414"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988776, part 4 - Preallocate WebIDL sequences from arrays. r=smaug,spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325665\n", "files": ["dom/bindings/Codegen.py", "js/public/ForOfIterator.h", "js/src/vm/ForOfIterator.cpp"], "git_node": "7b7d92fcff244d45dcd8cc05f27b1bd05db1c836", "git_parents": ["78ad85001bdd2923ecd008483a41c27c6af17356"], "node": "b95716a5cae33571dbe8b775108b4d67e32d5bb3", "parents": ["f4202d8c0767b32f2af79efce573794debc79fad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988776, part 5 - Retain single-object node storage when unbinding. r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325666\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsINode.cpp"], "git_node": "edadb6d10bb189a1889d26a18465a951b6212b0b", "git_parents": ["7b7d92fcff244d45dcd8cc05f27b1bd05db1c836"], "node": "9e5f4a90767f2358389b2bba657cac126b329162", "parents": ["b95716a5cae33571dbe8b775108b4d67e32d5bb3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045801: Expand SitePolicies to support containerized site data. r=bsmth,baku\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323260\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_sitepolicies_container.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_sitepolicies_container.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/ContextualIdentityService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_policy.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/EnterprisePoliciesContent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/EnterprisePoliciesParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/nsIEnterprisePolicies.idl"], "git_node": "c9177aeb6bffe3587128640e4430fc331b898b60", "git_parents": ["edadb6d10bb189a1889d26a18465a951b6212b0b"], "node": "fe41f8396be2dea76c3a736f5c99f84bfff06e13", "parents": ["9e5f4a90767f2358389b2bba657cac126b329162"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yisi \u003cyisibl@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070943 [wpt PR 62501] - Test `w` or `b` components \u003e= 100%, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest `w` or `b` components \u003e= 100% (#62501)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5a5b2b591b39c59d5bca77819db305474dcfd18a\nwpt-pr: 62501\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-hwb.html"], "git_node": "28a8aaf48ce1c77e8b5a3649bb39b849335772aa", "git_parents": ["c9177aeb6bffe3587128640e4430fc331b898b60"], "node": "817a42bb22e859db0b5eb8aaec03499461cf3c79", "parents": ["fe41f8396be2dea76c3a736f5c99f84bfff06e13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070943 [wpt PR 62501] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62501\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-hwb.html.ini"], "git_node": "21ff388860ec725864c24ce91b3280720f33669e", "git_parents": ["28a8aaf48ce1c77e8b5a3649bb39b849335772aa"], "node": "f7c2a4c485bd373fd0ce17d7adedc44c6f9049b0", "parents": ["817a42bb22e859db0b5eb8aaec03499461cf3c79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Watts \u003cleowatts34@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070948 [wpt PR 62533] - xpath: Fix `name`, `local-name` and `namespace-uri` to correctly process attributes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix xpath functions to correctly process attributes\n\nSigned-off-by: Leo Watts \u003cleowatts34@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 953f0dcf78e628290d499fba695a93306cd440d1\nwpt-pr: 62533\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domxpath/fns-name-related.html"], "git_node": "bfd88b88b30c9df0a25e65e2c12b7ef710b3fe78", "git_parents": ["21ff388860ec725864c24ce91b3280720f33669e"], "node": "593baffe152bde24b7941cc9c3952a7a5f9e6ad7", "parents": ["f7c2a4c485bd373fd0ce17d7adedc44c6f9049b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070950 [wpt PR 62523] - VT: Abort transition when scope disconnects or loses LayoutObject., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nVT: Abort transition when scope disconnects or loses LayoutObject.\n\nThis patch ensures that we are robust when the scope disconnects or\nloses the layout object. It reuses the unsupported capture check and\nupdates that a little bit, since any time an unsupported condition\nstarts to apply, we should abort the transition\n\nR=kevers@chromium.org, freedebreuil@google.com\n\nBug: 553293786\nChange-Id: Ic1440216070787d5e1513f5cb6d30dabe67bde9f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8323527\nReviewed-by: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694584}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a2d577976b5e7f9929525a82078497e15adb37db\nwpt-pr: 62523\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/crashtests/element-moved-to-new-document.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/element-moved-to-new-document.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/scope-display-none.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/start-view-transition-on-disconnected-element.html"], "git_node": "fa6622ebfe92550b2742c96927cce958f3931736", "git_parents": ["bfd88b88b30c9df0a25e65e2c12b7ef710b3fe78"], "node": "48f02795fb42b631f79b8510f9a1b9c9ad811eac", "parents": ["593baffe152bde24b7941cc9c3952a7a5f9e6ad7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070950 [wpt PR 62523] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62523\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/crashtests/element-moved-to-new-document.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/element-moved-to-new-document.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/scope-display-none.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/start-view-transition-on-disconnected-element.html.ini"], "git_node": "8d20ec199fb0b43a75934a82e10ca907b858471e", "git_parents": ["fa6622ebfe92550b2742c96927cce958f3931736"], "node": "5f5477d12479ca22f361b7849691d91e65390ed3", "parents": ["48f02795fb42b631f79b8510f9a1b9c9ad811eac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1895406 [wpt PR 46121] - Add lints for lone testharnessreport.js & testdriver-vendor.js, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd TESTHARNESSREPORT-WITHOUT-TESTHARNESS lint\n\nThis checks that testharnessreport.js only occurs when testharness.js\ndoes, as vendor implementations can have unexpected side effects in\nother test types.\n\n--\nAdd TESTDRIVER-VENDOR-WITHOUT-TESTDRIVER lint\n\nThis checks that testdriver-vendor.js only occurs when testdriver.js\ndoes, as vendor implementations can have unexpected side effects.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: df608f1c6d50a1bf9bbfefc4dfa4066d4c6cc841, 940536a0933f83021255f39d0a855c12838c384b\nwpt-pr: 46121\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domxpath/xpath-evaluate-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/editing/other/shadow_root_iteration_in_block_style.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/lint/lint.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/lint/rules.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/lint/tests/test_file_lints.py"], "git_node": "951c6c91162fdea24ad54ee7bbc6b37f3d33ff45", "git_parents": ["8d20ec199fb0b43a75934a82e10ca907b858471e"], "node": "e60393aa6e65ad2b929ceb05c87edc6222cfd581", "parents": ["5f5477d12479ca22f361b7849691d91e65390ed3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1895406 [wpt PR 46121] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 46121\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domxpath/variables-in-expression-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "73ecdb7e9e502bfc2c93d019995788c3b8ba4669", "git_parents": ["951c6c91162fdea24ad54ee7bbc6b37f3d33ff45"], "node": "d7f5ac4ee03e2d4cee2df4938aa287a19d6e5089", "parents": ["e60393aa6e65ad2b929ceb05c87edc6222cfd581"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lia Hiscock \u003cliahiscock@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071040 [wpt PR 62574] - [WebInstallAPI] Resolve relative manifest URLs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebInstallAPI] Resolve relative manifest URLs\n\nResolve manifest URLs supplied through navigator.install() and the\n\u003cinstall\u003e element against the document's base URL. Previously, relative\nvalues were treated as invalid absolute URLs.\n\nBug: 333795265\nChange-Id: Ia0c6c2db6302ad4e512ce0d0c5573c089864c0e8\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8341388\nReviewed-by: Daniel Murphy \u003cdmurph@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Lia Hiscock \u003cliahiscock@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Lu Huang \u003cluhua@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nate Chapin \u003cjaphet@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694773}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d9a4f1961740f2390857dfc58677cd200001b21c\nwpt-pr: 62574\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/web-install/navigator-install-bad-inputs.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "d1157bba5362c3df3447a22e4a3e12527d56ba16", "git_parents": ["73ecdb7e9e502bfc2c93d019995788c3b8ba4669"], "node": "2b6f56505169df0ac65fe4efe7de5e5e22286f71", "parents": ["d7f5ac4ee03e2d4cee2df4938aa287a19d6e5089"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071040 [wpt PR 62574] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62574\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/web-install/navigator-install-bad-inputs.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "aaa51b4082e9ff9226d563c388ebf870ce894bb2", "git_parents": ["d1157bba5362c3df3447a22e4a3e12527d56ba16"], "node": "2e0d03a9f225cb17f3fd95e40dd926f9d0c69ef3", "parents": ["2b6f56505169df0ac65fe4efe7de5e5e22286f71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "taher \u003c8665427+nullhook@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071047 [wpt PR 62580] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323798, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323798 (#62580)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8acb63e4cbe9e031a58a1de81366cdf02af91c9e\nwpt-pr: 62580\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/css-linked-parameters-precedence-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/css-linked-parameters-precedence-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/img-with-url-fragment-identifiers-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/img-with-url-fragment-identifiers-2.html"], "git_node": "fb3f4d7d077dad98a0f9f3ab4686d173aefdeaca", "git_parents": ["aaa51b4082e9ff9226d563c388ebf870ce894bb2"], "node": "c6def116321ba8f7df519878b21fb8af7e32e2a6", "parents": ["2e0d03a9f225cb17f3fd95e40dd926f9d0c69ef3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071052 [wpt PR 62575] - Fix JPEG XL CMYK color conversion, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix JPEG XL CMYK color conversion\n\nDecode the Black extra channel separately and apply the embedded CMYK\nprofile while preserving alpha and existing non-CMYK behavior.\n\nBug: None\nChange-Id: I61b58fbcaee4db7f74db6b2c35bcd6d2836b8d45\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8275513\nCommit-Queue: Luca Versari \u003cveluca@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Luca Versari \u003cveluca@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694782}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ddcca5943fd41232d42149aaa19d9a04c5651b18\nwpt-pr: 62575\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/cmyk-basic-conversion-reftest.html"], "git_node": "7a962fbeccd8e3ea4a690c307ef9f2bf6599ece6", "git_parents": ["fb3f4d7d077dad98a0f9f3ab4686d173aefdeaca"], "node": "0fc451327fc9231e9faf74ccc12a0a020ed41bf5", "parents": ["c6def116321ba8f7df519878b21fb8af7e32e2a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071052 [wpt PR 62575] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62575\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/jpegxl/cmyk-basic-conversion-reftest.html.ini"], "git_node": "225c9f9546353e98e71f44d4ba3fb73d2c0f3f85", "git_parents": ["7a962fbeccd8e3ea4a690c307ef9f2bf6599ece6"], "node": "7ba5d489d8b05cfbb54f79efd93afebd25664d2a", "parents": ["0fc451327fc9231e9faf74ccc12a0a020ed41bf5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071057 [wpt PR 62579] - Make ::interest-button a layout tree sibling of originating element, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake ::interest-button a layout tree sibling of originating element\n\nPreviously, ::interest-button was attached as a layout child and relied\non UA anchor positioning to sit adjacent to its originating element.\nThis prevented it from flowing naturally at the end of multi-line text\n(e.g., wrapped elements).\n\nThis CL attaches ::interest-button as an in-flow layout sibling of its\noriginating element, following the model used by ::scroll-button and\n::scroll-marker-group. The pseudo-element is inserted directly after\nthe originating element in box-tree order and placed under the\noriginating element's layout parent for layout tree attachment. UA\nstyles in html.css are updated from absolute anchor positioning to in-\nflow display: inline-block.\n\nBug: 453705247\nChange-Id: I38b2735c5bb46c367625c66cf05fb8cdf2755eb4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8351847\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1694968}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 15ea54db0ddb4c478fa423f57aeb04acaf21b084\nwpt-pr: 62579\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-abspos-appearance-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-abspos-appearance.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-appearance-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-appearance.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-block-button.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-both-table-display.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-contents-appearance-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-contents-appearance.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-counter-appearance-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-counter-appearance.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-flex-appearance-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-flex-appearance.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-float-appearance-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-float-appearance.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-multiline-link-appearance-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-multiline-link-appearance.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-pseudo-table-display.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-quotes-appearance-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-quotes-appearance.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-table-cell.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/resources/interest-button-styles.css"], "git_node": "ba6632412ec