903626d8ea92a4bea0fca9f7c8f935"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Attard \u003csamuel.r.attard@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071061 [wpt PR 62572] - Compare pointer-valued properties by value in CSSPropertyEquality, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCompare pointer-valued properties by value in CSSPropertyEquality\n\nSeveral properties (scrollbar-color, quotes, marker-*, list-style-type,\nview-transition-name/class, font-feature-settings,\nfont-variant-alternates) were compared with == on a pointer, so two\ncomputed styles built from the same declarations compared unequal and\ntransitions could start between identical values. Use\nbase::ValuesEquivalent() for them.\n\nAlso store nullptr for `font-feature-settings: normal` and no tree scope\nfor the non-overridable list-style-type keywords, so that declared\nvalues compare equal to the corresponding initial/UA values.\n\nBug: 558028324\nChange-Id: Ib3d8efb11c9e507947f2ab304721f668207c06b4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8360638\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Samuel Attard \u003csamuel.r.attard@gmail.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695023}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2b6223e2c8ca580ef20e55c548f1b94e6bb4948d\nwpt-pr: 62572\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/list-style-type-transition-tree-scope-custom-ident.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/list-style-type-transition-tree-scope-keyword.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transitions/no-transition-for-unchanged-pointer-valued-properties.html"], "git_node": "2b78e7a545e252f9d76724a31b3a0bfd9c2d0b4f", "git_parents": ["16dd5ddd952328b5c1c1f13cb50e414beb582072"], "node": "e11c2d3af325e505f02dfa6a19ee2207ad292c06", "parents": ["72698e035a66e895f5fb4acdc69526787fb98e72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071061 [wpt PR 62572] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62572\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-lists/list-style-type-transition-tree-scope-custom-ident.html.ini"], "git_node": "bf9cd0bde9cc9f551c818bd1f33ae3b03bca67f0", "git_parents": ["2b78e7a545e252f9d76724a31b3a0bfd9c2d0b4f"], "node": "051391fad261e78ae4e24c7cf6bec45fcbd1d594", "parents": ["e11c2d3af325e505f02dfa6a19ee2207ad292c06"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071062 [wpt PR 62581] - [HiC] Add tests for onpaint when removing elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Add tests for onpaint when removing elements\n\nVerify that the onpaint event fires when elements are removed from\nthe canvas subtree, and that the event reports the expected set of\nchanged elements.\n\n* When a drawable element is removed, the event fires with an empty\n  changedElement list.\n* When a non-drawable element is removed, the event fires with the nearest\n  drawable ancestor as the changed element.\n\nBug: 417556295\nChange-Id: I9f6b9a2e30c2a7cef5b65d3b2f45b8c0394b3311\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8342807\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695070}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3b73cff907836728aad59b6f6f6edd098986ca3c\nwpt-pr: 62581\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-remove-drawable-element.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-remove-non-drawable-element.tentative.html"], "git_node": "842e20425d98c0c111da62831f9edaef9afb06a0", "git_parents": ["bf9cd0bde9cc9f551c818bd1f33ae3b03bca67f0"], "node": "f82afa73d520ed1bf2ed3f8ea6dc5e25dcbfa1fe", "parents": ["051391fad261e78ae4e24c7cf6bec45fcbd1d594"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071062 [wpt PR 62581] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62581\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-remove-drawable-element.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-remove-non-drawable-element.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "44ec08198086550e1ae19ffbcaedbdd12ca96423", "git_parents": ["842e20425d98c0c111da62831f9edaef9afb06a0"], "node": "24616fd5dec4ed817c54ff6a05bf010cc159642e", "parents": ["f82afa73d520ed1bf2ed3f8ea6dc5e25dcbfa1fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Lee \u003cleolee@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071070 [wpt PR 62540] - Require paste authorization for clipboard format metadata, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRequire paste authorization for clipboard format metadata\n\nRenderer-accessible ClipboardHost methods ReadAvailableTypes() and\nIsFormatAvailable() exposed OS clipboard format metadata without\nbrowser-side paste authorization.\n\nGate these methods with IsRendererPasteAllowed() and return neutral\nvalues when access is denied. Keep GetSequenceNumber() available to\nactive frames because Blink uses its storage-key-partitioned sequence to\nvalidate cached ClipboardItem representations after authorization\nchanges. Add unit and web-platform regression coverage.\n\nBug: 550512266\nChange-Id: If701e398bdbd1fd9f9fd5d5ba94e1cd81c84eb4a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8283983\nReviewed-by: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Leo Lee \u003cleolee@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ana Sollano Kim \u003cansollan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695102}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ed66e8beb8b59ef46aea496a121c0666b746da50\nwpt-pr: 62540\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/clipboard-apis/async-clipboard-cached-getType-permission-revocation.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "91fba87f16ac17675936bc20264e6ad3b9ecf37e", "git_parents": ["44ec08198086550e1ae19ffbcaedbdd12ca96423"], "node": "12d412f906f7d247c7a99ec5a6819d9a99bac24a", "parents": ["24616fd5dec4ed817c54ff6a05bf010cc159642e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071070 [wpt PR 62540] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62540\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/async-clipboard-cached-getType-permission-revocation.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/clipboard-copy-selection-line-break.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/permissions/readText-granted.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "8e4223d05cf2658157c0ff3be435fa0407d02dca", "git_parents": ["91fba87f16ac17675936bc20264e6ad3b9ecf37e"], "node": "19e391419a6fa69897c0ce57802563d82cd12280", "parents": ["12d412f906f7d247c7a99ec5a6819d9a99bac24a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Scott \u003cjamescscott@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071076 [wpt PR 59245] - Refactor Test262 update workflow to move logic to script, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRefactor Test262 update workflow to move logic to script\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5a0093842d7ee2b1cf04bd98f03084e93e88c1ae\nwpt-pr: 59245\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/.github/workflows/update-test262-tests.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/update-test262.sh"], "git_node": "c9f8fafa1520d0e62cfb33672b2b9bf5bb92c12a", "git_parents": ["8e4223d05cf2658157c0ff3be435fa0407d02dca"], "node": "eb7fbb128521cd54d08d21e6703e3ad11752e76a", "parents": ["19e391419a6fa69897c0ce57802563d82cd12280"], "tags": []}, {"author": "wpt-pr-bot \u003cwpt-pr-bot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071078 [wpt PR 62303] - Regenerate WPT certificates, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAutomated regeneration of WPT certificates\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 620df2fcc92e5cdaebb20b659636831f430ca084\nwpt-pr: 62303\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/certs/cacert.key", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/certs/cacert.pem", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/certs/web-platform.test.key", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/certs/web-platform.test.pem", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/browsers/chrome_spki_certs.py"], "git_node": "743c5616d299aa214ae4482f83d6aebc8e275031", "git_parents": ["c9f8fafa1520d0e62cfb33672b2b9bf5bb92c12a"], "node": "f43c032095f300c20cabea87b7183e0642c885cd", "parents": ["eb7fbb128521cd54d08d21e6703e3ad11752e76a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071082 [wpt PR 62563] - Add fuzzy match to object-position-svg reftests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd fuzzy match to object-position-svg reftests\n\nThe pixel differences in these tests come from pixel snapping when\nclipping the image, rather than the object positioning behavior being\ntested.\n\nBug: 40747033\nChange-Id: I3d42063a29d5810a963355b96335242baa543018\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8343367\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695179}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7cb81f04c2c9bf33d8dc2758041754445733ae27\nwpt-pr: 62563\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-position-svg-001i.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-position-svg-001p.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-position-svg-002i.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-position-svg-002p.html"], "git_node": "c6cc12f8d1aa797f9001a311abb8d98b339089e0", "git_parents": ["743c5616d299aa214ae4482f83d6aebc8e275031"], "node": "f71322a8ce407430b4a2010a7563230acd420362", "parents": ["f43c032095f300c20cabea87b7183e0642c885cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fran\u00e7ois Beaufort \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071084 [wpt PR 62582] - [WebMCP] Expose RegisteredTool.inputSchema as an object, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebMCP] Expose RegisteredTool.inputSchema as an object\n\nThis CL updates the WebIDL definition for RegisteredTool.inputSchema\nfrom DOMString to object to align with the WebMCP specification:\nhttps://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp/pull/241\n\nIn Blink, JSONStringToScriptObject() is used in\nModelContext::OnGetScriptToolsCompleted() to parse the mojo string\ninto a ScriptObject when constructing the RegisteredTool results.\n\nWeb platform tests in external/wpt/webmcp/imperative/ are updated to\nexpect inputSchema as a JavaScript object rather than a serialized\nJSON string.\n\nBug: 489045948\nChange-Id: I7cc1a2420b7536bea393871a8060c2816faa6163\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8362703\nReviewed-by: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695175}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c94abb33b8b0d162ab33f259c1dc44724d42f3d3\nwpt-pr: 62582\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/getTools-declarative-schema.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/toolchange-on-control-add-remove.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/exposedTo-cross-origin-child.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/exposedTo-defaults-same-origin.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/exposedTo-multiple-children.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/getTools-imperative-schema.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/resources/helpers.js"], "git_node": "45df747bed25dd06834e000eae4660334edac326", "git_parents": ["c6cc12f8d1aa797f9001a311abb8d98b339089e0"], "node": "a217abe84baf6f8767df3cf709684025b60b8114", "parents": ["f71322a8ce407430b4a2010a7563230acd420362"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071058 [wpt PR 62586] - Incorrect cast to CSSSuperellipseValue, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nIncorrect cast to CSSSuperellipseValue\n\nCSSValue for shape might be an identifier different from 'round'. We did\na cast to CSSSuperEllipseValue which caused a crash.\n\nUse DynamicTo\u003c\u003e instead.\n\nBug: 558810287\nChange-Id: Id647df72ed070a06d650b5cdc4d415e66e6bf41f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8378406\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695245}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c9c2cdd485d4a9e2c1367c7295b7164c28ab5598\nwpt-pr: 62586\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-valid.html"], "git_node": "7e13c63e9cae22bfff3a0c372bfc5e35ff6e1d1d", "git_parents": ["45df747bed25dd06834e000eae4660334edac326"], "node": "cc1d98633bdd3b4bfa60722d02975bc86076ec47", "parents": ["a217abe84baf6f8767df3cf709684025b60b8114"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071058 [wpt PR 62586] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62586\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-valid.html.ini"], "git_node": "8602d49eab13516e04c915376a7a353e4d2b0fdf", "git_parents": ["7e13c63e9cae22bfff3a0c372bfc5e35ff6e1d1d"], "node": "7cfdfc56d1f1e149acc01df6df37ac44e7db4d4d", "parents": ["cc1d98633bdd3b4bfa60722d02975bc86076ec47"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071032 [wpt PR 62564] - Sanitizer: fix the javascript: URL tests and cover the default configuration, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSanitizer: fix the javascript: URL tests and cover the default configuration\n\n5a6adac438 (#62421) removed the closing \u003c/script\u003e. The tokenizer then reaches EOF in the script data state, which sets the script element's \"already started\" to true, so none of the tests in the file run.\n\nThe unsafe methods were run against { sanitizer: new Sanitizer() } using the shared html5lib expectations, but those expectations assume a configuration that allows everything. The default configuration's allow lists drop area, button, form, input, the SVG animation elements, nothref, attributeName and xlink:href, so 15 of the 30 testcases could not pass.\n\nTest the default configuration on its own terms instead. HTML a/href and SVG a/href are the only pairs from the built-in navigating URL attributes list it keeps, so assert there that the unsafe methods remove a javascript: URL but keep a non-javascript one, and that setJavascriptURLs() is what makes the difference rather than the attribute allow list.\n\nAlso run the unsafe methods against a configuration that removeUnsafe() was called on, which is what whatwg/html#12898 was about.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5130aa2289ec8f5181593f046f2aaf92bbfd01a8\nwpt-pr: 62564\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-javascript-url.html"], "git_node": "5fd7f3250013bc37300138a3b130f190130364d7", "git_parents": ["8602d49eab13516e04c915376a7a353e4d2b0fdf"], "node": "ad5922b76bf6c8875e7cad265127699596427980", "parents": ["7cfdfc56d1f1e149acc01df6df37ac44e7db4d4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "github-actions[bot] \u003c41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071122 [wpt PR 62460] - Sync interfaces/ with @webref/idl 3.83.1, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSync interfaces/ with @webref/idl 3.83.1 (#62460)\n\nCo-authored-by: wpt-pr-bot \u003cwpt-pr-bot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c9ffdd73a621fede5301345b42d29b50758a5388\nwpt-pr: 62460\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/html.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/pointerevents.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/soft-navigations.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webaudio.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webcodecs.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webgpu.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webmcp.idl"], "git_node": "a8c3938625185ef053c56bbb3ff349f869c8a8c2", "git_parents": ["5fd7f3250013bc37300138a3b130f190130364d7"], "node": "ed4398ca9ce3a4b0274b8008f1235a0ebfb4b5a8", "parents": ["ad5922b76bf6c8875e7cad265127699596427980"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071122 [wpt PR 62460] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62460\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/FileAPI/blob/Blob-stream-byob-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-clear-encrypted.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-two-videos.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/api/credentials/cookies.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/pointerlock/pointerlock_suppress_mouse_boundary_events_when_locked.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/touch-events/hover-state-caused-by-compatibility-mouse-events.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/idlharness.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCDataChannel-close.html.ini"], "git_node": "40046c024f983fc15bf626a23cd4e41c5493f8f3", "git_parents": ["a8c3938625185ef053c56bbb3ff349f869c8a8c2"], "node": "788fbde17ce3588a97c83e69f248b49460266956", "parents": ["ed4398ca9ce3a4b0274b8008f1235a0ebfb4b5a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoav Weiss \u003cyoavweiss@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071025 [wpt PR 62592] - Do not cache failed module imports, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDo not cache failed module imports\n\nImplements https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10327 behind a flag to\nenable developers to retry failed module loads. It does so by removing\nmodule map entries from the map in case of a failure.\n\nThe test changes delete failing expectations and fix test flakiness\nthat resulted from a hardcoded UUID, by moving the tests to use a\ngenerated UUID (which requires .https serving for the test, and .sub\nserving for its resources).\n\nBug: 534781954\nChange-Id: I4b97894cfcfa6878077cd8a933ca54fdca0466e9\nBinary-Size: +12B is the generated base::Feature for new runtime flag.\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8102202\nReviewed-by: Hiroshige Hayashizaki \u003chiroshige@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Yoav Weiss (@Shopify) \u003cyoavweiss@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695318}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e4bdcd78c767c2437718e5964ffea6b0a035ccdd\nwpt-pr: 62592\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/shared-dependency-repeated-import.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/shared-dependency-repeated-import.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-a.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-a.sub.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-b.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-b.sub.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-repeated-import.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-repeated-import.https.html"], "git_node": "d82132e5cc4f2595b5068be85131efd17ed09104", "git_parents": ["40046c024f983fc15bf626a23cd4e41c5493f8f3"], "node": "22bd92a1c3c7bdae1f7a0a47a681715003fa2c32", "parents": ["788fbde17ce3588a97c83e69f248b49460266956"], "tags": []}, {"author": "BruceDai \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071050 [wpt PR 62584] - webnn: add tests of negative indices for scatterElements / scatterND, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebnn: add tests of negative indices for scatterElements / scatterND\n\nThis CL extends the existing scatterElements and scatterND\nconformance tests with negative indices cases, per the spec which\nallows their indices operand to be negative.\n\nTo check the behavior on different backends, this CL also adds\ntests covering input tensors of 0D through 5D with negative\nindices.\n\nChange-Id: I5a7fe27d9e5879156f041758e0c0eb782252adac\nBug: 553670706\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:win11-blink-rel, mac14.arm64-blink-rel, mac14-blink-rel, mac15.arm64-blink-rel, linux-blink-rel\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8313327\nCommit-Queue: Dai, Feng \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Hu, Ningxin \u003cningxin.hu@intel.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Dai, Feng \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Reilly Grant \u003creillyg@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695328}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d88f063189bcd46730b6c7c54b36ea528a7845a8\nwpt-pr: 62584\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/conformance_tests/scatterElements.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/conformance_tests/scatterND.https.any.js"], "git_node": "3b2729e904d65eef2ec851af98635826e3b0de6a", "git_parents": ["d82132e5cc4f2595b5068be85131efd17ed09104"], "node": "4ad8fe5b29d88d8861662562a0d628357ece6834", "parents": ["22bd92a1c3c7bdae1f7a0a47a681715003fa2c32"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071125 [wpt PR 62329] - Fetch: more coverage for parsing a single range header value, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFetch: more coverage for parsing a single range header value (#62329)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: df581310de2d1ab19c722c604652df7f8edaa79b\nwpt-pr: 62329\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/cors/cors-safelisted-request-header.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/range/blob.any.js"], "git_node": "3974ea39023437d57b49a22e32485173fc2f719c", "git_parents": ["3b2729e904d65eef2ec851af98635826e3b0de6a"], "node": "083b9c98bc61ea12ef1edf6158189992bfb6802e", "parents": ["4ad8fe5b29d88d8861662562a0d628357ece6834"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066710 [wpt PR 62209] - Patch aioquic so that it sends a truthful max_udp_payload_size, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPatch aioquic so that it sends a truthful max_udp_payload_size\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bc424d7a587eb331974798548e82cddcbd18ffb3\nwpt-pr: 62209\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/webtransport/h3/webtransport_h3_server.py"], "git_node": "60c1c33b6f40a1581c82775e9bbc789608281816", "git_parents": ["3974ea39023437d57b49a22e32485173fc2f719c"], "node": "851c43cfdc7e7ab00aa6b649e7a7bf9fe08eb8de", "parents": ["083b9c98bc61ea12ef1edf6158189992bfb6802e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071077 [wpt PR 62597] - Limit SVGAElement referrerPolicy reflection to known values, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nLimit SVGAElement referrerPolicy reflection to known values\n\nFilter the reflected value through the standard referrer policy\nkeywords and add WPT coverage for normalization and invalid values.\n\nBug: 555794209\nChange-Id: Iab2811b934262e953c7515166c8f877dccc8d251\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8382117\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695345}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2e87792d19b8601df5d8eaa6c2b730a363124635\nwpt-pr: 62597\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/scripted/a-referrerpolicy-reflection.html"], "git_node": "e5a59fdd2d53a8dcb0a6bb908a9012b6279a88a0", "git_parents": ["60c1c33b6f40a1581c82775e9bbc789608281816"], "node": "7d4408892ce69cabdbafe5c5519ab391fb5f36e2", "parents": ["851c43cfdc7e7ab00aa6b649e7a7bf9fe08eb8de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071077 [wpt PR 62597] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62597\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/linking/scripted/use-iframe-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "9a81d37c488073922a1deb42501e0362dc84215a", "git_parents": ["e5a59fdd2d53a8dcb0a6bb908a9012b6279a88a0"], "node": "a40fd0415e51f0d00aca01f90e80cfb693de61c6", "parents": ["7d4408892ce69cabdbafe5c5519ab391fb5f36e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071074 [wpt PR 62596] - Refactor Element::StyleForPseudoElement, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRefactor Element::StyleForPseudoElement\n\nThe function had slightly different paths for inherited ::first-line\nstyles, pseudo-elements which were categorized as \"before-or-after-\nlike\", and other pseudo-elements.\n\nThe display:contents handling should not be limited to a subset of\npseudo-elements. The pseudo-elements generating sibling boxes already\nhandled display:contents since they always call LayoutParentElement()\nfor updating layout_parent_override.\n\nThe remaining special part of before-or-after-like was locale style\nadjustments only relevant to ::before/::after for UA rendered HTML \u003cq\u003e\nelements.\n\nThe resulting change was:\n\n1. Move StyleForFirstLineInherited() into a separate function\n2. Use a common ResolveStyle() path for the rest of the pseudo-elements\n   where we are:\n   - Adjusting layout_parent_style for pseudo-elements which are pulled\n     out as siblings of their inheritance parent (originating element)\n   - Adjusting layout_parent_style for all other pseudo elements where a\n     display:contents style was passed in\n   - Adjust the resulting style for ::before/::after of \u003cq\u003e elements\n\nAlso, added a wpt test that fails if the display:contents adjustment is\nremoved since we didn't have coverage for that.\n\nChange-Id: I1f7384d5236c724ab0e8aff71a361aae49714018\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8378405\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695367}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7c3bae55cab5840dc333e99ffd56d5422811ce2c\nwpt-pr: 62596\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-propagation-display-contents-003.html"], "git_node": "fd4da0ca519047d3362402aec92ef34f5d09ba9a", "git_parents": ["9a81d37c488073922a1deb42501e0362dc84215a"], "node": "a026d96e3dc6dd73b32a8a95c867a2afb5484f88", "parents": ["a40fd0415e51f0d00aca01f90e80cfb693de61c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071130 [wpt PR 62577] - Invalidate shapes' percentage 'stroke-dasharray' on viewport resize, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nInvalidate shapes' percentage 'stroke-dasharray' on viewport resize\n\nWe previously only consider 'stroke-width' as depending on the viewport,\nbut the same should apply for 'stroke-dasharray'.\n\nAdd an additional case to the ComputeStrokeHasRelativeLengths() helper,\nand also move to using a bit to track the result of this function, since\nit's now potentially more costly - but can easily be tracked when\ncomputed style changes.\n\nFixed: 557807412\nChange-Id: Ic07c73e62110a9832f3e0ff35c64325a336d3ef7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8361775\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695413}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 09fba9ba75644031d35b8f15d3634886d94d810d\nwpt-pr: 62577\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/painting/reftests/svg-percent-stroke-dasharray-line-viewbox-update.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/painting/reftests/svg-percent-stroke-dasharray-path-viewbox-update.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/painting/reftests/svg-percent-stroke-dasharray-rect-viewbox-update.html"], "git_node": "93cd689b2a8f6af66eab6798577e720434150699", "git_parents": ["fd4da0ca519047d3362402aec92ef34f5d09ba9a"], "node": "bd1521c2940a26ef5e03a5b2dc16b9e999180859", "parents": ["a026d96e3dc6dd73b32a8a95c867a2afb5484f88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071131 [wpt PR 62576] - Fix transform computation in StylePath::GetPath(), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix transform computation in StylePath::GetPath()\n\nThe `path_scale` wouldn't apply to the offset from the reference box,\nwhich led to zoom being retained and thus incorrect geometry.\n\nFix the order in which the transform components are applied.\n\nFixed: 557415472\nChange-Id: I7466eb531f22a30ae868e05fcfb19478e6d60e99\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8364590\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695419}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 24d34b2dcd9f5db29751883f08754d81c0cb512e\nwpt-pr: 62576\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-path-with-zoom-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-path-with-zoom-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-path-with-zoom-hittest-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-path-with-zoom-hittest-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-path-with-zoom-hittest.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-path-with-zoom.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/reference/clip-path-path-with-zoom-002-ref.html"], "git_node": "9b694f1df0bea4c20abf50692786393a1d580f19", "git_parents": ["93cd689b2a8f6af66eab6798577e720434150699"], "node": "04dc0e6d7d6f1afd1ca738bdf4554d2f210cad0b", "parents": ["bd1521c2940a26ef5e03a5b2dc16b9e999180859"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071131 [wpt PR 62576] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62576\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/clip-path/animations/clip-path-transition-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-path-with-zoom.html.ini"], "git_node": "fb1bdb95bed4cf429e6d6575bed49638d6986b21", "git_parents": ["9b694f1df0bea4c20abf50692786393a1d580f19"], "node": "f112b2127e080f2ef6bf9a1af0f743f1ed271f0f", "parents": ["04dc0e6d7d6f1afd1ca738bdf4554d2f210cad0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071135 [wpt PR 62598] - [npw] Support start delay for bg-color on the compositor thread, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[npw] Support start delay for bg-color on the compositor thread\n\nAside from removing the fallback reason, an additional fix was needed\nto suppress short-circuiting of paint invalidation when bg-color\nchanges while the composited animation is *not* in effect. We need\npaint invalidation in this case to pick up the new underlying value.\n\nChange-Id: I29ddbe69703401cd3eb9e87040e23b56efaa3bee\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8295942\nCommit-Queue: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695557}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9bb2e105aedda9afb5735788ca86ddefeb484ccc\nwpt-pr: 62598\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-animations/animate-bg-color-with-change-during-delay-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-animations/animate-bg-color-with-change-during-delay.html"], "git_node": "21b66aaa8c32f308ee5061b281cf35ab85ce5e03", "git_parents": ["fb1bdb95bed4cf429e6d6575bed49638d6986b21"], "node": "41f5cf74e6e37592dbe776822fd5331c7f8d26c9", "parents": ["f112b2127e080f2ef6bf9a1af0f743f1ed271f0f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071160 [wpt PR 62605] - Prevent CSS transition from leaking tainted value, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPrevent CSS transition from leaking tainted value\n\nPreviously we could leak an attr-tainted value by stopping an\nanimation in the same frame that a transition starts that affects the\nsame property. Removal of the CSS animation can result in the start\nvalue of a transition being attr-tainted. We were incorrectly getting\nthe variable data from the previous update's style and not from\nbefore-change style.\n\nBug: 537107728\nChange-Id: Ie070a17a8d5af469895fff33fa19e9a114529815\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8386356\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695585}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6beb2ef7af1d375504e561a6eb520ef60c1918cc\nwpt-pr: 62605\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-variables/transition-with-attribute-taint.html"], "git_node": "688a4ad4c0e4f08a7a35853c9ebd8e8305b514dc", "git_parents": ["21b66aaa8c32f308ee5061b281cf35ab85ce5e03"], "node": "432e43aa67fe1fdc207139a4bb6c4fc347af041c", "parents": ["41f5cf74e6e37592dbe776822fd5331c7f8d26c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Verge \u003caverge@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071161 [wpt PR 62606] - [Fenced-Frames] Remove default-mode FencedFrameConfig constructor., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Fenced-Frames] Remove default-mode FencedFrameConfig constructor.\n\nGiven that Protected Audience and Shared Storage have been deprecated\nas part of the larger Privacy Sandbox deprecations, there is no valid\nway to generate a FencedFrameConfig in production. However, there is\na runtime-flag-gated constructor that allows for creating a\nFencedFrameConfig using only a URL. This is referred to as \"default\nmode.\" Default mode is heavily used in Fenced Frames' test suites to\nsimplify construction.\n\nGiven that Fenced Frames themselves are slated for removal in M154[1],\nand default-mode is never used in production codepaths, the simplest\noption is to just remove it, along with all of the tests that rely on\nit.\n\n[1]: https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/c9w5uH3eSuo/m/va7x_DYRDgAJ?e=48417069\n\nBug: 509847526,499191497\nFixed: 509847526,499191497\nChange-Id: I8b5c07fc8e65cc42eb59bd691ff423500362c7cf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8266472\nReviewed-by: Arthur Sonzogni \u003carthursonzogni@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mark Pearson \u003cmpearson@chromium.org\u003e\nSLSA-Policy-Verified: SLSA Policy Verification Service \u003cdevtools-gerritcodereview-exitgate@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Avi Drissman \u003cavi@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Xiaochen Zhou \u003cxiaochenzh@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Andrew Verge \u003caverge@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Peter Conn \u003cpeconn@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Shivani Sharma \u003cshivanisha@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Wenbin Zhang \u003cwenbinzhang@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695619}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7f029c79297bd1904380d9a6d86c92e3aac420e2\nwpt-pr: 62606\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/anchor-focus.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/autofocus-denied.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/background-fetch.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/background-sync.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/badging.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/battery_status.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/before-unload.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/change-src-attribute-after-config-installation-does-not-trigger-navigation.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/client-hints.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/client-hints.https.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/compute-pressure.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/config-installation-triggers-navigation-of-navigated-fenced-frame.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/config-installation-triggers-navigation.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/config-with-empty-url-installation-unloads-navigated-fenced-frame.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/consume-user-activation.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/content-index.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/coop-bcg-s