713\n", "files": ["toolkit/profile/docs/changes.md"], "git_node": "c8f9a3ee29fc25edb240885e0e4002586bf4e5cd", "git_parents": ["c989f4be2d323e9791f7df5a843124dc91266709"], "node": "10588b6aff08d5e1a7df1f437ce01cd992148e6c", "parents": ["4ee4e945c1c056767006aac3859a6bfbcd3001cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071683 - Fix the shavar-prod-lists link in the tracking lists documentation r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop DONTBUILD\n\nThe link text was itself a markdown link, so the outer target was not a URL.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325704\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/docs/tracking-lists/index.md"], "git_node": "e6f2e92d3f7e12be71ca37acdee63539615c05ff", "git_parents": ["c8f9a3ee29fc25edb240885e0e4002586bf4e5cd"], "node": "6316f4cb9ce0ba20eb73de25f10a70781561475d", "parents": ["10588b6aff08d5e1a7df1f437ce01cd992148e6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071683 - Point GIFFT at the histogram documentation under obsolete/ r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop DONTBUILD\n\nThe exponential histogram section moved when the legacy telemetry docs were\nmarked obsolete, and the link still used a .html target.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325705\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/docs/user/gifft.md"], "git_node": "a460b858c642bb4bed585e071d6524e346851db3", "git_parents": ["e6f2e92d3f7e12be71ca37acdee63539615c05ff"], "node": "e00abef3ba63e02370dee1cf42e1e0d7ec4aca49", "parents": ["6316f4cb9ce0ba20eb73de25f10a70781561475d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071683 - Fix broken links in the browser documentation r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop\n\nThe other-widgets Storybook page linked to anchors that live in the\nreusable-widgets page, and the remaining links used .html targets, an MDN\nwiki page name, or a nested markdown link.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325693\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/docs/building-and-testing.md", "browser/components/attribution/docs/index.md", "browser/components/storybook/docs/README.other-widgets.stories.md", "browser/docs/FrontendCodeReviewBestPractices.md", "browser/docs/how_to/template.md", "browser/extensions/newtab/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "52b27a297d1fde428ce24907d4eab32efff2083b", "git_parents": ["a460b858c642bb4bed585e071d6524e346851db3"], "node": "19c1a6b98a4e20cb8c1f589e6ed869083c7e0195", "parents": ["e00abef3ba63e02370dee1cf42e1e0d7ec4aca49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055661 - Use zero touch start/move tolerance on wpt. r=botond,whimboo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312601\n", "files": ["remote/shared/RecommendedPreferences.sys.mjs", "testing/marionette/client/marionette_driver/geckoinstance.py", "testing/profiles/web-platform/user.js", "testing/web-platform/meta/pointerevents/pointerevent_fractional_coordinates.html.ini"], "git_node": "e1edbccdcc90821acb80c22faf333826c14757c5", "git_parents": ["52b27a297d1fde428ce24907d4eab32efff2083b"], "node": "2dbea0cb5329dea64156e08fdda0730dec2029e7", "parents": ["19c1a6b98a4e20cb8c1f589e6ed869083c7e0195"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071793 - Extend the agent-skills-sync linter to the skills' scripts. r=linter-reviewers,marco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325789\n", "files": ["tools/lint/agent-skills-sync.yml", "tools/lint/agent-skills-sync/__init__.py", "tools/lint/test/test_agent_skills_sync.py"], "git_node": "7d3649ca537cac930f56e276c8d49d8cda587de5", "git_parents": ["e1edbccdcc90821acb80c22faf333826c14757c5"], "node": "1d73b7440d3a2a2bde5d7c8272e61d9fbda6c5b3", "parents": ["2dbea0cb5329dea64156e08fdda0730dec2029e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007259: Flush prefs.js before the unclean restart in test_caches_delete_cleanup_after_shutdown.py. r=dom-storage-reviewers,dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nThe unclean restart kills the process with SIGKILL, so the testing pref\nset in setUp only survives if the delayed asynchronous prefs.js save has\nalready happened. Save the pref file explicitly to remove the race.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323558\n", "files": ["dom/cache/test/marionette/test_caches_delete_cleanup_after_shutdown.py"], "git_node": "ed9710d0328a6db04ee803c74ec59b047999052c", "git_parents": ["7d3649ca537cac930f56e276c8d49d8cda587de5"], "node": "642e3350f67b99458aa9df25643efd6368ce6bae", "parents": ["1d73b7440d3a2a2bde5d7c8272e61d9fbda6c5b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068590: Report the time since install and update in the new-profile ping. r=jhirsch\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322906\n", "files": ["toolkit/profile/ProfileMetrics.sys.mjs", "toolkit/profile/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_profile_metrics_time_since_install.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_profile_metrics_time_since_no_files.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_profile_metrics_time_since_update.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "52b50c579de169dcd516a3cb35bbeab9362493a2", "git_parents": ["ed9710d0328a6db04ee803c74ec59b047999052c"], "node": "90481658bf0c2331e44be23aaafcf6669bcfe758", "parents": ["642e3350f67b99458aa9df25643efd6368ce6bae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071499 [Linux] Don't crash when rendering to hidden X11 window r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325823\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "de05e5eb3817c0016a6e8a482d48ac59b0dd8f6f", "git_parents": ["52b50c579de169dcd516a3cb35bbeab9362493a2"], "node": "aff6de5d1d153425487189e4dcd63309e657da8d", "parents": ["90481658bf0c2331e44be23aaafcf6669bcfe758"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071243 - Avoid \u003csystem_error\u003e under hidden visibility to fix libc++ 22+ builds r=sergesanspaille\n\nlibc++ 22 declares std::error_condition without _LIBCPP_EXPORTED_FROM_ABI in\n__system_error/error_category.h, but still defines it with the annotation in\n__system_error/error_condition.h. Under the `#pragma GCC visibility\npush(hidden)` that config/gcc_hidden.h force-includes on Linux and Android, the\ndeclaration picks up hidden visibility, and clang then rejects the definition\nwith \"visibility does not match previous declaration\". The annotation was\ndropped from the declaration by llvm/llvm-project#132602; libc++ 18 through 21\nhave it on both.\n\nUpstream (llvm/llvm-project#180679) is inclined to treat this as wontfix, so\nwork around it in the two places that reach \u003csystem_error\u003e:\n\n- third_party/fmt's format.h includes it, but the include is dead in our copy,\n  since comment-format-system-error.patch already comments out every API that\n  used std::system_error. Drop it, extending that patch so re-vendoring keeps\n  it dropped.\n\n- toolkit/components/protobuf's strtod.cc includes it directly, so add\n  system_error to config/stl-headers.mozbuild. Both\n  config/gcc-stl-wrapper.template.h and config/make-system-wrappers.py wrap the\n  include in `#pragma GCC visibility push(default)`, as already done for\n  \u003cstring\u003e and the other wrapped headers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325349\n", "files": ["config/stl-headers.mozbuild", "third_party/fmt/comment-format-system-error.patch", "third_party/fmt/include/fmt/format.h"], "git_node": "7682c5f254f9384b29452b212655b23aea63a3fc", "git_parents": ["de05e5eb3817c0016a6e8a482d48ac59b0dd8f6f"], "node": "10b0b126cef188ecef11b7f708369997160953d5", "parents": ["aff6de5d1d153425487189e4dcd63309e657da8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mayankleoboy1 \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070760 - Share the DOM subtree filter helpers with selectors. r=emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers\n\nMove the filter accessors from TElement to selectors::Element and extract\nthe hash conversion into selectors::subtree_filter. Update the existing\nDOM query callers without changing the filter representation, propagation,\nor query behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325750\n", "files": ["servo/components/selectors/lib.rs", "servo/components/selectors/subtree_filter.rs", "servo/components/selectors/tree.rs", "servo/components/style/dom.rs", "servo/components/style/dom_apis.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/wrapper.rs"], "git_node": "bfeb8e052da7f2e05b81ce28f854c01673bbc287", "git_parents": ["7682c5f254f9384b29452b212655b23aea63a3fc"], "node": "940fa8ff78545b89f2a0c179ee42392a37a6bbb0", "parents": ["10b0b126cef188ecef11b7f708369997160953d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066073 - Ignore the tab group and split view reindent in blame and annotate. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324514\n", "files": [".git-blame-ignore-revs", ".hg-annotate-ignore-revs"], "git_node": "4290620514a8b0c7eb7ff631946274854253ce6b", "git_parents": ["bfeb8e052da7f2e05b81ce28f854c01673bbc287"], "node": "2be2b67940f0a894ed4548be344a57e51f992247", "parents": ["940fa8ff78545b89f2a0c179ee42392a37a6bbb0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071793 - Skip the executable-mode sync test on Windows. r=bustage-fix\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325848\n", "files": ["tools/lint/test/test_agent_skills_sync.py"], "git_node": "4e33385827154da22008f808d503aa795819f913", "git_parents": ["4290620514a8b0c7eb7ff631946274854253ce6b"], "node": "1f66320c90959259fea53fa6204be4ad35ab0dcc", "parents": ["2be2b67940f0a894ed4548be344a57e51f992247"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070940 - Drop furthest block's children wehn adoption agency's formatting clone is removed r=tschuster\n\nAn example like `\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003cp\u003efoo\u003c/b\u003ebar\u003c/i\u003e` with `removeElements: [\"i\"]` the `\u003cp\u003e`\nhoisted into body must end up empty, not keep `\u003cb\u003efoo\u003c/b\u003ebar`. Blink does the\nsame:\n\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/parser/html_tree_builder.cc;l=1988-1992.\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12756#discussion_r3977977410 for more.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324966\n", "files": ["parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilderCppSupplement.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-in-adoption-agency.sub.dat"], "git_node": "5ea6a0a84a1a5f69b43d00b7ad79be81fd698333", "git_parents": ["4e33385827154da22008f808d503aa795819f913"], "node": "1ae4574b1abd7af6fbcc99b9e779086d06d4fc8e", "parents": ["1f66320c90959259fea53fa6204be4ad35ab0dcc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hubert B Manilla \u003chmanilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068517 - [devtools] Stop using the builtin MatchDecorator r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nThis removes the usage of the MatchDecorator due to its restrictions with\n - requiring a global regexp flag to be always set and\n - it not being infinte-loop safe\n\nLets instead handle the building of the decorations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324229\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/dist/search-worker.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/utils/build-query.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-search-file.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/shared-head.js", "devtools/client/shared/sourceeditor/editor.js"], "git_node": "e17b42233cd386da9c5e2ef5738eed6c308bb373", "git_parents": ["5ea6a0a84a1a5f69b43d00b7ad79be81fd698333"], "node": "703758f2bdc6d3fe24aa6f654e4a48bdfc20f439", "parents": ["1ae4574b1abd7af6fbcc99b9e779086d06d4fc8e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068934 - Support javascriptURLs in the configuration of sanitizer. r=tschuster,webidl,smaug,keithamus\n\nWhen javascriptURLs is set to false, unsafe methods will remove javascript URLs from the input.\n\nIn Safe methods javascript URLs always be removed regardless of config.\n\nUpdated related comments in the sanitizer.\n\nImplements https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12898\n\nWPT: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62421\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324577\n", "files": ["dom/security/sanitizer/Sanitizer.cpp", "dom/security/sanitizer/Sanitizer.h", "dom/webidl/Sanitizer.webidl", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-boolean-defaults.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-config.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-default-config.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-modifiers.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-removeUnsafe.html.ini"], "git_node": "b590a088bc733b1fcd30d2834f2596686d82d8a8", "git_parents": ["e17b42233cd386da9c5e2ef5738eed6c308bb373"], "node": "fa0eea47cef9a377e76f9243b20a2977f59a09c9", "parents": ["703758f2bdc6d3fe24aa6f654e4a48bdfc20f439"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071704 - Use a currentColor color-mix for the ghost button hover and active backgrounds in the native theme. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio\n\nThe toolbar button tokens map back to ghost, restoring the reference bug 2069042 removed; every regime resolves to the value it did before.\n\nGhost's forced-colors values become explicit: the pinned native-theme value shadows the ones it inherited through --button-background-color-hover and -active.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325786\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/nova/_tokens.scss", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/nova/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-platform.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/button.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/button.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbarbutton.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbarbutton.tokens.json"], "git_node": "35fbc58d44b7a114d216a3ddfec63843853c33d1", "git_parents": ["b590a088bc733b1fcd30d2834f2596686d82d8a8"], "node": "4ac68f36e764846c1e7f26693a0f7f10bba6af84", "parents": ["fa0eea47cef9a377e76f9243b20a2977f59a09c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2068590: Report the time since install and update in the new-profile ping. r=jhirsch\" for causing xpc failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 52b50c579de169dcd516a3cb35bbeab9362493a2.\n", "files": ["toolkit/profile/ProfileMetrics.sys.mjs", "toolkit/profile/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_profile_metrics_time_since_install.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_profile_metrics_time_since_no_files.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_profile_metrics_time_since_update.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "73707cce60ea3b4aa52ac84e366d114a7e7809bb", "git_parents": ["35fbc58d44b7a114d216a3ddfec63843853c33d1"], "node": "95924bce6c457c6b416896a1d0f921a331ffaf9d", "parents": ["4ac68f36e764846c1e7f26693a0f7f10bba6af84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061526 - Harden JAR URI deserialization r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323545\n", "files": ["modules/libjar/nsJARURI.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/res/SubstitutingJARURI.h", "netwerk/protocol/res/SubstitutingProtocolHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "3432782e7713ef0eb5eaa822bd6a3c3ed80439b0", "git_parents": ["73707cce60ea3b4aa52ac84e366d114a7e7809bb"], "node": "1f11a1ab1609d39b3dadd57758021c73c576b514", "parents": ["95924bce6c457c6b416896a1d0f921a331ffaf9d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070424 - Update metadata for css/css-borders/corner-shape/render-corner-shape.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325829\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/render-corner-shape.html.ini"], "git_node": "2f8b06a583bed0861fbdcbf358dd5784fe2403f1", "git_parents": ["3432782e7713ef0eb5eaa822bd6a3c3ed80439b0"], "node": "a4caa2150e2167d18015874d50e7922b5ec6fad7", "parents": ["1f11a1ab1609d39b3dadd57758021c73c576b514"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071574 - Enable the \"mathml.a.element.enabled\" preference for html/dom/idlharness.https.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325826\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/idlharness.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "0a7b3d2c1283dfa4bcb3737a6918928c7e8d3ea3", "git_parents": ["2f8b06a583bed0861fbdcbf358dd5784fe2403f1"], "node": "c06732e3caa9e1be5088afdee9b359aecf631688", "parents": ["a4caa2150e2167d18015874d50e7922b5ec6fad7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071683 - Fix two bug links in the obsolete telemetry documentation r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,TravisLong,mossop\n\nBoth had the word bug glued to the URL.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325709\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/obsolete/collection/events.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/obsolete/collection/scalars.md"], "git_node": "8c9666ebcb0ec15a3f445b9010b518d825cc9b20", "git_parents": ["0a7b3d2c1283dfa4bcb3737a6918928c7e8d3ea3"], "node": "6cffb85bb2da0746adc689b9d51436e3f5ed5ae6", "parents": ["c06732e3caa9e1be5088afdee9b359aecf631688"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071683 - Fix the Translations overview table of contents r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop\n\nIt listed an Enabling Translations section that the page does not have, and\nomitted Using Translations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325710\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/docs/resources/01_overview.md"], "git_node": "8d176bc54a5ad50d608d77c732b5e98c8df61157", "git_parents": ["8c9666ebcb0ec15a3f445b9010b518d825cc9b20"], "node": "1ab495262cc6e5ab938fd55a7c0517a405deb968", "parents": ["6cffb85bb2da0746adc689b9d51436e3f5ed5ae6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062329 - Add use counters for the SpeechRecognition API. r=dom-core-reviewers,webidl,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319563\n", "files": ["dom/base/UseCounters.conf", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "dom/webidl/SpeechRecognition.webidl"], "git_node": "57d8c026c74d1be249bb78fec439a14c5193bef6", "git_parents": ["8d176bc54a5ad50d608d77c732b5e98c8df61157"], "node": "9f1fad08fb634f7f2de2731bbf54d15fbd7839aa", "parents": ["1ab495262cc6e5ab938fd55a7c0517a405deb968"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062329 - Record speech recognition usage, outcomes and errors with Glean. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu,TravisLong\n\nsession_ended is recorded from Reset(), the one path every teardown goes\nthrough. No transcript text or audio is recorded.\n\nA session_id on both events pairs them, so a start and its outcome can be\njoined instead of subtracted as two populations across a day boundary.\n\nsession_started also reports the model and locale the session negotiated to,\nnot just the tag the page asked for: en, en-US and en-us all run the same\nmodel, and only the negotiated locale can be grouped on.\n\ninit_failure records the start failures whose cause content knows, because\nthe error codes the spec makes us fire are coarser: service-not-allowed alone\ncovers four distinct causes. The unsupported-language one is rejected before\n[[started]], so it records no session events at all and would otherwise be\ninvisible; it is also exactly why error and session_ended do not add up.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319564\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/metrics.yaml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_telemetry.js", "toolkit/components/glean/metrics_index.py"], "git_node": "286cd620fde00bb770535ee477322b76539b2ca1", "git_parents": ["57d8c026c74d1be249bb78fec439a14c5193bef6"], "node": "1d0dd56427a79ac900304186b615438280a1874d", "parents": ["9f1fad08fb634f7f2de2731bbf54d15fbd7839aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062329 - Measure speech recognition latency in the content process. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nTwo timing distributions are recorded content-side:\n\n- session_init_time measures the page-visible wait between start() and the\n  model becoming ready for recognition. It only has a sample when init\n  succeeded, so its description says to read it against init_failure: a\n  regression turning slow inits into failures would otherwise look like an\n  improvement.\n- result_latency records one sample per session: the mean capture-to-JS\n  latency of its results, using the capture timestamps already plumbed end to\n  end by AudioCaptureTiming.h.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319565\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/metrics.yaml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_telemetry.js", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_parakeet_e2e.html"], "git_node": "009671a0e927ce4036daff7f88a2605bc7bb5955", "git_parents": ["286cd620fde00bb770535ee477322b76539b2ca1"], "node": "ce98eca74cc1c10b2b14459040671acecd6ea5fc", "parents": ["1d0dd56427a79ac900304186b615438280a1874d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062329 - Measure inference cost and init failures in the HWInference process. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nRecorded in the utility process, where inference happens:\n\n- model_load_time measures reading the GGUF into memory. Like\n  session_init_time it only has a sample on success, which its description\n  now says.\n- inference_realtime_factor records one per-session mean of per-chunk\n  throughput as audio duration divided by compute time, times 100 (400 means\n  4x faster than real time). Recognition happens continuously on chunks of\n  similar size, so getting the average is meaningful here. The range reaches\n  100x rather than 20x, because hardware that runs this model comfortably\n  sits above 20x and would otherwise land entirely in the top bucket; the\n  bounds also put a bucket boundary exactly at 100, so falling behind real\n  time is a clean cut.\n- init_failure gains the inference-process labels, one per step that can\n  fail, so a spike says where init broke rather than only that it did. The\n  previous model_load_failed covered six unrelated steps, two of which were\n  not model loads at all, and other covered four.\n\nThe tests verify that starting without an installed model reaches the\ncorresponding failure label and run real recognition end-to-end. They check\nthat the timing metrics have one session-level sample and log values rather\nthan asserting timings, since those depend on the machine.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319566\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/metrics.yaml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionParent.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_inference_telemetry.js", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "12943f71e1fc271d79c419b87a256b684b37adfd", "git_parents": ["009671a0e927ce4036daff7f88a2605bc7bb5955"], "node": "592602b763369c559f657c246dc89e257d5a0a7b", "parents": ["ce98eca74cc1c10b2b14459040671acecd6ea5fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062329 - Attribute MLModelHubService downloads to the requesting task. r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\n\nMLModelHubService used the constant \"ml-model-hub-service\" as the feature ID for every native caller, so the existing firefox_ai_runtime.model_download events could not be selected by feature.\n\nPass the caller-provided task name as featureId, matching getModelBlob(). The browser test downloads through nsIMLModelHub and checks that every lifecycle event is attributed to speech-recognition.\n\nRemove an attribute that was wrongly added and causes this to fail.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322658\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ml/MLModelHubService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "3e87324fc356704eb8c9a8666c86503295f35b66", "git_parents": ["12943f71e1fc271d79c419b87a256b684b37adfd"], "node": "c1131466b7db2dd3aede906a8d7b97cb47d71916", "parents": ["592602b763369c559f657c246dc89e257d5a0a7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "omansfeld \u003comansfeld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071860: Add Zed to the IDE integration docs. r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,sylvestre DONTBUILD\n\nZed support through `./mach ide zed` was added in Bug 1953147 a while\nago.\n\nAlso adding the top level `Other Editors` title so it doesn't render as\n`Eclipse` anymore.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325858\n", "files": ["docs/contributing/editors/others.md"], "git_node": "0fd560fc8d1074f23d90e77a39f7315c4eb64a28", "git_parents": ["3e87324fc356704eb8c9a8666c86503295f35b66"], "node": "49520bd4b18809d7b5512fd95cab41e90bb586fb", "parents": ["c1131466b7db2dd3aede906a8d7b97cb47d71916"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070333 - Build the urlbar result menu's container submenu from the parent's containers. r=daisuke\n\nThe menu is unchanged, accesskeys included. Bug 2071753 drops those from every container menu.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324483\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarContentUtils.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_urlbar_contextmenu.js"], "git_node": "7043a76be2bfe72e0e94c53fddeb1a4db28096e8", "git_parents": ["0fd560fc8d1074f23d90e77a39f7315c4eb64a28"], "node": "d6bde6bfb1a8486fac9e540fa1f8a5aac2a57eb4", "parents": ["49520bd4b18809d7b5512fd95cab41e90bb586fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070333 - Offer the result menu's open-in commands in the New Tab search bar. r=daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324484\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarNewTabComponentRegistrant.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_resultMenuOpenIn.js"], "git_node": "71d1083c8041616680ad9395ae13e31ec6721452", "git_parents": ["7043a76be2bfe72e0e94c53fddeb1a4db28096e8"], "node": "ec02c94071dd4aba903934cd64ee6d25b8928110", "parents": ["d6bde6bfb1a8486fac9e540fa1f8a5aac2a57eb4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070960 - Show a urlbar result's menu button whenever its menu has commands. r=daisuke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325004\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_urlbar_contextmenu.js"], "git_node": "b389ab0ebf7e2e239ca442a8b5b1c0d03704b6e1", "git_parents": ["71d1083c8041616680ad9395ae13e31ec6721452"], "node": "c0c6c8e864b4ebcd4a9a0b1f7c3ee3079fe2f214", "parents": ["ec02c94071dd4aba903934cd64ee6d25b8928110"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2068934 - Support javascriptURLs in the configuration of sanitizer. r=tschuster,webidl,smaug,keithamus\" for causing wpt failures @Sanitizer.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit b590a088bc733b1fcd30d2834f2596686d82d8a8.\n", "files": ["dom/security/sanitizer/Sanitizer.cpp", "dom/security/sanitizer/Sanitizer.h", "dom/webidl/Sanitizer.webidl", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-boolean-defaults.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-config.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-default-config.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-modifiers.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-removeUnsafe.html.ini"], "git_node": "19edd9c685cbec0e61d8505ac7820a99c3c67768", "git_parents": ["b389ab0ebf7e2e239ca442a8b5b1c0d03704b6e1"], "node": "f46ff0e93d7f4dbfafa92e2cc4b2ddbfc92995ac", "parents": ["c0c6c8e864b4ebcd4a9a0b1f7c3ee3079fe2f214"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069302 - Separate consecutive speech recognition results with a space. r=media-webspeech-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nThe spec requires that concatenating consecutive results produce a proper\ntranscript of the session. Pages do just that, with nothing in between, so\nwithout the separator the last word of a result runs into the first word of the\nnext one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324938\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_parakeet_eou_flush.html"], "git_node": "7c0bda3d73864b36f99bfa7a984629c8788cf039", "git_parents": ["19edd9c685cbec0e61d8505ac7820a99c3c67768"], "node": "f8a5e7cee5c190887119c9927c94856b1f1f40ed", "parents": ["f46ff0e93d7f4dbfafa92e2cc4b2ddbfc92995ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069715 - Feed SpeechRecognition silence when the track is cross-origin. r=pehrsons,media-webspeech-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324936\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDocumentWarningList.inc", "dom/locales/en-US/chrome/dom/dom.properties", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_speech_recognition_cross_origin.html"], "git_node": "83b898d4a9f0d05a474ae9d6f744cf3d117a9894", "git_parents": ["7c0bda3d73864b36f99bfa7a984629c8788cf039"], "node": "c0cd355f5a4b98cad54b2acb6bcb606c6be93f36", "parents": ["f8a5e7cee5c190887119c9927c94856b1f1f40ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070849 - Rename the tab strip element script to .mjs. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman,frontend-codestyle-reviewers\n\nThe .mjs extension turns on no-shadow with builtinGlobals, so three locals shadowing window.name, window.parent and window.closed are renamed here.\n\nThe subscript loader does not read the extension, so the file still loads as before. Dropping \"use strict\", which eslint rejects in a .mjs, leaves it sloppy until the next commit makes it a real module; nothing outside the class body depends on strictness.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325111\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-main.js", "browser/base/content/test/performance/browser_tabdetach.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabs.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabs.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/tab-events.md", "browser/components/tabbrowser/jar.mn", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_interaction_telemetry.js", "eslint-file-globals.config.mjs"], "git_node": "e3ff7020e148bc4bfeb03a21d08caecb6c91b4b5", "git_parents": ["83b898d4a9f0d05a474ae9d6f744cf3d117a9894"], "node": "0dff829f609e9f3cde81dbfbd46b955a240c1adc", "parents": ["c0cd355f5a4b98cad54b2acb6bcb606c6be93f36"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067254 - Improve the source URL provenance information for clipboard copies. r=edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325348\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsCopySupport.cpp", "dom/base/nsCopySupport.h", "dom/events/Clipboard.cpp", "dom/events/DataTransfer.cpp", "dom/events/test/clipboard/browser.toml", "dom/events/test/clipboard/browser_clipboard_source_url.js", "dom/tests/mochitest/general/test_clipboard_disallowed.html"], "git_node": "d0fc0d21fa2444b3f641f596a2e81c20840bb47c", "git_parents": ["e3ff7020e148bc4bfeb03a21d08caecb6c91b4b5"], "node": "98e71df97336925845c1df8e5fbc53a4247c1880", "parents": ["0dff829f609e9f3cde81dbfbd46b955a240c1adc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hubert B Manilla \u003chmanilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071830  - [devtools] Make the sourcetree item types constants r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323389\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/actions/context-menus/source-tree-item.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/components/PrimaryPanes/SourcesTree.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/components/PrimaryPanes/SourcesTreeItem.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/constants.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/reducers/sources-tree.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/selectors/sources-tree.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/utils/test-mockup.js"], "git_node": "e4371be310c4776e56102e11c96f1dc052bb9ebd", "git_parents": ["d0fc0d21fa2444b3f641f596a2e81c20840bb47c"], "node": "c9126a39dbe995a017bbf05d12d2148d914032b1", "parents": ["98e71df97336925845c1df8e5fbc53a4247c1880"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaron Train \u003caaron.train@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071469 - verifyAddAddressView should wait for the Gecko-provided address structure to load before dismissing the soft keyboard r=ajoltan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325553\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/robots/SettingsSubMenuAutofillRobot.kt"], "git_node": "aa8c8abc4fe59935573a654f7ca4ace7328bb76f", "git_parents": ["e4371be310c4776e56102e11c96f1dc052bb9ebd"], "node": "b0afb16e68b63bb9e7f6188d69987d1f6f36e3c9", "parents": ["c9126a39dbe995a017bbf05d12d2148d914032b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Josh Porter \u003cjoporter@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061552 - Add preference to hide the neterror illustrations. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,kcochrane\n\nThe pref defaults to true. When it is false, net-error-card omits the\nillustration container, and the card shrinks to its widest text line,\nso the text stays visually centered instead of sitting left of center.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324950\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutNetError_feltprivacy_illustrations.js", "toolkit/content/net-error-card.mjs", "toolkit/modules/RemotePageAccessManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/aboutNetError.css"], "git_node": "308e8b02f5fc92ed25af6e27eee4b2a74cd67f2e", "git_parents": ["aa8c8abc4fe59935573a654f7ca4ace7328bb76f"], "node": "e53a49b48b004fe52119d7303b57e73bd1853d8e", "parents": ["b0afb16e68b63bb9e7f6188d69987d1f6f36e3c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071267 - Fade out a mermaid diagram at the edge it scrolls past. r=sylvestre,firefox-source-docs-reviewers\n\nipc/docs/ipdl.md is the page to build and open. Its four diagrams run from 585 to 1289 pixels wide, so a window whose column width falls in that range shows both the fade on a diagram that scrolls and no fade on one that fits. The negative margin is what keeps the second case honest: a diagram scrolls at exactly the width it did before, since the padding the fade needs comes out of the column's gutter.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325846\n", "files": ["docs/_static/custom_theme.css"], "git_node": "6c010dd126548a463951e1fe44f7f98f188db256", "git_parents": ["308e8b02f5fc92ed25af6e27eee4b2a74cd67f2e"], "node": "e72a760ea422f3e1c6a607084f54452c0c51bf67", "parents": ["e53a49b48b004fe52119d7303b57e73bd1853d8e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071268 - Make a scrolled code block or diagram reachable with the keyboard. r=sylvestre,firefox-source-docs-reviewers\n\nipc/docs/ipdl.md is the page to build and open. Twenty of its forty scroll containers overflow at the 442px column a 982px window gives, and those twenty are the ones that take focus; widening the window until the column reaches 891px leaves two.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325856\n", "files": ["docs/_static/custom_theme.css", "docs/_static/scrollable_regions.js", "docs/conf.py"], "git_node": "eaea042471bfd675971af3514249176e756c0fca", "git_parents": ["6c010dd126548a463951e1fe44f7f98f188db256"], "node": "f546a4efbe1ea8528eac3b60a82ffd0d048fe302", "parents": ["e72a760ea422f3e1c6a607084f54452c0c51bf67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henrik Skupin \u003cmail@hskupin.info\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047745 - [wdspec] Cleanup wpt meta data for Windows. r=webdriver-reviewers,Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325117\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/browser/get_client_windows/get_client_windows.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/browser/set_download_behavior/download_behavior_denied.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/browser/set_download_behavior/global.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/download_will_begin/download_will_begin.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/navigation_started/navigation_started.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/continue_response/invalid.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/get_data/invalid.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/script/get_realms/get_realms.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/script/get_realms/invalid.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/storage/set_cookie/cookie_name.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/accept_alert/accept.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/element_send_keys/scroll_into_view.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/find_elements_from_shadow_root/find.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/get_computed_role/get.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/new_session/create_alwaysMatch.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/new_session/unhandled_prompt_behavior.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/new_window/user_prompts.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/perform_actions/key_events.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/perform_actions/pointer_mouse.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/perform_actions/pointer_origin.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/release_actions/release.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/switch_to_frame/cross_origin.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/take_element_screenshot/iframe.py.ini"], "git_node": "99ebef30df041a048c8033a2b86f09af4001175c", "git_parents": ["eaea042471bfd675971af3514249176e756c0fca"], "node": "ab68f4c659a0c57fb977a624e273411844211ab6", "parents": ["f546a4efbe1ea8528eac3b60a82ffd0d048fe302"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070389 - Ensure Glean has something to delete in deletion-request test r=chumphreys\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325523\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/marionette/tests/client/test_fog_deletion_request_ping.py"], "git_node": "6277224809fadd167043a84794eae09a4f32a55d", "git_parents": ["99ebef30df041a048c8033a2b86f09af4001175c"], "node": "aeae53fc49e0a60356912616a66b87bab2c59d10", "parents": ["ab68f4c659a0c57fb977a624e273411844211ab6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068483 - [devtools] Don't check registered property syntax for declaration value using substitution functions. r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy.\n\nIn the StyleActor, we're checking for invalid at computed value time registered property declarations.\nWe were already skipping such check if the declaration was using var().\nThis patch extends the guard so we won't check for invalid syntax if\nthe value is using any of the substitution function (var()/attr()/env()).\nA test is added to make sure we're not displaying the IACVT warning icon\nin such case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324313\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_registered-custom-properties.js", "devtools/server/actors/style-rule.js"], "git_node": "284799d203f78e8ab28389bbd68a3b898e37287a", "git_parents": ["6277224809fadd167043a84794eae09a4f32a55d"], "node": "b4c42fb38b8d5e4299eab90a320359d47c6554f9", "parents": ["aeae53fc49e0a60356912616a66b87bab2c59d10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071659 - [loong64] Part 1: Move the definition of is_{,u}intN forward in Assembler-loong64.h. r=jandem\n\nThis helps reusing them in branch offset immediate classes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325643\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h"], "git_node": "f573f4d3074086cf2dba0787eb97ec99cd974c72", "git_parents": ["284799d203f78e8ab28389bbd68a3b898e37287a"], "node": "53266ee40bc8ff4ea11c9183dd82fac381160557", "parents": ["b4c42fb38b8d5e4299eab90a320359d47c6554f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071659 - [loong64] Part 2: Use is_{,u}intN helpers in immediate classes. r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325644\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h"], "git_node": "e7fdf82ab3647042ae9be25d4ea82cbb737cd9a7", "git_parents": ["f573f4d3074086cf2dba0787eb97ec99cd974c72"], "node": "57d731307f43b692b6d63417ab79f9c533b36208", "parents": ["53266ee40bc8ff4ea11c9183dd82fac381160557"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071659 - [loong64] Part 3: Fix data extraction of BOffImm16 and JOffImm26. r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325645\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h"], "git_node": "56cd74de6b23902e8f9cd97a8ff9f9496b72b3c5", "git_parents": ["e7fdf82ab3647042ae9be25d4ea82cbb737cd9a7"], "node": "09d04de93f5085d5e68fdcebaea811e0ae93e9aa", "parents": ["57d731307f43b692b6d63417ab79f9c533b36208"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071659 - [loong64] Part 4: Introduce ma_jump36 for +-128GiB PC-relative jumps. r=jandem\n\nThis is almost the CALL36 pseudoinstruction of the LoongArch assembly,\nbut with $zero as destination register.\n\nLink:\n https://github.com/loongson/la-asm-manual/blob/e706139e69868840ad33a72526ac072cc6a81510/adoc/CHAPTER-9.Pseudo_Instruction_Set/9.Pseudo_Instruction_Set.adoc#923-call36\n (\"Assembly Language Programming Guide for the LoongArch(tm)\n Architecture, CHAPTER 9. Macro Instructions, 9.2.3 call36\")\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325646\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.h"], "git_node": "aabacbb9013a95831f220105ae64109c42c59d24", "git_parents": ["56cd74de6b23902e8f9cd97a8ff9f9496b72b3c5"], "node": "f46fad6766a86ba8fc228cf7013a4f96f3c81029", "parents": ["09d04de93f5085d5e68fdcebaea811e0ae93e9aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071659 - [loong64] Part 5: Use ma_jump36 for intra-JIT jumps to Labels. r=jandem\n\nThis is possible since jump36 provides an offset range of +-128GiB,\nwhich is beyond the 2044MiB limit set by MaxCodeBytesPerProcess.\n\nSuggested-by: Yao Zi \u003cme@ziyao.cc\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325647\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/binop-divrem-with-constant-loong64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/binop-loong64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp"], "git_node": "b5f7627a384db4aa3a0d3b4780eaf86ed7dc0f23", "git_parents": ["aabacbb9013a95831f220105ae64109c42c59d24"], "node": "4fea2e61a8f1c788d65eac3520a565a81c439098", "parents": ["f46fad6766a86ba8fc228cf7013a4f96f3c81029"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071659 - [loong64] Part 6: (Drive-by) Fix typo: continous -\u003e continuous. r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325648\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp"], "git_node": "750858c6d1012ef6983443df5dbb6223f5a121d7", "git_parents": ["b5f7627a384db4aa3a0d3b4780eaf86ed7dc0f23"], "node": "9f711f1e0e7258146b4f86b258060e396f9cf5e6", "parents": ["4fea2e61a8f1c788d65eac3520a565a81c439098"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071659 - [loong64] Part 7: Introduce ma_call36 for +-128GiB PC-relative calls. r=jandem\n\nThis is the canonical CALL36 pseudoinstruction. See also Part 4.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325649\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.h"], "git_node": "c94f5e46d8f9b7f2b8c8419a613130c24993632f", "git_parents": ["750858c6d1012ef6983443df5dbb6223f5a121d7"], "node": "b99d721c1f6ce672efb1d9b74794c7c2876d4720", "parents": ["9f711f1e0e7258146b4f86b258060e396f9cf5e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071659 - [loong64] Part 8: Use ma_call36 for intra-JIT code region calls. r=jandem\n\nSimilar to Part 5, we can freely use CALL36 thanks to the upper bound of\nJIT-compiled code span by MaxCodeBytesPerProcess. Native calls are not\nsafe to do so.\n\nSuggested-by: Yao Zi \u003cme@ziyao.cc\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325650\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.h"], "git_node": "006d92eb90d8e199949a73f131f9f5796a7cf964", "git_parents": ["c94f5e46d8f9b7f2b8c8419a613130c24993632f"], "node": "2618f0a861b9b1d8ba701a6620a32a19335344b2", "parents": ["b99d721c1f6ce672efb1d9b74794c7c2876d4720"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cornelius Emase \u003ccorneliuslochipi@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070442 - Use bailoutFrom in arm64/x86 bailout helpers r=jandem\n\nMake bailoutCmp32, bailoutTest32, and bailoutCmpPtr use the same\npattern as the other backends: make a label, branch to it, call\nbailoutFrom. Deletes old per-architecture switch statements.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325550\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm/CodeGenerator-arm.h", "js/src/jit/arm64/CodeGenerator-arm64.h", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/CodeGenerator-x86-shared.h"], "git_node": "9ca9c1bbf40632e1ac3e6e2dc2e87de8f590dae5", "git_parents": ["006d92eb90d8e199949a73f131f9f5796a7cf964"], "node": "58a8520c7cd5d4df92f28b4bc062e5dd057de9eb", "parents": ["2618f0a861b9b1d8ba701a6620a32a19335344b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067526 - Avoid integer overflow when layouting mpadded using voffset or lspace. r=emilio,layout-reviewers\n\nProof 2 still pass without this patch, not sure it's because of UB or the value get clamped elsewhere.\n\nWe should get more offset when the container is bigger when using the same percentage, this match Chrome and WebKit.\n\nBut in Firefox, the offset is the same.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323149\n", "files": ["layout/mathml/nsMathMLmpaddedFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/attribute-overflow.html"], "git_node": "6b3a08b9e13bf9ef5ea73ab89538bb625c1491f0", "git_parents": ["9ca9c1bbf40632e1ac3e6e2dc2e87de8f590dae5"], "node": "59a2e535dbaa9812727aba4ca1c41e85af927806", "parents": ["58a8520c7cd5d4df92f28b4bc062e5dd057de9eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2062329 - Attribute MLModelHubService downloads to the requesting task. r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\" for causing bc failures @browser_speech_recognition_telemetry.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 3e87324fc356704eb8c9a8666c86503295f35b66.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2062329 - Measure inference cost and init failures in the HWInference process. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit 12943f71e1fc271d79c419b87a256b684b37adfd.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2062329 - Measure speech recognition latency in the content process. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit 009671a0e927ce4036daff7f88a2605bc7bb5955.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2062329 - Record speech recognition usage, outcomes and errors with Glean. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu,TravisLong\"\n\nThis reverts commit 286cd620fde00bb770535ee477322b76539b2ca1.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2062329 - Add use counters for the SpeechRecognition API. r=dom-core-reviewers,webidl,smaug\"\n\nThis reverts commit 57d8c026c74d1be249bb78fec439a14c5193bef6.\n", "files": ["dom/base/UseCounters.conf", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "dom/media/webspeech/metrics.yaml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionBackend.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionParent.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_inference_telemetry.js", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_telemetry.js", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_parakeet_e2e.html", "dom/webidl/SpeechRecognition.webidl", "toolkit/components/glean/metrics_index.py", "toolkit/components/ml/MLModelHubService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "3dcdff1226aef589fabe4f019a89ef149bf9bed5", "git_parents": ["6b3a08b9e13bf9ef5ea73ab89538bb625c1491f0"], "node": "ba47c6d5ec8beea552ed3c361b2dd09b02d5234b", "parents": ["59a2e535dbaa9812727aba4ca1c41e85af927806"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071004 - update wpt metadata.\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/web-extensions/browser.storage.extension.js.ini"], "git_node": "5ddda3cd69ad127a60c1546fe102b77d96831f9d", "git_parents": ["3dcdff1226aef589fabe4f019a89ef149bf9bed5"], "node": "920a716d206a6703c279eab4ee2457aee0325e3f", "parents": ["ba47c6d5ec8beea552ed3c361b2dd09b02d5234b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071707 - Give the ghost button's resting text color a high contrast value in chrome. r=mstriemer,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nOnly chrome changes: in-content already resolved both values through the brand layer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325787\n", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-brand.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/button.tokens.json"], "git_node": "7c5557a7170097c3c9dcc59bfd071aed69dd6724", "git_parents": ["5ddda3cd69ad127a60c1546fe102b77d96831f9d"], "node": "ac7f1306bc0baec141866a41f99d4ba429f888eb", "parents": ["920a716d206a6703c279eab4ee2457aee0325e3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071854 - Sync every tracked file under the skills directories. r=marco\n\nThe extension allowlist stood in for skipping junk, since the walk is filesystem-based; tracking is the better test for it, and an untracked file under a skill is a `.pyc`, a `.DS_Store` or an `*.orig` left by a conflict rather than anything a skill ships. Bug 2071793 proposed `get_ignored_files_finder()` instead, which lists every ignored path in the repo (6.5s and 107k paths against 0.27s for the tracked list, in a checkout whose objdir sits inside it) and which jj does not implement.\n\nA file is discovered only once it is `git add`ed, which is already what `--fix` needs to propagate an add.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325854\n", "files": ["tools/lint/agent-skills-sync.yml", "tools/lint/agent-skills-sync/__init__.py", "tools/lint/test/test_agent_skills_sync.py"], "git_node": "4c2ce73798f14ea4a27542af1bab62bc519f6147", "git_parents": ["7c5557a7170097c3c9dcc59bfd071aed69dd6724"], "node": "df34d2f466134cf08aeb3b3c32cfdfbc4aff4d06", "parents": ["ac7f1306bc0baec141866a41f99d4ba429f888eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062836 - Only suggest an address once when several of them fill the form identically. r=credential-management-reviewers,NeilDeakin\n\nA section made of a single email field, as seen on Google Forms, leaves\n_getSecondaryLabel() with no other field to show, so every stored address\nsharing that email produced an identical popup row.\n\nCollapse the addresses that would fill every field of the section with the same\nvalues, keeping the most recently used one. Rebuild _matchingProfiles from the\nrows that were emitted, since getCommentAt() looks the address up by row index;\nthat also stops rows from shifting onto the wrong address when one is skipped\nfor having no value for the focused field.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324308\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_email_dropdown.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_profileAutocompleteResult.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/ProfileAutoCompleteResult.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "a5e4780c7751304864c65cc3d6c704cffc0f9391", "git_parents": ["4c2ce73798f14ea4a27542af1bab62bc519f6147"], "node": "cff7d671145943d14abf4c6a402b42c2a2330976", "parents": ["df34d2f466134cf08aeb3b3c32cfdfbc4aff4d06"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067877 part 1 - Add clipboard_copy content analysis prefs, enterprise policy and telemetry. r=jneuberger,dlp-reviewers,jmendez,handyman\n\nAdds the configuration surface for analyzing clipboard copy operations:\n\n  browser.contentanalysis.interception_point.clipboard_copy.enabled\n  browser.contentanalysis.interception_point.clipboard_copy.plain_text_only\n\nand the corresponding ContentAnalysis.InterceptionPoints.ClipboardCopy\nenterprise policy. Later patches in this series read these prefs when\ndoing the copy analysis.\n\nenabled defaults to false so that existing content analysis deployments\nare unaffected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322719\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ExternalAgentBackend.cpp", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_content_analysis_policies.js"], "git_node": "20d706b79d13135ceaa879ac1f880214f73f2483", "git_parents": ["a5e4780c7751304864c65cc3d6c704cffc0f9391"], "node": "2a6535a01e2d56eb1c5f91bf46ffc71564d94427", "parents": ["cff7d671145943d14abf4c6a402b42c2a2330976"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067877 part 2 - Thread the request reason through clipboard content analysis requests. r=dlp-reviewers,handyman\n\nNo real behavior changes here, just setting up for later patches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322720\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysis.cpp", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/gtest/TestContentAnalysisTelemetry.cpp"], "git_node": "b9a15c157dd03a3f36562bb99326bc8bfe9e15fe", "git_parents": ["20d706b79d13135ceaa879ac1f880214f73f2483"], "node": "cb37a08fb1afa0bd495094f4abced36b60a21974", "parents": ["2a6535a01e2d56eb1c5f91bf46ffc71564d94427"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067877 part 3 - Say \"copy\" rather than \"paste\" in content analysis dialogs for copies. r=dlp-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,handyman\n\nNothing creates copy requests yet, so this has no effect until later patches.\nTests are in part 5.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322721\n", "files": ["browser/components/contentanalysis/content/ContentAnalysis.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysis.cpp", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysis.h", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysisUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/nsIContentAnalysis.idl", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_paste_changingclipboardexternal_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_paste_changingclipboardinternal_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_paste_chat_shortcuts.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_paste_file_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_paste_inputandtextarea_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_paste_inputandtextarea_iframe_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_paste_noformatting_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_paste_prompt_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_paste_redirect_focus_in_paste_event_listener.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_read_async_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/gtest/TestContentAnalysis.cpp", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/gtest/TestContentAnalysisTelemetry.cpp", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/xpcshell/test_wasm_backend.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/contentanalysis/contentanalysis.ftl"], "git_node": "3e89b801f7bb1558cde1e43a036bd160a82d0169", "git_parents": ["b9a15c157dd03a3f36562bb99326bc8bfe9e15fe"], "node": "7a72ac62fafd4e968badf3f9b285f919a4cb576f", "parents": ["cb37a08fb1afa0bd495094f4abced36b60a21974"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067877 part 4 - Give nsBaseClipboard::SetData an optional completion callback. r=edgar\n\nPreparation for the next patch, which needs to defer a clipboard write\nuntil an asynchronous content analysis check has answered.\n\nMoves the body of SetData into SetDataImpl, which takes an optional\ncompletion that is handed the final result. AsyncSetClipboardData::SetData\nnow notifies its nsIAsyncClipboardRequestCallback from that completion\ninstead of from the return value.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322722\n", "files": ["widget/nsBaseClipboard.cpp", "widget/nsBaseClipboard.h"], "git_node": "8f6e812bb0d4a0e1d7729ab426d2d27583c75cc3", "git_parents": ["3e89b801f7bb1558cde1e43a036bd160a82d0169"], "node": "0c1ec7518cd6ff0f29479749c535e572ee75a3b8", "parents": ["7a72ac62fafd4e968badf3f9b285f919a4cb576f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067877 part 5 - Analyze clipboard copies from web content. r=edgar,dlp-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,handyman,ipc-reviewers\n\nThe content analysis check is added to nsBaseClipboard::SetData since\nevery content-initiated clipboard write passes through there. When a copy\nneeds analyzing the write is held back as a PendingCopy, and the data\nreaches the clipboard only once the agent allows it.\n\nIn most cases the check is synchronous like paste is to avoid breaking\nwebsites that may expect copies to happen by the time the command is done.\n\nSome notes:\n - A newer write replaces the PendingCopy, which makes the older verdict a\n   no-op, so the write issued last always wins no matter which verdict\n   arrives first. EmptyClipboard and the destructor cancel pending copies.\n - A blocked copy replaces the clipboard contents with a localized notice\n   rather than leaving them alone, so that the user cannot silently paste\n   whatever was there beforehand.\n - As with paste, we don't analyze copies coming from chrome or\n   parent-rendered windows.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322723\n", "files": ["ipc/ipdl/sync-messages.ini", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysis.cpp", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysis.h", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_copy_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/clipboard_copy.html", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/contentanalysis/contentanalysis.ftl", "widget/ClipboardContentAnalysisParent.cpp", "widget/ClipboardContentAnalysisParent.h", "widget/PClipboardContentAnalysis.ipdl", "widget/nsBaseClipboard.cpp", "widget/nsBaseClipboard.h", "widget/nsClipboardHelper.cpp", "widget/nsClipboardProxy.cpp"], "git_node": "5a1b7e10cf4ef20da6b24a05dbf2988af7cc8eb3", "git_parents": ["8f6e812bb0d4a0e1d7729ab426d2d27583c75cc3"], "node": "291e2d0ab86c96bef9d2bb887fc7b6f4a1c478b1", "parents": ["0c1ec7518cd6ff0f29479749c535e572ee75a3b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067877 part 6 - Analyze clipboard copies from alert() and prompt() dialogs. r=dlp-reviewers,handyman\n\nLike paste, we need to treat alert()/confirm()/prompt() specially, since\nthey are from chrome which are normally exempt, but their content comes\nfrom a page.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322724\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysisUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_copy_prompt_content_analysis.js", "toolkit/components/prompts/content/commonDialog.js", "widget/nsBaseClipboard.h"], "git_node": "6ade0a1be950f57e92dd048fa515a2dbed224ce0", "git_parents": ["5a1b7e10cf4ef20da6b24a05dbf2988af7cc8eb3"], "node": "098bd7a12e05ebe6388b221dccfb5cf21ca259c1", "parents": ["291e2d0ab86c96bef9d2bb887fc7b6f4a1c478b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrej Glavic \u003caglavic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070172 - Bootstrap depot_tools before running fetch in the CaR and V8 toolchain builds r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\ndepot_tools commit d4e958941a37 made `fetch` and `ninja` run through the\nhermetic python-bin/python3 wrapper. That wrapper exits 1 when\npython3_bin_reldir.txt is absent, which is the case on a checkout that has\nnever been bootstrapped. Both toolchain scripts clone depot_tools and call\n`fetch` straight away, so every CaR build and linux64-custom-v8 started\nfailing a few seconds in, before producing any artifact.\n\nRun ensure_bootstrap before the first fetch. Unlike `gclient`, it bootstraps\nthe checkout in place without syncing the depot_tools repository, which would\notherwise make the revision recorded in DEPOT_TOOLS_REV stale. win64 is left\nalone because build-custom-car.sh already runs `gclient` before fetch there,\nand ensure_bootstrap deliberately skips the python bootstrap on Windows.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325088\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-custom-car.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-custom-v8.sh"], "git_node": "a8bbb36f6edcad65ce358a2b6c6252333ec70f44", "git_parents": ["6ade0a1be950f57e92dd048fa515a2dbed224ce0"], "node": "c37bdf5