998449636a48e2c4a362809085b600a0174e1f2-6-llvmorg-23-init-19482-g53d18800.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/rust-toolchain-b998449636a48e2c4a362809085b600a0174e1f2-6-llvmorg-23-init-19482-g53d18800.tar.xz,Win/rust-toolchain-b998449636a48e2c4a362809085b600a0174e1f2-6-llvmorg-23-init-19482-g53d18800.tar.xz..Linux_x64/rust-toolchain-0913b18e489ac1011b580e31fa5559654be12bfc-2-llvmorg-24-init-3796-g20e97c4b.tar.xz,Mac/rust-toolchain-0913b18e489ac1011b580e31fa5559654be12bfc-2-llvmorg-24-init-3796-g20e97c4b.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/rust-toolchain-0913b18e489ac1011b580e31fa5559654be12bfc-2-llvmorg-24-init-3796-g20e97c4b.tar.xz,Win/rust-toolchain-0913b18e489ac1011b580e31fa5559654be12bfc-2-llvmorg-24-init-3796-g20e97c4b.tar.xz\n    * src/third_party/siso/cipd: git_revision:1b1109fc6f5e177a439a195b87931224efc7a007..git_revision:bc45e8f67ae0f37d337190ad64aa8bb440c791eb\n    * src/third_party/turbine/cipd: iGvH-EemiZZWQXTgQ2YZQVRVkuH7tXiG5WjOXuHpXx0C..x7YCQkT0AvVA-g-D7_U-cmSVgjxgy3FefNyP30-KubkC\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/19842ca784..50941e9892\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/86ca5f98b6..fd4ce00a99/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: If8c29bfc95b5cdcaf2521b5e18955f0686ba97be\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496480\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48373}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "c0b4925905f935ac85102c068f999bae0e5d2302", "git_parents": ["93e1d01af517c176cb735c911c8853a52cd83aa3"], "node": "6f82dbcb31840054c6cd3d6e92746459603c78ae", "parents": ["8be0b9fbe68d9b4019765bcf3049cf7a319a4f42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from f43a2db583\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f43a2db5838141c3b631e8b08693e60015b2d578\n    Fix SSRC grouping in RTCP report plots\n\n    In CreateSenderAndReceiverReportPlot, report blocks were being grouped by\n    the SSRC of the RTCP packet sender (rtcp.sr.sender_ssrc() /\n    rtcp.rr.sender_ssrc()) instead of the SSRC of the RTP media stream being\n    reported on (block.source_ssrc()). As a result, when an RTCP packet contained\n    report blocks for multiple media SSRCs, all metrics were merged into a single\n    graph keyed by the RTCP sender SSRC.\n\n    Additionally, GetStreamName was invoked using the direction of the RTCP\n    packet rather than the direction of the reported media stream (which is\n    the opposite direction).\n\n    Bug: webrtc:547965202\n    Change-Id: I8cecc72c8c1fe6ca618a89a69109668c2a543dc5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496460\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48374}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/rtc_event_log_visualizer/analyze_rtp_rtcp.cc"], "git_node": "014b70caab8d7371a92002f407fca6f340432d6d", "git_parents": ["c0b4925905f935ac85102c068f999bae0e5d2302"], "node": "fa4d361763b22c8d251fd14b40762eb7ae4557eb", "parents": ["6f82dbcb31840054c6cd3d6e92746459603c78ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from e73976c996\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e73976c996d3241580ea004f73cc5ff95cf9ef47\n    Revalidate STUN response integrity when password differs from request\n\n    When an ice-pwd update / ICE restart happens between sending a STUN ping\n    request and receiving its response, Connection::OnReadPacket pre-validates\n    the response packet using the remote candidate's new password, setting\n    msg-\u003eintegrity() to kIntegrityOk with the new password.\n\n    When StunRequestManager::CheckResponse processes this message,\n    msg-\u003epassword() differs from request-\u003emsg()-\u003epassword(). Previously,\n    this fell through to RTC_CHECK_NOTREACHED(), causing a crash.\n\n    This CL fixes the issue by calling RevalidateMessageIntegrity with the\n    request's password whenever msg-\u003epassword() does not match the request's\n    password.\n\n    Bug: b/522975734\n    Change-Id: Ifa80ccd97451cb74df75530c9d23cbf5863f0ce5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/493580\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48375}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_request.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_request_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "3ed5740f6a4cbe7989166a1d1f0f0ac669f5a93a", "git_parents": ["014b70caab8d7371a92002f407fca6f340432d6d"], "node": "efcc44afc4af43f714ced342a49f623ff11a9c59", "parents": ["fa4d361763b22c8d251fd14b40762eb7ae4557eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from e12c39e03c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e12c39e03c3dcab594f73a1e524b1f2c17dfdcb8\n    Remove inactive owner from OWNERS files\n\n    Remove srte@webrtc.org (inactive as reviewer since 4+ years) from OWNERS\n    files and update unit OWNERS to list Internals Area Lead\n    eshr@webrtc.org.\n\n    Bug: b/483056241\n    Change-Id: Icdd1c8c0e6fcdc19b6aed876b15eba379aab6f10\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496380\n    Auto-Submit: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48376}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/test/OWNERS", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/units/OWNERS", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/experiments/OWNERS", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/units/OWNERS", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/OWNERS", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/scenario/OWNERS"], "git_node": "b91c8c30e57f20bf30866e6858a0d7a6527c1e8f", "git_parents": ["3ed5740f6a4cbe7989166a1d1f0f0ac669f5a93a"], "node": "b0695b87e08604b4727cfd04c5055fcbec195105", "parents": ["efcc44afc4af43f714ced342a49f623ff11a9c59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3fcbddbc27\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3fcbddbc2728c740e19edaf157c298351336dc4d\n    Add stopped() to FrameDecodeScheduler, VideoStreamBufferController\n\n    The property indicates whether the scheduler or controller has been\n    stopped. Landing this separately as part of a larger change.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I8edf41be7e6b10436fdff67fe7964e03a8fad882\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496120\n    Commit-Queue: Stefan Holmer \u003cstefan@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Stefan Holmer \u003cstefan@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48377}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0057.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0059.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0064.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/decode_synchronizer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/decode_synchronizer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/frame_decode_scheduler.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/task_queue_frame_decode_scheduler.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/task_queue_frame_decode_scheduler.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_buffer_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_buffer_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_buffer_controller_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "269ca53e33be1f6891ea37627267dc4e3db92a71", "git_parents": ["b91c8c30e57f20bf30866e6858a0d7a6527c1e8f"], "node": "ae0ff8237eba36d535bc5d5e9ac711b6162c9d72", "parents": ["b0695b87e08604b4727cfd04c5055fcbec195105"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0fb9275433\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored 45a54bd886.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0fb9275433b8692e9b0a3f94d806248dee3fc22d\n    Revert \"Include outstanding data in RetransmissionQueue handover state.\"\n\n    This reverts commit 45a54bd88620504498cc47fc9bb77517da9a108d.\n\n    Reason for revert: Breaks downstream test.\n\n    Failure Link: \u003cLINK TO FAILURE\u003e\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Include outstanding data in RetransmissionQueue handover state.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e This adds enable_handover_with_outstanding_data,\n    \u003e and wires up outstanding data and send queue handover.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: webrtc:477364365\n    \u003e Change-Id: I70433e4f7b88e7870ae9641993fabea38f4641a3\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/452060\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Victor Boivie \u003cboivie@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Priya Rajarathinam \u003crajarathinam@google.com\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48370}\n\n    Bug: webrtc:477364365\n    Change-Id: Ibee9ebbb25fb461db1952818e453e02541671b2f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496680\n    Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48378}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/0fb9275433.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch"], "git_node": "cc493557d7066bfe0fba82a4e2fdf5db1da1a49c", "git_parents": ["269ca53e33be1f6891ea37627267dc4e3db92a71"], "node": "eb08fc6e297c869ceec07c812572e33d32ac25a0", "parents": ["ae0ff8237eba36d535bc5d5e9ac711b6162c9d72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from cd81696dce\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/cd81696dce9728804fb4797dae3b969947e15da1\n    Add PhasedSequenceChecker to VideoReceiver2\n\n    Introduce PhasedSequenceChecker to allow updating decoder settings on\n    the worker thread before decoding starts, and verifying correct sequence\n    usage afterwards.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:510361625, webrtc:42233985\n    Change-Id: I5ec9364f828ecb71c95994b95315be50c3e5d098\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496140\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48379}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/video_receiver2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/video_receiver2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0037.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0042.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0057.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0093.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0095.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0141.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2.cc"], "git_node": "13b9d76b91976d5e90d649c2f468e4f2fdc1fd87", "git_parents": ["cc493557d7066bfe0fba82a4e2fdf5db1da1a49c"], "node": "0562ac15318d3d6dafebba3505925ccb00c382fa", "parents": ["eb08fc6e297c869ceec07c812572e33d32ac25a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9b33b6c524\n\nWe cherry-picked this in bug 2059127.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9b33b6c524a185a20586741af262370291000b69\n    Screen capture: validate and snapshot cursor and videocrop metadata\n\n    Cap cursor_meta-\u003esize against the negotiated maximum and validate that\n    bitmap_offset and the bitmap pixel data offset both point within the\n    metadata region before forming pointers and copying data.\n\n    Copy cursor and videocrop metadata headers from shared memory into\n    local storage before validating and using their fields, so the\n    producer cannot modify them between validation and use.\n\n    Bug: chromium:546101645, chromium:546124538\n    Change-Id: I114b00ee9f1563b11f99e6b2914143e61131cded\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496060\n    Reviewed-by: Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jan Grulich \u003cgrulja@gmail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48380}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/9b33b6c524.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0072.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0073.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0125.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0147.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0148.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0149.patch"], "git_node": "9e38f5376d5b29847f992a744d5ef290ce59fb04", "git_parents": ["13b9d76b91976d5e90d649c2f468e4f2fdc1fd87"], "node": "8b86b7b2fb2f07cff51efa8a16ca52fea109417f", "parents": ["0562ac15318d3d6dafebba3505925ccb00c382fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0257403734\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0257403734a9e8d45e62797313751d36b753e7d8\n    Clean up CPPLINT_EXCEPTIONS in PRESUBMIT.py\n\n    Remove non-existent paths and lint-clean files from CPPLINT_EXCEPTIONS.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42235102\n    Change-Id: I2c41f5fa4b40fc4ea25ceadb9a998ff034d2f835\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496540\n    Reviewed-by: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48381}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "3596a0fa212cdef96873e9a7952f7c80e519ac23", "git_parents": ["9e38f5376d5b29847f992a744d5ef290ce59fb04"], "node": "07540fdc1d9cb2adb47026d4872ea1cc6bb404d5", "parents": ["8b86b7b2fb2f07cff51efa8a16ca52fea109417f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 24b08c9e2e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/24b08c9e2e901576a12eed498490504b056cdbcb\n    Roll chromium_revision fd4ce00a99..57ed38e9f7 (1681235:1682199)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/fd4ce00a99..57ed38e9f7\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/fd4ce00a99..57ed38e9f7\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/8f616df949..8a8d38839a\n    * src/buildtools/linux64: git_revision:1c79e13d17a1760d6c6401c90061411842bd4881..git_revision:2481edf51ea7789c66aede9725ff0e202dfae812\n    * src/buildtools/mac: git_revision:1c79e13d17a1760d6c6401c90061411842bd4881..git_revision:2481edf51ea7789c66aede9725ff0e202dfae812\n    * src/buildtools/win: git_revision:1c79e13d17a1760d6c6401c90061411842bd4881..git_revision:2481edf51ea7789c66aede9725ff0e202dfae812\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/8e1fd7aa29..5d7b18687e\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/f75f983415..b96dbc743d\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/e8f417d40f..8f1da83155\n    * src/third_party/android_sdk/public: zpvajSBSzdpfFqTOmyRC3nQ2h6OxCa1N5P_2qPaz-pAC..vO477CZmV97fP5b9ZnNGZYK-23J4g_6FPPhhdSNvTfsC\n    * src/third_party/boringssl/src: https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl.git/+log/bb2b3174e6..d9cace2c91\n    * src/third_party/compiler-rt/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/compiler-rt.git/+log/0ccff08262..66e09cd480\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/8ff4a322a1..ce5a30784f\n    * src/third_party/eigen3/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen.git/+log/0192017d2c..7c8275ef88\n    * src/third_party/fuzztest/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/fuzztest.git/+log/8bc765afc3..d579aa9e14\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/3ab6b6bbad..c6b6da1dd0\n    * src/third_party/harfbuzz/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz.git/+log/dfdc088c4d..886fc1e645\n    * src/third_party/libvpx/source/libvpx: https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libvpx.git/+log/8729fc25ea..5ae5478f99\n    * src/third_party/libyuv: https://chromium.googlesource.com/libyuv/libyuv.git/+log/87c797b3c2..26e56be0f9\n    * src/third_party/llvm-libc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libc.git/+log/20fd93c3ba..4cd0847bb0\n    * src/third_party/perfetto: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/perfetto.git/+log/b5c58adf53..de794788d5\n    * src/third_party/r8/cipd: q7wBY9a5xN_VZyRneV14Sm1lrX9TTSaPJJMOso9kCCMC..gfbyk0tBsuxhygIXcmbMgdAWUL9LrI7cF4qPTEAdKTMC\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/50941e9892..b4235c8a2c\n    * src/tools/luci-go: git_revision:2de3d5d5b1e9c5e75f930c363904413000823425..git_revision:0e4cb6152e3aee32eca411edf436f6017c39068a\n    * src/tools/luci-go: git_revision:2de3d5d5b1e9c5e75f930c363904413000823425..git_revision:0e4cb6152e3aee32eca411edf436f6017c39068a\n    * src/tools/luci-go: git_revision:2de3d5d5b1e9c5e75f930c363904413000823425..git_revision:0e4cb6152e3aee32eca411edf436f6017c39068a\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/fd4ce00a99..57ed38e9f7/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: If2d602b72d8e0f13246c99ae836f8ba5dceece10\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496661\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48382}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "6708e8a5e0f30e6f95bc4cf7640c7880b5dd5226", "git_parents": ["3596a0fa212cdef96873e9a7952f7c80e519ac23"], "node": "8262f2d87385f88a70c41975e0d3176f9882b52c", "parents": ["07540fdc1d9cb2adb47026d4872ea1cc6bb404d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from c84dbe590a\n\nWe cherry-picked this in bug 2054622.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c84dbe590a5519bc1404a268dd8816088ffe8980\n    PipeWire: encapsulate mmap in ScopedBuf and fix mapoffset handling\n\n    Move mmap into ScopedBuf::initialize so callers no longer manage mmap\n    flags and cleanup directly. Use MAP_PRIVATE for read-only MemFd\n    consumers and MAP_SHARED for DmaBuf and read-write consumers. Fix\n    screen capture's double mapoffset application by passing the offset\n    to mmap directly. Add AccessMode and BufferType enums for clarity\n    and delete copy/move to prevent double-munmap.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225999\n    Change-Id: Id37354c20a4a520908c09fd3fa9d318e1caf033e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496720\n    Reviewed-by: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48383}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/c84dbe590a.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0072.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0073.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0125.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0147.patch"], "git_node": "2c1417058b9287bb4fcb9959d8ff8007ee2212b5", "git_parents": ["6708e8a5e0f30e6f95bc4cf7640c7880b5dd5226"], "node": "0571178b6d036a35048a9bd17d72d22f13b5c628", "parents": ["8262f2d87385f88a70c41975e0d3176f9882b52c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 984444e8b0\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/984444e8b0b13058b1bae93b9a6e909d30bc7556\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-08-20T04:08:16).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ie7ef4705abb4d63ec96b0f21e47db4f4b9012ac8\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496840\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48384}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "ecb0fa050e06bc97a3ea9a4ee5a691f93aaab03f", "git_parents": ["2c1417058b9287bb4fcb9959d8ff8007ee2212b5"], "node": "8500d175ba65eec44a672a0c8701b6eb4cf66e0e", "parents": ["0571178b6d036a35048a9bd17d72d22f13b5c628"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1462d73a7f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1462d73a7f79bc76d999de9f1aa0c502afc66050\n    Add unit test for CPPLINT_EXCEPTIONS and format presubmit test files\n\n    Add CheckCpplintExceptionsTest in presubmit_test.py to verify that all\n    paths in CPPLINT_EXCEPTIONS exist on disk.\n\n    Format presubmit_test.py and presubmit_test_mocks.py with 4-space\n    indentation, add score=no to pylint configs, and list presubmit test\n    files in PYLINT_OLD_STYLE.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42235102\n    Change-Id: Iab8b42cd21b02f55c25a1d5afe9c7ebcf5c48a32\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496740\n    Reviewed-by: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48385}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pylintrc_old_style"], "git_node": "bdd487882f48c251dafb78f628c4556e75cf3fc7", "git_parents": ["ecb0fa050e06bc97a3ea9a4ee5a691f93aaab03f"], "node": "1572e08b91631c81f57eeb36b4f454017a28618a", "parents": ["8500d175ba65eec44a672a0c8701b6eb4cf66e0e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from bff4a9e71e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bff4a9e71e3813d65d6382997ed9a42edf61946c\n    Allow allocation probing outside ALR by default\n\n    When max_total_allocated_bitrate increases, allow allocation probes\n    even outside ALR, controlled by probe_max_allocation_without_alr\n    (default true). Only probe on increases so bitrate decreases do not\n    trigger probes. Update BweRampUpWhenCapacityIncrease to sample BWE\n    before the capacity increase scheduled 3s after the first sent packet.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:534082923\n    Change-Id: I01fffea8d806317e70531e77a1f5e76c1fa15ef0\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/489040\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48386}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc/probe_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc/probe_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc/probe_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/bwe_ramp_up_test.cc"], "git_node": "83a6c20601eebe8a004bbb574268d4ba7d79c4d9", "git_parents": ["bdd487882f48c251dafb78f628c4556e75cf3fc7"], "node": "28968609518a88464f422cd76db147a5a848d59a", "parents": ["1572e08b91631c81f57eeb36b4f454017a28618a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 538a7c6681\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/538a7c6681472459a4ff0663a012e6a9684fecd0\n    Video capture: stop calling SetApplyRotation from capture backend\n\n    SetApplyRotation is a client-level opt-in to have libyuv physically\n    rotate pixels. Keep SetCaptureRotation so the transform is still\n    reported, but leave the pixel-rotation decision to the caller.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:15464\n    Change-Id: Ibb3bd3baf191442494d49e7498d2b0276c6ce8d9\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496860\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jan Grulich \u003cgrulja@gmail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48387}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_capture/linux/video_capture_pipewire.cc"], "git_node": "29b968608feb4c8b0ea3bf305c71b31a004597a7", "git_parents": ["83a6c20601eebe8a004bbb574268d4ba7d79c4d9"], "node": "cc08a06ea654ff5a9b2001afe00eaf35697e9187", "parents": ["28968609518a88464f422cd76db147a5a848d59a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6150b82ebb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6150b82ebb22bc9557896c4f79de0fafae598446\n    Delete deprecated AudioEncoder::OnReceivedUplinkBandwidth method\n\n    OnReceivedUplinkBandwidth is deprecated in favor of OnReceivedUplinkAllocation.\n    This CL removes the deprecated method declaration and implementation.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I03f20f40008a0f20571cf22cacb1cf9dfd4c2213\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/495700\n    Reviewed-by: Jakob Ivarsson\u200e \u003cjakobi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48388}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio_codecs/audio_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio_codecs/audio_encoder.h"], "git_node": "2527c5815078190550a31233453d50ad07424efd", "git_parents": ["29b968608feb4c8b0ea3bf305c71b31a004597a7"], "node": "f4d39dd861c76e96d480a10fd2d1a948802d1074", "parents": ["cc08a06ea654ff5a9b2001afe00eaf35697e9187"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 79ddeae52f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/79ddeae52f915e180374a4fe453cd5046e0971bf\n    Use receive clock when calculating receive rate in SCReAM.\n\n    Previously, UpdateReceiveRate() used feedback_time (sender's local clock)\n    to measure elapsed time between feedback reports for received_rate_.\n    If feedback was delayed or paused, this could lead to inaccurate received\n    rate calculations.\n\n    This change uses the latest received packet's timestamp from the feedback\n    report to measure the elapsed duration on the remote receive clock.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I1268363ed1159b49c5ec5f48120c753044e1bbd9\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496781\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48389}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_feedback.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_feedback.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "7219b525d4f8fc8bcb008be50f804a3091c0361e", "git_parents": ["2527c5815078190550a31233453d50ad07424efd"], "node": "105a493acbaf328b44144fab6a318ce90655ce97", "parents": ["f4d39dd861c76e96d480a10fd2d1a948802d1074"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from b0904c6d8d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b0904c6d8dbbbee20df31c44c8f19524e2439d9a\n    Extract utility code in VideoReceiveStream2 into helper methods.\n\n    Introduce VerifyNoDuplicatePayloadTypes and ConfigureCodecs helper\n    methods in VideoReceiveStream2. This facilitates upcoming changes in\n    this class that will require the same check/operation.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I0fb9622350a79309996de1d8d2c41ce9266c5efa\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496200\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Stefan Holmer \u003cstefan@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48390}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0037.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0042.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0057.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2.h"], "git_node": "d7bfd770e469272efae7732d52746237cdb166c3", "git_parents": ["7219b525d4f8fc8bcb008be50f804a3091c0361e"], "node": "c7f34b1622881efe9e3be2264f50e0b4221605a0", "parents": ["105a493acbaf328b44144fab6a318ce90655ce97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6cb8d652d8\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6cb8d652d8ddc645b5a1933b42c8b1d5c1c76b6c\n    Notify BitrateAllocator and VideoStreamEncoder when cwnd_reduce_ratio changes.\n\n    CongestionControlHandler::GetUpdate() previously only checked target_rate,\n    loss_rate_ratio, and round_trip_time for changes, completely ignoring\n    cwnd_reduce_ratio. As a result, when cwnd_reduce_ratio changed while bitrate\n    and RTT were constant, GetUpdate() returned std::nullopt, silently dropping\n    the pushback update without forwarding it to BitrateAllocator and VideoStreamEncoder.\n\n    This change includes cwnd_reduce_ratio in the change check and adds unit tests.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: Ib9bf04141be71b589839ddb7136d1b9617eb8bec\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496880\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48391}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/rtp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/rtp/control_handler.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/rtp/control_handler_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "760f64ca604d3138c9974ad93c90e0a96da683ce", "git_parents": ["d7bfd770e469272efae7732d52746237cdb166c3"], "node": "c01256b973894ab02d48bf138259c5f558961348", "parents": ["c7f34b1622881efe9e3be2264f50e0b4221605a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from d7d3681589\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d7d36815896d5914ab0fab58ebbe660a7250b6bd\n    Guard config_ and extract const member variables in VideoReceiveStream2\n\n    Guard config_ with worker_sequence_checker_ and extract const member\n    variables remote_ssrc_, renderer_, decoder_factory_, and\n    require_frame_encryption_. Remove const_cast usages in setter methods.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: Ia5a1d5ca4949f7b7b55282943c0c62ece973b587\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496220\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48392}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0037.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0042.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0057.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2.h"], "git_node": "e0215890312a377fa281c25c21bfeffd71f19eb9", "git_parents": ["760f64ca604d3138c9974ad93c90e0a96da683ce"], "node": "59b6d4b610cb621ab8704d3cee273963af618a92", "parents": ["c01256b973894ab02d48bf138259c5f558961348"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from e6fa5cc760\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e6fa5cc7607949054d245e56cc4b4e7d3aeab49b\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-08-21T04:06:19).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I006a948c9fe45748acc4674058afb2c97a032766\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496940\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48393}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "642c369e61fdfde9edac5f432a833d5c3d403d5c", "git_parents": ["e0215890312a377fa281c25c21bfeffd71f19eb9"], "node": "516092751604b78fdfbc6c714055d71ae90cb98e", "parents": ["59b6d4b610cb621ab8704d3cee273963af618a92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 71012ee73c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/71012ee73c7e4f5218191bd1c38c10bbbfe9015c\n    Remove obsolete libyuv InitCpuFlags TSan suppression\n\n    libyuv now uses C11 atomics (__atomic_load_n and __atomic_store_n) to\n    guard TestCpuFlag and SetCpuFlags for cpu_info_.\n\n    Bug: chromium:42280450\n    Change-Id: Ib01fdd683ff77457f4aeda98f979725f0e8b2ea8\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496960\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48394}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/sanitizers/tsan_suppressions_webrtc.cc"], "git_node": "06ec4512447dc380955a7532ef624342d34e5efe", "git_parents": ["642c369e61fdfde9edac5f432a833d5c3d403d5c"], "node": "0788c152a65f0bc8a6ae352d22f74e02ae617978", "parents": ["516092751604b78fdfbc6c714055d71ae90cb98e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 06ed2fa13e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/06ed2fa13e6e2c32549f1bb2ac04c867a28e8bcf\n    Support in-place updates for receive codecs in RtpVideoStreamReceiver2\n\n    Add SetReceiveCodecs to RtpVideoStreamReceiver2 to allow reconfiguring\n    receive codecs in-place. Previously, modifying the set of active codecs\n    required clearing and re-registering everything, which wiped the packet\n    buffer and could disrupt the assembly of in-flight video frames.\n\n    Unchanged codecs now preserve their depacketizer instances and state by\n    checking if their payload configuration has actually changed. Codecs no\n    longer present in the new configuration are removed, while new ones are\n    added seamlessly without clearing unchanged state or dropping packets.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I4bcc42cc542dc4704174b66b2bfa40937d43e928\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496260\n    Reviewed-by: Stefan Holmer \u003cstefan@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48395}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0030.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0035.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0037.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0042.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0057.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0058.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0059.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0060.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0139.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "528fc0e03132d5afbcce6942b8385d64cae06dbe", "git_parents": ["06ec4512447dc380955a7532ef624342d34e5efe"], "node": "3437fb199c6605ce3f308c94ab842cb726cae4ae", "parents": ["0788c152a65f0bc8a6ae352d22f74e02ae617978"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 33e6cec2de\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/33e6cec2deecbb0d0b8e8ab0004c322e5e086b9e\n    video: treat an encoding maxBitrate of zero as configured, not unset\n\n    VideoStream::max_bitrate_bps uses -1 as its unset sentinel, but several\n    checks tested \"\u003e 0\" where they meant \"is configured\". An explicit\n    maxBitrate of 0 was therefore collapsed with unset and silently\n    uncapped: a single video encoding got the ~424 kbps default bitrate\n    instead.\n\n    Zero is a valid value per\n    https://w3c.github.io/webrtc-pc/#dom-rtcrtpencodingparameters-maxbitrate\n    The resulting stream is configured 0/0/0 and then floored at 30 kbps by\n    the bitrate allocator, which matches \"even a bitrate of zero will allow\n    sending one frame\".\n\n    IsLayerActive() in webrtc_video_engine.cc still treats a zero max\n    bitrate as inactive. It only feeds reconfigure detection, so it is left\n    for a follow-up.\n\n    Bug: chromium:501879826,webrtc:545191307\n    Change-Id: Ic404b5ea9d420e68c711c9ca8eef57a2417239af\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496500\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48396}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/video_codec_initializer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/config/encoder_stream_factory.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/config/encoder_stream_factory_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "825100f117f02b9074ef38ef280f9c3e5caba5fb", "git_parents": ["528fc0e03132d5afbcce6942b8385d64cae06dbe"], "node": "5a6111138cdc19eecdd9c8266104be98a0a8d192", "parents": ["3437fb199c6605ce3f308c94ab842cb726cae4ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from e9b79b4201\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e9b79b4201914ce8b96b84fa058cfc2fa9c308b3\n    Remove obsolete LSan suppressions\n\n    Remove LSan suppressions for HttpServer, HttpClient (StartDNSLookup),\n    and unstarted_task_test which were deleted from WebRTC.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42228746, webrtc:42229088\n    Change-Id: I18feca1f9ecd11f294c9a25e23a937efea8c0d2b\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497020\n    Auto-Submit: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48397}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/sanitizers/lsan_suppressions_webrtc.cc"], "git_node": "5be974313690510221664f5af8809f00bc58fcd4", "git_parents": ["825100f117f02b9074ef38ef280f9c3e5caba5fb"], "node": "f8d3151dc485129afeca7e6a3938c976995bad3e", "parents": ["5a6111138cdc19eecdd9c8266104be98a0a8d192"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from e824d282f3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e824d282f3b8da9ec95f90d090dc69db6d0a7562\n    Remove obsolete absl Waiter::Post TSan suppression\n\n    Abseil refactored Waiter into dedicated platform classes (FutexWaiter,\n    PthreadWaiter, etc.). The symbol\n    absl::synchronization_internal::Waiter::Post is no longer emitted.\n\n    Bug: chromium:40161385\n    Change-Id: Icae9412fe4819beaa14edce2e1ebd49fc6a9d879\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497000\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48398}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/sanitizers/tsan_suppressions_webrtc.cc"], "git_node": "e3244f42a797a6e99b4ee0259c1c5d9ad218b186", "git_parents": ["5be974313690510221664f5af8809f00bc58fcd4"], "node": "d98419829282180daf6128c532c0d3599dd37670", "parents": ["f8d3151dc485129afeca7e6a3938c976995bad3e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from c48c416cf7\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c48c416cf75a3886ed7c65d4181be49b94ea73bb\n    Clean up launched experiment WebRTC-Video-CalculatePsnr\n\n    Bug: webrtc:388070060\n    Change-Id: Ib822c11ee5d3ffd7a071999b28470263e8f10514\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497060\n    Auto-Submit: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48399}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/experiments/field_trials.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_speed_config_factory.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_speed_config_factory.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_speed_config_factory_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/h264/h264_encoder_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/h264/h264_encoder_impl.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp8/libvpx_vp8_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp8/libvpx_vp8_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/libvpx_vp9_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/libvpx_vp9_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/frame_sampler.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0018.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0093.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0095.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0124.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0133.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0135.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0141.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/experiments/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/experiments/psnr_experiment.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/experiments/psnr_experiment.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/experiments/psnr_experiment_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/vp9_encoder_references_fuzzer.cc"], "git_node": "59301537b5a37876e0b848dfed2d560b5b32e46d", "git_parents": ["e3244f42a797a6e99b4ee0259c1c5d9ad218b186"], "node": "ef8cd1d8f898506db0780940d5d579012d8e7ae6", "parents": ["d98419829282180daf6128c532c0d3599dd37670"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from c48c416cf7 - moz.build file updates\n", "files": ["CLOBBER", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/experiments/psnr_experiment_gn/moz.build"], "git_node": "49b7c8a718a36269fd01f0587bb92c9046cf2e49", "git_parents": ["59301537b5a37876e0b848dfed2d560b5b32e46d"], "node": "3b373211e4fb1ca254c88f0581a2f8e7d5634c12", "parents": ["ef8cd1d8f898506db0780940d5d579012d8e7ae6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from fe2e8bba90\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/fe2e8bba90857aa9a498b14a72916484cf3b5a5d\n    Reland \"Include outstanding data in RetransmissionQueue handover state.\"\n\n    This reverts commit 0fb9275433b8692e9b0a3f94d806248dee3fc22d.\n\n    Reason for revert: In a different change, protobuf serialization was added for the new fields in dcsctp_handover_state.\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Revert \"Include outstanding data in RetransmissionQueue handover state.\"\n    \u003e\n    \u003e This reverts commit 45a54bd88620504498cc47fc9bb77517da9a108d.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Reason for revert: Breaks downstream test.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Failure Link: \u003cLINK TO FAILURE\u003e\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Original change's description:\n    \u003e \u003e Include outstanding data in RetransmissionQueue handover state.\n    \u003e \u003e\n    \u003e \u003e This adds enable_handover_with_outstanding_data,\n    \u003e \u003e and wires up outstanding data and send queue handover.\n    \u003e \u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Bug: webrtc:477364365\n    \u003e \u003e Change-Id: I70433e4f7b88e7870ae9641993fabea38f4641a3\n    \u003e \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/452060\n    \u003e \u003e Reviewed-by: Victor Boivie \u003cboivie@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Commit-Queue: Priya Rajarathinam \u003crajarathinam@google.com\u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48370}\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: webrtc:477364365\n    \u003e Change-Id: Ibee9ebbb25fb461db1952818e453e02541671b2f\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496680\n    \u003e Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    \u003e Auto-Submit: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48378}\n\n    Bug: webrtc:477364365\n    Change-Id: I4a461e382547860be13c0313f606bab067bad542\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496920\n    Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Priya Rajarathinam \u003crajarathinam@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Victor Boivie \u003cboivie@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48400}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/dcsctp_socket.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/stream_reset_handler_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/transmission_control_block.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/transmission_control_block.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/retransmission_queue.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/retransmission_queue.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/retransmission_queue_test.cc"], "git_node": "c57bbe8535e2f158f97d7c735b4909577260079e", "git_parents": ["49b7c8a718a36269fd01f0587bb92c9046cf2e49"], "node": "54301b5096b76dc639e8d15b5762b95e8d726f23", "parents": ["3b373211e4fb1ca254c88f0581a2f8e7d5634c12"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from f3ae3eb62e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f3ae3eb62e2a5609d77fd30de8e8e2a04f28ee58\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-08-22T04:08:42).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I138dad4bfd1327b04bd73b11a0937608742ff148\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497200\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48401}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "ec776f86338357ad8546b1e27b6723289f15ca55", "git_parents": ["c57bbe8535e2f158f97d7c735b4909577260079e"], "node": "0931444b9ba12ea5e60d43b290ee6bdf152eafb5", "parents": ["54301b5096b76dc639e8d15b5762b95e8d726f23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from f83dda82fb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f83dda82fb34ada6954b08f595d450e471994564\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-08-23T04:11:18).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ibbd29048830d5707da4e310876757452b2ea57b6\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497220\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48402}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "c8eb044e88d1e25b64a8d1e942f9c190abdfbf1f", "git_parents": ["ec776f86338357ad8546b1e27b6723289f15ca55"], "node": "26ac9cc6d99bbb68e4c4a436fa8dcf64dcfe960d", "parents": ["0931444b9ba12ea5e60d43b290ee6bdf152eafb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 2d7d346588\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/2d7d346588d47a68371d357f1ab942c7b55988bf\n    dtls-in-stun: Disable testcases that can no longer occur\n\n    With the introduction of a SDP negotiation part into\n    dtls-in-stun the scenario when the callee (peer that get\n    the offer) does not know the dtls-in-stun capability of the\n    caller (peer creating the offer) simply does not exist.\n\n    The caller though if having dtls-in-stun=true must\n    accept data (or lack there of) before the answer\n    SDP arrives since the callee might start sending stun pings\n    before the answer arrives.\n\n    This patch does not modify any code but only\n    disables 184 test cases. The value of this\n    is that it will make it easier to cleanup TODOS\n    and some minor bugs in the code.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:367395350\n    Change-Id: If97f3d499533c531ce232b1df0e65ba0aecac860\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496160\n    Commit-Queue: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48403}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/dtls/dtls_ice_integration_fixture.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/dtls/dtls_transport_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "c2e2e165703e3b93c02cf0aaee6e6e100ebcebd9", "git_parents": ["c8eb044e88d1e25b64a8d1e942f9c190abdfbf1f"], "node": "233e3b23c43e6162b6116e60bba05307f8f8b9a2", "parents": ["26ac9cc6d99bbb68e4c4a436fa8dcf64dcfe960d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 16c9fde7cb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/16c9fde7cb5f773f6cff1c6942da350f3402caf3\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-08-24T04:10:34).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I917b0b8808022760d8ea3b41bd92530f018cd0d4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497240\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48404}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "c6903598c780ba793a597a0b67e948e33936ec84", "git_parents": ["c2e2e165703e3b93c02cf0aaee6e6e100ebcebd9"], "node": "6d0d48b64dfe17c601839c733db0ab5c3dcdc786", "parents": ["233e3b23c43e6162b6116e60bba05307f8f8b9a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 14692c9ebb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/14692c9ebb72a3c9e078df621dca059dac456000\n    Remove obsolete LSan suppressions\n\n    Remove LSan suppressions for VideoEngineTest, VideoMediaChannelTest,\n    WebRtcVideoCapturerTest, and WebRtcVideoEngineTestFake which were\n    removed during media engine refactoring.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I1f2da8769d8212a1e991292357b124e14f2bdd13\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497040\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48405}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/sanitizers/lsan_suppressions_webrtc.cc"], "git_node": "947b610d0aba7432e717f8c5bc200699d9e5eb59", "git_parents": ["c6903598c780ba793a597a0b67e948e33936ec84"], "node": "6e8896cf3310cd501aae66ecb0f97daff335cd22", "parents": ["6d0d48b64dfe17c601839c733db0ab5c3dcdc786"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 54c6a235c8\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/54c6a235c8a806b57eeb0d65a40b1aa1fc8f830e\n    Remove obsolete LSan suppressions\n\n    Remove LSan suppressions for WebRtcSessionTest, WebRtcSdpTest,\n    PeerConnectionInterfaceTest and related code triggered in\n    peerconnection_unittests.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: If1ca61d32de8824af498499782017c97ea31c4da\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497001\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48406}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/sanitizers/lsan_suppressions_webrtc.cc"], "git_node": "35fdb3106ece9987609ee88b5576c1584790c92d", "git_parents": ["947b610d0aba7432e717f8c5bc200699d9e5eb59"], "node": "39dbe818acb586b2f750ae31a9018ee1bd5581cd", "parents": ["6e8896cf3310cd501aae66ecb0f97daff335cd22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6546aa98ce\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6546aa98cec67e7f25701bff34840e42af9a943a\n    Pause packet queue aging when PacingController is congested\n\n    When PacingController is congested, packets are retained in the\n    queue until the congestion window clears. Previously, time spent\n    in the congested state was counted towards packet queue aging,\n    which caused drain_large_queues to over-inflate the adjusted media\n    rate and dump queued packets in an instantaneous wire-speed burst\n    upon exiting congestion.\n\n    This change ensures that SetCongested(true) pauses packet queue\n    aging in PrioritizedPacketQueue similarly to Pause(), preventing\n    artificial queue aging while maintaining keepalives and unpaced\n    packet delivery during congestion.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:548989575\n    Change-Id: Iee0a96e351f93af788c37f58ba2c6676da92077f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497080\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48407}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/pacing/pacing_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/pacing/pacing_controller_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "9bc58ea7415554929808d7f1788bb5ae8a63c9ae", "git_parents": ["35fdb3106ece9987609ee88b5576c1584790c92d"], "node": "0407b012a8f26be3986efda944fa8410e7ffbfce", "parents": ["39dbe818acb586b2f750ae31a9018ee1bd5581cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 5fe4baa193\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5fe4baa193b2a3150642b6f6119d603c611a1861\n    Remove obsolete LSan suppressions\n\n    Remove WebRTC unit test suppressions for FakeNetworkInterface,\n    CodecTest, DtmfSenderTest, CreateIceCandidate,\n    PeerConnectionInterfaceTest, and WebRtcSdpTest following code\n    modernizations.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I70f7dc74e16415e9353ad05bbe505303498a553f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497301\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48408}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/sanitizers/lsan_suppressions_webrtc.cc"], "git_node": "5fa50a348a6d315a776a1d649cf5b3703f84cb06", "git_parents": ["9bc58ea7415554929808d7f1788bb5ae8a63c9ae"], "node": "1f942fa8802d31d6bb1c62d30a2e4df1ed34be72", "parents": ["0407b012a8f26be3986efda944fa8410e7ffbfce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from 59899d5f14\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/59899d5f14f13e793c59bfc82df4c129cfe8a3d7\n    Guard buffer_ and handle stream restart in VideoReceiveStream2\n\n    Store decode_sync_ pointer in VideoReceiveStream2 and guard buffer_ with\n    worker_sequence_checker_. Recreate buffer_ in Start() if it has been\n    stopped.\n\n    Recreating buffer_ in Start() when it has been stopped allows\n    VideoReceiveStream2 to be stopped and restarted cleanly. Calling Stop()\n    marks the underlying VideoStreamBufferController as stopped, which halts\n    frame decode scheduling; recreating the controller upon restart resets\n    it to an active state, clears stale frame and timer state from the\n    previous run, and re-registers a fresh decode scheduler with\n    DecodeSynchronizer.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: Ic57ebaf991e1b047665524839fc9367801428afe\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496240\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48409}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0037.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0042.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0057.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "8ef6a8c25c4b4ad26e64e6ee1bb9a7ae31e86dfc", "git_parents": ["5fa50a348a6d315a776a1d649cf5b3703f84cb06"], "node": "588e79213c9ec603e48be35781a895dcf9aecbf5", "parents": ["1f942fa8802d31d6bb1c62d30a2e4df1ed34be72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from bf5cba3caf\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bf5cba3caf04798b7b91012b0dad88966a91eb5c\n    Fix some clang findings.\n\n    testing::InvokeWithoutArgs, testing::Invoke and testing::DoAll are being deprecated.\n\n    Change-Id: I34d1ab006a573d9fd6067e08a51e01496857dc21\n    Bug: None\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497300\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48410}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/audio_receive_stream_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/audio_send_stream_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/sctp/dcsctp_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/acm2/audio_coding_module_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/neteq/neteq_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_device/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_device/audio_device_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_mixer/audio_mixer_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/mock/mock_render_delay_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc/agc_manager_direct_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/input_volume_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/audio_processing_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/test/conversational_speech/mock_wavreader_factory.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/linux/wayland/shared_screencast_stream_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/screen_capturer_mac_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/test/vp9_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0093.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0095.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0100.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/local_network_access_port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/p2p_transport_channel_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/datagram_connection_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/proxy_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/integration_test_helpers.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/integration_test_helpers.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/crypto_random_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/adaptation/overuse_frame_detector_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_send_stream_impl_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "83d5c0c21e7d33ec37accc49955ded73fc640a42", "git_parents": ["8ef6a8c25c4b4ad26e64e6ee1bb9a7ae31e86dfc"], "node": "9b79087114a30b244e221a36fbfd0ea2e1b1f387", "parents": ["588e79213c9ec603e48be35781a895dcf9aecbf5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069067 - Vendor libwebrtc from c267248921\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c267248921182b9d432bc97c030b705020d1927d\n    android: Pass Context to AudioRecord.Builder on Android 14+\n\n    When constructing an AudioRecord on Android 14 (U) and above, passing\n    the application Context is necessary to ensure the AudioRecord respects\n    virtual device associations and remote submix audio routing.\n\n    Without providing the context, AudioRecord may ignore virtual device\n    routing rules (such as those used for Split Compute or smart glasses)\n    and inadvertently fall back to capturing from the phone's default\n    built-in microphone.\n\n    Bug: b/538640903\n    Change-Id: Ief71689330ddf05c445951f4a6b3c13d4dbf3642\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496820\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Joseph Martinez \u003cjtmartinez@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48411}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0142.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/src/java/org/webrtc/audio/WebRtcAudioRecord.java"], "git_node": "15adec1696e7a6f23d82ea99bac6865db77b96ca", "git_parents": ["83d5c0c21e7d33ec37accc49955ded73fc640a42"], "node": "dc0a13096ecc78c353715907d2ad3899d9b27e83", "parents": ["9b790871