003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071980 - Update PDF.js to 88f6044946105b3976d10ff74201f2de74624bbf r=pdfjs-reviewers,calixte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325949\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsVersion.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "022e3aaf8b7182a431f0e11054d1f827c75ec4ff", "git_parents": ["6cb29c3545ab0b1a126d684674ed819666ac5aec"], "node": "886f94eeceb87910697d49fb526bb5747d5c39da", "parents": ["46d93393954cc9ac31ab056e4278dd027eb1a534"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Carlos Jeurissen \u003ccarlos-mozilla@jeurissen.co\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1992418 - add runtime.getVersion() r=robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D267514\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/web-extensions/browser.runtime.extension.js.ini", "toolkit/components/extensions/child/ext-runtime.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/schemas/runtime.json", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/test_ext_all_apis.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_runtime_getVersion.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell-common.toml"], "git_node": "3d535ced967b52d4048c5a52cfc2b00807a7afa7", "git_parents": ["022e3aaf8b7182a431f0e11054d1f827c75ec4ff"], "node": "2dcb2e9d7f6ff6a0959a522762a62387e0a8b006", "parents": ["886f94eeceb87910697d49fb526bb5747d5c39da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070936 - Stop the async-storage setItem error handler retaining the stored value, r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe.\n\nThe debugger writes pending breakpoints, blackboxed ranges and opened URLs\nthrough asyncStorage.setItem() without awaiting the result, so a write can still\nbe in flight when the toolbox is destroyed. setItemOnError does not use the\nvalue, but it is created in setItem()'s scope and so keeps it alive, and the\nvalue reaches the debugger window through the browser loader sandbox it was\ncreated in and that sandbox's window.console. That is the \"leaked 1 window(s)\nuntil shutdown [url = about:devtools-toolbox]\" failure on\nbrowser_dbg-editor-gutter.js and browser_dbg-expressions.js.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325042\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/async-storage.js"], "git_node": "f2868ad28c04d71bef93022b782155ced12bf1b1", "git_parents": ["3d535ced967b52d4048c5a52cfc2b00807a7afa7"], "node": "2f967728970187e741e19a57a4fe86d7b2345273", "parents": ["2dcb2e9d7f6ff6a0959a522762a62387e0a8b006"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071237 - [devtools] Let the object inspector tolerate an object actor that has gone away, r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe.\n\n`loadItemProperties` issues its requests in one `Promise.all`, where the five\n`enum*` helpers treat a failed request as \"no data\" and `getPrototype`,\n`getGlobal`, `getPromiseState` and `getProxySlots` reject. Inline previews run\nfrom a floating promise in `fetchScopes`, so an object actor released under\n`getPrototype` leaves an unhandled `Protocol error (noSuchActor)`, which fails\nbrowser_dbg-reloading.js on linux tsan.\n\nThe catches swallow every error rather than only actor death, in a helper the\nconsole, inspector and netmonitor share too; that is what the five `enum*`\nsiblings already do, so this makes the four outliers consistent rather than\nadding a behaviour.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325406\n", "files": ["devtools/client/shared/components/object-inspector/utils/client.js"], "git_node": "dfeef072178ecd1323c44fd3e6f386f103be1af0", "git_parents": ["f2868ad28c04d71bef93022b782155ced12bf1b1"], "node": "2faf0a63e2ddea8149b49b4301f1c8ed243c50aa", "parents": ["2f967728970187e741e19a57a4fe86d7b2345273"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071230 - Move the rules view source link click handler onto the link, r=nchevobbe.\n\nThe handler was on the wrapper div rather than the anchor it wraps, so\ngetRuleViewLinkByIndex handed tests a click target with no accessible,\nwhich is what the Bug 1849028 annotations absorbed. Moving it makes the\nhandler and the click target coincide; the helper now returns the anchor\nand the seven tests that reached through it follow.\n\nbrowser_dbg-telemetry-stylesheets.js also fails on the debugger's source\ntree, so its annotation only retires once Bug 2070909 has landed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325409\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-telemetry-stylesheets.js", "devtools/client/framework/browser-toolbox/test/browser_browser_toolbox_ruleview_stylesheet.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_part2.toml", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_invalid-source-map.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_original-source-link.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_original-source-link2.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_style-editor-link.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/views/rule-editor.js", "devtools/client/inspector/test/shared-head.js", "devtools/client/styleeditor/test/browser.toml", "devtools/client/styleeditor/test/browser_styleeditor_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "7602e2edc8eedc7050462fe298e37c10688205e5", "git_parents": ["dfeef072178ecd1323c44fd3e6f386f103be1af0"], "node": "a4b5faa60e3eecfbcbbe726b60b6e4346e1d6892", "parents": ["2faf0a63e2ddea8149b49b4301f1c8ed243c50aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071228 - Name the custom formatter collapse button, r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe.\n\nThe button is image-only and had no accessible name, which is what the\nBug 1849028 annotations absorbed. Reps has no localization, so the string\nis untranslated like the others in that directory.\n\nbrowser_dbg-custom-formatters.js also clicks the button inside the Scopes\ntree, where it is unfocusable until Bug 2070909 lands, so its annotation\nonly retires after that.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325410\n", "files": ["devtools/client/shared/components/reps/reps/custom-formatter.mjs", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/_webconsole_ak.toml"], "git_node": "a915f6ec60deaa1c5c5a540526cf7c54ef4b1836", "git_parents": ["7602e2edc8eedc7050462fe298e37c10688205e5"], "node": "346e284a990f7637bd6f94aa72f54b8124432921", "parents": ["a4b5faa60e3eecfbcbbe726b60b6e4346e1d6892"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071233 - Label the DOM mutation breakpoint checkboxes, r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe.\n\nThe enable checkbox of a DOM mutation breakpoint had no accessible name. The\nname has to carry the node as well as the mutation type, or every checkbox in\nthe pane sharing a type reads the same. It cannot be borrowed from the row with\naria-labelledby, because the node label is a Rep which renders an \"open in\ninspector\" button whose title would be pulled in, so it is composed from the\nnode front instead.\n\nThe a11y_checks annotations this retires were filed as Bug 1849028.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325412\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/components/SecondaryPanes/DOMMutationBreakpoints.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_af.toml", "devtools/client/inspector/markup/test/browser.toml", "devtools/client/locales/en-US/debugger.properties"], "git_node": "8b61af9c839bd0a3e63351b30c227bcd4a71fd33", "git_parents": ["a915f6ec60deaa1c5c5a540526cf7c54ef4b1836"], "node": "8bed1fd95f0957d38422137b1b76faf6d6ffb6aa", "parents": ["346e284a990f7637bd6f94aa72f54b8124432921"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071236 - Make the debugger's thread list rows real buttons, r=nchevobbe.\n\nA row in the Threads pane was a clickable div, so it had no interactive\naccessible and no way to reach it from the keyboard. A button gets both for\nfree, and aria-pressed carries the selection, for assistive technology and for\nthe styling alike.\n\nThe a11y_checks annotations this retires were filed as Bug 1849028.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325414\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/components/SecondaryPanes/Thread.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/components/SecondaryPanes/Threads.css", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_af.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-inspector-integration.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-windowless-workers.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_gp.toml"], "git_node": "0ef6191642d2272982fb94a14bc5800529a5ec0f", "git_parents": ["8b61af9c839bd0a3e63351b30c227bcd4a71fd33"], "node": "978afddcce37a5d5a4a7e60ba32ea20b95fd3858", "parents": ["8bed1fd95f0957d38422137b1b76faf6d6ffb6aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Rubino \u003cdrubino@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049951 - Remove launch on login Run values for missing executables when registering a new one. r=iholmes\n\nBuilds that run from a throwaway location and are then deleted without an\nuninstall (each step of a mozregression bisection, an unzipped build that is\nlater deleted) leave their \"Mozilla-Firefox-\u003chash\u003e\" value behind in\nHKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run forever, and Windows lists\nevery one of them under Settings \u003e Apps \u003e Startup.\n\nWhen createLaunchOnLoginRegistryKey writes our own value it now also removes\nvalues with the same vendor-app prefix whose executable no longer exists. A\nvalue is only removed when its path is on a local drive that is still present,\nso an entry for a Firefox on an unplugged removable drive is left alone. UNC\nand unparseable values are also left alone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325623\n", "files": ["toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/WindowsLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/tests/xpcshell/test_WindowsLaunchOnLogin_missingExecutables.js", "toolkit/modules/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "aacdc2dd7d6988e6610f50657f83a9327e7f4da7", "git_parents": ["0ef6191642d2272982fb94a14bc5800529a5ec0f"], "node": "d0098a7b5b4714ae6beb443c172fadf75e0f168f", "parents": ["978afddcce37a5d5a4a7e60ba32ea20b95fd3858"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069285 - Emit one SpeechRecognition final result per utterance. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski,media-webspeech-reviewers,ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\n\nThe model commits words several times over while an utterance is being spoken,\nand each commit used to be dispatched as its own final result, so a sentence\nreached the page as a string of one-word results. Words now accumulate until\nthe utterance ends and go out as one final; the intermediate commits are\ndispatched as interim results instead, which keeps the same latency without\nclaiming that a word is a complete result.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323664\n", "files": ["config/external/mozinference/mozinference.symbols", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionParent.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_parakeet_eou_flush.html", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/include/parakeet_capi.h", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/moz.yaml", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/parakeet-chunk-samples.patch", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/src/parakeet_capi.cpp", "toolkit/components/ml/backends/llama/LlamaRuntimeLinker.h"], "git_node": "5a47dd23f8ec7fb4fb38c42795585c1a396da1e1", "git_parents": ["aacdc2dd7d6988e6610f50657f83a9327e7f4da7"], "node": "6d202400fa3a46470a97298a5915563c7e38037e", "parents": ["d0098a7b5b4714ae6beb443c172fadf75e0f168f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069285 - End an utterance when the decoder stops emitting tokens. r=media-webspeech-reviewers,ai-platform-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nThe multilingual model has no \u003cEOU\u003e token, so we have to pick the end of an\nutterance ourselves. We now end one when the decoder has emitted nothing for\nmedia.webspeech.recognition.endpoint_blank_ms of audio. The decoder only emits\non speech, so this works at any background noise level.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325454\n", "files": ["config/external/mozinference/mozinference.symbols", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionParent.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_parakeet_endpoint_blank.html", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/include/parakeet_capi.h", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/moz.yaml", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/parakeet-end-utterance.patch", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/src/parakeet_capi.cpp", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/src/streaming.cpp", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/src/streaming.hpp", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/src/streaming_encoder.cpp", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/src/streaming_encoder.hpp", "toolkit/components/ml/backends/llama/LlamaRuntimeLinker.h"], "git_node": "8a3a6fe4c52420597cdf72221959a6d542b2d7d3", "git_parents": ["5a47dd23f8ec7fb4fb38c42795585c1a396da1e1"], "node": "6d57a7a20d3bec3d5adf7e301920ce36875f73b0", "parents": ["6d202400fa3a46470a97298a5915563c7e38037e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069285 - Reset the encoder cache at \u003cEOU\u003e, so a word isn't repeated during silence. r=media-webspeech-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nAt \u003cEOU\u003e we reset the decoder but kept the encoder cache, unlike NeMo. The\ncache still holds the context of the utterance that just ended, so during the\nsilence that follows, the model keeps recognizing its last word and emits it\nagain on every chunk. Saying a single word gave 25 results, one every 150ms,\nfor as long as the user stayed quiet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325455\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/single_word_dog.opus", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_parakeet_one_word.html", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/moz.yaml", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/parakeet-eou-reset-encoder.patch", "third_party/parakeet.cpp/src/streaming.cpp"], "git_node": "35b46ae50208e1713fac1074d8e0645fa9379426", "git_parents": ["8a3a6fe4c52420597cdf72221959a6d542b2d7d3"], "node": "51ef924dc3d178b10fda0cb4c636b5a0e7bf2bb3", "parents": ["6d57a7a20d3bec3d5adf7e301920ce36875f73b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069324 - Implement SpeechRecognition.continuous. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323665\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_parakeet_continuous.html"], "git_node": "08ad3c84f3070abdb7545b68f342bcebb12c2684", "git_parents": ["35b46ae50208e1713fac1074d8e0645fa9379426"], "node": "a80f967d9c2ffc173e3a0804143784a80052a971", "parents": ["51ef924dc3d178b10fda0cb4c636b5a0e7bf2bb3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071279 - Make SpeechRecognition result, nomatch and error events not bubble. r=media-webspeech-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nThe spec says they don't bubble. They were already not cancelable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325457\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_event_bubbles.html", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_stop_returns_result_or_nomatch.html"], "git_node": "5fbf71b1f44b1ce628d3952563f310399a6500ba", "git_parents": ["08ad3c84f3070abdb7545b68f342bcebb12c2684"], "node": "6be74b39339f77a5f1c518523c24eee74aa7813e", "parents": ["a80f967d9c2ffc173e3a0804143784a80052a971"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072200 - Update the component for toolkit/mozapps/pushnotificationhelper/ r=iholmes,saschanaz DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326142\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/pushnotificationhelper/moz.build"], "git_node": "d46b31ca89013bae33a7dbb55d810af59078238e", "git_parents": ["5fbf71b1f44b1ce628d3952563f310399a6500ba"], "node": "136cbb370413aa0c3cadc0ee3ce2870326fb47f9", "parents": ["6be74b39339f77a5f1c518523c24eee74aa7813e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063995 - Fix stale AV1 RTP spec anchors in comments. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nThe av1-rtp-spec anchors were section-numbered (#721-..., #722-...), but the\nspec's generated ids are unnumbered, so these links all 404. Point them at the\ncurrent ids: 7.2.1 -\u003e #sdp-mapping-media-subtype and 7.2.2 -\u003e #rid.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321186\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/sdp/SdpAttribute.h", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/stats.js"], "git_node": "d54def1b91d0c383f7c33f661cec3b4b18abb8be", "git_parents": ["d46b31ca89013bae33a7dbb55d810af59078238e"], "node": "b4539e2cb7b12ccc68a44909bae9a871947d2f32", "parents": ["136cbb370413aa0c3cadc0ee3ce2870326fb47f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063995 - Fix AV1 fmtp profile/level-idx parsing bugs in the sipcc and rsdparsa SDP parsers. r=webrtc-reviewers,ng\n\nsipcc's RTP_AV1 case wrote the parsed level-idx into the profile field\ninstead of levelIdx (copy/paste bug), and used the ambiguous shared\nH.263 profile field (with a `\u003e 0` guard that silently dropped the\nvalid profile=0) instead of the dedicated av1_profile/av1_has_profile\nfields, which sdp_attr.c never actually populated. Wire those fields\nup and read them instead.\n\nAlso add the missing \"AV1\" case to rsdparsa's strToCodecType, which\npreviously tagged AV1 rtpmaps as kOtherCodec instead of kAV1, unlike\nthe sipcc parser.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321187\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/sdp/RsdparsaSdpAttributeList.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/sdp/SdpAttribute.h", "dom/media/webrtc/sdp/SipccSdpAttributeList.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/sdp_unittests.cpp", "third_party/sipcc/sdp_attr.c"], "git_node": "47b5a2342aba050318867e107d1d6eab73532356", "git_parents": ["d54def1b91d0c383f7c33f661cec3b4b18abb8be"], "node": "8b543a1a0e0dbb3f2b413e1377923525de8a78a4", "parents": ["b4539e2cb7b12ccc68a44909bae9a871947d2f32"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063995 - Populate and correctly negotiate AV1 fmtp parameters in jsep. r=webrtc-reviewers,ng\n\nFirefox never emitted an a=fmtp line for AV1, leaving remote peers\nwithout our declared profile/level-idx/tier. Populate real default\nvalues (profile=0, level-idx=9 i.e. level 4.1, tier=0) in\nCreateDefaultAV1 instead of leaving them unset, which is what\nsuppressed the fmtp line via Av1Parameters::ShouldSerialize().\n\nPer the AV1 RTP spec, these are receiver-declared and asymmetric,\nunlike VP8/VP9's hierarchically negotiated max-fs/max-fr: the sender\nmust encode at or below whatever the remote receiver declared, while\neach side's own receive declaration is independent of the other side.\nReplace the previous hierarchical-min negotiation (which conflated our\nown receive declaration with our encode capability) with: on send,\nadopt the remote's declared params outright; on receive, leave our own\ndeclared config untouched. This also removes the now-unused\nNegotiateHierarchicalParam helper.\n\nAlso fix ApplyConfigToFmtp's AV1 branch to apply the configured params\nunconditionally (matching VP8/VP9), since RTCRtpTransceiver's\ngetCapabilities() and SetCodecPreferences() call it with a null\nstarting point and previously saw no AV1 params at all.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321188\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepCodecDescription.h", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/jsep_session_unittest.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/jsep_track_unittest.cpp"], "git_node": "b46484d725192c9d9c6f93f562bd672c30ac5a5d", "git_parents": ["47b5a2342aba050318867e107d1d6eab73532356"], "node": "198698a33a33894853a769c2c1bb4b8f559a635b", "parents": ["8b543a1a0e0dbb3f2b413e1377923525de8a78a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063995 - Exclude AV1's asymmetric profile fmtp parameter from RTCRtpSender's codec dictionary match. r=webrtc-reviewers,ng\n\nRTCRtpSender::CheckAndRectifyEncodings's codec dictionary match algorithm\nalready excludes H264's level/subprofile (encoded together in\nprofile-level-id) from the strict fmtp comparison when ignoring levels, since\nthose are asymmetric/declarative per RFC 6184. AV1's profile parameter is the\nsame kind of asymmetric/declarative value (see\nhttps://aomediacodec.github.io/av1-rtp-spec/#723-usage-with-the-sdp-offeranswer-model),\nbut it's a separate fmtp key from level-idx, not encoded together with it,\nso it was never being extracted and always participated in the strict\nparameter-set comparison. Add an independent profile extraction for AV1,\nalongside the existing level/subprofile mechanism.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321189\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpSender.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/protocol/av1-profile-asymmetry.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "d1071a59bc3ee7a33b4ef5e5b54e1da69099c13d", "git_parents": ["b46484d725192c9d9c6f93f562bd672c30ac5a5d"], "node": "6c02e5bb9278ddc942f53f797f54703a1f935125", "parents": ["198698a33a33894853a769c2c1bb4b8f559a635b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071715 - pass --yes to moz-phab in periodic-updates job to avoid interactive prompt hang. r=releng-reviewers,bhearsum DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326107\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/periodic_file_updates.sh"], "git_node": "7cee42a08141cccfc7c52fa33c807cbc9646f2c6", "git_parents": ["d1071a59bc3ee7a33b4ef5e5b54e1da69099c13d"], "node": "8b83f55edabde1f4aa0e050cae99dfef11a3b41f", "parents": ["6c02e5bb9278ddc942f53f797f54703a1f935125"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066020 - Enable SharedSurface_AndroidHardwareBuffer with WebGL on Android r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nMove AndroidHardwareBuffer to higher priority.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320845\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/CanvasRenderer.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "db84017056679339df21115fe2fe84ae775c52a0", "git_parents": ["7cee42a08141cccfc7c52fa33c807cbc9646f2c6"], "node": "c425043976f8edd459b4e979a2bbe8f5095d2bbb", "parents": ["8b83f55edabde1f4aa0e050cae99dfef11a3b41f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070478 - Fix macOS exception handling for child processes that don't register their own exception handler. r=crashreporting-reviewers,afranchuk\n\nWhen we receive an exception that is not meant for us, we claim we\nwant to ignore the exception. However, what we actually tell the\nkernel is that we handled the exception and it can resume the thread\nthat crashed. This causes a crash loop where the process gets\ncontinually resumed at the crashing point, generating a new\nexception and then getting resumed again. It never gets terminated\nby the kernel.\n\nFix that by telling the kernel we didn't handle the exception, so\nthat the exception continues to propagate and the process crashes.\n\nDiscovered while writing tests where the updater binary crashes as\na child of xpcshell. The updater binary does not register an\nexception handler. The tests were failing with a timeout.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324566\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/breakpad-client/mac/handler/exception_handler.cc", "toolkit/crashreporter/test/gtest/TestMacExceptionHandler.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "a8a1a0e069aa0ad28ceb7ac49ff47c2b1ae564f2", "git_parents": ["db84017056679339df21115fe2fe84ae775c52a0"], "node": "5720bcacd93fcbef883375f8bd82c23f4a9d7d8b", "parents": ["c425043976f8edd459b4e979a2bbe8f5095d2bbb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046798 - Fix a/ b/ file paths in zucchini patch 0024. r=bobowen\n\nThe a/ b/ paths in vendored patch 0024 were incorrectly prefixed\nwith third_party/zucchini/chromium/. Correct them to the\nupstream-relative paths.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310325\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/vendor-verify-expected-fail.yml", "third_party/zucchini/chromium-shim/patches/0024-Detect-OOM-when-memory-mapping-fails-in-MappedFileRe.patch"], "git_node": "9fa7fa2911c68eaae7f54d1b745b1dd8f8b15416", "git_parents": ["a8a1a0e069aa0ad28ceb7ac49ff47c2b1ae564f2"], "node": "2bb5207b7dda96d4ba0d0d527808b54bfa6271b4", "parents": ["5720bcacd93fcbef883375f8bd82c23f4a9d7d8b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046798 - Wrap zucchini entry points to catch exceptions. r=sergesanspaille,application-update-reviewers,cdupuis\n\nIn the previous exception handling design, our SEH __try/__except only\ncovered the bodies of MappedPatch::Load and MappedPatch::ApplyUnsafe,\nand only partially.\n\nThis patch instead splits exception handling into two layers, each\ncovering a different concern:\n\n1. BEGIN_ENTRY_POINT / END_ENTRY_POINT: Wraps every entry point from\n   updater.cpp, catching any potential std::bad_alloc exception. Ensures\n   wrapped zucchini code returns an OOM status code upon standard\n   library allocation failures instead of crashing the process.\n\n2. BEGIN_PAGE_ERROR_TRY_EXCEPT / END_PAGE_ERROR_TRY_EXCEPT: Mirrors the\n   exception catching present in upstream zucchini::ApplyCommon to catch\n   page errors from mapped file I/O.\n\nWith the follow-up patch covering crc32, this ensures that our exception\nhandling covers as much zucchini surface as possible. This two-layer\nstructure also helps implement the follow-up patch that transitions to\nC++ exceptions, where layer 1 gets a cross-platform implementation\nwhereas layer 2 stays Windows-only.\n\nIn the current patch, layer 1 also covers CHECK failures, but it gets\nrestricted to C++ exceptions in a later patch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308183\n", "files": ["third_party/zucchini/moz_zucchini.cc", "third_party/zucchini/moz_zucchini.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "7621866953f2f41ae39715d862ff07efe30043bd", "git_parents": ["9fa7fa2911c68eaae7f54d1b745b1dd8f8b15416"], "node": "60d7367be64a47f36004f58f10700a90296f811a", "parents": ["2bb5207b7dda96d4ba0d0d527808b54bfa6271b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046798 - Wrap zucchini crc32 computation to catch exceptions. r=application-update-reviewers,cdupuis\n\nThis patch extends the entry-point wrapping from the previous patch to\nalso cover crc32 computation. This requires changing the abstract\ninterface used by the updater for crc32 computations, so that we can\npropagate updater status codes that match with the failures raised from\nzucchini.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308184\n", "files": ["third_party/zucchini/moz_zucchini.cc", "third_party/zucchini/moz_zucchini.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "bb2e80f4831bdc0820b2d1f69ce03b42e2bd7e39", "git_parents": ["7621866953f2f41ae39715d862ff07efe30043bd"], "node": "bee35f43ee2d4cb4bb5fc5a4aa8f9d72ccd95fc8", "parents": ["60d7367be64a47f36004f58f10700a90296f811a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043122 - Remove Windows-only zucchini crash recovery. r=application-update-reviewers,cdupuis\n\nThe updater is now resilient to crashes that occur while drafting a\npatch. We can safely remove the zucchini workaround that previously\ntried to mitigate these crashes at the zucchini level on Windows.\n\nThis workaround was less reliable than it pretended to be anyway,\nbecause moving the failure location around (like we do further in the\npatch stack) would make the CheckDestructor test fail. The root cause\nbeing that SEH has weaker guarantees on calling destructors than C++\nexception handling.\n\nUpdate tests accordingly. Now, only recovering from C++ std::bad_alloc\nexceptions must ensure that destructors are called and that we fail\ngracefully. CHECK failures are now immediate crashes that bypass updater\nrollback, so they are expected to leave .moz-draft files behind in\nnon-staged updates. It is the updater's responsibility to clean stale\n.moz-draft files during the next update.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324342\n", "files": ["third_party/zucchini/moz_zucchini.cc", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/xpcshellUtilsAUS.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialZucchiniBadAllocDestructor_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialZucchiniCheckDestructor_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialZucchiniCheck_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/xpcshell_base.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "1cae125cb5d55b9d1c9124f92d1f6f4c88592e02", "git_parents": ["bb2e80f4831bdc0820b2d1f69ce03b42e2bd7e39"], "node": "8119850ba53ffe668205184d25f85fb469250c4d", "parents": ["bee35f43ee2d4cb4bb5fc5a4aa8f9d72ccd95fc8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043122 - Cross-platform handling of std::bad_alloc in zucchini. r=application-update-reviewers,firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille,cdupuis\n\nThis patch extends std::bad_alloc recovery to macOS and Linux platforms,\nby replacing the previous Windows-only SEH-based zucchini crash recovery\nwith one based on C++ exceptions instead. To this end, we enable C++\nexceptions when compiling the zucchini library on all platforms,\nincluding Windows.\n\nWe make the updater fail with an OOM status code when std::bad_alloc\nfailures occur, allowing the updater to correctly assess the reason\nzucchini failed -- the updater behaves differently upon OOM failures.\n\nThis makes Windows crash recovery more reliable as well, because the\nguarantees around calling the destructors of C++ objects when unwinding\nare stronger with C++ exceptions than with SEH.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324343\n", "files": ["third_party/zucchini/moz.build", "third_party/zucchini/moz_zucchini.cc", "third_party/zucchini/moz_zucchini.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/data/xpcshellUtilsAUS.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialZucchiniBadAlloc.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialZucchiniBadAllocDestructor.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialZucchiniBadAllocDestructor_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialZucchiniBadAlloc_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialZucchiniCheck.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialZucchiniCheck_win.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/xpcshell_base.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "8e886d0c0dbcc2d11cb76ad531fee3c8906e4fc9", "git_parents": ["1cae125cb5d55b9d1c9124f92d1f6f4c88592e02"], "node": "f614603d42084b1d75dda679d6a2b7e8016f3172", "parents": ["8119850ba53ffe668205184d25f85fb469250c4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043122 - Simulate zucchini test failures mid-patch-application. r=application-update-reviewers,iholmes\n\nMove the zucchini failure simulation used by updater tests into the\npatch-application loop, so tests exercise failures while the new image\nis still open and mapped. This is the worst case for updater recovery,\nso this patch increases our confidence in the recovery mechanisms.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310327\n", "files": ["third_party/zucchini/moz_zucchini.cc", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialZucchiniCheck.js"], "git_node": "1053be10ad17d0f9092f8f840f5f6abc234ae2cb", "git_parents": ["8e886d0c0dbcc2d11cb76ad531fee3c8906e4fc9"], "node": "9e587fb064151ca3312c3a8ecc485285f4d27dfc", "parents": ["f614603d42084b1d75dda679d6a2b7e8016f3172"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975960 - Regenerate zucchini shim patches that diverged. r=bobowen\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324878\n", "files": ["third_party/zucchini/chromium-shim/patches/0006-Define-only-the-required-functions-from-file_util.h.patch", "third_party/zucchini/chromium-shim/patches/0009-Limit-dependencies-in-file_path.cc.patch", "third_party/zucchini/chromium-shim/patches/0020-Limit-dependencies-in-foundation_util.mm.patch"], "git_node": "936aedc26415175bdc29bb34f2298b14d957fe35", "git_parents": ["1053be10ad17d0f9092f8f840f5f6abc234ae2cb"], "node": "aaaab83998f84de97530d48c8b1e87a97097b4b2", "parents": ["9e587fb064151ca3312c3a8ecc485285f4d27dfc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975960 - Update zucchini vendoring to prepare for mingwclang support. r=bobowen\n\n- base/files/file_util_win.cc: OpenFile() uses _SH_DENYNO, which the MSVC CRT\n  headers happen to expose transitively but mingw-w64 only declares in\n  \u003cshare.h\u003e.\n\n- base/base_paths_win.cc: \u003cKnownFolders.h\u003e is not found when cross-compiling,\n  as mingw-w64 spells the header knownfolders.h and the build host can have a\n  case-sensitive filesystem. Its only user, FOLDERID_ApplicationShortcuts in\n  the DIR_APP_SHORTCUTS case is already excluded under MOZ_ZUCCHINI.\n\n- components/zucchini/suffix_array_unittest.cc: libc++ ships no\n  std::char_traits\u003cunsigned char\u003e specialization, so\n  std::basic_string\u003cunsigned char\u003e cannot be instantiated. The test only ever\n  uses the alias as a sized random-access container (construction from an\n  iterator pair, begin/end/size), so under MOZ_ZUCCHINI it becomes\n  std::vector\u003cunsigned char\u003e.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324879\n", "files": ["third_party/zucchini/chromium-shim/patches/0025-Prepare-zucchini-sources-for-mingwclang-builds.patch", "third_party/zucchini/chromium/base/base_paths_win.cc", "third_party/zucchini/chromium/base/files/file_util_win.cc", "third_party/zucchini/chromium/components/zucchini/suffix_array_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "34ee118f88dcc587f6c66d49d88eda4db800977e", "git_parents": ["936aedc26415175bdc29bb34f2298b14d957fe35"], "node": "4049101505b369fa97ba5b1d7046123d93da148f", "parents": ["aaaab83998f84de97530d48c8b1e87a97097b4b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975960 - Add zucchini support for mingwclang builds. r=bobowen,firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille,sandbox-reviewers\n\nZucchini uses SEH to catch the EXCEPTION_IN_PAGE_ERROR exceptions that\nWindows raises when an I/O error occurs while accessing a memory-mapped\nfile. MinGW compilers do not support SEH, which is why we were disabling\nzucchini in mingwclang builds.\n\nWe now deal with this the same way as our sandbox code: mozilla-config.h\nreplaces __try with if (true) and __except with else when compiling\nzucchini code. In MinGW builds, an I/O error on the mapped files thus\ncrashes updater.exe rather than making zucchini return an error status.\nThis is acceptable now that the updater is resilient to crashes that\noccur while drafting a patch (bug 2060275).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324618\n", "files": ["browser/config/mozconfigs/win32/mingwclang", "browser/config/mozconfigs/win64/mingwclang", "mozilla-config.h.in", "security/sandbox/moz.build", "third_party/zucchini/README.md", "third_party/zucchini/moz.build", "third_party/zucchini/moz_zucchini.cc"], "git_node": "5a32546c35010c71404a3c4ac0501498613d1d7c", "git_parents": ["34ee118f88dcc587f6c66d49d88eda4db800977e"], "node": "08a0bde4c6dea82ec25176138688b9a616851964", "parents": ["4049101505b369fa97ba5b1d7046123d93da148f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1955304 - Repurpose the win32k-conflict crate to read Windows process mitigation r=bobowen,yjuglaret,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nThat crate is unused, and already has substantial code to read\nprocess mitigations from the registry.\n\nThis reworks the crate to do just that, so that we can later document\nwhich mitigations are applied to our process, both from system-wide\noptions as well as exec-specific ones. The first user of the new code\nwill come in a subsequent patch in this set.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307073\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "toolkit/crashreporter/win32_process_mitigations/.gitignore", "toolkit/crashreporter/win32_process_mitigations/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/crashreporter/win32_process_mitigations/src/error.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/win32_process_mitigations/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/win32_process_mitigations/src/query.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/win32_process_mitigations/src/registry.rs", "toolkit/library/rust/moz.build", "toolkit/library/rust/shared/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/library/rust/shared/lib.rs", "toolkit/xre/detect_win32k_conflicts.h", "toolkit/xre/detect_win32k_conflicts/.gitignore", "toolkit/xre/detect_win32k_conflicts/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/xre/detect_win32k_conflicts/src/detect.rs", "toolkit/xre/detect_win32k_conflicts/src/error.rs", "toolkit/xre/detect_win32k_conflicts/src/ffi.rs", "toolkit/xre/detect_win32k_conflicts/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/xre/detect_win32k_conflicts/src/registry.rs", "toolkit/xre/detect_win32k_conflicts/tests/basic.rs", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp", "tools/lint/clippy.yml"], "git_node": "bbdb9ecc4dd727ca6997cc1c90cd82fe8cc8014b", "git_parents": ["5a32546c35010c71404a3c4ac0501498613d1d7c"], "node": "caf1e45728b226a4f6e9b5ba8a5a5291145a9ca8", "parents": ["08a0bde4c6dea82ec25176138688b9a616851964"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1955304 - crashhelper: record static annotations at process start r=gsvelto\n\nFor now those are limited to the appinfo, will grow platform-specific\ndata in later patches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310833\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/ipc_server.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "c7de30e9cf106faea426b2d5b894e72f7c5ce7d9", "git_parents": ["bbdb9ecc4dd727ca6997cc1c90cd82fe8cc8014b"], "node": "6402a915362367f593374c71dae4e1157ad501a5", "parents": ["caf1e45728b226a4f6e9b5ba8a5a5291145a9ca8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1955304 - crash_helper_server: rework error reporting r=gsvelto\n\nThe point of this patch is actually the helper to create error\nannotations, all the improvements around are just a bonus.\nOf note, we now get the actual errors behind the missing global\nannotations, not just the fact that we're missing them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310834\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/mozannotation_server/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/library/rust/moz.build"], "git_node": "8936b4bb68d1d2d810b027d03b45d85de2d57e1d", "git_parents": ["c7de30e9cf106faea426b2d5b894e72f7c5ce7d9"], "node": "5064632fdbe4958d877d6973c310349ac2ac2e42", "parents": ["6402a915362367f593374c71dae4e1157ad501a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1955304 - crash_helper_common: move the current process handle duplication into ProcessHandle r=gsvelto\n\nThis will allows usage elsewhere, e.g. tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314649\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_client/src/platform/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/windows.rs"], "git_node": "fa467b7110e2d62d047c381db9c17059b2e588fe", "git_parents": ["8936b4bb68d1d2d810b027d03b45d85de2d57e1d"], "node": "b2e8908136a95c8c35d080608af2ee3d12a13384", "parents": ["5064632fdbe4958d877d6973c310349ac2ac2e42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1955304 - appinfo: add a windows-only method to get the executable path r=gsvelto,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nThis will come in handy to get the mitigations for the parent process. The\nfull path, rather than just the file name, is what the Exploit Protection\npath filters are matched against.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310983\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/appinfo.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/appinfo/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "226be9f538a9d3a6be2e6b62f0b6c5b724478172", "git_parents": ["fa467b7110e2d62d047c381db9c17059b2e588fe"], "node": "3ff1a00f9c3d4cadf2d4081592b190018444e1eb", "parents": ["b2e8908136a95c8c35d080608af2ee3d12a13384"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1955304 - Record Windows process mitigations in crash annotations r=gsvelto,bobowen,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nRecords an amalgamation of per-application and system-wide MitigationOptions bitmasks\n(as raw hex) as present at the start of the parent process. This should\nreflect the mitigations applied to our processes at creation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307074\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "toolkit/crashreporter/CrashAnnotations.yaml", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation/linux.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation/mach.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation/macos.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation/windows.rs"], "git_node": "79a4abc0b25e18084b877c9fda56c15a84448d4c", "git_parents": ["226be9f538a9d3a6be2e6b62f0b6c5b724478172"], "node": "94adee4aba53ae50443694f759cf1612f1b0fdd0", "parents": ["3ff1a00f9c3d4cadf2d4081592b190018444e1eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1955304 - Add a human-readable summary of the process mitigations r=gsvelto,bobowen,yjuglaret,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nDecodes the MitigationOptions bitmask into named mitigations using data\nmined from WinBase.h. Sadly, we cannot use the Rust bindings for this as\nthose constants are not exposed.\n\nSince this is for human consumption, we consolidate the data. If you\nwant to know precisely where the mitigation comes from, check the raw\nhex.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307075\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/CrashAnnotations.yaml", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/win32_process_mitigations/scripts/Calibrate-MitigationOptions.ps1", "toolkit/crashreporter/win32_process_mitigations/src/decode.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/win32_process_mitigations/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "032ebee691ec0a4bae5a8fd17ee1f3308681e4dd", "git_parents": ["79a4abc0b25e18084b877c9fda56c15a84448d4c"], "node": "a36606b3ae28e86502f1ad1f7ec8537fd25a31f1", "parents": ["94adee4aba53ae50443694f759cf1612f1b0fdd0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2020133 - [devtools] Properly cancel auth prompts when the related channel closes r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325063\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkAuthListener.sys.mjs", "devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkResponseListener.sys.mjs", "devtools/shared/network-observer/test/browser/browser_networkobserver_auth_listener.js"], "git_node": "7ee5513c7cd9c3a03d888ae63d8ebd6ef52250c2", "git_parents": ["032ebee691ec0a4bae5a8fd17ee1f3308681e4dd"], "node": "9c1026bc27b210e655632624383121506e24b5aa", "parents": ["a36606b3ae28e86502f1ad1f7ec8537fd25a31f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072051 - Stop skipping the speech recognition telemetry tests on artifact builds. r=media-webspeech-reviewers,pehrsons\n\nI've been told by our telemetry folks that we can now generally run\ntelemetry tests on artifact builds. There are some exception but they\ndon't apply here, quoting :chutten:\n\n\u003e The only limits for writing instrumentation tests in artifact should\n\u003e now be 1) You've changed instrumentation that lives in the compiled code\n\u003e and, uh, decided to use an artifact build locally to test it. or 2) You\n\u003e are testing in JS a custom ping via testBeforeNextSubmit or\n\u003e testSubmission when that ping is submitted in Rust\n\nThose test were written prior to him landing the changes that repaired\nthis.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326153\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_inference_telemetry.js", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser_speech_recognition_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "08ed548ecbeded6feb2e923f4558a1fd42b2bfb9", "git_parents": ["7ee5513c7cd9c3a03d888ae63d8ebd6ef52250c2"], "node": "dcd8d3f242ae51a53cb1f4971b5472f3760ddab5", "parents": ["9c1026bc27b210e655632624383121506e24b5aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "RuslanSemchenko \u003clastdayserq22@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041999 - Limit wasm-smith memory64 sizes r=bvisness\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326101\n", "files": ["js/src/fuzz-tests/gluesmith/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "0c614384c81ecbd28cf0caa74d6868639e93d4cb", "git_parents": ["08ed548ecbeded6feb2e923f4558a1fd42b2bfb9"], "node": "964b7ae933f04b8bb63d30e92e7239e786a55162", "parents": ["dcd8d3f242ae51a53cb1f4971b5472f3760ddab5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069002 - [webdriver-bidi] Add support for the \"imageSize\" argument to the \"browsingContext.captureScreenshot\" command. r=whimboo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324303\n", "files": ["remote/shared/Capture.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/browsingContext.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "da52a3a7cdf39a96d14262b4abe4c80b2e037b59", "git_parents": ["0c614384c81ecbd28cf0caa74d6868639e93d4cb"], "node": "5cc0995e1b433cf085dcafca2a825a43d6ddb760", "parents": ["964b7ae933f04b8bb63d30e92e7239e786a55162"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069002 - [wpt] Add support for the \"imageSize\" argument to the \"browsingContext.captureScreenshot\" command in the WebDriver BiDi client. r=jgraham,whimboo,webdriver-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324304\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/webdriver/webdriver/bidi/modules/browsing_context.py"], "git_node": "44bb6bbea593c41e4effc561c68275ef94ecc0c4", "git_parents": ["da52a3a7cdf39a96d14262b4abe4c80b2e037b59"], "node": "d6e3c128d0f7fb203f7db927185f1eb8450a7dc7", "parents": ["5cc0995e1b433cf085dcafca2a825a43d6ddb760"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069002 - [wdspec] Add tests for the \"imageSize\" argument of the \"browsingContext.captureScreenshot\" command. r=whimboo,webdriver-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324305\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/capture_screenshot/image_size.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/capture_screenshot/invalid.py"], "git_node": "b2b5b005cd982f3cc454a419895257e57fd4e66d", "git_parents": ["44bb6bbea593c41e4effc561c68275ef94ecc0c4"], "node": "003de61cf2de272c04db31299bfbd5959e163ede", "parents": ["d6e3c128d0f7fb203f7db927185f1eb8450a7dc7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071289 - Bring the documentation skill's diagram guidance up to the sizing and color-scheme changes. r=ai4dev-reviewers,suhaib DONTBUILD\n\nThe behavior it now describes landed in bug 2071258 (intrinsic size), bug 2071267 (the edge fade), bug 2072107 (centering) and bug 2071163 (the page color scheme).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326103\n", "files": [".agents/skills/documentation/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/documentation/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "4d322e497d051be2674280f220ed2776c73da53b", "git_parents": ["b2b5b005cd982f3cc454a419895257e57fd4e66d"], "node": "333a1147c7e30868e791ac6db904af797a73ff45", "parents": ["003de61cf2de272c04db31299bfbd5959e163ede"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071771 - Use ETW::IsProfilingGroup in EmitETWMarker instead of testing gETWCollectionMask directly. r=profiler-reviewers,florian\n\nEmitETWMarker tested the ETW keyword mask by hand even though ETWTools.h\nalready provides IsProfilingGroup, which evaluates the same expression.\nThe duplication is historical: the inline test landed with the original\nETW marker support in bug 1869835, and IsProfilingGroup was extracted\nlater in bug 1923463 so that profiler_thread_is_profiling_runnables()\ncould perform the same check from outside this header.\n\nNo behaviour change: the two expressions are identical, IsProfilingGroup\nis static inline, and both perform a single load of gETWCollectionMask.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325783\n", "files": ["tools/profiler/public/ETWTools.h"], "git_node": "62766d4cf24f211720f281965f83f15eb873d218", "git_parents": ["4d322e497d051be2674280f220ed2776c73da53b"], "node": "bffcac191bc6abda033f515ab3881a1c51e2bc8d", "parents": ["333a1147c7e30868e791ac6db904af797a73ff45"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057608 - Add an about:pdf#features view for the built-in PDF tools. r=fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles,bolsson,Itiel\n\nabout:pdf gains a #features view listing eight built-in PDF tools. The\n\"Explore PDF tools\" button opens it; Back uses session history when available\nand otherwise restores the main view. Both views share the existing\ndefault-handler promo.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319451\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/static/browser_all_files_referenced.js", "browser/themes/shared/icons/canvas.svg", "browser/themes/shared/jar.inc.mn", "toolkit/actors/AboutPDFParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/content/aboutPDF.css", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/content/aboutPDF.html", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/content/aboutPDF.mjs", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/tests/browser/browser_aboutPDF_features.js", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/tests/browser/head.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/aboutPDF.ftl", "toolkit/modules/RemotePageAccessManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/desktop-jar.inc.mn", "toolkit/themes/shared/icons/canvas.svg", "toolkit/themes/shared/icons/comment-24.svg", "toolkit/themes/shared/icons/find-in-page-24.svg", "toolkit/themes/shared/icons/highlighter-24.svg", "toolkit/themes/shared/icons/odd-spreads-24.svg", "toolkit/themes/shared/icons/presentation-mode-24.svg", "toolkit/themes/shared/icons/signature-24.svg"], "git_node": "9f0b6839bbe97678754719d171c3b7c38baf7a11", "git_parents": ["62766d4cf24f211720f281965f83f15eb873d218"], "node": "0c03fdc339c74673641c5caa3ec5d4b980ca4e39", "parents": ["bffcac191bc6abda033f515ab3881a1c51e2bc8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057608 - Promote the PDF tools with a notification bar on about:pdf and in the PDF viewer. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,tgiles,mossop\n\nBoth surfaces host the shared moz-message-bar, which the viewer can load now\nthat bug 2066198 exempts trusted module loads from CORS in resource:\ndocuments. The bar links to about:pdf#features and its strings live in\ntoolkit/about/pdfFeaturesNotification.ftl.\n\nA parent-process counter limits the bar to two impressions across both\nsurfaces by default. Dismissing the bar or visiting the features view hides\nevery open bar and prevents future impressions.\n\nThe viewer markup and wiring come from the pdf.js side, so this patch lands\nafter the pdf.js update that hosts the moz-message-bar.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319454\n", "files": ["toolkit/actors/AboutPDFChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/actors/AboutPDFParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/content/aboutPDF.css", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/content/aboutPDF.html", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/content/aboutPDF.mjs", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/tests/browser/browser_aboutPDF_features.js", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/tests/browser/browser_aboutPDF_notification.js", "toolkit/components/aboutpdf/tests/browser/head.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsFeaturesNotification.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfStreamConverter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/jar.mn", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_features_notification.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_features_notification_sync.js", "toolkit/modules/RemotePageAccessManager.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "1a092f41fa99d742d3c20eaf35b529d0c244336e", "git_parents": ["9f0b6839bbe97678754719d171c3b7c38baf7a11"], "node": "3b6e63ed6eefa54fbac8c4efb2d08add87d03947", "parents": ["0c03fdc339c74673641c5caa3ec5d4b980ca4e39"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Segun Famisa \u003csfamisa@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054470 - Create NavigationEvent to handle view-level navigations and fix MenuDialogMiddleware memory leaks r=android-reviewers,marcin\n\nMenuDialogMiddleware and MenuDialogNavigationMiddleware had callback references which are captured by the enclosing MenuDialogFragment. This meant that whenever the request to add-ons did not complete before the menu was closed, then we would end up having those references retained until the requested completed or failed, and causing a memory leak.\n\nThe solution is to create a NavigationEvent - that is emitted via the store reference, and collected in the fragment.\n\nThis is not a widely adopted pattern in the project, but it exists in the WebCompatReporterStore. I believe this is how we should handle \"effects\" such as navigations that require a reference to the enclosing \"view-level\" components (fragments, activities, composables, etc)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325661\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuDialogMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuNavigationMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/store/MenuStore.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/store/NavigationEvent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuDialogMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuNavigationMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "757e970d0ed2885ae3f12fdabfca28a408b54a0a", "git_parents": ["1a092f41fa99d742d3c20eaf35b529d0c244336e"], "node": "44c815ee68183b91f2c175df84a704499ed6694f", "parents": ["3b6e63ed6eefa54fbac8c4efb2d08add87d03947"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064245 - Remove the XPCOM component manager's GetClassObject methods. r=xpcom-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325476\n", "files": ["xpcom/components/nsComponentManager.cpp", "xpcom/components/nsComponentManager.h", "xpcom/components/nsComponentManagerUtils.cpp", "xpcom/components/nsComponentManagerUtils.h", "xpcom/components/nsIComponentManager.idl"], "git_node": "2dc6f6123d9cbb5045bc9345e6e34b07c85243fe", "git_parents": ["757e970d0ed2885ae3f12fdabfca28a408b54a0a"], "node": "14afaa3ed9e99075938a085a915d44bdc001faa0", "parents": ["44c815ee68183b91f2c175df84a704499ed6694f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068346 - Unwrap a copy in GetJSValFromKeyPathString. r=dom-storage-reviewers,jari\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326021\n", "files": ["dom/indexedDB/KeyPath.cpp"], "git_node": "6681c4d0c4fa7741ce0bae7b93b59a89f4b929f2", "git_parents": ["2dc6f6123d9cbb5045bc9345e6e34b07c85243fe"], "node": "53679a51321379df40cee45538dd294a35699b19", "parents": ["14afaa3ed9e99075938a085a915d44bdc001faa0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071964 - Rewrite try auto instructions to require human intervention r=ai4dev-reviewers,marco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325941\n", "files": ["AGENTS.md"], "git_node": "af78faba9fe010b2f0fb89bf463fd25796c6626f", "git_parents": ["6681c4d0c4fa7741ce0bae7b93b59a89f4b929f2"], "node": "d8a0a7ef62d672256c82e8d082a069f300c0a85d", "parents": ["53679a51321379df40cee45538dd294a35699b19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "any1here \u003cany1here@duck.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072055 - Avoid UserInteraction errors when telemetry is disabled r=chutten\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326037\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/core/Stopwatch.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/core/TelemetryUserInteraction.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/core/TelemetryUserInteraction.h"], "git_node": "51c97f63714852ef96aac132d5c57ccff99a5118", "git_parents": ["af78faba9fe010b2f0fb89bf463fd25796c6626f"], "node": "7997d647c43e2c877a4de298043e664a82538ed7", "parents": ["d8a0a7ef62d672256c82e8d082a069f300c0a85d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051510 - Route MediaCapabilities decoder creation through PDMFactorySupport::IsSupportedAsync to ensure remote processes have reported their supported codecs. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309552\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediacapabilities/MediaCapabilities.cpp", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/media-capabilities/decodingInfo-api-modes.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "42c9a1a5fc264058fb3a36b6dbb11a153c5fda31", "git_parents": ["51c97f63714852ef96aac132d5c57ccff99a5118"], "node": "1d6c5421cb65a521c07e475023fbc213ec120ae2", "parents": ["7997d647c43e2c877a4de298043e664a82538ed7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "any1here \u003cany1here@duck.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070732 - Use MOZ_APP_NAME and MOZ_APP_BASENAME for migration r=migration-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,mconley,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324783\n", "files": ["browser/components/migration/FirefoxProfileMigrator.sys.mjs", "browser/components/migration/FirefoxSelectableProfileMigrator.sys.mjs", "browser/components/migration/MigrationUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/migration/tests/browser/browser_disabled_migrator.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/migrationWizard.ftl", "tools/lint/fluent-lint/exclusions.yml"], "git_node": "1b3e94bf7545997330b1d9569b1f1700dcb91949", "git_parents": ["42c9a1a5fc264058fb3a36b6dbb11a153c5fda31"], "node": "34181027174ec007c1f78c6eb22585eb90ae68fb", "parents": ["1d6c5421cb65a521c07e475023fbc213ec120ae2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071968 - Enable 'media.audio.reuse-stream-on-seek' by default on macOS. r=media-playback-reviewers,jolin\n\nTurn the stream reuse back on for macOS on every channel. The other platforms keep the Nightly-only default they have today.\n\nIt was restricted to Nightly while bug 2065711 and bug 2065393 were open. Both are fixed on 157, which is where this flip lands too, so it should not go back any further than that.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325948\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "cc7df561acc50eebf42529caf8bc7e31d66df23b", "git_parents": ["1b3e94bf7545997330b1d9569b1f1700dcb91949"], "node": "2c5befbed0bfe45122dd30dad6932a25901270cd", "parents": ["34181027174ec007c1f78c6eb22585eb90ae68fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hanna.alemu \u003chalemu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069104 - Add a targeting attribute for the number of origins allowed to send notifications. r=omc-reviewers,andhuang,nimbus-reviewers,aminomancer\n\nAdds `allowedNotificationOrigins` to the ASRouter targeting context: a count\nof the origins the user has granted the desktop-notification permission to.\nBlocks are not counted, so the value is 0 on a fresh profile and returns to 0\nwhen every notification permission is removed.\n\nThe attribute is also recorded in the `nimbus_targeting_context` ping via\nTargetingContextRecorder, so it is available for experiment analysis. The\nClosed-Browser Web Notifications Delivery experiment pre-registers a \"number\nof allowed origins\" segment (1, 2-4, 5+), which needs the count per enrolled\nclient rather than the boolean the targeting expression provides.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323738\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/docs/targeting-attributes.md", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouterTargeting.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_asrouter_targeting.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/TargetingContextRecorder.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "c05ed532198f18d65ae0cfb53bd79e026adb1652", "git_parents": ["cc7df561acc50eebf42529caf8bc7e31d66df23b"], "node": "29d53b9c161974cd333e922f61517b62678a3075", "parents": ["2c5befbed0bfe45122dd30dad6932a25901270cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047566 - Update to Glean v70.0.0 r=chutten,supply-chain-reviewers,mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThis does not vendor the new Rust sources.\nThat will be done in a later commit, together with an appservices\nupdate, to avoid any duplication.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319437\n", "files": ["Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/Cargo.toml", "gradle/libs.versions.toml", "python/sites/mach.txt", "supply-chain/config.toml"], "git_node": "5df39d1d0120e084ec65628503f75358c899fac2", "git_parents": ["c05ed532198f18d65ae0cfb53bd79e026adb1652"], "node": "97bfee097710feea88993d78be4b246c3dba12f5", "parents": ["29d53b9c161974cd333e922f61517b62678a3075"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.