b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nsv-SE -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nta -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nte -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nth -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\ntl -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\ntr -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\ntrs -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nuk -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nur -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nuz -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nvi -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nwo -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nxh -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nzam -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nzh-CN -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\nzh-TW -\u003e 18a2cbde6063b51b0ebd35dd76d1a21c3bc555d3\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "99f333944aa8fdad6e315773c5800fc5e1c631e5", "git_parents": ["8490c099c405efbd84615fa4eb7a3d1e8d8ce3a5"], "node": "666dba7ba25b4a9dcd688a8546d3839af23b450b", "parents": ["c5f608889517770a082f385bc36e37792aa954d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067504 [Linux] Implement UpdateRendererUsageLocked() and get GlobalRefsSet status from all DMABuf surfaces in one call r=alwu,media-playback-reviewers\n\n- Implement DMABufSurface::GetGlobalRefsSet() to poll array of DMABufSurface fd's\n- Implement UpdateRendererUsageLocked() to get usage status of all DMABufSurface's from video pool\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325328\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoFramePool.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoFramePool.h", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.h"], "git_node": "1fd7be717ddde9d2b9ed8e36b622762927d8a5fb", "git_parents": ["99f333944aa8fdad6e315773c5800fc5e1c631e5"], "node": "4c8f86c3323a8d15af5c54c6f86328a789f41d02", "parents": ["666dba7ba25b4a9dcd688a8546d3839af23b450b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067504 [Linux] Use MOZ_REQUIRES(lock) for VideoFramePool r=alwu,media-playback-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326130\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoFramePool.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoFramePool.h"], "git_node": "79d564aa246b4ad0b6336482b58476d0847a7ac0", "git_parents": ["1fd7be717ddde9d2b9ed8e36b622762927d8a5fb"], "node": "9498adb11015a723d9c2fe8a29cc1cdac824eaed", "parents": ["4c8f86c3323a8d15af5c54c6f86328a789f41d02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069551 - [Linux][Vulkan Video] Defer vkDestroyDevice until no decoder holds any cached device. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nLoaders before 1.4.345 race vkDestroyDevice on one VkDevice with\nvkGetDeviceProcAddr on another. Keep every (lib, deviceName) holder\nalive while any decoder is still a client, then destroy them together\nunder sDeviceHolders. GetOrCreate also keeps that lock across\nav_hwdevice_ctx_create so two threads cannot each build a device.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325806\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/VulkanDeviceHolder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/VulkanDeviceHolder.h"], "git_node": "4dd0bcf92d5e3268e8579337cb2819e7fd464c22", "git_parents": ["79d564aa246b4ad0b6336482b58476d0847a7ac0"], "node": "3d0d7e8b3f9dba369fa2a553cbef52e5192bf0fc", "parents": ["9498adb11015a723d9c2fe8a29cc1cdac824eaed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Farre \u003cfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069288 - Make tests using XSLT flip the pref on. r=dom-core-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dom-worker-reviewers,emilio,smaug,edenchuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323551\n", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser-xslt.toml", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser.toml", "docshell/test/chrome/chrome-xslt.toml", "docshell/test/chrome/chrome.toml", "dom/base/test/mochitest-bug1.toml", "dom/base/test/mochitest-bug2.toml", "dom/base/test/mochitest-xslt.toml", "dom/events/test/mochitest-xslt.toml", "dom/events/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/html/test/mochitest-bug1.toml", "dom/html/test/mochitest-xslt.toml", "dom/security/permissionspolicy/test/mochitest/mochitest-xslt.toml", "dom/security/permissionspolicy/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "dom/security/test/csp/mochitest-xslt.toml", "dom/security/test/csp/mochitest.toml", "dom/serviceworkers/test/mochitest-common.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/bugs/mochitest-xslt.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/bugs/mochitest.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/general/mochitest-xslt.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/general/mochitest.toml", "dom/tests/reftest/reftest.list", "dom/tests/reftest/xml-stylesheet/reftest.list", "dom/xml/test/mochitest-xslt.toml", "dom/xml/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/xslt/crashtests/crashtests.list", "dom/xslt/tests/browser/browser.toml", "dom/xslt/tests/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list", "testing/web-platform/meta/content-security-policy/xslt/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/idlharness.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/service-workers/service-worker/xsl-base-url.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/xml/xslt/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": "6e0998406503c7df86c96826fc0dc9cc76b6b87e", "git_parents": ["4dd0bcf92d5e3268e8579337cb2819e7fd464c22"], "node": "fe981d85d70444abd0ec18289d1ae9f9c45da6f5", "parents": ["3d0d7e8b3f9dba369fa2a553cbef52e5192bf0fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041248 - Prevent NTLM login attempt with empty credentials r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326121\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpNTLMAuth.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpNTLMAuth.h"], "git_node": "31cbb927cdd57c35d98d4336d2f4018a5a68f85d", "git_parents": ["6e0998406503c7df86c96826fc0dc9cc76b6b87e"], "node": "042b8331cb71c0a932cf818db32fd706026d4ba6", "parents": ["fe981d85d70444abd0ec18289d1ae9f9c45da6f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "elkal98 \u003ckhalid.alhaddad98@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1979386 - KeyShortcuts constructor takes an unused window argument. r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325825\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/components/App.js", "devtools/client/framework/browser-toolbox/window.js", "devtools/client/framework/toolbox.js", "devtools/client/inspector/breadcrumbs.js", "devtools/client/inspector/computed/computed.js", "devtools/client/inspector/inspector.js", "devtools/client/inspector/markup/markup.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/rules.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/Toolbar.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/previews/SourcePreview.js", "devtools/client/shared/components/SearchBox.js", "devtools/client/shared/key-shortcuts.js", "devtools/client/shared/sourceeditor/editor.js", "devtools/client/shared/test/browser_key_shortcuts.js", "devtools/client/shared/widgets/tooltip/SwatchBasedEditorTooltip.js", "devtools/client/storage/ui.js", "devtools/client/styleeditor/StyleEditorUI.sys.mjs", "devtools/client/webconsole/webconsole-ui.js"], "git_node": "40a4cf87495b37defdcf70c55c7849ffea911db8", "git_parents": ["31cbb927cdd57c35d98d4336d2f4018a5a68f85d"], "node": "d77fbc3313c7bfd12ac15bb431d8c66faec8cfb7", "parents": ["042b8331cb71c0a932cf818db32fd706026d4ba6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hojun-Cho \u003cghwns6743@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066829 - Make a surface depend on the snapshots it displays. r=nical\n\nNothing reads image_dependencies, so a snapshot's render task has no\ndependents and is scheduled in the last pass, after the image that\ndisplays it from inside an intermediate surface has already sampled the\ntexture cache entry. On the frame the entry is allocated it is\nuninitialized.\n\nMake the surface that displays a snapshot depend on its task.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321707\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs"], "git_node": "afdd2de4a131e7d04ad42befcd1a621a9491e00b", "git_parents": ["40a4cf87495b37defdcf70c55c7849ffea911db8"], "node": "83fefb5510fdabc32bc2a91ac7b30553e3a3f661", "parents": ["d77fbc3313c7bfd12ac15bb431d8c66faec8cfb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hojun-Cho \u003cghwns6743@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066829 - Fix the filter key in the snapshot-dependency reftest. r=nical\n\nThe test used the singular filter: key, which wrench ignores, so the image\nit displays was never nested in filter surfaces and the test passed even\nwithout the dependency.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321708\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/snapshot-dependency-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/snapshot-dependency.yaml"], "git_node": "0f91edbeda6605468a0129515857bf5c2856c4d4", "git_parents": ["afdd2de4a131e7d04ad42befcd1a621a9491e00b"], "node": "7fa7b556f151b72d7467b6fbdadcdf29c56e604b", "parents": ["83fefb5510fdabc32bc2a91ac7b30553e3a3f661"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050313 - Partition DictionaryCache not partitioned by OriginAttributes r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320045\n", "files": ["netwerk/cache2/CacheEntry.cpp", "netwerk/cache2/CacheIndex.cpp", "netwerk/cache2/CacheStorageService.cpp", "netwerk/cache2/Dictionary.cpp", "netwerk/cache2/Dictionary.h", "netwerk/cache2/nsICacheTesting.idl", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpHandler.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_content_decoding_error_telemetry.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_dictionary_oa_isolation.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_dictionary_replacement.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "27557128682ea6ed92b09a4982968a964b592a46", "git_parents": ["0f91edbeda6605468a0129515857bf5c2856c4d4"], "node": "04812536c94042970a98a9dce1b0514581783023", "parents": ["7fa7b556f151b72d7467b6fbdadcdf29c56e604b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072505 - Add @Critical annotation to the deleteDownloadedFileTest efficiency and legacy UI tests r=mbarone\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326386\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/DownloadTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/DownloadTest.kt"], "git_node": "698b4ebdbf839c8e8a81e03043051900ee82d3fb", "git_parents": ["27557128682ea6ed92b09a4982968a964b592a46"], "node": "fcbcbbccb5baa85beb1ef07d402f67dc51d3559d", "parents": ["04812536c94042970a98a9dce1b0514581783023"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070909 - Name an active descendant on the DevTools trees that manage focus, r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau,nchevobbe.\n\nTree.js and VirtualizedTree.js emitted aria-activedescendant only once an item\nhad been focused, so until then the tree was a tab stop with no current item.\nName the first rendered node, but only where the container passes onFocus:\nwithout one nothing ever becomes focused, so claiming the pattern would hide a\nkeyboard defect rather than fix one. The attribute exempts these trees'\nnegative-tabindex rows from the keyboard-focusability check, which is what the\nannotations removed here absorbed; they cite Bug 1849028 and Bug 1858041.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325020\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/components/PrimaryPanes/ProjectSearch.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_af.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_gp.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_qz.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/integration/browser.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/sourcemaps/browser.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/tracer/browser.toml", "devtools/client/inspector/extensions/test/browser.toml", "devtools/client/memory/test/browser/browser.toml", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_mz.toml", "devtools/client/shared/components/Tree.js", "devtools/client/shared/components/VirtualizedTree.js", "devtools/client/shared/components/test/node/components/tree.test.js", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/_jsterm.toml", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/_webconsole_ak.toml", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/_webconsole_lz.toml", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/_webconsole_object_inspector.toml"], "git_node": "aa1a63586ae357b674c92bde083d36f8701ff76f", "git_parents": ["698b4ebdbf839c8e8a81e03043051900ee82d3fb"], "node": "d7988f299c826d4cbb90d5c93bb47f118db1e963", "parents": ["fcbcbbccb5baa85beb1ef07d402f67dc51d3559d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070914 - Let a focusable ARIA separator satisfy the mochitest accessibility checks, r=Jamie,devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe.\n\nARIAMap.cpp gives separator and scrollbar eNoAction, so the action count rule\ncan never pass for them, and findInteractiveAccessible walks past them because\nit consults INTERACTIVE_ROLES only. Bug 1860733 makes the DevTools SplitBox\nsplitter a focusable separator, so adjust both the action count rule and\nfindInteractiveAccessible to handle this case.\n\nBoth only apply while the separator is focusable, as the same role covers\ndecorations that can never be: XULMap.inc maps the nav-bar toolbarspring to\nXULToolbarSeparatorAccessible, and several urlbar tests click it on purpose to\ndismiss the panel with mustHaveAccessibleRule turned off.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325025\n", "files": ["devtools/client/framework/test/browser.toml", "testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/AccessibilityUtils.js"], "git_node": "d2fc2f22fe59965e0412342d3d2cfb0f824385e3", "git_parents": ["aa1a63586ae357b674c92bde083d36f8701ff76f"], "node": "40590e94cecdc8e39821bb49b1fd47b068a82f4e", "parents": ["d7988f299c826d4cbb90d5c93bb47f118db1e963"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071232 - Give the editor's column breakpoint markers an accessible name, r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy.\n\nThe marker is a button holding only an SVG, so it had no accessible name at\nall. A line can hold several and they are identical but for their position, so\nthe name gives the line and column. aria-pressed carries the state the\nactive class shows visually.\n\nThe a11y_checks annotations this retires were filed as Bug 1849028.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325413\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/components/Editor/ColumnBreakpoints.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_af.toml", "devtools/client/locales/en-US/debugger.properties"], "git_node": "af7de84600caf0e8e5efa781fca8463088fab520", "git_parents": ["d2fc2f22fe59965e0412342d3d2cfb0f824385e3"], "node": "442200b47de24d884c0c8ad757a1e0ba83772c09", "parents": ["40590e94cecdc8e39821bb49b1fd47b068a82f4e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860733 - Make the SplitBox splitter keyboard operable, r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe.\n\nDraggable rendered role=\"presentation\" with no tab index, so the splitter was\nabsent from the accessibility tree and could only be dragged. Its other two\nconsumers, the netmonitor column resizer and GridElementWidthResizer, stay\npointer-only.\n\nThe toolbox host splitter in toolbox-hosts.js already implements this, so the\nposition is reported in pixels and set from a ResizeObserver rather than\nrendered, since the split box is resized without this component re-rendering.\nbrowser_net_tabbar_focus.js's annotation cites Bug 1849028; it is the same\nsplitter.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325026\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_gp.toml", "devtools/client/locales/en-US/components.properties", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_mz.toml", "devtools/client/shared/components/splitter/Draggable.js", "devtools/client/shared/components/splitter/SplitBox.css", "devtools/client/shared/components/splitter/SplitBox.js", "devtools/client/shared/components/test/browser/browser.toml", "devtools/client/shared/components/test/browser/browser_split_box_keyboard.js"], "git_node": "3697b70e011ecfef79871eefd37d5d87fed8f55f", "git_parents": ["af7de84600caf0e8e5efa781fca8463088fab520"], "node": "c71933f567ad4fef90722dc49539a89924333b36", "parents": ["442200b47de24d884c0c8ad757a1e0ba83772c09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Frederik Braun \u003cfbraun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069273 - collect telemetry for Sanitizer API configuration r=tschuster,webidl,emilio,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323532\n", "files": ["dom/base/UseCounters.conf", "dom/base/test/browser.toml", "dom/base/test/browser_use_counters.js", "dom/base/test/file_use_counter_sanitizer_config.html", "dom/base/test/file_use_counter_sanitizer_default.html", "dom/base/test/file_use_counter_sanitizer_empty.html", "dom/base/test/file_use_counter_sanitizer_invalid.html", "dom/base/test/file_use_counter_sanitizer_methods.html", "dom/base/test/file_use_counter_sanitizer_noop.html", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "dom/security/sanitizer/Sanitizer.cpp", "dom/security/sanitizer/Sanitizer.h", "dom/webidl/Sanitizer.webidl", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilderCppSupplement.h"], "git_node": "be453496002d6b418d33d785aae6b33a6fd4c121", "git_parents": ["3697b70e011ecfef79871eefd37d5d87fed8f55f"], "node": "f2b5b87998fbfbe3b01ad8e60a04c4e2ef88b25d", "parents": ["c71933f567ad4fef90722dc49539a89924333b36"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Frederik Braun \u003cfbraun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069273 - sanitizer global is a window r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323999\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/security/sanitizer/Sanitizer.cpp", "dom/security/sanitizer/Sanitizer.h"], "git_node": "917ec062545e787010eb7b62761de5778e693c78", "git_parents": ["be453496002d6b418d33d785aae6b33a6fd4c121"], "node": "8ff8044b32b3293cf220ea5189b1e9bcda4503f5", "parents": ["f2b5b87998fbfbe3b01ad8e60a04c4e2ef88b25d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Frederik Braun \u003cfbraun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069273 - add counter for Sanitizer javascriptURLs config r=tschuster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326077\n", "files": ["dom/base/UseCounters.conf", "dom/base/test/browser_use_counters.js", "dom/base/test/file_use_counter_sanitizer_config.html", "dom/base/test/file_use_counter_sanitizer_methods.html", "dom/base/test/file_use_counter_sanitizer_noop.html", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "dom/security/sanitizer/Sanitizer.cpp"], "git_node": "cd49d78fc055f59da3a1c7d260e393fdde9aa552", "git_parents": ["917ec062545e787010eb7b62761de5778e693c78"], "node": "25a3a8ad3c1fb69d8e4acd1a958ad525c78f6c91", "parents": ["8ff8044b32b3293cf220ea5189b1e9bcda4503f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Corentin Bect \u003ccbect@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065565 - Determine the privacy report notification's content outside the notification helper r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nbuildPrivacyReportNotification used to have two responsibilities: determining the notification content to display and building the notification.\n\nThis patch introduces PrivacyReportNotificationContent, a data holder for the resolved notification's title and text, with a factory method for each variant. PrivacyReportNotificationWorker, which owns the blocked tracker logic, now builds the notification content based on the blocked tracker count, and then hands it to showPrivacyReportNotification, which just posts the notification.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322882\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationContent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationHelper.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationWorker.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationContentTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationHelperTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationWorkerTest.kt"], "git_node": "5ec3111910c4644d3249c71d01ff24cc236c5a64", "git_parents": ["cd49d78fc055f59da3a1c7d260e393fdde9aa552"], "node": "7fc7a42bc352296d22866e678e46813ae5845e76", "parents": ["25a3a8ad3c1fb69d8e4acd1a958ad525c78f6c91"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Corentin Bect \u003ccbect@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070897 - Return to the build-in VPN settings screen once a location is selected r=android-reviewers,Roger\n\nSelecting a location in the VPN locations list applied the selected choice but left the user on this screen.\n\n Now the app returns to the built-in VPN settings screen once a location is selected by the user and applied. It pops to `R.id.ipProtectionFragment` destination rather than one entry up using `popBackStack()` so that a double tap can't pop the back stack twice.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325864\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/ipprotection/IPProtectionLocationsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/ipprotection/IPProtectionLocationsFragmentTest.kt"], "git_node": "264e977fb8819d14b79e32c0fc599978044830e1", "git_parents": ["5ec3111910c4644d3249c71d01ff24cc236c5a64"], "node": "7fb5afdeba8610b56d6de86329840fff98f6d34c", "parents": ["7fc7a42bc352296d22866e678e46813ae5845e76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072135: Clearing a container should also clear entries from closed windows. r=sessionstore-reviewers,sfoster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326116\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_clear_container_closed_windows.js"], "git_node": "585b14c17e54eea28383f2884c6a267098f09552", "git_parents": ["264e977fb8819d14b79e32c0fc599978044830e1"], "node": "8daef47986d92c77c226ffb6deb3caf526e3c10e", "parents": ["7fb5afdeba8610b56d6de86329840fff98f6d34c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072119 - Add telemetry for why DNS lookups miss the cache r=necko-reviewers,valentin,mxinden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326128\n", "files": ["netwerk/dns/HostRecordQueue.cpp", "netwerk/dns/metrics.yaml", "netwerk/dns/nsHostRecord.cpp", "netwerk/dns/nsHostRecord.h", "netwerk/dns/nsHostResolver.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_dns_cache_miss_telemetry.js", "netw