tasiak.at\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1719394 - Preserve early WebSocket frames. r=devtools-reviewers,necko-reviewers,kershaw,jdescottes\n\nFrames can be delivered before webSocketOpened reaches the DevTools\nwatcher. Carry the HTTP channel ID on every frame callback so those\nframes can be associated immediately instead of being discarded.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320711\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/test/file_ws_early_backend_wsh.py", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/websockets/browser.toml", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/websockets/browser_net_ws-early-connection.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/websockets/html_ws-early-connection-page.html", "devtools/server/actors/resources/websockets.js", "devtools/server/tests/xpcshell/test_websocket_watcher.js", "devtools/server/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "dom/websocket/tests/test_websocket_frame.html", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/PWebSocketEventListener.ipdl", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerChild.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventService.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventService.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/nsIWebSocketEventService.idl", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts"], "git_node": "8437595478a076ad7ca58aedb5fdbd75d471e458", "git_parents": ["0383dea6095fb202f3b0704e8802c7ab655cba92"], "node": "4be950c89eb3ad5b121a77ef7c779a3397a570d1", "parents": ["4642eac18a6bd8809bc1aef326da114705f34d84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jakub Stasiak \u003cjakub@stasiak.at\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1719394 - Remove WebSocket connection map. r=devtools-reviewers,necko-reviewers,jdescottes,kershaw\n\nD320711 makes the HTTP channel ID available without consulting the\nWebSocket connection map for frame notifications. Carry the ID on close\nnotifications as well so the DevTools watcher can remove that map.\n\nDepends on D320711.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324117\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/resources/websockets.js", "dom/websocket/WebSocket.cpp", "dom/websocket/tests/test_websocket_frame.html", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/PWebSocketEventListener.ipdl", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerChild.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventListenerParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventService.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketEventService.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/nsIWebSocketEventService.idl", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts"], "git_node": "9b6fd2c2d8ae5519a99e692ae3695830b1e3609b", "git_parents": ["8437595478a076ad7ca58aedb5fdbd75d471e458"], "node": "8262f7bdd206e3e3bbf15cf30d8efa2757b77e61", "parents": ["4be950c89eb3ad5b121a77ef7c779a3397a570d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068982 - P1. Add a shared autofill storage migrator and port addresses to it r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers\n\nCredit cards need the copy addresses already have, and it does not depend on\nthe collection: the same seven methods, differing only in the prefs that budget\nthe run, the Glean category it reports to, and how two records are compared.\n\nSo AddressStorageMigrator becomes AutofillStorageMigrator, and a subclass at the\nfoot of the file supplies the rest as members -- the way RustAutofillAdapterBase\nand the JSON store's AutofillRecords both parameterise. Addresses behave as\nbefore, except that a few log messages no longer name the collection: the logger\nprefix already does.\n\n_report moves to the shared class, so the address migration test stubs it there.\nAssigning to the subclass prototype would shadow the real method and restoring\nwould leave undefined in its place. It keeps its underscore because that test\nreaches it from another module, which is not true of the new members.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324550\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_address_migration.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/AddressStorageMigrator.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/AutofillStorageMigrator.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillStorage.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "9a0dd752fd8704a84844e7afaa3d98cb33175242", "git_parents": ["9b6fd2c2d8ae5519a99e692ae3695830b1e3609b"], "node": "e5daabcb32156c72867dc17e7b1e70955dd5d357", "parents": ["8262f7bdd206e3e3bbf15cf30d8efa2757b77e61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068982 - P2. Support migrating credit cards to the Rust store and serving them from it r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers\n\nServes credit cards from the Rust store once a profile has copied them across,\nbehind extensions.formautofill.creditCards.storage.rust.enabled, with the shape\naddresses use: a dry run that measures and discards, a real run budgeted to\nthree attempts, and a copy back when the pref is turned off.\n\nThe copy is P1's AutofillStorageMigrator; this adds the credit card subclass.\nTwo parts of it are new rather than a rename of the address version:\n\n  - fieldDiffers goes through creditCardFieldDiffers. cc-number is a mask, and\n    the two stores build it at different widths, so only the last four digits\n    compare; cc-number-encrypted compares by presence, encryption not being\n    deterministic.\n  - #migrate asks the source to export each record first, so the number crosses\n    in the clear and the target encrypts it under its own scheme rather than\n    inheriting ciphertext it cannot read. A record that will not export is\n    counted failed rather than copied without its number, and the exported\n    records are dropped once the write is done rather than held for the rest\n    of the copy. This runs for addresses too, where the source has no\n    _recordForMigrationExport and the record comes back unchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324551\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/AutofillStorageMigrator.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillStorageBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillCreditCardStorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillStorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "ce266bf6f202c58cf0d1746fd227fd0037ba3c0f", "git_parents": ["9a0dd752fd8704a84844e7afaa3d98cb33175242"], "node": "6e7eaa667022c308ed613d66821ac61a778924fa", "parents": ["e5daabcb32156c72867dc17e7b1e70955dd5d357"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068982 - P3. Test the credit card migration r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers\n\nCovers the copy in both directions, and what is specific to cards: the number\narrives re-encrypted by the target rather than as the bytes it was handed.\n\nThe two failure tests are the point. A decrypt that starts working and then\nstops, as a keychain locking mid-run would, must leave the profile where it is\nand the source records byte-identical, so a later launch can still copy them. A\nkey store that will not open at all must defer without spending the retry\nbudget. Both failures are transient on purpose: a permanently lost key is lost\nwhichever way the copy is written, so only a recoverable one tells refusing a\nrecord apart from copying it without its number.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324552\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_migration.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "a3f12212eac0b6bece10958b5f362690a3fd40e2", "git_parents": ["ce266bf6f202c58cf0d1746fd227fd0037ba3c0f"], "node": "b93ed08c0ee4e4f29545b7c5121dd1890244c464", "parents": ["6e7eaa667022c308ed613d66821ac61a778924fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1949178 - Introduce a platform-specific thread handle r=afranchuk\n\nThis is supposed to mirror the native representation of a thread on each\nplatform, which would make it a HANDLE on Windows. However we're\nsticking with a thread id there for compatibility with Breakpad's\ninterfaces. Once we drop Breakpad in favor of a bare minidump-writer\nbackend it can be changed to a HANDLE. As for Linux we stick with a tid\nbut leave the possibility of making it a pidfd in the future.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323671\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/linux.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/mach.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/windows.rs"], "git_node": "885d10c2f554f02531a1c7d7a197d23fcf85ec29", "git_parents": ["a3f12212eac0b6bece10958b5f362690a3fd40e2"], "node": "50e1a3b4314c3055f6a69adc6440316cd3e3a8b4", "parents": ["b93ed08c0ee4e4f29545b7c5121dd1890244c464"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1949178 - Replace the ProcessReaderHandle type with a proper raw representation of the crash helper process handle abstract type r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323672\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/messages.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/linux.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/mach.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation.rs"], "git_node": "30102f22ffaa386378128a87ad28b40d6752a448", "git_parents": ["885d10c2f554f02531a1c7d7a197d23fcf85ec29"], "node": "a819740e64d36fbcd8ac884d761dcde6fe850436", "parents": ["50e1a3b4314c3055f6a69adc6440316cd3e3a8b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1949178 - Introduce an IPC message for minidump generation r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323673\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_client/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/messages.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/ipc_server.rs"], "git_node": "1b29c30687f0d4d9ea00ade2fa6448b6a1b41ff6", "git_parents": ["30102f22ffaa386378128a87ad28b40d6752a448"], "node": "5f2ee185f3e0983fa023e697d3612900c3716802", "parents": ["a819740e64d36fbcd8ac884d761dcde6fe850436"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1949178 - Fix type used for looking up auxiliary vector information r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323674\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/breakpad_wrapper/breakpad_wrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "8b39d1c9d3285e52b63cd244f1166e11086c9321", "git_parents": ["1b29c30687f0d4d9ea00ade2fa6448b6a1b41ff6"], "node": "2b00c2466c49d361abf395a44d57ad6860f439d7", "parents": ["5f2ee185f3e0983fa023e697d3612900c3716802"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1949178 - Add a wrapper function to generate a minidump on demand rather than via the exception handler r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323675\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/breakpad_wrapper/breakpad_wrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "7b72c47cc5e8cdd784180c9ec888cabf05a09f0d", "git_parents": ["8b39d1c9d3285e52b63cd244f1166e11086c9321"], "node": "4382c08998c2184656d6483f276642453c5c48eb", "parents": ["2b00c2466c49d361abf395a44d57ad6860f439d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1949178 - Make the crash helper handle and respond to minidump generation messages r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323676\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/breakpad/unix_strings.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/breakpad/windows_strings.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/cbindgen.toml", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/breakpad_crash_generator.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/ipc_server.rs"], "git_node": "d41cfdc5f1403ea15cf25ebae6a6bff9a2ff2475", "git_parents": ["7b72c47cc5e8cdd784180c9ec888cabf05a09f0d"], "node": "e2ce366d38a9e84d96db150a78f4729cd316eb83", "parents": ["4382c08998c2184656d6483f276642453c5c48eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1949178 - Add support for generating minidumps via the crash helper client code r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323677\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_client/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "6b0d9f0d9077c99412b6979b36222a6b66e63fd2", "git_parents": ["d41cfdc5f1403ea15cf25ebae6a6bff9a2ff2475"], "node": "f63c90467b755b3c379a7b222ca54756bed133b1", "parents": ["e2ce366d38a9e84d96db150a78f4729cd316eb83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1949178 - Re-enable capturing child process shutdown hangs r=afranchuk,ipc-reviewers,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nWhile this change re-enables pre-existing functionality it changes both\nits implementation and interface. We now request dumping a process via\nits Gecko process id rather than via its PID, this avoids races that\ncould be caused by PID reuse. Additionally the dumping process still\nblocks the calling thread but takes place entirely in the crash helper\nprocess, not in the main process anymore.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323678\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/CrashReporterHost.cpp", "ipc/glue/CrashReporterHost.h", "toolkit/crashreporter/nsDummyExceptionHandler.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/nsExceptionHandler.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/nsExceptionHandler.h"], "git_node": "84af319863faf38918384b5adc2ba8fefd984ff8", "git_parents": ["6b0d9f0d9077c99412b6979b36222a6b66e63fd2"], "node": "07f39c12aa597d665c7a19b5654d26f7d466f5c0", "parents": ["f63c90467b755b3c379a7b222ca54756bed133b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1949178 - Remove some needless includes of CrashReporterHost.h r=afranchuk,ipc-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,padenot,nika,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324067\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RDDChild.cpp", "ipc/glue/CrashReporterHost.h", "xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcher.h", "xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherLinux.cpp", "xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherMac.cpp"], "git_node": "4645d8f8ea77bcde75f9088cd3cc57f9383d1f50", "git_parents": ["84af319863faf38918384b5adc2ba8fefd984ff8"], "node": "c54024e4c354ee3b8580dff6cef34f613d467c6f", "parents": ["07f39c12aa597d665c7a19b5654d26f7d466f5c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071837 - Add test coverage for the addresses.storage.rust.enabled pref r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers\n\nTwo manifests run existing address tests a second time, with the Rust store\nserving every address read and write:\n\n- test/browser/rust/browser.toml includes test/browser/address/ wholesale, so\n  those tests and their skip-if annotations are inherited rather than copied.\n  The entries it lists are the address tests that live in test/browser/ instead,\n  whose manifest also holds credit card, passport and ML tests that must not run\n  against this store; each of those is a shim that loads its original.\n\n- test/unit/xpcshell_rust.toml does the same for test_getRecords.js, and names\n  the storage tests that cannot be shared: they reach either for sync APIs the\n  Rust adapter does not answer, since its sync goes through a bridged engine, or\n  past the collection API into the JSON store.\n\nBoth head.js files assert rust.active once the pref is set. The pref only asks:\nFormAutofillStorage keeps serving JSON until the migration completes, so a run\ncould otherwise pass having never touched the Rust store.\n\nbrowser_address_migration.js moves out of test/browser/rust/, because it covers\nthe migration rather than re-running a test under a different pref. Its fixture\nnow carries a multi-line street address and a phone number, so the fields Rust\nderives on read from the single column it stores are asserted against a record\nthe migration copied.\n\nEverything left under test/browser/rust/, and every entry in xpcshell_rust.toml,\nis a second run of a test that lives elsewhere, so both can be deleted whole\nonce the Rust store is the only one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325843\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/moz.build", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_address_migration.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/head.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_address_migration.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_autofill_address_housenumber.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_autofill_address_level.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_autofill_address_name.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_autofill_address_select.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_autofill_address_select_inexact.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_autofill_address_select_match_isoid.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_autofill_address_textarea.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_autofill_duplicate_fields.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_clearPopulatedForm.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_editAddressDialog.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_fillclear_events.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_manageAddressesDialog.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/browser_previewFormFields.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rust/head.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/head.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/xpcshell_rust.toml"], "git_node": "94680093d2357a635eb94a256270f258a431d20e", "git_parents": ["4645d8f8ea77bcde75f9088cd3cc57f9383d1f50"], "node": "3116245d24e89b07a65cda34dba59ce0deea9b33", "parents": ["c54024e4c354ee3b8580dff6cef34f613d467c6f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072331 - Update comment about when MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT is enabled. r=mfbt-reviewers,sergesanspaille DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326263\n", "files": ["mfbt/Assertions.h"], "git_node": "952c6cc9b1ce3fbb6fed7e81699070fb75f48a0d", "git_parents": ["94680093d2357a635eb94a256270f258a431d20e"], "node": "aa0ec4df6bef0110d545a818bbbd18832149c89f", "parents": ["3116245d24e89b07a65cda34dba59ce0deea9b33"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072510 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to c4efcd9321ce6063a31b8959dfbbaa268fdeebd9 r=release-managers,diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326388\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "ba8abbeca347a9941f5ade67bc8448dd2054d029", "git_parents": ["952c6cc9b1ce3fbb6fed7e81699070fb75f48a0d"], "node": "98f14c775c22a3f640d8b9a780ece59f40b9a9e3", "parents": ["aa0ec4df6bef0110d545a818bbbd18832149c89f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072302 - Avoid using ThinVec with a zero-size type in speculationrules. r=avandolder,dom-core-reviewers\n\nA single variant enum uses a ZST under the hood by default. Prevent it\nto be able to forbid ZSTs in ThinVec altogether.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326427\n", "files": ["dom/base/speculationrules/lib.rs"], "git_node": "73f959f215890858a67fda22160edf082e61dca8", "git_parents": ["ba8abbeca347a9941f5ade67bc8448dd2054d029"], "node": "b546fdb2c8a1af4039cf4cc89e37a8c50d626039", "parents": ["98f14c775c22a3f640d8b9a780ece59f40b9a9e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2013936 - Constrain WebRTC video encoder resolution/framerate to the negotiated H264/AV1 level (both codecs). r=webrtc-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,ng,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321191\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAV1FmtpParser.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestH264FmtpParser.cpp", "dom/media/mediacapabilities/MediaCapabilities.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/AV1FmtpParser.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/AV1FmtpParser.h", "dom/media/webrtc/H264FmtpParser.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/H264FmtpParser.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepCodecDescription.h", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/VideoConduit.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/jsep_session_unittest.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/jsep_track_unittest.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/protocol/h264-profile-levels.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/media-capabilities/encodingInfo-webrtc-av1-fmtp.any.js", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/media-capabilities/encodingInfo-webrtc-h264-fmtp.any.js"], "git_node": "8733ffd0da7ae69fad694d1bf576fd67b002271c", "git_parents": ["73f959f215890858a67fda22160edf082e61dca8"], "node": "61474bf443eb01b51218b3d9c9d18fb019631237", "parents": ["b546fdb2c8a1af4039cf4cc89e37a8c50d626039"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2013936 - Measure real encoded framerate in the H264 profile-levels WPT test, and un-skip the remaining ?rest variant. r=webrtc-reviewers,ng\n\nh264-profile-levels.https.html assumed the encoder always sends at the\ncapture's nominal 30fps, and checked a negotiated level's\nmacroblocks-per-second cap using that fixed value against only the received\nvideo's resolution. That's only valid for implementations that satisfy a\nlevel exclusively by downscaling resolution; an implementation that instead\n(or additionally) reduces framerate, like ours, was assumed non-conformant\neven when its encoder output genuinely fits within the level's constraints.\nThis is what still failed for the ?rest variant's lower levels after the\nprior commit's encoder fix (the ?interop-2026 variant's levels all happen to\nbe satisfiable by resolution alone, and were already un-skipped there).\n\nFix the test to measure the sender's real encoded framerate from the RTP\ntimestamps of the frames presented by the receiving video element (via\nrequestVideoFrameCallback), and use that in the macroblocks-per-second check\ninstead of the hardcoded capture framerate. RTP timestamps are immune to the\njitter of wall-clock stats sampling, and the measurement leaves one frame\nout to account for a frame-dropping cadence not aligning with the measured\nspan, so an encoder sitting exactly at a level's cap is not failed by\nmeasurement noise. Now that both the encoder-side fix and this test are\ncorrect, un-skip the remaining ?rest variant.\n\nOn Android the emulator's encoder cannot handle the resolutions implied by\nlevel 5 and above, so both variants hang on the first such level and are\nexpected to time out there (bug 2014007).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321192\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/protocol/h264-profile-levels.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc/protocol/h264-profile-levels.https.html"], "git_node": "6d23a3a2d48425efae0e7239993ddd118da6e400", "git_parents": ["8733ffd0da7ae69fad694d1bf576fd67b002271c"], "node": "55f05d7230736758d1b9a67abb95310d1bfef9ec", "parents": ["61474bf443eb01b51218b3d9c9d18fb019631237"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072326 - Use the fetched mozcheck binary directly and resolve it only once. r=linter-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nIn CI, the mozcheck toolchain is fetched by the task into MOZ_FETCHES_DIR,\nbut the linter still went through bootstrap_toolchain to locate it. That\nspawns `mach taskgraph tasks -k fetch -k toolchain` and takes about ten\nseconds in the rejected-words task, for a binary that was already on disk.\n\nLook in MOZ_FETCHES_DIR first, and cache the resolved binary so that the\nlookup done by `setup` in the parent process is reused by the forked\nmozlint workers instead of being repeated for every linter and every job.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326264\n", "files": ["tools/lint/mozcheck/__init__.py"], "git_node": "39229d5838debe19fc2e782f3a9e474058091d7a", "git_parents": ["6d23a3a2d48425efae0e7239993ddd118da6e400"], "node": "f188b8a7007162f66be502120bb4290575143845", "parents": ["55f05d7230736758d1b9a67abb95310d1bfef9ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072327 - Don't expand glob excludes when mozlint generates jobs. r=linter-reviewers,sergesanspaille,taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau\n\nLintRoller._generate_jobs calls filterpaths for every linter over the\ntop-level entries of the tree and discards the second return value, the\nlist of paths to exclude. Computing that list requires expanding every\nglob exclude (for instance `**/node_modules` and `**/package-lock.json`\nfrom the global exclude lists) by walking the whole tree with FileFinder,\nthen collapsing the result. When linting the whole tree in CI this takes\nabout six seconds per linter before any worker starts.\n\nAdd an `expand_excludes` parameter to filterpaths and pass False from\n_generate_jobs. The workers still run filterpaths on their own chunk and\ncompute the excludes there, so linter behaviour is unchanged. The l10n\nlinter and the mozlint optimization strategy in taskgraph also discard the\nexclude list, so they pass False too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326265\n", "files": ["python/mozlint/mozlint/pathutils.py", "python/mozlint/mozlint/roller.py", "python/mozlint/test/test_pathutils.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/optimize/mozlint.py", "tools/lint/python/l10n_lint.py"], "git_node": "ea299b87b45c8889f902809dc89b7b656e9dbf69", "git_parents": ["39229d5838debe19fc2e782f3a9e474058091d7a"], "node": "fd6543089e84d9a9bb2bdac8b9aed8b7a1f645d3", "parents": ["f188b8a7007162f66be502120bb4290575143845"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072329 - Make mozcheck walk all files when a linter has no extensions. r=linter-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nmozlint's built-in linter types lint every file under a directory when the\nlinter declares no `extensions`. mozcheck's walk_directory instead returned\nwithout walking anything, so when Bug 2023411 moved the rejected-words\nlinters to mozcheck, avoid-gobbledygook, which has no extension list, only\never checked the top-level files it was handed directly and never the\ncontents of directories.\n\nApply the extension filter only when there is one, and walk every file\notherwise, matching mozlint's behaviour.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326266\n", "files": ["tools/lint/mozcheck/src/pathutil.rs"], "git_node": "6a8d8d370f49979ef67ca24c0032a2b4f43c540d", "git_parents": ["ea299b87b45c8889f902809dc89b7b656e9dbf69"], "node": "efbd79d95e7b69ecacf4fa95c20aea03d5e384f9", "parents": ["fd6543089e84d9a9bb2bdac8b9aed8b7a1f645d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071976 - Update metadata for webcodecs/*.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326550\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/full-cycle-test.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/opus-multichannel.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/reconfiguring-encoder.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/temporal-svc-encoding.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/transfering.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-decoder-no-size-in-configure.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "642b568ccf3bc9482ab853666fd6263043670a80", "git_parents": ["6a8d8d370f49979ef67ca24c0032a2b4f43c540d"], "node": "aeabe415f096eeed82da52c6c735f7dccda011cd", "parents": ["efbd79d95e7b69ecacf4fa95c20aea03d5e384f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052474 - Support SpecialFrontendLocation in BaseMarkerType r=canova,profiler-reviewers\n\nAdd a UseSpecialFrontendLocation opt-in to BaseMarkerType, mutually exclusive\nwith a Locations array, so marker types with special frontend handling can\nderive from BaseMarkerType. MarkerTypeDisplay branches on it up front and\nreturns a bare SpecialFrontendLocation schema, so those types need no Locations\nand no display properties; PayloadFields stays optional and, when present,\nstill drives payload serialization and ETW. Static assertions enforce that\nexactly one of Locations and UseSpecialFrontendLocation is declared, and that a\nUseSpecialFrontendLocation type sets none of the ignored display properties.\n\nMigrate ScreenshotMarker as the first consumer; it keeps its custom\nStreamJSONMarkerData for the conditional url/windowWidth/windowHeight\nproperties, and sets ETWStoreName so ETW can tell the CompositorScreenshot and\nCompositorScreenshotWindowDestroyed markers apart.\n\nMigrate NativeAllocationMarker too, exercising the other half of the support:\nit declares PayloadFields and calls StreamJSONMarkerDataImpl from its custom\nStreamJSONMarkerData, and gains the ETW support it did not have before. The\nJSON payload is unchanged.\n\nAlso document UseSpecialFrontendLocation in the markers guide.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310301\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ProfilerScreenshots.cpp", "mozglue/baseprofiler/public/BaseProfilerMarkersPrerequisites.h", "tools/profiler/core/memory_hooks.cpp", "tools/profiler/docs/markers-guide.md"], "git_node": "632402d200481aa58dd980a95f3c35423f8de461", "git_parents": ["642b568ccf3bc9482ab853666fd6263043670a80"], "node": "7c4494aa30f468ffebb7dfa959bdda1113555ed3", "parents": ["aeabe415f096eeed82da52c6c735f7dccda011cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068322 - Make BrowserParent::mBrowserHost a strong reference. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324465\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.h"], "git_node": "6909f01fab27d6d4e85e415369f73f2706fd978b", "git_parents": ["632402d200481aa58dd980a95f3c35423f8de461"], "node": "f2602d16326b8f590e006a935e5d263b34a0ff43", "parents": ["7c4494aa30f468ffebb7dfa959bdda1113555ed3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068322 - Make BrowserParent::mBrowserBridgeParent a WeakPtr. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nEvery user of the field runs on the parent process main thread, which\nWeakPtr's debug-only owning-thread assertions now enforce.\nBrowserBridgeParent::Destroy() still clears it explicitly, so the pointer\nis dropped when the actor is destroyed rather than when the\nBrowserBridgeParent is freed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324466\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserBridgeParent.h", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.h"], "git_node": "e693b8ca03b46d413f90cedca43b34ad3604a4cb", "git_parents": ["6909f01fab27d6d4e85e415369f73f2706fd978b"], "node": "01b3a5a339c77dec255646a3e1add7e0fc0db8b8", "parents": ["f2602d16326b8f590e006a935e5d263b34a0ff43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068322 - Don't let a content process name an already-embedded tab as the new tab in CreateWindow. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nIn TryRemoteBrowserInternal, don't create a new BrowserHost is we're going to\nfail immediately anyways. This could result in failing to clean up properly.\n\nFor the two BrowserParent set methods, check in release builds that we are\neither clearing the field or the BrowserParent is not already in use.\n\nIn ContentParent::RecvCreateWindow, make sure that the child is handing us a\nfresh BrowserParent, or we can get into a weird state because things aren't\ncleaned up properly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324467\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsFrameLoader.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.h", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp"], "git_node": "53d9d849afbf54c683b6fe70d2f1373943dbf379", "git_parents": ["e693b8ca03b46d413f90cedca43b34ad3604a4cb"], "node": "4cd463b579c3ad8c1beb29741f096a3220a6a368", "parents": ["01b3a5a339c77dec255646a3e1add7e0fc0db8b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068322 - Wait to set BrowserParent::mBrowserBridgeParent. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDon't set BrowserParent::mBrowserBridgeParent until we've set the strong half of\nthe cycle, BrowserBridgeParent::mBrowserParent, in case we hit any failure states.\n\nBrowserParent::mBrowserBridgeParent is now only set alongside the strong\nBrowserBridgeParent::mBrowserParent reference, and the two are cleared together,\nso Destroy() can only ever be clearing its own back pointer. Assert that, so\nthis doesn't silently regress into clobbering another bridge's pointer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324468\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserBridgeParent.cpp"], "git_node": "81d0c99e0a6fa032bf7148a707da83f9859e721c", "git_parents": ["53d9d849afbf54c683b6fe70d2f1373943dbf379"], "node": "66c9a75fa7f505724a2c7c56afe90edc43799b53", "parents": ["4cd463b579c3ad8c1beb29741f096a3220a6a368"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068322 - Don't embed a discarded BrowsingContext from RecvCreateWindow. r=dom-core-reviewers,farre\n\nThis is like a semi-related cleanup found while working on the other patches.\n\nThe existing BrowsingContext validation checks the shape of the new tab's\nBrowsingContext but not whether it is still live, so a discarded one would be\nadopted as the new frameloader's pending BrowsingContext by CreateBrowsingContext\nin nsFrameLoader.cpp and then embedded.\n\nUnlike the other checks here this isn't necessarily the child's fault, so fail\nthe window open the way we already do for a missing parent rather than killing\nthe child.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324469\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp"], "git_node": "4920e3c2aa21c4e9f37c0150acfd1edc0d0d773f", "git_parents": ["81d0c99e0a6fa032bf7148a707da83f9859e721c"], "node": "854f7eb2b462e11db6ab1dffaeeb27359784ad8a", "parents": ["66c9a75fa7f505724a2c7c56afe90edc43799b53"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Vandolder \u003cavandolder@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072213 - Consider speculative loads on links changes. r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326223\n", "files": ["dom/base/SpeculationRules.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/document-rules.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "f8941394ea376f1d5471b37d72ce2fb82dcb44eb", "git_parents": ["4920e3c2aa21c4e9f37c0150acfd1edc0d0d773f"], "node": "1e2a447e8995b858be5d851ee38a40d5d1d5db09", "parents": ["854f7eb2b462e11db6ab1dffaeeb27359784ad8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Farre \u003cfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067973 - Validate PWebBrowserPersistDocument actor state in the parent process. r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324050\n", "files": ["dom/webbrowserpersist/WebBrowserPersistDocumentParent.cpp", "dom/webbrowserpersist/WebBrowserPersistDocumentParent.h", "dom/webbrowserpersist/WebBrowserPersistResourcesParent.cpp"], "git_node": "a9439dc36d18ccffec05634ad6185c879196c60c", "git_parents": ["f8941394ea376f1d5471b37d72ce2fb82dcb44eb"], "node": "97a5096c24f26e076da97c7f321a047a494de120", "parents": ["1e2a447e8995b858be5d851ee38a40d5d1d5db09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1949178 - Remove some needless includes of CrashReporterHost.h r=afranchuk,ipc-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,padenot,nika,crashreporting-reviewers\" for causing build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit 4645d8f8ea77bcde75f9088cd3cc57f9383d1f50.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1949178 - Re-enable capturing child process shutdown hangs r=afranchuk,ipc-reviewers,crashreporting-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 84af319863faf38918384b5adc2ba8fefd984ff8.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1949178 - Add support for generating minidumps via the crash helper client code r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 6b0d9f0d9077c99412b6979b36222a6b66e63fd2.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1949178 - Make the crash helper handle and respond to minidump generation messages r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit d41cfdc5f1403ea15cf25ebae6a6bff9a2ff2475.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1949178 - Add a wrapper function to generate a minidump on demand rather than via the exception handler r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7b72c47cc5e8cdd784180c9ec888cabf05a09f0d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1949178 - Fix type used for looking up auxiliary vector information r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 8b39d1c9d3285e52b63cd244f1166e11086c9321.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1949178 - Introduce an IPC message for minidump generation r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 1b29c30687f0d4d9ea00ade2fa6448b6a1b41ff6.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1949178 - Replace the ProcessReaderHandle type with a proper raw representation of the crash helper process handle abstract type r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 30102f22ffaa386378128a87ad28b40d6752a448.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1949178 - Introduce a platform-specific thread handle r=afranchuk\"\n\nThis reverts commit 885d10c2f554f02531a1c7d7a197d23fcf85ec29.\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RDDChild.cpp", "ipc/glue/CrashReporterHost.cpp", "ipc/glue/CrashReporterHost.h", "toolkit/crashreporter/breakpad_wrapper/breakpad_wrapper.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_client/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/breakpad/unix_strings.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/breakpad/windows_strings.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/messages.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/linux.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/mach.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/cbindgen.toml", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/breakpad_crash_generator.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/crash_generation/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/ipc_server.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/nsDummyExceptionHandler.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/nsExceptionHandler.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/nsExceptionHandler.h", "xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcher.h", "xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherLinux.cpp", "xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherMac.cpp"], "git_node": "902faee396f959ba55d331083dfb36dcda6d524b", "git_parents": ["a9439dc36d18ccffec05634ad6185c879196c60c"], "node": "8dc81294776ec863224b2779d1d4c22f26358ce2", "parents": ["97a5096c24f26e076da97c7f321a047a494de120"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeremy Swinarton \u003cjswinarton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041030: Part 1 - Update the default o