 "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/ui.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/ui.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "1ce29de90e0efb389a29e9bfc9e7dde1fcabd3c1", "git_parents": ["2a6dd3b42b38bcf1d854694e3d16c5ace8e96870"], "node": "b0e0205906d8caed2f21044b704d1a3231c2ed7c", "parents": ["37bdc1f33397acdc4bc4c400d14746d977bb6c14"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make -moz-box-align a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326659\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "0339bdc01ad7c52e7aecfeb4c93c547e60737193", "git_parents": ["1ce29de90e0efb389a29e9bfc9e7dde1fcabd3c1"], "node": "3cf64a44a690c2caa18e8dc6c312bde2500f3deb", "parents": ["b0e0205906d8caed2f21044b704d1a3231c2ed7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make -moz-box-direction a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326660\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "dfdb5de68c3a0c901789745ac60505c0663e769c", "git_parents": ["0339bdc01ad7c52e7aecfeb4c93c547e60737193"], "node": "dfb06794588427c9e1cce9a70b2186557916cd62", "parents": ["3cf64a44a690c2caa18e8dc6c312bde2500f3deb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make -moz-box-orient a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326662\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "702fcee8c3939d0b8a91ea3faec3870888f560b7", "git_parents": ["dfdb5de68c3a0c901789745ac60505c0663e769c"], "node": "accb8704215e7ea4f334399c616697236fece988", "parents": ["dfb06794588427c9e1cce9a70b2186557916cd62"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make -moz-box-pack a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326663\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "9c0c87c9561ef832fff1274bec0f47814f6ebb56", "git_parents": ["702fcee8c3939d0b8a91ea3faec3870888f560b7"], "node": "027c9e8023653f3beec299cc61ea9d539aa3e32f", "parents": ["accb8704215e7ea4f334399c616697236fece988"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make mix-blend-mode a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326664\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/effects.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/effects.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "b38129fbee12490a46d884eec2dabf81a46f6704", "git_parents": ["9c0c87c9561ef832fff1274bec0f47814f6ebb56"], "node": "a2f186c02920bd49fdc7fbf12390efda9bd000cf", "parents": ["027c9e8023653f3beec299cc61ea9d539aa3e32f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make math-style a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nThe presentation attribute mapping now goes through FromPrimitive like\nthe other keyword properties, since the value Gecko passes is the enum\nitself.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326665\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "196d211e5029f2d36575ee4283400e8182f3115c", "git_parents": ["b38129fbee12490a46d884eec2dabf81a46f6704"], "node": "a249548f5043eaa975ac58ca774a23262d2a1f9b", "parents": ["a2f186c02920bd49fdc7fbf12390efda9bd000cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make -moz-math-variant a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nThe presentation attribute mapping now goes through FromPrimitive like\nthe other keyword properties, since the value Gecko passes is the enum\nitself.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326666\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "fe4054ca6a7e1d428302d66d4fda6f471ad6fb87", "git_parents": ["196d211e5029f2d36575ee4283400e8182f3115c"], "node": "79400f5dca1b58295a8b53b9f589927c55928ccf", "parents": ["a249548f5043eaa975ac58ca774a23262d2a1f9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make font-variant-emoji a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in gfxFontConstants.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326667\n", "files": ["gfx/src/nsFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontConstants.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.h", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "32a851978305e61474aa3a599c5d7987febacc99", "git_parents": ["fe4054ca6a7e1d428302d66d4fda6f471ad6fb87"], "node": "fd9b0b709ee935080e9842bfa9d393971dd79018", "parents": ["79400f5dca1b58295a8b53b9f589927c55928ccf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make direction a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nThe Rust type is called DirectionProperty to avoid clashing with the\nexisting Direction types in logical_geometry and selector_parser (like\nWritingModeProperty), and is renamed back to StyleDirection for C++.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326668\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "6523b900ab938cf9ff3967679d99a4842a044519", "git_parents": ["32a851978305e61474aa3a599c5d7987febacc99"], "node": "06d860b67ba41257099f8236807808d5ce17d2a9", "parents": ["fd9b0b709ee935080e9842bfa9d393971dd79018"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make text-decoration-style a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nThe discriminants are kept as they were in C++ since they round-trip\nthrough the LookAndFeel underline style integers. The Sentinel alias is\nreplaced by Wavy, which is what it was.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326669\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsTextPaintStyle.cpp", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/text.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/text.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "0e68817bb781d74f32ef51a69ad5fda04a7623a5", "git_parents": ["6523b900ab938cf9ff3967679d99a4842a044519"], "node": "4746345bc6513ec449e25e0ff0b21f97e1e24c6c", "parents": ["06d860b67ba41257099f8236807808d5ce17d2a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make color-interpolation and color-interpolation-filters predefined types. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nBoth properties share the StyleColorInterpolation enum in Gecko, so\ndefine a single ColorInterpolation enum in Rust and export it through\ncbindgen instead of keeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h. The\nGecko style struct then stores the computed value type directly and the\nstyle struct getters can hand out references.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326670\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/svg.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/svg.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "2c2c06e040e077422054d5a3ec400485416f16dd", "git_parents": ["0e68817bb781d74f32ef51a69ad5fda04a7623a5"], "node": "9670a4074804a6657425c43f690de5b17288ab91", "parents": ["4746345bc6513ec449e25e0ff0b21f97e1e24c6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make font-optical-sizing a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen, and use it in\nnsFont instead of a uint8_t holding NS_FONT_* constants, so the Gecko\nstyle struct stores the computed value type directly and the style\nstruct getter can hand out a reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326671\n", "files": ["gfx/src/nsFont.cpp", "gfx/src/nsFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontConstants.h", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "26a3c27e28d6da4812652a626d00c0cb3785a5f0", "git_parents": ["2c2c06e040e077422054d5a3ec400485416f16dd"], "node": "1ba43ba45746db280e8f1447c52b9248324763aa", "parents": ["9670a4074804a6657425c43f690de5b17288ab91"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make font-kerning a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen, and use it in\nnsFont instead of a uint8_t holding NS_FONT_* constants, so the Gecko\nstyle struct stores the computed value type directly and the style\nstruct getter can hand out a reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326672\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "gfx/src/nsFont.cpp", "gfx/src/nsFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontConstants.h", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "6976aef4ba452236cd51b12f1bd794264e2641ba", "git_parents": ["26a3c27e28d6da4812652a626d00c0cb3785a5f0"], "node": "196f372f8f444c29523c6e8b51a0e702a2f53e0b", "parents": ["1ba43ba45746db280e8f1447c52b9248324763aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make -moz-osx-font-smoothing a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen, and use it in\nnsFont instead of a uint8_t holding NS_FONT_* constants, so the Gecko\nstyle struct stores the computed value type directly and the style\nstruct getter can hand out a reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326673\n", "files": ["gfx/src/nsFont.cpp", "gfx/src/nsFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontConstants.h", "layout/generic/TextOverflow.cpp", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.h", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "30fc9061a2c0328740266e9fc510868e8e2f1fd4", "git_parents": ["6976aef4ba452236cd51b12f1bd794264e2641ba"], "node": "07c88ea206752d5543733e15a49ca7e3e7ed5f08", "parents": ["196f372f8f444c29523c6e8b51a0e702a2f53e0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make font-variant-position a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen, and use it in\nnsFont instead of a uint8_t holding NS_FONT_* constants, so the Gecko\nstyle struct stores the computed value type directly and the style\nstruct getter can hand out a reference.\n\ngfxFontStyle::variantSubSuper becomes the enum too, so the constants go\naway entirely.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326674\n", "files": ["gfx/src/nsFont.cpp", "gfx/src/nsFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontConstants.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.cpp", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "e1de069b00cc9d19f7adaa5891c4fe3d45b0e1e8", "git_parents": ["30fc9061a2c0328740266e9fc510868e8e2f1fd4"], "node": "67f8c20113e07141aeddd4f0451b5b1ceb319e2d", "parents": ["07c88ea206752d5543733e15a49ca7e3e7ed5f08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make font-variant-caps a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen, and use it in\nnsFont instead of a uint8_t holding NS_FONT_* constants, so the Gecko\nstyle struct stores the computed value type directly and the style\nstruct getter can hand out a reference.\n\ngfxFontStyle::variantCaps becomes the enum too, so the constants go\naway entirely.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326675\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "gfx/src/nsFont.cpp", "gfx/src/nsFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontConstants.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxGraphiteShaper.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxHarfBuzzShaper.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.cpp", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "afbe05727e0381730130efeeceb1830941f433ce", "git_parents": ["e1de069b00cc9d19f7adaa5891c4fe3d45b0e1e8"], "node": "880cb43432a1659a1256b6787a024738dd59cc08", "parents": ["67f8c20113e07141aeddd4f0451b5b1ceb319e2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make white-space-collapse a predefined type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDefine the enum in Rust and export it through cbindgen instead of\nkeeping a hand-written copy in nsStyleConsts.h, so the Gecko style\nstruct stores the computed value type directly and the style struct\ngetter can hand out a reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326676\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsTextPaintStyle.cpp", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/text.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/text.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "7ef45017a9b49934ac1575e78f91028d76f1b52f", "git_parents": ["afbe05727e0381730130efeeceb1830941f433ce"], "node": "893e0c0d3952b4a2095f3a725e10f7106fe993c8", "parents": ["880cb43432a1659a1256b6787a024738dd59cc08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Remove the keyword conversion templates and use the borrowed getters for the migrated keywords. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nAll the single-keyword longhands that Gecko stores now use the computed\nvalue type, so impl_keyword and friends have no remaining users.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326677\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/logical_geometry.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/gecko.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/properties.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/style_adjuster.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs"], "git_node": "e585eb2cf6752e8339d5abc40fe600b7c2a4b9b1", "git_parents": ["7ef45017a9b49934ac1575e78f91028d76f1b52f"], "node": "43fba7824a6a22f355264d981e5610fcba37e15b", "parents": ["893e0c0d3952b4a2095f3a725e10f7106fe993c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make background-blend-mode use the Blend type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nGecko already stores it as StyleBlend, which is now the Rust Blend enum\nthat mix-blend-mode uses, so share the type instead of converting through\nan inexhaustive keyword match. This also makes background-blend-mode\naccept plus-lighter, which the compositing spec allows and which\nbackground-blend-mode-plus-lighter.html in WPT tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326678\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/compositing/background-blending/background-blend-mode-plus-lighter.html.ini"], "git_node": "f83dc0ac7f41fd9324a8e1c4badcf0aeb22c9cac", "git_parents": ["e585eb2cf6752e8339d5abc40fe600b7c2a4b9b1"], "node": "73a371a3a9640c9a165f3102ead082e3aba0fdf4", "parents": ["43fba7824a6a22f355264d981e5610fcba37e15b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make background-origin and mask-origin predefined types. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nAdd a BackgroundOrigin enum shared by both properties (like\nBackgroundClip), with background-origin rejecting the SVG boxes at parse\ntime, and store it in nsStyleImageLayers::Layer instead of the\nStyleGeometryBox superset. ComputeBoxValueForOrigin maps it to the\ngeometry box the painting code uses, so the MarginBox assertion is moot.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326679\n", "files": ["layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.cpp", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "layout/style/nsStyleStruct.cpp", "layout/style/nsStyleStruct.h", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/background.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/background.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "56da5ffe5167ed62ee6e7e654aaede9568b36e0b", "git_parents": ["f83dc0ac7f41fd9324a8e1c4badcf0aeb22c9cac"], "node": "a9f6534c1ea013d98ee62b39b48cb9a337a31b1f", "parents": ["73a371a3a9640c9a165f3102ead082e3aba0fdf4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Make -servo-top-layer use the TopLayer type. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nIt's the last single-keyword longhand. It is internal to Servo, so reuse\nthe -moz-top-layer enum (none / auto) rather than adding a separate one;\nServo layout can adapt downstream.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326680\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/properties.mako.rs"], "git_node": "c8c1e1fd0081763b07894de8bc4b46d071163dac", "git_parents": ["56da5ffe5167ed62ee6e7e654aaede9568b36e0b"], "node": "b6a6998f0dd31b0012a69746c6198d7729a39984", "parents": ["a9f6534c1ea013d98ee62b39b48cb9a337a31b1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Remove the single-keyword longhand machinery. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nEvery longhand now has a predefined type, so the Keyword class, the\nkeyword branch of the longhand template and the image layer keyword\nconversions have no users left.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326681\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/gecko.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/helpers.mako.rs"], "git_node": "19b2d639cb876803bf309a25c6284cdfd38bf0b3", "git_parents": ["c8c1e1fd0081763b07894de8bc4b46d071163dac"], "node": "a4ca562cfa0c7415b0e2d1bf778a6625c1d2270f", "parents": ["b6a6998f0dd31b0012a69746c6198d7729a39984"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Collapse the use statements for the new types into the existing ones. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326682\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/computed/background.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/border.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/column.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/list.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/position.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/svg.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/table.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/text.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/ui.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs"], "git_node": "0db6a7c5d492a6620050a2c4d3c5d3f86939b283", "git_parents": ["19b2d639cb876803bf309a25c6284cdfd38bf0b3"], "node": "65e4357c0d1f381a4a82a2916e6cbe8f10e96afa", "parents": ["a4ca562cfa0c7415b0e2d1bf778a6625c1d2270f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["t-linux.html", "t.html"], "git_node": "fb25824ffea9a9852d8c81139d5151eca2cad025", "git_parents": ["0db6a7c5d492a6620050a2c4d3c5d3f86939b283"], "node": "4113afefc42d39c6169ab9c6bdfac0707c370c61", "parents": ["65e4357c0d1f381a4a82a2916e6cbe8f10e96afa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-pl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-pl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-el/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ru/strings.xml"], "git_node": "6284d438cf352028d37dc090cd5708dbb1569143", "git_parents": ["fb25824ffea9a9852d8c81139d5151eca2cad025"], "node": "fc7a628ad6982f624deb46be3ca54cb9df86d1a9", "parents": ["4113afefc42d39c6169ab9c6bdfac0707c370c61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Remove accidentally added files.\n", "files": ["t-linux.html", "t.html"], "git_node": "58dba9430c6b1df55fa6bb41c3c855133b6fc7e1", "git_parents": ["6284d438cf352028d37dc090cd5708dbb1569143"], "node": "e494e86e0d5d6a25ea97e1df6f90b80882d08011", "parents": ["fc7a628ad6982f624deb46be3ca54cb9df86d1a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072049 - Add snappy to the vendor-verify algorithms group. r?#taskgraph-reviewers DONTBUILD\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/vendor-verify.yml"], "git_node": "5edfc5475c9a622805241a21f938075174b56872", "git_parents": ["58dba9430c6b1df55fa6bb41c3c855133b6fc7e1"], "node": "dc1456c9e32b4cffa066cc2dcfb900aa08c151b7", "parents": ["e494e86e0d5d6a25ea97e1df6f90b80882d08011"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063192 - Refactor SetDeferredPurge a little r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318379\n", "files": ["memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "f4514162c7abc44ff198080d6f3595de29198a8f", "git_parents": ["5edfc5475c9a622805241a21f938075174b56872"], "node": "7cf584371495620ac32502ad3787596263956a3d", "parents": ["dc1456c9e32b4cffa066cc2dcfb900aa08c151b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2066486 - Added text under Wayback Button r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,parker,jdelorenzo\" for causing fenix ui failures\n\nThis reverts commit ac6a76590fd15fefda57a7eebaeb501dc863992a.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/README.md", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/errorpages/ErrorPages.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/errorpages/ErrorPagesTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/WaybackMachineErrorPageTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/assets/lowMediumErrorPages.js", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/assets/low_and_medium_risk_error_pages.html", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/assets/low_and_medium_risk_error_style.css"], "git_node": "e6dda8b814919195bcab883a26c2d8a42b789097", "git_parents": ["f4514162c7abc44ff198080d6f3595de29198a8f"], "node": "40a484417eac7d56fb82d5e7dd3a333a1218331b", "parents": ["7cf584371495620ac32502ad3787596263956a3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2068782 - Add base styling for AITab components - r=jlewis\" for causing bc failures @ browser_parsable_css.js\n\nThis reverts commit e25c942383d5e8a935557032ca569136eecbe90f.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-base.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-header/aitab-header.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-header/aitab-header.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-header/aitab-header.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-page-actions/aitab-page-actions.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-page.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-shared.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/aitab.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn"], "git_node": "133027851a3ae9909cd72520a1831004076e7a7c", "git_parents": ["e6dda8b814919195bcab883a26c2d8a42b789097"], "node": "4f56e2d9245e9bdd3776b5ea64a3a30421d7aecd", "parents": ["40a484417eac7d56fb82d5e7dd3a333a1218331b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072642 - Force-enable tab sharing pref in getUserMedia source telemetry test r=webrtc-reviewers,ng\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326762\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_getUserMedia_sourceGrantedGlean_displayCapture.html"], "git_node": "51a93e67c5586d9ed31f459f9623e95fe50407a0", "git_parents": ["133027851a3ae9909cd72520a1831004076e7a7c"], "node": "310e65899a58232d78d4deb187dab192ff3198f0", "parents": ["4f56e2d9245e9bdd3776b5ea64a3a30421d7aecd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059195 - Track each pipeline's embedder LayersId in CompositorBridgeParent::LayerTreeState. r=gfx-reviewers,aosmond\n\nExtend NotifyChildCreated, MapAndNotifyChildCreated, and NotifyChildRecreated\nto carry the LayersId of the pipeline that embeds the newly (re)created one,\nand record it on LayerTreeState as mEmbedderLayersId. It is derived in\nRemoteLayerTreeOwner::Initialize(), once the embedding widget's WindowRenderer\nexists: from the embedding document's BrowserParent for a nested remote frame,\nand from the hosting chrome window's widget otherwise.\n\nAlso extend AdoptChild to carry a freshly-recomputed embedder id, rather than\npreserving whatever was previously recorded: adopting a child under a new\nCompositorBridgeParent can mean a tab was moved to a different top-level\nwindow, which does change who embeds it, so the old value would otherwise go\nstale.\n\nThis establishes a parent-process-trusted ground truth for which LayersId\nembeds which, to be used by a follow-up change to validate scroll-data\nreferent claims from content.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316408\n", "files": ["gfx/ipc/GPUProcessManager.cpp", "gfx/ipc/GPUProcessManager.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeChild.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/ContentCompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/ContentCompositorBridgeParent.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/PCompositorBridge.ipdl", "layout/ipc/RemoteLayerTreeOwner.cpp"], "git_node": "fa31398de650fe5d1e8de80b192ed967b290c253", "git_parents": ["51a93e67c5586d9ed31f459f9623e95fe50407a0"], "node": "03ce7f1b42aa4229c1e054fb2be4797572c09f2c", "parents": ["310e65899a58232d78d4deb187dab192ff3198f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059195 - Clear WebRenderScrollData referent ids that the sender doesn't actually embed. r=botond\n\nValidate every referent claim in WebRenderBridgeParent::ProcessDisplayListData\nagainst the parent process's own record of the frame tree (LayerTreeState's\nnew mEmbedderLayersId), and clear the claims it doesn't confirm.\n\nClearing rather than dropping the transaction, because a referent can\nlegitimately be gone by the time the claim is validated: DeallocateLayerTreeId\nerases the entry via a dispatched runnable while the embedder still has a\ntransaction in flight naming it.\n\nSkip the check for a root WebRenderBridgeParent, whose transactions come from\nthe parent process rather than from content. After the GPU process restarts\neach layer tree re-registers independently, driven from its own content\nprocess, while the root pipeline repaints straight away, so a root can name\nreferents that have no LayerTreeState yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316409\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderBridgeParent.h", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderScrollData.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderScrollData.h"], "git_node": "a4cb3dee073a247dede97340f5be4b513202a33f", "git_parents": ["fa31398de650fe5d1e8de80b192ed967b290c253"], "node": "f06e51c6361bd7b5e7d88f02544f171c9e1b8030", "parents": ["03ce7f1b42aa4229c1e054fb2be4797572c09f2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072488 - Fix C++ representation of computed colors. r=sajidanwar\n\nThis patch makes the C++ representation of computed colors, which\ncurrently involves a specified calc node, correct.\n\nThis is mostly a band-aid fix, there are two issues that are worth\nfixing here:\n\n * Now that we have computed calc nodes, it probably makes sense to use\n   those properly for colors, even if a bit of a pain.\n\n * RandomKey stores a specified::Number but the C++ code only knows\n   about computed::Number. This all kinda works out because RandomKey is\n   boxed and shouldn't get to computed nodes anyway, but might go away\n   or move soon enough, see bug 2071971.\n\n * I made the GenericPercentageLeaf less generic because it made things\n   complicated for no good reason.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326798\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/ServoStyleConstsForwards.h", "servo/components/style/color/component.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/calc.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/length_percentage.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/percentage.rs", "servo/components/style/values/generics/calc.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/calc.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/percentage.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/random.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/crashtests/firefox-bug-2072488.html"], "git_node": "3a8485990c8bd5b93ac2f37976222203f812f595", "git_parents": ["a4cb3dee073a247dede97340f5be4b513202a33f"], "node": "db1969f29a5447afed8ec12c5b9cc7859068c66e", "parents": ["f06e51c6361bd7b5e7d88f02544f171c9e1b8030"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072718 - Update property_database now that background-blend-mode accepts plus-lighter.\n", "files": ["layout/style/test/property_database.js"], "git_node": "44f62c04bcc4044fbc1d1a57a66701aade332312", "git_parents": ["3a8485990c8bd5b93ac2f37976222203f812f595"], "node": "e9b5fe0761a2136ff588042faecb26c2a3259ded", "parents": ["db1969f29a5447afed8ec12c5b9cc7859068c66e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072582 - pressKey should wait for Editable changes. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nSome tests in `TextInputDelegateTest` are failing because `pressKey`\ndoes not wait for the Editable to be updated.\n\nSo we should wait for the selection of Editable to be updated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326428\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/TextInputDelegateTest.kt"], "git_node": "442d0aed9a364a9d4f3e64be0da0acee92bec9ec", "git_parents": ["44f62c04bcc4044fbc1d1a57a66701aade332312"], "node": "3e5a4fb21f22b95fe7f727ef426aa5dc1a50cd51", "parents": ["e9b5fe0761a2136ff588042faecb26c2a3259ded"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072504 - Don't offer Open in New Tab/Window items for switch-to-tab suggestions r=adw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326396\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_urlbar_contextmenu.js"], "git_node": "9dd0b20d7febdbc9351396d86320a9c610ba1728", "git_parents": ["442d0aed9a364a9d4f3e64be0da0acee92bec9ec"], "node": "405c3962a31dbc7b9308403d3e9a5ce794d8bb43", "parents": ["3e5a4fb21f22b95fe7f727ef426aa5dc1a50cd51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 1: Unify the hint charset handling between the script preload and regular script load. r=bthrall,dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nStore the hint charset attribute into the ScriptLoadRequest field, both for the\npreload and the regular load, so that the remaining part of the preload and\nthe cache handling doesn't have to distinguish between them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324186\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.h", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.cpp", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.h", "dom/workers/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/loader/ModuleLoadRequest.cpp", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.cpp", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/script-charset-03.html.ini"], "git_node": "60fdbe2fa9cf2204e3a1dcf5d1d8cdb61cf0c5dd", "git_parents": ["9dd0b20d7febdbc9351396d86320a9c610ba1728"], "node": "1e5a00622b2369f2ba66cf3c6007342f05dcce07", "parents": ["405c3962a31dbc7b9308403d3e9a5ce794d8bb43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 2: Include the hint charset into the cache key string for the ChromeUtils.getCachedJavaScriptSource. r=bthrall,devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314577\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/network-monitor/network-event-actor.js", "devtools/server/actors/resources/network-events-content.js", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.cpp", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.h", "dom/chrome-webidl/ChromeUtils.webidl", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.cpp", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.h", "remote/shared/NetworkResponse.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "5654b1cdee7dfab47520c67bf892cbe3506ea863", "git_parents": ["60fdbe2fa9cf2204e3a1dcf5d1d8cdb61cf0c5dd"], "node": "c20f8503786e4eda7d7841c02166c1964c847c80", "parents": ["1e5a00622b2369f2ba66cf3c6007342f05dcce07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 3: Move the alignment handling out of LoadedScript methods and clarify the input/output. r=bthrall\n\nThe later patch will put an extra section between the SRI+padding and the\nserialized stencil.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324187\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/loader/LoadedScript.h"], "git_node": "b2b60ca23a668c5ad0051754c6951c0a5f0c3435", "git_parents": ["5654b1cdee7dfab47520c67bf892cbe3506ea863"], "node": "80f42f93a973c6964da89399a4f503d0832940ee", "parents": ["c20f8503786e4eda7d7841c02166c1964c847c80"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 4: Add ScriptLoader::GetClassicScriptFallbackEncoding. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324188\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.h"], "git_node": "b710491e0c0e30eed5168af325568221aaa4ac92", "git_parents": ["b2b60ca23a668c5ad0051754c6951c0a5f0c3435"], "node": "e29a47fe2b7409aadf82b684946056ae0671c963", "parents": ["80f42f93a973c6964da89399a4f503d0832940ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 5: Put the encoding into the serialized stencil. r=bthrall\n\nThe encoding becomes a part of the cached value.\nWhen encoding doesn't match, the cache is treated in the same way as corrupted,\nand the load restarted, bypassing the cache.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324189\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.h", "js/loader/LoadedScript.h"], "git_node": "a7b908d4edac3cb5f22a6fa723a94e9cc507b244", "git_parents": ["b710491e0c0e30eed5168af325568221aaa4ac92"], "node": "c50c6d18e7091390f210cee7a0f8bc63273b7c03", "parents": ["e29a47fe2b7409aadf82b684946056ae0671c963"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 6: Use the encoding when looking up the in-memory script cache. r=bthrall\n\nCompare the hint encoding also for the in-memory cache, but only when the\nhint encoding was actually used.\n\nFor script preloads, the document's encoding may not have been settled yet,\nand in that case, the check is performed in the OnDelayedReady.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324190\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.h", "js/loader/LoadedScript.cpp", "js/loader/LoadedScript.h", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.cpp", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.h"], "git_node": "e8fb8428b6e6e93c1fc0d47f9535f6151bcb94ca", "git_parents": ["a7b908d4edac3cb5f22a6fa723a94e9cc507b244"], "node": "ca028c1e7e9baf04fc34759763a86d1eb341eb9c", "parents": ["c50c6d18e7091390f210cee7a0f8bc63273b7c03"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 7: Add tests. r=bthrall,perftest-reviewers,sparky\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314581\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/browser.toml", "dom/base/test/browser_script_loader_js_cache_charset.js", "dom/base/test/file_js_cache_charset_html.sjs", "dom/base/test/file_js_cache_charset_js.sjs", "dom/base/test/head.js"], "git_node": "6c4485450b59aa8691546e7d5c0125474eaedaa7", "git_parents": ["e8fb8428b6e6e93c1fc0d47f9535f6151bcb94ca"], "node": "d1c9348468d9fda935d1631455395990d82b02f2", "parents": ["ca028c1e7e9baf04fc34759763a86d1eb341eb9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["js/loader/LoadedScript.h", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.cpp"], "git_node": "5d7fa88ccd6cbbaa06e714c4bf53b03b555c728a", "git_parents": ["6c4485450b59aa8691546e7d5c0125474eaedaa7"], "node": "953941ff9db7f269b5f6941ce243240c8d23dced", "parents": ["d1c9348468d9fda935d1631455395990d82b02f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069579 - Allocate the extent node before locking in Recycle r=glandium\n\nRecycle() released then re-locked mMutex to call BaseAlloc::alloc() in\nmid operation in order to prevent a deadlock.  However if the allocation\nfailed it would leak the original node.\n\nAllocate the node up front instead (TryRecord() already does this for\nthe same reason) and hold the lock over the whole tree manipulation.  If\nthe allocation fails the operation is aborted before the split begins.\n\nThe node describing the recycled range is released through a\nUniqueBaseNode so it is freed after the lock is dropped, as before.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323830\n", "files": ["memory/build/Chunk.cpp"], "git_node": "a5d459e471f2b7fb337bb3b2029bd9de48eaeb36", "git_parents": ["5d7fa88ccd6cbbaa06e714c4bf53b03b555c728a"], "node": "ef85b0ddade0e6f0c7ed9694a097c0a5509942c6", "parents": ["953941ff9db7f269b5f6941ce243240c8d23dced"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069579 - Use more snake_case for local variables r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326081\n", "files": ["memory/build/Chunk.cpp"], "git_node": "18c2795d63a4e74b2e03841d38c6cfb2374b3674", "git_parents": ["a5d459e471f2b7fb337bb3b2029bd9de48eaeb36"], "node": "66e91649cd2614765f1a8b0d19e9c6b5c33ea6c5", "parents": ["ef85b0ddade0e6f0c7ed9694a097c0a5509942c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070083 - logalloc-replay can read input from a file r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324820\n", "files": ["memory/replace/logalloc/replay/Replay.cpp"], "git_node": "33a0a7c840d648d65ccf415ddd032c67a60fc453", "git_parents": ["18c2795d63a4e74b2e03841d38c6cfb2374b3674"], "node": "4c6aca28e4b31c9d41d81ed520ee0c2c9dc14885", "parents": ["66e91649cd2614765f1a8b0d19e9c6b5c33ea6c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072465. Remove the unused ImgDecoder threads in the profiler UI and add the new JxlDecode threads. r=profiler-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,canova,bolsson\n\nImage decoding has been running on the TaskController thread pool since bug 1672597 in 2020, so no thread named ImgDecoder is ever created.\n\nJPEG XL decoding gained a pool of its own recently (in bug 2065753), named JxlDecode, so add that.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326354\n", "files": ["devtools/client/locales/en-US/perftools.ftl", "devtools/client/performance-new/components/aboutprofiling/Settings.js"], "git_node": "93ee1b50ca3e9489fcf1443a4d86a70e06ae8b07", "git_parents": ["33a0a7c840d648d65ccf415ddd032c67a60fc453"], "node": "cbe25f45c5ccf764de79ed360be895e64b34b8c5", "parents": ["4c6aca28e4b31c9d41d81ed520ee0c2c9dc14885"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072468. Record the image decoding threads in the profiler graphics preset. r=profiler-reviewers,gfx-reviewers,android-reviewers,lsalzman,canova,tcampbell\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326355\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/performance-new/prefs-presets.sys.mjs", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/perf/ProfilerUtils.kt"], "git_node": "8ede1dc1e8a1b344dc14928625012f17c989d880", "git_parents": ["93ee1b50ca3e9489fcf1443a4d86a70e06ae8b07"], "node": "6d733ec1501c0efbe45935294c36b400b1496d90", "parents": ["cbe25f45c5ccf764de79ed360be895e64b34b8c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2072488 - Fix C++ representation of computed colors. r=sajidanwar\" for causing wpt failures\n\nThis reverts commit 3a8485990c8bd5b93ac2f37976222203f812f595.\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/ServoStyleConstsForwards.h", "servo/components/style/color/component.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/calc.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/length_percentage.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/percentage.rs", "servo/components/style/values/generics/calc.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/calc.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/percentage.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/random.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/crashtests/firefox-bug-2072488.html"], "git_node": "876bb5ec7153a2a8e78492a10cc224ce1baba9d7", "git_parents": ["8ede1dc1e8a1b344dc14928625012f17c989d880"], "node": "e769eaf1bad3fe4a87d5226a16e5a7bc66a1b9e4", "parents": ["6d733ec1501c0efbe45935294c36b400b1496d90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054243: Clear stale shared locks when EnsureTemporaryFileId fails. r=dom-storage-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313490\n", "files": ["dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemDataManager.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/fs/FileSystemFileHandle-cross-primitive-locking.https.tentative.worker.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fs/FileSystemWritableFileStream.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "056251234749ca175666b002ea3e2e982223ca23", "git_parents": ["876bb5ec7153a2a8e78492a10cc224ce1baba9d7"], "node": "177558a57693042ad2638e2a673501f25942c08e", "parents": ["e769eaf1bad3fe4a87d5226a16e5a7bc66a1b9e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ayoub hedri \u003cahedri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069931 - Created a binding for document.permissionsPolicy and iframe.permissionsPolicy and added tests r=webidl,smaug,simonf\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325086\n", "files": ["dom/security/permissionspolicy/test/mochitest/test_featureList.html", "dom/webidl/Document.webidl", "dom/webidl/HTMLIFrameElement.webidl"], "git_node": "8b5b57fc78ade8e1223435cd7525af2f1edeee20", "git_parents": ["056251234749ca175666b002ea3e2e982223ca23"], "node": "3bd46fb41b81664a25bb26eceb2ba948541ccfaf", "parents": ["177558a57693042ad2638e2a673501f25942c08e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ayoub hedri \u003cahedri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069931 - Enabling prefs for Permissions-Policy WPTs and updating expectations r=simonf\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326423\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/historical.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/idlharness.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/payment-supported-by-permissions-policy.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-frame-policy-allowed-for-all.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-frame-policy-allowed-for-self.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-frame-policy-allowed-for-some-override.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-frame-policy-allowed-for-some.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-frame-policy-disallowed-for-all.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-header-policy-allowed-for-all.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-header-policy-allowed-for-malformed-wildcard.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-header-policy-allowed-for-self.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-header-policy-allowed-for-some.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-header-policy-allowed-for-wildcard.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-header-policy-declined.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-header-policy-disallowed-for-all.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-nested-header-policy-allowed-for-all.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-nested-header-policy-allowed-for-self.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-nested-header-policy-disallowed-for-all.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/picture-in-picture-disabled-by-permissions-policy.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/picture-in-picture-supported-by-permissions-policy.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/camera-reporting.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/encrypted-media-reporting.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/fullscreen-reporting.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/geolocation-reporting.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/microphone-reporting.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/midi-reporting.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/picture-in-picture-reporting.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/report-only-and-enforce.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/report-to-multiple-endpoints.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/report-to-single-endpoint.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/screen-wake-lock-reporting.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/reporting/serial-reporting.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "11aa160e3c62c8179e956363706f6e6bb4cc6fb4", "git_parents": ["8b5b57fc78ade8e1223435cd7525af2f1edeee20"], "node": "68c93cb188b1ebb9d84200e0786611538bac42c9", "parents": ["3bd46fb41b81664a25bb26eceb2ba948541ccfaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Farrell \u003cmicolous+git@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068826 - Try calling `rustup` for `rustup which {name}`, and actually fall back to using `PROG` r=ahochheiden\n\nHomebrew `rustup` 1.29.0_1 replaced Rust tool symlinks with\n`write_env_script` wrappers, which don't pass `argv[0]`.\n\nFirefox's build scripts depended on being able to call `cargo` and `rustc`\nwith `argv[0] == \"rustup\"`, and (contrary to code comments) *wouldn't* fall\nback to using the original binary (due to no `onerror` parameter).\n\nThis change makes it so that if calling `cargo` and `rustc` as `rustup`\nfails, fall back to looking for an adjacent `rustup` binary and call that\ninstead.  If calling an adjacent `rustup` binary also fails, then use the\noriginal binary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323147\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/rust.configure"], "git_node": "9a0ddbf5250116b5c7dc66784a56ff5fbbeefbc0", "git_parents": ["11aa160e3c62c8179e956363706f6e6bb4cc6fb4"], "node": "846e1bc520abc31fe93f86ca68e2bfccee597d55", "parents": ["68c93cb188b1ebb9d84200e0786611538bac42c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1865078 part 1 - Remove unused Zone::maybeDiscardJitCode. r=jonco\n\nUnused since bug 1934108.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326157\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Zone.cpp", "js/src/gc/Zone.h"], "git_node": "92f8371237f0175b15cf4d1dad9525c73a5e76f3", "git_parents": ["9a0ddbf5250116b5c7dc66784a56ff5fbbeefbc0"], "node": "1535436c28e0251c6a10e725feff1722a4f9f32e", "parents": ["846e1bc520abc31fe93f86ca68e2bfccee597d55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1865078 part 2 - Move CacheIRStubKey to a new jit/CacheIRStubKey.h header. r=iain\n\nThis avoids an include cycle with the `Realm`/`JitRealm`/`JitZone` changes in later patches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326158\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CacheIRStubKey.h", "js/src/jit/JitZone.h"], "git_node": "561692b7945d86e5b8d69ff6431f2ba73c6ee4bf", "git_parents": ["92f8371237f0175b15cf4d1dad9525c73a5e76f3"], "node": "2aa8e408bd0c12fb9055918e024c94bf991f61f7", "parents": ["1535436c28e0251c6a10e725feff1722a4f9f32e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1865078 part 3 - Add a JitRealm class. r=iain\n\nLater patches will make more JIT state per-realm, so this adds a `JitRealm` class\nthat currently contains just the Baseline compile queue.\n\nUnlike `JitZone`, `JitRealm` is stored by value inside `Realm`. This is simpler\nand avoids an extra load in JIT code for the compile queue.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326159\n", "files": ["js/src/frontend/Stencil.cpp", "js/src/gc/Zone.cpp", "js/src/jit/BaselineJIT.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitRealm.h", "js/src/jit/JitScript.h", "js/src/vm/JSScript.cpp", "js/src/vm/Realm.cpp", "js/src/vm/Realm.h"], "git_node": "5fb49ad1e97b9e9e506c930dec066b8b6158bf51", "git_parents": ["561692b7945d86e5b8d69ff6431f2ba73c6ee4bf"], "node": "cf92f990eab35e22948d56ae80aefd6b1c97fe19", "parents": ["2aa8e408bd0c12fb9055918e024c94bf991f61f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1865078 part 4 - Move the CacheIR LifoAlloc from JitZone to JitRealm. r=iain\n\nThis lets us later discard scripts per realm instead of zone.\n\nFor `MarkActiveICScriptsAndCopyStubs`, instead of cloning into a new LifoAlloc\npassed as argument (`newStubSpace`), we now empty the LifoAllocs before the call\n(by moving the chunks out) and then use the realm's allocator for the cloned stub.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326160\n", "files": ["js/public/MemoryMetrics.h", "js/src/gc/Zone.cpp", "js/src/gc/Zone.h", "js/src/jit/BaselineCacheIRCompiler.cpp", "js/src/jit/ICStubSpace.h", "js/src/jit/Ion.cpp", "js/src/jit/IonCacheIRCompiler.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitRealm.h", "js/src/jit/JitScript.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitScript.h", "js/src/jit/JitZone.h", "js/src/vm/MemoryMetrics.cpp", "js/src/vm/Realm.cpp", "js/src/vm/Realm.h", "js/xpconnect/src/XPCJSRuntime.cpp"], "git_node": "eecc8303dbfbdd5dc3db4a51cc8d1f0504d79041", "git_parents": ["5fb49ad1e97b9e9e506c930dec066b8b6158bf51"], "node": "6ff8debf4e6afa6ae509b550f1ef0a9df7872855", "parents": ["cf92f990eab35e22948d56ae80aefd6b1c97fe19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1865078 part 5 - Move IonCacheIRStubInfoSet from JitZone to JitRealm. r=iain\n\nThe Baseline map (`BaselineCacheIRStubCodeMap`) continues to live in `JitZone` because\nentries are discarded automatically by the GC when the stub code is dead, and we want\nto still share Baseline stub code across all realms in a zone.\n\nFor Ion ICs we use a Set only to de-duplicate and manage allocated `CacheIRStubInfo`s.\nThis Set is purged after we discard IC code, so it should live in `JitRealm` now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326161\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Zone.cpp", "js/src/jit/Ion.cpp", "js/src/jit/IonCacheIRCompiler.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitRealm.h", "js/src/jit/JitZone.h"], "git_node": "de7e3e8cf6e4814e5e5833be3d6a4ed217cc7eb8", "git_parents": ["eecc8303dbfbdd5dc3db4a51cc8d1f0504d79041"], "node": "ea49fb1d0fba4c97bb9fb4d1f7168537e5b4418e", "parents": ["6ff8debf4e6afa6ae509b550f1ef0a9df7872855"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1865078 part 6 - Move lastDiscardedCodeTime_ and gcPreserveCode_ from Zone to JitRealm. r=iain,jonco\n\nThe flag no longer has to be cleared at the start of each GC because `endPreparePhase`\nassigns it for each realm.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326162\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Compacting.cpp", "js/src/gc/GC.cpp", "js/src/gc/Zone.cpp", "js/src/gc/Zone.h", "js/src/jit/JitRealm.h"], "git_node": "2ea7b98bd9116c6296d3ec3c03bc2a1acc62f4db", "git_parents": ["de7e3e8cf6e4814e5e5833be3d6a4ed217cc7eb8"], "node": "ea821ab06d5f33d402dcfdced0614d5239adb165", "parents": ["ea49fb1d0fba4c97bb9fb4d1f7168537e5b4418e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1865078 part 7 - Let the caller of InvalidateActivation decide which scripts to invalidate. r=iain\n\nThe lambda in `InvalidateAll` just returns true now, but later we can check the\nscript's realm there.\n\nTo avoid code bloat from the new template argument, the invalidate-frame code was\nmoved to a separate `InvalidateFrame` function.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326163\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/Ion.cpp"], "git_node": "4d7edbcabc03302b3a2d6faa38da4ff9b6624cd1", "git_parents": ["2ea7b98bd9116c6296d3ec3c03bc2a1acc62f4db"], "node": "1e1861550b10007606acd70e71295a612dd7d373", "parents": ["ea821ab06d5f33d402dcfdced0614d5239adb165"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1865078 part 8 - Discard JIT code per realm instead of per zone. r=iain,jonco\n\n`GCRuntime::maybeDiscardJitCodeForGC` is now the only place where the JitRealm's\npreserve-code flags are set, because we clear the flags after discarding JIT code.\nWe assert the flags are cleared in `Zone::discardJitCodeForAllRealms`.\n\nOnly for realms that are not preserving code, we now invalidate scripts, mark\nscripts as active, or purge the IC stub LifoAlloc.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326164\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/GC.cpp", "js/src/gc/GCAPI.cpp", "js/src/gc/GCRuntime.h", "js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/gc/Zone.cpp", "js/src/gc/Zone.h", "js/src/irregexp/RegExpNativeMacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit/Invalidation.h", "js/src/jit/Ion.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitScript.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitScript.h", "js/src/jit/TrialInlining.cpp"], "git_node": "7c6afa24c432f411d98637e3efe08796bdb61a1e", "git_parents": ["4d7edbcabc03302b3a2d6faa38da4ff9b6624cd1"], "node": "6c0810ccd45c50166d0410d20ad8f0cd278183d9", "parents": ["1e1861550b10007606acd70e71295a612dd7d373"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1865078 part 9 - Replace active-compartment check with a realm-specific check. r=iain,jonco\n\nWe were still preserving code for all realms in the 'active' compartment. We can\nnow replace this with a realm-specific check. Workloads like Speedometer 3 have\nmany realms in a single compartment.\n\nCombined with part 8 this reduces peak IC stub LifoAlloc memory in the content\nprocess from \u003e 30 MB to less than 1 MB on a Speedometer 3 run. It also reduces\nMajorGC time by 10-20% on that benchmark. It doesn't seem to affect the score\nbecause it's outside measured time, but it's still an improvement.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326165\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/GC.cpp", "js/src/gc/GCRuntime.h", "js/src/gc/Zone.cpp", "js/src/gc/Zone.h"], "git_node": "3b73208458f4b9a6929e77865f0eda5113fdbb21", "git_parents": ["7c6afa24c432f411d98637e3efe08796bdb61a1e"], "node": "ba1d64eb950e68a3fe2c5e57c6e6fbcf38edeea4", "parents": ["6c0810ccd45c50166d0410d20ad8f0cd278183d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2056134: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing wpt failures in child-src-worker-allowed.sub.html.\n\nThis reverts commit 5d7fa88ccd6cbbaa06e714c4bf53b03b555c728a.\n\nThis reverts commit 6c4485450b59aa8691546e7d5c0125474eaedaa7.\n\nThis reverts commit e8fb8428b6e6e93c1fc0d47f9535f6151bcb94ca.\n\nThis reverts commit a7b908d4edac3cb5f22a6fa723a94e9cc507b244.\n\nThis reverts commit b710491e0c0e30eed5168af325568221aaa4ac92.\n\nThis reverts commit b2b60ca23a668c5ad0051754c6951c0a5f0c3435.\n\nThis reverts commit 5654b1cdee7dfab47520c67bf892cbe3506ea863.\n\nThis reverts commit 60fdbe2fa9cf2204e3a1dcf5d1d8cdb61cf0c5dd.\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/network-monitor/network-event-actor.js", "devtools/server/actors/resources/network-events-content.js", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.cpp", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.h", "dom/base/test/browser.toml", "dom/base/test/browser_script_loader_js_cache_charset.js", "dom/base/test/file_js_cache_charset_html.sjs", "dom/base/test/file_js_cache_charset_js.sjs", "dom/base/test/head.js", "dom/chrome-webidl/ChromeUtils.webidl", "dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.h", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.cpp", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.h", "dom/workers/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/loader/LoadedScript.cpp", "js/loader/LoadedScript.h", "js/loader/ModuleLoadRequest.cpp", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.cpp", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.h", "remote/shared/NetworkResponse.sys.mjs", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/script-charset-03.html.ini"], "git_node": "b5572f5cae174a1d3da7fa23b0048806fb2981e7", "git_parents": ["3b73208458f4b9a6929e77865f0eda5113fdbb21"], "node": "bc106720fcca90621aab2dab56bfbce5d7e2a843", "parents": ["ba1d64eb950e68a3fe2c5e57c6e6fbcf38edeea4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069931 - Enabling prefs for Permissions-Policy WPTs and updating expectations r=simonf\" for causing wpt failures in encrypted-media-supported-by-permissions-policy.tentative.html.\n\nThis reverts commit 11aa160e3c62c8179e956363706f6e6bb4cc6fb4.\n\nThis reverts commit 8b5b57fc78ade8e1223435cd7525af2f1edeee20.\n", "files": ["dom/security/permissionspolicy/test/mochitest/test_featureList.html", "dom/webidl/Document.webidl", "dom/webidl/HTMLIFrameElement.webidl", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/historical.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/idlharness.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/payment-supported-by-permissions-policy.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-frame-policy-allowed-for-all.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-frame-policy-allowed-for-self.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-frame-policy-allowed-for-some-override.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-frame-policy-allowed-for-some.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-frame-policy-disallowed-for-all.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-header-policy-allowed-for-all.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-header-policy-allowed-for-malformed-wildcard.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-header-policy-allowed-for-self.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/permissions-policy-heade