2062651 - Remove dead PanelUI-fxa-menu-setup-sync-container from the account panel r=nsharpley,desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323174\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/browser-sync.js", "browser/base/content/test/sync/browser_sync.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/appmenu.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css"], "git_node": "c8712790787ddccb848c471940d316a098a30c5b", "git_parents": ["d9cb96ad432248c74082393af8ad367cbbfa458c"], "node": "9afcfdfed9d3fee15548588839b2b8e673c3529e", "parents": ["b7c34c0358926fb19aeb5ed8b1ba655790de05c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yubin Jamora \u003cyjamora@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072378 - Support adding url without putting https:// r=tetchart,ngrato,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326687\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-item/agent-monitor-item.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_item.js", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl"], "git_node": "960fa9d764e560ab984aba6194d10b9891ab1122", "git_parents": ["c8712790787ddccb848c471940d316a098a30c5b"], "node": "b183b6e6c8585bdc633437c31265370ff3bb7dea", "parents": ["9afcfdfed9d3fee15548588839b2b8e673c3529e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061155 - Reserve block-end padding on New Tab Customize menu to prevent footer from overlapping controls. r=thecount\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326734\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/_CustomizeMenu.scss"], "git_node": "db749c7c3b4533da173e5c1eb900a6d6dff5c507", "git_parents": ["960fa9d764e560ab984aba6194d10b9891ab1122"], "node": "393d9b63f28ad3b30ab38e7f4898d6336b7c57ac", "parents": ["b183b6e6c8585bdc633437c31265370ff3bb7dea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1954806 - Test that NV12 conversion accepts the sources I420 conversion does r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nRun every source layout through both outputs as is, scaled down and scaled\nup, and the matrix and fourth-byte checks through NV12 for all four 32-bit\nRGB formats. Also check that NV12 refuses RGB565, that both outputs reject\nstrides shorter than a row, and that a downscaled NV12 source keeps its\nchroma rows in NV12 output too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325186\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestImageConversion.cpp"], "git_node": "7d65e7153ab82e8b61605f229d8c8a271d86faa7", "git_parents": ["db749c7c3b4533da173e5c1eb900a6d6dff5c507"], "node": "ad684d531739d4da57bb2fdc851e6f858985c3e3", "parents": ["393d9b63f28ad3b30ab38e7f4898d6336b7c57ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1954806 - Share the conversion pipeline between the I420 and NV12 outputs r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nRun both outputs through one pipeline that dispatches each libyuv call on\nthe destination layout, so every path still writes its output directly and\nnone gains a pass or a buffer. NV12 output thereby accepts the same sources\nas I420 where libyuv converts to it, and both outputs reject strides shorter\nthan a row.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325187\n", "files": ["dom/media/ImageConversion.cpp", "dom/media/ImageConversion.h"], "git_node": "d6b8df32116f9d072ff9329dec3ca0ddb4a34f1b", "git_parents": ["7d65e7153ab82e8b61605f229d8c8a271d86faa7"], "node": "401514b96adeeed8a696fbb06a328ca0170723e3", "parents": ["ad684d531739d4da57bb2fdc851e6f858985c3e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Neeco Fabian \u003cneecofabian@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070182 - Fix focus outline in FRO Import Screen dropdown r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles,emcminn\n\n- Remove focus outline from inner summary text, add outline to container\n- has() selector required to check the child, but modify the parent\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326301\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/migration/migration-wizard.css"], "git_node": "111a4643c956b7a8b67e4a75a2518b75b12849b5", "git_parents": ["d6b8df32116f9d072ff9329dec3ca0ddb4a34f1b"], "node": "041d1aaf8c5776b41028e481ccea4a73183f6022", "parents": ["401514b96adeeed8a696fbb06a328ca0170723e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072535 - Update test_renderer_strings's KNOWN_ON_CI strings for Metal ANGLE. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nWith ANGLE enabled, the renderer and vendor strings reported by the\nARM macOS 15 workers now include \"ANGLE\" and \"Google Inc.\"\nrespectively. Metal ANGLE is blocked on macOS versions older than 12,\ntherefore the strings reported by the macOS 10.15 workers are\nunaffected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326498\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/test/webgl-mochitest/test_renderer_strings.html"], "git_node": "2bd5f767f2f9187ebb4f868e877b0adf978dec28", "git_parents": ["111a4643c956b7a8b67e4a75a2518b75b12849b5"], "node": "7f762cef4e8832f4cb501b4aac03fee81a42c3ef", "parents": ["041d1aaf8c5776b41028e481ccea4a73183f6022"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072535 - Enable Metal ANGLE for WebGL on Nightly. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326499\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "54d6e161bdc94d2f5d4daeff9cbce946d3cd281f", "git_parents": ["2bd5f767f2f9187ebb4f868e877b0adf978dec28"], "node": "45b80a6e4256223e6996898d1bfa99db1ee6c181", "parents": ["7f762cef4e8832f4cb501b4aac03fee81a42c3ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072535 - Update test expectations. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nEnabling Metal ANGLE for WebGL causes a bunch of tests to now pass on\naarch64 macOS 15 workers.\n\nHowever, there are additionally a few tests that must now be skipped\ndue to assertion failures in debug builds. Note that these are already\nskipped on Windows for the same reason.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326500\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/generated/generated-mochitest-webgl1-ext-conformance-glsl-misc.toml", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/generated/generated-mochitest-webgl2-core-conformance-misc.toml", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/generated/generated-mochitest-webgl2-core-conformance2.toml", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/generated/generated-mochitest-webgl2-ext-conformance-glsl-misc.toml", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/mochitest-errata.toml", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-mochitest/mochitest.toml"], "git_node": "eafafacf835c39d95f250fec0351b20fa9382fe4", "git_parents": ["54d6e161bdc94d2f5d4daeff9cbce946d3cd281f"], "node": "c9f9a67f54c76e2c690952d12564b1b7f8d46c3a", "parents": ["45b80a6e4256223e6996898d1bfa99db1ee6c181"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073226: Skip null elements when tracing Wasm GC struct payloads. r=bvisness\n\nAfter this, all the AnyRef tracing in WasmGCObject.cpp skips null refs. There are some remaining cases in Instance::traceFrame and Val::trace that somebody on the Wasm team might want to look into.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327057\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmGcObject.cpp"], "git_node": "6f60fb5a5bb2b5afaaea7d9e96bd8cf84c205912", "git_parents": ["eafafacf835c39d95f250fec0351b20fa9382fe4"], "node": "84e18251f5c1137efa5a97b73dfbf86b322b745b", "parents": ["c9f9a67f54c76e2c690952d12564b1b7f8d46c3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065458 - Scroll the target into view before clicking it in the pdf.js tests r=marco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320403\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/head.js"], "git_node": "d0c57d32f23536c1d7aa2fbc7ad1dac6e086f2e5", "git_parents": ["6f60fb5a5bb2b5afaaea7d9e96bd8cf84c205912"], "node": "c1882d37e1e45ba80ca8a8a522ce8be7ed768350", "parents": ["84e18251f5c1137efa5a97b73dfbf86b322b745b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1808333 - Stop relying on render events in browser_pdfjs_zoom.js. r=marco\n\nA render event cannot synchronize these tasks: a zoom schedules a delayed\nredraw, so a wait can be satisfied by the previous step's leftover render, and\na cancelled render dispatches nothing at all. Check the state of the DOM\ninstead, the way the comment on top of head.js recommends.\n\nThe zoom label also needs an explicit translateElements, as Fluent translates\nit asynchronously.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321580\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_zoom.js"], "git_node": "d4d348e1fa07d8c728ab2291116987d9c5471015", "git_parents": ["d0c57d32f23536c1d7aa2fbc7ad1dac6e086f2e5"], "node": "5a01b3813935e1977aeac26359b51cfc51f8e3fd", "parents": ["c1882d37e1e45ba80ca8a8a522ce8be7ed768350"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067096 - Fix the intermittent failures with browser_pdfjs_editing_contextmenu.js. r=marco\n\nThe timeouts came from the context menu never opening: the synthesized\ncontextmenu event can be dispatched before the content window received its\ndimensions from the parent process. With a zero-sized viewport, or while\npainting is still suppressed. So wait for the target window and its ancestors\nto be hit-testable first.\n\nThe assertion failures came from checking isCurrentGlobal on the stale frame:\nit requires CanSend(), hence it races the teardown of the window global. Only\nassert isActiveInTab, which is what the code relies on, and null-check the\nwindow global in PdfJsContextMenu.cmd() where the same race threw.\n\nThe helpers duplicated by browser_pdfjs_pages_contextmenu.js move to head.js.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321846\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsContextMenu.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_editing_contextmenu.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_pages_contextmenu.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/head.js"], "git_node": "fb4ee53249996426748b05aee7c9c8462bd73081", "git_parents": ["d4d348e1fa07d8c728ab2291116987d9c5471015"], "node": "a0267e12c9d67e49e4674d7d20359bbe2f66fdcc", "parents": ["5a01b3813935e1977aeac26359b51cfc51f8e3fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064678 - Plumb H264 profile and level into AndroidDataEncoder, matching the GMP/FFmpeg/Apple/WMF encoder backends. r=media-playback-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,padenot,tcampbell\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321194\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/android/AndroidDataEncoder.cpp", "widget/android/bindings/MediaCodec-classes.txt"], "git_node": "6f0fb26ba9a6712e9f633dcf8fafbf8bd3bf3c9c", "git_parents": ["fb4ee53249996426748b05aee7c9c8462bd73081"], "node": "024060c5f31c46e8ae56cdf9539401a8c8fb89fa", "parents": ["a0267e12c9d67e49e4674d7d20359bbe2f66fdcc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064678 - Balance the leaked active-request count when RemoteManager.createCodec() fails to init a codec. r=media-playback-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,jolin,tcampbell\n\nIf CodecProxy.init() fails (e.g. Codec.configure() found no matching codec\nfor the requested profile/level/resolution), createCodec() returns null\nwithout ever calling IMediaManager.endRequest() to balance the\ncreateCodec() call already made on the remote. releaseCodec(), which is\nthe only other endRequest() call site, is never reached for a codec that\nwas never added to mCodecs.\n\nThis leaves the :media process's mNumActiveRequests permanently\nover-counted by one. The next time the client unbinds the service (e.g.\nbecause its last successfully-created codec was released and\nreleaseIfNeeded() unbound), MediaManager.onUnbind() sees a nonzero\nmNumActiveRequests and calls Process.killProcess() on itself, believing\nthe caller died abnormally. Android then respawns the :media process,\nwhich looks like a bind/unbind/process-restart cycle with no obvious\ntrigger. Failing codec creations (e.g. by requesting an H264 level 5/6\nresolution the platform's encoder doesn't support) reliably reproduce\nthis.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321195\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/media/RemoteManager.java"], "git_node": "1c4bf062ecc3675707ea4345b0dae7a02c172afd", "git_parents": ["6f0fb26ba9a6712e9f633dcf8fafbf8bd3bf3c9c"], "node": "f2d6b9c676d6340380a27296256bc96bd080cfae", "parents": ["024060c5f31c46e8ae56cdf9539401a8c8fb89fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064678 - Report H264 QP thresholds from WebrtcMediaDataEncoder so libwebrtc's QualityScaler can track it. r=webrtc-reviewers,ng\n\nWebrtcMediaDataEncoder::GetEncoderInfo() never populated scaling_settings,\nleaving it at ScalingSettings::kOff. This means libwebrtc's\nQualityScalerResource cannot be kept alive across a switch onto this\nencoder: VideoStreamEncoderResourceManager::UpdateQualityScalerSettings()\nsees no QP thresholds and calls RemoveResource(), which -- if quality\nscaling was the only resource currently imposing a resolution\nrestriction -- resets restrictions to unconstrained via\nVideoStreamAdapter::ClearRestrictions().\n\nOn Android this produces an unbounded retry loop for resolutions beyond\nwhat the hardware MediaCodec encoder actually supports: the hardware\nencoder fails to configure, libwebrtc falls back to a software encoder\n(which reports QP thresholds and gets downscaled by the QualityScaler\nafter seeing 100% frame drop), and the moment that downscaled resolution\nlets the hardware encoder succeed again, its lack of QP thresholds tears\ndown the QualityScalerResource and wipes the very restriction that made\nit succeed -- so the next frame is requested at the full, unconstrained\nresolution again, repeating forever.\n\nReporting the same QP thresholds WebrtcGmpVideoEncoder already uses lets\nthe single, long-lived QualityScalerResource survive the switch (only\nSetQpThresholds() runs, not Remove/AddResource), so a resolution\nrestriction earned via the fallback encoder persists once the hardware\nencoder takes back over.\n\nMove the threshold constants into WebrtcGmpVideoCodec.h (as constexpr,\nshared by both encoder wrappers) instead of duplicating them: as\nstatic const int in each .cpp they collided under unified builds, which\nconcatenate both files into one translation unit.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321196\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcGmpVideoCodec.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcGmpVideoCodec.h", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcMediaDataEncoderCodec.cpp"], "git_node": "abbba500cfea94c0dbf1292bedeb13a8c740bb65", "git_parents": ["1c4bf062ecc3675707ea4345b0dae7a02c172afd"], "node": "d3b6bfc4949e28e96f5f6a6b411bc1bce999908b", "parents": ["f2d6b9c676d6340380a27296256bc96bd080cfae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064678 - Add gtest coverage for encoding below Android's real per-frame macroblock cap at a Level 5-implied resolution. r=media-playback-reviewers,jolin\n\nMediaDataEncoderTest.H264Encodes4K* already covers the previously-documented\n4K resolution limit, but the actual platform limit turned out to be a\ntighter, ~8192-macroblock-per-frame budget (roughly Level 4-equivalent) --\nindependent of the declared H264 level -- discovered while investigating\nthe Level 5/6 profile-levels WPT hang. Add a resolution below the 4K\nthreshold but still over that macroblock budget, once with a deliberately\nmismatched (too-low) declared level and once with a level that actually\nmatches it, to cover both axes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321197\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "1df782d9734a2c69f617271f486603f470f64675", "git_parents": ["abbba500cfea94c0dbf1292bedeb13a8c740bb65"], "node": "6f8506768a061e012672bbabd319da83c7541f37", "parents": ["d3b6bfc4949e28e96f5f6a6b411bc1bce999908b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nickgrato \u003cngrato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068261 - [Monitor Agent] [FE] Open monitor alert URLs into new tab group r=yjamora,tabbrowser-reviewers,niklas import uuid\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326783\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-panel/agent-monitor-panel.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-panel/agent-monitor-panel.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/MonitorPanel.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_monitor_button_panel.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/TabMetrics.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d48eba5fb8baa39aab4b8de3562c1fe192b130c5", "git_parents": ["1df782d9734a2c69f617271f486603f470f64675"], "node": "381613499b6aa401b59fbb2b5de6c68685ed8a3f", "parents": ["6f8506768a061e012672bbabd319da83c7541f37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072818 - Remove ONNX 1.22 Availability Telemetry Probe r=valentinp,ai-platform-reviewers\n\nThis commit removes the temporary telemetry probe that helps\nus check for native ONNX runtime availability for ONNX version 1.22.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326987\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "testing/profiles/base/user.js", "toolkit/components/ml/content/EngineProcess.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_native_ort_availability_probe.js"], "git_node": "d0b295703acde02c1f865690db77cd13ad000ba5", "git_parents": ["d48eba5fb8baa39aab4b8de3562c1fe192b130c5"], "node": "b74b140220e97f1adde8a40b9dcd5db19d30b543", "parents": ["381613499b6aa401b59fbb2b5de6c68685ed8a3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073175 - Cleanup Native ONNX availability between tests r=ai-platform-reviewers,jbowser\n\nThis commit ensures that tests that concern themselves with the\nnative ONNX availability cache properly clear the cache before\nand after testing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327020\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_best_onnx.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_best_onnx_fallback.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_engine_creation_interceptor.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_native_ort_availability.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "ced21f17c20c2004016e1c36a036905ed33f4fa9", "git_parents": ["d0b295703acde02c1f865690db77cd13ad000ba5"], "node": "bd515d7c9683e3f675e9c695af6c1071dc3329df", "parents": ["b74b140220e97f1adde8a40b9dcd5db19d30b543"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068877 - Part 2: Rename DefaultTopSitesBinding to DefaultPinnedSitesBinding r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\n- This binding will add a list of default pinned sites into PinnedSiteStorage on the first run of the application.\n- Going forward, this will only be used to seed the Google pinned site and all other sites will become a default top site that is used to backfill and fill up the available slots on the Top Sites UI.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323485\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/DefaultPinnedSitesBinding.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/DefaultTopSitesBinding.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/raw/default_pinned_shortcuts.json", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/raw/initial_shortcuts.json", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/DefaultPinnedSitesBindingTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/DefaultTopSitesBindingTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/resources/raw/test_default_pinned_shortcuts.json", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/resources/raw/test_initial_shortcuts.json"], "git_node": "4d10976a9455e556f2c47ca6bd12ec8248521ba0", "git_parents": ["ced21f17c20c2004016e1c36a036905ed33f4fa9"], "node": "25bfb6e118ab6bf537d584be4526632ae2bb8a9e", "parents": ["bd515d7c9683e3f675e9c695af6c1071dc3329df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2040905 - nsStandardURL::Deserialize should reparse the URL r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309064\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "b30705dd16ae7452d8f63f2d3b270e145dae519b", "git_parents": ["4d10976a9455e556f2c47ca6bd12ec8248521ba0"], "node": "2ce7362c0088b4dc2f3ef1b5f6ef36cb3186f5a7", "parents": ["25bfb6e118ab6bf537d584be4526632ae2bb8a9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Do not restore URL state on failure r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nPreviously, when URLs were mutable, we'd need to restore URL state\nwhen a setter operation failed. However, this copy of the URL state is now\nredundant, as any mutator operation that fails will simply throw away\nthe state.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308229\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_standardurl.js"], "git_node": "6a8dcf07fca22e95ec3732c9552f55b53f1892c6", "git_parents": ["b30705dd16ae7452d8f63f2d3b270e145dae519b"], "node": "fc916c279febcef887818c6e414a55904eb87a28", "parents": ["2ce7362c0088b4dc2f3ef1b5f6ef36cb3186f5a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - avoid strlen call r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308230\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "fa4325ab40f3440f5ddfaafe7100f257f38d4bb0", "git_parents": ["6a8dcf07fca22e95ec3732c9552f55b53f1892c6"], "node": "d2118cf42b13786cc7dfbd497090eea4672bef7f", "parents": ["fc916c279febcef887818c6e414a55904eb87a28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Optimize IsSpecialProtocol r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308231\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "892cad1b4db6f2507c2c2f18f4c659e28c3828b0", "git_parents": ["fa4325ab40f3440f5ddfaafe7100f257f38d4bb0"], "node": "d350af3be583e16650920c21ec86d83da7152a42", "parents": ["d2118cf42b13786cc7dfbd497090eea4672bef7f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Optimize coalescePath r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308232\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_standardurl.js"], "git_node": "806ec6b27dc061db0d1daed8b5691fe52ae75017", "git_parents": ["892cad1b4db6f2507c2c2f18f4c659e28c3828b0"], "node": "e15549a076c665f081bcff44a1f0ace5b7e83b0b", "parents": ["d350af3be583e16650920c21ec86d83da7152a42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Optimize SegmentIs r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308233\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.h"], "git_node": "cf1dc88aca9c61f585d4352a72c060555309eb7d", "git_parents": ["806ec6b27dc061db0d1daed8b5691fe52ae75017"], "node": "3f6c2ea2fb770786f556ac8d9cd54f22e8858b4a", "parents": ["e15549a076c665f081bcff44a1f0ace5b7e83b0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Optimize CalculateParity r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308234\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.h"], "git_node": "9f771353a7fe781cc0d6d985a1f5223038044dc9", "git_parents": ["cf1dc88aca9c61f585d4352a72c060555309eb7d"], "node": "19d3b8273878135853dcf60d15f74cf4f776cc23", "parents": ["3f6c2ea2fb770786f556ac8d9cd54f22e8858b4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Fewer string passes r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308235\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsURLHelper.cpp"], "git_node": "27734a9aee00e22c1bd25726c8aeb7cb32be5dbc", "git_parents": ["9f771353a7fe781cc0d6d985a1f5223038044dc9"], "node": "55cc02c5d4907964e94f6d44f666fd89966752a5", "parents": ["19d3b8273878135853dcf60d15f74cf4f776cc23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Fast path for BuildNormalized r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308236\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "7a2ebe2230775697d2d59efc2a3752db1e89ad8b", "git_parents": ["27734a9aee00e22c1bd25726c8aeb7cb32be5dbc"], "node": "94764edf52fbbfa34a9747acd9e9f6f8b3dca52d", "parents": ["55cc02c5d4907964e94f6d44f666fd89966752a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Add nonXPCOM ParseAll method to nsBaseURLParser r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308237\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.h", "netwerk/base/nsURLHelper.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsURLHelper.h", "netwerk/base/nsURLParsers.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsURLParsers.h"], "git_node": "42bbbe72d3d5d5c66d21ab83680d25f1616a13ac", "git_parents": ["7a2ebe2230775697d2d59efc2a3752db1e89ad8b"], "node": "d4b8c0cc910ec15fb9086dbe489b854d40bf18dd", "parents": ["94764edf52fbbfa34a9747acd9e9f6f8b3dca52d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Don't assert on non-UTF-8 input in nsSegmentEncoder r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nnsStandardURL's setters take nsACString, which carries no UTF-8 guarantee, so\nthe MOZ_ASSERT_UNREACHABLE in EncodeSegmentCount asserts on something callers\ncan legitimately do. SetQueryWithEncoding reaches it on its own: a legacy\ncharset makes mEncoding non-null, and any non-UTF-8 byte in the query then\nlands in that branch.\n\nThe code immediately below already handles the case correctly, decoding the\ninput to UTF-8 and substituting U+FFFD for invalid sequences, so the assertion\nonly turns a handled input into a debug-build crash. Drop it and add a gtest\nthat pins the resulting normalization.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325944\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "50dd3f44d7c3a99522eb74b0cdd6205d01f3a56d", "git_parents": ["42bbbe72d3d5d5c66d21ab83680d25f1616a13ac"], "node": "3d61ee65ed4f9927a41fc67dca317c599bcf1f76", "parents": ["d4b8c0cc910ec15fb9086dbe489b854d40bf18dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2062651 - Remove dead PanelUI-fxa-menu-setup-sync-container from the account panel r=nsharpley,desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\" for causing bc tests failures at /sync-off.svg\n\nThis reverts commit c8712790787ddccb848c471940d316a098a30c5b.\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/browser-sync.js", "browser/base/content/test/sync/browser_sync.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/appmenu.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css"], "git_node": "b729f233da0d39847ebba45170139160a44d8d8c", "git_parents": ["50dd3f44d7c3a99522eb74b0cdd6205d01f3a56d"], "node": "2ec8a9310a751eb4a1c5b6803ba8ca9c240979e3", "parents": ["3d61ee65ed4f9927a41fc67dca317c599bcf1f76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2064678 - Add gtest coverage for encoding below Android's real per-frame macroblock cap at a Level 5-implied resolution. r=media-playback-reviewers,jolin\" for causing gtests failures at MediaDataEncoderTest\n\nThis reverts commit 1df782d9734a2c69f617271f486603f470f64675.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064678 - Report H264 QP thresholds from WebrtcMediaDataEncoder so libwebrtc's QualityScaler can track it. r=webrtc-reviewers,ng\"\n\nThis reverts commit abbba500cfea94c0dbf1292bedeb13a8c740bb65.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064678 - Balance the leaked active-request count when RemoteManager.createCodec() fails to init a codec. r=media-playback-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,jolin,tcampbell\"\n\nThis reverts commit 1c4bf062ecc3675707ea4345b0dae7a02c172afd.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064678 - Plumb H264 profile and level into AndroidDataEncoder, matching the GMP/FFmpeg/Apple/WMF encoder backends. r=media-playback-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,padenot,tcampbell\"\n\nThis reverts commit 6f0fb26ba9a6712e9f633dcf8fafbf8bd3bf3c9c.\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataEncoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/android/AndroidDataEncoder.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcGmpVideoCodec.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcGmpVideoCodec.h", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcMediaDataEncoderCodec.cpp", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/media/RemoteManager.java", "widget/android/bindings/MediaCodec-classes.txt"], "git_node": "145b7876bf67359c04fc4699ae89e9a538e83e02", "git_parents": ["b729f233da0d39847ebba45170139160a44d8d8c"], "node": "b4a57262d051315042440eadc4ef993bd554847e", "parents": ["2ec8a9310a751eb4a1c5b6803ba8ca9c240979e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073274 - Skip ProfileLockedTest and StorageControllerTest on code coverage builds. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nBoth classes push the ccov emulator into lmkd: ProfileLockedTest starts two extra GeckoRuntimes next to the\nmain test runtime, and StorageControllerTest cycles through many content processes. On ccov each Gecko process\nis large enough that lmkd SIGKILLs one of the main runtime's utility processes; with\nMOZ_CRASHREPORTER_SHUTDOWN set that abnormal exit quits the runtime, and the next test aborts the whole junit\nrun with a harness timeout (the bug 1916019 signature).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327157\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/build.gradle", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/ProfileLockedTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/StorageControllerTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/util/Environment.java"], "git_node": "93223003f83652000046fd3f6997cddfdb2dc582", "git_parents": ["145b7876bf67359c04fc4699ae89e9a538e83e02"], "node": "aa5c2b622cff9d7e26ef245a4bb498950ef7bc6e", "parents": ["b4a57262d051315042440eadc4ef993bd554847e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073030 - Lint all spidermonkey headers through clang-tidy r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nChanges includes:\n- using C++20 type traits\n- making deleted methods public\n- making some methods default\n- use std::forward instead of std::move to prevent lifetime issues\n- avoid confusing constructor through universal references\n- rework some include dependencies to make header self contained\n\nAll changes were detected either by header compilation failure, or by\nclang-tidy.\n\nFixes are either generated by clang-tidy or hand-made.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326931\n", "files": ["js/loader/ScriptKind.h", "js/loader/ScriptLoaderInterface.h", "js/public/CompileOptions.h", "js/public/Debug.h", "js/public/ForOfIterator.h", "js/public/GCAPI.h", "js/public/GCHashTable.h", "js/public/JSON.h", "js/public/Printer.h", "js/public/ProfilingSources.h", "js/public/ProfilingStack.h", "js/public/PropertySpec.h", "js/public/Proxy.h", "js/public/RootingAPI.h", "js/public/SourceText.h", "js/public/StableStringChars.h", "js/public/StructuredClone.h", "js/public/SweepingAPI.h", "js/public/TraceKind.h", "js/public/UbiNode.h", "js/public/Value.h", "js/public/WeakMapPtr.h", "js/public/experimental/BindingAllocs.h", "js/public/experimental/JSStencil.h", "js/public/friend/CycleCollector.h", "js/src/frontend/ScopeBindingCache.h", "js/src/gc/Cell.h", "js/src/gc/GCLock.h", "js/src/gc/GCRuntime.h", "js/src/gc/HashUtil.h", "js/src/gc/TraceMethods-inl.h", "js/src/vm/CompletionKind.h", "js/src/vm/SavedStacks.h", "js/xpconnect/loader/IOBuffers.h", "js/xpconnect/src/JSServices.h", "js/xpconnect/src/XPCJSMemoryReporter.h", "js/xpconnect/src/xpcObjectHelper.h", "js/xpconnect/src/xpcpublic.h"], "git_node": "2a131bc709d0cc20c9eb15b9de1bac03c88310e2", "git_parents": ["93223003f83652000046fd3f6997cddfdb2dc582"], "node": "3b55a9b7c511c9abfe1ce402996698ff71a4d8fa", "parents": ["aa5c2b622cff9d7e26ef245a4bb498950ef7bc6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "sarah541 \u003csarahkhan1107@hotmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067904 - Show two full rows of shortcuts at every width r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\nThe homepage grid lays out between four and eight columns depending on the\navailable width, but the collapsed section still showed a fixed eight\nshortcuts. That meant the wider the screen, the fewer rows it held: two full\nrows on a phone, a row and a partial one at six columns, and a single row on\na tablet, where \"Show all\" appeared with obvious room to spare.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323046\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSiteState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSites.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSitesLayout.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSiteStateTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSitesExpandToggleTest.kt"], "git_node": "481ae42edf7f72f3cee4f8ea04a3afe25c950109", "git_parents": ["2a131bc709d0cc20c9eb15b9de1bac03c88310e2"], "node": "0e8dfe639101d3b9fd5e5c9486d8ff390e0784bd", "parents": ["3b55a9b7c511c9abfe1ce402996698ff71a4d8fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072796 - Update nestegg to 767aab25013acefbdcc6d68a2a7a2c9081303e3f r=kinetik\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326804\n", "files": ["media/libnestegg/moz.yaml", "media/libnestegg/src/nestegg.c"], "git_node": "b5a5f530cf20e9135b8dae973d8a446b0adbfd83", "git_parents": ["481ae42edf7f72f3cee4f8ea04a3afe25c950109"], "node": "e7bb76f36bfa5bd4809475bcea5ba61531d3ba67", "parents": ["0e8dfe639101d3b9fd5e5c9486d8ff390e0784bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris DuPuis \u003ccdupuis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037979 - Improve logging of updater invocation scenarios r=application-update-reviewers,aborondo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321713\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/maintenanceservice/workmonitor.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/UpdateService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/elevation_type.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/elevation_type.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatecommon.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatecommon.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updater_invocation.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updater_invocation.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/gtest/ElevationTypeTests.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/gtest/README.md", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/gtest/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "2f4e1be33d5f7046e30a09e4c647897c11019c01", "git_parents": ["b5a5f530cf20e9135b8dae973d8a446b0adbfd83"], "node": "1476f2eeb0b6d6fdabea12e104a3310d42c20d23", "parents": ["e7bb76f36bfa5bd4809475bcea5ba61531d3ba67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Niklas Baumgardner \u003cnbaumgardner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066812 - Remove duplicate fxa-menu-header-title ids. r=jhirsch\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326218\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml"], "git_node": "148deb5004041870a35439d6cc4df33e70db6b4f", "git_parents": ["2f4e1be33d5f7046e30a09e4c647897c11019c01"], "node": "d1887deac9ef3a83dae74693d6f824bae40d99d4", "parents": ["1476f2eeb0b6d6fdabea12e104a3310d42c20d23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072627: If the managing WindowGlobal is no longer current for its BrowsingContext, a received PDocAccessible will die shortly, so just ignore it. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nWe only ever care about the document for the current WindowGlobal.\nVarious places enforce this, including BrowserBridgeParent::GetDocAccessibleParent.\nPreviously, if a PDocAccessible for an OOP iframe arrived late after the WindowGlobal is no longer current (e.g. due to a process switch), we would try to add it as a child doc, causing a crash because BrowserBridgeParent::GetDocAccessibleParent refuses to return a non-current document.\nTo avoid this, ignore the document early and return, just as we already do for a discarded BrowsingContext.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326814\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp"], "git_node": "1714abe1689dfc099ec9ca9eaa57dc829c1d7cf5", "git_parents": ["148deb5004041870a35439d6cc4df33e70db6b4f"], "node": "5b481528aa4c7af5716660a2caa03d5cf33f2bb4", "parents": ["d1887deac9ef3a83dae74693d6f824bae40d99d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072101 part 1: Make Accessible support RefPtr. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326834\n", "files": ["accessible/atk/nsMaiInterfaceComponent.cpp", "accessible/basetypes/Accessible.h", "accessible/ipc/RemoteAccessible.h", "accessible/mac/mozAccessible.mm", "accessible/windows/ia2/ia2Accessible.cpp", "accessible/windows/uia/uiaRawElmProvider.cpp", "accessible/xpcom/xpcAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "43fae04566e55b0cbcc5f30c627b3200ace92ec8", "git_parents": ["1714abe1689dfc099ec9ca9eaa57dc829c1d7cf5"], "node": "d28b2994e096d8fa568a38b4fe36ed818009e1fc", "parents": ["5b481528aa4c7af5716660a2caa03d5cf33f2bb4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072101 part 2: Use RefPtr for CachedTableAccessible. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326835\n", "files": ["accessible/base/CachedTableAccessible.h"], "git_node": "1c23c71c5994a6eac27b4ba934146c8f8c48af2f", "git_parents": ["43fae04566e55b0cbcc5f30c627b3200ace92ec8"], "node": "12e08fd73f53d885355599f1f5490085ac31c4eb", "parents": ["d28b2994e096d8fa568a38b4fe36ed818009e1fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Manuel Rego Casasnovas \u003crego@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073191 - Fire SENSITIVE event when disabled attribute changes r=Jamie\n\nFirefox is failing the following WPT test:\nhttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62768\n\nBecause it triggers ENABLED state-change event,\nbut doesn't do the same for SENSITIVE.\nWhich should be the case according to the spec:\nhttps://w3c.github.io/aria/core-aam/#event-aria-disabled\n\nFirefox actually triggers both events when aria-disabled attribute\nis modified.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327026\n", "files": ["accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "3569216547a8ee8cccee927cdca556f21af65cb2", "git_parents": ["1c23c71c5994a6eac27b4ba934146c8f8c48af2f"], "node": "736f251f1f4904e81aec31c531367fadddd934d2", "parents": ["12e08fd73f53d885355599f1f5490085ac31c4eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Tighe \u003cmatthewdtighe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064869 - enqueue synthesized chunks as a playlist r=android-reviewers,moyin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326772\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenAction.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenReducer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/fakes/Listen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/playback/ListenPlayer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/playback/PlaybackController.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenReducerTest.kt"], "git_node": "c65daecfe9c2072da9855c495b34f48e813ea1db", "git_parents": ["3569216547a8ee8cccee927cdca556f21af65cb2"], "node": "e589ebeb6bc0997acbdd68845040f62c2173fbb1", "parents": ["736f251f1f4904e81aec31c531367fadddd934d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072425: Propagate regexp interrupt termination immediately r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326348\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/regexp/bug2072425.js", "js/src/vm/RegExpObject.cpp"], "git_node": "86591a421b02c203de00af144182f2f59d6341cc", "git_parents": ["c65daecfe9c2072da9855c495b34f48e813ea1db"], "node": "0ac43890e9635ad86f6d75d85e7685ac591c68e8", "parents": ["e589ebeb6bc0997acbdd68845040f62c2173fbb1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072715 - Drop rasterized glyphs above a size limit r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nFONT_SIZE_LIMIT bounds the size the font backends are asked for, not what\nthey return: a near-degenerate transform decomposes into a tiny minor axis\nscale that the quantized glyph size rounds away, leaving the compensating\nshape matrix uncancelled, so the glyph grows as the reciprocal of the\ndeterminant.\n\nBug 2063377 packs 16 sub-pixel variants of such a glyph into one atlas\nentry, sized in i32, which overflows and aborts in the allocator.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327172\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wr_glyph_rasterizer/src/rasterizer.rs"], "git_node": "c2e9eaa4922b70d74737dd8a07838638766dcacd", "git_parents": ["86591a421b02c203de00af144182f2f59d6341cc"], "node": "97bff41666879121f33c5a3bb9f19e38176abb2d", "parents": ["0ac43890e9635ad86f6d75d85e7685ac591c68e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2049622, Bug 2040905 - Don't assert on non-UTF-8 input in nsSegmentEncoder r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\" for causing failures at browser_xpcom_graph_wait.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 50dd3f44d7c3a99522eb74b0cdd6205d01f3a56d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2049622 - Add nonXPCOM ParseAll method to nsBaseURLParser r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 42bbbe72d3d5d5c66d21ab83680d25f1616a13ac.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2049622 - Fast path for BuildNormalized r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7a2ebe2230775697d2d59efc2a3752db1e89ad8b.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2049622 - Fewer string passes r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 27734a9aee00e22c1bd25726c8aeb7cb32be5dbc.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2049622 - Optimize CalculateParity r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9f771353a7fe781cc0d6d985a1f5223038044dc9.\n\n