 []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2053167 - Part 7: Test the content classifier engines' memory reporting r=emz\" for causing failures at browser_content_classifier_memory_reporter.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 71aa02e0553f71bd61630eab4768abb6864bf302.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053167 - Part 6: Attribute the content classifier engines' resource backend r=emz,mccr8\"\n\nThis reverts commit 31638915b6a27587d7b612b2e853ff4f4f322116.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053167 - Part 5: Attribute the content classifier engines' cosmetic cache r=emz,mccr8\"\n\nThis reverts commit 26638fa3172aa89c771e389995159a757f10adfe.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053167 - Part 4: Attribute the content classifier engines' blocker memory r=emz,mccr8\"\n\nThis reverts commit 2471324096b6a134c064831ed497e40733ea6906.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053167 - Part 3: Attribute the content classifier engines' filter data in about:memory r=emz,mccr8\"\n\nThis reverts commit 8704e2a1d01a307808a78a09563ad7b386cb9be6.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053167 - Part 2: Report the content classifier engines to about:memory r=emz,mccr8\"\n\nThis reverts commit c918a50497d1186f03413b0213cc160bc80ed97b.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053167 - Part 1: Ensure every engine consumer holds mLock r=emz\"\n\nThis reverts commit 635e71bd8b9cf66de61d0eadda0a3cf83c6ad682.\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.h", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/ContentClassifierEngine.h", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/engine.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/flatbuffers/unsafe_tools.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/malloc_size_of_impls.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/regex_manager.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/resources/resource_storage.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_memory_reporter.js"], "git_node": "ebd5da0b8f26bbd49a15311cf07b793689223b73", "git_parents": ["7e0098d1d221a0d1f715c8a74aa1bd6fc9b0c012"], "node": "0975b566890cd507441714205bf9f5a5f0e4f07a", "parents": ["9478b18cf289761f981e9184a75847f2c8a21907"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2070729 [Wayland] Force toplevel window repaint by positioning child subsurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\" for causing bustages in nsWindowWayland.\n\nThis reverts commit 3cb2190a6131804c01f087ab99bfdf2ed7e040d0.\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp", "widget/gtk/MozContainerWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.h"], "git_node": "4b5c93b1b7f111275eae2024f7fced0bfc5139f9", "git_parents": ["ebd5da0b8f26bbd49a15311cf07b793689223b73"], "node": "e2ab53bea44f9d742b2fb01a668d130e6545bd5c", "parents": ["0975b566890cd507441714205bf9f5a5f0e4f07a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070956 - Let ContentClassifierPrefMirror release or hand over the content prefs it mirrors. r=emz\n\nThis patch replaces the boolean mirror pref with a mode pref. The mode\npref supports three modes:\n  0 (Off): The default mode. The mirror is off and clear mirrored prefs\n  1 (On): The mirror is on to mirror the prefs\n  2 (Handover): The mirror stop mirroring the prefs and don't clear\n                them.\nThis behavior supports rolling back from the mirror state, and allow\nhanding over the mirrored prefs once we no longer need mirroring.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325068\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierPrefMirror.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierPrefMirror.h", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_engines_pref.js", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_pref_mirror.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "d994658a278538efa16535f84b4a39b61e9538e5", "git_parents": ["4b5c93b1b7f111275eae2024f7fced0bfc5139f9"], "node": "7b85280694a5bd347271257697b7480f8dee3830", "parents": ["e2ab53bea44f9d742b2fb01a668d130e6545bd5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052474 - Migrate JsAllocationMarker to the new API r=canova,profiler-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326478\n", "files": ["tools/profiler/core/ProfilerThreadRegistrationData.cpp"], "git_node": "f84f9caa1035c13ff22330abf4be8a26079f6878", "git_parents": ["d994658a278538efa16535f84b4a39b61e9538e5"], "node": "525889f543a5f4be2ef2730806e3cffb03079a0e", "parents": ["7b85280694a5bd347271257697b7480f8dee3830"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1456885 - Rename SpeechGrammarList.addFromURI to SpeechGrammarList.addFromUri to match Chrome r=webidl,media-webspeech-reviewers,pehrsons,smaug\n\nThis is an inert interface that exist solely for web compat, and it\ndoesn't do anything to the Speech Recognition process.\n\nWe don't need to implement it for Web Compat. I have implemented some\nbits of the rest of the interface so it returns things that are\nmeaningful, but that is apparently not needed either. We might be able\nto remove that when we're a bit more confident.\n\nBecause of the wrong capitalization, it was not found, breaking Google\nDocs. I also removed exception throwing that weren't necessary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326946\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechGrammar.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechGrammar.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechGrammarList.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechGrammarList.h", "dom/webidl/SpeechGrammar.webidl", "dom/webidl/SpeechGrammarList.webidl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/speech-api.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/speech-api/idlharness.https.window.js"], "git_node": "2c724d0b3d0ce904ac72c4c112697df478cb7e60", "git_parents": ["f84f9caa1035c13ff22330abf4be8a26079f6878"], "node": "ee1b8c6173b792a2dca68fd340761c61921844f5", "parents": ["525889f543a5f4be2ef2730806e3cffb03079a0e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073174 - Update metadata for webaudio/the-audio-api/the-mediastreamaudiosourcenode-interface/mediastreamaudiosourcenode-routing.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327299\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-mediastreamaudiosourcenode-interface/mediastreamaudiosourcenode-routing.html.ini"], "git_node": "d59fcbbbb943a3efc02854fa4c146d5c0b71c294", "git_parents": ["2c724d0b3d0ce904ac72c4c112697df478cb7e60"], "node": "19db474ef67e939fd450df1d34f46c669326dc13", "parents": ["ee1b8c6173b792a2dca68fd340761c61921844f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071976 - Update metadata for webcodecs/*.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327306\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/full-cycle-test.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder-canvasImageSource.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder-config.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder-content-hint.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder-flush.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder-hbd.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "ff2ef120d7e887b22602157c1f0bd3c38311840c", "git_parents": ["d59fcbbbb943a3efc02854fa4c146d5c0b71c294"], "node": "2cf25e146a6b7b717c8d605195b1f48eef0c8b73", "parents": ["19db474ef67e939fd450df1d34f46c669326dc13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1846712 - Fix login to msn.com on Android by enabling webcompat features r=emz,webcompat-reviewers,android-reviewers,twisniewski,tcampbell\n\nThe site staying logged in depends on the navigation heuristic.\nThe navigation heuristic only works if the bounce tracking is in DRY_RUN mode\n(not STANDBY).\n\nMake DRY_RUN bounce tracking mode the default in recommended settings on\nAndroid. Enable the navigation heuristic on Android.\nDisable the recently_visited heuristic on Android.\nThis makes the behaviour the same on Desktop and Android.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318096\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/GeckoEngineTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/EngineSession.kt", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_storageAccessWithDynamicFpi.js"], "git_node": "131fe8793ff033052984aba9b899b8197d6b1f5e", "git_parents": ["ff2ef120d7e887b22602157c1f0bd3c38311840c"], "node": "d76bcaad0ff9e0769f583c0e7339dfa38477e09f", "parents": ["2cf25e146a6b7b717c8d605195b1f48eef0c8b73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073374 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to b0f0f5146c1f7f52aac1eb83227a5de0ed511a90 r=release-managers,diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327244\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "ebea63d72967aae494f6e4a7db8c48e5ef845778", "git_parents": ["131fe8793ff033052984aba9b899b8197d6b1f5e"], "node": "543b59c497674fcfa6fadbf512a7efc119a1e575", "parents": ["d76bcaad0ff9e0769f583c0e7339dfa38477e09f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072835 - Renew the private_browsing.cleanup.* metrics until Firefox 170. r=manuel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327307\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/cleardata/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "4f8a1d4463eff953a56b3b5afa97d6646023276a", "git_parents": ["ebea63d72967aae494f6e4a7db8c48e5ef845778"], "node": "c1960ef72766dada4f0af8f96c428380e4bbbd8a", "parents": ["543b59c497674fcfa6fadbf512a7efc119a1e575"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cornelius Emase \u003ccorneliuslochipi@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071916 - Move bailout helpers into CodeGeneratorShared r=jandem,iain\n\nI've moved deoptLabel_, bailoutFrom, bailout, and the three\nbailoutCmp*/bailoutTest* wrappers from each backend into\nCodeGeneratorShared. The one architectural difference is isolated\nin a single #ifdef.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326080\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm/CodeGenerator-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/CodeGenerator-arm.h", "js/src/jit/arm64/CodeGenerator-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/CodeGenerator-arm64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/CodeGenerator-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/CodeGenerator-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/CodeGenerator-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/CodeGenerator-mips-shared.h", "js/src/jit/none/CodeGenerator-none.h", "js/src/jit/none/MacroAssembler-none.h", "js/src/jit/riscv64/CodeGenerator-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/CodeGenerator-riscv64.h", "js/src/jit/shared/CodeGenerator-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/shared/CodeGenerator-shared.h", "js/src/jit/wasm32/CodeGenerator-wasm32.h", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/CodeGenerator-x86-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/CodeGenerator-x86-shared.h"], "git_node": "94896ff7992e5bb251aac09b274d954264ff7a77", "git_parents": ["4f8a1d4463eff953a56b3b5afa97d6646023276a"], "node": "9185b97f3a55e43a902d9584742b759f5379618b", "parents": ["c1960ef72766dada4f0af8f96c428380e4bbbd8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073000 - Pass the spatial tree to prepare_quad instead of the entire frame context. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nPatternBuilderContext::spatial_tree becomes unused (it already was but in a way that did not fifer by compiler warnings). It will be removed in a followup commit.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327001\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border_image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/box_shadow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/borders.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "8bb9229b9017a7c314e06c17aa371a8ae7e511a7", "git_parents": ["94896ff7992e5bb251aac09b274d954264ff7a77"], "node": "8dd3c6addc49ccbc9f330caf83244e9a74620dc8", "parents": ["9185b97f3a55e43a902d9584742b759f5379618b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073000 - Remove PatternBuilderContext and pass the pattern rect directly. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327002\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border_image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/backdrop.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/box_shadow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/cutout.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/filter.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/mix_blend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/repeat.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/yuv.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/conic.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/linear.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/radial.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "b66df54d9d650dd01308cf0fb2363597a93b2d46", "git_parents": ["8bb9229b9017a7c314e06c17aa371a8ae7e511a7"], "node": "efa6b2f7b101e20207974f8fb78159e7b93b278d", "parents": ["8dd3c6addc49ccbc9f330caf83244e9a74620dc8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073000 - Remove the offset parameter and fold it into the pattern_rect. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327003\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border_image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/backdrop.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/box_shadow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/cutout.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/filter.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/mix_blend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/repeat.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/yuv.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/conic.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/linear.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/radial.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "82b49d098aefb014078ffb5cc7aa1530b4dc7203", "git_parents": ["b66df54d9d650dd01308cf0fb2363597a93b2d46"], "node": "dd7a28a13e5b3bac6e8dddfcfcd55d5d835d0566", "parents": ["efa6b2f7b101e20207974f8fb78159e7b93b278d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073000 - Store gradient start/end/center as vectors instead of points. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nThis addresses something that has been bothering me for a long time. These parameters are relative to the top-left corner of the primitive rectangle and not relative to the primitive's spatial node, even though the latter would be also make perfect sense. Storing them as vector is more self-explanatory and avoids a pretty easy trap to fall into.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327005\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/conic.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/linear.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/radial.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/gradient_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interned_prims.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/prim_geometry.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_helper.rs", "layout/painting/nsCSSRenderingBorders.cpp", "layout/painting/nsCSSRenderingGradients.cpp"], "git_node": "fe5ece00ae1c5988255eeb8d7bf1c5d9ebb57e1f", "git_parents": ["82b49d098aefb014078ffb5cc7aa1530b4dc7203"], "node": "bc85ca5d930892d7e63d9636d8e428ef145f676c", "parents": ["dd7a28a13e5b3bac6e8dddfcfcd55d5d835d0566"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073000 - Compute the visible rect of repeated quads from the cached quad transform. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\ncompute_surface_visible_rect built a SpaceMapper per primitive, which walks the spatial tree to recompute the prim-to-surface transform, and then mapped the device rect through picture space before inverting that transform. Both callers already hold a QuadTransformState with the prim-to-raster mapping and the surface's device pixel scale, which together are exactly the local-to-device transform. Unmapping through it directly avoids the spatial tree walk and the spatial tree parameter, and in the common 2D case is a single inverse scale-offset.\n\nAlso pass the surface's clipping rect so that a followup commit can stop passing the surface data all over the prepare_quad funcitons.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327006\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs"], "git_node": "0e2d55c2dc38b83b675fac99d315468313600a9d", "git_parents": ["fe5ece00ae1c5988255eeb8d7bf1c5d9ebb57e1f"], "node": "ab3b8592d5726853a3d94eb83c84690862c00c31", "parents": ["bc85ca5d930892d7e63d9636d8e428ef145f676c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073000 - Store the surface's clipping rect in the QuadClipStack. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nThis centralizes the clipping information into the clip stack and removes the need for passing the picture context into prepare_quad functions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327007\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border_image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/box_shadow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/borders.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad_clip.rs"], "git_node": "233b58258e8861ae9ff9e0c5db15e1a3fbe19d29", "git_parents": ["0e2d55c2dc38b83b675fac99d315468313600a9d"], "node": "a37966cdbc6e4ec0c8c5d6abb556017140bd4365", "parents": ["ab3b8592d5726853a3d94eb83c84690862c00c31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073000 - Remove unused sub_rect paramer from PatternBuilder::build. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327012\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border_image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/backdrop.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/box_shadow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/cutout.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/filter.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/mix_blend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/repeat.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/yuv.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/conic.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/linear.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/radial.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "f8470ec0653c4115f921a6851f70e351664d53bd", "git_parents": ["233b58258e8861ae9ff9e0c5db15e1a3fbe19d29"], "node": "49a7648f7740c2f3b077d2366a0f794d90d4bd9d", "parents": ["a37966cdbc6e4ec0c8c5d6abb556017140bd4365"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073000: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "layout/painting/nsCSSRenderingBorders.cpp"], "git_node": "859c98ba66593cdd47fb726db64524db805e3d39", "git_parents": ["f8470ec0653c4115f921a6851f70e351664d53bd"], "node": "14bb87d138fafc511a4efae6a29a17d9e009e33f", "parents": ["49a7648f7740c2f3b077d2366a0f794d90d4bd9d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Zoya \u003czfatima@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064866 - Added voice list for player r=android-reviewers,moyin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324779\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenReducer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/fakes/Listen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/playback/PlaybackController.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/synthesis/SpeechSynthesizer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/VoiceSelection.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenReducerTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/synthesis/AndroidTtsSpeechSynthesizerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/listentopage/ListenToPageTools.kt"], "git_node": "559b46e192de19c418e700571bb91a39039fd783", "git_parents": ["859c98ba66593cdd47fb726db64524db805e3d39"], "node": "5f683fce71befb4526fc806cb981f4d277baad26", "parents": ["14bb87d138fafc511a4efae6a29a17d9e009e33f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2070956 - Let ContentClassifierPrefMirror release or hand over the content prefs it mirrors. r=emz\" for causing bustages in ContentClassifierPrefMirror.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit d994658a278538efa16535f84b4a39b61e9538e5.\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierPrefMirror.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierPrefMirror.h", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_engines_pref.js", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_pref_mirror.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "14c5bccce43e05bb24cb41053ce0ec2fa99c001f", "git_parents": ["559b46e192de19c418e700571bb91a39039fd783"], "node": "26a15c1aa85829efa5a22f24399648c26a0f6e82", "parents": ["5f683fce71befb4526fc806cb981f4d277baad26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072239 - Split mochitest and xpcshell manifest `environment` values on newlines, not whitespace. r=florian,ci-and-tooling,ahal\n\nmanifestparser joins a TOML list into a newline-separated string, so splitting\non whitespace breaks any environment variable whose value contains a space,\nsuch as a profiler thread filter list including \"DOM Worker\".\n\nAdd `manifestparser.util.split_manifest_list` and use it for both `prefs` and\n`environment` in both harnesses, so the four call sites stay consistent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326188\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/runtests.py", "testing/mozbase/manifestparser/manifestparser/util.py", "testing/mozbase/manifestparser/tests/test_util.py", "testing/xpcshell/runxpcshelltests.py", "testing/xpcshell/selftest.py"], "git_node": "745f7ff9c3df8f0ffd620d3e024f8481feb8ee13", "git_parents": ["14c5bccce43e05bb24cb41053ce0ec2fa99c001f"], "node": "f259ba17b81026e8fbbb4036f909d7924cccda60", "parents": ["26a15c1aa85829efa5a22f24399648c26a0f6e82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072239 - Profile the threads speech recognition actually runs on in its mochitests. r=media-webspeech-reviewers,alwu\n\nMOZ_PROFILER_STARTUP_FILTERS replaces the profiler's built-in thread list rather\nthan adding to it (ParseFeature() has a \"default\" pseudo-entry, thread filter\nparsing has none), so the four defaults are restated alongside ours: the graph\nand audio callback threads that capture, the content-side resampling and IPC\nthreads, and Parakeet, the utility-process loop the inference markers are\nrecorded on. Matching is case-insensitive substring, so \"Speech\" covers both\nSpeechResampler and SpeechIPC.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326189\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/browser.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/mochitest.toml"], "git_node": "ffdeb310c3e4069830871e9550b170c1eecea80a", "git_parents": ["745f7ff9c3df8f0ffd620d3e024f8481feb8ee13"], "node": "2bb4e077ee3fd87e5df687b17e12569e442f936c", "parents": ["f259ba17b81026e8fbbb4036f909d7924cccda60"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064227 Update ffvpx to ffmpeg 9.0.1 r=padenot\n\nThis commit updates local ffvpx copy to official ffmpeg 9.0.1 release with Mozilla specific changes applied.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321843\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/ffmpeg63/include/libavcodec/bsf.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/ffmpeg63/include/libavcodec/codec_id.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/ffmpeg63/include/libavcodec/version.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/ffmpeg63/include/libavutil/frame.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/ffmpeg63/include/libavutil/pixfmt.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/ffmpeg63/include/libavutil/version.h", "media/ffvpx/README_MOZILLA", "media/ffvpx/changes.patch", "media/ffvpx/config_android_x86_64.asm", "media/ffvpx/config_components_audio_only.h", "media/ffvpx/config_components_audio_video.h", "media/ffvpx/config_darwin64.asm", "media/ffvpx/config_darwin64.h", "media/ffvpx/config_unix64.asm", "media/ffvpx/config_win32.asm", "media/ffvpx/config_win64.asm", "media/ffvpx/dxva2-bind-s