DE_MESSAGE with newer assets instead of removing the message entirely, since [[ https://mozilla.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/1818?Submission+Timestamp+Date=30+day+ago+for+30+day&Message+ID=%25FX_MR_106_UPGRADE%25&Locale=&Normalized+Country+Code=&Normalized+Channel=release&Version=&Metadata+User+Agent+OS=&Branch=&Experiment= | according to Skylight ]] the message is still getting a fair amount of impressions, and the CTR is quite high (about 10%).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326010\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-static/browser_all_files_referenced.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/br-kit-with-heart.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/mr-amo-collection.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/mr-gratitude.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/mr-import.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/mr-pinprivate.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/mr-pintaskbar.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/mr-privacysegmentation.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/mr-settodefault.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/nuo-taborientation.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/jar.mn", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_multistage_mr.js", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/content-src/components/MultiSelect.test.jsx"], "git_node": "afb44409cb4f13304fb60b08647cbb1182c760bd", "git_parents": ["ebea95ef8e78821faa8ceda75655e1b4b5d58f32"], "node": "1850feb13baaf2dace699aad53f81f059996c6e3", "parents": ["84c2b127d86a54ad0285eaa6e72c848f0a5df24e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073131 - Lint all layout/ headers through clang-tidy r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nChanges includes:\n- using C++20 type aliases and inline variables\n- making deleted methods public\n- making some methods default\n- rework some include dependencies to make header self contained\n- move some implementation from header to source file to break circular\n  dependencies\n\nAll changes were detected either by header compilation failure, or by\nclang-tidy.\n\nFixes are either generated by clang-tidy or hand-made.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326978\n", "files": ["layout/base/FrameProperties.h", "layout/base/MVMContext.h", "layout/base/MotionPathUtils.h", "layout/generic/LayoutMessageUtils.h", "layout/generic/ScrollbarActivity.h", "layout/generic/TextDrawTarget.h", "layout/generic/Visibility.h", "layout/generic/WritingModes.h", "layout/inspector/ServoStyleRuleMap.h", "layout/mathml/nsIMathMLFrame.h", "layout/painting/RetainedDisplayListHelpers.h", "layout/painting/TransformClipNode.h", "layout/painting/nsDisplayItemTypes.h", "layout/style/AnimatedPropertyIDSet.h", "layout/style/CSSCounterStyleRule.h", "layout/style/CSSFontFaceRule.h", "layout/style/CachedInheritingStyles.cpp", "layout/style/CachedInheritingStyles.h", "layout/style/GeckoBindings.cpp", "layout/style/ImageLoader.h", "layout/style/PreloadedStyleSheet.h", "layout/style/ServoComputedData.h", "layout/style/ServoTraversalStatistics.h", "layout/style/ShadowParts.cpp", "layout/style/TimelineManager.h", "layout/style/nsCSSPropertyIDSet.h", "layout/style/nsStyleChangeList.h", "layout/style/nsStyleStructFwd.h", "layout/style/nsStyleUtil.h"], "git_node": "f3b24211666e7f8dab054334d29c168a319bf48c", "git_parents": ["afb44409cb4f13304fb60b08647cbb1182c760bd"], "node": "b0a815034cbba5d919093c5300542ace62f7d0c5", "parents": ["1850feb13baaf2dace699aad53f81f059996c6e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071547 - Rename the jj split and reorganize skills to stack-split-commit and stack-reorganize. r=padenot DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325967\n", "files": [".agents/skills/stack-reorganize-jj/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/stack-reorganize/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/stack-split-commit/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/stack-split-jj/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize-jj/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/stack-split-commit/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/stack-split-jj/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "cfe818bc4b622b90be84f12e9fd4c51cf9b95eeb", "git_parents": ["f3b24211666e7f8dab054334d29c168a319bf48c"], "node": "98ce9318e04f45ec7bd3eb12abd0d5b5674524b3", "parents": ["b0a815034cbba5d919093c5300542ace62f7d0c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071547 - Give stack-reorganize back the patch-series guidance the doc move removed. r=padenot DONTBUILD\n\nD325592 moved this prose into docs/contributing/reviewable-patch-series.md and left the skill citing the doc, but the skill acts on what it moved: it reaches into the doc for \"Multiple bugs\" by name, and its jj mechanics use \"land-early nuggets\" as a term only the doc defines.\n\nAuthor: mstange; the prose is his, restored unchanged apart from heading levels, so every added line appears as a removed line in D325592. The restored \"better approach\" FAQ replaces the `# The contract` paragraph, which was that same answer with its question dropped.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326923\n", "files": [".agents/skills/stack-reorganize/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "80899d321d32cc53ee54bce82ce7ab2088173c15", "git_parents": ["cfe818bc4b622b90be84f12e9fd4c51cf9b95eeb"], "node": "c82986e955227f1a2aa58af9b2be613505b81ab7", "parents": ["98ce9318e04f45ec7bd3eb12abd0d5b5674524b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071547 - Drop the trailing commas from the stack skills' allowed-tools lists. r=padenot DONTBUILD\n\nEach comma is part of the entry's string rather than YAML syntax. Claude Code splits an entry on commas outside parentheses before parsing it as a permission rule, so the grants work either way; the commits above add entries and would otherwise spread the noise.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326924\n", "files": [".agents/skills/stack-reorganize/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/stack-split-commit/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/stack-split-commit/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "c7732895cadebd130f5ef0b0ae96a3fe26349972", "git_parents": ["80899d321d32cc53ee54bce82ce7ab2088173c15"], "node": "5b61ec66e3b445f5790997add39589518c1be038", "parents": ["c82986e955227f1a2aa58af9b2be613505b81ab7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071547 - Bring stack-reorganize's restored guidance up to the doc's current wording. r=padenot DONTBUILD\n\n`# Goals` picks up the two edits the doc gained after the move, the build/lint/test clause on the third bullet and the no-forward-references bullet, so the description need no longer carry the invariant and becomes a trigger description.\n\nThe FAQ's escape hatch was scoped to cosmetic differences, which forbade what the doc's worked example presents as the best outcome, so it now covers a patch that is not in the original diff at all.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326925\n", "files": [".agents/skills/stack-reorganize/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "293f868e853dc2bbfafed20c4852d46148be5909", "git_parents": ["c7732895cadebd130f5ef0b0ae96a3fe26349972"], "node": "4da541090fa2d30d64313aae9c3ce43c23260e59", "parents": ["5b61ec66e3b445f5790997add39589518c1be038"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071547 - Make stack-split-commit cover git as well as jj. r=padenot DONTBUILD\n\nThe jj half keeps mstange's wording, and bug 2072516 carries the defects review found in it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325590\n", "files": [".agents/skills/stack-split-commit/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/stack-split-commit/references/git.md", ".agents/skills/stack-split-commit/references/jj.md", ".claude/skills/stack-split-commit/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/stack-split-commit/references/git.md", ".claude/skills/stack-split-commit/references/jj.md"], "git_node": "6cedc423195ee6f4f7494462e22aa661ab82faad", "git_parents": ["293f868e853dc2bbfafed20c4852d46148be5909"], "node": "a66e155dfc395c9cbd3bb50bf20dd280490ad79b", "parents": ["4da541090fa2d30d64313aae9c3ce43c23260e59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071547 - Make stack-reorganize cover git as well as jj. r=padenot DONTBUILD\n\nThe jj half keeps mstange's wording, and bug 2072516 carries the defects review found in it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325591\n", "files": [".agents/skills/stack-reorganize/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/stack-reorganize/references/drop-superseded.md", ".agents/skills/stack-reorganize/references/fold-resplit.md", ".agents/skills/stack-reorganize/references/git.md", ".agents/skills/stack-reorganize/references/jj.md", ".agents/skills/stack-reorganize/scripts/git-churn.sh", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize/references/drop-superseded.md", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize/references/fold-resplit.md", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize/references/git.md", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize/references/jj.md", ".claude/skills/stack-reorganize/scripts/git-churn.sh"], "git_node": "9a2505e69fbeeccfda43b739fcdb7018ea5f4983", "git_parents": ["6cedc423195ee6f4f7494462e22aa661ab82faad"], "node": "3704ca95e8b06a93f246e8bcd1c660e587fc8c90", "parents": ["a66e155dfc395c9cbd3bb50bf20dd280490ad79b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071407 - Widgets 4x4 ad: Add the widgets-ad-large page layout variant. r=ini\n\nAdds the variant value for the experiment that puts a sponsored card in one large cell of the widgets row, plus the pref and metric descriptions and an entry in the devtools layout picker. Selecting it renders nothing yet.\n\nAlso lists auto-minimize-widgets in the metric description, which was missing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326267\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/PageLayoutVariants.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/common/PageLayoutVariants.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.test.jsx"], "git_node": "a07b42e65b78331ed6a491166606adcd0dd59a71", "git_parents": ["9a2505e69fbeeccfda43b739fcdb7018ea5f4983"], "node": "96ad371e380cce7a23c18e80b7456ddd35324f15", "parents": ["3704ca95e8b06a93f246e8bcd1c660e587fc8c90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071410 - Widgets 4x4 ad: Show a sponsored card in the widgets row. r=ini\n\nBehind the widgets-ad-large page layout variant, the widgets row gives its last slot to a sponsored card, to the design on HNT-3082.\n\nThe card is the first ad off the existing Stories set, so the Stories fill drops that exact object and every story ad shifts up one. Both sides call selectWidgetsRowAd so they cannot disagree about which ad the row took. Ads preferred this to a dedicated placement.\n\nPlacement is by grid-column per container width, which makes widgets flow around the ad rather than push it off the end. The column follows the last widget rather than sitting at a fixed slot, so a row holding fewer widgets than it has room for does not leave a gap before the card. One card column stacks everything, so the spot comes from the markup instead. A drag preview puts an inline order on every widget that would beat a stylesheet one, so the card renders after whichever widget the preview shows first.\n\nRendering reuses DSCard and nova-section-card-medium. The card forwards attribution and is_ad_eligible_position, without which NewTabAttributionFeed reports no view or click. The cell never drags, resizes or shows up in the customize panel.\n\nThe impression event is built from the tile fields only, so it carries no source. What separates the row's ad from a story ad is pos 0 with no section, alongside the page layout variant the session reports. Story ads cannot collide, since their positions default to 1, 5, 7, 11, 18 and 20. There is no half-height sponsored card yet, so a minimized row holding this one keeps the large card's height.\n\nKeyboard order does not match visual order for the card from three card columns up, and from two when small widgets sit ahead of it. Accessibility triaged that S3 and it is tracked in bug 2072338.\n\nValidation: mach format, mach lint, stylelint and 4010 jest pass. Checked in a local build against live sponsored content, including the one card column drag and the about:home startup cache path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326268\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/PageLayoutVariants.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/DSCard/_DSCard.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsRowAd.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/_WidgetsRowAd.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/useWidgetDnD.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/lib/selectLayoutRender.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/activity-stream.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsRowAd.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/lib/selectLayoutRender.test.js"], "git_node": "cc492dcf157bf5578458324c6d3bdaafdaa4d130", "git_parents": ["a07b42e65b78331ed6a491166606adcd0dd59a71"], "node": "c3ce8ebb0866b67b5d7ed00a71f9e287006834bf", "parents": ["96ad371e380cce7a23c18e80b7456ddd35324f15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2023234 - Write a skill about committing. r=smaug,ai4dev-reviewers,marco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D287624\n", "files": [".agents/skills/firefox-commits/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/firefox-commits/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "2c4b3e789cd6af526039c1e43e15df7434dbb076", "git_parents": ["cc492dcf157bf5578458324c6d3bdaafdaa4d130"], "node": "28c4468536931f4b437f0a5eebf05dd2f4ffb409", "parents": ["c3ce8ebb0866b67b5d7ed00a71f9e287006834bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071615 - Update Android SDK Command-line Tools to version 23.0. r=android-reviewers,tthibaud\n\nStarting with this release, Google publishes the macOS archive per CPU architecture (mac_arm64 and mac_x86_64)\ninstead of a single mac one.\n\nIts sdkmanager is a shell wrapper around a new, no longer Java-based \"Android CLI\" tool that ignores the\n-Dos.arch JVM property the old sdkmanager used to pick the CPU architecture when cross-installing macOS/arm64\npackages from a Linux/x86_64 host. Its wrapper forwards REPO_OS_OVERRIDE straight through as its own\n--platform=\u003cos\u003e_\u003carch\u003e flag once the value already contains an underscore, so switch the macOS SDK repack to\nthat.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325618\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/android-sdk.configure", "python/mozboot/mozboot/android.py", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/repack-android-sdk-macos.sh"], "git_node": "ff621ca0c9b91c031e44f94f24676ff0b4d47a73", "git_parents": ["2c4b3e789cd6af526039c1e43e15df7434dbb076"], "node": "c52da277785ea47adf784013c36b5ae667666f49", "parents": ["28c4468536931f4b437f0a5eebf05dd2f4ffb409"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071615 - Compile with Android SDK 37.2. r=android-reviewers,tthibaud\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325619\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/android-sdk.configure", "mobile/android/android-components/.config.yml", "python/mozboot/mozboot/android-packages.txt", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/android.py"], "git_node": "c26823778771dcb1e7ba4f984499ad667aaacb9a", "git_parents": ["ff621ca0c9b91c031e44f94f24676ff0b4d47a73"], "node": "2a62ce7f9ec36e37d112bf952bb5a621d40b4747", "parents": ["c52da277785ea47adf784013c36b5ae667666f49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071615 - Register CarUxRestrictionsManager's listener with a UI context. r=android-reviewers,joberhauser\n\nregisterListener, unregisterListener, and the context-less getCurrentCarUxRestrictions are deprecated as of\nAndroid SDK 37.2 in favor of *ForUiContext variants that take an application Context and, for registration, an\nExecutor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325620\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/automotive/CarUxRestrictionsFeature.kt"], "git_node": "57181436c492e6174a0c3b2314b03f91a0f862a5", "git_parents": ["c26823778771dcb1e7ba4f984499ad667aaacb9a"], "node": "442b38897efb974802cedd37459c5003b6548f00", "parents": ["2a62ce7f9ec36e37d112bf952bb5a621d40b4747"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071616 - Update NDK to r30. r=android-reviewers,tcampbell\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325621\n", "files": ["python/mozboot/mozboot/android.py"], "git_node": "fcd90d6b75314b735daf882393d2d5b955839f96", "git_parents": ["57181436c492e6174a0c3b2314b03f91a0f862a5"], "node": "533adec520edd344974d4252cd43dc6d5d7070fa", "parents": ["442b38897efb974802cedd37459c5003b6548f00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anna Kulyk \u003cakulyk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072756 - Fix moz-toggle colors in HCM with Nova enabled r=desktop-theme-reviewers,reusable-components-reviewers,mstriemer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327238\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/moz-toggle/moz-toggle.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-toggle/moz-toggle.tokens.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-toggle/moz-toggle.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/nova/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs"], "git_node": "4f3f17b6c355962e97c5408379db775b7a4bb07f", "git_parents": ["fcd90d6b75314b735daf882393d2d5b955839f96"], "node": "23d7dd014453ca122b12cd5432a24dafffdcb0b5", "parents": ["533adec520edd344974d4252cd43dc6d5d7070fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072791 - Rename about:aitab to about:smartpage r=echa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327047\n", "files": ["browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/about/AboutRedirector.cpp", "browser/components/about/components.conf", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AITabChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AITabParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-page.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_actions.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_blocks.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_page.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_store_integration.js"], "git_node": "586322b871b68bd8ceb0cdf280eb7ec5b93759f1", "git_parents": ["4f3f17b6c355962e97c5408379db775b7a4bb07f"], "node": "2f6c87ec87d929060d9c4c8a4ea5d04bb658b386", "parents": ["23d7dd014453ca122b12cd5432a24dafffdcb0b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "scottdowne \u003csdowne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068165 - Newtab fixing spaces stories opt in bug r=ini\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326705\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PrefsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/PrefsFeed.test.js"], "git_node": "c85b428ffd2b4783833fcfeef5d1e2ee8f301eaf", "git_parents": ["586322b871b68bd8ceb0cdf280eb7ec5b93759f1"], "node": "0f4a649269357319d2d0152409e963c8e3f688e7", "parents": ["2f6c87ec87d929060d9c4c8a4ea5d04bb658b386"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073525 - Add UITour.showHome() to navigate to about:home with optional hash r=nbarrett\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327381\n", "files": ["browser/components/uitour/UITour-lib.js", "browser/components/uitour/UITour.sys.mjs", "browser/components/uitour/test/browser_UITour_showNewTab.js"], "git_node": "bd3a2ae4b9e14bb9718e368ad3e1352023ef8a38", "git_parents": ["c85b428ffd2b4783833fcfeef5d1e2ee8f301eaf"], "node": "4f41a545d951a45ebe8bc6f23a48132f3b583526", "parents": ["0f4a649269357319d2d0152409e963c8e3f688e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Meridel Walkington \u003cmwalkington@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071926 - Use sentence case for the Edit controls customize toolbar label. r=flod,fluent-reviewers\n\nThe label for the combined Cut/Copy/Paste toolbar item (\"edit-controls\"),\nshown in Customize Toolbar mode, is Title Case (\"Edit Controls\"). This is\ninconsistent with Firefox's sentence-case convention for desktop UI labels,\nand with the same widget's own tooltip, which already reads \"Edit controls\".\n\nbrowser/locales/en-US/chrome/browser/customizableui/customizableWidgets.properties:\n  edit-controls.label: \"Edit Controls\" -\u003e \"Edit controls\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327391\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/chrome/browser/customizableui/customizableWidgets.properties"], "git_node": "e6094eb4aceb08586d3510a8b8c346d2eb3b7b1d", "git_parents": ["bd3a2ae4b9e14bb9718e368ad3e1352023ef8a38"], "node": "c9859db9320b3f844a47fe59378482dfc2e98d3a", "parents": ["4f41a545d951a45ebe8bc6f23a48132f3b583526"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073526 - Implicitly enable browser.urlbar.unifiedSearchButton.always for search bars. r=daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327384\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_searchModeSwitcher.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchModeSwitcher.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchbarOverflow.js", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "c1f58bf46b01a2259020e362fa53c59459eb3531", "git_parents": ["e6094eb4aceb08586d3510a8b8c346d2eb3b7b1d"], "node": "fa1324495c075c7d63b8d99ffeca371b74ca06a4", "parents": ["c9859db9320b3f844a47fe59378482dfc2e98d3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1456885 - Rename SpeechGrammarList.addFromURI to SpeechGrammarList.addFromUri to match Chrome r=webidl,media-webspeech-reviewers,pehrsons,smaug\n\nThis is an inert interface that exist solely for web compat, and it\ndoesn't do anything to the Speech Recognition process.\n\nWe don't need to implement it for Web Compat. I have implemented some\nbits of the rest of the interface so it returns things that are\nmeaningful, but that is apparently not needed either. We might be able\nto remove that when we're a bit more confident.\n\nBecause of the wrong capitalization, it was not found, breaking Google\nDocs. I also removed exception throwing that weren't necessary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326946\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechGrammar.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechGrammar.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechGrammarList.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechGrammarList.h", "dom/webidl/SpeechGrammar.webidl", "dom/webidl/SpeechGrammarList.webidl", "testing/web-platform/meta/speech-api/idlharness.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/speech-api.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/speech-api/idlharness.https.window.js"], "git_node": "ccfc862609a4b6c2253c27c1e16339f2a5578d37", "git_parents": ["c1f58bf46b01a2259020e362fa53c59459eb3531"], "node": "531ceb0e2c764d9c57195faa6a62a7f7d1cbab7c", "parents": ["fa1324495c075c7d63b8d99ffeca371b74ca06a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olivia Hall \u003cohall@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068644 - Hoist the PDF signature state out of the overlay composables r=android-reviewers,pollymce\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326599\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/pdf/PdfToolsIntegration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/pdf/SignatureActions.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/pdf/ui/PdfOverlayContent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/pdf/PdfToolsContentTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/pdf/PdfToolsIntegrationTest.kt"], "git_node": "5f18b5a4f84ad65bd5ccb0f8ce5c6daeab4c3aeb", "git_parents": ["ccfc862609a4b6c2253c27c1e16339f2a5578d37"], "node": "3cbab13dab004787739e538950194eb1e6235d8a", "parents": ["531ceb0e2c764d9c57195faa6a62a7f7d1cbab7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "yazan \u003cyalmacki@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072363 - Anchor corner_image to the card outside the fullscreen layout, and add direction-relative positions. r=mimi,omc-reviewers\n\ncorner_image only rendered for 'position: \"center-large\"' with 'fullscreen', and\npositioned against 'main.screen', so it was unusable on a regular Spotlight\ncard. It now renders inside '.section-main' for every other layout, so the\noffsets resolve against the card, and '.brand-logo' is blockified there to drop\nthe baseline gap that kept it off the edge. The fullscreen layout is unchanged.\n\nAdds 'bottom-start' / 'bottom-end' / 'top-start' / 'top-end', which resolve to a\nphysical corner from the text direction, and and 'rtl' block on 'corner_image'\n(and 'logo' for consistency) for right-to-left image URLs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326286\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.bundle.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_configurable_ui.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/MultiStageProtonScreen.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.bundle.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/content-src/components/MultiStageAWProton.test.jsx", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/MultiStageProtonScreenSchemas/MultiStageProtonScreenSchemas.json"], "git_node": "133075a3169f34c7daa16daf742868b5f6d26212", "git_parents": ["5f18b5a4f84ad65bd5ccb0f8ce5c6daeab4c3aeb"], "node": "430f806d9a84396ff565dfbec9475d2708ccb28f", "parents": ["3cbab13dab004787739e538950194eb1e6235d8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vanessa Prema \u003cvprema@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063407 - feat(pbw): add private window basics educational spotlight to private browsing r=desktop-theme-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,omc-reviewers,tgiles,bolsson,emcminn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322679\n", "files": ["browser/actors/AboutPrivateBrowsingChild.sys.mjs", "browser/actors/AboutPrivateBrowsingParent.sys.mjs", "browser/base/content/spotlight.html", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.bundle.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/MultiStageProtonScreen.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/TileList.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.bundle.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.html", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.js", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/test/browser/browser_privatebrowsing_about_default_pin_promo.js", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/test/browser/browser_privatebrowsing_about_kit_intro.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aboutPrivateBrowsing.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/privatebrowsing/aboutPrivateBrowsing.css", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/MultiStageProtonScreenSchemas/MultiStageProtonScreenSchemas.json", "toolkit/modules/RemotePageAccessManager.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "361ead4a7cc6914769615ff2c31bb5266366ee91", "git_parents": ["133075a3169f34c7daa16daf742868b5f6d26212"], "node": "dbfd29b9651ec5db9495b52c61d71f321b4889ee", "parents": ["430f806d9a84396ff565dfbec9475d2708ccb28f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vasish Baungally \u003cvbaungally@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073203 -  Add observer on document instead of documentElement in Smart Form Fill. r=omarg,mshillabeer\n\nSmart Form Fill observes documentElement, so a page that replaces it leaves the\nobserver on a detached tree: the form is pruned and the row never appears again.\nObserving the document, which is documentElement's parent, makes the replacement\nan observed mutation, so the new fields get picked up.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327122\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillDocument.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartformfill_mutations.js"], "git_node": "7bd124e46b25bfab76d7b4cc5b639b3e6b729aed", "git_parents": ["361ead4a7cc6914769615ff2c31bb5266366ee91"], "node": "d77804feccb948725f1cdf47031e9a5408a79228", "parents": ["dbfd29b9651ec5db9495b52c61d71f321b4889ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris DuPuis \u003ccdupuis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037979 - Improve logging of updater invocation scenarios r=application-update-reviewers,aborondo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321713\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/maintenanceservice/workmonitor.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/UpdateService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/elevation_type.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/elevation_type.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatecommon.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatecommon.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updater_invocation.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updater_invocation.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/gtest/ElevationTypeTests.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/gtest/README.md", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/gtest/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "ba9ef43e140ebe55daa2501dd3602020dbe41c4b", "git_parents": ["7bd124e46b25bfab76d7b4cc5b639b3e6b729aed"], "node": "f09ea267c49d3855ba25bb8830a325e033380cfa", "parents": ["d77804feccb948725f1cdf47031e9a5408a79228"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073403 - Show module reviewer groups before Herald reviewers in mach file-info reviewers r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,marco DONTBUILD\n\nThe mots.yaml module reviewer groups are the more useful suggestion to act\non, since Herald adds its own reviewers by itself once the patch is\nsubmitted, so print them first in both the plain and the JSON output.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327389\n", "files": ["docs/contributing/reviews.md", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "aa42856bc1279fb533d2494bc29a8d76f2668826", "git_parents": ["ba9ef43e140ebe55daa2501dd3602020dbe41c4b"], "node": "37a0535d7af42348de6a0acadb536977fbe830a7", "parents": ["f09ea267c49d3855ba25bb8830a325e033380cfa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073555 - Name only the first PMyManager.ipdl include r=ipc-reviewers,mccr8 DONTBUILD\n\nThe IPDL page includes the file twice, once in the protocol overview and\nonce in the actor implementation walkthrough, and both claimed the same\ntarget name, which docutils rejects as a duplicate. Nothing references the\nname, so keep it on the first include only.\n\nDrop the allowed warning, which now matches nothing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327417\n", "files": ["docs/config.yml", "ipc/docs/ipdl.md"], "git_node": "c73a4a46693ebc0861407e3b8d9912340edac434", "git_parents": ["aa42856bc1279fb533d2494bc29a8d76f2668826"], "node": "b9d5e8555633bf0d498d8334eb7af4394c64774e", "parents": ["37a0535d7af42348de6a0acadb536977fbe830a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070956 - Let ContentClassifierPrefMirror release or hand over the content prefs it mirrors. r=emz\n\nThis patch replaces the boolean mirror pref with a mode pref. The mode\npref supports three modes:\n  0 (Off): The default mode. The mirror is off and clear mirrored prefs\n  1 (On): The mirror is on to mirror the prefs\n  2 (Handover): The mirror stop mirroring the prefs and don't clear\n                them.\nThis behavior supports rolling back from the mirror state, and allow\nhanding over the mirrored prefs once we no longer need mirroring.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325068\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierPrefMirror.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierPrefMirror.h", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_engines_pref.js", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_pref_mirror.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "e95b1d6c06d75cd5535436c133e527a24b454767", "git_parents": ["c73a4a46693ebc0861407e3b8d9912340edac434"], "node": "5d7d5c02dca23d6642ffb2887aa1c252e761aa31", "parents": ["b9d5e8555633bf0d498d8334eb7af4394c64774e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073555 - Drop the stray tag text under SUGGEST_PREFS's @type r=urlbar-reviewers,Standard8 DONTBUILD\n\n`{object} defaultValues` is a leftover from a tag that is no longer\nthere: the properties it names are documented on the SuggestPrefsRecord\ntypedef above. jsdoc reads it as a description on @type, which that tag\ndoes not permit.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327408\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/QuickSuggest.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "830c8a6ab34dafa62688081d93dc443fbda61441", "git_parents": ["e95b1d6c06d75cd5535436c133e527a24b454767"], "node": "d0d9052e7c261edb6974c07571fa8533f1f33eef", "parents": ["5d7d5c02dca23d6642ffb2887aa1c252e761aa31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073555 - Give L10nCachedMessage a type so jsdoc stops reading one out of its prose r=urlbar-reviewers,Standard8 DONTBUILD\n\njsdoc takes a tag's type expression from the first `{` in the tag's text\nwhatever that text is. The typedef was written without one, so the `{\nvalue: ..., attributes: ... }` in its worked example was parsed as the\ntype and logged a build ERROR. Naming the type puts the right braces\nfirst.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327407\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/L10nCache.mjs"], "git_node": "c8da360d569352716c5858f2f6f59a393facf032", "git_parents": ["830c8a6ab34dafa62688081d93dc443fbda61441"], "node": "a4b0cf94815817665ea2bbc8e1d8ff12d1e2cf49", "parents": ["d0d9052e7c261edb6974c07571fa8533f1f33eef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1931724 - Allow ZenUML diagrams in the source docs. r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nThe plugin loads only on a page that has a zenuml block, so every other page is unchanged. In custom_theme.css, a zenuml block takes the column width where the other diagram types are content-sized, because ZenUML measures its diagram against the box it is given, and the dark scheme inverts the diagram, because the plugin ignores mermaid's theme.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327395\n", "files": ["docs/_static/custom_theme.css", "docs/conf.py", "tools/moztreedocs/docs/mermaid-integration.md"], "git_node": "ec2b8bd7fd5a17f353c5c306cf6729eeebc728bd", "git_parents": ["c8da360d569352716c5858f2f6f59a393facf032"], "node": "82963cd4c5dfebe68890aba98b540749d772219b", "parents": ["a4b0cf94815817665ea2bbc8e1d8ff12d1e2cf49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073571 - Let a ZenUML diagram wider than the docs column scroll like the other diagram types. r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327429\n", "files": ["docs/_static/custom_theme.css"], "git_node": "4981ac1ebe4cf5bf7f5c5f3761f7a1eb8b496fc0", "git_parents": ["ec2b8bd7fd5a17f353c5c306cf6729eeebc728bd"], "node": "26a89be9673e02f77a54cbffce1a656546ea01e1", "parents": ["82963cd4c5dfebe68890aba98b540749d772219b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073332 - Stop exporting WidgetPinnedReceiver. r=android-reviewers,adhingra\n\nThe receiver is only reached through its own explicit PendingIntent, and nothing sends the action its\nintent-filter declared.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327209\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml"], "git_node": "203ab6c28773a7149efb877bdf13bdb076e192fe", "git_parents": ["4981ac1ebe4cf5bf7f5c5f3761f7a1eb8b496fc0"], "node": "5dfa691d3ff8d9a167033f9a0882faabbee02b54", "parents": ["26a89be9673e02f77a54cbffce1a656546ea01e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073332 - Fix the ContentDescription lint findings. r=android-reviewers,adhingra\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327210\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/toolbar/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/toolbar/src/main/res/layout/mozac_browser_toolbar_displaytoolbar.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/browser/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/browser/src/main/res/layout/fragment_browser.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/browser/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/sign_in_preference.xml"], "git_node": "2327e429a76f375bc36d2d87adc44fc44a4c36f0", "git_parents": ["203ab6c28773a7149efb877bdf13bdb076e192fe"], "node": "63efe7689ef0b1d5667ec981c31dda23dfa0b40b", "parents": ["5dfa691d3ff8d9a167033f9a0882faabbee02b54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073332 - Suppress DataExtractionRules in the samples that disable backups. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327211\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/samples/compose-browser/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/compose-browser/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/dataprotect/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/dataprotect/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml"], "git_node": "cb9f692a90703ec5d05c22f4b170e763763fab57", "git_parents": ["2327e429a76f375bc36d2d87adc44fc44a4c36f0"], "node": "b96498ebfb032ad2896147cde2963e0d76140f60", "parents": ["63efe7689ef0b1d5667ec981c31dda23dfa0b40b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073332 - Dispatch DiffUtil updates from the Focus domain list adapters. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nBoth lists reload from storage on every change; a diff lets the RecyclerView animate the rows that changed\ninstead of reb