al Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326032\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/list-rule-eagerness-conservative-pointerdown-preventdefault.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/list-rule-eagerness-conservative-pointerdown.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/list-rule-eagerness-moderate-hover.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/resources/utils.sub.js"], "git_node": "1934478e3cae790aece732551c3366667fd1f916", "git_parents": ["f2155e16caee61342fef1d98f5d3bcb677955ed6"], "node": "a699860dd728ee3833ab5a4c33ec21d7000e7a25", "parents": ["66aeadf05069b04bc759e3c40b5feb965f79515f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Vandolder \u003cavandolder@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071501 - Fire eager speculation rules on hover after a shorter timeout then moderate. r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326608\n", "files": ["dom/base/SpeculationRules.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.h", "dom/base/test/browser.toml", "dom/base/test/browser_speculation_rules_hover_delays.js", "dom/base/test/file_speculation_rules_hover_source.html", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/list-rule-eagerness-eager-hover.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "49008f12963ac58a97f4e95aeec69df9adde1104", "git_parents": ["1934478e3cae790aece732551c3366667fd1f916"], "node": "70a30f4968982ea1fadcc6e67391d4c1cf507a09", "parents": ["a699860dd728ee3833ab5a4c33ec21d7000e7a25"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073555 - Spell the one-line @type comments over several lines r=extension-reviewers,robwu DONTBUILD\n\njsdoc only recognizes a tag at the start of a line, so in\n`/** @type {T} Some prose. */` the prose is a description on @type,\nwhich that tag does not permit, and it is dropped. Unlike the multi-line\nform this cannot be fixed in the jsdoc plugin, because moving the prose\nwould mean adding lines and renumbering the file.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327410\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/ConduitsParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/Extension.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/ExtensionContent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/ExtensionParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d1ddf42fc56bfb018a955dfcde617e3557dff2af", "git_parents": ["49008f12963ac58a97f4e95aeec69df9adde1104"], "node": "f330f0502d4f56d5b264e94fe5a199291c598e9b", "parents": ["70a30f4968982ea1fadcc6e67391d4c1cf507a09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073555 - Spell lastBackupDate's one-line @type comment over several lines r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,Gijs DONTBUILD\n\njsdoc only recognizes a tag at the start of a line, so in\n`/** @type {T} Some prose. */` the prose is a description on @type,\nwhich that tag does not permit, and it is dropped.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327411\n", "files": ["browser/components/backup/BackupService.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "3f03e46c8697d03a7f42099de5bb9a105b2a31d8", "git_parents": ["d1ddf42fc56bfb018a955dfcde617e3557dff2af"], "node": "b93ad421db87829ffe2b1c632c8960aca179b251", "parents": ["f330f0502d4f56d5b264e94fe5a199291c598e9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Smagin Ivan \u003csmag.vav@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1987276 - Add test for unknown content dialog for unknown MIME type without extension. r=Gijs\n\nAdded a browser-chrome test in toolkit/mozapps/downloads/tests/browser/ that verifies the unknownContentType dialog appears when downloading a file with an unknown MIME type (application/x-unknown-test) and no file extension.\nThe test enables browser.download.always_ask_before_handling_new_types, serves the file via a local HTTP server, waits for the dialog, cancels it, and asserts that no download was created.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326881\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/downloads/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/downloads/tests/browser/browser_unknownContentType_openwith.js"], "git_node": "9572bb388f47b38a9736fc96e891c759e7942e49", "git_parents": ["3f03e46c8697d03a7f42099de5bb9a105b2a31d8"], "node": "87697687c5c6ce63f2068c2a0d98996ad29e91ea", "parents": ["b93ad421db87829ffe2b1c632c8960aca179b251"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073465 - Tweak font-size quantization to prefer snapping to integer appUnit sizes. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327426\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/firefox-bug-2073465-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/firefox-bug-2073465.html"], "git_node": "1056773d7e9917a214ae88a257c43c5d162234f9", "git_parents": ["9572bb388f47b38a9736fc96e891c759e7942e49"], "node": "ef2b00251f8ec92fc2fd4dc78535d8c6f61e6cba", "parents": ["87697687c5c6ce63f2068c2a0d98996ad29e91ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072852 - [ots] Reject CFF fonts where a charstring tries to execute an excessive number of operations. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327310\n", "files": ["gfx/ots/src/cff_charstring.cc", "gfx/ots/src/cff_charstring.h"], "git_node": "b6e02c8b0600b7ff6cab863012702dd673f1465f", "git_parents": ["1056773d7e9917a214ae88a257c43c5d162234f9"], "node": "f6ad3c778ea462bf6c740cbee355ada23ba7e834", "parents": ["ef2b00251f8ec92fc2fd4dc78535d