l collided with the one the NSS API structure extract defines, and\nsecurity/nss/doc is mirrored from upstream NSS, so rename this side. The\nheading keeps the anchor myst_heading_anchors generates for it, and the\nonly reference to the label is in this same document.\n\nDrop the allowed warning, which now matches nothing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327416\n", "files": ["docs/code-quality/coding-style/coding_style_cpp.md", "docs/config.yml"], "git_node": "b80d6ee2ac7bc52a323bd4fbafc251bf0a454432", "git_parents": ["c2709488f25cc8dc36064464826a858bb74733e4"], "node": "4ddc0559e921dccc8770fd927c69d888443510b2", "parents": ["0e2dae329fe416f2e605ef6f5de6ef485d2cf40f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073555 - Move #previousEngineChangedEvent's description above its @type r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,search-reviewers,mcheang,ahal DONTBUILD\n\njsdoc reads a doclet's description from the text before its first tag, so\nprose written under @type is discarded with a warning rather than\nrendered.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327409\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/search/SearchService.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f046692d3bc93a7ff476f0cdb3ef153208ca0533", "git_parents": ["b80d6ee2ac7bc52a323bd4fbafc251bf0a454432"], "node": "7e1e2b4eee00ba338db812382c6b25c09a9cbcc8", "parents": ["4ddc0559e921dccc8770fd927c69d888443510b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070254 - Fix broken redirect for the Tab Unloading docs link on about:unloads r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327022\n", "files": ["docs/config.yml"], "git_node": "de980af5229f910a5246d3685b6b3c9a747e4979", "git_parents": ["f046692d3bc93a7ff476f0cdb3ef153208ca0533"], "node": "9f5a72e13344495f78322922641adcb4900db094", "parents": ["7e1e2b4eee00ba338db812382c6b25c09a9cbcc8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073555 - Document MozHttpd and MozconfigLoader once each r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\nThe mozhttpd page runs automodule over the module and then autoclass over\nMozHttpd, which the automodule already emitted, and the mozconfigs page\ndocuments MozconfigLoader that the generated python/mozbuild pages also\ncover. Mark the redundant descriptions no-index so only one of each owns\nthe cross-reference target.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327406\n", "files": ["build/docs/mozconfigs.md", "testing/mozbase/docs/mozhttpd.md"], "git_node": "63e739831053153c81782b35f6412babf4b9ebae", "git_parents": ["de980af5229f910a5246d3685b6b3c9a747e4979"], "node": "42d59310ed7258f8f27170b258e5fc9d3be4ee32", "parents": ["9f5a72e13344495f78322922641adcb4900db094"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073200 r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327546\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/ImageBridgeParent.cpp"], "git_node": "186cfaa80deb85b662a2b9cbedeb1575ca079c2e", "git_parents": ["63e739831053153c81782b35f6412babf4b9ebae"], "node": "f1f4e9e456638e49fc4545e1bef4c8166a00998f", "parents": ["42d59310ed7258f8f27170b258e5fc9d3be4ee32"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072852 - [ots] Reject CFF fonts where a charstring tries to execute an excessive number of operations. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327310\n", "files": ["gfx/ots/moz.yaml", "gfx/ots/ots-cff-charstring-ops-limit.patch", "gfx/ots/src/cff_charstring.cc", "gfx/ots/src/cff_charstring.h"], "git_node": "9e4a75f7cc911258416db670634831839dba282f", "git_parents": ["186cfaa80deb85b662a2b9cbedeb1575ca079c2e"], "node": "0a3b36a2cebf272f2f0892ba6fb857998566f219", "parents": ["f1f4e9e456638e49fc4545e1bef4c8166a00998f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sajid Anwar \u003csajidanwar94@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068667 - Fix text-box on scroll containers and fieldsets. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327555\n", "files": ["layout/style/res/forms.css", "layout/style/res/ua.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-fieldset-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-scroll-container-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-scroll-container-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-scroll-container-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-scroll-container-004.html"], "git_node": "b913687dcbef9dff0349d151d86f9606e856c34a", "git_parents": ["9e4a75f7cc911258416db670634831839dba282f"], "node": "e2fa1dd51e77d1123c35b79ee812f202af9a0598", "parents": ["0a3b36a2cebf272f2f0892ba6fb857998566f219"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2072852 - [ots] Reject CFF fonts where a charstring tries to execute an excessive number of operations. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\" for causing lint failures\n\nThis reverts commit 9e4a75f7cc911258416db670634831839dba282f.\n", "files": ["gfx/ots/moz.yaml", "gfx/ots/ots-cff-charstring-ops-limit.patch", "gfx/ots/src/cff_charstring.cc", "gfx/ots/src/cff_charstring.h"], "git_node": "0ac9bfe94edeb3a460bad9e25c35a5c639166a24", "git_parents": ["b913687dcbef9dff0349d151d86f9606e856c34a"], "node": "8d6c66b2c3883ca9edc16d8316c85ac0059108c7", "parents": ["e2fa1dd51e77d1123c35b79ee812f202af9a0598"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789854280, "git_changesets": ["1d6fda130f63eabfe3ee159d5fcab38018e2cb84", "bb78b0e91b512d588427af8fb82acbf9e734acca", "fcd114abb7c7840937b2a87ea07f3ef8b433c65d", "80ec7cb78a24b6be706470ed85b2114db17b8070", "e61aa379b6871fafa34c69c948f21f3ff6a9aa77", "1baf415e5a200fe54c76284dfb0bfa4aabdac099", "241f6e138ed51f3e9deeb92c8999e94869111da8", "5d5fed6bc486a4dc27bd4a1cd392d864b5f8f838", "c2709488f25cc8dc36064464826a858bb74733e4", "b80d6ee2ac7bc52a323bd4fbafc251bf0a454432", "f046692d3bc93a7ff476f0cdb3ef153208ca0533", "de980af5229f910a5246d3685b6b3c9a747e4979", "63e739831053153c81782b35f6412babf4b9ebae", "186cfaa80deb85b662a2b9cbedeb1575ca079c2e", "9e4a75f7cc911258416db670634831839dba282f", "b913687dcbef9dff0349d151d86f9606e856c34a", "0ac9bfe94edeb3a460bad9e25c35a5c639166a24"], "user": "ctuns@mozilla.com"}, "45367": {"changesets": [{"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2073200 r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\" for causing assertion failures @ ImageBridgeParent.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 186cfaa80deb85b662a2b9cbedeb1575ca079c2e.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/ImageBridgeParent.cpp"], "git_node": "4452e9a17a29f762c5af6326f45c000dcf3117bb", "git_parents": ["0ac9bfe94edeb3a460bad9e25c35a5c639166a24"], "node": "8e40c4fb7992bc1a2eb4b54084d6e71b145321ac", "parents": ["8d6c66b2c3883ca9edc16d8316c85ac0059108c7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789854737, "git_changesets": ["4452e9a17a29f762c5af6326f45c000dcf3117bb"], "user": "abutkovits@mozilla.com"}, "45368": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073465 - Tweak font-size quantization to prefer snapping to integer appUnit sizes. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327426\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/firefox-bug-2073465-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/firefox-bug-2073465.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/update-subpixel-rem-unit.html"], "git_node": "afc091e0d198a533fe1ed139e726683621e73535", "git_parents": ["0ac9bfe94edeb3a460bad9e25c35a5c639166a24"], "node": "35e4bbdc21e4e99103709f9a6b12fa8b19a17438", "parents": ["8d6c66b2c3883ca9edc16d8316c85ac0059108c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073165 - Give the search mode switcher button an aria-label matching its tooltip. r=daleharvey,urlbar-reviewers,bolsson\n\nThe switcher formats the message itself and sets both attributes, so the strings stay as they are. In search mode the visible engine name and the nested close button's label used to join the name computed from content; the tooltip now drops out of the description as a duplicate of the name.\n\nBumping the three string ids and adding an .aria-label to each in the ftl, with a migration copying the title, would also work; say so if you prefer that.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327033\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchModeSwitcher.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchModeSwitcher.js"], "git_node": "99300d4a7b67967394992ca0fcac0fce69792f2c", "git_parents": ["afc091e0d198a533fe1ed139e726683621e73535"], "node": "ff216d820174cb27da9501d42aa3bd16370249bc", "parents": ["35e4bbdc21e4e99103709f9a6b12fa8b19a17438"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2073200 r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\" for causing assertion failures @ ImageBridgeParent.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 186cfaa80deb85b662a2b9cbedeb1575ca079c2e.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/ImageBridgeParent.cpp"], "git_node": "ce46923f684cea3f0cfb3ea602ec1c6cdddfe1e0", "git_parents": ["99300d4a7b67967394992ca0fcac0fce69792f2c"], "node": "d2059835e40daa480295e0c672a55a9fe96c0002", "parents": ["ff216d820174cb27da9501d42aa3bd16370249bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073756 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to 2a1973ad219a6fb0be226458512d73663b649fab r=release-managers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327565\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "eb3aee41f0f338517d0cd090b1443abc008da6dd", "git_parents": ["ce46923f684cea3f0cfb3ea602ec1c6cdddfe1e0"], "node": "62f07e8b55d5bc6099a1ee44064953958f64636d", "parents": ["d2059835e40daa480295e0c672a55a9fe96c0002"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072448 - Fix PatternT::IsWeak() to compare against the correct type. r=gfx-reviewers,tnikkel\n\ndecltype(*this) inside a const method is actually const Foo&, instead of just Foo.\nThis caused IsWeak to always return false. Fix it to use the correct comparison of\nis_same\u003cdecltype(this), const Weak*\u003e.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327559\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/2D.h"], "git_node": "cae1f0c18d3bbe13b35584c958066debaed366a0", "git_parents": ["eb3aee41f0f338517d0cd090b1443abc008da6dd"], "node": "088bb563a2baf1840957c466cb75e634a4a8035e", "parents": ["62f07e8b55d5bc6099a1ee44064953958f64636d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ole Baumann \u003cgit@darkintaqt.dev\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070873 - Remove redundant level from UrlbarUtils.getBackspaceBlock's return value. r=urlbar-reviewers,jteow\n\nUrlbarUtils.getBackspaceBlock no longer returns the level of the block, because callers can already derive it from the URL. Update the JSDoc, simplify the redundant parent-controller check, and remove assertions from unit-tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327208\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarUtils_autofillBackspaceCount.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarUtils_getBackspaceBlock.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarUtils_reintegrateAutofill.js"], "git_node": "be251d73cfc1aa4f732c33f05998890c1cf4249b", "git_parents": ["cae1f0c18d3bbe13b35584c958066debaed366a0"], "node": "1485bcfeb4dd5302a28e8418681971e4624d021e", "parents": ["088bb563a2baf1840957c466cb75e634a4a8035e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teow \u003cjteow@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073155 - Add tests for SERP impressions reporting on interrupted SERP loads - r=search-reviewers,scunnane\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327311\n", "files": ["browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser.toml", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_impression_interrupted_load.js"], "git_node": "b96bafd5c5b4f2677d51abd53e8441cb7b848917", "git_parents": ["be251d73cfc1aa4f732c33f05998890c1cf4249b"], "node": "0dcb443c4fc9830dc6ed8c05de3f3a7d1578a936", "parents": ["1485bcfeb4dd5302a28e8418681971e4624d021e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073555 - Tag the nested CSS examples for a lexer that can read them r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal\n\nPygments has no support for CSS nesting, so its css lexer errors on the\nfirst @layer or @media inside a rule and Sphinx warns before retrying in\nrelaxed mode. Its scss lexer parses those, so use it for the examples that\nnest.\n\nThe ghost button example in the HCM checklist needs more than that: the\nscss lexer rejects a percentage in a value, which the color-mix() call\nthere has, so no lexer reads the whole block. Mark it as forced instead,\nwhich keeps the relaxed-mode highlighting without the warning.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327404\n", "files": ["accessible/docs/HCMCSSChecklist.md", "docs/code-quality/lint/linters/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/rules/use-paired-color-tokens.md", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/docs/README.design-tokens.stories.md"], "git_node": "b25776ffe98fc357d44601121bd74439465d8e82", "git_parents": ["b96bafd5c5b4f2677d51abd53e8441cb7b848917"], "node": "8557871b29204f6db1c28ec2ab7ba4924836671c", "parents": ["0dcb443c4fc9830dc6ed8c05de3f3a7d1578a936"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rob Wu \u003crob@robwu.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1634240 - Stop exposing non-browser windows in windows.onFocusChanged r=zombie\n\nThe extension APIs cannot do anything meaningful with windowId for\nnon-browser windows. Stop exposing them in windows.onFocusChanged, which\nis a known way to leak non-browser windowIds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D217478\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-windows.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-windows.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_windows_onFocusChanged.js"], "git_node": "775d74a844a45520bcec43eb75c6c652dd024c97", "git_parents": ["b25776ffe98fc357d44601121bd74439465d8e82"], "node": "7e8c4050bd630a396549f166ea07744bb248d4e0", "parents": ["8557871b29204f6db1c28ec2ab7ba4924836671c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073224 - Remove version 156 newtab trainhop compatibility shim for insertBrowser in BrowserTestUtils. r=dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327058\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/BrowserTestUtils/BrowserTestUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "b893b4179316362589f6ff2e39ba2df34154f3b5", "git_parents": ["775d74a844a45520bcec43eb75c6c652dd024c97"], "node": "191ae49700ecf3be927b84eeaa5e99e85303a5e6", "parents": ["7e8c4050bd630a396549f166ea07744bb248d4e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2073465 - Tweak font-size quantization to prefer snapping to integer appUnit sizes. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\" for causing failures at test_textScaleFactor_system_font.html.\n\nThis reverts commit afc091e0d198a533fe1ed139e726683621e73535.\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/firefox-bug-2073465-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/firefox-bug-2073465.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/update-subpixel-rem-unit.html"], "git_node": "e75f46fa6a6361946e5d7909aca674df164cd88d", "git_parents": ["b893b4179316362589f6ff2e39ba2df34154f3b5"], "node": "32148593be21ba38301ee74116e773a9cbd0ec8e", "parents": ["191ae49700ecf3be927b84eeaa5e99e85303a5e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2073165 - Give the search mode switcher button an aria-label matching its tooltip. r=daleharvey,urlbar-reviewers,bolsson\" for causing failures complaining about test_searchmode_switcher.\n\nThis reverts commit 99300d4a7b67967394992ca0fcac0fce69792f2c.\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchModeSwitcher.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchModeSwitcher.js"], "git_node": "eed6742555a203c3c1ca925b66528100cfe3e2ce", "git_parents": ["e75f46fa6a6361946e5d7909aca674df164cd88d"], "node": "b149ad72d8ec7ae4f1abf12bc22f38ae1b5375bc", "parents": ["32148593be21ba38301ee74116e773a9cbd0ec8e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071764 - Add missing debug-mode stackmaps for all wasm traps except Trap::IndirectCallBadSig and Trap::StackOverflow.  r=yury.\n\nBug 2049604, bug 2067169 and bug 2067174 add missing debug-mode stackmaps for\nthe majority of traps that get created in practice. This patch adds stackmaps\nfor all the remaining traps (in baseline compilation) except for\nTrap::IndirectCallBadSig and Trap::StackOverflow. The latter occur in function\nprologues and may require special handling in stackmap construction, hence are\nleft for future work.\n\nChanges:\n\n* The core change: MacroAssembler::{wasmCallIndirect, wasmReturnCallIndirect}\n  now return a FaultingCodeRange describing the trapping insn they might\n  create ..\n\n* .. and BaseCompiler::callIndirect uses the returned FaultingCodeRange to\n  create and register a stackmap, as required.\n\nAll the remaining changes support the above:\n\n* MacroAssembler::masm.loadWasmPinnedRegsFromInstance, which is called from\n  MacroAssembler::{wasmCallIndirect, wasmReturnCallIndirect}, has been split\n  into two variants: one that takes a TrapSite, and one that doesn't.  The one\n  that takes a TrapSite returns a FaultingCodeRange; the other variant doesn't.\n  This avoids having to deal with invalid FaultingCodeRanges when there's no\n  TrapSite required.\n\n  The majority of changes in the patch merely handle calls to the above.\n\n* class FaultingCodeRange: add documentation clarifying how/why an invalid\n  value may arise.\n\n* MacroAssembler::appendAndVerify: per previous point, explicitly ignore\n  attempts to register traps whose FaultingCodeRange is invalid.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325834\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmCodegenTypes.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmStacks.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmStubs.cpp"], "git_node": "8d04be6aff3dd762c4633b3e5712ae25d1ad6895", "git_parents": ["eed6742555a203c3c1ca925b66528100cfe3e2ce"], "node": "1017c018d8d12adfb2291d7bd13c621cc25f48a4", "parents": ["b149ad72d8ec7ae4f1abf12bc22f38ae1b5375bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003cr