b\nnn-NO -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\noc -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\npa-IN -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\npl -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\npt-BR -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\npt-PT -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nrm -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nro -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nru -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nsk -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nsl -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nson -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nsq -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nsr -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nsv-SE -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nta -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nte -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nth -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\ntl -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\ntr -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\ntrs -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nuk -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nur -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nuz -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nvi -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nwo -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nxh -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nzam -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nzh-CN -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\nzh-TW -\u003e 169e5b51c9250c34217af441fc231be2ac608b9b\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "791a92c301f99701a542232b0cff146704179869", "git_parents": ["9e0d97ae9afa4f38e8c55151feb7444161dbf677"], "node": "7d32c7a134dec7fc65fa92175330c0e0859d4b48", "parents": ["26b8157799ab7b7dd6c5674a93731a2dc8bb77e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "aurora \u003caurora@starsinthesky.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072275 - Remove some unused interface impls and properties in nsWebBrowser. r=mossop\n\nI mainly did this to remove the nsIWebBrowserPersist interface, which\ndoesn't seem to be used anywhere (anything that saves a document\nusually just makes a new nsWebBrowserPersist, which is exactly what\nnsWebBrowser did). That also made nsICancelable and\nnsIWebProgressListener redundant, since they don't seem to have any\neffect outside of persistence.\n\nWhile I'm here, I also noticed that a few member fields aren't actually\nused, so clean those up too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326228\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/browser/nsWebBrowser.cpp", "toolkit/components/browser/nsWebBrowser.h"], "git_node": "6b3963c4c58a8428380e267dcf7865705db4ddd0", "git_parents": ["791a92c301f99701a542232b0cff146704179869"], "node": "9138be030f748418f04694ba99b7a62d8300a536", "parents": ["7d32c7a134dec7fc65fa92175330c0e0859d4b48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072795 - Don't start a picture cache slice at a scroll root with no scrollable range or below the minimum scroll root size. r=gw\n\nunderlay-mask-on-translucent-slice.yaml gets a content-size so that its scroll frame keeps its slice, which is what that reftest is about.\n\nFixed-position text on a page whose root scroll frame has no range now shares an opaque slice with the rest of the page and gets subpixel AA on Windows, which is the two-pixel fringe behind the wpt expectation changes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327232\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/spatial_tree.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/slice_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/real_scroll_root.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/redundant_scroll_root_small.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/redundant_scroll_root_zero_range.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor-surface/underlay-mask-on-translucent-slice.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/test_invalidation.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-multicol/fixedpos-static-pos-with-viewport-cb-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-multicol/fixedpos-static-pos-with-viewport-cb-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/massive-element-below-and-on-top-of-viewport-partially-onscreen-new.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/massive-element-below-and-on-top-of-viewport-partially-onscreen-old.html.ini"], "git_node": "b06f6b85a64ee03fd33d9d47730d972c3de7db1a", "git_parents": ["6b3963c4c58a8428380e267dcf7865705db4ddd0"], "node": "5175251ffe51f4a888af9a0096965242c911bd7c", "parents": ["9138be030f748418f04694ba99b7a62d8300a536"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072784 - Pt 1 - Give WebRender device resources backend-neutral handles r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nTexture, ExternalTexture, Program, VAO, TransferBuffer and the framebuffer\nand buffer id newtypes now hold plain integers rather than gleam types, and\nTexture holds the ImageBufferKind it was created from rather than a GL enum,\nconverting at the call sites that issue GL. DepthFunction becomes a plain\nenum with the GL mapping in to_gl. This lets the resource types be shared\nwith another backend without depending on gleam.\n\nNo behaviour change: from_gl_target, which could not tell\nTextureExternalBT709 from TextureExternal, is no longer needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326787\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs"], "git_node": "1f2fb4e383022f596e2b1445567d36684a7652d0", "git_parents": ["b06f6b85a64ee03fd33d9d47730d972c3de7db1a"], "node": "28d6ee4697ad4a34e87493b807a35e1f7dfada2a", "parents": ["5175251ffe51f4a888af9a0096965242c911bd7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072784 - Pt 2 - Trim the WebRender Device API to what the renderer uses r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nRemove UniformLocation, get_uniform_location and draw_triangles_u16, none of\nwhich had callers, and the phantom type parameter of reuse_render_target.\nPrivatise the helpers only called from inside the device: bind_read_target,\nbind_external_draw_target, reset_draw_target, depth_bits, compile_shader,\ninvalidate_depth_target, create_transfer_buffer and\nrequired_upload_size_and_stride.\n\nWhat remains is what a backend trait will have to express, so it should be\nas small as possible. No behaviour change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326788\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs"], "git_node": "e5dfbe0e75c7d11fb161724f701d19b6f1b72de4", "git_parents": ["1f2fb4e383022f596e2b1445567d36684a7652d0"], "node": "2e82a5313a09ddd8a69eba9307e7d2cd3fb5d132", "parents": ["28d6ee4697ad4a34e87493b807a35e1f7dfada2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072784 - Pt 3 - Drive WebRender texture uploads through device primitives r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nUploadBufferPool and TextureUploader reached into the GL context to\nallocate, map, flush and orphan pixel buffers, to create and poll sync\nobjects, and to issue texture updates. Express those as Device operations\nany backend can provide: allocate, map, flush and orphan_upload_buffer,\nupload_texture_region, and create, poll and delete_fence over Fence and\nFenceStatus. UploadChunk becomes the public description of one copy from an\nupload buffer into a texture, and flush_upload_buffer performs a batch of\nthem, which is the shape of a staging buffer copy in explicit graphics APIs.\nThe pool and uploader then use only Device and Capabilities, so they can\nmove out of the GL backend.\n\nGL calls are the same except that the pixel unpack buffer is unbound at the\nend of each flush and orphan rather than once per returned buffer, adding a\nrebind when an oversized buffer is orphaned, and that a recycled\npersistently mapped buffer is no longer bound while being handed out, since\nnothing used the binding.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326789\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs"], "git_node": "ae2ee4182231938ad9941066bf62edff2b73d45b", "git_parents": ["e5dfbe0e75c7d11fb161724f701d19b6f1b72de4"], "node": "07a7a0922e209c53ad2ab05e7de1661eea82e48d", "parents": ["2e82a5313a09ddd8a69eba9307e7d2cd3fb5d132"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072784 - Pt 4 - Drive the WebRender GPU profiler through a query trait r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe GPU profiler held its own GL context handle for timer and occlusion\nqueries and for debug marker groups, and picked the GL debug extension\nitself. Give it a GpuQueryBackend trait with the operations it needs,\nimplemented for GL by GlQueries in the device, which also owns the extension\nchoice. The file is renamed query_gl.rs to query.rs; its module path\ndevice::query is unchanged. No behaviour change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326790\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/query.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/query_gl.rs"], "git_node": "efb88336ab01e72e381963c09c3b2aaf1f4b254f", "git_parents": ["ae2ee4182231938ad9941066bf62edff2b73d45b"], "node": "3878799c78e172609b6a678aceee02d30f93cdbd", "parents": ["07a7a0922e209c53ad2ab05e7de1661eea82e48d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072784 - Pt 5 - Bundle WebRender blend, depth and color-write state into a pipeline bind r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nExplicit graphics APIs bake blend, depth test, depth write and color write\nmask into a pipeline object together with the shader, so a backend needs to\nsee them when the program is bound rather than as separate GL-style toggles.\nAdd RenderState holding those four settings and bind_pipeline(program,\nstate). The set_blend_mode, set_depth_test, set_depth_write and\nset_color_write methods now only record the requested state and bind_program\napplies it, so renderer call sites are unchanged. Debug builds still assert\nthat a draw follows the program bind, which is what makes the state known at\nbind time.\n\nThe GL device caches the state the context holds and issues calls only for\nthe parts that differ, invalidating the cache in reset_state, which the\nrenderer already calls after external code may have used the context. The\ncolor mask is the exception, assumed untouched by external code as it always\nhas been, because SWGL does not implement glColorMask and it must not be\nissued unless the renderer asks for it. Clears set the depth write mask they\nneed themselves, being independent of pipeline state in explicit APIs, and\nthe stencil test is disabled once in begin_frame instead of through a\nseparate disable_stencil call. The GL calls issued are otherwise the same or\nfewer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326791\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs"], "git_node": "20c65f421f7f143f194228632ba3f45d3b4a983d", "git_parents": ["efb88336ab01e72e381963c09c3b2aaf1f4b254f"], "node": "0a48ebae16fac80183e1dc3ef4803c74b164d876", "parents": ["3878799c78e172609b6a678aceee02d30f93cdbd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072784 - Pt 6 - Carve the GpuBackend trait out of the WebRender Device r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nDevice becomes a thin wrapper around Box\u003cdyn GpuBackend\u003e, the trait a\ngraphics API backend implements, and the GL implementation is renamed\nGlDevice. The trait covers resource creation and destruction, render passes,\nbind_pipeline, texture and vertex binding, uploads, readback, fences,\nqueries and draws, with vertex, instance and texel data passed as bytes so\nthat it is object safe.\n\nThe wrapper derefs to the backend, so renderer call sites are unchanged, and\nowns what is backend independent: the requested RenderState and its set_*\nmethods, bind_program, the debug check that a draw follows a program bind,\nthe typed helpers over sampler types and typed slices, create_program_linked,\nblit_render_target_invert_y and upload_texture. MappedTransferBuffer holds\nthe backend and unmaps through a new unmap_transfer_buffer, and the texture\ncounters become accessors.\n\nMost of the diff is GlDevice's methods splitting into a trait impl block and\na private one; review with --color-moved. The GL calls issued are unchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326792\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs"], "git_node": "32fba8b922d168de728168a6613e3af948ed2c02", "git_parents": ["20c65f421f7f143f194228632ba3f45d3b4a983d"], "node": "0cb7d640b527bcff26f9f31ebb1a62735ce07d87", "parents": ["0a48ebae16fac80183e1dc3ef4803c74b164d876"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072784 - Pt 7 - Move the backend-neutral WebRender device types out of the GL backend r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nMove the resource types, state and descriptor structs, targets and the\nprogram binary cache from device/gl.rs to device/types.rs, and the upload\nbuffer pool and texture uploader to device/upload.rs, so that gl.rs holds\nonly the GL backend. The moved code is unchanged apart from imports and the\nfields and helpers the GL backend fills in becoming pub(super). Methods that\nneed GL, such as DepthFunction::to_gl and ProgramSourceInfo::new, stay in\ngl.rs as inherent impls on the moved types.\n\nThe gl_leaks test now scans everything except device/gl.rs. device/mod.rs\njoins the allowlist because Device::new still takes the GL context, which\nPt 8 replaces with a backend selection. No behaviour change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326793\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/types.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/upload.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/tests/gl_leaks.rs"], "git_node": "610425bffda8755a6fe773c54e13cfd291b59957", "git_parents": ["32fba8b922d168de728168a6613e3af948ed2c02"], "node": "d146346fdc034484b37f5afdef668c630dd8a354", "parents": ["0cb7d640b527bcff26f9f31ebb1a62735ce07d87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072784 - Pt 8 - Select the WebRender GPU backend through GpuBackendConfig r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\ncreate_webrender_instance and Device::new took the GL context directly,\nwhich tied the embedder API to gleam. They now take GpuBackendConfig, an\nenum with one variant per backend carrying what that backend needs from the\nembedder; Gl carries the GL context. Gecko, wrench and the examples wrap\ntheir context in GpuBackendConfig::Gl.\n\nWith that, renderer/init.rs and lib.rs no longer mention GL, so the gl_leaks\nallowlist is empty. device/mod.rs is permanently allowed, since selecting a\nbackend means naming each one's native context type. No behaviour change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326794\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/common/boilerplate.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/multiwindow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/init.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/tests/gl_leaks.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/wrench.rs"], "git_node": "4e9e72bf38a2c14c509245e77f52eea3227aecfd", "git_parents": ["610425bffda8755a6fe773c54e13cfd291b59957"], "node": "a6fcce2bb53dc6831aaf8a27a68e794e5278d39f", "parents": ["d146346fdc034484b37f5afdef668c630dd8a354"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072901 - Run the same teardown and collections before the leak check when a test times out, r=Gijs.\n\nbrowser-test.js releases the resources it keeps alive until shutdown, and\ncollects twice, before checking for leaks. A test that times out ended the\nsession without either step, so those resources were blamed on whichever\nearlier test created them - hence browser_getScreenshots.js's intermittent\nbackgroundPageThumbs.xhtml window and docShell leaks.\n\nThe release step, the two local collection rounds and the build-type gate are\nnow shared, which changes what every timing-out browser-chrome test in the tree\ndoes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327094\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/browser-test.js"], "git_node": "a980d5ebf96933a8856aec930b15134cbddc298f", "git_parents": ["4e9e72bf38a2c14c509245e77f52eea3227aecfd"], "node": "c35ef7c351041f7f51fc1448d67fe907bfb7c9e0", "parents": ["a6fcce2bb53dc6831aaf8a27a68e794e5278d39f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073163 - Fall back to strtof/strtod in wasm2c on openbsd. r=shravanrn,gaston\n\nhttps://github.com/WebAssembly/wabt/commit/b7ad849395485e6adf9ab2bfad8226741038690d\nswitched from strtof/strtod to strtof_l/strtod_l, which are not\navailable on OpenBSD.\n\nRevert to strtof/strtod on OpenBSD.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327199\n", "files": ["config/external/wasm2c_sandbox_compiler/moz.yaml", "config/external/wasm2c_sandbox_compiler/openbsd-no-strtod-l.patch", "third_party/wasm2c/src/literal.cc"], "git_node": "fb3a621ffbb240b11a9b65207fe19ce635fea7e1", "git_parents": ["a980d5ebf96933a8856aec930b15134cbddc298f"], "node": "7b3ae21354598f5518acbdac79a598ab76a99f84", "parents": ["c35ef7c351041f7f51fc1448d67fe907bfb7c9e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072952 - Keep wasm2c guard-page bounds checking enabled under clang-cl. r=shravanrn\n\nclang-cl doesn't define __GNUC__, but does accept the GCC asm barriers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327204\n", "files": ["config/external/wasm2c_sandbox_compiler/allow-guard-pages-with-clang-cl.patch", "config/external/wasm2c_sandbox_compiler/moz.yaml", "third_party/wasm2c/src/prebuilt/wasm2c_simd_source_declarations.cc", "third_party/wasm2c/src/prebuilt/wasm2c_source_declarations.cc", "third_party/wasm2c/wasm2c/wasm-rt.h"], "git_node": "2f0e7ebf9622a8d86a3010c90851fee6e863ddc6", "git_parents": ["fb3a621ffbb240b11a9b65207fe19ce635fea7e1"], "node": "396d9c52be2b956f536ccddce88043f785ccecf2", "parents": ["7b3ae21354598f5518acbdac79a598ab76a99f84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068459 - Eliminate the type confusion of AxisEndPoint. r=layout-reviewers,emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers\n\nTo avoid the type confusion via IPC when using serde for shape commands,\nwe change the type of the computed value of `AxisEndPoint` to avoid\nusing `AxisPosition`, which could be a length percentage or a keyword.\ni.e.\nspecified value of `AxisEndPoint`: as of it is.\ncomputed value of `AxisEndPoint`: both enum arms, `ToPosition` and\n`ByCoordinate` use `LengthPercentage` instead.\n\nTherefore, we can make sure the receiver of IPC always gets\n`LengthPercentage`.\n\nThis is pretty similiar to what we do for `Position`. The only drawback is\nthat we need to add one more generics type parameter for all the shape\ntypes.\n\nFor `PathCommand`, we always use `AxisEndPoint\u003cCSSFloat, CSSFloat\u003e`\nbecause its specified value and computed value are the same and it always\nuses `CSSFloat` to represent the coordinate, for hline and vline.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324476\n", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGAnimatedPathSegList.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGPathData.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGPathSegUtils.h", "layout/style/ServoStyleConstsInlines.h", "servo/components/style/values/computed/basic_shape.rs", "servo/components/style/values/generics/basic_shape.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/basic_shape.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/svg_path.rs"], "git_node": "1ee1faf71a6c5333180d58099972e23d2f5e5afd", "git_parents": ["2f0e7ebf9622a8d86a3010c90851fee6e863ddc6"], "node": "7573cfdd74d1ed2f31629c63d7efd79f082e9c8e", "parents": ["396d9c52be2b956f536ccddce88043f785ccecf2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1452337 - Restrict WebRender image sampling to the visible part of an image r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nA sprite sheet is pushed as the whole sheet clipped to one cell with nothing\nrestricting sampling, so filtering at fractional raster scales pulls in the\nneighbouring cells. Narrow the source rect with add_sub_rect, the way\nborder-image already does per nine-patch slice.\n\nScene building derives the visible part from what the clip rect leaves of the\nbounds and keeps it as a fraction; prepare_image_quads resolves it against the\nsize the image is really rasterized at, snapped out to whole texels so the\nshader's half-texel clamp cannot land mid-texel and shift the image. Skipped\nwhen the pattern repeats, since each repetition samples the whole image.\n\nThe fraction is measured against the stretch size anchored at the rect's origin\nrather than the rect itself, because Gecko trims a repeating background's rect\nto the fill area while leaving its origin on the first tile (bug 2068996; at an\nextreme ratio the misread saturates and floods the element with a single texel,\nbug 2069245).\n\nsub-rect-trimmed-bounds pins that saturating case, and sub-rect-clamp-external\ncovers the sub-rect through an external image's DeferredUvCopy path. 403181-1\nnow matches exactly, so its fuzz annotation goes with it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318633\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border_image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_task_graph.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/gpu_buffer.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interned_prims.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/key_types.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/sub-rect-clamp-external.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/sub-rect-clamp-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/sub-rect-clamp.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/sub-rect-trimmed-bounds-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/sub-rect-trimmed-bounds.yaml", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-clamp-1-ref.html", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-clamp-1.html", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-clamp-2-ref.html", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-clamp-2.html", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-clamp-ref.png", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-clamp.png", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-strip-ref.png", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-strip.png", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list"], "git_node": "feecee85446703941c0527150193372339d7084a", "git_parents": ["1ee1faf71a6c5333180d58099972e23d2f5e5afd"], "node": "6e0b1f3a07e97dd68eec15efd47493b8fc5eb621", "parents": ["7573cfdd74d1ed2f31629c63d7efd79f082e9c8e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072927 - Fix PERFHERDER_DATA matching in testing/gtest/bench.py. r=ahal\n\nbench.py looked for benchmark results with a startswith() check anchored at\nthe start of the line.  However that's broken since each line now\ncontains a prefix.  This patch now matches PERFHERDER_DATA using a\nregular expression, which replicates PERFHERDER_MATCHER in rungtests.py.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326885\n", "files": ["testing/gtest/bench.py"], "git_node": "3642c0aaec6e4411a756afb14ebd60f4b2e410b6", "git_parents": ["feecee85446703941c0527150193372339d7084a"], "node": "4aea3df6887c0d327a14b20437328a8ad9cff3b5", "parents": ["6e0b1f3a07e97dd68eec15efd47493b8fc5eb621"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072927 - Make stddev calculation safe when there's one replicate of the test. r=ahal\n\nstatistics.stdev raises StatisticsError when given a single data point.\nLeave the deviation blank in that case, since there is none to report.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326886\n", "files": ["testing/gtest/bench.py"], "git_node": "ff336468d20f0b84c7be61c79e518de674628f0b", "git_parents": ["3642c0aaec6e4411a756afb14ebd60f4b2e410b6"], "node": "013076fe038e949089bc1236c819858207e40f6a", "parents": ["4aea3df6887c0d327a14b20437328a8ad9cff3b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cs/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rMX/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-zh-rTW/strings.xml"], "git_node": "c33a1a5a273e68253e6d5ef7917fa37b5cfc4820", "git_parents": ["ff336468d20f0b84c7be61c79e518de674628f0b"], "node": "893d7575983c1c9ad7e63778778c3879d33d9411", "parents": ["013076fe038e949089bc1236c819858207e40f6a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "chloezhouny \u003cchloezhouny@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052358 - Render Smart Window chat replies block by block to reduce streaming jank r=Mardak\n\nWe used to re-parse the whole message and rebuild the whole DOM on every streamed chunk, so long replies got janky as they grew.\n\nNow we render one markdown block at a time and only re-render the blocks that changed, so finished blocks (like a table) keep their existing DOM instead of being rebuilt each chunk. Also throttle the overflow ResizeObserver to an animation frame and render the message list with a keyed repeat().\n\nA performance.measure marker around the render shows the per-chunk render cost and how many blocks were rebuilt in the Firefox Profiler.\n\nTests check that block-by-block rendering matches whole-message rendering and that a finished block's DOM node is reused across chunks.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326324\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-message/ai-chat-message.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-table/ai-chat-table.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatMarkdownParser.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_message.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_message_table.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_chat_markdown_parser.js"], "git_node": "41f616292e9f6511c26f53ae50dd731461feeb53", "git_parents": ["c33a1a5a273e68253e6d5ef7917fa37b5cfc4820"], "node": "ad9dc82bc357bdde57063b35c1b0fdae9b274163", "parents": ["893d7575983c1c9ad7e63778778c3879d33d9411"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068443 - Follow up for fixing the points which were pointed at the last review r=smaug\n\nI forgot to update D323542 before landing the patch due to the tight\nschedule before the vacation week in Japan. This patch fixes the points:\n1. The wrong warning message in `CompositionTransaction`\n2. Unnecessary early return for the error case before `NS_WARNING_ASSERTION` in `DeleteTextTransaction::UndoTransaction`\n3. Unnecessary editor reference in `AutoTextEditVerifier`\n4. Bad error handlings in `Do*Text` methods which may ignore `NS_ERROR_EDITOR_DESTROYED`\n5. Unsafe `Destroyed` check remove in `EditorBase::InsertTextIntoTextNodeWithTransaction`\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327721\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/CompositionTransaction.cpp", "editor/libeditor/DeleteTextTransaction.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorBase.cpp"], "git_node": "d1fb63c76d6201d82d077136daac0240662777f9", "git_parents": ["41f616292e9f6511c26f53ae50dd731461feeb53"], "node": "6a87c1675d0ad40442fb8c4372bdd664c3e22ebb", "parents": ["ad9dc82bc357bdde57063b35c1b0fdae9b274163"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jack Brown \u003cjbrown@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072457 - Add a Nimbus feature for the dnsNotFound search CTA - r=nimbus-reviewers,beth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326367\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "87642cd9bacc3b8a9e77ebb9b6e5e870a2328fd1", "git_parents": ["d1fb63c76d6201d82d077136daac0240662777f9"], "node": "2e36862bad233b7157efa6605a88934e3d81c8e1", "parents": ["6a87c1675d0ad40442fb8c4372bdd664c3e22ebb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070359 - Stocks widget: show multiple matches for a ticker search instead of a single result r=reemhamz\n\nUpdate the Stocks widget to use Merino's ticker search\n(`request_type=ticker_search`) for the search panel. It returns up to ten\nranked matches with a name, symbol and exchange and no price, so the panel now\nlists every match as a two-line add row in a list that scrolls when the card\nis full, instead of showing the single quote the old lookup returned. Picking\na match adds the symbol to the watchlist as before; the watchlist quote fetch\nis a separate bug.\n\nThe results list and the large watchlist list are focusable, so keyboard\nusers can scroll them even when no row control is enabled, such as when the\nwatchlist is full and every add button is disabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326074\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/Reducers.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/StockSearch.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/StockTicker.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/Stocks.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/_Stocks.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/StocksFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/StockSearch.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/StockTicker.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_StocksFeed.js"], "git_node": "82fb7d8d703fbb94510e5907d406b93fb39b3775", "git_parents": ["87642cd9bacc3b8a9e77ebb9b6e5e870a2328fd1"], "node": "e06583e8009a8dc9a1836e803f2fc36efe2c4315", "parents": ["2e36862bad233b7157efa6605a88934e3d81c8e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067467 - Add context menu aria-label for Crossword, Clocks, Privacy widgets. r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson,nina-py\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327249\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Clocks/Clocks.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Crossword/Crossword.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy/Privacy.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Clocks.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Crossword.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy.test.jsx", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "025151afd666ff44cd20c832ece9234f826d5682", "git_parents": ["82fb7d8d703fbb94510e5907d406b93fb39b3775"], "node": "12fe56988c4dd8c158e1c33d6687490502a41116", "parents": ["e06583e8009a8dc9a1836e803f2fc36efe2c4315"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073341 - Recycle Path storage into PathBuilder. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nPathBuilderRecording gives its storage to PathRecording on Finish. PathBuilderRecording\nmust then reallocate the storage again for the next path, even if the builder is reused.\nIn cases where we know the path is no longer used, this storage can be recycled back to\nthe builder, reducing another potential source of frequent reallocation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327233\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.h", "gfx/2d/2D.h", "gfx/2d/PathCairo.cpp", "gfx/2d/PathCairo.h", "gfx/2d/PathRecording.cpp", "gfx/2d/PathRecording.h", "gfx/2d/PathSkia.cpp", "gfx/2d/PathSkia.h", "gfx/2d/ScaledFontBase.cpp", "gfx/2d/ScaledFontBase.h"], "git_node": "13e848c3ed7daef0266dd40f0de4c3aebb9f9364", "git_parents": ["025151afd666ff44cd20c832ece9234f826d5682"], "node": "da961058d8e09a8392e95f40ada9324289f45725", "parents": ["12fe56988c4dd8c158e1c33d6687490502a41116"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073341 - Remove duplicate StrokeCircle and StrokeLine optimizations. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nNow that PathRecording construction costs are much lower, there is no need to have duplicate\nchecks for StrokeLine and StrokeCircle higher up on PathBuilderRecording to avoid the PathRecording\nconstruction cost. Remove the duplicate optimizations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327697\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.cpp"], "git_node": "96c704c411b7f5b0a0385c035adad349a5b3695e", "git_parents": ["13e848c3ed7daef0266dd40f0de4c3aebb9f9364"], "node": "b9193a1451824363f52a7494aebd9860160e1a1a", "parents": ["da961058d8e09a8392e95f40ada9324289f45725"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2073341 - Remove duplicate StrokeCircle and StrokeLine optimizations. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\" for causing mochitest plain failures at 2d.clip.winding.html\n\nThis reverts commit 96c704c411b7f5b0a0385c035adad349a5b3695e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2073341 - Recycle Path storage into PathBuilder. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 13e848c3ed7daef0266dd40f0de4c3aebb9f9364.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.h", "gfx/2d/2D.h", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.cpp", "gfx/2d/PathCairo.cpp", "gfx/2d/PathCairo.h", "gfx/2d/PathRecording.cpp", "gfx/2d/PathRecording.h", "gfx/2d/PathSkia.cpp", "gfx/2d/PathSkia.h", "gfx/2d/ScaledFontBase.cpp", "gfx/2d/ScaledFontBase.h"], "git_node": "58f173d47d89a1f895bf89ecc13ae28ab25b5e10", "git_parents": ["96c704c411b7f5b0a0385c035adad349a5b3695e"], "node": "fd9cc39f1458318d19bf91b3ad634a1bb25635b6", "parents": ["b9193a1451824363f52a7494aebd9860160e1a1a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abel Kalu \u003c59095867+BlessedOneKobo@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035151 - Localize devtools project-wide search result label. r=devtools-reviewers,flod,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326941\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/components/PrimaryPanes/ProjectSearch.js", "devtools/client/locales/en-