[]}, {"author": "Filip Skokan \u003cpanva.ip@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071814 [wpt PR 62670] - [WebCryptoAPI] Fix digest transfer timing tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebCryptoAPI] Fix digest transfer timing tests (#62670)\n\nTransfer SHA-1/2 input buffers from the algorithm name getter so the\n\"during call\" tests actually detach them during digest(), matching\nSHA-3 and cSHAKE.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c09e95940d9d64ae3d6a058531eb346f9095a8c7\nwpt-pr: 62670\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/WebCryptoAPI/digest/digest.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/WebCryptoAPI/digest/digest.js"], "git_node": "e14a764ac4c7ef49042c6d90fd4f899fc61e21dc", "git_parents": ["20de7620e6646a3f08716db1f0366ee7679c2dce"], "node": "ddb6d4e08d8f754b0217220bb60dece70557bd94", "parents": ["f96d36e8a44038055d1a296a5716a3b930fbd296"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071814 [wpt PR 62670] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62670\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/digest/digest.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "cb911f08fb96f5a32464db9579fcc61af6cfcd0b", "git_parents": ["e14a764ac4c7ef49042c6d90fd4f899fc61e21dc"], "node": "2b19f3a891c0e8477a01c2e87978bb3bd673f1a8", "parents": ["ddb6d4e08d8f754b0217220bb60dece70557bd94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071757 [wpt PR 62666] - [css-shadow] Tests not properly exported from WebKit, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-shadow] Add the missing rel=match to slotted-text-with-flex.html\n\nThe test ships a slotted-text-with-flex-ref.html reference but never links to\nit, and it does not use testharness.js either, so as imported it asserts\nnothing. The reference matches the expected rendering, so link it.\n\n--\n[css-shadow] Test that ancestor :hover invalidates a slotted descendant\n\nHovering an element restyles its ancestor chain, which for slotted content has\nto cross out of the shadow tree the content is slotted into. The test hovers\nunrelated shadow content first, so that the common ancestor with the slotted\nsubtree is the host and the following hover chain starts inside the shadow\nscope.\n\nWritten for https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315930 but never exported.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: db7b9d3748d2bb1867ed75cca20b1c4e8930f3cf, 85eb0a2f9531c1051e3168a35191a02ccddce4f5\nwpt-pr: 62666\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shadow/hover-invalidates-slotted-descendant.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shadow/slotted-text-with-flex.html"], "git_node": "087c238f94113fef520598df1fda9be20d2ee19d", "git_parents": ["cb911f08fb96f5a32464db9579fcc61af6cfcd0b"], "node": "da24c435ee875e0257604470ecae0c6ebdaa5af4", "parents": ["2b19f3a891c0e8477a01c2e87978bb3bd673f1a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071757 [wpt PR 62666] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62666\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-shadow/hover-invalidates-slotted-descendant.html.ini"], "git_node": "ea484f26ca8e4d463ec1d55c37e8619084a209e2", "git_parents": ["087c238f94113fef520598df1fda9be20d2ee19d"], "node": "a562df3ba90c3af55300650816be647c9b651019", "parents": ["da24c435ee875e0257604470ecae0c6ebdaa5af4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Nguyen \u003cnt1m@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071159 [wpt PR 62480] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323469, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export: [Custom Highlight] Support ::highlight(*) (#62480)\n\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323469\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 821fce9f3768447587d226c9b43a832cdb76d535\nwpt-pr: 62480\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-escaped-star.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-parsing-and-computed-style.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/parsing/pseudo-elements-valid-with-classes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/parsing/pseudo-elements-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/pseudo-escaped-star-specificity.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/pseudo-escaped-star-view-transition-group.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/pseudo-get-computed-style-escaped-star.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/pseudo-match-escaped-star.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/pseudo-mismatch-escaped-star.html"], "git_node": "e97729d1a91f938cac39acf007756882dc84823f", "git_parents": ["ea484f26ca8e4d463ec1d55c37e8619084a209e2"], "node": "d48e33b88c5050b8e1fc1f39f02a092aee1e1b91", "parents": ["a562df3ba90c3af55300650816be647c9b651019"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071159 [wpt PR 62480] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62480\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-escaped-star.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/navigation/opt-in-without-frame-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "731a29b3acccd79d9ae43c18329b300cdbb61346", "git_parents": ["e97729d1a91f938cac39acf007756882dc84823f"], "node": "6c30217f11b9182d759f2d92e588ecb4e0b3b8ba", "parents": ["d48e33b88c5050b8e1fc1f39f02a092aee1e1b91"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brent Fulgham \u003c44174109+brentfulgham@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071553 [wpt PR 62640] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322753, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322753 (#62640)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a9b9508807a780ac5c5249011cbe4b639f889614\nwpt-pr: 62640\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/synthetic-bold-combining-mark-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/synthetic-bold-combining-mark-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/synthetic-bold-combining-mark-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/synthetic-bold-combining-mark-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/letter-spacing/letter-spacing-combining-mark-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/letter-spacing/letter-spacing-combining-mark-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/letter-spacing/reference/letter-spacing-combining-mark-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/letter-spacing/reference/letter-spacing-combining-mark-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/tools/generate-mark-anchor-font.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/word-spacing/reference/word-spacing-combining-mark-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/word-spacing/reference/word-spacing-combining-mark-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/word-spacing/word-spacing-combining-mark-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/word-spacing/word-spacing-combining-mark-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fonts/mark-anchor-test.ttf"], "git_node": "28fddb52e9e96e469b95ca6d163c3d90865fffc7", "git_parents": ["731a29b3acccd79d9ae43c18329b300cdbb61346"], "node": "7d75514b2ffeccc2497a8196f18c5025c291c90d", "parents": ["6c30217f11b9182d759f2d92e588ecb4e0b3b8ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071718 [wpt PR 62662] - Ensure default paste behavior doesn't leak changed clipboard content, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nEnsure default paste behavior doesn't leak changed clipboard content\n\nA synchronous paste reads the clipboard lazily, so if the paste event\nhandler doesn't read the clipboard, the clipboard read only happens\nafter the paste event when the default paste behavior runs.\n\nThe page could potentially slow down the paste event handler with a busy\nloop, creating a gap where the clipboard contents could change. The\nresult is that the default paste behavior could paste the new content\nrather than the content on the clipboard at the time the paste action\nwas invoked. ClipboardPromise or DataObjectItem each have their own\nsequence number checks, but the default paste behavior doesn't go\nthrough either.\n\nIn this CL, fix this by having ClipboardCommand record the sequence\nnumber at the start of the paste. If these diverge, don't perform\nthe default paste action that would inject the content into the\npage. Also, don't pass actual clipboard data to the beforeinput event\nif we detect that the clipboard has changed by that point.\n\nClipboardCommands::ExecutePasteAndMatchStyle was missing a\nScopedSystemClipboardSnapshot, so add one so that it gets the same\nsequence number checking and IPC coalescing as Paste.\n\nFixed: 517584808\nChange-Id: I29fc34d6e84b74914287f819bb3f66e44459ab7d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8217390\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697410}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a05f84223b17a6b20bafc082e921e15f1da3573e\nwpt-pr: 62662\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/editing/other/paste-clipboard-change.tentative.html"], "git_node": "6bae80cad8c99c9b988ca7424aad5c7d12d0d80d", "git_parents": ["28fddb52e9e96e469b95ca6d163c3d90865fffc7"], "node": "bd289663bbb687a3c94b10f578e1b53208184244", "parents": ["7d75514b2ffeccc2497a8196f18c5025c291c90d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071718 [wpt PR 62662] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62662\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/editing/other/paste-clipboard-change.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "09ff82a14e9089521589489cf4c7e6fc38056e3d", "git_parents": ["6bae80cad8c99c9b988ca7424aad5c7d12d0d80d"], "node": "6e55221d0311cb2cd52e421bae7362242913ad81", "parents": ["bd289663bbb687a3c94b10f578e1b53208184244"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071988 [wpt PR 62680] - [html-in-canvas] Disallow SVG masks that are outside a canvas subtree, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Disallow SVG masks that are outside a canvas subtree\n\nAs with SVG patterns, we disallow the use of masks defined outside of a\ncanvas subtree, where privacy protections are not available.\n\nFixed: 553135213\nChange-Id: Id4fa486444b0896e574dbf51d65579bb56b86e9b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8398235\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697429}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5f828d94bc0133c7a3fe127d6ea6c93b375afc2f\nwpt-pr: 62680\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-mask-filter.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-mask-nested-filter.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-mask-visited.tentative.https.sub.html"], "git_node": "a899c0dfb31c3968f5fc9731b7ae52c1e0686ccf", "git_parents": ["09ff82a14e9089521589489cf4c7e6fc38056e3d"], "node": "46619388370eeacf50d22a0a66d680a289a5e1c7", "parents": ["6e55221d0311cb2cd52e421bae7362242913ad81"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071988 [wpt PR 62680] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62680\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-mask-visited.tentative.https.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "34e774532cc3a890b90b72096c254973db3dd6f2", "git_parents": ["a899c0dfb31c3968f5fc9731b7ae52c1e0686ccf"], "node": "bec5e2e2d82c1fbaca95646b02ff75f90cdc9bd1", "parents": ["46619388370eeacf50d22a0a66d680a289a5e1c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072069 [wpt PR 62694] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=308017, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=308017 (#62694)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b6082e07802fd6b9d17a3e27c85abf67275796bc\nwpt-pr: 62694\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/gradient-transform-template-inheritance-expected.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/gradient-transform-template-inheritance.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/linear-gradient-transform-empty-attr-expected.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/linear-gradient-transform-empty-attr.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/pattern-transform-empty-attr-expected.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/pattern-transform-empty-attr.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/pattern-transform-template-inheritance-expected.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/pattern-transform-template-inheritance.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/radial-gradient-transform-empty-attr-expected.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/radial-gradient-transform-empty-attr.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/reference/gradient-transform-template-inheritance-ref.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/reftests/reference/pattern-transform-template-inheritance-ref.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/scripted/linear-gradient-transform-clear-expected.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/scripted/linear-gradient-transform-clear.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/scripted/radial-gradient-transform-clear-expected.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/pservers/scripted/radial-gradient-transform-clear.svg"], "git_node": "2c640c92dee3b81aab63432c0b973aaea612d4a1", "git_parents": ["34e774532cc3a890b90b72096c254973db3dd6f2"], "node": "586d6779a509ef2ad42df1027abf76dcfe6828d8", "parents": ["bec5e2e2d82c1fbaca95646b02ff75f90cdc9bd1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072018 [wpt PR 62685] - [html-in-canvas] Fire paint events when nested canvases change, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Fire paint events when nested canvases change\n\nWhen nested canvases change, or request paint, they should cause\nancestor paint events to fire as well. The only exception to this is\nfor canvas changes which occur during the canvas's own paint event.\n\nThis patch fixes three bugs in this area:\n1. ShouldSkipPaintInvalidation returned true for layout subtree\n   canvases, which prevented nested layoutsubtree canvases from\n   invalidating when they were modified outside their paint event.\n2. Canvas.requestPaint() did not mark the canvas for paint invalidation\n   which prevented ancestor canvases from firing paint events.\n3. DidDraw has been updated to not invalidate for canvas changes made\n   during a paint event handler.\n\nFixed: 556296445\nChange-Id: I40933a21de9b00003bc6be03fe462f79390e21c8\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8360469\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697630}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: db60730013c0869ff70330aba8f6ed796100562a\nwpt-pr: 62685\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-iframe-nested-invalidation.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/lint.ignore"], "git_node": "09dbb2d1a9abd135ac8488e724b6a6853f33865f", "git_parents": ["2c640c92dee3b81aab63432c0b973aaea612d4a1"], "node": "fa516aa985f90a960fa987edd1a91b971d7ad9a9", "parents": ["586d6779a509ef2ad42df1027abf76dcfe6828d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072018 [wpt PR 62685] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62685\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-iframe-nested-invalidation.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "40e106215643a2a0ce9322df869161266790bd6a", "git_parents": ["09dbb2d1a9abd135ac8488e724b6a6853f33865f"], "node": "71bc6b2bc8eb34ae10c9776cbcb1c1ab1133a7f2", "parents": ["fa516aa985f90a960fa987edd1a91b971d7ad9a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras Tenorio \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072060 [wpt PR 62690] - [multicol] Fix for painting rules beside empty columns, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[multicol] Fix for painting rules beside empty columns\n\nI found a bug with a multicol container with content only in its first\ncolumn can have no recorded gaps, which leads to no rules being painted\neven on `rule-visibility-items: all`.\n\nCreate the missing gaps before checking whether the geometry is empty.\nPosition the first gap relative to the first column when no previous gap\nexists. Keep the existing visibility filtering so normal and between\nremain unchanged.\n\nChange-Id: I324570e38d7790835527dc2377ad3e5f728d2bc4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8406449\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697656}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 09a4275d19d3558a29f9416b96e3a83f0621a3e0\nwpt-pr: 62690\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/multicol-gap-decorations-visibility-all-empty-columns-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/multicol-gap-decorations-visibility-all-empty-columns.html"], "git_node": "2afea90b7ba8c136309abc93ee0b46272f26faa3", "git_parents": ["40e106215643a2a0ce9322df869161266790bd6a"], "node": "c4a986b20ab5615a719940e0b490bd2462122d5c", "parents": ["71bc6b2bc8eb34ae10c9776cbcb1c1ab1133a7f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072060 [wpt PR 62690] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62690\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/multicol/multicol-gap-decorations-visibility-all-empty-columns.html.ini"], "git_node": "0ae6c8dfd9a5fb5ca911e7d5f89be179ac8dc869", "git_parents": ["2afea90b7ba8c136309abc93ee0b46272f26faa3"], "node": "6199d64e834cbeec454595955e26a2273f2bb319", "parents": ["c4a986b20ab5615a719940e0b490bd2462122d5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras Tenorio \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072047 [wpt PR 62688] - [masonry] Fix insets for overlapping gutters, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[masonry] Fix insets for overlapping gutters\n\nGrid-lanes resolved percentage insets against a single crossing gutter,\neven when items adjacent lanes formed a wider overlapping junction.\n\nWe now reuse flex's opening/closing overlap-window representation to\nmodel each connected gap junction with two endpoints, as per the spec\n[1]. We reuse some of the existing logic for `Next` via a new helper\nfunction.\n\nWe then resolve percentage insets against the union of its gutters (per\nthe spec as well).\n\nBecause grid-lanes can have spanning items, we retain \"blocked\" state\ninside a window separately from the state after it.\n\n[1] https://www.w3.org/TR/css-gaps-1/#segment-endpoints\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: Ifa6bf873f8b928b5e797de47bdab61359f708c51\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8386618\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697672}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 658347437cc9f0228c77ec771ce8fea3da2a5d0f\nwpt-pr: 62688\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-negative-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-negative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-spanner-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-spanner.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-negative-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-negative.html"], "git_node": "a5d357adf6b78e4d873bf1d281ed2332e0782621", "git_parents": ["0ae6c8dfd9a5fb5ca911e7d5f89be179ac8dc869"], "node": "95975b439d74b3bde1d7430ecf594fed5a09e316", "parents": ["6199d64e834cbeec454595955e26a2273f2bb319"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072047 [wpt PR 62688] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62688\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-negative.html.ini"], "git_node": "2c32bfdbce872acf64200e7d28aaa5f8babb8d30", "git_parents": ["a5d357adf6b78e4d873bf1d281ed2332e0782621"], "node": "a768df9bbce781d3a317eb4e9b080cdaf21f0007", "parents": ["95975b439d74b3bde1d7430ecf594fed5a09e316"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072079 [wpt PR 62697] - [svg] Make use-element-web-animations.html actually animate, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[svg] Make use-element-web-animations.html actually animate (#62697)\n\nThe test never ran. Two separate problems, both silent.\n\nfont-size is not a legal identifier in a JavaScript object literal, so\nthe script was a SyntaxError and no animation was ever started. Quoting\nthe key is not enough: a dashed keyframe key is not a valid keyframe\nproperty name either, and it is dropped in Chrome 155, Firefox 158 and\nSafari 26.4 and 27.0, all measured. That is already pinned by\nweb-animations/interfaces/KeyframeEffect/processing-a-keyframes-argument-001.html,\nwhere 'font-size' sits in gNonAnimatableProps commented \"Supported\nproperty that uses dashes\", and that test is 73/73 in all four engines.\nSo the key has to be fontSize.\n\nWith that fixed the animation ran, but in Safari and Firefox it slid\nlinearly from 120px to 80px, because steps(2, start) was on the empty\nfirst keyframe. Per the effect value algorithm, keyframes with no value\nfor the target property are removed before interval selection, an\nimplicit keyframe with no easing is synthesized at offset 0 in their\nplace, and the transformed distance uses the easing of the first\ninterval endpoint. So the author's easing could never reach font-size,\nand the rendering depended on when the screenshot was taken: it matched\nthe reference only at exactly currentTime 50000.\n\nMoving the easing into the effect options makes the value flat across\nthe whole first half in all three engines, so the timing dependence is\ngone everywhere. It also matches the sibling use-element-animations.html,\nwhere steps(2, start) is the animation-level timing function.\n\nThe empty first keyframe is kept on purpose. The point of the test is\nthat each element starts from its own computed font-size, 120px for the\noriginal and 40px for the use copy, so the start value must not be\nwritten down.\n\nMeasured after the change, against use-element-transitions-ref.html: the\noriginal text animates to 100px in all three engines and its bounding\nbox matches the reference, while the use copy stays at its inherited\n40px. So the test now fails because the shadow tree instance gets no\nmirrored animation, which needs ShadowAnimation and is implemented\nnowhere, rather than because the script did not parse. It is still\nexpected to fail in every engine, and no expectation metadata changes.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6af7ac5b790af38f889319a4d138fb0d1f515f0c\nwpt-pr: 62697\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/use-element-web-animations.html"], "git_node": "440a907edc1ced36f21e67a42eb3bb667a79922b", "git_parents": ["2c32bfdbce872acf64200e7d28aaa5f8babb8d30"], "node": "011d4150a556c7702dff89510a35927f3050a950", "parents": ["a768df9bbce781d3a317eb4e9b080cdaf21f0007"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Evan Stade \u003cevanstade@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072067 [wpt PR 62692] - IDB: correctly handle SharedArrayBuffer as key., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nIDB: correctly handle SharedArrayBuffer as key.\n\nThe spec says any \"buffer source type\" is a valid key, and that includes\nSharedArrayBuffer. This is in contrast to values, which use the\nstructured serialization algorithm, which specifically bans SAB when\nserializing for storage.\n\nBug: 558764482\nChange-Id: I790db66baf596154c3139cc6e9621b90f37d19b0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8393497\nCommit-Queue: Evan Stade \u003cevanstade@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Evan Stade \u003cevanstade@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nate Chapin \u003cjaphet@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697719}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8541c81a23fa405b61dc6cc12fbde3fd789147c0\nwpt-pr: 62692\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/IndexedDB/sharedarraybuffer-key.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/IndexedDB/sharedarraybuffer-key.https.html.headers"], "git_node": "473bd9cf596068bbd95d13521a738464ee0547ef", "git_parents": ["440a907edc1ced36f21e67a42eb3bb667a79922b"], "node": "ed30fdac3db83be06f1e2db25de91851c46eed4a", "parents": ["011d4150a556c7702dff89510a35927f3050a950"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072067 [wpt PR 62692] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62692\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/IndexedDB/idbfactory_cmp.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/IndexedDB/sharedarraybuffer-key.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "995b074e698eb6197a36d43394ceb50fc9d58d53", "git_parents": ["473bd9cf596068bbd95d13521a738464ee0547ef"], "node": "46f9edadf05ab7e12b15b827b66c0093125fc21f", "parents": ["ed30fdac3db83be06f1e2db25de91851c46eed4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Minseong Kim \u003cjja08111@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072094 [wpt PR 62698] - [css-overflow] Fix inaccurate engine claim in text-overflow WPT comments, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-overflow] Fix inaccurate engine claim in text-overflow WPT comments\n\nThe comments in text-overflow with focused textarea WPTs asserted that\n\"all current engines\" treat as clip while editing form controls. But,\nWebKit does not support text-overflow on textarea, so it clips for an\nunrelated reason.\n\nThis CL narrows the statement to what is actually observed: Chromium\nand Gecko suppress the ellipsis while editing a textarea, and WebKit\ndoes so for input.\n\nAnd, this has no behavior change.\n\nBug: 556432992\nChange-Id: I55767f5863309cc4131feaaceb971996d4db5fe4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8402261\nAuto-Submit: Minseong Kim \u003cjja08111@gmail.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697788}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 59a81aba6b91457c92fb2818c62ba8b29849d89a\nwpt-pr: 62698\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/text-overflow-in-readonly-textarea-focused.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/text-overflow-string-in-textarea-after-blur.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/text-overflow-string-in-textarea-focused.html"], "git_node": "76b68216981382b38483c44029194030e787ab31", "git_parents": ["995b074e698eb6197a36d43394ceb50fc9d58d53"], "node": "e854a952e7cc31535659b26ba2a65d98bc21546b", "parents": ["46f9edadf05ab7e12b15b827b66c0093125fc21f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antoine Quint \u003cgraouts@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072141 [wpt PR 62703] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324070, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324070 (#62703)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0ba14732347b80d178ab7c65741648dd80c5efe1\nwpt-pr: 62703\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-sticky-inline-ancestor.html"], "git_node": "3526718091a9e3d21100cb8f34aa6427469e306d", "git_parents": ["76b68216981382b38483c44029194030e787ab31"], "node": "e758695ccf1bb37f0795cbc2cd7d0441266a1851", "parents": ["e854a952e7cc31535659b26ba2a65d98bc21546b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antoine Quint \u003cgraouts@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072147 [wpt PR 62702] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313142, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313142 (#62702)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 63ff666e50e7ef4c11a6885612a05951f6f63547\nwpt-pr: 62702\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transitions/parsing/transition-property-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transitions/parsing/transition-property-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transitions/parsing/transition-property-valid.html"], "git_node": "c6680062c3066b5bfcb8e8ed406eab276b3afe61", "git_parents": ["3526718091a9e3d21100cb8f34aa6427469e306d"], "node": "44353c625154d6297d0b9fd9f83ac206b1a91dc5", "parents": ["e758695ccf1bb37f0795cbc2cd7d0441266a1851"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rich Waters \u003crich@waters.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072071 [wpt PR 62695] - Skip ignored subtrees when checking for block boundaries, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSkip ignored subtrees when checking for block boundaries\n\nWhen collecting text between block boundaries for matching,\nFindBuffer::IsInSameUninterruptedBlock is used to check for a boundary\nby looking for a different inline formatting context in the nodes\nbetween its two arguments. It skips ignored nodes, but it still descends\ninto their children.\n\nThis patch skips over the children of an ignored node so that the\nchildren's contents are also ignored. This fixes the matching across\nbroken images for text directives, because those broken images\nhave a shadow subtree for the alt text of an image even if that\nalt text is empty or not specified. That subtree causes a block\nboundary to be reported which causes CollectTextUntilBlockBoundary\nto split up the buffer and prevent matching around it.\n\nThis image behavior is only relevant when the MatchAcrossIgnoredNodes\nfind option is set, as otherwise a kNonCharacter is inserted in place\nof the image and that prevents the matching.\n\nA new test in find-range-from-text-directive.html exercises the\nnew behavior. FindBufferTest is unsuitable, as it doesn't attempt\nthe image load that exposes the broken image and does not build\nthe extra shadow subtree.\n\nGuarded by runtime flag FindBufferSkipIgnoredSubtrees.\n\nFixed: 558819236\nChange-Id: Iba173672752cfd3b7eaf5a4234072b6533bb9d36\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8374106\nReviewed-by: David Bokan \u003cbokan@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697855}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 77b7676b7022c6d8993c06411dcc81f3cf9ed975\nwpt-pr: 62695\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-to-text-fragment/find-range-from-text-directive-target.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-to-text-fragment/find-range-from-text-directive.html"], "git_node": "92cbb08b67351223c809cb1e25842202fe3ecc97", "git_parents": ["c6680062c3066b5bfcb8e8ed406eab276b3afe61"], "node": "4deaa6b91fba2807ac5c4754cd14884057f4e666", "parents": ["44353c625154d6297d0b9fd9f83ac206b1a91dc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072153 [wpt PR 62704] - Don't fold expressions to NaN/Inf while resolving a CalculationValue, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDon't fold expressions to NaN/Inf while resolving a CalculationValue\n\nIn an expression like \"calc(4px / round(100% / 25px))\", evaluating with\na max value of 1 will yield infinity - which is not correct. Disable\nthis code behind the flag CSSCalcEarlyNaNAndInfFolding.\n\nFixed: 560226430\nChange-Id: I663b7c8a4920e564eab9ace95b42b686cc7a337e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8398590\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697876}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4c0dce55407b8f7d54d02ec1b482ccb9782404cc\nwpt-pr: 62704\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/typed_arithmetic.html"], "git_node": "ec88cc341903cdfd9d08d46fe922c4eafdea6b65", "git_parents": ["92cbb08b67351223c809cb1e25842202fe3ecc97"], "node": "22097b3552ab3c500db24bc9ffbc4244dd6af496", "parents": ["4deaa6b91fba2807ac5c4754cd14884057f4e666"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072153 [wpt PR 62704] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62704\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/attr-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "1ba5f6ec74f193bb2ebe8ba2718dfae59d7bcc48", "git_parents": ["ec88cc341903cdfd9d08d46fe922c4eafdea6b65"], "node": "d638172e342df8ba5ae28fc7fe7d8c0bf03ec78e", "parents": ["22097b3552ab3c500db24bc9ffbc4244dd6af496"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sampath Samaraweera \u003csampath.samaraweera@codimite.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072288 [wpt PR 62709] - Apply page zoom to the \u003cclipPath\u003e transform for HTML elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nApply page zoom to the \u003cclipPath\u003e transform for HTML elements\n\nFor objectBoundingBox units, the zoom reached the clip transform only\nas the magnitude of the zoomed reference box, so it scaled the bbox\nbasis but not the `transform` attribute on the \u003cclipPath\u003e element,\nwhich sits outside it. The clip came out the right size in the wrong\nplace, off by (zoom - 1) * transform: correct at 100% zoom, diverging\nfrom an equivalent SVG element as the page is zoomed in.\n\nApply the zoom outside the whole transform instead, so that the\ntransform attribute is scaled along with the bounding box basis, and\npass an unzoomed reference box to CalculateClipTransform() so that the\nobjectBoundingBox scale does not apply the zoom a second time.\n\nFixed: 558945742\nChange-Id: I94ea34572e0e4dba403ab9346b4fee38326d6aaf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8402117\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697998}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9a3fd4d9e69f037c1369e45ff586c089c6ffc634\nwpt-pr: 62709\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-with-transform-and-zoom-hittest.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-with-transform-and-zoom.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/reference/clip-path-with-transform-and-zoom-ref.html"], "git_node": "ac60cd2465c68037fad1ae1efb542e2c937edcab", "git_parents": ["1ba5f6ec74f193bb2ebe8ba2718dfae59d7bcc48"], "node": "9e11f2d7e15aff7771217e99e08cd32a97072bdf", "parents": ["d638172e342df8ba5ae28fc7fe7d8c0bf03ec78e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072288 [wpt PR 62709] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62709\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-with-transform-and-zoom-hittest.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-with-transform-and-zoom.html.ini"], "git_node": "5f52d0c43301beec4cadac09972ea7c9f33fbbc2", "git_parents": ["ac60cd2465c68037fad1ae1efb542e2c937edcab"], "node": "405e91fa4b98a7edc28f5973c0e4da2c90d34b4b", "parents": ["9e11f2d7e15aff7771217e99e08cd32a97072bdf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072295 [wpt PR 62712] - Pass referrer to ExternalSVGResourceDocumentContent, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPass referrer to ExternalSVGResourceDocumentContent\n\nThe document loading the stylesheet would otherwise leak as a referrer\nto the SVG request.\n\nBug: 560664595\nChange-Id: I5952fbf2282384384a8d7cebd7f63aa12b6ac16c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8410307\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698068}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dc89ffbad02c42ad0ee484438f38d6ddf49be3ed\nwpt-pr: 62712\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/referrer-policy/css-integration/svg/filter-no-referrer.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/referrer-policy/css-integration/svg/filter.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/referrer-policy/css-integration/svg/filter.py"], "git_node": "7e7188bbe1417d280f7e883fe4b5ba15f10a7948", "git_parents": ["5f52d0c43301beec4cadac09972ea7c9f33fbbc2"], "node": "c83b1eabcc89b3841cf611e475bcb8acc1b7231c", "parents": ["405e91fa4b98a7edc28f5973c0e4da2c90d34b4b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072295 [wpt PR 62712] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62712\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/referrer-policy/css-integration/svg/filter-no-referrer.html.ini"], "git_node": "7bd1efc6399dd8832068e787e1246e3a44c4812f", "git_parents": ["7e7188bbe1417d280f7e883fe4b5ba15f10a7948"], "node": "87512692cb7125c9e24de0ef38b1ccba0b872451", "parents": ["c83b1eabcc89b3841cf611e475bcb8acc1b7231c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071984 [wpt PR 62679] - [Reference Target] Ensure events fire even when source targets its host, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Reference Target] Ensure events fire even when source targets its host\n\nWith reference target the command, interest, toggle, and submit events\ntreat the source/submitter element as the relatedTarget for event\ndispatch purposes. If the source event targets its own shadow host,\nthis actually causes the event path to be shrunk to nothing during\nEventPath::AdjustForRelatedTarget, preventing the event from being\ndispatched at all.\n\nEnsure the event is still dispatched against the host in such cases\nby using the original target (the host) as the related target.\n\nBug: 559225364\nChange-Id: I6afaf1d863f53daae0fbdff062cc574bcd1cc3ab\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8392862\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698141}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5762f1a4547d25c075c82d0be216f4283956e9eb\nwpt-pr: 62679\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/form-submission-0/submit-event-shadow-host.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestevent-dispatch-shadow.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/the-button-element/command-and-commandfor/commandfor-shadow-host.html"], "git_node": "c16625a8982794789cc2f424d7724aaa352f678c", "git_parents": ["7bd1efc6399dd8832068e787e1246e3a44c4812f"], "node": "e4879c26cbf51a22da4552cd42721e05458253d6", "parents": ["87512692cb7125c9e24de0ef38b1ccba0b872451"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071984 [wpt PR 62679] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62679\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/interestfor/interestevent-dispatch-shadow.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "07d77685da9fc4ae301c16c732e22da04333f717", "git_parents": ["c16625a8982794789cc2f424d7724aaa352f678c"], "node": "7c5921c991a2ba79bb3260704229a4377c1fc500", "parents": ["e4879c26cbf51a22da4552cd42721e05458253d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072385 [wpt PR 62453] - Reject invalid charsets in \u003clink rel=stylesheet\u003e, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReject invalid charsets in \u003clink rel=stylesheet\u003e\n\nThe page-windows-1251-charset-attribute-bogus WPT fails in Blink but is\npassing in Gecko and WebKit. In Blink, we only reject empty charsets.\nThis change upgrades this to an IsValid() check (which also rejects\nempty charsets). There weren't any tests for empty charset attribute\nvalues so this change adds one.\n\nBug: 40767468\nChange-Id: I96b780352750d2f3b1fdc0fa393102597d988a23\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8340310\nReviewed-by: Anders Hartvoll Ruud \u003candruud@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1693860}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3e032b690350e49daca68900bc0e38326de61eaf\nwpt-pr: 62453\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-syntax/charset/MANIFEST", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-syntax/charset/page-windows-1251-charset-attribute-empty.html"], "git_node": "367cb8b577bc06ae3d55f71def4f2df16d7b44b4", "git_parents": ["07d77685da9fc4ae301c16c732e22da04333f717"], "node": "957e9033ef005a9f88b89fa0e5aa5c65005a384c", "parents": ["7c5921c991a2ba79bb3260704229a4377c1fc500"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071525 [wpt PR 62578] - Fix XML parser crash when calling stop() from onreadystatechange., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix XML parser crash when calling stop() from onreadystatechange.\n\nThis applies the same fix to both the libxml and xml-rs parsers.\n\nFixed: 557778285\nChange-Id: Ia33a84aa315b7b2d18fd425430750b7059d2c8e3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8381676\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1696410}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a167d503e571fd7f3d93c31b49d3c679928a15ce\nwpt-pr: 62578\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/xml/onreadystatechange-crash-on-stop.xhtml"], "git_node": "d5f8ade3cb20207990bd6f8c69163f4dec165daa", "git_parents": ["367cb8b577bc06ae3d55f71def4f2df16d7b44b4"], "node": "7d1c064635d95627a564b82a6d3e358108693e97", "parents": ["957e9033ef005a9f88b89fa0e5aa5c65005a384c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071525 [wpt PR 62578] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62578\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/xml/onreadystatechange-crash-on-stop.xhtml.ini"], "git_node": "b3b418d3805338f0885ef7d440dd3ef788958030", "git_parents": ["d5f8ade3cb20207990bd6f8c69163f4dec165daa"], "node": "3faa940397b8943839408192d5f14b40a575e909", "parents": ["7d1c064635d95627a564b82a6d3e358108693e97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072339 [wpt PR 62716] - Maintain the kIsInShadowTree node flag in TreeScopeAdopter., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMaintain the kIsInShadowTree node flag in TreeScopeAdopter.\n\nDuring node insertion and removal operations we traverse the\ninserted/removed subtree and call InsertedInto or RemovedFrom on the\nnodes in the subtree.  During an InsertedInto or RemovedFrom call on a\nnode in the subtree, other nodes in the subtree are in a \"bad\" state\nwhere they have been inserted/removed, but InsertedInto/RemovedFrom has\nnot yet been called.\n\nThis change keeps the kIsInShadowTree flag more consistent with the tree\nscope, so that it is no longer one of the things that can be \"bad\" in\nthat bad state, and means that during a traversal of Node::InsertedInto\nor Node::RemovedFrom calls, the kIsInShadowTree flag has already been\nupdated for all of the nodes being traversed.\n\nRight now RemovedFrom can trigger other traversals via the following stack:\n    RemovedFrom () at element.cc:4652\n    RemoveFromTopLayerImmediately () at document.cc:8758\n    ElementRemovedFromTopLayer () at display_lock_document_state.cc:247\n    MarkAncestorContextsHaveTopLayerElement () at display_lock_document_state.cc:257\n    ParentElement () at flat_tree_traversal.h:219\n    Parent () at flat_tree_traversal.h:213\n    TraverseParent () at flat_tree_traversal.cc:180\n    AssignedNodes () at html_slot_element.cc:87\n    GetSlotAssignment () at shadow_root.h:120\nIn this stack, Node::RemovedFrom calls RemoveFromTopLayerImmediately,\nwhich does a fresh set of flat tree traversals from all elements that\nremain in the top layer.  Those traversals can reach elements that are\nstill to come in the Node::RemovedFrom traversal, and that thus without\nthis change will have their kIsInShadowTreeFlag set incorrectly, which\ncan lead to a null dereference when HTMLSlotElement::AssignedNodes calls\nGetSlotAssignment() on the null result of ContainingShadowRoot() because\nSupportsAssignment() checked the (stale) flag and returned true.\n\nFixed: 550975373\nChange-Id: Id9579dd24a7cbe85ce0f0b3d8cdb9e4267e95e73\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8389929\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698198}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a878e03641dc4500b9447342def9f031a4ebb8ca\nwpt-pr: 62716\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-position/crashtests/top-layer-slot-adopt-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-position/crashtests/top-layer-slot-remove-crash.html"], "git_node": "98b3ae25a5c0d78f5bec30dbdad7a599fdce087f", "git_parents": ["b3b418d3805338f0885ef7d440dd3ef788958030"], "node": "fddf8db2cf836d161ebb72832b30e5ae07053bf4", "parents": ["3faa940397b8943839408192d5f14b40a575e909"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071174 [wpt PR 62611] - Reland \"Move Translator create user activation WPT to its own file\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReland \"Move Translator create user activation WPT to its own file\" (#62611)\n\nThis is a reland of commit 5edb7e90d621f54db30c9777b7616d0da07c2ffb\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Built-In AI: Move Translator create user activation WPT to its own file\n\u003e\n\u003e When running chrome_wpt_tests on bots with pre-installed or sideloaded\n\u003e models, Translator availability starts as available. This caused the\n\u003e downloadable precondition assertion in\n\u003e translator.optional.https.window.js to fail, flakily failing the entire\n\u003e test suite despite all translation functionality subtests passing.\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: 510552929\n\u003e Change-Id: I7987656d0a8eb8f24299277d927c2a8f1d9fb332\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8280374\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Danilo Tedeschi \u003cdanft@google.com\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Danilo Tedeschi \u003cdanft@google.com\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1687658}\n\nBug: 510552929\nChange-Id: I5ec38d6670c75667d33866f6ca8b82ebadd3c2e5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8392297\nReviewed-by: Danilo Tedeschi \u003cdanft@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Paula G\u00f3mez \u003cpaugomez@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1695854}\n\nCo-authored-by: Paula Gomez \u003cpaugomez@google.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e03210d8366a4f330e19b4929023d1a2b5e1230c\nwpt-pr: 62611\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/ai/resources/util.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/translator/resources/util.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/translator/translator-create-user-activation.optional.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/translator/translator.optional.https.window.js"], "git_node": "e0a5faa0cb99b2431238a46da2f577a322d2741c", "git_parents": ["98b3ae25a5c0d78f5bec30dbdad7a599fdce087f"], "node": "939a81821e644685d9f3147bf660c4d59dae270c", "parents": ["fddf8db2cf836d161ebb72832b30e5ae07053bf4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071174 [wpt PR 62611] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62611\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/ai/language-model/language-model-create.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/language_detection/detector.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/semantic_embedder/semantic-embedder-downloadprogress-abort.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/translator/translator-create-user-activation.optional.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/translator/translator.optional.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "709996bd2070439f0f28211818b2e02030ef2bd3", "git_parents": ["e0a5faa0cb99b2431238a46da2f577a322d2741c"], "node": "c9dce95c701e823f937e06b2a3566e14835c0d2c", "parents": ["939a81821e644685d9f3147bf660c4d59dae270c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072397 [wpt PR 62722] - [Translator API WPTs] Fix test preconditions for downloadable models, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Translator API WPTs] Fix test preconditions for downloadable models\n\nFixes Translator WPT failures on bots where the translation models are\n'downloadable' rather than immediately 'available'\n(https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chrome/builders/luci.chrome.ci/optimization_guide-mac-arm64).\n- util.js: Allow createTranslator() to proceed if the model is\n  'downloadable', as the helper already provides the user activation\n  needed to trigger the download.\n- translator-create-user-activation: Make the test resilient to the\n  initial model availability state by only enforcing the user\n  activation rejection check if the model actually needs to be\n  downloaded. Also fixes premature consumption of transient user\n  activation that caused spurious NotAllowedError failures.\n\nBug: 510552929\nChange-Id: I1e779be32ac2a2a22cef77f55630fe423fd1edc1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8395053\nCommit-Queue: Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Paula G\u00f3mez \u003cpaugomez@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1696661}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 20c4d6d49cb41d33f119f42eee16befd4d4d6a53\nwpt-pr: 62722\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/ai/translator/resources/util.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/translator/translator-create-user-activation.optional.https.window.js"], "git_node": "ab5b5afb7af4af5e1832af809dcd4ebd16ed84be", "git_parents": ["709996bd2070439f0f28211818b2e02030ef2bd3"], "node": "7c91bdeee67d27bf2cf88e1fe527f9d63005da5e", "parents": ["c9dce95c701e823f937e06b2a3566e14835c0d2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072397 [wpt PR 62722] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62722\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/ai/translator/translator-create-user-activation.optional.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "e1343c5816f7bb0688278cf724b53cdd0e12c64f", "git_parents": ["ab5b5afb7af4af5e1832af809dcd4ebd16ed84be"], "node": "bf236b82a578929be960e91e88d38640435ad03e", "parents": ["7c91bdeee67d27bf2cf88e1fe527f9d63005da5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072375 [wpt PR 62720] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=304242, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=304242 (#62720)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2837762f3245f59f87cabf5d4455a3896e0b3373\nwpt-pr: 62720\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-template-columns-rows-resolved-values-003.html"], "git_node": "b1d153005260f0dd01ed1c1ee1177f3a9a6147e3", "git_parents": ["e1343c5816f7bb0688278cf724b53cdd0e12c64f"], "node": "cd4beb80a71844054656a59ec4be2ce5961fa336", "parents": ["bf236b82a578929be960e91e88d38640435ad03e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072368 [wpt PR 62718] - Serialize timeline-trigger shorthand as empty when lengths don't match, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSerialize timeline-trigger shorthand as empty when lengths don't match\n\nThe timeline-trigger shorthand requires all longhands to be included. If\nthe lengths of the longhand comma-separate lists don't match, serialize\nas the empty string.\n\nFixes out-of-bounds array access crash while also only serialize\nshorthand values which can round-trip.\n\nBug: 559456620, 558415429\nChange-Id: I83ef08dd5471610b83eb1b1b39833ba4c807e658\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8395869\nReviewed-by: David A \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698259}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4bdf8816a8df45081257ba387fccd240855c9bd0\nwpt-pr: 62718\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/animation-trigger/parsing/timeline-trigger-empty-shorthand.tentative.html"], "git_node": "15286ba23c5067a51799b10d7ed7369b2ed5c1f3", "git_parents": ["b1d153005260f0dd01ed1c1ee1177f3a9a6147e3"], "node": "57da6840b4d638c74fdeef966640553546b8382d", "parents": ["cd4beb80a71844054656a59ec4be2ce5961fa336"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072368 [wpt PR 62718] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62718\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/animation-trigger/parsing/timeline-trigger-empty-shorthand.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "1c64939cd2df52a8d448662947e6e5f8f3b03bd9", "git_parents": ["15286ba23c5067a51799b10d7ed7369b2ed5c1f3"], "node": "bd1d00af5e8a24c3193a09a5d37190858d375f25", "parents": ["57da6840b4d638c74fdeef966640553546b8382d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072402 [wpt PR 62711] - [css-animation]: Fix tracking of attr-taint, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-animation]: Fix tracking of attr-taint\n\nAttr-taint was being tracked in CSSInterpolationEnvironment and in\nCSSDefaultInterpolationValue, for transition and non-transition cases,\nrespectively. For CSS Animations, the taint may be caught after\ncreating of the environment and passing as a const reference to the\ninterpolation code. In addition, the signature of the resolve method\nsuggests the same environment may be shared. It was not, and this is\nnow clarified by baking the PropertyHandle into the environment.\nWhether the value is tainted or not is now stored directly in the\ninterpolation value. This addresses both constness of the environment\nand consolidation of the code paths.\n\nThanks to Yoshisato Yanagisawa for the prototype patch, which served\nas a basis for this patch including tests.\n\nBug: 537109293\nChange-Id: Ie5ced2263c5bc64a333ba47422e3552c3a965afa\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8405230\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698281}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cdc36a0e3a858e6050db31148263963ee6ab7780\nwpt-pr: 62711\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/attr-security-animation.html"], "git_node": "6974c3cadab4f2fd76a84bb050053737a72cdf8d", "git_parents": ["1c64939cd2df52a8d448662947e6e5f8f3b03bd9"], "node": "b3cb5ea99e7e09828d9d95e6013d238b53fc08ac", "parents": ["bd1d00af5e8a24c3193a09a5d37190858d375f25"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072408 [wpt PR 62723] - Visibility should not affect scrollability, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nVisibility should not affect scrollability\n\nThis patch brings our behavior in-line with Gecko.\n\nFixed: 41291752, 425353152\nChange-Id: I0c45acc7f3eb591a7aeed22bc32aab6891f0fad6\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8404256\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698341}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2b96f72d7142f22d1fecf225031e7b43a7b94bf9\nwpt-pr: 62723\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/events/scrolling/visibility-hidden-scrolls.html"], "git_node": "e4217ace6fe0effb55e2ec252f92a61758970856", "git_parents": ["6974c3cadab4f2fd76a84bb050053737a72cdf8d"], "node": "a53d0ed857ef73d32e91be9f4116c991f39fcba8", "parents": ["b3cb5ea99e7e09828d9d95e6013d238b53fc08ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072408 [wpt PR 62723] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62723\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/events/scrolling/scroll-cross-origin-iframes.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/events/scrolling/visibility-hidden-scrolls.html.ini"], "git_node": "b7c24d27396f534995bd5c9e36d85d5b2ca8d3e1", "git_parents": ["e4217ace6fe0effb55e2ec252f92a61758970856"], "node": "8c129e73254064ef792f792f32b5e5665b7c965e", "parents": ["a53d0ed857ef73d32e91be9f4116c991f39fcba8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Manuel Rego \u003crego@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072477 [wpt PR 62548] - aamtests: Refactor find_node to share implementation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\naamtests: Refactor find_node to share implementation (#62548)\n\nEach platform wrapper was re-implementing this method.\nThis patch moves it to ApiWrapper so the code is shared.\n\nThe only behavioral change is that AT-SPI wasn't using _poll_for()\nwhen searching for the element (the other platforms already do it).\nThis seems a better option in case the node isn't exposed yet,\nand makes tests more consistent across platforms.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 39371374c6d1f4b06c5652ba85cffd80c6689d9b\nwpt-pr: 62548\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/core-aam/aamtests/support/api_wrapper.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/core-aam/aamtests/support/atspi_wrapper.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/core-aam/aamtests/support/axapi_wrapper.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/core-aam/aamtests/support/ia2_wrapper.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/core-aam/aamtests/support/uia_wrapper.py"], "git_node": "8f98810f1e700bd3497643663839b4851ac908fa", "git_parents": ["b7c24d27396f534995bd5c9e36d85d5b2ca8d3e1"], "node": "9ea97322eccbbc350102dd476e81e6e8e396c70c", "parents": ["8c129e73254064ef792f792f32b5e5665b7c965e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Jansen \u003cjohnjansen@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072444 [wpt PR 62724] - Add two tests based on conversation with CSSWG and ARIA., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd two tests based on conversation with CSSWG and ARIA.\n\nConcern was raised in the CSSWG that line-clamp and overflow-clip were\nnot behaving as expected in the DOM. After a conversation in ARIA, it\nwas determined they are.\n\nThese tests were suggested to confirm they always do.\n\nR=jamescscott@google.com\n\nChange-Id: I66bcfacaca06c91216f75b8a147a6241c6708a05\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8352688\nCommit-Queue: John Jansen \u003cjohnjansen@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698509}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a5c37c15a6527ede34ec8715c5c75711fbc50340\nwpt-pr: 62724\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-preserves-dom-content.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/overflow-clip-preserves-dom-content.html"], "git_node": "826294e4ad89fa611974ac29072f8a7809b90f1a", "git_parents": ["8f98810f1e700bd3497643663839b4851ac908fa"], "node": "59f97a8026f710101b95641f95e18fc397fc0f39", "parents": ["9ea97322eccbbc350102dd476e81e6e8e396c70c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072486 [wpt PR 62730] - [AI WPTs] Move Summarizer concurrent summarize WPT to its own file, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[AI WPTs] Move Summarizer concurrent summarize WPT to its own file\n\nMove the 'Multiple Summarizer.summarize() calls are resolved\nsuccessfully' subtest into a separate test file\n(summarizer-summarize-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js).\n\nOn NanoV3 CPU, concurrent calls reject with AbortError due to an\non-device model service crash (crbug.com/560176361). Isolating this\nsubtest allows the remaining five subtests in\nsummarizer-summarize.tentative.https.window.html to maintain strict\npass expectations without being masked by file-level failure\nexpectations.\n\nBug: 560176361\nChange-Id: Ib0d8ff70729bbaaaa6526e0adaea16a650d1a450\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8394095\nAuto-Submit: Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike Wasserman \u003cmsw@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698533}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: de4b591a7619053dde5ea91a8718071f90119099\nwpt-pr: 62730\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/ai/summarizer/summarizer-summarize-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/summarizer/summarizer-summarize.tentative.https.window.js"], "git_node": "8efe85e862aacae928237b144d7d4aae60d53039", "git_parents": ["826294e4ad89fa611974ac29072f8a7809b90f1a"], "node": "03d50991a121844395013bc304ad7b07912f4c27", "parents": ["59f97a8026f710101b95641f95e18fc397fc0f39"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072486 [wpt PR 62730] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62730\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/ai/summarizer/summarizer-summarize-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "14cf9c8e499ed93d230b60e42eebf2dce7a563b0", "git_parents": ["8efe85e862aacae928237b144d7d4aae60d53039"], "node": "c6b09ad336f6bb135ac205a969113ac38c23108a", "parents": ["03d50991a121844395013bc304ad7b07912f4c27"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072500 [wpt PR 62733] - [svg] Mark the z-index test tentative, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[svg] Mark the z-index test tentative (#62733)\n\nSVG 2 deferred z-index to a future version of SVG (svgwg#483, PR#489),\nso nothing normative requires this rendering today and the test's\nrel=help at render.html#ZIndexProperty has not resolved since. It fails\nin every shipping engine.\n\nRemoval was the obvious move and is the wrong one. WebKit's\nlayer-based SVG engine renders it: LBSE makes every SVG renderer an\nordinary CSS layer, so the generic z-index sorting reaches SVG elements\nand the reference is what gets painted. It has been marked passing in\nWebKit's LBSE expectations since January. Deleting the file would leave\nthat rendering with no coverage anywhere the day that engine ships, and\nsvgwg#483 deferred the feature rather than rejecting it, so the question\nis open rather than settled.\n\nTentative says what removal was meant to say, that no specification\nrequires this, without discarding the test.\n\n  https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/issues/62732\n  https://github.com/w3c/svgwg/issues/483\n  https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=309046\n\nrel=help now points at render.html#RenderingOrder, which exists, plus\nthe tracking issue, matching how the other tentative tests under svg/\ncite theirs. The WEB_FEATURES.yml row is dropped rather than renamed\nbecause no tentative test under svg/ appears in one, and a\nnon-normative test should not count toward a feature's support numbers.\n\nz-index-ref.svg keeps its name, as with use-element-transitions-ref.html\nnext to use-element-transitions.tentative.html.\n\nNo test results change.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 086382f6be913c002086731f3d786aa43cf1a8df\nwpt-pr: 62733\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/render/order/WEB_FEATURES.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/render/order/z-index.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/render/order/z-index.tentative.svg"], "git_node": "1b4c4b5ec897bd8e1d8c006a66c87b208ed0a973", "git_parents": ["14cf9c8e499ed93d230b60e42eebf2dce7a563b0"], "node": "a17b4d61618d92e1eadc572f550d92e1c9622093", "parents": ["c6b09ad336f6bb135ac205a969113ac38c23108a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072500 [wpt PR 62733] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62733\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/render/order/z-index.svg.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/render/order/z-index.tentative.svg.ini"], "git_node": "6965ddc5fd8682ae96717bd06d4b8a520dedcc98", "git_parents": ["1b4c4b5ec897bd8e1d8c006a66c87b208ed0a973"], "node": "c8e92229528aa4e46c56cc826cd9f7014c214990", "parents": ["a17b4d61618d92e1eadc572f550d92e1c9622093"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072485 [wpt PR 62729] - [gap-decorations] Preserve multicol rule pattern across fragmentation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[gap-decorations] Preserve multicol rule pattern across fragmentation\n\nPer CSSWG resolution [1], a row gap suppressed at a fragmentation\nboundary still consumes one value from the gap-decoration pattern, so\nlist-valued row rules are assigned consistently in fragmented and\nunfragmented contexts. Grid implements this already; this change does\nthe same for multicol.\n\nThis change preserves the row-rule pattern, including auto repeaters,\nacross those fragments.\n\nThe break token records where the next fragment should continue in the\nrow-rule pattern, counting suppressed row gaps but not rows that\ncontinue across a boundary. During painting, this saved position is\ncombined with the gap's index in its fragment, while the last fragment\nprovides the total row-gap count needed by auto repeaters. We ignore\nspanner main gaps because they do not represent painted row gaps.\n\n[1]\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13754#issuecomment-4298143982\n\nBug: 505387221\nChange-Id: Ib2a01dbf125a60c1ea63db4393a831ed5f5fac03\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8373741\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698547}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5c3111d503f82f9f7e8b14ea9bf3079e8dad7069\nwpt-pr: 62729\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-004.html"], "git_node": "0c9eb93b75850326a72f7a2262ff4bc02c07f5ad", "git_parents": ["6965ddc5fd8682ae96717bd06d4b8a520dedcc98"], "node": "deb0e59218f2c64c627150b088cf380440accb41", "parents": ["c8e92229528aa4e46c56cc826cd9f7014c214990"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072485 [wpt PR 62729] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62729\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-gap-decorations-fragmentation-004.html.ini"], "git_node": "71d36a77779d1bb69d935d207ae3a5b91a6b5f42", "git_parents": ["0c9eb93b75850326a72f7a2262ff4bc02c07f5ad"], "node": "91fbf9b715b05891c1a934930bbe0e7b266254a9", "parents": ["deb0e59218f2c64c627150b088cf380440accb41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072479 [wpt PR 62727] - [menu a11y] Change submenu aria role to list, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[menu a11y] Change submenu aria role to list\n\nWhen a page violates the content model of the new\nmenubar/menuitem/menulist/submenu elements, only the top-most menu\nshould get a role of dialog. If submenus also got dialog (as is the case\ntoday), there would be nested dialogs, which would be confusing for the\nSR user. So we are going to try giving submenus a list role.\n\nWe will test this in a few screen readers and might have to punt to just\ngiving submenus a generic role if the list announcements are incongruous\nwith the keyboard interaction pattern.\n\nWe also now count more elements in the X of Y announcements, e.g.\n\u003cmenubar\u003e\n  \u003cmenuitem\u003eFile\u003c/menuitem\u003e \u003c!-- \"1 of 3\" --\u003e\n  \u003cbutton\u003eInvalid\u003c/button\u003e  \u003c!-- \"2 of 3\" --\u003e\n  \u003cmenuitem\u003eEdit\u003c/menuitem\u003e \u003c!-- \"3 of 3\" --\u003e\n\u003c/menubar\u003e\n\nPreviously, we did not count the violating content, which is the button\nin that example.\n\nNote that these announcement rules are subject to change pending\nfeedback from screen-reader users.\n\nBug: 425682466\nChange-Id: Id4de3cd61f11685e71dc412a6042f5c765968577\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8401197\nCommit-Queue: David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Lucas Radaelli \u003clucasradaelli@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698579}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7c20438303d2b39c8a2b924ed57dfa6448fd2ed2\nwpt-pr: 62727\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-content-model-violation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/reparent-with-pending-dialog-microtask.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/valid-submenu-invalid-root.html"], "git_node": "2cb9d3246d4dee52dc57dd07239e8bfc121252ae", "git_parents": ["71d36a77779d1bb69d935d207ae3a5b91a6b5f42"], "node": "6f51ac407a909ebd3966e0df963128b63ef83b87", "parents": ["91fbf9b715b05891c1a934930bbe0e7b266254a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072479 [wpt PR 62727] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62727\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-content-model-violation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/valid-submenu-invalid-root.html.ini"], "git_node": "ab5b717f33b8261abf13a11b6f359a53cfa83269", "git_parents": ["2cb9d3246d4dee52dc57dd07239e8bfc121252ae"], "node": "cdc3ec029d62cacfc5c1cbbcdaab5f3c4f06ab65", "parents": ["6f51ac407a909ebd3966e0df963128b63ef83b87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072298 [wpt PR 62715] - Fetch: a FormData body should survive collection of its source, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFetch: a FormData body should survive collection of its source\n\nA body extracted from a FormData object keeps that object as its source, so the\nFiles it holds, and their blob URL registrations, have to stay alive for as long\nas the body can be read. Covers Response, Request, a clone, and reading the body\nas a stream.\n\nWebKit kept only the blob URLs, so reading such a body after a collection failed\nwith an InvalidStateError.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d556bd72998c2a11556dc692a3e7c10347d1accc\nwpt-pr: 62715\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/api/basic/gc.any.js"], "git_node": "7a5f8b9f1f207e096819a0c846ea0c67e98b9469", "git_parents": ["ab5b717f33b8261abf13a11b6f359a53cfa83269"], "node": "b98921a05e64de66adc9dcaf398bb9b05e2e5c28", "parents": ["cdc3ec029d62cacfc5c1cbbcdaab5f3c4f06ab65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072531 [wpt PR 62738] - Fetch: a moved FormData body should survive collection of its source, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFetch: a moved FormData body should survive collection of its source\n\nConstructing a Request from a Request moves the body over, so the FormData that\nis its source has to move with it. Follow-up to the cases covered by the\npreceding commit.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c7382326bf8a90cef4490a6522b9593e43894fe6\nwpt-pr: 62738\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/api/basic/gc.any.js"], "git_node": "635691402e18ffa0ed503e2138de5318cb4df6c0", "git_parents": ["7a5f8b9f1f207e096819a0c846ea0c67e98b9469"], "node": "253baa4d72a50b6081daa2bbee5f063a180a29da", "parents": ["b98921a05e64de66adc9dcaf398bb9b05e2e5c28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Will Harris \u003cwfh@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072451 [wpt PR 62725] - Validate accessor callability in V8ObjectToPropertyDescriptor, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nValidate accessor callability in V8ObjectToPropertyDescriptor\n\nV8ObjectToPropertyDescriptor previously omitted checking whether present\nget and set attributes are callable or undefined per ECMA-262\nToPropertyDescriptor (steps 12.b and 14.b). During reentrant descriptor\nconversion in the ObservableArray defineProperty trap, non-callable\nvalues could be passed to v8::PropertyDescriptor and installed as an\nAccessorPair, causing type confusion in V8.\n\nEnforce that present getter and setter properties are either undefined\nor callable functions, throwing a TypeError otherwise.\n\nBug: 557523002\nChange-Id: Ia524d3c71cb5bb6085ef1d2bc0af650b55a87e9c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8405731\nReviewed-by: Nate Chapin \u003cjaphet@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Will Harris \u003cwfh@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698665}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 22e06bc9a294de61e3d7c32b3af29ee3f4c7dea0\nwpt-pr: 62725\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/adoptedstylesheets-observablearray.html"], "git_node": "b82e3d9bf6af16051e81e96a193e55e17372f875", "git_parents": ["635691402e18ffa0ed503e2138de5318cb4df6c0"], "node": "ecfffe084748fc6636ec1ef91c35a86f38187695", "parents": ["253baa4d72a50b6081daa2bbee5f063a180a29da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072451 [wpt PR 62725] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62725\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom/CSSRuleList-appendRule-keyframe-001-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom/CSSRuleList-appendRule-keyframe-002-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom/adoptedstylesheets-observablearray.html.ini"], "git_node": "e3a92fc1440358aa70e40f54f0ae192607510a9f", "git_parents": ["b82e3d9bf6af16051e81e96a193e55e17372f875"], "node": "dcff5117db8756619d55c53a47b17e266ac08d60", "parents": ["ecfffe084748fc6636ec1ef91c35a86f38187695"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fran\u00e7ois Beaufort \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072343 [wpt PR 62717] - [WebMCP] Disallow declarative tool registration without allow-scripts, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebMCP] Disallow declarative tool registration without allow-scripts\n\nScheduleDeclarativeWebMCPToolRegistration() in HTMLFormElement did not\nverify whether scripts are allowed before scheduling declarative WebMCP\ntool registration. Consequently, sandboxed iframes without\nallow-scripts were able to register declarative WebMCP tools via \u003cform\u003e\nattributes.\n\nThis CL adds a check for IsSandboxed(WebSandboxFlags::kScripts) to\nScheduleDeclarativeWebMCPToolRegistration() to prevent registration in\ncontexts where script execution is sandboxed, matching the capability\nrequirements of the imperative registerTool() API.\n\nBug: 526451590\nChange-Id: I5eb9bb96997dc320a7333cd5afc9dcb2c4127869\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8394892\nCommit-Queue: Fr \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698689}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2c948ca7cd1a9bff711cdc8e5b2406fd10041ef8\nwpt-pr: 62717\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/sandboxed-iframe.https.html"], "git_node": "33a952ef7701765b9f418730628d16c5e017d198", "git_parents": ["e3a92fc1440358aa70e40f54f0ae192607510a9f"], "node": "dc01f8a9fa3d68199ce1b57ba46043675333a2f2", "parents": ["dcff5117db8756619d55c53a47b17e266ac08d60"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072343 [wpt PR 62717] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62717\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/declarative/sandboxed-iframe.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "49923d6e81ebbc2c756ad73b3f768946f9d2418a", "git_parents": ["33a952ef7701765b9f418730628d16c5e017d198"], "node": "5d18e7f8f9c01ebb240765369c261fcd20900abb", "parents": ["dc01f8a9fa3d68199ce1b57ba46043675333a2f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Minseop Choi \u003cminsubb13@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072525 [wpt PR 62737] - [WebCrypto] Fix exportKey() and wrapKey() error ordering, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebCrypto] Fix exportKey() and wrapKey() error ordering\n\nBoth methods are specified to check that the key's algorithm supports\nthe export key operation before checking [[extractable]]. Blink skipped\nthe first check and threw an InvalidAccessError where the spec requires\na NotSupportedError:\n\nhttps://w3c.github.io/webcrypto/#SubtleCrypto-method-exportKey\nhttps://w3c.github.io/webcrypto/#SubtleCrypto-method-wrapKey\n\nAdd kWebCryptoOperationExportKey to the algorithm info table and check\nit first. HKDF and PBKDF2 are the only algorithms that do not register\nthe operation, so the HKDF exportKey web test is rebaselined.\n\nBug: 41264071\nChange-Id: I08f50b826fe970a5dcb49098dc158a341ca0faf2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8312049\nCommit-Queue: Minseop Choi \u003cminsubb13@gmail.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: David Benjamin \u003cdavidben@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Daniel Cheng \u003cdcheng@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698698}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f91bc17a225a1f884b85351f580634308bb5f554\nwpt-pr: 62737\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/WebCryptoAPI/export-key-error-order.https.any.js"], "git_node": "0938d3ec4793c95b224497d6a5f7c58ddb6c0401", "git_parents": ["49923d6e81ebbc2c756ad73b3f768946f9d2418a"], "node": "66e1bb474f818a822e5dcd916b68412f717bf0d3", "parents": ["5d18e7f8f9c01ebb240765369c261fcd20900abb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072525 [wpt PR 62737] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62737\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/export-key-error-order.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "d283bfc9667f0a0cc90667af6af0ad1ece135bd8", "git_parents": ["0938d3ec4793c95b224497d6a5f7c58ddb6c0401"], "node": "c1b62563bb9aaab0ca81f8780b33c5672dbfdd11", "parents": ["66e1bb474f818a822e5dcd916b68412f717bf0d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Euclid Ye \u003cyezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072112 [wpt PR 62700] - webdriver: Dispatch element click and send keys via \"dispatch a list of actions\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwdspec: Element click dispatches its pointer actions in a single tick.\n\nSigned-off-by: Euclid Ye \u003cyezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a8ca9a003ebedd1dea54990b8f6fc82feaf6bb6e\nwpt-pr: 62700\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/element_click/single_tick.py"], "git_node": "121e4ff6b93ba66aefb3e343e5ad004face822cf", "git_parents": ["d283bfc9667f0a0cc90667af6af0ad1ece135bd8"], "node": "9edb08e3e72487f07c8688de18051a3ad41a6db2", "parents": ["c1b62563bb9aaab0ca81f8780b33c5672dbfdd11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072112 [wpt PR 62700] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62700\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/element_click/bubbling.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/element_click/center_point.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/element_click/click.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/element_click/user_prompts.py.ini"], "git_node": "61876d147a70ac46dae4642415247f554e9e9b1f", "git_parents": ["121e4ff6b93ba66aefb3e343e5ad004face822cf"], "node": "9123214f9e0bbe02b1fe0afbe9120d25df0c58a8", "parents": ["9edb08e3e72487f07c8688de18051a3ad41a6db2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071803 [wpt PR 62669] - [MathML] Add a test to trigger click from a keydown event, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[MathML] Add a test to trigger click from a keydown event\n\nThe user agent should allow the user to manually trigger elements that\nhave an activation behavior, for instance using keyboard or voice\ninput.[1]\n\n[1] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#activation\n\nBug: 510487697\nChange-Id: Ie6074431e0bf2962e3bd4eec40c595ebd1a809f2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8253691\nReviewed-by: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Manuel Rego Casasnovas \u003crego@igalia.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698726}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8663db42d894db3522a8ac635de99317c37ae888\nwpt-pr: 62669\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-keydown-enter.html"], "git_node": "604f480c2c30e1d3350081f407f2e0479991cd03", "git_parents": ["61876d147a70ac46dae4642415247f554e9e9b1f"], "node": "15ac2f2c00d30c2b63276699d56e51314381ed8f", "parents": ["9123214f9e0bbe02b1fe0afbe9120d25df0c58a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Ding \u003calanding@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072021 [wpt PR 62337] - ai: Pre-append prompt templates and establish init barrier for Writing Assistance APIs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nai: Pre-append prompt templates and establish init barrier for Writing Assistance APIs\n\nPre-append static options and shared context (the system prompt\ntemplate) to the on-device session during creation for AISummarizer,\nAIWriter, and AIRewriter via OnDeviceSession::SetInput.\n\nPer-request dynamic execution fields (article, instructions,\nrewrite_text, and per-request context) are marked as pending on the\ninitial MultimodalMessage so that template substitution halts at the\nstatic prefix without evaluating empty execution strings or generating\npremature control tokens.\n\nThis change accomplishes two objectives:\n- crbug.com/540980352: Blocks create() promise resolution until the underlying On-Device Model Service (ODMS) has fully initialized the engine and model weights, eliminating the cold-start penalty currently incurred during the first summarize()/write()/rewrite() call.\n- crbug.com/390006887: Pre-populates and caches the static prompt options and shared context in the session KV cache during session creation, avoiding redundant re-tokenization on every execution call.\n\nAutomated tests:\n- Add prompt verification tests across AIWriter, AIRewriter, and\n  AISummarizer unit tests to check substituted prompt strings.\n- Add multi-execution session reuse tests to verify shared context\n  caching across sequential requests.\n- Add unit test for MultimodalMessage::Merge pending overlay clearance.\n\nBug: 390006887, 540980352\nChange-Id: I199e35e62e6f084f490965a7d8bb7eafda27393c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8255743\nCommit-Queue: Alan Ding \u003calanding@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nathan Memmott \u003cmemmott@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Steven Holte \u003cholte@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike Wasserman \u003cmsw@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698718}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ba6d9f678ee91de9f58097921ed34e9b6b6849d3\nwpt-pr: 62337\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/ai/rewriter/rewriter-create-user-activation.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/summarizer/summarizer-create-user-activation.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/writer/writer-create-user-activation.tentative.https.window.js"], "git_node": "1b17cd2f577cd7e681a0ec962a5953a1337bfbbf", "git_parents": ["604f480c2c30e1d3350081f407f2e0479991cd03"], "node": "ca0d89e2374e744cea10cab0f792f1b4690cb50e", "parents": ["15ac2f2c00d30c2b63276699d56e51314381ed8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Lilley \u003cchris@w3.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071145 [wpt PR 62570] - Add style query tests for powerless color components (CSS Color 4 step 1), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd style query tests for powerless color components (CSS Color 4 step 1) (#62570)\n\n* Add style query tests for powerless color components\n\nCSS Color 4 step 1 of the equivalent-colors algorithm converts powerless\ncomponents to missing components before anything is compared, so two colors\ndiffering only in a powerless hue are equivalent. Nothing covered this: the\nexisting query-style-color.html compares spellings of black that all differ\nin notation, so it exercises the sRGB grouping and step 4 but never a pair\nin the same color space with differing powerless hues.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\n* Drop the hsl() and hwb() epsilon-boundary subtests\n\nhsl() and hwb() resolve to sRGB colors, so at the powerless epsilon the\nresidual hue leaves the two resolved values exactly 1e-5 apart. Step 2's\nepsilon is implementation-defined, so an implementation may legitimately\ncall that pair equal or unequal, and the subtests asserted an answer the\nspec does not determine. The lch() and oklch() boundary cases are kept:\nthose colors keep their own color space, so their hues stay far apart and\nonly the powerless step can make them equal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 15df54d4459b78242d32ae36f9c094a96972bedc\nwpt-pr: 62570\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/container-queries/query-style-color-powerless.html"], "git_node": "9d8da811b352f9901f87761553d396b9d4f31a76", "git_parents": ["1b17cd2f577cd7e681a0ec962a5953a1337bfbbf"], "node": "fc3b4a583a5cfd3a02e977392bf437a5a6b94c1a", "parents": ["ca0d89e2374e744cea10cab0f792f1b4690cb50e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071145 [wpt PR 62570] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62570\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/crashtests/br-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/crashtests/canvas-as-container-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/query-style-color-powerless.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/whitespace-update-after-removal.html.ini"], "git_node": "78b8eb0b996802c7646005e3c7a9ec233968bd91", "git_parents": ["9d8da811b352f9901f87761553d396b9d4f31a76"], "node": "28056025c3d239ce380eeef4d0d8ecb3507a0c5d", "parents": ["fc3b4a583a5cfd3a02e977392bf437a5a6b94c1a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072892 - [wpt-sync] Update web-platform-tests to 15df54d4459b78242d32ae36f9c094a96972bedc, a=testonly\n\nMANUAL PUSH: wpt sync bot\n\nwpt-head: 15df54d4459b78242d32ae36f9c094a96972bedc\nwpt-type: landing\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/ai/summarizer/summarizer-summarize.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/translator/translator-create-user-activation.optional.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/translator/translator.optional.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/core-aam/aamtests/attribute/aria_autocomplete_inline_list_both.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/core-aam/aamtests/attribute/aria_braillelabel.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/render-corner-shape.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/ink-overflow-001-print.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/whitespace-update-after-removal.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-parsing-and-computed-style.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/mask-image/backdrop-filter-bad-mask-image.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/mask-image/backdrop-filter-mask-image-while-loading.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overscroll-behavior/overscroll-behavior.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/text-transform/text-transform-upperlower-108.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/api/cors/cors-cookies.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/api/credentials/cookies.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/local-network-access/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/local-network-access/service-worker.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html-ruby-extensions/html-ruby-415.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/the-window-object/window-aliases.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/the-window-object/window-open-invalid-url.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/interaction/focus/processing-model/focus-fixup-rule-one-no-dialogs.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/common-HTMLOptionsCollection.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-summary-element/interactive-content.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-content-model-violation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/valid-submenu-invalid-root.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/modulepreload-referrerpolicy.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/infrastructure/assumptions/blank.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/infrastructure/webdriver/tests/test_load_file.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/dynamic-mozilla-162063.xhtml.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-record/passthrough/MediaRecorder-passthrough.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mozilla-sync", "testing/web-platform/meta/pointerevents/pointerevent_touch-action-pan-up-css_touch.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/resize-observer/observer-in-cross-origin-frame.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/screen-capture/getdisplaymedia-framerate.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/storage-access-api/storage-access-headers.tentative.https.sub.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/types/scripted/SVGGraphicsElement.getBBox-02.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/video-rvfc/request-video-frame-callback-webrtc.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-analysernode-interface/realtimeanalyser-fft-scaling.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-convolvernode-interface/convolution-mono-mono.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-convolvernode-interface/convolver-cascade.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-convolvernode-interface/convolver-response-1-chan.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-mediastreamaudiosourcenode-interface/mediastreamaudiosourcenode-routing.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-oscillatornode-interface/osc-basic-waveform.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-pannernode-interface/panner-hrtf-negative-elevation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/full-cycle-test.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder-hbd.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder-rescaling.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/videoFrame-copy