 "parents": ["845a1b8a6550439e0a035a8f3316b1b33eef0b0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "theidkamp \u003ctheidkamp@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072671 - Remove the primary-password guard from storage_operation_time telemetry r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers,dimi\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327300\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/browser/browser_login_storage_migrator.js"], "git_node": "e794155692781ddbec3cdaa9f629dd7c97237812", "git_parents": ["0ab7da7868c75a0443d70a29223cb804d37b080e"], "node": "707cfe811edc2a77579a185c0a65dee079967fb6", "parents": ["96515c76b20d4bd2866af3cfe72aa336c8ba2ce2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072568 - Anti-alias horizontal edges in SWGL. r=lsalzman\n\nSWGL edge anti-aliasing only computes coverage along left and right edges.\naa_span derives per-pixel coverage from the horizontal distance to these\ntwo edges and the blend stage takes the minimum of the two. Nothing accounts\nfor how much of a row the polygon covers vertically, and with AA enabled the\nrow range is rounded outward, so the partially covered top and bottom rows\nof an axis-aligned quad were drawn at full opacity. Sloped edges were fine\nbecause they are traced as left or right edges. Exactly horizontal edges\nnever are, since they connect the two start vertices or the two end\nvertices of the traced edges.\n\nRow coverage:\n\nEach row is now bounded by the fraction of the row that lies between the\npolygon's anti-aliased horizontal top and bottom edges, if any. The blend\nstage clamps the per-pixel coverage to that bound instead of a constant,\nso the per-pixel cost is unchanged. Taking the minimum of the horizontal\nand vertical coverage matches what rectangle_aa_fragment does on the GPU\npath (max of the per-axis distances), so corner pixels come out the same\nas the reference. On partially covered rows the opaque region of the span\nis emptied so that every pixel goes through the AA blend stage.\n\nRow rounding:\n\nThe row range used to be rounded outward for the whole polygon as soon as\nAA was enabled, regardless of which edges were anti-aliased. This made\nhorizontal edges without AA bleed by a row, so a translucent primitive\ndrawn as a center part plus edge strips double-blended the row where the\ncenter met the bottom strip. It also skipped the bottom row entirely when\nthe bottom edge's fractional part was below 0.5, because the initial row\nlimit was not rounded outward. Rounding is now decided per edge:\noutward past an anti-aliased horizontal edge, to the nearest row across a\nhorizontal edge without AA, and unchanged for a top or bottom vertex.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326487\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/swgl/src/blend.h", "gfx/wr/swgl/src/rasterize.h", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad.glsl", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/motion/offset-path-shape-polygon-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/motion/offset-path-shape-polygon-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/motion/offset-rotate-005.html.ini"], "git_node": "e456b76069704106d398e7fc2e730de1070ac1c6", "git_parents": ["e794155692781ddbec3cdaa9f629dd7c97237812"], "node": "c775ae82a12e3e14ec17d88ea3c981e37f24fae3", "parents": ["707cfe811edc2a77579a185c0a65dee079967fb6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025752 - Wait on panel-list's shown and hidden events instead of its open attribute in browser_topsites_section.js, r=mconley.\n\npanel-list sets `open` synchronously in show(), deliberately so since bug\n2010864, and only finishes opening two animation frames later. Waiting on the\nattribute let these tests assert on aria-expanded and on focus before either\nwas set, and dispatch mouse events at a panel setAlign() had not moved off the\ntile yet, so the click landed on the neighbouring tile.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327083\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_topsites_section.js"], "git_node": "1c3d713169a4819e465c6cdca3ef773cb5ab2133", "git_parents": ["e456b76069704106d398e7fc2e730de1070ac1c6"], "node": "51b6ae5c979f6127e1340517741b42408a5cead7", "parents": ["c775ae82a12e3e14ec17d88ea3c981e37f24fae3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072711 - Restore the diagnostic on newtab's #root render wait, r=mconley.\n\n`TestUtils.waitForCondition` rejects immediately when its condition throws, so\nan absent `#root` used to name itself in the failure message. The optional\nchaining bug 2016217 added makes the condition evaluate to undefined instead,\nso the wait now reports a bare timeout, the same message a `#root` that exists\nbut never gets children produces. `#root` is in the prerendered markup, so\nthere is nothing for the check to guard.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327086\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "52cab01dfd77ab8f7daa901aa2f5d2192fcc3d24", "git_parents": ["1c3d713169a4819e465c6cdca3ef773cb5ab2133"], "node": "5296620fe01b0097a0e3990cab84aad831beb42e", "parents": ["51b6ae5c979f6127e1340517741b42408a5cead7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072711 - Remove unreachable skip-if conditions from the newtab browser test manifest, r=mconley.\n\nsocketprocess_networking can no longer be true: bug 2004381 removed the variant\nthat set it, and bug 2057871, which the remaining condition cites, is fixed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327087\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "7ce5ab13c147112f1995bede57670f25755fed45", "git_parents": ["52cab01dfd77ab8f7daa901aa2f5d2192fcc3d24"], "node": "d7810ab9eda0741b7a092ef7dba6841be80d1768", "parents": ["5296620fe01b0097a0e3990cab84aad831beb42e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072905 - Wait for newtab and Nimbus startup in browser_SmartShortcuts.js, r=mconley.\n\nEvery task reads AboutNewTab.activityStream, which onBrowserReady() assigns\nonly after its startup awaits, and enrolls without waiting for\nExperimentManager.onStartup(). The ExperimentAPI.ready() calls dropped here\nwere no-ops, since NimbusTestUtils.enroll() already awaits store.ready()\nitself.\n\nThe skip-if is from the bug 1995208 sweep and meant a bare \"verify\", which\npasses on an unmodified tree.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327089\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_SmartShortcuts.js"], "git_node": "c01c7974f9bff7170d8484ae72150b587583379b", "git_parents": ["7ce5ab13c147112f1995bede57670f25755fed45"], "node": "98258f051ec381b530bb4324de3e720bc115bfd2", "parents": ["d7810ab9eda0741b7a092ef7dba6841be80d1768"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072905 - Wait for AboutNewTab.activityStreamPromise in browser_activation_window.js, r=mconley.\n\nThe setup read AboutNewTab.activityStream before onBrowserReady() had assigned\nit: the await it replaces was on ActivityStream.initialized, a plain boolean,\nso it never waited for anything. The await on prefsFeed.store.initialized goes\nfor the same reason, the newtab Store not defining it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327090\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_activation_window.js"], "git_node": "edd519606befe400a832bff90fba1930adb755f9", "git_parents": ["c01c7974f9bff7170d8484ae72150b587583379b"], "node": "17d3684175679566c956e748bc622ad69130ea60", "parents": ["98258f051ec381b530bb4324de3e720bc115bfd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1970996 - Discard the preloaded newtab left behind by browser_enabled_newtabpage.js, r=mconley.\n\nSetting browser.newtabpage.enabled to false makes about:newtab resolve to\nblanktab.html, which has no #root. A preloaded about:newtab whose load is\nalready in flight when this test flips that pref comes back blank and is never\nreloaded, since NewTabPagePreloading gates preload creation on that pref rather\nthan refreshing an existing preload. The next test_newtab caller in\nbrowser.toml then consumes it and fails head.js's \"Should render activity\nstream content\" wait.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327091\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_enabled_newtabpage.js"], "git_node": "82e08c8b79f1cae78a683642b3a075f550589012", "git_parents": ["edd519606befe400a832bff90fba1930adb755f9"], "node": "4405d0d586b72fa21d5a7b7db20a99e2ecba02f9", "parents": ["17d3684175679566c956e748bc622ad69130ea60"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2023930 - Stop browser_as_render.js testing the newtab that was preloaded before its pref push, r=mconley.\n\nThe preloaded about:newtab left behind by an earlier test is already mounting\n\u003cmoz-urlbar\u003e when add_setup turns browser.urlbar.newtab.featureGate off, and\nnever swaps it for the handoff search bar test_render_search_handoff drives.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327092\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_as_render.js"], "git_node": "0a36786a9a86156769b2b22f575730024a1166c3", "git_parents": ["82e08c8b79f1cae78a683642b3a075f550589012"], "node": "7ae9b5ccc75ab921a13651bc6010a0414e9736ca", "parents": ["4405d0d586b72fa21d5a7b7db20a99e2ecba02f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1781344 - Keep browser_getScreenshots.js's thumbnail from expiring while the test reads it, r=mconley.\n\nPageThumbsExpiration registers browser-cleanup-thumbnails with a last-update\ntime of zero, so UpdateTimerManager runs it 30 seconds into the session, and\nexpireFilesInDirectory then deletes every thumbnail that no expiration filter\nasks to keep, with no age check. The test's own capture is one of them, which\nis how get_pixels ends up waiting for an image that will never load.\n\nRegister an expiration filter for the duration of the test, and reject from an\nerror listener so that a thumbnail that fails to load for some other reason\nsays so rather than parking the test until the harness kills it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327093\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_getScreenshots.js"], "git_node": "f0c916c7e224f402bf9269887edf1652a4368708", "git_parents": ["0a36786a9a86156769b2b22f575730024a1166c3"], "node": "48d7971a82df92d3298ab9a2ee61ff7682cc4f38", "parents": ["7ae9b5ccc75ab921a13651bc6010a0414e9736ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073002 - Keep one newtab feed's throw from withholding an action from the others, r=mconley.\n\nStore's middleware dispatches each action to every feed in a bare loop, so a\nsynchronous onAction that throws ends the loop: the later feeds never see the\naction, and the throw unwinds into whoever dispatched it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327096\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Store.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_Store.js"], "git_node": "8a184dabdee0980300d6dcab4de316710f361769", "git_parents": ["f0c916c7e224f402bf9269887edf1652a4368708"], "node": "727b635ccf74f7a996aa5c4d54c6d3b4bb9b40c2", "parents": ["48d7971a82df92d3298ab9a2ee61ff7682cc4f38"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2031557 - Compare the top site's real href in defaultTopSites_dismiss, r=mconley.\n\n`First default topsite was dismissed` compares `getAttribute(\"href\")` on the\n`.top-site-outer` list item, but the href is on the `.top-site-button` anchor\ninside it, so both sides of the comparison are null and the wait passes on its\nfirst poll whatever the row holds. A row that never updates now fails on that\ncheck rather than on the tile count above it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327099\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_topsites_contextMenu_options.js"], "git_node": "9b98f475b2602a5c98b2c12d64057ed3023666be", "git_parents": ["8a184dabdee0980300d6dcab4de316710f361769"], "node": "2297f146c862ffe7b865c147455be30233be062d", "parents": ["727b635ccf74f7a996aa5c4d54c6d3b4bb9b40c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2011958 - Restore the dismissed sponsored top site in browser_topsites_sponsored.js, r=mconley.\n\ntest_dismiss clears the three preferences its dismissal wrote, but clearing the\none behind `NewTabUtils.blockedLinks` leaves that module's in-memory copy\nholding the block, and the top sites feed does not re-read its inputs on its\nown either. So the dismissed sponsored tile never comes back, and the next run\nof this file in the same browser, as under `--verify`, starts with one\nsponsored tile instead of two.\n\nUndo the block through `NewTabUtils.undoAll()` and refresh the feed, as\n`add_setup` already does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327102\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_topsites_sponsored.js"], "git_node": "8250d6e6e9baa9fcc77af1e62db93affa76bc19d", "git_parents": ["9b98f475b2602a5c98b2c12d64057ed3023666be"], "node": "ff20b86a9f7a4b80d2d101669d5beabab7d78c05", "parents": ["2297f146c862ffe7b865c147455be30233be062d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061014 - Open the menu of the last visible top site rather than of a fixed column in browser_newtab_last_LinkMenu.js, r=mconley.\n\ntest_newtab_last_LinkMenu checks that the context menu of the top site at the\nright edge of the row opens to the left. It reached that tile with\n`.top-site-outer:nth-child(6n)`, which counts the placeholders and the\nadd-shortcut tile along with the top sites, so as soon as the row holds one\ntile fewer than the selector assumes, the position lands on a tile that has no\ncontext menu and the wait for `.context-menu-button` never finishes.\n\nThe last top site that has a context menu and a non-zero box is the tile the\nold selector picked on a full row. Search shortcuts are excluded so that the\ncheck cannot pass on a row where the default top sites never rendered.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327103\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_newtab_last_LinkMenu.js"], "git_node": "2ca9ddbdf64117943240160c34a0987866e046a4", "git_parents": ["8250d6e6e9baa9fcc77af1e62db93affa76bc19d"], "node": "2eb9b704ce243ff82902a7c5863bf84ab5068af0", "parents": ["ff20b86a9f7a4b80d2d101669d5beabab7d78c05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022285 - Don't ask for an animation frame in a hidden newtab, r=mconley.\n\nA newtab test closes its about:newtab tab, tabbrowser immediately starts\nloading a replacement preloaded about:newtab with docShellIsActive false, and\nComponentPerfTimer mounts in it and calls requestAnimationFrame. That keeps\nnsRefreshDriver ticking at the full vsync rate without running the request, so\nvsync stays enabled and browser-test.js's ensureVsyncDisabled can time out.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327105\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/ComponentPerfTimer/ComponentPerfTimer.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/ComponentPerfTimer.test.jsx"], "git_node": "e5c50ec897b9723bb886b1be19b9407ca50f3b15", "git_parents": ["2ca9ddbdf64117943240160c34a0987866e046a4"], "node": "143b6a6517f63852fb4811a7dd1140affebab669", "parents": ["2eb9b704ce243ff82902a7c5863bf84ab5068af0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072913 - Wait for the bookmark card to stop being one in browser_highlights_section.js, r=mconley.\n\nThe wait that follows the Remove Bookmark click passed `querySelectorAll` to\n`waitForCondition`. A NodeList is truthy when empty, so the condition held on\nthe first poll whatever the click did, and it is the test's only assertion\nafter the click.\n\nRemoving the bookmark does not remove the card: the highlight stays on the page\nas a history item and loses its `.icon-bookmark-added` context icon. Nothing\nestablished the card was a bookmark to begin with either, so the new wait needs\nthe precondition above it or it can pass by running early.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327106\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_highlights_section.js"], "git_node": "a7b54c35a19a762e517385fad695da0dac35554d", "git_parents": ["e5c50ec897b9723bb886b1be19b9407ca50f3b15"], "node": "67877153899394e3371886540b3b66c12367ab55", "parents": ["143b6a6517f63852fb4811a7dd1140affebab669"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073009 - Stop opening a tab per allowlist reset in browser_attribution_actor.js, r=mconley.\n\n`setAllowList()` opened a tab at https://example.com solely to obtain an\nAttributionParent instance and call setAllowListForTest on it. That method\nassigns the module-global allowlist and never reads `this`, so the tab only\ndoubled the test's tab churn and its content process launches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327112\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_attribution_actor.js"], "git_node": "7bb27b9ebb72212ca82cc487580053340815d4df", "git_parents": ["a7b54c35a19a762e517385fad695da0dac35554d"], "node": "39445d833a71cc8d3e750ad1bc664bd0dbf15478", "parents": ["67877153899394e3371886540b3b66c12367ab55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053167 - Part 1: Ensure every engine consumer holds mLock r=emz\n\nClassifyForCancel, ClassifyForAnnotate and ProbeBlocking all hold mLock across\nmatching. ProbeFeature took it only to look the engine up and then matched with\nthe lock released.\n\nNothing goes wrong today, because every engine consumer runs on the\nurl-classifier background thread and so cannot overlap. Closing the gap makes\nthe invariant hold everywhere: an engine is only ever used with mLock held.\n\nThe later parts of this bug depend on that. Reporting an engine's memory reads\nit from the main thread while the background thread may be matching, so an\nengine that is reachable without the lock would be read without one.\n\nClassifyWithEngines gains MOZ_REQUIRES(mLock) to match the other members that\nalready carry it. It previously relied on mLock.AssertCurrentThreadOwns(), which\nis declared MOZ_ASSERT_CAPABILITY and so tells the analyser the lock is held\nrather than asking callers to prove it; the annotation moves that obligation to\nthe callers, where the gap was.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320906\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.h"], "git_node": "655897c96426aa7da4d9d37d437d99bcbf74d571", "git_parents": ["7bb27b9ebb72212ca82cc487580053340815d4df"], "node": "7e2f4aca0fa9d2783337cc0280f782a420956abf", "parents": ["39445d833a71cc8d3e750ad1bc664bd0dbf15478"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053167 - Part 2: Report the content classifier engines to about:memory r=emz,mccr8\n\nThis part wires up the Gecko half of the reporting and leaves etp_engine\nuntouched. ContentClassifierService already keeps one engine per feature, so it\nimplements nsIMemoryReporter and emits a leaf under\nexplicit/content-classifier/engines/\u003cfeature\u003e/, which about:memory sums back\ninto a per-feature node. Keeping the per-feature path an interior node also\nmakes it visible when several engines end up holding the same rules.\n\nOnly the engine objects are measured here. Everything they point to lives behind\nprivate etp_engine types, which later parts measure.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320907\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.h", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/ContentClassifierEngine.h", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "3bb6771b95599a27022ebd1ce46d8ce8122881ff", "git_parents": ["655897c96426aa7da4d9d37d437d99bcbf74d571"], "node": "fe6ab7ca4e32067abfdea07e295b815701abd77e", "parents": ["7e2f4aca0fa9d2783337cc0280f782a420956abf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053167 - Part 3: Attribute the content classifier engines' filter data in about:memory r=emz,mccr8\n\nThis part introduces an optional malloc-size-of feature and an\nEngineMemoryBreakdown to etp_engine, splitting an engine's heap by what holds\nit.\n\nThe most of measure code lives in a new file to keep the diff to upstream\nminimal. The measure code in Engine is still required to reach the\nfilter_data_context.\n\nThe reported total excludes compiled regexes, which regex::bytes::Regex does not\nexpose.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320908\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/ContentClassifierEngine.h", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/engine.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/flatbuffers/unsafe_tools.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/malloc_size_of_impls.rs"], "git_node": "128201c4b4b464d74bad96db9832df16c6ccc19f", "git_parents": ["3bb6771b95599a27022ebd1ce46d8ce8122881ff"], "node": "a12fe3cd1d4779dcbff940f75e2848e820980a5e", "parents": ["fe6ab7ca4e32067abfdea07e295b815701abd77e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053167 - Part 4: Attribute the content classifier engines' blocker memory r=emz,mccr8\n\nThis part measures what the blocker owns: enabled-tags, the set of tag names\ngating tagged filters, and regex-table, the lookup table the matcher compiles\nregexes into. Nothing in Gecko enables a tag today, so enabled-tags reads zero,\nbut it is measured rather than assumed so that it cannot become an unnoticed\ngap.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320909\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/engine.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/malloc_size_of_impls.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/regex_manager.rs"], "git_node": "86b051737db3b97a9b01eb6d955c4b4cbea41f20", "git_parents": ["128201c4b4b464d74bad96db9832df16c6ccc19f"], "node": "b2f91ccbc85c2f15621be5e89bbd98d983bae028", "parents": ["a12fe3cd1d4779dcbff940f75e2848e820980a5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053167 - Part 5: Attribute the content classifier engines' cosmetic cache r=emz,mccr8\n\nThis part measures CosmeticFilterCache, which holds nothing but a clone of the\nreference Engine already measures, so the leaf reads zero. It is measured anyway\nso that a field added to the type is not silently dropped.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320910\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/engine.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/malloc_size_of_impls.rs"], "git_node": "828756a54e60699e0f84324a5d62311f1d2d2ac4", "git_parents": ["86b051737db3b97a9b01eb6d955c4b4cbea41f20"], "node": "d55d2bb5acca837282124cb704c8da23fb83cfad", "parents": ["b2f91ccbc85c2f15621be5e89bbd98d983bae028"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053167 - Part 6: Attribute the content classifier engines' resource backend r=emz,mccr8\n\nThis part measures the boxed backend of ResourceStorage. The box is allocated\nwhether or not the backend holds anything, so the leaf reports a non-zero size\neven though Gecko never puts anything in it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320911\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/engine.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/malloc_size_of_impls.rs", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/etp_engine/src/resources/resource_storage.rs"], "git_node": "c7bb39079be2752b22b341c69c53832ed65eb1bd", "git_parents": ["828756a54e60699e0f84324a5d62311f1d2d2ac4"], "node": "4ce57a238df448136e364e493bc107c1f098c817", "parents": ["d55d2bb5acca837282124cb704c8da23fb83cfad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053167 - Part 7: Test the content classifier engines' memory reporting r=emz\n\nCovers what the earlier parts built:\n\n - a live engine is reported, with the kind and units about:memory expects\n - each active feature reports under its own path, so two engines do not\n   collapse into one node\n - the reported flatbuffer and domain index grow with the size of the list the\n   engine was built from, which is what distinguishes them from the fixed cost\n   of the engine objects\n - the regex table is attributed once a request has actually been matched\n   against a filter needing a regex\n - every field of ContentClassifierEngineSizes reaches a leaf, so one that stops\n   being reported fails the suite\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320912\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_memory_reporter.js"], "git_node": "5ae643f95fb026adbd3644917fe775128f1d36b1", "git_parents": ["c7bb39079be2752b22b341c69c53832ed65eb1bd"], "node": "56374d38ad553cb067417443b6a5e4860b366610", "parents": ["4ce57a238df448136e364e493bc107c1f098c817"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2071783 - Remove unused HTML editor beforeinput and mutation observer telemetry probes. r=masayuki,webidl,smaug,TravisLong\" for causing crashtest failures\n\nThis reverts commit 75ee7c59a0d3b10c69271634f08caf25c16b5a65.\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.cpp", "dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.h", "dom/base/nsPIDOMWindow.h", "dom/events/EventListenerManager.cpp", "dom/webidl/MutationObserver.webidl", "editor/libeditor/EditorBase.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorBase.h", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.h", "editor/libeditor/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/glean/metrics_index.py"], "git_node": "a26a3a4e1cea29f4a3daa5db353e596e53af154c", "git_parents": ["5ae643f95fb026adbd3644917fe775128f1d36b1"], "node": "ea53bc25235d7845c56bca0381535193859d44e3", "parents": ["56374d38ad553cb067417443b6a5e4860b366610"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072438 - Rework bidi-engine management to allow nested use of nsBidiPresUtils::Resolve. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327605\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsBidiPresUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresContext.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresContext.h"], "git_node": "bbfcbae6ae57eaad436b138add1f1133b701ddb3", "git_parents": ["a26a3a4e1cea29f4a3daa5db353e596e53af154c"], "node": "678d081a7a16e8beb34529de0fc8c0ee5be75d73", "parents": ["ea53bc25235d7845c56bca0381535193859d44e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071997 - Use the remapped local clip rect as the picture composite clip bounds. r=gw\n\nWhen a picture is rasterized in a different coordinate system than its own\nspatial node, prepare_picture_primitive composites it through a synthetic\nscale-offset that maps the local rect onto its raster-space bounds, and remaps\nthe local clip rect into that space. The composite clip stack bounds were still\nset from the unadjusted local clip rect, and prepare_quad intersects the two.\nUnder a flip (scale: 1 -1) the rects are mirrored relative to each other, so\nthe intersection is shifted or empty and the picture is misplaced or dropped.\n\nAdd wrench reftests for a flipped, clipped blur picture with a rectangular clip\nand with a rounded clip (target mask path).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327468\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/filter-blur-flipped-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/filter-blur-flipped-rounded-clip-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/filter-blur-flipped-rounded-clip.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/filter-blur-flipped.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/reftest.list"], "git_node": "e7c26582712c57c2d6d0b0395ee2c62878d0e723", "git_parents": ["bbfcbae6ae57eaad436b138add1f1133b701ddb3"], "node": "7f31a5c9f5bb97e2ceb03e6f11080698b331438d", "parents": ["678d081a7a16e8beb34529de0fc8c0ee5be75d73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "eri \u003ceri@inventati.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1784381 - Add /run/udev permissions to flatpak. r=releng-reviewers,jrmuizel,ahal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322275\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/repackaging/flatpak.py"], "git_node": "6fa9a616bb0040a87d01fcd4a3b9c138c09c0f7e", "git_parents": ["e7c26582712c57c2d6d0b0395ee2c62878d0e723"], "node": "3289efd4fe9214d3511896f457329d93de9dbc96", "parents": ["7f31a5c9f5bb97e2ceb03e6f11080698b331438d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073030 - Lint all image/ headers through clang-tidy r=saschanaz\n\nChanges includes:\n- making deleted methods public\n- rework some include dependencies to make header self contained\n\nAll changes were detected either by header compilation failure, or by\nclang-tidy.\n\nFixes are either generated by clang-tidy or hand-made.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327330\n", "files": ["image/ICOFileHeaders.h", "image/ImageUtils.h"], "git_node": "b336b4263f74b1c3a1a16a124b913510c87191fc", "git_parents": ["6fa9a616bb0040a87d01fcd4a3b9c138c09c0f7e"], "node": "19213ced36f2f8ee99434525236bff2991ef41c8", "parents": ["3289efd4fe9214d3511896f457329d93de9dbc96"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jason Birchall \u003cjason.birchall@pm.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1990883 - Remove colorway migration code and UI informing users about colorways on AMO. r=rpl,frontend-codestyle-reviewers,dao\n\nRemove ColorwayThemeMigration.sys.mjs and its browser-idle-startup\nregistration, the colorway-removal-notice about:addons component, the\nisBuiltinColorwayTheme AddonWrapper property, and the associated fluent\nstrings and browser test. The one-shot cleanup from bug 1815898 has\nshipped since Firefox 139, past the Firefox 151 removal target agreed\non the bug, so any remaining profiles have long been migrated.\n\nThe extensions.colorway-builtin-themes-cleanup pref is intentionally\nleft behind to become inert in existing profiles; remaining colorways\nreferences are tracked by Bug 1815896.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326937\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/themes/BuiltInThemes.sys.mjs", "eslint-rollouts.config.mjs", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/aboutAddons.ftl", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/global/extensions.ftl", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/ColorwayThemeMigration.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/aboutaddons.html", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/aboutaddons.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/colorway-removal-notice.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIDatabase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIInstall.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_colorwaybuiltins_notification.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "388970d2c72d5f376a434b5499ee674c0902be85", "git_parents": ["b336b4263f74b1c3a1a16a124b913510c87191fc"], "node": "56a99acfde51be9b8497549c939dc2e5bc9f9c89", "parents": ["19213ced36f2f8ee99434525236bff2991ef41c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070817 - Resolve AudioContext operation promises on the graph thread. r=karlt\n\nPendingResumeOperation::Apply() unsuspended the context's tracks on the graph\nthread but dispatched the promise resolution to a main thread stable state\nrunnable. Resolving there only queues the MozPromise Then callback as a further\nmain thread task, so AudioContext::OnStateChanged() -- which is what settles the\npromises in mPendingResumePromises -- ran one task later again.\n\nAn AudioWorklet starts producing as soon as the tracks are unsuspended, so its\nport messages can reach main thread inside that window. A close() from such a\nmessage handler then found mPendingResumePromises non-empty and rejected the\nresume promises with \"Closed before resume completed\", for a resume that had in\nfact completed -- OnStateChanged() reached Running on the very next tick.\n\nResolve directly on the graph thread instead. Suspend, Close and pending Resume\noperations are all applied before the iteration's processing, so the main thread\nupdates from the previous iteration already describe the state for the rendered\ntime; there is nothing for a stable state runnable to wait for. Suspend and\nClose are changed the same way so that promises for one AudioContext keep\nsettling in the order the operations were applied.\n\nOn try this takes\nwebaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletprocessor-unconnected-outputs.https.window.js\non Windows opt from 50/80 failures to 0/40.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322503\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "44344e84f2166fdd67b204294f54cedf2b20f933", "git_parents": ["388970d2c72d5f376a434b5499ee674c0902be85"], "node": "81e76a1d3a426533a7f6946ebfcc859b5bc8c004", "parents": ["56a99acfde51be9b8497549c939dc2e5bc9f9c89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070817 - Resolve NotifyWhenDeviceStarted promises on the graph thread. r=karlt\n\nThe promise was resolved from a main thread runnable so that the graph thread\nwould not take MozPromise's mutex. Dispatching that runnable directly to the\nmain thread however used to, when this code was originally written, grab a much\nmore contended lock for the main thread event queue.\n\nWith the graph now using tail dispatch, dispatches to main thread grabs no lock.\nResolving directly on the graph thread only takes the promise mutex. Since this\nis an exclusive promise there is at most a single consumer, i.e. virtually no\ncontention. Compared to the original code this is a net win, and provides\neasier reasoning of the order of events than the original resolve-on-main did.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324925\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "faff05dbfa738f903adae4f97e41072fe8e80494", "git_parents": ["44344e84f2166fdd67b204294f54cedf2b20f933"], "node": "32bcf9d3ee2bf799b94e66efe93630e2a1a80a1d", "parents": ["81e76a1d3a426533a7f6946ebfcc859b5bc8c004"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070817 - Add nsIEventTarget::SUPPORTS_TAIL_DISPATCH. r=xpcom-reviewers,nika\n\nThis lets code holding an nsISerialEventTarget tell whether dispatching to it\nfrom a tail dispatching AbstractThread goes through the tail dispatcher, without\nknowing the concrete type. It is set by the AbstractThread implementations\nwhose TailDispatchPolicy is not NoTailDispatch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324926\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "xpcom/threads/AbstractThread.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TaskQueue.cpp", "xpcom/threads/nsIEventTarget.idl"], "git_node": "3db33edea1ed6a8dd633cdeaba16f67cbb7d4e52", "git_parents": ["faff05dbfa738f903adae4f97e41072fe8e80494"], "node": "cda396e60f864e35069d3295b7323b5d672a42ce", "parents": ["32bcf9d3ee2bf799b94e66efe93630e2a1a80a1d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070817 - Add MozPromiseHolder::RequireTailDispatch(). r=xpcom-reviewers,nika\n\nA producer settling a promise from a tail dispatching AbstractThread, such as\nthe MediaTrackGraph, can do so cheaply only if the Then callbacks are dispatched\nthrough its tail dispatcher. That depends on the consumer passing an event\ntarget that supports tail dispatch; otherwise Resolve() dispatches to the target\ndirectly, which for the main thread means taking its heavily contended event\nqueue lock, on an audio callback thread. RequireTailDispatch() lets the producer\nstate that requirement so it is asserted when the callbacks are dispatched,\nrather than being a convention.\n\nIt is exposed on the holder only, so that it can be set before any Then handler\ncould have been dispatched, and it applies to that promise alone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324927\n", "files": ["xpcom/tests/gtest/TestMozPromise.cpp", "xpcom/threads/MozPromise.h"], "git_node": "032177a7cabcd40922042cc2c9412d4f06631f16", "git_parents": ["3db33edea1ed6a8dd633cdeaba16f67cbb7d4e52"], "node": "54fcc04b8a8969f04fafaef9196d7fd7cd550305", "parents": ["cda396e60f864e35069d3295b7323b5d672a42ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070817 - Remove AudioContext::GetMainThread(). r=karlt,media-playback-reviewers\n\nIt dispatched to the owner window's labeled event target for Quantum DOM task\nscheduling, with a fallback for a torn down window. Labeled event targets are\ngone and nsIGlobalObject::SerialEventTarget() is the main thread event target\nfor windows, so both branches returned the same thing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324928\n", "files": ["dom/media/webaudio/AudioContext.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioContext.h"], "git_node": "c87b4e1a13e9e2ab7efe36a2bd9b3fc2cf2b2007", "git_parents": ["032177a7cabcd40922042cc2c9412d4f06631f16"], "node": "5442b681654eea98f83de52d4b34fab220afa0b1", "parents": ["54fcc04b8a8969f04fafaef9196d7fd7cd550305"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070817 - Handle MediaTrackGraph promises on AbstractThread::MainThread(). r=karlt,webrtc-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,bwc\n\nThe graph settles these promises on the graph thread. Dispatching the Then\ncallbacks only goes through the graph's tail dispatcher if the event target is\nthe AbstractThread for the main thread; with the plain nsIThread event target,\nResolve() would take the main thread's event queue lock from the audio callback.\n\nAs a side effect, multiple audio context operations tail-dispatched from a\nsingle graph iteration will fire \"statechange\" events from a single main thread\ngroup runnable, with no microtask checkpoints in between. This is against spec.\nThis patch therefore adds an extra bounce to the main thread nsThread for the\nrelevant uses.\n\nWaitFor() in gtests uses the current AbstractThread for the same reason, as it\nalready does for MediaEventSource listeners.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324929\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioContext.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioContext.h", "dom/media/webrtc/transportbridge/MediaPipeline.cpp", "testing/gtest/mozilla/WaitFor.h"], "git_node": "58a782c8d1f6bc1749e2f9f19277ed71663d8b9e", "git_parents": ["c87b4e1a13e9e2ab7efe36a2bd9b3fc2cf2b2007"], "node": "1b91912d938384b5bda3aef65efea2e262c69fb1", "parents": ["5442b681654eea98f83de52d4b34fab220afa0b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070817 - Require tail dispatch for MediaTrackGraph promises. r=karlt\n\nThe graph settles these promises on the graph thread, which is cheap only when\nthe Then callbacks are dispatched through its tail dispatcher rather than\nstraight to the main thread. That holds only when the event target supports\ntail dispatch, so require it rather than leave it to convention.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324930\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "2584bf820691113d76e7c096284630b51e0cd791", "git_parents": ["58a782c8d1f6bc1749e2f9f19277ed71663d8b9e"], "node": "a6607529c17817ed0d485b16f7870850eabad1e7", "parents": ["1b91912d938384b5bda3aef65efea2e262c69fb1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068372 - nsSimpleNestedURI::Deserialize should reparse the inner URI r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327278\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsSimpleNestedURI.cpp"], "git_node": "83273ab6be278fee9e1800c73a1f57c47ad4e72e", "git_parents": ["2584bf820691113d76e7c096284630b51e0cd791"], "node": "a02251bbc18b1b970ee23ceb0c0bfd7e982b256b", "parents": ["a6607529c17817ed0d485b16f7870850eabad1e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070729 [Wayland] Force toplevel window repaint by positioning child subsurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nForce commit to toplevel GdkWindow (mShell) to propagate\nchanges made to mContainer. There's only way how to force Gtk3 to\ndo the commit without actual painting (Bug 2070729) and that's child\nsubsurface position change.\n\nWe create a temporary child window located outside of the window\norigin without any content and move it to issue synced commit to toplevel\nwindow.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326465\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp", "widget/gtk/MozContainerWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.h"], "git_node": "e53ab5b22ece5ee68d0538be9e3f8368dd58ada3", "git_parents": ["83273ab6be278fee9e1800c73a1f57c47ad4e72e"], "node": "22f53bae53212e5e5c4e772eec941e5e95152727", "parents": ["a02251bbc18b1b970ee23ceb0c0bfd7e982b256b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061969: Check IsShuttingDown before repository init work. r=ArnaudBienner\n\nInitializeRepository could hang during shutdown because\nLoadOriginCacheIntoMap and the post-walk rename loop ran without\nshutdown checks. Add an early IsShuttingDown guard before the cache\nquery and a per-iteration check in the renameAndInitInfos loop.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322354\n", "files": ["dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/quota/test/gtest/TestQuotaManager.cpp", "dom/quota/test/xpcshell/test_shutdownDuringRepositoryInitialization.js", "dom/quota/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "510e9cf5e10cd9fd956254df7b3fd337d83e993e", "git_parents": ["e53ab5b22ece5ee68d0538be9e3f8368dd58ada3"], "node": "81768f54751e41bf3b03cbe33db1d4f54b09254d", "parents": ["22f53bae53212e5e5c4e772eec941e5e95152727"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069839 - [customizable-menu] Show the refresh menu item in browser screen's menu r=android-reviewers,petru\" for causing fenix failure\n\nThis reverts commit 0ab7da7868c75a0443d70a29223cb804d37b080e.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/RefreshMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilder.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuSectionConfiguration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/RefreshMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "22f91a803813bc773ddaac42b89fe975bc275bce", "git_parents": ["510e9cf5e10cd9fd956254df7b3fd337d83e993e"], "node": "5b162d0381b6e6a9b599102f77bc5d4b23b5798b", "parents": ["81768f54751e41bf3b03cbe33db1d4f54b09254d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Corentin Bect \u003ccbect@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071372 - Keep the VPN location row clickable during the activation so that the ripple keeps being drawn r=android-reviewers,Roger\n\nWhen the VPN is enabled, selecting a location dispatches an `IPProtectionAction.LocationChanged` event, which posts an `PendingActivationRequest.Activate` leading `IPProtectionState.isActivationInFlight` to return true. Given that this value is observed in the Compose screen, the location list is recomposed and each `LocationOption` gets assigned a null `onClick`.\n\n`LocationOption` is indirectly based on `ListItem`, which attaches its `combinedClickable` conditionally:\n```\n.thenConditional(\n    modifier =\n        Modifier.combinedClickable(\n            onClick = { ... },\n            onLongClick = { ...},\n        ),\n    predicate = { (onClick != null || onLongClick != null) && enabled },\n)\n```\nSo a null `onClick` completely removes the click Modifier, and it's indication. As a result, when a location row is tapped, its `combinedClickable` is detached as well, along its associated indication / ripple effect so the ripple is never drawn.\n\n`LocationOption` now always passes a non null callback and checks `isActivating` inside it. That way the ripple is drawn correctly. Also, semantics have been updated to mark the row as disabled when it's activating so that screen readers describe the correct state.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326970\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/ipprotection/IPProtectionLocations.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/ipprotection/IPProtectionLocationsScreenTest.kt"], "git_node": "203d12b4c7ae3ce1710a0b3900757dfa122da211", "git_parents": ["22f91a803813bc773ddaac42b89fe975bc275bce"], "node": "ee0f1ac101c529d49248f51e4c269355b854f0ee", "parents": ["5b162d0381b6e6a9b599102f77bc5d4b23b5798b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073200 r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327546\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/ImageBridgeParent.cpp"], "git_node": "57e98b5849b58f59560fdda208ec53c92ff61503", "git_parents": ["203d12b4c7ae3ce1710a0b3900757dfa122da211"], "node": "7150d7e1d4be32c24baba533b59e518faec0a8d1", "parents": ["ee0f1ac101c529d49248f51e4c269355b854f0ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071783 - Remove unused HTML editor beforeinput and mutation observer telemetry probes. r=masayuki,webidl,smaug,TravisLong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325788\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.cpp", "dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.h", "dom/base/nsPIDOMWindow.h", "dom/events/EventListenerManager.cpp", "dom/webidl/MutationObserver.webidl", "editor/libeditor/EditorBase.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorBase.h", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.h", "editor/libeditor/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/glean/metrics_index.py"], "git_node": "fc441a90e612a3aa7f0801a07316cf814390f1f2", "git_parents": ["57e98b5849b58f59560fdda208ec53c92ff61503"], "node": "84608c69f4179da8d364a0834ea3409413cb5713", "parents": ["7150d7e1d4be32c24baba533b59e518faec0a8d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "chloezhouny \u003cchloezhouny@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069683 - Split browser_aiwindow_smartbar_inline_mentions.js so it stops timing out intermittently. r=flozia\n\nThe file opened one AI window per task and kept hitting the per-file timeout. Split it into three files along what the tasks actually cover, so each one opens roughly a third of the windows.\n\nNo test logic changed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324165\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_inline_mentions.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_inline_mentions_context.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_inline_mentions_suggestions.js"], "git_node": "0ced8dd68cbc97ea74d4db8b87057043f30efb93", "git_parents": ["fc441a90e612a3aa7f0801a07316cf814390f1f2"], "node": "4fa3c90aab82132151097681c4d0370ba1f10115", "parents": ["84608c69f4179da8d364a0834ea3409413cb5713"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Tunru \u003cvtunru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070204 - Don't reveal the address bar tracker-count pill when the tracker count feature is disabled. r=urlbar-reviewers,kandres,adw\n\nWhen the address bar tracker count is disabled (trackerCountFeatureGate=false, the current default, or trackerCount.enabled=false), the trust icon must stay static. #updateUrlbarIcon was adding the `has-blocked-trackers` class whenever #computeTrackerCount() \u003e 0, independent of the feature prefs. On a tab switch the browser's content-blocking log is already populated, so switching back to a tab with blocked trackers revealed the tracker-count pill with the stale default \"0 trackers blocked\" text and played the reveal/width animation, shifting the URL for no reason .\n\nGate the `has-blocked-trackers` class on the tracker-count feature, and consolidate the four repeated `trackerCountFeatureGate && trackerCount.enabled` checks into a single #trackerCountEnabled getter.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326421\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-trustPanel/browser_trust_panel_icon.js"], "git_node": "62fffecf9bbb65469c0dad710f142d71cdbc100a", "git_parents": ["0ced8dd68cbc97ea74d4db8b87057043f30efb93"], "node": "e23b142f6f4b9dd79f4880a8158c764aacfdeb7a", "parents": ["4fa3c90aab82132151097681c4d0370ba1f10115"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2070817 - Require tail dispatch for MediaTrackGraph promises. r=karlt\" for causing gtests failures at MozPromise\n\nThis reverts commit 2584bf820691113d76e7c096284630b51e0cd791.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2070817 - Handle MediaTrackGraph promises on AbstractThread::MainThread(). r=karlt,webrtc-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,bwc\"\n\nThis reverts commit 58a782c8d1f6bc1749e2f9f19277ed71663d8b9e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2070817 - Remove AudioContext::GetMainThread(). r=karlt,media-playback-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit c87b4e1a13e9e2ab7efe36a2bd9b3fc2cf2b2007.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2070817 - Add MozPromiseHolder::RequireTailDispatch(). r=xpcom-reviewers,nika\"\n\nThis reverts commit 032177a7cabcd40922042cc2c9412d4f06631f16.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2070817 - Add nsIEventTarget::SUPPORTS_TAIL_DISPATCH. r=xpcom-reviewers,nika\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3db33edea1ed6a8dd633cdeaba16f67cbb7d4e52.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2070817 - Resolve NotifyWhenDeviceStarted promises on the graph thread. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit faff05dbfa738f903adae4f97e41072fe8e80494.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2070817 - Resolve AudioContext operation promises on the graph thread. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit 44344e84f2166fdd67b204294f54cedf2b20f933.\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioContext.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioContext.h", "dom/media/webrtc/transportbridge/MediaPipeline.cpp", "testing/gtest/mozilla/WaitFor.h", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestMozPromise.cpp", "xpcom/threads/AbstractThread.cpp", "xpcom/threads/MozPromise.h", "xpcom/threads/TaskQueue.cpp", "xpcom/threads/nsIEventTarget.idl"], "git_node": "ca7cc178883d85127ba89285856ee116b266a7f4", "git_parents": ["62fffecf9bbb65469c0dad710f142d71cdbc100a"], "node": "d2a8a135b0c96444a08c7657f7a65e37bef25702", "parents": ["e23b142f6f4b9dd79f4880a8158c764aacfdeb7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074047 - Measure AsyncShutdown's crash countdown against a clock that stops while the system is suspended. r=webidl,smaug\n\nSince bug 2065080 the countdown compares ChromeUtils.now() against a\ndeadline. On Windows that clock keeps counting while the machine sleeps,\nand relative timers that expire during sleep fire on wake, so a shutdown\ninterrupted by a suspend crashed on the first beat after resume, naming\nwhatever blocker had not yet had a chance to run. Blockers that give up\non their own after a few seconds, like the native messaging host\ncleanup, showed up this way.\n\nExpose mozglue's AwakeTimeStamp as ChromeUtils.awakeNow() and\nuse it for the countdown, so that, like nsTerminator, it only counts time\nthe system was awake.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327786\n", "files": ["dom/base/ChromeUtils.cpp", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.h", "dom/chrome-webidl/ChromeUtils.webidl", "toolkit/components/asyncshutdown/AsyncShutdown.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "3494f833873d38249bbf89dd4cd9cb74362ea0c2", "git_parents": ["ca7cc178883d85127ba89285856ee116b266a7f4"], "node": "a3de9514f3e20400443d3f19092c0906895b2704", "parents": ["d2a8a135b0c96444a08c7657f7a65e37bef25702"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066763 - Add telemetry for deliberate ETP disablement action in the Trust Panel r=urlbar-reviewers,timhuang,jteow\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324254\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/base/content/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-trustPanel/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-trustPanel/browser_trust_panel_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "e6a6e3b89f64bd9c1ca11f2107a43b17169ca46b", "git_parents": ["3494f833873d38249bbf89dd4cd9cb74362ea0c2"], "node": "60b262f172406f4337f872570b7ea61438199e94", "parents": ["a3de9514f3e20400443d3f19092c0906895b2704"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066764 - Add telemetry for Clear Cookies and Site Data option in the new Trust Panel r=urlbar-reviewers,timhuang,daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324255\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/components/controlcenter/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-trustPanel/browser_trust_panel_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "b0f37f2a6314011ac7eb5587bca85fb77a9c67b4", "git_parents": ["e6a6e3b89f64bd9c1ca11f2107a43b17169ca46b"], "node": "7faac00090d70b77e67bccc4d8d6ace22e0b4cbd", "parents": ["60b262f172406f4337f872570b7ea61438199e94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066765 - Add telemetry for security info subview in the new Trust Panel r=urlbar-reviewers,timhuang,daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324256\n", "files": ["browser/base/c