dfdcf317010f8", "00c4095d8d43700f5c87b1720044c5b3554cec7c", "cdaf0856029bf62d6d17de39f6b34182eea1192b", "f88b762877c752343d567dbadfff0760a1461eee", "359d77fb0c49f3387fbea69908ae4d30a9c246d8"], "user": "smolnar@mozilla.com"}, "45382": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033703 - Flush APZ repaints and paints before the synthesized tap in the dynamic toolbar tests. r=geckoview-reviewers,hiro,ohall\n\nshowDynamicToolbar and showDynamicToolbarOnFrameReconstruction tap right after changing the vertical clipping,\nso the tap can be hit-tested against compositor state that has not caught up and never produce the toolbar\ncallback. The later dynamic toolbar tests already wait with flushApzRepaints() and promiseAllPaintsDone()\nbefore tapping; do the same here.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327487\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/DynamicToolbarTest.kt"], "git_node": "b480039c693cdc6196ef54f46b96dc364accea89", "git_parents": ["359d77fb0c49f3387fbea69908ae4d30a9c246d8"], "node": "a85f7f5451b1a0df809c39b56208606b0f6b1846", "parents": ["4d5216592535badef64a33022512c562e3d4f946"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1921935 - Wait for the resize event before tapping in hitTestOnPositionSticky. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall,hiro\n\nsetVerticalClipping reaches the content process through an async PBrowser DynamicToolbarOffsetChanged message,\nwhile flushApzRepaints goes through the test-support port, so the flush can complete before content has\napplied the new toolbar offset and reflowed. The tap then lands where the toolbar was, before content has\nmoved the position: sticky button into that area, so the click hits the body and the button's promise never\nresolves. Content fires a window resize event once the toolbar is completely hidden, as windowInnerHeight\nalready relies on, so wait for it before the flushes and the tap, and wait for the paint like the sibling test\ndoes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327717\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/DynamicToolbarTest.kt"], "git_node": "602f5893bfaf71a156e900d88ebd29008b800ef4", "git_parents": ["b480039c693cdc6196ef54f46b96dc364accea89"], "node": "cdcdde4e97b1ec42aba620497bf963c5bcdbe5f9", "parents": ["a85f7f5451b1a0df809c39b56208606b0f6b1846"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029263 - Wait for the cross-origin iframe's content transforms before touching it in touchEventWithXOrigin. r=geckoview-reviewers,hiro\n\nThe test loads touch_xorigin.html and touches the iframe as soon as the top-level page has stopped loading,\npainted and flushed APZ. With Fission the iframe lives in another process, and none of those waits cover it:\nin the failing runs the touch is sent about 30 ms after the iframe committed, before the compositor can\nhit-test it, so APZ handles the event itself and reports INPUT_RESULT_HANDLED instead of\nINPUT_RESULT_HANDLED_CONTENT. Every trunk failure of this test is on the fission variants.\n\nwaitForContentTransformsReceived is the existing wait for a frame's transforms to reach its process, but the\ntest-support implementation only asked the top-level frame's BrowserChild. Ask every process root in the tab's\nbrowsing context tree, which covers out-of-process iframes, and have the test wait for it before the existing\npaint and APZ flushes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327720\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/test-api.js", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/PanZoomControllerTest.kt"], "git_node": "7f82b3a9cefc260d91682dc84393fbf386af91f9", "git_parents": ["602f5893bfaf71a156e900d88ebd29008b800ef4"], "node": "6a8a0429eceef07a1e96b07a0db10adb075c93e2", "parents": ["cdcdde4e97b1ec42aba620497bf963c5bcdbe5f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Thompson \u003csthompson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073794 - fix backup string \"Not an email address\" r=kpatenio,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327909\n", "files": ["browser/components/backup/content/password-rules-tooltip.mjs", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/backupSettings.ftl"], "git_node": "7cca78c1f6ba36b8fcf01d7fa9f1ed08db411e31", "git_parents": ["7f82b3a9cefc260d91682dc84393fbf386af91f9"], "node": "bfc255d29ce49b30c94b580f8367c6dda3ab5f80", "parents": ["6a8a0429eceef07a1e96b07a0db10adb075c93e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Thompson \u003csthompson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065228 - remove `hidden` features from session state r=sfoster\n\nDuring manual session restore, only use existing windows that can be modified to match the restoring window. In particular, we will no longer convert popup windows into normal windows and vice versa.\n\nThis will lead in some cases to opening one more window than we used to on manual session restore.\n\nAfter bug 2060396 and bug 2064683, the only hideable element left is the toolbar, but it can only be hidden at window creation time. It's no longer possible to change the visibility of chrome elements in existing windows via bar properties.\n\nWe already store `isPopup` on window state and the value is determined by toolbar visibility.\n\nThis means that each window's `hidden` string no longer does anything and no longer stores any unique information.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322711\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/session.schema.json", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_354894_perwindowpb.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_495495.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_597071.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_oldformat.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_restored_window_features.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/manifest.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/session_store_test_case.py", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/test_close_last_nonpopup_window.py", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/test_restore_last_session_window_mismatch.py"], "git_node": "365f51979f63dae19ebb64af74796f09e67ed7b0", "git_parents": ["7cca78c1f6ba36b8fcf01d7fa9f1ed08db411e31"], "node": "db8dace59de1d3d38b7054b5236a1f7503338f60", "parents": ["bfc255d29ce49b30c94b580f8367c6dda3ab5f80"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1963810: Never use native menus on macOS in headless mode. r=mstange,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327525\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/NativeMenuSupport.mm", "widget/tests/chrome.toml"], "git_node": "f4b22b627455aa5927045d9c7d10b5a0708571b5", "git_parents": ["365f51979f63dae19ebb64af74796f09e67ed7b0"], "node": "5106822807884f48b7a46cdcf7950e1d9e31aee3", "parents": ["db8dace59de1d3d38b7054b5236a1f7503338f60"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065228 - remove `hidden` features from session state r=sfoster\" for causing mochitest failures @ test_close_last_nonpopup_window\n\nThis reverts commit 365f51979f63dae19ebb64af74796f09e67ed7b0.\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/session.schema.json", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_354894_perwindowpb.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_495495.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_597071.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_oldformat.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_restored_window_features.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/manifest.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/session_store_test_case.py", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/test_close_last_nonpopup_window.py", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/test_restore_last_session_window_mismatch.py"], "git_node": "a2b2a31427d0957df868e8ff46ce0ee7c401be8d", "git_parents": ["f4b22b627455aa5927045d9c7d10b5a0708571b5"], "node": "bca61d381fcac31140fc8dca3dce03af0174448a", "parents": ["5106822807884f48b7a46cdcf7950e1d9e31aee3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073543. Don't crash when jxl-rs can't build an ICC profile for the JXL output color space. r=saschanaz,gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nBuilding an ICC profile from a color encoding can fail, and as_icc unwraps it.\nUse try_as_icc instead. We already handle not getting a profile by decoding\nwithout color management.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327587\n", "files": ["image/rust/jxl/src/decoder.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/custom-primaries-icc-overflow-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/resources/custom-primaries-icc-overflow.jxl"], "git_node": "5c535b413051127e12460dab77bb09040a0a402e", "git_parents": ["a2b2a31427d0957df868e8ff46ce0ee7c401be8d"], "node": "ffe0553d6b40adca90ca1d14d89b1188d915578e", "parents": ["bca61d381fcac31140fc8dca3dce03af0174448a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066805: Report a fullscreen change that macOS refuses to run. r=emilio,mac-reviewers,extension-reviewers,robwu,bradwerth\n\nWhen AppKit gives up on a native fullscreen transition it has already started, it calls windowDidFailToEnterFullScreen: instead of windowDidEnterFullScreen:. We deal with that by pretending we just arrived at the opposite state, which brings nsCocoaWindow back in line with what the window is really doing. If the refusal comes in before AppKit has resized the window, though, we never updated our own fullscreen state in the first place, so there is nothing to bring back in line and no size mode event goes out.\n\nThat leaves the window waiting. nsGlobalWindowOuter::mFullscreen is set before we even ask the widget, and the only thing that clears it is FinishFullscreenChange(), which runs off a size mode event. So window.fullScreen keeps saying true while window.windowState says STATE_NORMAL, and since mInProcessFullscreenRequest is never cleared either, every later fullscreen request for that window gets dropped.\n\nTell the window about the change that is not going to happen, through a new nsIWidgetListener call that AppWindow turns into the FinishFullscreenChange() it has been waiting for. Both directions end up in code the DOM already has for a widget that failed to toggle its fullscreen state, including the macOS-only case of failing to exit.\n\nAlso drop the pending update of our fullscreen state on the next resize, which would otherwise let some unrelated resize apply the transition that failed, and drop the assertion that our size mode has already reached fullscreen, which is not the case when the refusal comes first. The two failure methods take the window rather than a notification, see NSWindow.h and the NSWindowDelegate documentation.\n\nThe check in Window.setState() that pointed at this bug stays, since window.fullScreen still leads window.windowState for as long as a transition is running, but its comment now says that rather than naming a bug that is fixed.\n\nThere is no automated test. Getting AppKit to refuse a transition takes a competing animation or a user gesture at the same moment, and there is no way for a test to set that up. Bug 1916152 comment 13 has a manual reproduction: open a modal panel while entering fullscreen.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327673\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-browser.js", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm", "widget/nsIWidgetListener.h", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.cpp", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.h"], "git_node": "f95b5a8eef79698273adfe84ed3cdf08712ef7bb", "git_parents": ["5c535b413051127e12460dab77bb09040a0a402e"], "node": "e1f53cb87efb4e7ca7385177282054eaf2bd2da1", "parents": ["ffe0553d6b40adca90ca1d14d89b1188d915578e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072134: Acknowledge ASWebAuthenticationSession cancellations that the requesting app initiated. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327610\n", "files": ["toolkit/xre/ASWebAuthSessionHandler.mm"], "git_node": "adf7e8ed6293a85172d2dd3800d133aebd310636", "git_parents": ["f95b5a8eef79698273adfe84ed3cdf08712ef7bb"], "node": "de3f7b640309b5bd3a8c4684d585b65727e11a95", "parents": ["e1f53cb87efb4e7ca7385177282054eaf2bd2da1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072134: Cancel queued ASWebAuthenticationSession requests at shutdown. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327611\n", "files": ["toolkit/xre/ASWebAuthSessionHandler.mm"], "git_node": "036930ff44171c1deae8f1301895b6d848c0b5c4", "git_parents": ["adf7e8ed6293a85172d2dd3800d133aebd310636"], "node": "d247c3bfd97df0ca70a64c7c5b1344aa208a0438", "parents": ["de3f7b640309b5bd3a8c4684d585b65727e11a95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072951 - Stop the Your images thumbnails blanking when a wallpaper is applied. r=reemhamz\n\nClicking a picture in Your images blanks every thumbnail in the grid and causes flickers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327450\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/WallpaperCategories/WallpaperCategories.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/WallpaperCategories/WallpaperCategories.test.jsx"], "git_node": "ce2b4b7660050a274d2a3c4938a787e6a8956ba3", "git_parents": ["036930ff44171c1deae8f1301895b6d848c0b5c4"], "node": "ab710cc805f5a45b54e47381844667b27c5e4318", "parents": ["d247c3bfd97df0ca70a64c7c5b1344aa208a0438"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068991: Register the ASWebAuthenticationSession handler on macOS 10.15 and 11. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nASWebAuthenticationSessionWebBrowserSessionManager, the ASWebAuthenticationSessionWebBrowserSessionHandling protocol and every ASWebAuthenticationSessionRequest member we touch outside the existing 14.4 guards are all declared API_AVAILABLE(macos(10.15)) in the SDK headers, and the online documentation gives the same floor. The 12.0 guards therefore left no session handler installed on macOS 10.15 and 11, while ASWebAuthenticationSessionWebBrowserSupportCapabilities in Info.plist advertised support unconditionally. The system picked Firefox for the auth request, launched it, and the request was never handled.\n\nFolding RegisterObservers() into RegisterASWebAuthSessionObservers() since the indirection only existed to carry the availability annotation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327564\n", "files": ["toolkit/xre/ASWebAuthSessionHandler.mm"], "git_node": "911ba2f0c49de25191da1b9327d16df2defc1bc9", "git_parents": ["ce2b4b7660050a274d2a3c4938a787e6a8956ba3"], "node": "5d0fe43fe547b42cc91d004e093db34319c928fc", "parents": ["ab710cc805f5a45b54e47381844667b27c5e4318"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063562 - Don't count a restoring about:blank tab as a duplicate. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jswinarton\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327453\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_multiselect_tabs_close_duplicate_tabs.js"], "git_node": "664e8a12ba6f9279a4d2d23c9fc90ee4f011c5fc", "git_parents": ["911ba2f0c49de25191da1b9327d16df2defc1bc9"], "node": "f7df03fc04b7ae5ac877cfb0651c5bcbf2f9a135", "parents": ["5d0fe43fe547b42cc91d004e093db34319c928fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069301 - p1. Move the dl_iterate_phdr callback into a new class r=mstange,profiler-reviewers\n\nBy moving the dl_iterate_phdr callback into a new class the class\nmembers can be used as state.  This also lets us remove the temporary\nvector of LoadedLibraryInfo objects and the LoadedLibraryInfo class.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327295\n", "files": ["mozglue/baseprofiler/core/shared-libraries-linux.cc"], "git_node": "8d84d40418194ec82f9109c2372237c39e70d32f", "git_parents": ["664e8a12ba6f9279a4d2d23c9fc90ee4f011c5fc"], "node": "bb6a7b4036dd37253a9add2e966e7c8e5fce7448", "parents": ["f7df03fc04b7ae5ac877cfb0651c5bcbf2f9a135"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069301 - p2. Avoid some raw C-style strings r=mstange,profiler-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327296\n", "files": ["mozglue/baseprofiler/core/shared-libraries-linux.cc"], "git_node": "ad95a0b330808524a307442c713698c8bdeb67b4", "git_parents": ["8d84d40418194ec82f9109c2372237c39e70d32f"], "node": "f7d238ddcab0b2aef0f5448fe6fc626b7f24c4d5", "parents": ["bb6a7b4036dd37253a9add2e966e7c8e5fce7448"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069301 - p3. Identify the main executable from the aux vector r=jld,mstange,profiler-reviewers\n\nOn Linux the profiler can avoid system calls during GetInfoForSelf()\nwhich prevents it from falling afaul of sandboxing restrictions.\n\nThe ELF auxiliary vector can be used to find the path of the executable\n(AF_EXECFN).  Also because the first object retrieved by dl_iterate_phdr\nis the executable detecting the executable can be simplified.\n\nThe profiler still uses /proc/self/maps on Android.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323963\n", "files": ["mozglue/baseprofiler/core/shared-libraries-linux.cc", "tools/profiler/tests/xpcshell/test_shared_library.js"], "git_node": "727d42e88d4c5b4cf503aa78429b65f8d27f1d42", "git_parents": ["ad95a0b330808524a307442c713698c8bdeb67b4"], "node": "03f29ca69f60bce036a2b2e7f92ffc703ad5543a", "parents": ["f7d238ddcab0b2aef0f5448fe6fc626b7f24c4d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069301 - p3. Identify the main executable from the aux vector r=jld,mstange,profiler-reviewers\" for causing bustages in shared-libraries-linux.cc.\n\nThis reverts commit 727d42e88d4c5b4cf503aa78429b65f8d27f1d42.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2069301 - p2. Avoid some raw C-style strings r=mstange,profiler-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit ad95a0b330808524a307442c713698c8bdeb67b4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2069301 - p1. Move the dl_iterate_phdr callback into a new class r=mstange,profiler-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 8d84d40418194ec82f9109c2372237c39e70d32f.\n", "files": ["mozglue/baseprofiler/core/shared-libraries-linux.cc", "tools/profiler/tests/xpcshell/test_shared_library.js"], "git_node": "f9a73919fe039381777330403e5f94918735a5e7", "git_parents": ["727d42e88d4c5b4cf503aa78429b65f8d27f1d42"], "node": "e089cf67542197b4bea0e63d991a3d1d362e4b0a", "parents": ["03f29ca69f60bce036a2b2e7f92ffc703ad5543a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790069752, "git_changesets": ["b480039c693cdc6196ef54f46b96dc364accea89", "602f5893bfaf71a156