e order of policies changed and this test\nfails. Running tests with https: is good practice anyway, so let's do\nthat.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327776\n", "files": ["dom/security/test/csp/file_bug886164.html", "dom/security/test/csp/file_bug886164_2.html", "dom/security/test/csp/file_bug886164_3.html", "dom/security/test/csp/file_bug886164_4.html", "dom/security/test/csp/file_bug886164_5.html", "dom/security/test/csp/file_bug886164_6.html", "dom/security/test/csp/file_multi_policy_injection_bypass.html", "dom/security/test/csp/file_multi_policy_injection_bypass_2.html"], "git_node": "a5929a36488a680040784c257edae0bbbdb7ecf9", "git_parents": ["d13258d8d92e4307266bd16e1954eef95057fae1"], "node": "9af912b6a8f59cdd6c7b87f948ac83fcc2aaca9b", "parents": ["e5f675c305643803e4eb985425c193b0f6a6be39"], "tags": []}, {"author": "f3tch \u003cftech169@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070577 - Allow permissions.setPermission and WebDriver:SetPermission to set camera and microphone permissions. r=Sasha,webdriver-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327436\n", "files": ["remote/shared/Permissions.sys.mjs", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-streams/GUM-deny.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "b159abdc6857d09f71ad27edcee13fec6953f02d", "git_parents": ["a5929a36488a680040784c257edae0bbbdb7ecf9"], "node": "a1a77f9f0a9c23a3a8139b3424d29261b994f5d3", "parents": ["9af912b6a8f59cdd6c7b87f948ac83fcc2aaca9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "f3tch \u003cftech169@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070577 - [wdspec] Add tests for camera and microphone permissions. r=Sasha,webdriver-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327848\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/external/permissions/set_permission/set_permission.py"], "git_node": "a22fb216815dfb83b5c39cbb6d384041970e4559", "git_parents": ["b159abdc6857d09f71ad27edcee13fec6953f02d"], "node": "b56b2037946f9690bae3dbc5a145c4e655c2c1f6", "parents": ["a1a77f9f0a9c23a3a8139b3424d29261b994f5d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071777 - Make LoadHistoryEntry MOZ_CAN_RUN_SCRIPT. r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,saschanaz,win-reviewers,dom-worker-reviewers,smaug,gstoll,valentin,asuth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325771\n", "files": ["accessible/generic/ImageAccessible.h", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.h", "docshell/base/nsIDocShell.idl", "docshell/base/nsIRefreshURI.idl", "docshell/base/nsIWebNavigation.idl", "docshell/base/nsRefreshTimer.cpp", "docshell/base/nsRefreshTimer.h", "dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/base/Location.h", "dom/base/LocationBase.h", "dom/base/nsFrameLoader.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.h", "dom/base/nsPIDOMWindow.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerChild.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerService.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientNavigateOpChild.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientOpenWindowUtils.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientOpenWindowUtils.h", "dom/credentialmanagement/identity/WebIdentityChild.cpp", "dom/credentialmanagement/identity/WebIdentityChild.h", "dom/documentpip/DocumentPictureInPicture.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserChild.h", "dom/ipc/ContentChild.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h", "dom/navigation/Navigation.cpp", "dom/navigation/Navigation.h", "dom/notification/NotificationHandler.cpp", "editor/composer/nsEditingSession.h", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.h", "security/manager/pki/nsNSSDialogHelper.h", "security/manager/ssl/PKCS11ModuleDB.h", "security/manager/ssl/PKCS11ModuleParent.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsICertificateDialogs.idl", "security/manager/ssl/nsIX509CertDB.idl", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCallbacks.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCertificateDB.h", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsXULAlerts.h", "toolkit/components/commandlines/nsCommandLine.cpp", "toolkit/components/commandlines/nsICommandLineHandler.idl", "toolkit/components/startup/public/nsIAppStartup.idl", "toolkit/components/windowcreator/nsIWindowCreator.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsIWindowWatcher.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsPIWindowWatcher.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.cpp", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.h", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp", "widget/nsIPrintDialogService.idl", "widget/windows/nsPrintDialogWin.cpp", "widget/windows/nsPrintDialogWin.h", "xpcom/build/nsXULAppAPI.h", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.h", "xpfe/appshell/nsAppShellService.h", "xpfe/appshell/nsIAppShellService.idl", "xpfe/appshell/nsIAppWindow.idl"], "git_node": "6deacd2c33c2c94160d5cdbd0b462048185ad286", "git_parents": ["a22fb216815dfb83b5c39cbb6d384041970e4559"], "node": "96676046125a6daed4482e6ba38ceb619b16c346", "parents": ["b56b2037946f9690bae3dbc5a145c4e655c2c1f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073437. Update fuzz on some jpegxl wpt reftests. r=saschanaz\n\nFor progressive-1: we had to have fuzz to cover for the difference until a new (improved) reference got merged from wpt. It's merged now so we can remove.\n\nFor progressive-2 and progressive-3: jxl-rs changed dithering again. We need slightly more fuzz on these files then Chrome did when they updated the fuzz values.\n\nFor icc-uncommon-profile-reftest: the fuzz in the html file got updated and we no longer need our ini to pass.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327293\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/jpegxl/icc-uncommon-profile-reftest.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/jpegxl/progressive-1.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/jpegxl/progressive-2.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/jpegxl/progressive-3.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/progressive-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/progressive-3.html"], "git_node": "0a923796d0903c8290bc77ada2aeead54aa8a788", "git_parents": ["6deacd2c33c2c94160d5cdbd0b462048185ad286"], "node": "c64b6b4c2707b8bb0ab5f008294cab170a9ccc89", "parents": ["96676046125a6daed4482e6ba38ceb619b16c346"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073437. Adjust fuzz on jpegxl/cmyk-basic-conversion-reftest.html to account for CMS differences. r=saschanaz\n\nUpstream tightened maxDifference to 3 in\nhttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62575, which is what Chrome\nhits. We need 9 because how qcms implements CMYK conversions is faster but less\nprecise, especially for CMYK values that lie outside of the destination color\nspace (sRGB).\n\nRunning through the calculation at one of the pixels that ends up 9 off is\nillustrative of the issue. At (240, 321) the image has CMYK 194, 10, 104, 4\n(out of 255, with 0 meaning no ink). At full precision the ICC profile's A2B0\ntag takes that to L* 63.50, a* -40.66, b* -7.10. Converting that to linear sRGB\ngives -0.0062, 0.4192, 0.3758. Negative red component means that sRGB cannot\nquite reach this color. Clamping that negative to 0 and encoding gives 0,\nwhich is what the reference PNG has.\n\nqcms uses a 17x17x17x17 lookup table with interpolation to compute the whole\nCMYK to encoded RGB conversion in one step, not just the A2B0 part. We run the\nconversion above at each grid point and store it in the table. Then we use\ntetrahedral interpolation between the closest grid points to compute the final\nvalue. Because the table holds finished values, its points are stored already\nclamped into the output gamut (ie non negative). The eight grid points around\nour pixel (when we computed them) had true linear reds from -0.0326 to +0.0095,\nwith four of them being positive and four of them being negative (those are\nstored as 0 after clamping and gamma encoding to sRGB). The +0.0095 (in [0,1],\nlinear sRGB) one encodes to 25 (in [0,255], sRGB). The slope near zero of sRGB\nis steep so 1% of full scale in linear light becomes ~10% when gamma encoded.\nInterpolation of eight values, four of which are 0, and four of which are\npositive can never reasonably give back the 0 that we require for the\nreference, so it comes out close to 10, which is the difference the fuzz has to\ncover.\n\nTrying to let the table hold negatives actually makes the image worse overall,\nmoving more pixels further away from the reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327294\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/jpegxl/cmyk-basic-conversion-reftest.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/cmyk-basic-conversion-reftest.html"], "git_node": "45cf2fd46a5c508482ffe4a62ca8b569c011300f", "git_parents": ["0a923796d0903c8290bc77ada2aeead54aa8a788"], "node": "0bdb0e8debf5cd779f01ad601c3848b992f210fc", "parents": ["c64b6b4c2707b8bb0ab5f008294cab170a9ccc89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074101 - Create new verifyTheRemoteImprovementsItemsTest and verifyTheDownloadSettingsItemsTest regression UI tests r=aaronmt\n\nBoth UI tests successfully passed 25x on Firebase \u2705\nAll UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase \u2705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327818\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/NavigationReachabilityParameterizedTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/PageContext.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/CustomTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAdvancedDownloadSettingsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAdvancedRemoteImprovementsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/CustomTabsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsAdvancedDownloadSettingsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsAdvancedRemoteImprovementsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SettingsAdvancedTest.kt"], "git_node": "d4b5907b314695b4aded6c02f8af1bb00a8a9da5", "git_parents": ["45cf2fd46a5c508482ffe4a62ca8b569c011300f"], "node": "6c1f7dca4e2596138af5935f5b86ee75c8c7588d", "parents": ["0bdb0e8debf5cd779f01ad601c3848b992f210fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073612 - Close the urlbar view when its last result is removed. r=daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327598\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_trendingDismissal.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-results/browser_acknowledgeFeedbackAndDismissal.js"], "git_node": "12c2c3b1478ce1b632ceec74fc684655b0cd8a90", "git_parents": ["d4b5907b314695b4aded6c02f8af1bb00a8a9da5"], "node": "dd5afed799cd5630c5d36af0dc72075d764b93cf", "parents": ["6c1f7dca4e2596138af5935f5b86ee75c8c7588d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072113 - Give the urlbar input box a zero flex basis so the Not Secure label keeps its width in a narrow window. r=daleharvey,urlbar-reviewers\n\nThe XUL flex attribute computed to `flex: 1`, and bug 2062215 replaced it with `flex-grow: 1`, so the box's own content width started competing with the site-info slot's when the container shrinks.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327675\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "88c52eea51954a02b639bfcd0a31cf6d8b7e8b7b", "git_parents": ["12c2c3b1478ce1b632ceec74fc684655b0cd8a90"], "node": "39bb5caa1c5782d20874846221469629e9bda4dd", "parents": ["dd5afed799cd5630c5d36af0dc72075d764b93cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "f3tch \u003cftech169@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1917288 - Increase expiry date range for network cookie tests. r=jdescottes,webdriver-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327607\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/__init__.py"], "git_node": "e5e64c8ed818679edd73139b61b3212310472bc2", "git_parents": ["88c52eea51954a02b639bfcd0a31cf6d8b7e8b7b"], "node": "5875be42a5bdec56179c2114f2e855f9d97ed8a3", "parents": ["39bb5caa1c5782d20874846221469629e9bda4dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074396 - Use moz-src for browser/components/protocolhandler r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328085\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/components/protocolhandler/components.conf", "browser/components/protocolhandler/moz.build", "browser/components/tests/browser/browser_default_webprotocol_handler_mailto.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "b44ad8bb6b98ea400ab0ca18abc1126caafd96d2", "git_parents": ["e5e64c8ed818679edd73139b61b3212310472bc2"], "node": "cfdbfe6f1fee62f316797b6fd3ac7a48c91f5441", "parents": ["5875be42a5bdec56179c2114f2e855f9d97ed8a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074293 - Skip the videoOrientation reftests on mingw builds, which disable WebRTC. r=webrtc-reviewers,ng\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328017\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/tests/reftest/reftest.list"], "git_node": "fba5c5949b5dfa2845491af1e772936164bf680e", "git_parents": ["b44ad8bb6b98ea400ab0ca18abc1126caafd96d2"], "node": "d1e8dee41abb143d7607c766ce4af80de69d39e6", "parents": ["cfdbfe6f1fee62f316797b6fd3ac7a48c91f5441"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2040905 - nsStandardURL::Deserialize should reparse the URL r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309064\n", "files": ["dom/security/test/unit/test_csp_deserialization.js", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "2a3948b8c0117550d4750fbc4cbc9133de660c88", "git_parents": ["fba5c5949b5dfa2845491af1e772936164bf680e"], "node": "8460a7e47a842f9c6503d2f1e6274fe1114eb57b", "parents": ["d1e8dee41abb143d7607c766ce4af80de69d39e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Do not restore URL state on failure r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nPreviously, when URLs were mutable, we'd need to restore URL state\nwhen a setter operation failed. However, this copy of the URL state is now\nredundant, as any mutator operation that fails will simply throw away\nthe state.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308229\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_standardurl.js"], "git_node": "a00819d9a2bb71881784c2dacea2753f53a71cc5", "git_parents": ["2a3948b8c0117550d4750fbc4cbc9133de660c88"], "node": "a89cbbcd578c463c7d1c9e80f2863deb74fe14a0", "parents": ["8460a7e47a842f9c6503d2f1e6274fe1114eb57b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - avoid strlen call r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308230\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "98c26b1ef056f5abd93021f58985cecff99bea64", "git_parents": ["a00819d9a2bb71881784c2dacea2753f53a71cc5"], "node": "2e0602f77c69f72ac283cae57bb479c69f4018dd", "parents": ["a89cbbcd578c463c7d1c9e80f2863deb74fe14a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Optimize IsSpecialProtocol r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308231\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "25b941be42b23d21147cbdb54866032d56a62bf4", "git_parents": ["98c26b1ef056f5abd93021f58985cecff99bea64"], "node": "ea275b8b057f563bc9d676139bf7b9a643e8caa8", "parents": ["2e0602f77c69f72ac283cae57bb479c69f4018dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Optimize coalescePath r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308232\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_standardurl.js"], "git_node": "a005d2952f1d39ef61d1872f7be0db610ef19db5", "git_parents": ["25b941be42b23d21147cbdb54866032d56a62bf4"], "node": "c6ae994eb5424941c208859afd86dda62a9412f7", "parents": ["ea275b8b057f563bc9d676139bf7b9a643e8caa8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Optimize SegmentIs r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308233\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.h"], "git_node": "69858105f989a488016481ce7a29038b04d5dce6", "git_parents": ["a005d2952f1d39ef61d1872f7be0db610ef19db5"], "node": "9688fe21f7581e8f71504c2629fef9df66728141", "parents": ["c6ae994eb5424941c208859afd86dda62a9412f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Optimize CalculateParity r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308234\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.h"], "git_node": "5ea0170b63aa4815feb1e545c0ed72bc7eb1cc72", "git_parents": ["69858105f989a488016481ce7a29038b04d5dce6"], "node": "ec427f364264a739a9da579aa8f00df3aff6c9fa", "parents": ["9688fe21f7581e8f71504c2629fef9df66728141"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Fewer string passes r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308235\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsURLHelper.cpp"], "git_node": "9f8f8041b2838f738739973b69adbe84431a8ebf", "git_parents": ["5ea0170b63aa4815feb1e545c0ed72bc7eb1cc72"], "node": "1e8af188737cdfe21c95f690ec57248ef034a1aa", "parents": ["ec427f364264a739a9da579aa8f00df3aff6c9fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Fast path for BuildNormalized r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308236\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "55e67704b69e832da8b8f787f68ccad31c0d519f", "git_parents": ["9f8f8041b2838f738739973b69adbe84431a8ebf"], "node": "8451ba77b60d266fc1035e7bf50900e3453044f8", "parents": ["1e8af188737cdfe21c95f690ec57248ef034a1aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Add nonXPCOM ParseAll method to nsBaseURLParser r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308237\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.h", "netwerk/base/nsURLHelper.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsURLHelper.h", "netwerk/base/nsURLParsers.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsURLParsers.h", "toolkit/components/backgroundtasks/tests/browser/browser_xpcom_graph_wait.js"], "git_node": "47a1b005e3652a6e6d4c9a12e688c0322e81011c", "git_parents": ["55e67704b69e832da8b8f787f68ccad31c0d519f"], "node": "c1612fcfabedc2b918b5c5b0f2eaa5494229651d", "parents": ["8451ba77b60d266fc1035e7bf50900e3453044f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049622 - Don't assert on non-UTF-8 input in nsSegmentEncoder r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nnsStandardURL's setters take nsACString, which carries no UTF-8 guarantee, so\nthe MOZ_ASSERT_UNREACHABLE in EncodeSegmentCount asserts on something callers\ncan legitimately do. SetQueryWithEncoding reaches it on its own: a legacy\ncharset makes mEncoding non-null, and any non-UTF-8 byte in the query then\nlands in that branch.\n\nThe code immediately below already handles the case correctly, decoding the\ninput to UTF-8 and substituting U+FFFD for invalid sequences, so the assertion\nonly turns a handled input into a debug-build crash. Drop it and add a gtest\nthat pins the resulting normalization.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325944\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "9257c2181ae2fda3a13eb420e8d5bf2a4ee874f0", "git_parents": ["47a1b005e3652a6e6d4c9a12e688c0322e81011c"], "node": "a0bc3a3aa3e1e4896bdd174c209268e409eafeda", "parents": ["c1612fcfabedc2b918b5c5b0f2eaa5494229651d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cristian Tuns \u003cctuns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2071777 - Make LoadHistoryEntry MOZ_CAN_RUN_SCRIPT. r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,saschanaz,win-reviewers,dom-worker-reviewers,smaug,gstoll,valentin,asuth\" for causing build bustages in nsWindow.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 6deacd2c33c2c94160d5cdbd0b462048185ad286.\n", "files": ["accessible/generic/ImageAccessible.h", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.h", "docshell/base/nsIDocShell.idl", "docshell/base/nsIRefreshURI.idl", "docshell/base/nsIWebNavigation.idl", "docshell/base/nsRefreshTimer.cpp", "docshell/base/nsRefreshTimer.h", "dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/base/Location.h", "dom/base/LocationBase.h", "dom/base/nsFrameLoader.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.h", "dom/base/nsPIDOMWindow.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerChild.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerService.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientNavigateOpChild.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientOpenWindowUtils.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientOpenWindowUtils.h", "dom/credentialmanagement/identity/WebIdentityChild.cpp", "dom/credentialmanagement/identity/WebIdentityChild.h", "dom/documentpip/DocumentPictureInPicture.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserChild.h", "dom/ipc/ContentChild.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h", "dom/navigation/Navigation.cpp", "dom/navigation/Navigation.h", "dom/notification/NotificationHandler.cpp", "editor/composer/nsEditingSession.h", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.h", "security/manager/pki/nsNSSDialogHelper.h", "security/manager/ssl/PKCS11ModuleDB.h", "security/manager/ssl/PKCS11ModuleParent.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsICertificateDialogs.idl", "security/manager/ssl/nsIX509CertDB.idl", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCallbacks.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCertificateDB.h", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsXULAlerts.h", "toolkit/components/commandlines/nsCommandLine.cpp", "toolkit/components/commandlines/nsICommandLineHandler.idl", "toolkit/components/startup/public/nsIAppStartup.idl", "toolkit/components/windowcreator/nsIWindowCreator.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsIWindowWatcher.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsPIWindowWatcher.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.cpp", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.h", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp", "widget/nsIPrintDialogService.idl", "widget/windows/nsPrintDialogWin.cpp", "widget/windows/nsPrintDialogWin.h", "xpcom/build/nsXULAppAPI.h", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.h", "xpfe/appshell/nsAppShellService.h", "xpfe/appshell/nsIAppShellService.idl", "xpfe/appshell/nsIAppWindow.idl"], "git_node": "cdc57d8e4d9dd63153e48d80006d3b9843e282de", "git_parents": ["9257c2181ae2fda3a13eb420e8d5bf2a4ee874f0"], "node": "058b34e46526ec020e722722438647c636790060", "parents": ["a0bc3a3aa3e1e4896bdd174c209268e409eafeda"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ayoub hedri \u003cahedri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063005 - Copy original channel's permissionsPolicyInfo to the new channel for javascript URLs r=tschuster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327785\n", "files": ["dom/jsurl/nsJSProtocolHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "38628560257ab36e0bdee0dca2fa6ccdbd45a497", "git_parents": ["cdc57d8e4d9dd63153e48d80006d3b9843e282de"], "node": "1eaf73f223f1b9dac7906cfc4cd060295b8f18d0", "parents": ["058b34e46526ec020e722722438647c636790060"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erich Gubler \u003cerichdongubler@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067035 - refactor(webgpu): set `constantEntry.key` from `constantKeys`, not `key` r=webgpu-reviewers,teoxoy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321793\n", "files": ["dom/webgpu/Device.cpp"], "git_node": "b41cd50a8b7401f0950ed6607dcb4009d2d25dec", "git_parents": ["38628560257ab36e0bdee0dca2fa6ccdbd45a497"], "node": "00cf7bec45533206375b38c55d660ca2bdc0ee93", "parents": ["1eaf73f223f1b9dac7906cfc4cd060295b8f18d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041621 - [devtools] Handle percentage values in InspectorUtils.getComputationSteps. r=layout-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio,ochameau.\n\nWe now pass the property name to the method so we can properly compute the\npercentage basis (it might depend on the width/height/inline/block size of the\nelement/its parent).\nWe can then pass this percentage basis to `Servo_GetComputationSteps` so we\ncan substitute those with actual size.\n\nWe're bailing out on a few case: if the passed property is unknown, or if it's\na shorthand for which the % value would be computed differently for the longhands\nit represents, or if the property % value is more challenging to compute (e.g.\nbackground-position-*, which depends on the background image size).\n\nTest cases are added to cover this feature.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326471\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_css_explainers.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/utils/utils.js", "devtools/client/shared/widgets/tooltip/css-explainers-tooltip-helper.js", "devtools/server/actors/style-rule.js", "devtools/shared/specs/style-rule.js", "dom/chrome-webidl/InspectorUtils.webidl", "layout/inspector/InspectorUtils.cpp", "layout/inspector/InspectorUtils.h", "layout/inspector/tests/test_getComputationSteps.html", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "bec60f3c689010562a86244434edc8cd5f608e82", "git_parents": ["b41cd50a8b7401f0950ed6607dcb4009d2d25dec"], "node": "9bbca40b683caa484a1cbf6f566680bc26d97894", "parents": ["00cf7bec45533206375b38c55d660ca2bdc0ee93"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070166 - [devtools] Add InspectorUtils method that returns the substituted value of a given expression. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326952\n", "files": ["dom/chrome-webidl/InspectorUtils.webidl", "layout/inspector/InspectorUtils.cpp", "layout/inspector/InspectorUtils.h", "layout/inspector/tests/mochitest.toml", "layout/inspector/tests/test_getSubstitutedValue.html", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "2481988c660ff52893eea73a872bbe030e423dd0", "git_parents": ["bec60f3c689010562a86244434edc8cd5f608e82"], "node": "2382129cfd4a5c9040e1150fd0c4cd84c4fc25af", "parents": ["9bbca40b683caa484a1cbf6f566680bc26d97894"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074405 - Accept simple dimension and percentage expressions in Servo_GetComputationSteps. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio.\n\nUntil now, we were only accepting function calls expressions (e.g. calc(1px * 2).\nThis patch handles dimensions (e.g. `1em`, `2vw`, `3lh`, \u2026) as well as percentage (e.g. `50%`).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327269\n", "files": ["layout/inspector/tests/test_getComputationSteps.html", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "7851e55b7c87f7d739a08e38cc1a353af539152d", "git_parents": ["2481988c660ff52893eea73a872bbe030e423dd0"], "node": "fb758881ed13154f46fedb883ea3e9bcec440010", "parents": ["2382129cfd4a5c9040e1150fd0c4cd84c4fc25af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073144 - Lint all dom/animation headers through clang-tidy r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nActually, just rework forward declaration to make header self contained.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327948\n", "files": ["dom/animation/AnimationTarget.h"], "git_node": "918cea246650bacee1df4090aaef0575cb12d3bf", "git_parents": ["7851e55b7c87f7d739a08e38cc1a353af539152d"], "node": "b07128ed162acab004edf18b662d9579dfde888a", "parents": ["fb758881ed13154f46fedb883ea3e9bcec440010"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073144 - Lint all dom/bindings headers through clang-tidy r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nChanges includes:\n- using C++20 type aliases and inline variables\n- using nullptr where appropriate\n- making deleted methods public\n- making some methods default\n- rework some include dependencies to make header self contained\n\nAll changes were detected either by header compilation failure, or by\nclang-tidy.\n\nFixes are either generated by clang-tidy or hand-made\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327949\n", "files": ["dom/bindings/BindingDeclarations.h", "dom/bindings/CallbackObject.h", "dom/bindings/ErrorResult.h", "dom/bindings/RootedOwningNonNull.h", "dom/bindings/RootedRefPtr.h", "dom/bindings/SpiderMonkeyInterface.h", "dom/bindings/ToJSValue.h", "dom/bindings/TypedArray.h", "dom/bindings/UnionMember.h"], "git_node": "14ef8c098f19ee12e03dac82c6aa7530c1ed7be1", "git_parents": ["918cea246650bacee1df4090aaef0575cb12d3bf"], "node": "3c37079caf5f91ba02c60fc9aae601c3b9cc3bcc", "parents": ["b07128ed162acab004edf18b662d9579dfde888a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tiaan Louw \u003ctlouw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1995348 - Implement the \"grid-lanes\" value for the \"display\" property r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,dholbert,emilio\n\nUse the \"display: grid-lanes\" value to conform to current usage in web\nplatform tests.\n\nTwo tests are marked as CRASH, because the masonry code uses a sort\ncomparitor that is not valid strick weak ordering as required, so it\nasserts in debug builds. See bug 2068688.\n\nSee: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-grid-3/#masonry-model\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D273845\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.cpp", "layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/inspector/tests/test_bug877690.html", "layout/style/test/property_database.js", "layout/style/test/test_position_float_display.html", "modules/l