/phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327997\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webrtc/mdns-candidate-obfuscation.html"], "git_node": "4f93cc8628bb730e4702283a0f8bf01a7473b232", "git_parents": ["fb2c7d57dc57d21338b5a65af47e61ebfdccde78"], "node": "e68b454ced2f54cd1bd08263d2aaf6be1e361941", "parents": ["6d0e09d88abe0e5289f86633078c96e8220d47cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045846: Fix CSS zoom for translations. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326739\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/AnimationInfo.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/painting/ActiveLayerTracker.cpp", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp", "layout/style/StyleAnimationValue.cpp", "layout/style/nsComputedDOMStyle.cpp", "layout/style/nsStyleTransformMatrix.cpp", "layout/style/nsStyleTransformMatrix.h", "layout/svg/SVGUtils.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/reference/translate-zoom-anim-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/translate-matrix-zoom-anim-accumulate.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/translate-matrix-zoom-anim-accumulated-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/translate-zoom-anim-calc.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/translate-zoom-anim-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/translate-zoom-anim.html"], "git_node": "c059228ee48525dfec90fa9a3df704c54b097c29", "git_parents": ["4f93cc8628bb730e4702283a0f8bf01a7473b232"], "node": "72e0f6b7b5a2b3785f86dea652553b1d96c9d39a", "parents": ["e68b454ced2f54cd1bd08263d2aaf6be1e361941"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckagami@tb.pro\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067657 - Part 1: Pass NotNull\u003cPromise*\u003e to LoadImageAndShow and SendShow r=mccr8,dom-core-reviewers\n\nAnd remove existing branch based on null promise.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328173\n", "files": ["dom/notification/Notification.cpp", "dom/notification/Notification.h"], "git_node": "4124a39720772b266e51bbe25fe143b957d6a5d8", "git_parents": ["c059228ee48525dfec90fa9a3df704c54b097c29"], "node": "f8d2bbc57f489d6ce2208fccebccc76884a801fb", "parents": ["72e0f6b7b5a2b3785f86dea652553b1d96c9d39a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckagami@tb.pro\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067657 - Part 2: Check the mActor referent in Notification::SendShow r=mccr8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322789\n", "files": ["dom/notification/Notification.cpp", "dom/notification/Notification.h"], "git_node": "fd0114b068149cdb9d57ae9d076102270035e19f", "git_parents": ["4124a39720772b266e51bbe25fe143b957d6a5d8"], "node": "2193bdbd06120563471c4c2fdbc98e2a31768d47", "parents": ["f8d2bbc57f489d6ce2208fccebccc76884a801fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harveer Singh \u003chsingh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1374970: navigator.storage.estimate must return origin usage rather than groups.r=jari,dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324981\n", "files": ["dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/quota/OriginOperations.cpp", "dom/quota/OriginOperations.h", "dom/quota/PQuota.ipdl", "dom/quota/QuotaManager.h", "dom/quota/QuotaManagerService.cpp", "dom/quota/QuotaParent.cpp", "dom/quota/StorageManager.cpp", "dom/quota/nsIQuotaManagerService.idl", "dom/quota/test/xpcshell/common/head.js", "dom/quota/test/xpcshell/common/utils.js", "dom/quota/test/xpcshell/test_estimateGroupUsage.js", "dom/quota/test/xpcshell/test_estimateOrigin.js", "dom/quota/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerQuotaUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "b18691d1070e5750a6a6f44c44e1d3a8ae9f07ab", "git_parents": ["fd0114b068149cdb9d57ae9d076102270035e19f"], "node": "1d58d7e9df187f70a316fc995e93e889d92bdf29", "parents": ["2193bdbd06120563471c4c2fdbc98e2a31768d47"], "tags": []}, {"author": "chloezhouny \u003cchloezhouny@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070425 - Split browser_smartwindow_manage_tabs_tool.js so it stops timing out r=Mardak\n\nThe file grew to 19 tasks after bug 2061465 and now runs for about 102s against the 90s per-file limit, so it fails with \"This test exceeded the timeout threshold\" on most runs.\n\nSplit it along what the tasks actually cover, so each file gets its own timeout budget:\n\n- browser_smartwindow_manage_tabs_tool.js keeps the confirmation UI, retry, and cross-window closeSelectedTabs/undo behavior (6 tasks).\n- browser_smartwindow_manage_tabs_tool_telemetry.js takes the telemetry funnel tests built on captureFunnel (13 tasks).\n\nEach file imports only what it uses and carries its own add_setup. No test logic changed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327452\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_manage_tabs_tool.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_manage_tabs_tool_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "1a6ada7dcaafe54bfb8d32fed04bbcbd3751d52b", "git_parents": ["b18691d1070e5750a6a6f44c44e1d3a8ae9f07ab"], "node": "9d67a677fc5d92250e7e51235f4049813f536d93", "parents": ["1d58d7e9df187f70a316fc995e93e889d92bdf29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1632281 - Read the AutoConfig input prefs from the installation, not the profile. r=gstoll\n\nThe AutoConfig inputs are administrator settings, so nsReadConfig clears their\nuser values before evaluating the .cfg: a profile's prefs.js or user.js no\nlonger decides which file nsAutoConfig fetches or whether the vendor check\npasses. The .cfg can still set them with pref().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327889\n", "files": ["extensions/pref/autoconfig/src/nsReadConfig.cpp", "extensions/pref/autoconfig/test/unit/autoconfig-admin-pref.cfg", "extensions/pref/autoconfig/test/unit/autoconfig-admin-url-pref.cfg", "extensions/pref/autoconfig/test/unit/autoconfig-admin.cfg", "extensions/pref/autoconfig/test/unit/autoconfig-remote.jsc", "extensions/pref/autoconfig/test/unit/test_autoconfig_profile_prefs.js", "extensions/pref/autoconfig/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "ed634e3eb11b53fff30f31557c631cd6bdc82694", "git_parents": ["1a6ada7dcaafe54bfb8d32fed04bbcbd3751d52b"], "node": "ac7684d17649f7944fe3f6154d486ddc479c5412", "parents": ["9d67a677fc5d92250e7e51235f4049813f536d93"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074240 - Prioritize a reframe restore over a history restore. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nThe test doesn't seem particularly reliable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328160\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "0a59771f32b17b47e29aeb91fc4010c25516a274", "git_parents": ["ed634e3eb11b53fff30f31557c631cd6bdc82694"], "node": "e03869718628648d92f03df6673114c21ac876c4", "parents": ["ac7684d17649f7944fe3f6154d486ddc479c5412"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073940 - Only quit for a utility or socket process crash that produced a minidump. r=ipc-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,crashreporting-reviewers,nika,gsvelto\n\nMaybeTerminateProcess force-quits the parent under MOZ_CRASHREPORTER_SHUTDOWN on any AbnormalShutdown of the\nutility or socket process, including one the OS killed. On Android the utility, GPU and socket children are\nbound with BIND_WAIVE_PRIORITY while the app is in the background, which a junit run always is, so\nActivityManager trims the utility process as a cached-empty process whenever the cached-process cap is\nreached, and on coverage builds lmkd kills it under memory pressure; either way the whole test run dies with\nit. Those kills leave no minidump, so quit only when GenerateCrashReport produced one, and warn when a crash\nreport could not be taken so the skipped quit is visible in the log. Kills the parent performs itself, such as\nthe utility shutdown-timeout KillHard, also leave no minidump and no longer abort the run.\n\nThe minidump check only applies while the crash reporter is enabled: with the reporter disabled at runtime or\nbuilt as the dummy implementation (ASan and fuzzing builds), no crash produces a minidump, so the quit stays\nunconditional there.\n\nWith that, ProfileLockedTest and StorageControllerTest no longer need the coverage-build skip from bug\n2073274; Environment.isCoverageBuild stays for the next test that needs it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327719\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/CrashReporterHelper.h", "ipc/glue/UtilityProcessParent.cpp", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/ProfileLockedTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/StorageControllerTest.kt", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "7a1f047076bfcfa11afec49172869879c325ff0e", "git_parents": ["0a59771f32b17b47e29aeb91fc4010c25516a274"], "node": "5a86b87861197873a9b54fec8ff149296f6e10b5", "parents": ["e03869718628648d92f03df6673114c21ac876c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandre Lissy \u003clissyx+mozillians@lissyx.dyndns.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074486 - Use supported policy for Enterprise in null policy test r=mkaply\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328142\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_null_policy_value.js"], "git_node": "950d11a50733201db4275b7751ebedb465b29201", "git_parents": ["7a1f047076bfcfa11afec49172869879c325ff0e"], "node": "6c3a15233f693533074d0af7c21bb4e4d0922461", "parents": ["5a86b87861197873a9b54fec8ff149296f6e10b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Darnell \u003cdaniel@thunderbird.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046296 - Add ability to skip generating specified test archives. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310748\n", "files": ["build/gen_test_packages_manifest.py", "moz.configure", "testing/testsuite-targets.mk", "toolkit/moz.configure"], "git_node": "2c62c261d455c33347386b0c98c4973811927acb", "git_parents": ["950d11a50733201db4275b7751ebedb465b29201"], "node": "43f40fe6355ed89e3da7173b6bbd18da82e14ab8", "parents": ["6c3a15233f693533074d0af7c21bb4e4d0922461"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Roger Yang \u003croyang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074264 - Enable VPN by default and add the more countries to the allowed regions. r=android-reviewers,cbect\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328001\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml"], "git_node": "1d18d40da7e2486c2512ae4ef5fbeaccf6676e86", "git_parents": ["2c62c261d455c33347386b0c98c4973811927acb"], "node": "081ff39df8bd085aad2833943876592554ebb15f", "parents": ["43f40fe6355ed89e3da7173b6bbd18da82e14ab8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chaoya Li \u003charry75369@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2000420 - Don't scan the whole file for AAC frame count in MatroskaDemuxer. r=alwu,media-playback-reviewers\n\nSetContainerAudioCodecInfo called nestegg_read_total_frames_count()\nduring ReadMetadata for AAC tracks. That function reads clusters until\nEOS, so playback cannot start until the entire file is downloaded.\n\nNothing reads AacCodecSpecificData::mMediaFrameCount downstream (it is\nonly copied into never-read decoder members), so leave it at 0 and skip\nthe scan. This also removes a hard failure path: a counting error used\nto reject the whole file.\n\nTest: TEST(MatroskaDemuxer, AACNoFullFileScan) Inits output_aac.mkv\nand asserts mMediaFrameCount stays 0 while audio demuxes normally.\n\nVerified over throttled HTTP: ReadMetadata now completes 0.4s after\nstart (previously never within 32s) and A/V samples demux and decode\nnormally.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323906\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestWebMDemuxer.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build", "dom/media/webm/MatroskaDemuxer.cpp"], "git_node": "25ed56f8cb56ab7fda4d1016a780562f8868ee76", "git_parents": ["1d18d40da7e2486c2512ae4ef5fbeaccf6676e86"], "node": "0f0535bed7bf29ed486fdb43b517052606bf82bb", "parents": ["081ff39df8bd085aad2833943876592554ebb15f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chaoya Li \u003charry75369@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071759 - Make AAC media frame count a Maybe to distinguish unset from zero. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nAacCodecSpecificData::mMediaFrameCount was a plain uint64_t defaulting to\n0, so downstream code could not tell 'not parsed' apart from 'parsed,\nzero frames'. This matters since Bug 2000420 leaves the count unset for\nMatroska AAC tracks instead of scanning the whole file.\n\nMake it a Maybe\u003cuint64_t\u003e, unset by default and set only when an exact\ncount is known (MP4 with a sample index). Readers keep their behavior\nvia valueOr(0); IPC serialization is covered by the generic Maybe\nParamTraits.\n\nTest: TEST(MatroskaDemuxer, AACFrameCountNotParsed) now asserts the\ncount is Nothing instead of 0.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325819\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaInfo.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestWebMDemuxer.cpp", "dom/media/mp4/DecoderData.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/apple/AppleATDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFAudioMFTManager.cpp"], "git_node": "7f3c15fc8b8e9f4440c8b40b1553d81e72f4c5fd", "git_parents": ["25ed56f8cb56ab7fda4d1016a780562f8868ee76"], "node": "6921e2e38d0e15b1b3a26178b3aa41694449522b", "parents": ["0f0535bed7bf29ed486fdb43b517052606bf82bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074503 - Implement CSSNumericValue.equals(); r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nThe implementation determines whether numeric values are structurally equal,\nrequiring the same type and value and recursively comparing compound values\nsuch as CSSMathSum and CSSMathProduct in the same order.\n\nIt uses the existing CSSNumericValue subclass infrastructure to implement the\nstructural comparison algorithm.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328161\n", "files": ["layout/style/typedom/CSSNumericValue.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSNumericValue.h", "layout/style/typedom/CSSUnitValue.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/numeric-objects/equals.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "5813645774cebb259eae20a9c1b490e055246d4e", "git_parents": ["7f3c15fc8b8e9f4440c8b40b1553d81e72f4c5fd"], "node": "7daba1a2ae7a2b2d770295d740addd362316338f", "parents": ["6921e2e38d0e15b1b3a26178b3aa41694449522b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nishu Sheth \u003cnsheth@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843808: Add haptic feedback when performing history swipe gesture on MacBook. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328059\n", "files": ["widget/SwipeTracker.cpp", "widget/SwipeTracker.h", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.h", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm", "widget/nsIWidget.h"], "git_node": "00c8cc7be1d80238a8f041536e48e1f0f539fd0d", "git_parents": ["5813645774cebb259eae20a9c1b490e055246d4e"], "node": "b893cba0693e4433d4d02defb4f3e8654c69c293", "parents": ["7daba1a2ae7a2b2d770295d740addd362316338f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2039193: Don't report a non-finite media duration to the platform media controls. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nHTMLMediaElement::Duration() is NaN while the element has no decoder, which is the case for a moment whenever a site switches sources, and infinite for a stream. The guessed position state handed both to the platform backends. navigator.mediaSession.setPositionState() cannot produce either value because WebIDL rejects a non-finite double, so the check only belongs on the guessed path.\n\nThe Cocoa backend ignored an empty position state, which would now leave the previous track's duration on the Now Playing timeline, so it removes the timeline keys instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328054\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediacontrol/tests/browser/browser_media_control_position_state.js", "dom/media/mediacontrol/tests/gtest/TestMediaKeysEventMediaCenter.mm", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp", "widget/cocoa/MediaHardwareKeysEventSourceMacMediaCenter.mm"], "git_node": "e4d7feb4c0ccfefd5c2056be0e8e23485ee22c6f", "git_parents": ["00c8cc7be1d80238a8f041536e48e1f0f539fd0d"], "node": "a82a5592a94a2bc1fe765f4c514982377cbb394e", "parents": ["b893cba0693e4433d4d02defb4f3e8654c69c293"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066606 - Add the always-on-top mini window component behind a pref. r=mconley,tabbrowser-reviewers,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322131\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/customizableui/CustomizeMode.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/moz.build", "browser/components/moz.build", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab-bar-visibility.js", "browser/modules/BrowserDOMWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/modules/BrowserWindowTracker.sys.mjs", "browser/modules/URILoadingHelper.sys.mjs", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts"], "git_node": "f4a8ebb1bb323516b0c7b09a7feed733290fa176", "git_parents": ["e4d7feb4c0ccfefd5c2056be0e8e23485ee22c6f"], "node": "bdd31d539cce0473dccb7699a0c590eb90267a6e", "parents": ["a82a5592a94a2bc1fe765f4c514982377cbb394e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066606 - Exclude mini windows from the messaging system. r=omc-reviewers,mimi\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322133\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouter.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/InfoBar.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "193519cefbd434d231f4f15baea754633ca0b059", "git_parents": ["f4a8ebb1bb323516b0c7b09a7feed733290fa176"], "node": "0fa8d3be6d9450cd88077603c119bea74ac1d465", "parents": ["bdd31d539cce0473dccb7699a0c590eb90267a6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066606 - Return mini windows when the origin window's last tab is closed. r=mconley,tabbrowser-reviewers,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322134\n", "files": ["browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "02d13a41182202d8d09abe40b5ecf6f64df2e489", "git_parents": ["193519cefbd434d231f4f15baea754633ca0b059"], "node": "490f8a9559c79d03d6fb4962ce4869f7f0629b61", "parents": ["0fa8d3be6d9450cd88077603c119bea74ac1d465"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branc