0bc818c11e95fce8723ac72727483cd41", "8a4cce3a21f2a0663889fde41caf861cde42bc1a", "98775b6ba11154583a344a734cb30eeff6bf9f80", "bd7cf6d65792f20c1b6010d6db2d269c1e00b0ee", "f9b066a166766cd416640999dfd73d9846671872", "2ab4904e80bc7b917cb5682cee0929d09f396e98", "51213fb610ce472b32bf6358377958163a5379a1", "906a45bc27784742fede9457c2111c8e4c2519b3", "c278c474255dca4cfead850689a6f79fb35fd56a", "5e698b4bc0368870db2acc0903a37e7a1bc25168", "4f6dfc66ab10cfab3cc835fe033afba98fa70c03", "9b595d974dd5a4073db1555d948e5c04cb0de082", "853e8033cafe52ac8a16c5e6828e66e184d3c9d7", "e893294272b202f3a88ee498c2b3e11271dec6e5", "bcc068c1ea8a217b378f01b20afd99f912c43c93", "281872e7df7b7d31f0090788d747d44e5d124874"], "user": "asilaghi@mozilla.com"}, "45391": {"changesets": [{"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2074592 - fix(pbw): Relay promo and basics spotlight fixes from QA r=omc-reviewers,emcminn\" for causing node failures related to asrouter-newtab-multistage.\n\nThis reverts commit 853e8033cafe52ac8a16c5e6828e66e184d3c9d7.\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/BrowserUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "428af5c20dcedde48f4e6cc40e591f6115c85205", "git_parents": ["281872e7df7b7d31f0090788d747d44e5d124874"], "node": "631808b9e7769c9abb03b6eab7f09e2a0541325b", "parents": ["2f4d0547f3592dcc5ee6df96641f847831fef838"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790137470, "git_changesets": ["428af5c20dcedde48f4e6cc40e591f6115c85205"], "user": "asilaghi@mozilla.com"}, "45392": {"changesets": [{"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073419 - Only transition the newtab customize panel's visibility on the way out, r=nina-py.\n\n.customize-menu is visibility: hidden and transitions visibility along with its\nslide-in transform, so the first style resolution of the enter phase still\ncomputes hidden. Nothing in a hidden subtree is focusable, so the close button\nfocus the component takes from onEntered silently does nothing and nothing\nretries: the panel opens with focus still outside it.\n\nThe exit direction is what needs the transition, to keep the panel visible while\nit slides away, so declare visibility only there. The animation is unchanged:\nthe panel was hidden for one frame of the enter phase, with the transform\nholding it off screen anyway.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327287\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/_CustomizeMenu.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_customize_menu_content.js"], "git_node": "1c7ac40bc76efcc5c2d8537e67319b972ccb8242", "git_parents": ["281872e7df7b7d31f0090788d747d44e5d124874"], "node": "2a474f32ce2eeea48e93cdc58997eb56cea42b43", "parents": ["2f4d0547f3592dcc5ee6df96641f847831fef838"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072918 - Wait for the customize panel's own open state rather than its slide-in transform in browser_customize_menu_content.js, r=mconley.\n\nAll three tasks polled getComputedStyle(\".customize-menu\").transform for the\nidentity matrix, which only holds once the 250ms slide-in transition has run to\ncompletion, and a transition only advances while the refresh driver can tick: in\na job that cannot paint, the panel is open but the transform never moves. Wait\non the customize-animate-enter-done class and the dialog's open property, which\nthe component sets and which the sibling browser_customize_menu_render.js\nalready uses. The close checks get stronger too: open goes false in the panel's\nonExited, whereas the transform left the identity matrix as soon as the exit\ntransition started.\n\nThat poll was also the only style flush the enter phase got, and the close\nbutton focus does not take without one, so this depends on the patch that stops\ntransitioning the panel's visibility on the way in.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327113\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_customize_menu_content.js"], "git_node": "bbd85068caa272931a1dffc83376205845b91ea9", "git_parents": ["1c7ac40bc76efcc5c2d8537e67319b972ccb8242"], "node": "eed027150d81840f4224c323dbb300450aac9b13", "parents": ["2a474f32ce2eeea48e93cdc58997eb56cea42b43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1780305 - Wait for ExperimentManager.onStartup() before enrolling in NimbusTestUtils, r=nimbus-reviewers,beth.\n\nenroll() and enrollWithFeatureConfig() awaited only the experiment store, which\nis ready before ExperimentManager.onStartup() has run, so a caller using the\nglobal ExperimentManager could fail with the \"can't access property\n_annotateEnrollment\" of bug 1976460. A caller passing its own manager has\ninitialized it itself, so that path keeps the store-only wait.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327088\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/test/NimbusTestUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d60e2a0ca62fd3a15f4ad38492b083d1d4d87ec1", "git_parents": ["bbd85068caa272931a1dffc83376205845b91ea9"], "node": "177bd257a7e2b6f5107771cdefcf9dd21a4af454", "parents": ["eed027150d81840f4224c323dbb300450aac9b13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061014 - Return the window to the size browser_newtab_last_LinkMenu.js found it at, r=mconley.\n\nsetPrimaryContentSize fires no resize event when the content area already has\nthe size asked for, so setSize's wait for one hangs until the test times out.\nsetSize saved the window size on every call, so resetSize restored a size the\nfile had itself set, and it saved innerWidth/innerHeight but passed them to\nresizeTo, which takes the outer size; under test-verify the file walked itself\ninto that state on its third run in the same browser.\n\nThe size the file found is now saved once, as the content size.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327285\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_newtab_last_LinkMenu.js"], "git_node": "8cd5db7a1142f15563ad008388ae4968217fb8b5", "git_parents": ["d60e2a0ca62fd3a15f4ad38492b083d1d4d87ec1"], "node": "be388f0000d1861e9d6610931a2056f5ebc18097", "parents": ["177bd257a7e2b6f5107771cdefcf9dd21a4af454"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2031557 - Rebuild the top sites row without recreating TopSitesFeed in the newtab test helpers, r=ini.\n\nsetDefaultTopSites and setTestTopSites toggled feeds.system.topsites off and on\nto make the feed re-read the prefs they had just pushed, which destroys and\nrecreates TopSitesFeed. The destroyed instance still finishes the refresh it had\nin flight and broadcasts the row the test just replaced, so\nbrowser_topsites_section.js and browser_topsites_contextMenu_options.js wait for\na tile that never arrives. The toggle is not needed: TopSitesFeed observes\ndefault.sites itself.\n\nsetDefaultTopSites now pushes two pref environments rather than four, so\nbrowser_newtab_last_LinkMenu.js pops three rather than five.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327286\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_newtab_last_LinkMenu.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "295c956ce3f2a79d26ee71a1dae69eb997152c76", "git_parents": ["8cd5db7a1142f15563ad008388ae4968217fb8b5"], "node": "cf4dd026150bc0a343e293e5d39e801be50f7533", "parents": ["be388f0000d1861e9d6610931a2056f5ebc18097"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073421 - Stop TopSitesFeed dispatching a top sites row after uninit(), r=mconley.\n\nrefresh() lets only the newest refresh dispatch by comparing against\n_refreshGeneration, but that counter is per instance and uninit() does not touch\nit. When feeds.system.topsites is toggled, Store.onPrefChanged uninits the feed\nand constructs a new one while the old instance is still inside\ngetLinksWithDefaults(), so the old one passes its own generation check and\nbroadcasts a row built from the configuration that has just been replaced. An\nin-flight Contile fetch is a second way in, through the _readDefaults() it calls\nwhen it completes.\n\nMark the instance in uninit() and treat that mark like a superseded generation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327289\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TopSitesFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TopSitesFeed.js"], "git_node": "afe7d1b18c520c4468fcd330b6259a0f3f193cd4", "git_parents": ["295c956ce3f2a79d26ee71a1dae69eb997152c76"], "node": "42e006243ffeb3a3b56c06d7786f607a2efacd79", "parents": ["cf4dd026150bc0a343e293e5d39e801be50f7533"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073418 - Drive the newtab dwell time test's clock instead of racing EventStateManager's idle tick, r=mconley.\n\ntest_newtab_dwell_time_in_ping fabricated one \"active\" notification and slept\n100ms, but TelemetryFeed credits dwell only up to its last \"active\"\nnotification, so EventStateManager's idle tick, whose deadline the test does not\ncontrol, could land in the sleep, stop the stopwatch at zero and submit a ping\nwith no newtab.dwell_time.\n\nNotify twice with the feed's clock advanced in between, so a tick anywhere in\nthe window still has an interval to credit.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327288\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_newtab_ping.js"], "git_node": "aa6a813c3c23a54b8172a4e4369bc62fcca37b68", "git_parents": ["afe7d1b18c520c4468fcd330b6259a0f3f193cd4"], "node": "4dc39463692a9e3c4491f5221122c1312c800b63", "parents": ["42e006243ffeb3a3b56c06d7786f607a2efacd79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2074592 - fix(pbw): Relay promo and basics spotlight fixes from QA r=omc-reviewers,emcminn\" for causing node failures related to asrouter-newtab-multistage.\n\nThis reverts commit 853e8033cafe52ac8a16c5e6828e66e184d3c9d7.\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/BrowserUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d7d28d3dded0021e6791676c9d78c4fcda921ee0", "git_parents": ["aa6a813c3c23a54b8172a4e4369bc62fcca37b68"], "node": "e55b72282ee8d1bbaab15f719bd52be9fad58c51", "parents": ["4dc39463692a9e3c4491f5221122c1312c800b63"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070277 - Let a mouse release over a panel-list item choose it in content documents. r=mstriemer,urlbar-reviewers,daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324382\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_searchModeSwitcher.js", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/browser.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/browser_panel_item_click_on_mouseup.js", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_panel_item_mouseup_click.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.mjs"], "git_node": "0832035659110a26d63f12c76e5558c6491c6313", "git_parents": ["d7d28d3dded0021e6791676c9d78c4fcda921ee0"], "node": "04960170aa5a898fc03c10d17bcd671c5fc441e2", "parents": ["e55b72282ee8d1bbaab15f719bd52be9fad58c51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074595 - Don't let a garbage annotation read from a crashed process abort the crash helper. r=afranchuk,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nAfter writing a child's minidump, the crash helper reads the child's annotation table out of its memory. The\nchild may have kept running other threads while it waited, so an entry can be read mid-update or from a table\nthat was just reallocated, and its length is then garbage. copy_array sized its Vec directly from that length\nwith Vec::with_capacity(), so any length above isize::MAX panicked with \"capacity overflow\" and took the crash\nhelper down. Android's crash helper is not restarted after it dies, so every later child crash in that session\nwent unreported. This shows up in geckoview-junit as ContentCrashTest#crashContentJava and the crash tests\nafter it timing out once the helper has died. Before bug 2050534 the same bad entries crashed the helper with\na segfault inside retrieve_annotations instead. The same reads are used for the main process's annotations on\nevery crash report, and that process is just as live.\n\ncopy_array now reserves fallibly on every platform, which also rejects a byte count that would overflow, and\nreturns ReadError::TooLarge instead of panicking. mozannotation_server also rejects byte-buffer and nsCString\nlengths above 1 MiB, far above any real annotation, so a garbage length that happens to be allocatable doesn't\nturn into a multi-gigabyte ptrace read, and it stops walking the table after max_annotations entries. A bad\nentry is now dropped and the rest of the annotations and the minidump are still delivered.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328250\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/mozannotation_server/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/process_reader/src/error.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/process_reader/src/platform/linux.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/process_reader/src/platform/macos.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/process_reader/src/platform/windows.rs"], "git_node": "087b2047df330932b854b64851b988a4d2f3c7c6", "git_parents": ["0832035659110a26d63f12c76e5558c6491c6313"], "node": "c90d402ed38868e3115ac1a16a8a946e30ed58fd", "parents": ["04960170aa5a898fc03c10d17bcd671c5fc441e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074623 - Avoid using Skia for PathRecording::AsRect. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nAvoid constructing a Skia path every time PathRecording::AsRect is called. For\ncases AsRect is used (i.e. PushClip), we mostly just need a quick check to discover\nwell-formated rect paths, and don't need the more exhaustive and expensive checks\nSkia is doing, for which the overhead of constructing a Skia path is unjustified.\n\nInstead, use a check similar to Skia's own trivial_rect, which just quickly verifies\nthe path is composed of a MoveTo, 3 LineTos, and a Close op, and that the lines are\nall axis-aligned and orthogonal to each other.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328255\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/PathRecording.cpp", "gfx/2d/PathRecording.h"], "git_node": "3c7fa7671e4030fd820447b056200733577448de", "git_parents": ["087b2047df330932b854b64851b988a4d2f3c7c6"], "node": "9fb159fb1f5bd8c2933e84d6124d434512e564dd", "parents": ["c90d402ed38868e3115ac1a16a8a946e30ed58fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074628 - Avoid computing unused bounds for optimized shadow targets. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nFor optimized shadow drawing without filters, no bounds are actually needed. This can be\nexpensive for a PathRecording, where it incurs a conversions to a Skia path to compute\nprecise bounds that won't actually be used.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328258\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp"], "git_node": "970c363ab29771c578236497b8e869c0af8f262b", "git_parents": ["3c7fa7671e4030fd820447b056200733577448de"], "node": "cf11ec24d7ed8db848d2ef003f58e29a825507bb", "parents": ["9fb159fb1f5bd8c2933e84d6124d434512e564dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074665 - Notify ahochheiden of build times perf alerts r=perftest-reviewers,sparky\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328286\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/building/buildbase.py"], "git_node": "91d1defe84f38ec2f95d3b86932e40cf32288c8d", "git_parents": ["970c363ab29771c578236497b8e869c0af8f262b"], "node": "2269f9842bf79f29f31b64d230cb377c5eacb1b5", "parents": ["cf11ec24d7ed8db848d2ef003f58e29a825507bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073457 - Consolidate urlbar's open-state high-contrast border. r=adw\n\nBoth halves of the joint background read the open border variable, so one prefers-contrast override closes the border across the seam. Linux high contrast lacked the border, and on macOS the accent-colored outline becomes a text-colored border.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327790\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css", "browser/themes/windows/browser.css"], "git_node": "bf877b7eb3ade383ee922e0d3a3b6cb3d67b229a", "git_parents": ["91d1defe84f38ec2f95d3b86932e40cf32288c8d"], "node": "3b9bc57e9d8621de075dcc2d8bd3427e27f7daa2", "parents": ["2269f9842bf79f29f31b64d230cb377c5eacb1b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064663 - Add space between components in the urlbar r=dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324175\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/identity-block/identity-block.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "1a098add66b3564a570baa4b2d1ac8f803e1fc74", "git_parents": ["bf877b7eb3ade383ee922e0d3a3b6cb3d67b229a"], "node": "b82383b9361b75ac11975ce5144c1bca3604a614", "parents": ["3b9bc57e9d8621de075dcc2d8bd3427e27f7daa2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olivier Mehani \u003comehani@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "lando: remove old lando config (Bug 2067620) r=conduit-reviewers,sheehan DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326837\n", "files": [".lando.ini", "tools/tryselect/lando.py"], "git_node": "e0361512a7802c72a55a01c9fe1497c3863a3d7d", "git_parents": ["1a098add66b3564a570baa4b2d1ac8f803e1fc74"], "node": "f158079c9597f8acf5b2ce416ecb3fc2d5d7fa3e", "parents": ["b82383b9361b75ac11975ce5144c1bca3604a614"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": [], "git_node": "fe8af2900f1c9cba9319ef1c7fe607f824fb6f7e", "git_parents": ["e0361512a7802c72a55a01c9fe1497c3863a3d7d", "428af5c20dcedde48f4e6cc40e591f6115c85205"], "node": "4802412dbb95398b8521baa88be767c0c99645b8", "parents": ["f158079c9597f8acf5b2ce416ecb3fc2d5d7fa3e", "631808b9e7769c9abb03b6eab7f09e2a0541325b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bas Schouten \u003cbschouten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069900: Send FCP entry after scroll has happened. r=canova\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327842\n", "files": ["layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/paint-timing/fcp-only/fcp-after-scroll.html"], "git_node": "5ed077246fe6b93a4e12509005f4ab9a86f06db2", "git_parents": ["fe8af2900f1c9cba9319ef1c7fe607f824fb6f7e"], "node": "a51175125e0df8fd74bb887e9472ce1ebf254816", "parents": ["4802412dbb95398b8521baa88be767c0c99645b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Delia Pop \u003cdpop@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074464 - Update the verifyAddingTabToExistingGroupViaSelectionTest UI test r=aaronmt\n\nAdded the missing annotation @Critical for 2 regression UI tests.\n\nUpdated and renamed the verifyAddingTabToExistingGroupViaSelectionTest UI test to match the manual test. Added `longClickTabAndTapAddToGroup(tabTitle)`, which enters multi-select via `mozLongClick` on the tab (matching manual step\u00a02), then opens the selection three-dot menu -\u003e \"Add to group\".\n\nThe UI test successfully passed 50x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=95493  | Try ]]\nAll efficiency UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=95496  | Try ]]\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328131\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabDrawerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SettingsAboutTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/TabbedBrowsingTest.kt"], "git_node": "fed4db30135c84d7035506c51fc321e5e630dfe4", "git_parents": ["5ed077246fe6b93a4e12509005f4ab9a86f06db2"], "node": "11828d561eb58aa3187e35982ba1e508988bb5eb", "parents": ["a51175125e0df8fd74bb887e9472ce1ebf254816"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072511 - Add support of headless mode with GPU process r=geckoview-reviewers,gtk-reviewers,gfx-reviewers,emilio,owlish,nical\n\nOn Android, gecko already tries to use HeadlessCompositorWidget in GPU process during gtest.It is done without setting \"MOZ_HEADLESS=1\" on Android. And caused crashes during gtest. See Bug 2072484.\n\nThe change addresses the crash.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326389\n", "files": ["gfx/ipc/GPUProcessHost.cpp", "gfx/ipc/RemoteCompositorSession.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositor.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "widget/CompositorWidget.h", "widget/android/AndroidCompositorWidget.h", "widget/android/CompositorWidgetChild.cpp", "widget/cocoa/CocoaCompositorWidget.h", "widget/cocoa/CompositorWidgetChild.cpp", "widget/gtk/CompositorWidgetChild.cpp", "widget/gtk/GtkCompositorWidget.h", "widget/headless/HeadlessCompositorWidget.h", "widget/headless/HeadlessCompositorWidgetParent.cpp", "widget/headless/HeadlessCompositorWidgetParent.h", "widget/headless/HeadlessWidget.cpp", "widget/headless/HeadlessWidget.h", "widget/headless/moz.build", "widget/nsIWidget.cpp", "widget/windows/CompositorWidgetChild.cpp", "widget/windows/CompositorWidgetChild.h", "widget/windows/CompositorWidgetParent.cpp", "widget/windows/CompositorWidgetParent.h", "widget/windows/PCompositorWidget.ipdl"], "git_node": "506c82a93b4ecda7a35d3fc4180ab2297e5223f7", "git_parents": ["fed4db30135c84d7035506c51fc321e5e630dfe4"], "node": "1b5bba299ddcf2d8fa0e63c97feee874e94df9d9", "parents": ["11828d561eb58aa3187e35982ba1e508988bb5eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067165: When building the accessibility tree, traverse into descendants of an inert display: contents element. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,morgan\n\nWe don't (and shouldn't) create an Accessible for a display: contents element (including a \u003cslot\u003e inside shadow DOM) if it is inside an inert subtree.\nHowever, it's possible that it has descendants that are not inert; e.g. an open modal \u003cdialog\u003e.\nPreviously, if we chose not to create a display: contents Accessible, we skipped its entire subtree.\nIn the modal dialog case above, that meant we skipped the dialog, resulting in a completely empty document (since the rest of the document is inert when a modal dialog is open).\nThis only occurred if the initial tree was built after the dialog was shown; e.g. the accessibility service was started late.\nThe mutation path actually handled this correctly, since the dialog was inserted directly in that case, rather than walking from an ancestor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328035\n", "files": ["accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/base/nsCoreUtils.cpp", "accessible/base/nsCoreUtils.h", "accessible/moz.build", "accessible/tests/browser/lateServiceEnable/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/lateServiceEnable/browser_framelessAboveModalDialog.js", "accessible/tests/browser/lateServiceEnable/head.js"], "git_node": "e8a2c5954a210fa80c608a9ac4793c5234f6d49a", "git_parents": ["506c82a93b4ecda7a35d3fc4180ab2297e5223f7"], "node": "002238114d635dbe2ec39515134fb147bcbc06b3", "parents": ["1b5bba299ddcf2d8fa0e63c97feee874e94df9d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1917424. In reftest drawSnapshot mode, use the fullzoom to calculate the correct rect to draw. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328115\n", "files": ["gfx/tests/reftest/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/border-dotted/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/border-image/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/canvas/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/image-element/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/image/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/list-item/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/reftest-sanity/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/scrolling/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/svg/as-image/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/svg/as-image/zoom/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/svg/filters/css-filters/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/svg/filters/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/svg/image/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/svg/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/svg/svg-integration/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/svg/text/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/text-svgglyphs/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/transform-3d/reftest.list", "layout/tools/reftest/reftest.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "5eec471c8d533c58572662713f0efdc49feb46b1", "git_parents": ["e8a2c5954a210fa80c608a9ac4793c5234f6d49a"], "node": "7571501da8512dbebe1e475622d1dcc2330ff16a", "parents": ["002238114d635dbe2ec39515134fb147bcbc06b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Friedberger \u003csimon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072826 - Extend memory_phc metric expiry to 173 r=pbone\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328234\n", "files": ["xpcom/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "0ccba3d8bf8ac7ba8e399a4cbf441711210c6149", "git_parents": ["5eec471c8d533c58572662713f0efdc49feb46b1"], "node": "47bc9109d0961c619f1d33cd4f520b6f89dbf307", "parents": ["7571501da8512dbebe1e475622d1dcc2330ff16a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Friedberger \u003csimon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037232 - Remove stale legacy telemetry references from memory_phc metric descriptions r=pbone\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328274\n", "files": ["xpcom/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "79f09caaa97e349c1e689995aac09da30046db7e", "git_parents": ["0ccba3d8bf8ac7ba8e399a4cbf441711210c6149"], "node": "62c5a09ef1056397d65223798ec342623a106dbb", "parents": ["47bc9109d0961c619f1d33cd4f520b6f89dbf307"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Drew Willcoxon \u003cadw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070772 - Remove PartnerLinkAttribution and its one remaining use case in urlbar. r=daisuke,mconley,urlbar-reviewers\n\nRemove `sendAttributionRequest` on top-sites result payloads.\n`UrlbarProviderTopSites` calls `PartnerLinkAttribution.makeRequest()` and\nrecords `contextual.services.topsites` telemetry when `sendAttributionRequest`\nis true, so remove that code too.\n\nI didn't remove the `contextual.services.topsites` metric since\n`UrlbarProviderTopSites` still uses it for impressions and it also seems to\nstill be used by newtab [1], although that could be dead code, I don't know. If\nit's OK to remove, I think we can handle that in a follow-up.\n\nRemove `PartnerLinkAttribution.sys.mjs` since urlbar was the last consumer. Move\nthe `CONTEXTUAL_SERVICES_PING_TYPES` consts to `AmpSuggestions` and rename them\nto better fit their one remaining use case.\n\nRemove the following two prefs from `firefox.js` since they are now unused:\n\n```\nbrowser.partnerlink.attributionURL\nbrowser.partnerlink.campaign.topsites\n```\n\n[1] https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/e3285238626d45d2ec7ee8941fc1c49615730ba5/browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs#1057-1131\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327231\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderTopSites.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/AmpSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_top_sites_attribution.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/browser/browser_quicksuggest_ping_nullValues.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/browser/browser_quicksuggest_ping_offline.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/browser/browser_quicksuggest_ping_online.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/browser/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarProviderTopSites.js", "browser/modules/PartnerLinkAttribution.sys.mjs", "browser/modules/moz.build"], "git_node": "7af4d6fd6f9a733929bb6360d4be433e59dd297a", "git_parents": ["79f09caaa97e349c1e689995aac09da30046db7e"], "node": "39cd530d0d92d85a4afa82bf5d4298b8819bb57a", "parents": ["62c5a09ef1056397d65223798ec342623a106dbb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074465 - Convert verifyCreditCardsSectionTest regression UI test to the efficiency framework r=aaronmt\n\nThe UI test successfully passed 25x on Firebase \u2705\nAll UI tests successfully passed 1x on Fi